{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "ooh la la (Remix)", "line": "No computer, but this MAC got more shots than gigabytes", "vault_lines": ["No computer, but this MAC got more shots than gigabytes"], "meaning": "The MAC-10 is a fully-automatic firearm known for its rapid firing rate. Apple designs and manufactures Macintosh (“Mac”) computers, which have storage capacities measured in gigabytes. The MacBook Pro laptops released in the year of this remix’s release (2021), ranged from 512GB to 8,000GB (or 8TB).\n\nBy saying “no computer,” Wayne clarifies that he is not referring to a Mac computer, and that his MAC-10 clips contain more bullets than a Mac computer contains gigabytes of storage space.", "annotation_id": "38812410", "url": "https://genius.com/38812410", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "ooh la la (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Run-the-jewels-ooh-la-la-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "ooh la la (Remix)", "genius_id": 7226643, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "nasty (Remix)", "line": "I be filleting it, I be sautéing it", "vault_lines": ["I be filleting it, I be sautéing it"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne uses these culinary terms as a playful metaphor for sexual mastery and passion. Generally, “filleting” involves the precise, delicate removal of the best cuts of meat, while “sautéing” involves cooking something over high heat with quick, jumping movements. In this specific lyric, he uses these definitions to describe his performance: “filleting” suggests he is handling his partner with surgical precision and skill, while “sautéing” emphasizes the high heat and intensity of the encounter.", "annotation_id": "39639551", "url": "https://genius.com/39639551", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "nasty (Remix)", "line": "I’ll fuck up your makeup like Marilyn Manson", "vault_lines": ["I'll fuck up your makeup like Marilyn Manson"], "meaning": "Marilyn Manson’s signature look revolves around intentional distortion; he often performs with heavy lipstick and thick eyeliner that is smeared, smudged, or “melted” across his face to create an unsettling, gothic aesthetic [2, 4]. The lyric uses Manson as a shorthand for this smudged effect, comparing a “perfect” face of makeup being ruined during a passionate encounter to Manson’s purposefully messy and “fucked up” style [1, 3].", "annotation_id": "39639536", "url": "https://genius.com/39639536", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "nasty (Remix)", "line": "Add a little sugar to sweeten the Molly Like Pamela, Tommy, and Whitney and Bobby", "vault_lines": ["Add a little sugar to sweeten the Molly"], "meaning": "Pamela Anderson and Tommy Lee both took Molly on their first date, which lead to their quick engagement. Although Whitney Houston and Bobby Brown have not been reported to have used MDMA, their mutual drug addition lead to their subsequent divorce.", "annotation_id": "37336452", "url": "https://genius.com/37336452", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "nasty (Remix)", "line": "I’ll pull your titties out like Janet Jackson", "vault_lines": ["I'll pull your titties out like Janet Jackson"], "meaning": "The 2004 Super Bowl incident involving Janet Jackson and Justin Timberlake is referenced here, also known as “Janetgate” or “nipplegate” to many. At the end of the setlist, the duo performed Rock Your Body, with Timberlake pulling a part of Jackson’s outfit off during the final line. Most of her right breast was revealed, embellished with a nipple shield.", "annotation_id": "37336348", "url": "https://genius.com/37336348", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "nasty (Remix)", "line": "I play with that pussy like Carole Baskin’s", "vault_lines": ["I play with that pussy like Carole Baskin's"], "meaning": "This line refers to a prominent figure in the 2020 series Tiger King. Carole Baskin is someone who has devoted her entire life to tiger conservation, and protecting wild cats.", "annotation_id": "37336333", "url": "https://genius.com/37336333", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
