{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "high3r", "line": "And right now, do not know who I am", "vault_lines": ["And right now, do not know who I am"], "meaning": "Long before Mike WiLL invited him to take part in the Ransom 3, Weezy had already written in great detail ‘bout his worries in the autobiographical Carter V.\nHere are some lines:\n“I don’t know who you are anymore\nTalkin’ to the man in her mirror\nThat been fuckin' wit' these bitches\nAnd it’s dangerous, sleepin' wit' these strangers\n    Every night a different woman, doin' the same shit”", "annotation_id": "33428458", "url": "https://genius.com/33428458", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "high3r", "line": "Told her I can’t, she say, “Why, sir?” I told her that I can only be your sexual advisor", "vault_lines": ["Told her I can't, she say, \"Why, sir?\""], "meaning": "Fallin' in love doesn’t seem like somethin' special to him, Tune' also stated this in songs “Perfect Strangers” and “Demon”, both of these songs are imbued wit' long sadness and thirst for truth, but Tunechi’s forced to be just a spectator.", "annotation_id": "33420066", "url": "https://genius.com/33420066", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
