{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Zoo", "line": "Then I’m uptown, baby like I’m Peter Gunz, ha (Uptown!) Or Lord Tariq; to the Lord, I speak", "vault_lines": ["Then I'm uptown, baby like I'm Peter Gunz, ha (Uptown!)"], "meaning": "Reference to the Bronx Hip Hop duo Lord Tariq & Peter Gunz and their song “Deja Vu (Uptown Baby)”.\n\n\n\nA few years later, in 2010, Wayne would sign Peter Gunz' son Cory Gunz to his label YMCMB.", "annotation_id": "2646912", "url": "https://genius.com/2646912", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Zoo", "line": "It’s M.O.B. ’til the mortician dress me", "vault_lines": ["It's M.O.B. 'til the mortician dress me"], "meaning": "An elaborate way to say that Wayne will be about his money until he dies.\n\nM.O.B. stands for “money over bitches”; Wayne even has it tattooed on his chest.\n\n\n\nA mortician is a funeral director who dresses up corpses in suits when they are put into their casket.", "annotation_id": "2590827", "url": "https://genius.com/2590827", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
