{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "If you on the pole, play your position", "vault_lines": ["If you on the pole, play your position"], "meaning": "2 chainz is demanding his strippers to get on the poles and do their routine so he can throw some money for them.\n\nThis is also a play on the phrase “Pole Position” which in Motorsports is the starting position a racer gets in the very front of the race (closest to the starting line).", "annotation_id": "31537227", "url": "https://genius.com/31537227", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "All this ice on me, and my niggas playing freeze tag", "vault_lines": ["All this ice on me, and my niggas playing freeze tag"], "meaning": "Ice is slang for jewelry and 2 Chainz is decked in it. Freeze tag is a game in which one or multiple players assume the role of “it” and try to tag those who are not “it”. In order to be unfrozen, a teammate has to tag you. The freeze tag that Chainz and his crew are engaging in isn’t the actual game, but rather the purchasing of a bunch of jewelry.", "annotation_id": "12881375", "url": "https://genius.com/12881375", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "Two-gun gang, all-black Ferrari", "vault_lines": ["Two-gun gang, all-black Ferrari"], "meaning": "Much like the amount of chains on his neck, 2 Chainz and his crew carry two guns with them at all times. He reiterates this idea later in this verse, and has also recited similar lyrics in his songs “Feds Watching”, “Fuk Da Roof”, and “Too Easy”.\n\nTwo guns and I’m deuced up\n\n2 Chainz may be strapped up with two guns due to an incident where he was robbed in San Francisco. In his verse on Dave East’s “Can’t Ignore”, 2 Chainz vows to carry a weapon with him wherever he goes because of this incident.\n\nEver since a nigga tried me in Cali\nI took a chopper on tour", "annotation_id": "11720816", "url": "https://genius.com/11720816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "Me and my nigga pass your ho like a hot potato I be like, “You could get her”, he be like, ”You could get her” I be like, “You could have her”, he be like, ”You could have her” He be like, “It don’t matter”, I be like, ”Me neither”", "vault_lines": ["Me and my nigga pass your ho like a hot potato"], "meaning": "Hot Potato is a game in which players pass around an object with a clock running, and the loser is the one holding the object when time is up. Therefore, players pass the object around quickly. Here, 2 Chainz states that he will not only steal your girl, but he will pass her quickly to his friends if they want to fornicate with her.\n\nTold that lil bitch I’ll pass\nNigga watch the assist\n\nChainz then goes on to simulate dialogue with whoever he is considering passing the girl to, insinuating that they have sex with so many women that they have no preference whether or not they get to sleep with this woman.", "annotation_id": "11536452", "url": "https://genius.com/11536452", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "Two guns on me, both with extensions", "vault_lines": ["Two guns on me, both with extensions"], "meaning": "An extended clip is a large capacity magazine for a firearm. Chainz has one for each of his weapons. He also refers to this concept later in the album.\n\nExtendo clip, extendo roll\nWhen your girl leave me she need a hair salon", "annotation_id": "11536418", "url": "https://genius.com/11536418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "So many chains on, it look like my neck gone", "vault_lines": ["So many chains on, it look like my neck gone"], "meaning": "2 Chainz but I got me a few on\n\nAlthough his pseudonym suggests that he wears two necklaces, 2 Chainz will not hesitate to put on an excess of jewelry from his expensive collection.", "annotation_id": "11536324", "url": "https://genius.com/11536324", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "[Intro]", "vault_lines": ["My girl came through and brought an extra body"], "meaning": "A sample of 2 Chainz‘ daughter.", "annotation_id": "1595881", "url": "https://genius.com/1595881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "Yeah, I got the chopper for the correspondents", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I got the chopper for the correspondents"], "meaning": "Double entendre here.\n\nHe has an automatic gun, most likely an AK47 for those who play around.\n\nThis is also a play on Newscasts where a news correspondent reports a story in a helicopter, or chopper.", "annotation_id": "1027465", "url": "https://genius.com/1027465", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "[Chorus: Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": ["My girl came through and brought an extra body"], "meaning": "In an interview with MTV News, Wayne told them he thought he sounded “wack as hell” on this track.", "annotation_id": "1017832", "url": "https://genius.com/1017832", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "The bitch got a man, but she scheming on the low, how it go? It go, fuck them other niggas ’cause I’m down for my niggas", "vault_lines": ["The bitch got a man, but she scheming on the low, how it go?"], "meaning": "A common theme in Lil Wayne’s lyrics are that he doesn’t care about any other crews or rappers, he only cares about his team\n\n\n\nWeezy interpolates C-Murder’s hook on Snoop Dogg’s “Down 4 My Niggas”:\n\nFuck them other niggas ‘cause I’m down for my niggas\nFuck them other niggas 'cause I’m down for my niggas\nFuck them other niggas 'cause I ride for my niggas\nI die for my niggas (What), fuck them other niggas, niggas", "annotation_id": "994548", "url": "https://genius.com/994548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "2 Chainz, talking on the FLX phone", "vault_lines": ["2 Chainz, talking on the FLX phone"], "meaning": "The FLX phone turns your wireless phone into a wire phone. .\n\n\n\nUnsurprisingly in this rapper-as-brand marketplace, Chainz gets paid to like these phones. .", "annotation_id": "967320", "url": "https://genius.com/967320", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "I had enough of the broken promises So I’m in a room full of Pocahontases", "vault_lines": ["I had enough of the broken promises"], "meaning": "There have of course been countless broken promises to  Native Americans over the centuries.  One of the biggest was the Treaty of Fort Laramie\n\n“Pocahontas” refers to an actual Tsenacommacah woman connected to the establishment of Jamestown and John Smith circa 1607. She has been subsequently mythologized by both Smith and Disney, among others, but was, at the time, between 10-13, while Smith was is his late 20s. I hope that makes Disney creepy for you. 2 Chainz uses her name in plural to connect with the longer history of “broken promises” towards indigenous people by Europeans colonizers and, later, the U.S. Government.", "annotation_id": "967165", "url": "https://genius.com/967165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "I’m from where they send shots, then we send ’em back", "vault_lines": ["I'm from where they send shots, then we send 'em back"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is from College Park, Georgia, the Atlanta region’s most unsafe community, where there is a lot of gun violence. People shoot at him so he shoots back.", "annotation_id": "966831", "url": "https://genius.com/966831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "Yuck daddy Yuck daddy", "vault_lines": ["My girl came through and brought an extra body"], "meaning": "2 Chainz' daughter is on the intro and outro; the song is nasty, so his daughter is saying, “Yuck Daddy.” .", "annotation_id": "966706", "url": "https://genius.com/966706", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "Former Posturepedic I was slept on", "vault_lines": ["Former Posturepedic I was slept on"], "meaning": "When 2 Chainz was Tity Boi he was slept on, like a mattress!\n\n\n\nPosturepedic mattreses are high-end premium mattresses and arguably the best mattresses around whe it comes to comfort and everything a good mattress is supposed to do. Most people who buy them sleep on them but don’t know or seem to forget how good a quality of mattress they have. Like a posturepedic mattress, 2 Chainz has been a quality and outstanding rapper all along but was slept on (or overlooked) until just recently.", "annotation_id": "966548", "url": "https://genius.com/966548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "Man, life is a bitch, mine is a gold digger", "vault_lines": ["Man, life is a bitch, mine is a gold digger"], "meaning": "Play on the saying “life’s a bitch” (i.e. it sucks)\n\n\nBitch also refers to his chick, so if Wayne’s life is a bitch, his bitch is a gold digger.\nGold digger is a bitch only after his money but gold diggers are also found in (gold) mines\n\n\n\nBut we already knew this since it’s not the first time Weezy has spit this bar…", "annotation_id": "966531", "url": "https://genius.com/966531", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yuck!", "line": "Before Benihana’s it was canned goods Before canned goods it was Similac", "vault_lines": ["Before Benihana's it was canned goods"], "meaning": "Rappers sure do love their Benihana-visits-as-status-symbol\n\nHe could also be referring to his growth as an artist. Similac is a baby formula for infants:\n\n\n\nAfter Similac, he was doing canned goods which would be referring to him a little more older:\n\n\n\nFinally, he does Benihana’s which is far more sophisticated than Similac and canned goods thereby showing his growth from the time he started as a simple rapper to a more sophisticated and more successful rapper as most rappers view Benihana’s as a status symbol.", "annotation_id": "966519", "url": "https://genius.com/966519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
