{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "Give you the world if it was for me My diamond grill make it hard to see, I’m lying through my teeth", "vault_lines": ["Give you the world if it was for me"], "meaning": "“Lying through your teeth” is an expression to use when someone is just straight up lying with noremorse. Although hearing a lie has nothing to do with your ability to see, Wayne uses clever wordplay to flex the diamonds on his teeth saying that they make hard to see he’s “lying through his teeth” or just lying because he’s not really willing to give this girl the world", "annotation_id": "24924430", "url": "https://genius.com/24924430", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "You remind me of... my memory ain’t what it used to be”", "vault_lines": ["You remind me of... my memory ain't what it used to be\""], "meaning": "Wayne is acting like he’s getting ready to tell her something that she reminds him of but follows up saying his memory ain’t what it used to be, playing into his act. Saying “you remind me of” then not being able to remember where you were going with the sentence is definitely a form of bad memory however Wayne is just trying to distract the girl from their original, deeper convo", "annotation_id": "24924404", "url": "https://genius.com/24924404", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "You the best dressed with your breasts showing Like a salad, no dressing,", "vault_lines": ["You the best dressed with your breasts showing"], "meaning": "Chance is saying this girl looks the best when she’s wearing nothing, then continues this idea with saying she’s like a salad with no( Ranch) dressing.", "annotation_id": "16047762", "url": "https://genius.com/16047762", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "[Produced by Cam, Nate Fox, and Peter Cottontale]", "vault_lines": ["Ask for the bread, then fuck in the restroom"], "meaning": "Lots of samples on this track, 3 to be exact. One was from a Reverend W.A. Donaldson called “Baptizing Scene”, and the vocal sample appears at 0:04 in the track.\n\nThe second is the Michael Jackson sample Fox found in the song “The Way You Make Me Feel”, which the phrase “Go on girl!” was then chopped up into the beat. The last sample is the drums from a Joe Tex track called “Papa Was Too”\n\nProducer Nate Fox speaks on the beat to Complex:\n\nI get there at 11, and it’s me and Peter, Cam, Chance, and Pat, and everybody’s there. And he pulls us to the side and he’s like “So….we have to make a song for Dedication 5…tonight.” We were like, “Ok for sure, whatever you say.” And Chance was like, “No, for real, they called me, they said I can send them whatever I want. Not like Wayne has a song for me, Wayne needs a song from me.\n\nHere’s who did what:\n\n\nCam did justice with the drums, using the same effects on the sample as the drums from Vic Mensa’s track “Orange Soda”, confirmed by Vic and Cam themselves. Cam even showed us how to make those drums and effects!\nNate Fox found the Michael Jackson sample and chopped it up to add a somewhat soulful vibe to the track.\nCottontale started laying down those electric synth like chords to add another layer to the beat.\n\n\n\nhttps://soundcloud.com/producergenius/you-song-producer-genius", "annotation_id": "2901173", "url": "https://genius.com/2901173", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "And some strawberries and some chocolate And a fridge and some broccoli", "vault_lines": ["And some strawberries and some chocolate"], "meaning": "A well-known aphrodisiac and romantic gift. Chance has got game\n\n\n\nThe fridge would be good to store the strawberries so they don’t melt, but also where he’d keep this broccoli he doesn’t like…\n\nFun Fact: Chano likes strawberry lemonade.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/chancetherapper/status/213841812140457985", "annotation_id": "2170232", "url": "https://genius.com/2170232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "And I’ma buy a summer house, with a rec room", "vault_lines": ["And I'ma buy a summer house, with a rec room"], "meaning": "Chance is putting his newly stacked money into use, decorating his summer house, and fitting in a “recreation room” (a room used for a variety of purposes, such as parties, games, and other everyday/casual use)", "annotation_id": "2165601", "url": "https://genius.com/2165601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "Foxy, coffee Brown as the bosom I flew in on", "vault_lines": ["Brown as the bosom I flew in on"], "meaning": "The “man behind the curtain” for this tune is producer Nate Fox, a.k.a. Foxy\n\nChance uses his producer’s name to begin a series of references to iconic roles played by 70’s blaxploitation sex symbol Pam Grier.  She was the titular lead in 1973’s Foxy Brown and 1974’s Coffy", "annotation_id": "2162184", "url": "https://genius.com/2162184", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "Oh, and I forgot, I’ll take a microwave or oven So we could kick the butler out and we can make a muffin Maybe bake a dozen", "vault_lines": ["Oh, and I forgot, I'll take a microwave or oven"], "meaning": "In Chance’s buying spree he forgot to mention he’ll be purchasing a microwave oven. An interesting juxtaposition here since he just purchased this dope summer house with a rec room and a new car and has a chef! A microwave in a summer house with a chef is similar to putting Kool-Aid in a wine glass.\n\n“Muffin” here also refers to Chance wanting to get this girl pregnant (maybe even 12 times!)", "annotation_id": "2162000", "url": "https://genius.com/2162000", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "Dedication 5! Since ’05! Know that!", "vault_lines": ["Ask for the bread, then fuck in the restroom"], "meaning": "This is Wayne’s 5th installment of the Dedication series he does with DJ Drama, the first of which was released eight years ago on December 13, 2005. Check the other four on Rap Genius!\n\n\nThe Dedication\nDedication 2\nDedication 3\nDedication 4", "annotation_id": "2161980", "url": "https://genius.com/2161980", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "Nose round like the wheels that my rims spin on Lips full like the light on the dash was flickin’, oh wait, it wasn’t", "vault_lines": ["Nose round like the wheels that my rims spin on"], "meaning": "Describing the features of an African-American girl.\n\n\n\nBoth lines have sexual connotations – Chance will be nosing around her rims, and flicking her dash – clitoris.\n\nThe light on the dash is referring to the “empty” light, but because the gas tank (her lips) is full the light isn’t on. This technique of messing up on purpose to go along with the rhyme is used frequently by Wayne", "annotation_id": "2161968", "url": "https://genius.com/2161968", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "You the best bride and I’m the best groom Wedding presents got my best man at the Best Buy Buyin’ the Best of Fresh Prince for the bedroom", "vault_lines": ["You the best bride and I'm the best groom"], "meaning": "Chance and this girl would be perfect together. Chance sends his best man out to pick up a Fresh Prince DVD for their bridal bed. Sexy!\n\n\n\nThe fact that they’ll be watching TV in bed suggests Chance wants more than just sex and also that they like to be goofy and fun together\n\nCrazy alliteration here as well with best, bride, best, best, best, buy, buyin', best, bedroom", "annotation_id": "2161959", "url": "https://genius.com/2161959", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "It’s Wayne’s world, she say, “What is this world coming to?”", "vault_lines": ["It's Wayne's world, she say, \"What is this world coming to?\""], "meaning": "Wayne’s World is a 1992 film starring Dana Carvey and Michael Myers. Weezy has referenced Wayne’s World in a few other tracks.\n\nHe is very self-obsessed, which the girl can’t believe.\n\n\n\nThe girl is wondering if Wayne’s ‘world’ is ‘coming to’ – meaning if Wayne is going to orgasm as well, and also asking  where she will be in his world relationship-wise, etc.\n\nDamn", "annotation_id": "2161905", "url": "https://genius.com/2161905", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "And a car with no backseat and some leg room", "vault_lines": ["And a car with no backseat and some leg room"], "meaning": "He is referring to a Roadster, a two-seat car with emphasis on sporty handling.\n\n\n\nAs there’s no backseat, she’ll always be riding up-front with him", "annotation_id": "2161869", "url": "https://genius.com/2161869", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "[Verse 1: Chance The Rapper]", "vault_lines": ["Ask for the bread, then fuck in the restroom"], "meaning": "https://twitter.com/chancetherapper/status/374230607233949696\n\nFirst of all, it was super, super random. I decided to come out to Chicago just to kick it for a little bit. I really didn’t have a reason to be here. And Chance texted me saying “Come to the studio at 11.” I get there at 11, and it’s me and Peter, Cam, Chance, and Pat, and everybody’s there. And he pulls us to the side and he’s like “So….we have to make a song for Dedication 5…tonight.” We were like, “Ok for sure, whatever you say.” And Chance was like, “No, for real, they called me, they said I can send them whatever I want. Not like Wayne has a song for me, Wayne needs a song from me”\n- Nate Fox", "annotation_id": "2161860", "url": "https://genius.com/2161860", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "That’d be unfortunate, we’d have to rob a fortune teller", "vault_lines": ["That'd be unfortunate, we'd have to rob a fortune teller"], "meaning": "If they were just letters, it’d be unfortunate. Weezy plays with the word “unfortunate” claiming they’d have to rob a fortune teller to get their good fortune back", "annotation_id": "2161536", "url": "https://genius.com/2161536", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "You feel like Ruby Dee to me, great and powerful Ossie Who’s behind the man behind the curtain?", "vault_lines": ["You feel like Ruby Dee to me, great and powerful Ossie"], "meaning": "Ruby Dee is an American actress best known for co-starring in A Raisin in the Sun, whose second husband was the actor/director Ossie Davis. Also alluding to the lyric earlier in the song “you the best bride and I’m the best groom”, Chance’s girl feels like wifing up The Rapper. When asked by XXL about the reference he stated:\n\nThat’s just the perfect black couple.\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/chancetherapper/status/374715141939404802\n\nIn addition, Chance inserts a quick Wizard of Oz reference – you also hear the line as “the great and powerful Oz,” a catchphrase associated with the character.", "annotation_id": "2161286", "url": "https://genius.com/2161286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "’Cause I know you like vegetables even though I don’t I won’t say I won’t eat it if you chef it", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I know you like vegetables even though I don't"], "meaning": "Chance cares enough about his woman to buy her food and care for her needs and is kind enough to not rudely decline her cooking\n\n\n\nThis is also where the song starts to get bawdy – Chance is referring to a whole different kind of eating here as well.\n\nFun Fact: Chance is a chef:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/chancetherapper/status/188344646865399808", "annotation_id": "2161110", "url": "https://genius.com/2161110", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "My homeboy like your sister, maybe they can bake some cousins Ooh, isn’t that sweet? You feel like Kool-Aid in a wine glass", "vault_lines": ["Maybe bake a dozen"], "meaning": "Chance tries to hook his boy up with this girl’s sister, who presumably has similar genes and thus is beautiful\n\nMuffins are sweet, as is starting a family (…and Kool-Aid)\n\n\n\nChance also effortlessly displays masterful technique here, bringing his verse full circle back to the “Kool-Aid in a wine glass”, which is literally very sugary and “sweet”.", "annotation_id": "2160874", "url": "https://genius.com/2160874", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "I tried to change the subject So I said some crazy shit to her like ”What if you and I were just letters?", "vault_lines": ["I just happen to love you"], "meaning": "Tune goes completely off subject, using a classic pick-up line. U and I (you and I) are next to each other on a QWERTY keyboard. In her mind it probably sounded sweet!\n\n\n\nOn a second look, not only did Weezy want a change of subject, he also tried to hint his girl that they’d probably aren’t destined to be a couple. Hence the following line, “That’d be unfortunate we’d have to rob a fortune teller”", "annotation_id": "2160819", "url": "https://genius.com/2160819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "And she know me and whoever together, she hope we comin’ loose She told me that if she ain’t the one, she gon’ throw up the deuce", "vault_lines": ["And she know me and whoever together, she hope we comin' loose"], "meaning": "Wayne has multiple women, to the point where it doesn’t matter what their name is (me and whoever)\n\nHowever, this girl he’s with now wants to be his one and only, so she hopes he and his current girlfriend break up or she’s done\n\n\n\nClever wordplay here with “ain’t the one” and “throw up the deuce”", "annotation_id": "2160808", "url": "https://genius.com/2160808", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "But anyway, we can role-play or get straight to it Sorry, my mind in the gutter—better yet, sewer", "vault_lines": ["But anyway, we can role-play or get straight to it"], "meaning": "When your mind is “in the gutter” it means you’re thinking about something dirty (usually sexual). What Wayne is thinking about is so dirty, it’s worse than a gutter.\n\n“Role-playing” is a type of foreplay. Plays with the fact that Wayne just told the girl he doesn’t act\n\n\n\nBathrooms lead to the sewers and when a girl goes to the bathroom, she’s using her ass/vagina which is what is on Wayne’s mind", "annotation_id": "2160788", "url": "https://genius.com/2160788", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "You say I act like I don’t miss you, that’s because I don’t act", "vault_lines": ["You say I act like I don't miss you, that's because I don't act"], "meaning": "He is keeping it G – he just doesn’t miss her. The girl doesn’t seem to be happy about this.", "annotation_id": "2160783", "url": "https://genius.com/2160783", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "D5, what up 5?", "vault_lines": ["Ask for the bread, then fuck in the restroom"], "meaning": "A shout out to this mixtape and Birdman (5 star)", "annotation_id": "2160765", "url": "https://genius.com/2160765", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "Fuck it, I’ll hire Geoffrey to get a beverage if you should ever get parched", "vault_lines": ["Fuck it, I'll hire Geoffrey to get a beverage if you should ever get parched"], "meaning": "Chance continues the Fresh Prince puns here with a joke about Geoffrey, the put-upon butler from The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air", "annotation_id": "2160680", "url": "https://genius.com/2160680", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "Take you to your favorite restaurant Ask for the bread, then fuck in the restroom", "vault_lines": ["Ask for the bread, then fuck in the restroom"], "meaning": "Chance clearly cares about this girl since he takes her to her favorite restaurant. Before the meal even starts they’re already going at it\n\n\n\n“Ask for the bread” bread also means money, so could also be that this girl is cheap (like Kool-Aid) and only after Chance for his money", "annotation_id": "2160644", "url": "https://genius.com/2160644", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "You feel like Kool-Aid in a wine glass with your fine ass", "vault_lines": ["You feel like Kool-Aid in a wine glass with your fine ass"], "meaning": "Kool-Aid is a popular, cheap drink beloved by Chance’s Save Money crew. Wine has highbrow, classy associations. This great opening line says that the girl he’s talking to is the best of both worlds.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/chancetherapper/status/274695490107498498\n\nOn the outside she looks fine like a glass of wine, but on the inside she’s fun and normal. Chance has made the opposite comparison before, calling someone vodka in a redbull can.", "annotation_id": "2160601", "url": "https://genius.com/2160601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "Shout to Chi-Town!", "vault_lines": ["Ask for the bread, then fuck in the restroom"], "meaning": "The song’s feature and first verse is the illustrious Chance The Rapper who hails from Chicago. Drama is giving Chance’s hometown a shout out for having their MC on the record, salute.", "annotation_id": "2160476", "url": "https://genius.com/2160476", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "line": "You fine as two grapes gettin’ stomped out by a giant cask", "vault_lines": ["You fine as two grapes gettin' stomped out by a giant cask"], "meaning": "Stomping on grapes is traditionally how wine was made. A cask is something you keep wine in. Also, check the culinary wordplay between this line, “fine as two grapes” and the first line “You feel like kool-aid in a wine glass”", "annotation_id": "2160457", "url": "https://genius.com/2160457", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Song", "status": "done", "targets": 29, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-you-song-lyrics", "genius_title": "You Song", "genius_id": 212840, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "That’s why I’m movin’ all elusive These boys on they last resort and it’s givin’ us all inclusive", "vault_lines": ["That's why I'm movin' all elusive"], "meaning": "Drake here drops a double entendre. The other guys competing with Drake are now on their last legs after all their other attempts have failed. But when he says all inclusive, he also shows the gap between him and his competition financially as an all-inclusive resort is much cheaper than the non-inclusive resorts Drake stays at.", "annotation_id": "37868394", "url": "https://genius.com/37868394", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Yayo so clean, I told ’em call it, “Ajax”", "vault_lines": ["Yayo so clean, I told 'em call it, \"Ajax\""], "meaning": "“Yayo” is slang for cocaine, and Ajax is a brand of household cleaner. When cocaine is considered “clean,” it’s in its purest form—meaning it isn’t cut with any other substances like baking soda or talcum powder to save costs. Essentially, Ross only sells high quality product.", "annotation_id": "37256829", "url": "https://genius.com/37256829", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Damn, how can I forgive like this? I gotta dead a lot of shit just to live like this I had to fuck a lot of girls to get a kid like this I had to get a lot of cribs to get a crib like this", "vault_lines": ["Damn, how can I forgive like this?"], "meaning": "Drake is using the word “crib” as a double entendre. Initially, it refers to houses or luxury homes, suggesting that he had to work hard, invest, and buy multiple properties to be able to afford his current lifestyle. Metaphorically, it reflects the idea that achieving a high level of success requires gaining experience, and putting in effort and resources over time.\n\nDrake currently owns a $100-million mansion called The Embassy in his hometown of Toronto, which is the “crib” he is likely referring to in this line.", "annotation_id": "34114548", "url": "https://genius.com/34114548", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "All my chains look like snakes, that’s some real diamondbacks", "vault_lines": ["All my chains look like snakes, that's some real diamondbacks"], "meaning": "Weezy F shows off his vintage wordplay here, comparing his collection of snake chains to that of a Diamondback Rattlesnake. More people are bitten by the Western Diamondback each year than any other snake in the USA.", "annotation_id": "26461719", "url": "https://genius.com/26461719", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Brrrt, may I speak to pussy niggas? I just call it like I see it, I ain’t even lookin’, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Brrrt, may I speak to pussy niggas?"], "meaning": "This could be a callback to a lyric on Wayne’s December 2010 hit, “6 Foot 7 Foot,” where he raps:\n\nAnd I call it like I see it, and my glasses on", "annotation_id": "25145559", "url": "https://genius.com/25145559", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "I got sentenced, took some time and it was easier than simple", "vault_lines": ["I got sentenced, took some time and it was easier than simple"], "meaning": "In March 2010 Wayne got sentenced to 1 year in prison at Rikers Island for a weapons charge from a July 2007 incident. While Wayne was away there was a big ‘Free Weezy’ movement in the hip-hop world, and he was released in November after serving 8 months, going right back to running the rap game.\n\nWhile in jail, Wayne was mostly held in protective custody away from other prisoners, and his album I Am Not a Human Being became the first album since 2Pac’s 1995 album Me Against The World to reach the top position on the Billboard 200 while its artist was in prison. Safe to say his jail time was fairly easy.", "annotation_id": "24032128", "url": "https://genius.com/24032128", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Yeah, they plottin’ on me but they gotta do somethin’ Told my dawg two-somethin’ just to shoot somethin’ (M-M—) Left them niggas stretched out on the train tracks Rather you than me, here come that payback Got ‘em lookin’ for that paper that they can’t tax", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, they plottin' on me but they gotta do somethin'"], "meaning": "Ross likely makes a nod here back to his ninth studio album, Rather You Than Me which was released in March 2017.", "annotation_id": "23987829", "url": "https://genius.com/23987829", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Whip that big body Maybach like it’s a little Pontiac", "vault_lines": ["Whip that big body Maybach like it's a little Pontiac"], "meaning": "In his video for “Laugh Now Cry Later,” Drake displays concept cars.\nhttps://twitter.com/WordOnRd/status/1294162910932078592?s=20", "annotation_id": "23879902", "url": "https://genius.com/23879902", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Hialeah celebrated when Fidel died", "vault_lines": ["Hialeah celebrated when Fidel died"], "meaning": "Hialeah, the sixth largest city in Florida, has the highest percentage of Cuban and Cuban American residents of any city in the United States, at 73.37% of the population, making them a typical and prominent feature of the city’s culture.\n\nWhen Cuban dictator Fidel Castro died, the city erupted into a huge street party.", "annotation_id": "23878911", "url": "https://genius.com/23878911", "state": "pending", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Yeah, two-point-two for the Rafael Nadal", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, two-point-two for the Rafael Nadal"], "meaning": "This is likely a reference to the limited edition RM 27-04 watch made by Swiss watch company Richard Mille in partnership with Spanish Tennis player Rafael Nadal. In July 2021, Drake is known to have purchased one of these watches, of which only 50 were made available to the public. The watch was made to celebrate the 10 year anniversary of Richard Mille’s sponsorship of Nadal, who himself is known to wear some incredibly expensive sports watches during his Tennis matches.\n\n‘Two point two’ is most likely referring to a price of $2.2 million that Drake paid for the watch. The word ‘point’ could also be referring to a point in a game of Tennis.\n\n\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/CQ-ZPPJjmPj/?utm_source=ig_embed\n\nDrake wearing the watch\n\n\n\nRafael Nadal wearing the watch", "annotation_id": "23876337", "url": "https://genius.com/23876337", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Unthinkable when I think of the way these niggas been actin’ Yeah, I never did you nothin’ and you play like we family, huh? Next thing, you wanna shoot me down, it can’t be love Not sure where you was tryna send it, it can’t be up That day you sounded like a bitch, you fancy, huh?", "vault_lines": ["Unthinkable when I think of the way these niggas been actin'"], "meaning": "Drake is sending shots at Swizz Beatz, who reportedly did an Instagram Live with Busta Rhymes back in June 2020 while being intoxicated and seemingly called Drake a “pussy” over a possible record leaking and threatened to “shooting down” Drizzy’s newly acquired private jet. Even though Swizz did apologize the next day while saying “it’s all love”, Drizzy still remember the disrespect.\n\nSo here, Drake strung together “Unthinkable”, the title of a song he wrote with Alicia Keys, who is Swizz’s wife and interpolated ”Fancy”, a song from his own album Thank Me Later that he featured Swizz Beatz on the chorus.", "annotation_id": "23876246", "url": "https://genius.com/23876246", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Her ears popped, she lick my lollipop and my teardrops, Tunechi", "vault_lines": ["Her ears popped, she lick my lollipop and my teardrops, Tunechi"], "meaning": "Here Lil Wayne is suggesting she was so into his music, she “licked” him down below and on the face.\n\nLil Wayne has tear drop tattoos on his face. They’re controversial because a teardrop on the face can represent someone you’ve killed – Wayne has avoided this fact. https://www.stotkertattoo.com/tips/why-does-lil-wayne-have-a-teardrop-tattoo.html\n\nHe also released “Lollipop” on “Tha Carter III” in 2008:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2IH8tNQAzSs", "annotation_id": "23875398", "url": "https://genius.com/23875398", "state": "pending", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "I got bitches doin’ lines, I’m Adidas to ’em, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I got bitches doin' lines, I'm Adidas to 'em, nigga"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is suggesting he has girls “doin' lines” which could be a reference to cocaine. He is comparing himself to adidas as they are iconic for everyone wearing their 3 lines. Also they release successful lines of clothing.", "annotation_id": "23875379", "url": "https://genius.com/23875379", "state": "pending", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Been spazzin’ since CB was chunkin’ up the deuces, nigga Your shit was boo-boo, excuses, excuses, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Been spazzin' since CB was chunkin' up the deuces, nigga"], "meaning": "Chris Brown dropped the popular track “Deuces” in 2011 which Drake also featured on the remix. Drake is implying he has been doing his thing for over ten years now.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=11aMClGbrKE", "annotation_id": "23875368", "url": "https://genius.com/23875368", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "M-M—, M-M—", "vault_lines": ["Back to the real niggas glowin' in the dark (M-M—)"], "meaning": "This is the famous adlib for Maybach Music Group – voiced by Jessica Gomes.", "annotation_id": "23875355", "url": "https://genius.com/23875355", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Catalog is immaculate Still runnin’ the game, don’t ask me about the practice", "vault_lines": ["Still runnin' the game, don't ask me about the practice"], "meaning": "Describing his dominance over the rap industry, Drake references NBA Hall of Famer Allen Iverson’s infamous “practice” press conference from 2002. When a reporter asked Iverson about missing one practice, he expressed his displeasure at the question, responding with the following:\n\nWe’re talking about practice. Not a game! Not a game! Not a game! We’re talking about practice. Not a game; not the game that I go out there and die for and play every game like it’s my last, not the game, we’re talking about practice, man. I mean, how silly is that? We’re talking about practice.\n\nAs a basketball icon and NBA MVP, Iverson was upset that his premier status and willingness to practice were called into question. The lengthy nature of Iverson’s response also may have been triggered by the murder of his best friend, Rahsaan Langeford, seven months prior to the press conference. Like AI, Drake finds that his position or “run” atop the rap game will only continue and that “running” in practice is not of other’s concern.", "annotation_id": "23875131", "url": "https://genius.com/23875131", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Patti LaBelle, who knew that we would sell pies?", "vault_lines": ["Patti LaBelle, who knew that we would sell pies?"], "meaning": "Patti LaBelle is an American R&B and Soul artist known for  songs such as “If Only You Knew” and “On My Own.” In 2015, she began selling sweet potato pies at Walmart stores throughout the United States. Following a viral review from social media personality James Wright, the pies quickly sold out. In the years following the video, the pies continue to be a commercial success, with more than 36,000 sold each day.\n\nRoss uses pies as a double entendre to reference Patti LaBelle’s sweet potato dessert and drug trafficking. A pie is a slang term for a kilogram of cocaine, an amount which he expresses disbelief in his ability to sell. Ross himself drew his rap name from drug kingpin “Freeway” Ricky Ross, who established an extensive distribution network throughout Los Angeles in the 1980s and ‘90s.", "annotation_id": "23874932", "url": "https://genius.com/23874932", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Ho, you go on vacation, don’t ask me about relaxin’ Not sure if you know but I’m actually Michael Jackson The man I see in the mirror is actually goin’ platinum", "vault_lines": ["Ho, you go on vacation, don't ask me about relaxin'"], "meaning": "Drake compares his success in the music industry to legendary pop icon Michael Jackson. Jackson is remembered today for his live performances, his memorable record releases and the consistency of his music after departing from the The Jackson 5 group to start a solo career. After the King of Pop’s untimely death in 2009, his legacy was succeeded by his posthumous music, including his appearance on Drake’s 2018 album Scorpion, on the track “Don’t Matter to Me.” The song samples a once unreleased Jackson track and highlighted the similarity of both singers' careers. In 2016, Drake broke MJ’s record for most American Music Award nominations, establishing both as significant figures at the top of their respective genres.\n\nInterestingly enough, Drake boasts an appearance on the 2016 2 Chainz track “Big Amount,” rapping:\n\nMichael Jackson talkin' to me in my dreams\nAnd he say, “You bad and you know it”\nBetter shamone with my check then\nI’m a J. Prince investment\n\nIn those lines, Drake mentions the hit 1987 single “Bad,” similar to how he slyly mentions Jackson’s “Man in the Mirror” from 1988 on this track. Here, Drake uses the track’s title to boast his countless platinum certifications and is crowned as the top certified singles artist of the RIAA.", "annotation_id": "23874414", "url": "https://genius.com/23874414", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
