{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Mad Yet?", "line": "Niggas gettin’ mad lookin’ like they smellin’ horse shit But they never start shit,", "vault_lines": ["Niggas gettin' mad lookin' like they smellin' horse shit"], "meaning": "Wayne is, of course, The Shit, and when you smell something funky, your face screws up in disgust. In this case, jealousy as well as envy provokes a certain facial expression from people hating on Wayne.\n\nEnemies rarely get in to it though, Wayne’s reputation as a lyrical assassin precedes him.", "annotation_id": "6907717", "url": "https://genius.com/6907717", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Mad Yet?", "line": "Bitches takin’ portraits, why they in my fortress? Now wifey gettin’ mad, I’m like “ma’, they not important”", "vault_lines": ["Bitches takin' portraits, why they in my fortress?"], "meaning": "This is possibly a reference to the incident that happened at Wayne’s mansion – a hooker showed up and wanted have sex with Tunechi, of course in exchange for money. Tunechi denied that he ordered her.", "annotation_id": "6898742", "url": "https://genius.com/6898742", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Mad Yet?", "line": "Weed so fire, it gotta be arson Roaches in the ash tray, they probably need Orkin", "vault_lines": ["Weed so fire, it gotta be arson"], "meaning": "Fire signify’s potency. An arson has a love of fire, just as Wayne has a love of Weed.\n\nOrkin is a pest-removal company, and Wayne has an incredible roach problem.", "annotation_id": "6885836", "url": "https://genius.com/6885836", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Mad Yet?", "line": "I been had bands since Duran Duran, muthafucka", "vault_lines": ["I been had bands since Duran Duran, muthafucka"], "meaning": "Wordplay on “bands”, which is primarily used as a description for a collective of musicians, but in hip hop also a slang for money. Duran Duran is originally a band from the 80’s; meaning that Tunechi has had money since the 80’s.", "annotation_id": "6885725", "url": "https://genius.com/6885725", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Mad Yet?", "line": "Niggas say check me, he lied and he forged it", "vault_lines": ["Niggas say check me, he lied and he forged it"], "meaning": "Nobody tries to check Wayne, instead they forge their signature, fake thugs with fake threats.", "annotation_id": "6844332", "url": "https://genius.com/6844332", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Mad Yet?", "line": "Shoot the whole car up, and still don’t hit the car seat", "vault_lines": ["Shoot the whole car up, and still don't hit the car seat"], "meaning": "Wayne is such a talented shooter he is able to shoot up a car filled with people and not miss once; every bullet now rests in his enemy.\n\nA car seat is also another term for a child’s secure seat placed by parents. As was his message in “Only”;\n\n“Got two hoes with me, messed up, they got smaller guns\nAin’t thinkin' bout your son and daughter rooms”\n\nHis skill level is so high he can take out a car full of adults and leave the children unharmed.", "annotation_id": "6806568", "url": "https://genius.com/6806568", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Mad Yet?", "line": "She said it’s gonna cost me, I told her “bitch get off me” Her stripper name diamonds, her real name Swarovski", "vault_lines": ["She said it's gonna cost me, I told her \"bitch get off me\""], "meaning": "The perennial problem for a rapper: pick up a stripper and hope she doesn’t ask you for cash at the end of the experience.\n\nWayne’s one night stand is slightly misguided in her assessment of herself. Diamonds are one of the most expensive minerals in the world.\n\nSwarovski Crystals, however, are artificially made using a formula the company has themselves patented. Whilst Diamonds are the real thing, Swarovski is “fake”.\n\nIs this shade at the plastic surgery culture that is emerging in hip hop?", "annotation_id": "6775912", "url": "https://genius.com/6775912", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Mad Yet?", "line": "I’m lookin’ for a bitch to get it on with like Marvin", "vault_lines": ["I'm lookin' for a bitch to get it on with like Marvin"], "meaning": "Singer Marvin Gaye’s famous “Let’s Get It On” is referenced, although the romantic nature of that track is hardly mirrored in this statement.", "annotation_id": "6771424", "url": "https://genius.com/6771424", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Mad Yet?", "line": "Martian, martian around the world I orbit", "vault_lines": ["Martian, martian around the world I orbit"], "meaning": "Wayne is a martian.\n\nHe once proclaimed to be “Higher than a Kite”, but this is an entirely new level of high, channeling his inner David Bowie to be so high he is removed from the earth.", "annotation_id": "6771415", "url": "https://genius.com/6771415", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Mad Yet?", "line": "They love me and some of ’em wealthy and handsome", "vault_lines": ["They love me and some of 'em wealthy and handsome"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying all his “bitches love him and some,“ putting emphasis on the love. Wayne subliminally shouts out his homies from Migos. The group that gave rise to the popularity of the phrase \"handsome and wealthy” by naming a song after it. Tunechi can definitely relate to this term – he has a net worth of $140 million.", "annotation_id": "6770014", "url": "https://genius.com/6770014", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
