{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "I bring RAL to your funeral", "vault_lines": ["I bring RAL to your funeral"], "meaning": "RAL is a Euro colour matching system, Nuno or Blood gang colours are red.\n\n\n\n After he murders yo' ass Wayne will use these shades of red for your funeral decor in the form of; blood gang members and blood itself, belonging to your funeral guests.", "annotation_id": "671837", "url": "https://genius.com/671837", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "It’s Skull Gang from the chain to the lifestyle You surfboard dudes get wiped out totally", "vault_lines": ["It's Skull Gang from the chain to the lifestyle"], "meaning": "Skull Gang is Juelz’s rap group. He reps the group all the way, from the logo chain he wears to the gangster life he lives.\n\nA Max B diss (He had beef him with during taping the song). Max B is known for being the ‘'silver surfer’‘.", "annotation_id": "195311", "url": "https://genius.com/195311", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "They tryna tag him, spray a brother frame", "vault_lines": ["They tryna tag him, spray a brother frame"], "meaning": "“Triple entendre, don’t even ask me how”\n\n\nPeople are trying to shoot at him (“spray a brother frame”)\nTypically, though, the terms “tagging” and “spraying” are used in the graffiti community\nHe also plays off of Tag body spray, using “tag” and “spray” to carry the line. Using Tag makes ladies fall all over you, like the haters do to Fabolous", "annotation_id": "195293", "url": "https://genius.com/195293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "Tell Bluto I’m a Nuno,", "vault_lines": ["Tell Bluto I'm a Nuno,"], "meaning": "It’s a continuation of the previous Popeye themed line, Bluto is Popeyes antagonist in the cartoons.\n\n\n\nNuno is a bloods reference\n\nNotice how, when you pronounce the name, the first syllable sounds like “blue” which is the color associated with the Crips, who rival the bloods.", "annotation_id": "175181", "url": "https://genius.com/175181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "Leave you sloppy like seconds", "vault_lines": ["Leave you sloppy like seconds"], "meaning": "Leftover food isn’t as good as it was when it was first made, therefore it looks sloppy like seconds. He’s gonna leave you sloppy looking.\n\nSimilarly, it’s a reference to the phrase “sloppy seconds,” meaning having sex with a girl somebody else has already worn out. Again, you’ll look like a mess.", "annotation_id": "175172", "url": "https://genius.com/175172", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "And fly with the tongue, so if you feelin’ froggy, leap (Come on)", "vault_lines": ["And fly with the tongue, so if you feelin' froggy, leap (Come on)"], "meaning": "Frogs catch flies with their tongues\nFrogs are also known for leapin\n\nFabolous spits hot lines, so his tongue is fly. If you want to challenge him, you might as well leap away.", "annotation_id": "39026", "url": "https://genius.com/39026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "There will be nine, damn, I mean, there will be none", "vault_lines": ["There will be nine, damn, I mean, there will be none"], "meaning": "A play on the number 9 vs. the German word for “no” – nein!\n\nWayne hints that he and his goons will carry the 9mm guns killing everybody", "annotation_id": "28304", "url": "https://genius.com/28304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "And I got a four-four and a ’K, like eight stacks", "vault_lines": ["And I got a four-four and a 'K, like eight stacks"], "meaning": "He says “he has a .44 and a ‘K” i.e. a .44 inch caliber handgun and an AK assault rifle.\n\n He’s putting them together. Add 4 and 4 = 8. Add the “K' = 8K = 8000. Since 1 stack is $1000, 8K is \"8 stacks.”", "annotation_id": "28303", "url": "https://genius.com/28303", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "Get you three, four, get you Like the number after one, I’ma get me too", "vault_lines": ["Get you three, four, get you"], "meaning": "Wayne’s likely stating that this verse is on The Carter III, that he’ll “4 get” you, and that he’s going to get himself what he needs. The last section could also be a pun on thousands of things that come in pairs or twos — boobs, grams of the various drugs he loves, drinks, etc.", "annotation_id": "28301", "url": "https://genius.com/28301", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "I be wildin’ like Capital One, what is in your wallet?", "vault_lines": ["I be wildin' like Capital One, what is in your wallet?"], "meaning": "If you don’t pay Wayne the money you owe him, he’ll have to come to you and beat you up for it, referencing this corporate slogan\n\n I actually think he’s saying here that you better keep paying him (aka buying his records) or he’ll revert back to his street ways and start robbing people again, hence “what is in your wallet?!” Also, he’s playing on the Capital One Credit Card slogan. In Capital One’s advertisements, a gang of vikings would wile out on people", "annotation_id": "17306", "url": "https://genius.com/17306", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "Not me, not I, call me Young Popeye", "vault_lines": ["Not me, not I, call me Young Popeye"], "meaning": "Wayne loves Popeye references\n\nAlmost as much as he loves his spinach.\n\n\n\nSimilar to the previous line possibly referencing Hov, this could also be a reference to Big Poppa, meaning he’s the next in line to rap greatness: “ay popi!”", "annotation_id": "17305", "url": "https://genius.com/17305", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "Take that No, better yet, like Diddy, “Take that”", "vault_lines": ["No, better yet, like Diddy, \"Take that\""], "meaning": "Wayne softens his voice here to emulate Diddy\n\n In songs like “It’s all About the Benjamins” Diddy would start out the song saying, “Take that, take that, take that.” Again, wayne is taking what he just said and tell you to take it like a man, and then changes his mind in how he wanted to say it, and re-say the “Take That” to impersonate P.Diddy from his 90’s songs.", "annotation_id": "17304", "url": "https://genius.com/17304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "I let that semi twirl you (Get ’em), now you can follow the drip ’Cause one shot out of the clip’ll Jheri-curl you (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["I let that semi twirl you (Get 'em), now you can follow the drip"], "meaning": "If Juelz shoots you in the head, the blood will soak your hair similar to the popular hairdo of many people during the 1980’s\n\n\n\nThe “follow the drip” line is lifted from 80’s Los Angeles comedian Robin Harris, the joke being that you can’t do crime with a jheri curl because the police could just “follow the drip”", "annotation_id": "17297", "url": "https://genius.com/17297", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "You Ain’t Got Nuthin", "line": "It’s that Street Fam, man, we rep that (Hahahaha)", "vault_lines": ["It's that Street Fam, man, we rep that (Hahahaha)"], "meaning": "Fab’s clique is named the Street Family.\n\nAllegedly, they rob football players for their jewelry", "annotation_id": "15590", "url": "https://genius.com/15590", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
