{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yellow Tape", "line": "Your bitch so thirsty, Murcielago", "vault_lines": ["Your bitch so thirsty, Murcielago"], "meaning": "Referencing Mercy from Kanye West and the G.O.O.D Music crew is about the Lamborghini Murcielago car:\n\nOkay Lamborghini Mercy,\nyour chick, she so thirsty\nI’m in that two-seat Lambo with your girl,\nshe tryna jerk me\n\n\n\nFat Joe’s givin' your bitch the D", "annotation_id": "1179269", "url": "https://genius.com/1179269", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yellow Tape", "line": "Versace jacket, Versace shoes, Versace shades", "vault_lines": ["Versace jacket, Versace shoes, Versace shades"], "meaning": "Fat Joe is dressed in all Versace a very expensive italian fashion brand.", "annotation_id": "1178424", "url": "https://genius.com/1178424", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yellow Tape", "line": "Get that brown bag and I skate off like I’m Tony Hawk", "vault_lines": ["Get that brown bag and I skate off like I'm Tony Hawk"], "meaning": "“Skate” is slang for running away, or moving quickly. Tony Hawk is a professional skateboarder.", "annotation_id": "1178415", "url": "https://genius.com/1178415", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yellow Tape", "line": "Smoke that loud and keep it quiet, let that money talk", "vault_lines": ["Smoke that loud and keep it quiet, let that money talk"], "meaning": "Loud means smoking high grade pot, otherwise known as premium marijuana. Smoking loud is a slang that originates from Atlanta.\n\nAs they say, “money talks”, With his weed being as loud as it is, and him having so much money; he doesn’t see the need to talk very much.", "annotation_id": "1178414", "url": "https://genius.com/1178414", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yellow Tape", "line": "2 Chainz, show your Tity ho, damn right I got it", "vault_lines": ["2 Chainz, show your Tity ho, damn right I got it"], "meaning": "A tribute to the ubiquitous 2 Chainz with a pun on his former nom-de-trap, Tity Boi\n\n“Damn right, I got it” is borrowed from the chorus of one of 2 Chainz/Tity Boi’s most popular songs, Riot", "annotation_id": "1178411", "url": "https://genius.com/1178411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yellow Tape", "line": "Triple beam When I serve the fiends,", "vault_lines": ["When I serve the fiends,"], "meaning": "ACCEPTED COMMENT: Probably a triple beam scale used for cocaine. In the next line he says “when I serve the fiends” (coke addicts) and in other songs he has made references to cocaine.", "annotation_id": "1178402", "url": "https://genius.com/1178402", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
