{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "I aim at your collard green, bitch", "vault_lines": ["I aim at your collard green, bitch"], "meaning": "What Wayne really means is “I aim at your collar,” that is, he’s going for the headshot. However, he changes it to “collard green” to fit with the rhyme scheme, as it rhymes or nearly rhymes with “horror scene,” “Halloween,” “hide and seek,” “Socrates,” “bada-bing,” “solid, clean,” and “honestly.”", "annotation_id": "38461829", "url": "https://genius.com/38461829", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "She don’t even know it’s dry I can’t even open fire", "vault_lines": ["She don't even know her moms"], "meaning": "Continuing from the previous lines, He’s talking about her pussy being so dry that it doesn’t make him cum.\n\nHe can’t even bust or “open fire” from it.", "annotation_id": "21602776", "url": "https://genius.com/21602776", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "Kidnap, hide and seek, bitch", "vault_lines": ["Kidnap, hide and seek, bitch"], "meaning": "Following the previous line’s Halloween reference, he compares kidnapping to playing hide and seek. Playing on the trick or treat Halloween saying. Kidnapping is like a horror/adult version of the hide and seek game children play (ironically with the children of the adults being extorted).", "annotation_id": "13906233", "url": "https://genius.com/13906233", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "Then I tell her how to tell better lies Now her extra guys think she never lie We got a better bond, we have a better time", "vault_lines": ["Then I tell her how to tell better lies"], "meaning": "The woman in question is such a bad liar, Wayne not only picks up on it but recognizes it’s a necessary survival skill for professional rap girlfriends like her… and teaches her how to do it better (Awww) so now her side niggas can’t tell she’s lying allowing the impression of a better “relationship”, the opportunity for her to manipulate them better, and subsequently an even better relationship with Wayne as well …‘cause he gets her (Double Awww) eliminating her necessity to lie to him (tying in with what he says in the hook)", "annotation_id": "13906096", "url": "https://genius.com/13906096", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "You don’t even believe in peace I’m fuckin’ you with both my fingers", "vault_lines": ["She don't even believe in freedom"], "meaning": "Wayne makes a very smart play on meanings. He is referencing the peace sign which is where you hold two fingers up (the middle and your index, to be exact).", "annotation_id": "13519526", "url": "https://genius.com/13519526", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "V-neck polo tees, bitch", "vault_lines": ["V-neck polo tees, bitch"], "meaning": "White-T, neck V, glasses are Versace\n\nDuring the mid-late 2000’s, Weezy was known for rocking simple v-neck white t-shirts a lot of the time.", "annotation_id": "13496060", "url": "https://genius.com/13496060", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "I’m a New Orleans nigga, I make a second line I’m a Megatron", "vault_lines": ["I'm a New Orleans nigga, I make a second line"], "meaning": "Weezy was born and raised in New Orleans, Louisiana. He will forever be faithful to his hometown.\n\nMegatron is a character from the Transformers franchise, he was the feared leader of Decepticon. Megatron will attempt almost anything to achieve his goals.", "annotation_id": "13462259", "url": "https://genius.com/13462259", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "We had sex till nine, ate breakfast tired Fell asleep eye-to-eye, thigh-on-thigh", "vault_lines": ["We had sex till nine, ate breakfast tired"], "meaning": "Weezy plays on “sex” and “nine” here. 69 is a sex position in which two people align themselves so that each person’s mouth is near the other’s genitals, each simultaneously performing oral sex on the other. The participants are mutually inverted like the numerals 6 and 9 in the number 69.\n\n\n\nHe then follows it with another simple yet clever wordplay on “ate”, which sounds like the number 8.", "annotation_id": "13461836", "url": "https://genius.com/13461836", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "I got her legs up like the Omega sign", "vault_lines": ["I got her legs up like the Omega sign"], "meaning": "The Omega symbol is the last and 24th letter in the Greek alphabet.\n\nThis is its sign, which in Weezy’s vision looks like a woman having her legs up and wrapped around his neck:", "annotation_id": "13461705", "url": "https://genius.com/13461705", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "I’ma wake the block, I’ma break the lock Then rape your thot, then shake the spot I’ma shake your hand when I see you out I’ma shake my head when you turn around Cops shake they head when they see your house We shot it up, but look like we burned it down Hor-Horror scene, bitch", "vault_lines": ["I'ma wake the block, I'ma break the lock"], "meaning": "Take a second and imagine these lines actually happening. Wayne is using “imagery,” as a literary technique to describe a “Horror scene.” He has done this before, for example.\n\n\n\nThe cops are shaking their head because they are already too late to save the day.", "annotation_id": "13402760", "url": "https://genius.com/13402760", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "6 shit", "vault_lines": ["Ahh, ah, this that 6 shit"], "meaning": "This has been Wayne’s catchphrase throughout Dedication 6, signifying the 6th installment of his Dedication mixtape series.", "annotation_id": "13388562", "url": "https://genius.com/13388562", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "We don’t even socialize I feel like North Korea", "vault_lines": ["We don't even socialize"], "meaning": "A reference to North Korea’s strict and limited laws regarding internet access. In North Korea, internet access is only permitted with special authorization and primarily used for government purposes and by foreigners.", "annotation_id": "13377605", "url": "https://genius.com/13377605", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "You ain’t gotta lie to me But you might have to lie for me", "vault_lines": ["You ain't gotta lie to me"], "meaning": "Great wordplay here. Wayne says “You ain’t gotta lie to me” which means you don’t have to be pretend to be something your not around him. He wants his girl to be herself and stay true. But also, if she makes this commitment. She may have to “lie for me” meaning she may have to hypothetically, take the stand in a courtroom and lie in order to keep Weezy out of jail.\n\nIn other words he needs a “ride or die.”", "annotation_id": "13377547", "url": "https://genius.com/13377547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "You can’t even keep a secret Why you wear Victoria’s Secret?", "vault_lines": ["You can't even keep a secret"], "meaning": "Victoria’s Secret is the largest American retailer of women’s lingerie.\n\nWeezy plays on Victoria Secret’s name, he asks his girl how can she keep a Victoria secret when she cannot even keep a secret of her own.\n\n\n\nTune himself is familiar with Victoria Secret too:\n\nI have written down Victoria’s Secret\nDon’t tell nobody, don’t share your body with nobody", "annotation_id": "13366776", "url": "https://genius.com/13366776", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "Stickin’ to a nigga like Siamese And you just on the side of me", "vault_lines": ["Stickin' to a nigga like Siamese"], "meaning": "Siamese twins; are twins that are conjoined together. It is an extremely rare illness and Wayne uses this to reference how people “Copy his style; but are still on the side of him.”", "annotation_id": "13361741", "url": "https://genius.com/13361741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "And you don’t even like Adidas Why you wearin’ Yeezy sneakers?", "vault_lines": ["Why you wearin' Yeezy sneakers?"], "meaning": "Adidas Yeezy (or Yeezus, as stated here) is the official collaboration sneaker by Kanye West and Adidas. Released on February 14, 2015.", "annotation_id": "13357411", "url": "https://genius.com/13357411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "I’m a legend like Socrates, bitch", "vault_lines": ["I'm a legend like Socrates, bitch"], "meaning": "Though Wayne could be referring to the Greek philosopher famous for his pedagogic questioning style and teacher of Plato, he is probably referring to Sócrates, the famous Brasilian soccer player who nicknamed the “Brasilian Legend.”", "annotation_id": "13355503", "url": "https://genius.com/13355503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "And you don’t even believe in Yeezus Why you wearin’ Yeezy sneakers?", "vault_lines": ["She don't even believe in freedom"], "meaning": "Yeezus is the name of Kanye West’s 6th studio album and one of his many nicknames. In the past few years, many people have expressed their resentment towards Kanye’s vision, such as doubting him for being in a relationship with Kim Kardashian.\n\nAnd all the relationships, the somewhat friends that I had somewhat built up, completely turned their backs on her and me. They already had their back to her, and now they turned it to me.\n\nHowever, at the end of the day these same doubters still wait in lines and pay resell value for his sneakers, which have been selling for extraordinary prices.\n\nThese lines also flip Kodak Black’s bars on the original version of “Roll In Peace”:\n\nHe don’t even believe in Jesus\nWhy you got a Jesus piece?", "annotation_id": "13355444", "url": "https://genius.com/13355444", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeezy Sneakers", "line": "To be continued D6!", "vault_lines": ["This just part one!"], "meaning": "It’s rumored the second part of D6 will be dropped on New Years. This would make sense as Drake has claimed to have a feature on D6 that hasn’t been released.", "annotation_id": "13355419", "url": "https://genius.com/13355419", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
