{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeahhh", "line": "High notes like mariah", "vault_lines": ["But my pockets do hit high notes like mariah"], "meaning": "Those notes in Weezy’s pockets would have to be very high denominations if they’re to compare to the upper end of Mariah Carey’s famous vocal range. (There’s some debate about just what is the highest note that Mimi has ever hit live or on record, but some put it at a G#7.)\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_0TUphfi5zs", "annotation_id": "14261148", "url": "https://genius.com/14261148", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeahhh", "line": "Used to be a hot boy now I’m fire boy", "vault_lines": ["Used to be a hot boy now I'm fire boy"], "meaning": "As a young teen, Wayne began his rap career and had his first big success as a member of Cash Money’s Hot Boys.\n\nHowever, after the group dissolved and the other members left the label, he grew in massive strides as an artist-not only eventually living up to his claim of “Best Rapper Alive”, but also carrying the entire struggling Cash Money label on his back in the process.\n\nAfter hearing later releases such as “Da Drought 3” and “Tha Carter III”, it’s hard not to argue that Wayne went from hot to FIRE.", "annotation_id": "9180470", "url": "https://genius.com/9180470", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
