{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeah", "line": "No homo, they suck like Tony Romo", "vault_lines": ["No homo, they suck like Tony Romo"], "meaning": "In the 2006-2007 season, the cowboys had an opportunity to win a playoff game. All they needed to hit was a 20 yard field goal, but Tony Romo fumbled the snap, and they never got the opportunity. This is one of many occasions of Tony Romo not being as good as everyone says he is. (Lil Wayne is not one of those people)\n\nLil Wayne is saying that all these other rappers except for him and T.I. suck like Tony Romo.", "annotation_id": "198481", "url": "https://genius.com/198481", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeah", "line": "I keep the block jumpin’, just call me bunny man", "vault_lines": ["I keep the block jumpin', just call me bunny man"], "meaning": "The Bunny Man is an urban legend that probably originated from two incidents in Fairfax County, Virginia in 1970, but has been spread throughout the Washington D.C. area. There are many variations to the legend, but most involve a man wearing a rabbit costume (“bunny suit”) who attacks people with an axe. Many variations occur around “Bunny Man Bridge”, the concrete tunnel of a Southern Railway overpass on Colchester Road in Clifton.\n\n\n\nLil Wayne is saying that he keeps the block(hood) on lock.\n\nHe is also referring to bunny’s as they jump/hop to get around.", "annotation_id": "198474", "url": "https://genius.com/198474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Yeah", "line": "In the SLR, all the doors open thata way", "vault_lines": ["In the SLR, all the doors open thata way"], "meaning": "The Reference to SLR, is a reference to the car, Mercedes SLR.\n\n\n\nWhen T.I. says “all the doors open thata way” he is referring to the doors opening up into the air. If you look at the doors in the picture above you will see what he is talking about", "annotation_id": "198471", "url": "https://genius.com/198471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
