{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ya Dig", "line": "Colder than a polar bear’s toenail", "vault_lines": ["Colder than a polar bear's toenail"], "meaning": "Reference to ATLiens lyric by outkast, remember, wayne is not a human being.", "annotation_id": "28811913", "url": "https://genius.com/28811913", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ya Dig", "line": "[Verse 2]", "vault_lines": ["Can we talk about it now?"], "meaning": "As some of you might know, Weezy co-signed Kendrick Lamar in 2009 on the ‘C4’ tape. On the mixtape, Wayne came with a new verse on ‘Mr. Carter’. This verse is similar to the second verse on ‘Ya Dig’, but re-recorded.", "annotation_id": "24405377", "url": "https://genius.com/24405377", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ya Dig", "line": "Pour it up for Pimp C Pour it up for Screw and Moe, pour it up for Bun B Pour it up for young me, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Syrup pink, that ice pink, pour it up for Pimp C"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has always been one to shout out the OGs, here he namedrops Pimp C, DJ Screw, Big Moe, and Bun B, all legends of the south who were known for their consumption of codeine.\n\nThese lines are reminiscent of his classic song Me and My Drank:\n\nI sip that Big Moe, I drink that Pimp C\nRest in peace Big Moe, rest in peace Pimp C\nI sip that Big Moe, I drink that Pimp C\nRest in peace Big Moe, rest in peace Pimp C\nAnd fuck what they say\nMr. DJ Screw, I'ma do this for you\n\nHe also uses similar lines on his infamous freestyle on Tim Westwood TV https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xsyEjQ8a8XI&t=32s", "annotation_id": "24132620", "url": "https://genius.com/24132620", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ya Dig", "line": "And I’m kicking like a horse on the stick-shift Ferrari", "vault_lines": ["And I’m kicking like a horse on the stick-shift Ferrari"], "meaning": "To highlight his ability to rap, Wayne compares himself to the horse on the Ferrari logo, especially Ferraris with a manual transition whose engines are even more hardcore. He may also be referring to the horsepower of those cars.", "annotation_id": "24132599", "url": "https://genius.com/24132599", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ya Dig", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-ya-dig-lyrics", "genius_title": "Ya Dig", "genius_id": 7244541, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "[Verse 2: Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": ["D.A. got that dope"], "meaning": "For the first half of Wayne’s verse he mimmics the flow and wording of Kanye’s verse on I Love It with Lil Pump. Kanye’s opening line being:\n\nI’m a sick fuck, I like a quick fuck\n\nand Wayne’s:\n\nI’m a nasty fuck, I like a plastic slut", "annotation_id": "31920185", "url": "https://genius.com/31920185", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "I do like Nipsey and I give that hoe a slap (Ahh)", "vault_lines": ["I do like Nipsey and I give that hoe a slap (Ahh)"], "meaning": "After the June 2018 BET Awards, late rapper Nipsey Hussle got into a fight in a parking lot after a heated discussion about whether he could drive into an area blocked off by cones. See a video of the fight and how Hussle infamously slapped a man below:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_hV8NfDNDmg", "annotation_id": "20384698", "url": "https://genius.com/20384698", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "D.A. got that dope", "vault_lines": ["D.A. got that dope"], "meaning": "“D.A. got that dope” is the producer tag of D.A. Doman. The tag was most famously used on the 2018 hit track “ZEZE” by Kodak Black.\n\nDoman is also well known for producing the 2018 smash hit “Taste” by Tyga and the 2017 hit “Privacy” by Chris Brown.", "annotation_id": "18035335", "url": "https://genius.com/18035335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "Some say the ex make the sex best", "vault_lines": ["Some say the ex make the sex best"], "meaning": "He is referring to the biggie smalls song called “Fucking you tonight” Biggie said “Some say the X, make the sex spec-tacular”", "annotation_id": "16177632", "url": "https://genius.com/16177632", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "Word to 50, tell them bitches, “Get the strap” (Okay)", "vault_lines": ["Word to 50, tell them bitches, \"Get the strap\" (Okay)"], "meaning": "Kid Ink shoutouts 50 Cent, whose recent catchphrase has been to “get the strap”. He has even worn a t shirt with the saying written on it.\n\nHe could also be referencing Uncle Murda’s song Get The Strap, which 50 Cent featured on. On the chorus, 50 raps:\n\n(Grrr-rah) Yeah, yeah, go get the strap\n(Grrr-rah) Yeah, yeah, go get the strap\n(Grrr-rah) Yeah, yeah, go get the strap\n(Rrr) Go get the strap (rrr) nigga, go get the strap", "annotation_id": "16260352", "url": "https://genius.com/16260352", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "Venus fly trap when I make that ass clap (Yeah) If you give me good dick, you ain’t getting that back (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Venus fly trap when I make that ass clap (Yeah)"], "meaning": "The Venus flytrap is a carnivorous plant native to subtropical wetlands on the East Coast of the United States in North Carolina and South Carolina.\n\nIt catches its prey chiefly insects and arachnids with a trapping structure formed by the terminal portion of each of the plant’s leaves, which is triggered by tiny hairs on their inner surfaces.\n\nWhen an insect or spider crawling along the leaves contacts a hair, the trap prepares to close, snapping shut only if another contact occurs within approximately twenty seconds of the first strike. Triggers may occur if one-tenth of the insect is within contact. Then the plant will only begin digestion after five more stimuli to ensure it has caught a live bug worthy of consumption.\n\n\n\nSaweetie compares the venus flytrap to her ass clapping and compares the insect to her mans dick, when the D goes in ain’t coming back.\n\n\n\nsources say the D could possibly be Quavo’s", "annotation_id": "16260297", "url": "https://genius.com/16260297", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "Pull the microphone back, Jill Scott with the sack (Yass)", "vault_lines": ["Pull the microphone back, Jill Scott with the sack (Yass)"], "meaning": "Jill Scott is a Philly singer, her 2000 debut, Who Is Jill Scott? Words and Sounds Vol. 1, went platinum, and the follow-ups Beautifully Human: Words, Sounds Vol. 2 and The Real Thing: Words and Sounds Vol. 3 both achieved gold status.\n\n\n\nSaweetie compares pulling the microphone back possibly for a final note to oral sex.", "annotation_id": "16260257", "url": "https://genius.com/16260257", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "I got 69 problems and cumming is not one (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I got 69 problems and cumming is not one (Yeah)"], "meaning": "reference to lil wayne’s line previously about the 69 position.\nalso a reference the chorus famous song by jay z where on the chorus he raps:\n\n99 problems, but a bitch ain’t one\nIf you’re havin' girl problems, I feel bad for you, son\nI got 99 problems, but a bitch ain’t one – hit me!\n\n\n\nbut rather than than having no girl problems (or almost 100 problems) she nearly has 70 and she has no cumming ones.", "annotation_id": "16260167", "url": "https://genius.com/16260167", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "She started from a side bitch to a bottom bitch", "vault_lines": ["She started from a side bitch to a bottom bitch"], "meaning": "Wayne references long time friend and labelmate Drake’s hit song, “Started from the bottom”.\n\nDrake has also used this term as a metaphor for sex on “No New Friends”. In his verse, he raps:\n\nThat’s what yo' ass really call started from the bottom", "annotation_id": "16260099", "url": "https://genius.com/16260099", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "We can 69, or we can 96", "vault_lines": ["We can 69, or we can 96"], "meaning": "Continuing the sexuality in the song, 69 is a sex position, where a man lays on his back and receives oral sex from a woman, while also performing oral sex on her.\n96 is possibly the opposite of 69 where a women on her back receives oral sex from the man while performing oral sex on him.\n\nWeezy lets the girl choose to go either give him head or give her head.\n\nfellow lablemate Nicki Minaj (whom wayne mentored) has collaborated with the rapper Tekashi 6ix9ine on the song FEFE where she even referenced the position herself.\n\nHe-he tryna 69 like Tekashi, call him papi", "annotation_id": "16259821", "url": "https://genius.com/16259821", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YUSO", "line": "Tell her say my name, she say, “You got too many”", "vault_lines": ["Tell her say my name, she say, \"You got too many\""], "meaning": "Lil Wayne’s government name is Dwayne Michael Carter, Jr, however he is known to have many nicknames.\n\nThese nicknames include Weezy, Lil Weezy Ana, Lil Tunechi, Weezy F. Baby, and Young Mulah, among others.\n\nLil Wayne encourages his girl to say his name during sex but the girl is unsure of which name to call him due to the multiple nicknames he goes by.", "annotation_id": "16241175", "url": "https://genius.com/16241175", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
