{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YM Salute", "line": "I told my team I got us man, it’s all on me Like Volume two B.G., I got my crew with me", "vault_lines": ["I told my team I got us man, it's all on me"], "meaning": "He gets the title wrong slightly as this is a reference to former Cash Money Records artist B.G.’s album It’s All On U Volume 2.", "annotation_id": "41274488", "url": "https://genius.com/41274488", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YM Salute", "line": "I d-d-do it ’cause I did it for my ballerina girls", "vault_lines": ["I d-d-do it 'cause I did it for my ballerina girls"], "meaning": "This is not the first time Nicki has claimed to be a pioneer (and not the first time of her referring to ballerinas) in Hip-Hop music in her songs/features.\n\nBallerina’s are just one aspects of girls who have dreams of going into a competitive field full of dedication in hard work, much like the rap game.\n\n\n\nFunny how Sophia Grace and Rosie dress up like ballerina’s.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f9573kGBtuE\n\nHowever, that’s just a coincidence since this song came out way before Super Bass was even spoken of.", "annotation_id": "2430708", "url": "https://genius.com/2430708", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YM Salute", "line": "First place, never last Always on top and I’m a chief like a Seminole", "vault_lines": ["First place, never last"], "meaning": "The Seminole people are a Native American tribe originally from Florida but now live in Oklahoma. He compares himself to a “chief” or a holy man, which is not appropriate.\n\nEducate yourselves.", "annotation_id": "561799", "url": "https://genius.com/561799", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YM Salute", "line": "No Witten, Cowboys to a Piston A.I., no Wallace, your kids gettin’ demolished", "vault_lines": ["No Witten, Cowboys to a Piston"], "meaning": "A.I refers to Allen Iverson and Wallace refers to Rasheed Wallace who left the Detroit Pistons in 2008.\n\nor\n\nDr. Richard S. Wallace is the chairman of the board and co-founder of the A.L.I.C.E. Artificial Intelligence (A.I.) Foundation.\n\nI’m thinking it’s the prior, however.", "annotation_id": "177293", "url": "https://genius.com/177293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "YM Salute", "line": "’Cause Young Money is the Navy better yet the Army", "vault_lines": ["'Cause Young Money is the Navy better yet the Army"], "meaning": "Jay-Z said on the Takeover “RocAFella is the Army, better yet the Navy”. Nicki Minaj must certainly have been alluding to that famous line.\n\nIronically, Jay took that line from B.G.’s song “Cash Money is an Army”, which was a Cash Money song obviously, now it’s Young Money’s.\n\nEverything always seems to come full circle!", "annotation_id": "97661", "url": "https://genius.com/97661", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
