{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Y.U. Mad", "line": "I am the female Weezy,", "vault_lines": ["I am the female Weezy,"], "meaning": "Female Weezy serves as one of Nicki Minaj’s many alter egos, the most well known being Harajuku Barbie and Roman Zolanski. This line is directly sampled at the end of Nicki’s song Stupid Hoe from her 2012 album Pink Friday: Roman Reloded.", "annotation_id": "23548362", "url": "https://genius.com/23548362", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Y.U. Mad", "line": "Damn, Billboard, haha I mean, I’m winning but I’m still bored", "vault_lines": ["I mean, I'm winning but I'm still bored"], "meaning": "At the time of the song’s release, Nicki Minaj had 6 singles as lead artist that reached the top 40 on the Billboard Hot 100, with 3 hitting the top 20, and one hitting #3. (“Super Bass”)\n\nIn addition to such, she also had 7 singles crack the top 40 as a featured artist, 4 hitting the top 20 and the highest being #6, which was her feature on “Bottoms Up” by Trey Songz.\n\nMinaj is stating that despite her string of chart success at the time, she wasn’t satisfied and wanted to continue showing why she deserves more.", "annotation_id": "20986983", "url": "https://genius.com/20986983", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
