{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Y.U. Mad", "line": "C4", "vault_lines": ["I told Stunna I said you know they on that regular degular"], "meaning": "Birdman shouts out Lil Wayne’s recent album at the time, Tha Carter IV.\nhttps://genius.com/albums/Lil-wayne/Tha-carter-iv", "annotation_id": "20426715", "url": "https://genius.com/20426715", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Y.U. Mad", "line": "Shining AK blood, just like a trophy", "vault_lines": ["Shining AK blood, just like a trophy"], "meaning": "Birdman is, in a tradition of gangsta rap that dates back to N.W.A, hauling around the ever famous AK-47. The use of the “shining” adjective, however, could also be to denote Birdman’s particular amount of wealth (after all he is on the Forbes list).\n\nInteresting side note, an interest in having a shiny AK may be shared by Wu-Tang Clan member Raekwon.", "annotation_id": "3240450", "url": "https://genius.com/3240450", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Y.U. Mad", "line": "[Chorus: Nicki Minaj] That’s why you mad, that’s why you, why you mad mad That’s why you mad, that’s why you, why you mad mad That’s why you mad, that’s why you, why you mad mad That’s why you mad, that’s why you, why you mad mad", "vault_lines": ["That's why you mad, that's why you, why you mad mad"], "meaning": "In an MTV interview with Lil' Wayne, he says he doesn’t think anyone is actually mad and it’s just a figure of speech, Nicki sounds cooler saying “mad,” instead of “glad” in that point of the song.", "annotation_id": "406851", "url": "https://genius.com/406851", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Y.U. Mad", "line": "Triple OG, nigga, these hoes know me", "vault_lines": ["Triple OG, nigga, these hoes know me"], "meaning": "Birdman is stating he has been gang banging for 30 years or longer according to the Piru street gang ranking method.\n\n• L.Y.G. (Little Young Gangster) – members aged 13-17\n\n• Y.G. (Young Gangster) – after 0-4 active years of “banging” after the age of 18\n\n• O.Y.G. (Original Young Gangster) – after 5 active years of banging after the age of 18\n\n• O.G. (Original Gangster) – after 10 active years of banging no matter what age(Many people mistake O.G. as an older member, but someone can jump straight from L.Y.G. and become an O.G. at the age of 18 if they have been in the gang since they were 8.\n\n• O.O.G. (Double O.G.) – after 20 active years of banging\n\n• O.O.O.G. (Triple O.G.) – after 30 active years of banging\n\nA triple OG spoke more on the matter of rappers claiming Piru affiliation:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gt4Jw60ZkZY", "annotation_id": "357165", "url": "https://genius.com/357165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Y.U. Mad", "line": "Been had it on lock, gave the key to Nick’", "vault_lines": ["Been had it on lock, gave the key to Nick’"], "meaning": "Lil wayne’s has been running the rap game since 2006 and even longer for his true fans. With Nicki’s recent award at the VMAs for rap song of the year with super bass, he is passing the key to her. Lil wayne showing a rare moment of modesty.\n\n\n\nACCEPTED COMMENT: I think the last line refers to Weezy’s dick. ‘been had it on lock’ meaning he hasnt had sex for quite a while, gave the key to Nick refers to Nicki Minaj.", "annotation_id": "357160", "url": "https://genius.com/357160", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Y.U. Mad", "line": "That P on my hat is for Piru, not Pirates", "vault_lines": ["That P on my hat is for Piru, not Pirates"], "meaning": "Lil wayne commonly wears different sport teaming’s hats including the Pittsburgh Pirates. In his mind, the “P” stands for Piru, which is Compton bloods street gang.", "annotation_id": "357151", "url": "https://genius.com/357151", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Y.U. Mad", "line": "Swisha full of violet", "vault_lines": ["I got the world in my wallet, swisha full of violet"], "meaning": "He is probably referring to the purple kush in his blunt.\n\n\n\nIt is also possible that he is saying his blunt is dipped in promethazine, which is sometimes referred to as purple because it comes in purple cough syrup.", "annotation_id": "357149", "url": "https://genius.com/357149", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Y.U. Mad", "status": "done", "targets": 15, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Birdman-yu-mad-lyrics", "genius_title": "Y.U. Mad", "genius_id": 55482, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Playin’ the cards I was dealt, and that shit almost broke a nigga But I could be broker, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Playin' the cards I was dealt, and that shit almost broke a nigga"], "meaning": "Wayne played the cards he was dealt by staying with Birdman while the rest of the hot boys left.\nIn the end he found out Birdman was holding money from him and it broke him emotionally to be betrayed by his father figure.\nThis said he still has a lot of money and could be broker so he will perservere.", "annotation_id": "27116548", "url": "https://genius.com/27116548", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Cool as fuck, keepin’ my cool before my composure, nigga That’s poker, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Cool as fuck, keepin' my cool before my composure, nigga"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is commenting on his impeccable “poker face” or ability to keep his emotions in check rather than let it play out on his face. Even during interactions with police or authority he’s able to keep a poker face, giving nothing away.", "annotation_id": "22010641", "url": "https://genius.com/22010641", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "He ain’t the plug unless he foreign, nigga", "vault_lines": ["He ain't the plug unless he foreign, nigga"], "meaning": "This line alludes to the idea that the best drugs are from across seas (e.g. Colombia, cuba) and thats where his plugs would be from", "annotation_id": "21083014", "url": "https://genius.com/21083014", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Had to move the trap house to Florida, nigga Had to move The Carter by the water, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Had to move the trap house to Florida, nigga"], "meaning": "From living in New Orleans Lil Wayne then moved to Miami Living by the water", "annotation_id": "21082786", "url": "https://genius.com/21082786", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "From a D-O-G to the G-O-D", "vault_lines": ["From a D-O-G to the G-O-D"], "meaning": "This is clever wordplay on the word dog, which spelled backwards is god.\n\nLil wayne come from the slums of New Orleans and has been an street rapper for a while. Eventually Lil Wayne has been on top of the rap game and has rightfully so self proclaimed himself as the “Best/Greatest rapper alive”", "annotation_id": "21082751", "url": "https://genius.com/21082751", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "It’s Young Mula to the grave, bitch", "vault_lines": ["It's Young Mula to the grave, bitch"], "meaning": "Mula is an american alternative for money which originated in early 20th century. So when Lil Wayne says “Young mula” , it means he is shouting out to the label he himself founded “Young Money” with the likes of famous artists like Drake , Nicki Minaj , Gudda Gudda , Shanelle , Mack Maine(also the manager) among the others.", "annotation_id": "19947183", "url": "https://genius.com/19947183", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "I told my bitch if she cheat then she making a poor decision", "vault_lines": ["I told my bitch if she cheat then she making a poor decision"], "meaning": "Wayne uses a double entendre here with the word ‘poor’:\n\n\n“A poor decision” means ‘a bad decision’. So, if she leaves Wayne, she’s not making a wise choice.\n“Poor” also means ‘having little money’ so she will be also “poor” if she leaves him, compared to how rich she would be if she stayed with Wayne.", "annotation_id": "17901472", "url": "https://genius.com/17901472", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "We just landed in a spaceship", "vault_lines": ["We just landed in a spaceship"], "meaning": "Wayne claims to be an alien, from another planet.", "annotation_id": "16363544", "url": "https://genius.com/16363544", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "But I’m on the road to riches, and she can’t ignore the engine", "vault_lines": ["But I'm on the road to riches, and she can't ignore the engine"], "meaning": "The woman he’s talking about can’t ignore the sound of the engine of the car that Wayne is metaphorically driving (on the road to riches, as in he’s getting richer).", "annotation_id": "15699273", "url": "https://genius.com/15699273", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
