{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Time to run", "vault_lines": ["Guilty conscience pimpin', make my ho sit through the whole trial"], "meaning": "*tampering with no rubber. Wayne is emphasizing as well as acknowledging the risk factors associated with having unprotected sex. Hence the words “tampering”, “gambling”, & “Chancin' it like the rapper”", "annotation_id": "13932779", "url": "https://genius.com/13932779", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Stayin’ on my feet, no tappin’ on my toes, like Moses, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Stayin' on my feet, no tappin' on my toes, like Moses, nigga"], "meaning": "This line refers to Exodus 4:25 from the Bible. In order to save Moses' life, his' wife, Zipporah, circumcises her son and touches Moses' feet with the foreskin.\n\nWayne is saying in this line that he’s able to support himself and that he doesn’t need a savior or anyone to help him.", "annotation_id": "13837214", "url": "https://genius.com/13837214", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "You could D-I-E for a F-E-E", "vault_lines": ["You could D-I-E for a F-E-E"], "meaning": "This could have two meanings, either Wayne will pay his shooters a fee to kill you, or you could die over unpaid money, both being fees.", "annotation_id": "13696929", "url": "https://genius.com/13696929", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Got OCD and not your CD", "vault_lines": ["Got OCD and not your CD"], "meaning": "OCD is obsessive-compulsive disorder, something that Wayne clearly has, as evident in the perfection in all of his verses.\n\nHowever, while he does have this mental disorder, he certainly doesn’t have your trash music.", "annotation_id": "13696922", "url": "https://genius.com/13696922", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "I’ll D-I-E for my S-E-T", "vault_lines": ["I'll D-I-E for my S-E-T"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying he will Die(D-I-E) for his Set(S-E-T), His set is the gang/affiliation he is a part of! In the ABC News Interview,  Wayne tell the interviewer that he is a gang banger, much like he has in his music throughout his whole career.", "annotation_id": "13416709", "url": "https://genius.com/13416709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "My killers killin’ on purpose by accident", "vault_lines": ["My killers killin' on purpose by accident"], "meaning": "Nice juxtaposition of the contradicting pair on purpose and by accident, therefore futher emphasize his killer’s professionalism, they carry out their murder by faking it as an accident.", "annotation_id": "13367428", "url": "https://genius.com/13367428", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Two Ninas on me, you fuck with me, them girls goin’ wild", "vault_lines": ["Two Ninas on me, you fuck with me, them girls goin' wild"], "meaning": "Nina, or Nina Ross, is a 9mm handgun. Weezy has 2 of those on him, and he will not hesitate to use them on you if you mess with him.\n\nHe has described a little bit of his Nina before too:\n\nI got a bitch named Nina, and Nina’s so slutty Cause she’ll do him and everyone of his buddies\n\nhttps://pbs.twimg.com/media/B5okH8KIUAAhuOf.jpg:large", "annotation_id": "13366916", "url": "https://genius.com/13366916", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "It ain’t a car unless it’s foreign, nigga And a R plus another R, my nigga But I used to want a Ford Explorer, nigga", "vault_lines": ["It ain't a car unless it's foreign, nigga"], "meaning": "Out of the many cars Wayne has, the Rolls Royce could be his favorite. He has a song with 2 Chainz about it called “Rolls Royce Weather Everyday”, and he even mentioned it on his “Back 2 Back” remix:\n\nI keep the double-R, me and Steve Kerr\n\nThe Ford Explorer is also a brand new car. With the money Weezy has, he could buy any car he wants.", "annotation_id": "13365278", "url": "https://genius.com/13365278", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "I’m still finessin’, and I’m still progressin’", "vault_lines": ["I'm still finessin', and I'm still progressin'"], "meaning": "Baby E refers to his 2015 hit “Finessin'”, which is his most popular song to date. It appeared on his project Kill The Noise. Weezy even remixed it on his No Ceilings 2 mixtape.\n\nBaby E is still finessing and he is not stopping anytime soon!", "annotation_id": "13365237", "url": "https://genius.com/13365237", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Yeah, uh-huh, said, yeah This that Baby E and Wayne shit", "vault_lines": ["This that Baby E and Wayne shit"], "meaning": "Baby E is a Young Money Entertainment artist, who was officially signed with them in 2015. In the past 2 years, him and Weezy have collaborated twice, when they remixed “Finessin'” which appeared on Wayne’s 2015 mixtape No Ceilings 2 and on “Bando”.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xiTOUpzRpss", "annotation_id": "13365215", "url": "https://genius.com/13365215", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "I don’t know, guess I was bored, my nigga", "vault_lines": ["I don't know, guess I was bored, my nigga"], "meaning": "Referring to the last line, Weezy has so much money that he does not even know what to do with it anymore. He buys things that cost hundreds of thousands of dollars out of boredom now, just like he bought himself that medallion that costs as much as a Bentley Azure, which is around $347,645.", "annotation_id": "13365181", "url": "https://genius.com/13365181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "[Outro: Baby E] I don’t really care if you cry On the real, you should’ve never lied Should’ve saw the way she looked me in my eyes She said “I am not afraid to die” Push me to the edge All my friends are dead Push me to the edge All my friends are dead Push me to the edge All my friends are dead Push me to the edge", "vault_lines": ["I don't really care if you cry"], "meaning": "This song is a remix of Lil Uzi Vert’s #1 charting hit “XO TOUR Llif3”, and for the outro, Baby E interpolates the chorus word for word.", "annotation_id": "13364241", "url": "https://genius.com/13364241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "At the T-O-P smokin’ P-O-T", "vault_lines": ["At the T-O-P smokin' P-O-T"], "meaning": "This is clever wordplay on the word top, which spelled backwards is pot, a slang term for marijuana.\n\nLil Wayne has been on top of the rap game consistently for nearly a decade now, ever since his 2008 album Tha Carter III sold 1 million copies in it’s first week and was certified platinum. He is also the 9th best selling artist in hip-hop history.\n\nMarijuana has not only been a huge part of Wayne’s subject matter in his music, but his life. In his controversial ABC Nightline interview where he spoke out against the Black Lives Matter movement, he deemed weed as the 5th most important part of his life, just behind God, his family, his kids, and music.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/L6mBZSQdGCE?t=178", "annotation_id": "13364195", "url": "https://genius.com/13364195", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "I’m a young mogul, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm a young mogul, nigga"], "meaning": "A mogul is defined as an important or powerful person, and Lil Wayne definitely fits that criteria. He has changed hip-hop in a number of ways, but he’s also discovered two of the biggest rap artists of this age such as Drake and Nicki Minaj through his legendary Young Money label.\n\nHis power isn’t limited to his influence on music, though. Lil Wayne has also become a #1 best-selling author with 2010’s infamous Gone Til' November: A Journal of Rikers Island, which he wrote while serving time in prison for a gun charge. He’s also made history, becoming one of the only artists in music history who have had an album certified as platinum within one week with Tha Carter III.", "annotation_id": "13364170", "url": "https://genius.com/13364170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "To the Moon like Warren, nigga", "vault_lines": ["To the Moon like Warren, nigga"], "meaning": "This is a play on words referencing the Hall of Fame Quarterback Warren Moon.\n\n\n\nWarren Moon played for the Washington Huskies in college, went un-drafted and played in the Canadian football league, where he would be picked up by the Houston Oilers and would go on to play in 9 Pro Bowls and make make 7 playoff appearances.", "annotation_id": "13362227", "url": "https://genius.com/13362227", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "My office is oval, nigga", "vault_lines": ["My office is oval, nigga"], "meaning": "Lil wayne refers to himself many times as President Carter, and this is true to a sense that he is the President of Young Money. “The Oval Office” is located inside of The White House.", "annotation_id": "13361819", "url": "https://genius.com/13361819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Ain’t where or why you trap, it’s who you trappin’ with", "vault_lines": ["Ain't where or why you trap, it's who you trappin' with"], "meaning": "Wayne shares a popular business proverb in his own words so his demographic can grasp the importance of this success principle:\n\nIt’s not what you know but who you know.", "annotation_id": "13361279", "url": "https://genius.com/13361279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "I’m a young Hova, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm a young Hova, nigga"], "meaning": "Hova, short for J-Hova, is a play on the word Jehovah, the Hebrew word for God. Jay-Z has called himself the “god” of rap. In his “A Million and One Questions (Remix)” he raps:\n\nThey call me J-Hova cause the flow is religious\n\nLil Wayne is a part owner of Jay Z’s music streaming subscription Tidal. He’s also rumored to be joining Jay Z’s Roc Nation when his deal with Cash Money expires after the release of Carter 5. For this reason, it’s speculated that Birdman doesn’t want to put the album out, so he can keep Wayne under contract.\n\nWhen Jay Z retired in 2003 after releasing The Black Album, Wayne carried the rap torch:\n\nBest rapper alive, since the best rapper retired\n\nJay Z (Shawn Carter) and Lil Wayne (Dwayne Carter) share a last name. Jay acknowledges Wayne as a younger version of him on Tha Carter III song “Mr. Carter”\n\nYoung Carter, go farther, go further, go harder", "annotation_id": "13361236", "url": "https://genius.com/13361236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "I bought myself a medallion that cost an Azure, my nigga", "vault_lines": ["I bought myself a medallion that cost an Azure, my nigga"], "meaning": "The cost of Wayne’s chain, is around the same price of a Bentley Azure (which retailed at around $330,000).", "annotation_id": "13357004", "url": "https://genius.com/13357004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "I told my son that “Whatever the sun touch is yours, little nigga”", "vault_lines": ["I told my son that \"Whatever the sun touch is yours, little nigga\""], "meaning": "In The Lion King, Mufasa tells his son that whatever the sun touches is his kingdom.", "annotation_id": "13356021", "url": "https://genius.com/13356021", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "A tree without a bird ‘cause I deserve every fuckin’ leaf", "vault_lines": ["A tree without a bird 'cause I deserve every fuckin' leaf"], "meaning": "This is a subliminal diss to Birdman. Due to record label issues with his Bridman, Wayne has been unable to obtain payment for his long-awaited Carter 5 album.\n\nWayne thinks he deserves to profit more off of his own music.", "annotation_id": "13355970", "url": "https://genius.com/13355970", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
