{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Hit her with the D-O-P-E D That’s Dope Dick Tunechi, DDT", "vault_lines": ["Hit her with the D-O-P-E D"], "meaning": "In modern slang, “D” refers to the male’s genitals.\n\nIn wrestling, the DDT is a move in which one wrestler has their opponent in a front facelock or inverted headlock and falls down or backwards, driving their opponent’s face into the mat.\n\n\n\n\n\nDDT is now short for “dope dick Tunechi”.", "annotation_id": "13355565", "url": "https://genius.com/13355565", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Niggas don’t know a star from an asterisk", "vault_lines": ["Niggas don't know a star from an asterisk"], "meaning": "In Back on my Grizzy Wayne says\n\nI’m a crazy ass star like a fucking asterisk\n\nHere, he’s saying that critics can’t tell the difference between a star like him and an asterisk which looks like a star but is very different.", "annotation_id": "13355349", "url": "https://genius.com/13355349", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Smokin’ so much weed, I might just fuck around and hug a tree", "vault_lines": ["Smokin' so much weed, I might just fuck around and hug a tree"], "meaning": "Smoking weed can create a feeling of euphoria. A stereotypical “hippie” may be so happy they indeed “hug a tree” because they love everything around them.", "annotation_id": "13355282", "url": "https://genius.com/13355282", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Few bumps in the road, a little bump and grind I don’t mind Please know, for your fuckin’ piggy bank you could get hog tied", "vault_lines": ["You could D-I-E for a F-E-E"], "meaning": "Referencing the classic R. Kelly song “Bump n' Grind”, Wayne interpolates the lyric\n\nI don’t see nothing wrong with a little bump and grind\n\nto play off the expression “bumps in the road” which represents life’s obstacles.", "annotation_id": "13355268", "url": "https://genius.com/13355268", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Heaven’s gates was closed, I went to Hell, there was a long line Two hoes in the bed, it’s hard to wake up on the wrong side", "vault_lines": ["Heaven's gates was closed, I went to Hell, there was a long line"], "meaning": "Wayne continues his biblical metaphors implying that he died and went to Heaven and Hell and still couldn’t find tranquility.\nHowever, he doesn’t get discouraged because he surrounds himself with people who can give him pleasure through hard times. As the GOAT himself said “When life sucks, just enjoy the head”", "annotation_id": "13355265", "url": "https://genius.com/13355265", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Hard times R.I.P., baby, my phone died, but don’t cry", "vault_lines": ["R.I.P., baby, my phone died, but don't cry"], "meaning": "Wayne is alluding to his ongoing feud with Cash-Money owner Birdman, who has been battling Wayne in court over an unpaid $51 million. Because of this, he hasn’t been able to release Tha Carter V for nearly four years, or any of his own projects; recent years have definitely been hard times for Weezy fans.", "annotation_id": "13355261", "url": "https://genius.com/13355261", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "I been walkin’ on this water, bone dry,", "vault_lines": ["I been walkin' on this water, bone dry,"], "meaning": "This is a biblical reference to Jesus who could walk on water. Weezy is saying his feet don’t even get wet when they touch water, either implying that he’s Godly or non-human and he’s been doing it for a long time.", "annotation_id": "13355259", "url": "https://genius.com/13355259", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Just call me the rapper, I’m Chancin’ it", "vault_lines": ["Just call me the rapper, I'm Chancin' it"], "meaning": "This is a shoutout to Chance The Rapper. Wayne has collaborated before with Chance on the 2016 songs “No Problem” and “I’m the One” and on the previous dedication tape with “You Song”.", "annotation_id": "13354946", "url": "https://genius.com/13354946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Do it look like I’m playin’? Kaepernick", "vault_lines": ["Do it look like I'm playin'? Kaepernick"], "meaning": "Here Lil Wayne takes a jab at the issue between Colin Kaepernick and the NFL.\n\nEver since his National Anthem Protest sent shockwaves around the country, many owners and teams have been reluctant to sign him to their rosters.\n\nThe closest team to signing Kaep was the Baltimore Ravens, who looked to bring him on as a backup during the 2017 Preseason. According to Ravens legend Ray Lewis, they team was prepared to sign Kaepernick, until his girlfriend sent out a seemingly racist tweet about Lewis and team owner Steve Bisciotti.\nhttps://twitter.com/nessnitty/status/892902143983792128", "annotation_id": "13354816", "url": "https://genius.com/13354816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "XO Tour Life", "line": "Rest in peace, Lil Peep, we already miss you, homie", "vault_lines": ["Rest in peace, Lil Peep, we already miss you, homie"], "meaning": "Just over a month before this song’s release, rapper Lil Peep was found unresponsive in Tucson, AZ where he was set to perform a show, and later died.\n\n\n\nHis death has sent shockwaves through the music industry and the United States about the ongoing opioid epidemic. It was revealed in early December that Peep’s cause of death was an overdose of Fentanyl and Xanax.", "annotation_id": "13354779", "url": "https://genius.com/13354779", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
