{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Workin’ Em", "line": "I’m hotter than fire, she wetter than a bitch (Oww!) These niggas really pussy, and I’m harder than my dick", "vault_lines": ["I'm hotter than fire, she wetter than a bitch (Oww!)"], "meaning": "Weezy says that he’s hotter (as in being the best rapper or the most popping rapper) than fire. Pussy is slang for soft or weak. When a penis gets an erection, gets hard. Hard also means gangster or tough. Pussy connects with dick also because the act of sexual intercourse involves a pussy and a dick.", "annotation_id": "20439178", "url": "https://genius.com/20439178", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Workin’ Em", "line": "And since we like to travel, she let us run a train (Choo-choo) And my defense put me in the Hall of Fame (Geah) I make her turn over every time we play the game (Bitch)", "vault_lines": ["And since we like to travel, she let us run a train (Choo-choo)"], "meaning": "To run a train on a girl is to have multiple men have sex with her in succession. Wayne draws a parallel between trains being ran on a woman sexually and trains that are used for travelling. When he says “turn over” it could have 2 possible meanings:\n- The woman is turning over in bed as to switch from laying on her back or stomach\n - To turn over the ball in basketball is to lose the ball and give the other team the ball, playing good defense could result in a turnover, as this may connect with the previous line", "annotation_id": "20439153", "url": "https://genius.com/20439153", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Workin’ Em", "line": "See, baby, I’m a stunner", "vault_lines": ["I wear a lot of diamonds (Yeah)—see, baby, I'm a stunner"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Birdman, the founder of Cash Money the man who discovered Lil' Wayne, and eventually became his step-father (later becoming estranged in a legal battle(https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/unraveling-lil-wayne-and-birdmans-lengthy-road-to-reconciliation-news.91091.html). Birdman is also known by the nicknames ‘Baby\" and 'Stunna’. Lil Wayne is calling out to his step-father and mentor: Look Baby – I’m also a stunna. He’s a star just like Birdman in both his fame from rapping and the amount of bling he wears.", "annotation_id": "19921815", "url": "https://genius.com/19921815", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Workin’ Em", "line": "Bitches on my stick, but my name ain’t “Harry Potter” (Ill!)", "vault_lines": ["Bitches on my stick, but my name ain't \"Harry Potter\" (Ill!)"], "meaning": "Wayne references Quidditch, a fictional sport in fantasy novel/movie series Harry Potter. The game involves wizards and witches riding flying broomsticks. It takes the place that soccer takes for non-magic people.\n\nOf course, his stick isn’t a broom—it’s his penis.", "annotation_id": "15655508", "url": "https://genius.com/15655508", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Workin’ Em", "line": "They love a nigga vibe, so that’s why I got the cover (Cover)", "vault_lines": ["They love a nigga vibe, so that's why I got the cover (Cover)"], "meaning": "A “vibe” is an emotional quality or atmosphere that is sensed or experienced by someone.\n\nWeezy refers to the VIBE Magazine, who put him on their cover back in 2006, the same year Dedication 2 was released.\n\n\n\nHe was featured on the cover in 2007, 2008 and 2011 as well.", "annotation_id": "14601864", "url": "https://genius.com/14601864", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Workin’ Em", "line": "In a Ferrari, Jaguar, switching both lanes (Errrr!)", "vault_lines": ["In a Ferrari, Jaguar, switching both lanes (Errrr!)"], "meaning": "A reference to Jay-Z’s song “Money Ain’t A Thang”\n\nIn the Ferrari or Jaguar, switchin' four lanes\nWith the top down screamin out, money ain’t a thang", "annotation_id": "2332090", "url": "https://genius.com/2332090", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
