{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Words Of Advice", "line": "Bout to serve ’em like subpoenas", "vault_lines": ["Bout to serve 'em like subpoenas"], "meaning": "A subpoena is an order to appear for a court date (most likely as a result of a crime/alleged crime.) The related party is obliged to bring evidence before a judge. Thus, one would receive a subpoena, attend their court date, and serve their sentence.\n\nSome seem to think that Mack Maine is saying “Serve ‘em like 'Sevenus,’” which is purportedly a combination of Serena and Venus, as in Venus and Serena Williams, the professional tennis players. To commence a point, the ball is “served” to the opposing player’s side of the court; similarly, to “serve” someone is to make them look foolish.", "annotation_id": "608070", "url": "https://genius.com/608070", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Words Of Advice", "line": "Gotta recognize now man you know me", "vault_lines": ["Gotta recognize now man you know me"], "meaning": "Please understand immediately who you are dealing with.  In fact, just by knowing of me, you should really be conceding as we speak.", "annotation_id": "211314", "url": "https://genius.com/211314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Words Of Advice", "line": "I’ve been real since BC, guess this is the after life Drop out from heavens like, just to raise plenty hell Boy I’m tryna touch a billion bucks before 2012", "vault_lines": ["I’m looking like a racist?"], "meaning": "He’s strong in the rap game for a long time now (since Before Christ – like 2000 years). He’s living in the after life, in heaven, but dropped out to make his music on earth – ‘'just to raise plenty hell’‘ – And continuing with the religion references, he says he’s trying to have a billion bucks before the world supposedly ends (2012).\n\nHe did not achieve his goal.", "annotation_id": "197887", "url": "https://genius.com/197887", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Words Of Advice", "line": "Silent four five, potato head on it", "vault_lines": ["Silent four five, potato head on it"], "meaning": "Cleverly, 0.45 gun, which was outfitted with a potato to serve as a silencer. “Ghetto Silencer”. How resourceful!", "annotation_id": "197657", "url": "https://genius.com/197657", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Words Of Advice", "line": "The niggas keep me laughing like hyena’s", "vault_lines": ["The niggas keep me laughing like hyena’s"], "meaning": "I laugh at people, just like the sounds that are made by Hyenas, a vocal dog-like animal.\n\nSometimes Hyena’s bark sounds like laughter but its more like a wheezing noise, which makes Little Wayne’s nickname “Lil Weezy” so much more appropriate by this line.", "annotation_id": "197557", "url": "https://genius.com/197557", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
