{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Without You", "line": "I be trying to rest But Lord, the Devil busy And when I do, I dream of you And then the Devil pinch me Do you ever miss me? Do you ever wish we Get it right and the rest is history?", "vault_lines": ["I be trying to rest"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is trying to rest, or do anything but work, which in Wayne’s case anything but rapping. In the next line he says “But the devil’s busy\", which is a possible reference to Birdman. Wayne is saying whenever he does try to rest (not work/rap) so that he can spend time with the girl, the devil (Birdman) pinches him, and tells him to get back to work.\n\nWayne then goes on in the next line and talks about how back then she thought he’d rather grind, but he had to grind because he signed the contract, or sold his soul to Birdman and that’s why Baby was able to force him to work in the first place.\n\nHe also had a similar line in “My Heart Races On”, which is the 4th track off of the current album.\n\nI sold my soul to the devil he bought it then exchanged it", "annotation_id": "7229598", "url": "https://genius.com/7229598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Without You", "line": "I wish I could go back in time And fix my frame of mind Back when everything was fine And we would never think of dying And I was yours and you was mine And we combine and intertwine", "vault_lines": ["And when I do, I dream of you"], "meaning": "Wayne sounds regretful, and wishes that he could go back in time and fix his frame of mind, so that he would view, and do things differently – maybe he wouldn’t even have to break up with his girl.", "annotation_id": "7222183", "url": "https://genius.com/7222183", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Without You", "line": "Now you’ve been gone too long True or false, right or wrong?", "vault_lines": ["Now you've been gone too long"], "meaning": "This is similar to the Outro on Lil Wayne’s earlier song, “Blunt Blowin” from Tha Carter IV.\n\nNow however, instead of referring to how long Wayne had been in jail, he’s telling his lover she’s been out of the picture for much too long.", "annotation_id": "7219745", "url": "https://genius.com/7219745", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
