{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "This block booming, I’m not human", "vault_lines": ["This block booming, I’m not human"], "meaning": "The rap game has been booming, and Lil Wayne has rapped about the streets for decades in it, as a part of the Hot Boys well before his first solo album “Tha Block is Hot”\n\nHe’s always said hes an alien as well and refers himself as a “Martian”, in other songs, and has made two “I am not a human being” albums", "annotation_id": "26021819", "url": "https://genius.com/26021819", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "These niggas in the game – so sad to me I’m sure no one would care if we Just put them out their misery But no sympathy and no green, uh uh Leave home with no heat? Uh uh", "vault_lines": ["I’m throwed, no catchin me"], "meaning": "Many of these other rappers are broke and can’t rap like T.I.P.\n\nNobody would care if they were one hit wonders and then went broke\n\nAs for T.i. he would never leave the house unarmed in these streets, and always has heat on him.\nHe explains this is why he caught a gun charge in this song, “ Ready for Whatever”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lNQVT6e6AFo", "annotation_id": "26021767", "url": "https://genius.com/26021767", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "We ain’t playin, got 100 racks (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me) In the van got 100 gat (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me) Streets (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me) She’s (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me) He’s (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me) (I’m wit you!) We ain’t playin, got 100 racks (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me) In the van got 100 gat (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me) Strong (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me) Gas (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me) Drank (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me)", "vault_lines": ["We ain’t playin, got 100 racks (wit me, wit me, wit me, wit me)"], "meaning": "They have 100 racks of cash money as well as 100 gats, firearms with them.\n\nIn addition both T.I. and Lil Wayne have the streets on lock whenever they drop a new song, and they don’t play around.\n\nStrong Gas is Cannabis and Drank can be Alcohol or the Codeine Lil Wayne infamously uses.", "annotation_id": "26021747", "url": "https://genius.com/26021747", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "If you’re a rat you should’ve died as a mouse", "vault_lines": ["If you're a rat you should’ve died as a mouse"], "meaning": "Rat is another word used for snitches, so he’s saying anyone who snitches on somebody else illegal activity should have died when they were little, like this mouse", "annotation_id": "26021727", "url": "https://genius.com/26021727", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "Could sell bullshit to a Taurus", "vault_lines": ["Got bitches fallin like August could sell bullshit to a Taurus"], "meaning": "Taurus, Latin for “bull”, is a sign of the Zodiac, or in this case likely someone born under that sign.\n\n\n\nIf you’re a bull, bullshit isn’t difficult to obtain– but Weezy’s so cunning he could convince you to buy some anyway.", "annotation_id": "2238101", "url": "https://genius.com/2238101", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "Here today, gone today", "vault_lines": ["Here today, gone today"], "meaning": "Either:\n\nLil Wayne is physically present, but so stoned he is mentally absent.\n\n-or\n\nLil Wayne doesn’t spend the night, and bounces as soon as he is finished fucking “wit” you.", "annotation_id": "1821889", "url": "https://genius.com/1821889", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "Ask Tunechi and them", "vault_lines": ["I’m stupid, ask Tunechi and them"], "meaning": "Wayne and T.I. both have a lot of crazy shit in common (both got jailed for gun charges, for a start…)", "annotation_id": "1810792", "url": "https://genius.com/1810792", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "One giant leap for mankind I’m high as moon men, how have you been?", "vault_lines": ["One giant leap for mankind"], "meaning": "Wayne quotes Neil Armstrong’s famous line when he first stepped onto the moon: “That’s one small step for (a) man, a giant leap for mankind.”.\n\nNow, referencing the moon landing once again, Wayne says he is as high as them (with a triple entendre) drug-wise, distance-wise, and success-wise.", "annotation_id": "1802374", "url": "https://genius.com/1802374", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "Cash on deck, they be layin round wit it Got a K - fuck with us,", "vault_lines": ["Cash on deck, they be layin round wit it"], "meaning": "This line is saying that T.I. is richer than a motherfucka\n\n\n\nDon’t Hate", "annotation_id": "1790046", "url": "https://genius.com/1790046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "Got Lil Wayne on her ass, Lil Tunechi on her titties", "vault_lines": ["Got Lil Wayne on her ass, Lil Tunechi on her titties"], "meaning": "Double Entendre:\n\n\nTunechi is cumming all over her body, both ass and titties. She’s got Wayne’s babys all over her!\nShe’s a big fan of the YM Chief and has his name tattood on both ass and tits. She’s not the only crazy Lil Wayne fan…", "annotation_id": "1789386", "url": "https://genius.com/1789386", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "Before you judge me I plead guilty", "vault_lines": ["Before you judge me I plead guilty"], "meaning": "Wayne’s image is often scrutinized by the media and by the public, where his use of drugs is questioned, his gang affiliation is investigated, etc. Wayne is real and stands by what he says in his bars,and knows the consequences of being real in the rap game.\n\nAlso in references with his troubles with the law, Wayne pleaded guilty to gun charges in 2009 so he could avoid prior drug charges that were laid upon him, leaving the judge no room for any judgement.", "annotation_id": "1789382", "url": "https://genius.com/1789382", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "My bitch is badder than me, call that Adam & Eve", "vault_lines": ["My bitch is badder than me, call that Adam & Eve"], "meaning": "A Biblical reference to the famous Creation story in Exodus, where Eve was the first human to sin, before Adam was.\n\n\n\nWayne’s women is so attractive that it supersedes his stardom and his own celebrated image", "annotation_id": "1789346", "url": "https://genius.com/1789346", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "Drop codeine in my punch, I’m bout to take a swing", "vault_lines": ["Drop codeine in my punch, I’m bout to take a swing"], "meaning": "Codeine is often mixed with Sprite, which is the most popular mixture of the substance, but it also was mixed with Hawaiian Punch, as Wayne shows here:\n\n\n\nAnd UGK and Three 6 show here:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lOWKGXpl9E0\n\nThe Hawaiian Punch is a homonym for actually physically punching someone, which Wayne plays with punch (drank) and swing (swig).\n\nAlso referring to the last line “Till the fat lady sings”, until the very end, he’s going to drop his codeine and smoke his weed", "annotation_id": "1789318", "url": "https://genius.com/1789318", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wit Me", "line": "Let me tell you a little something bout me I talk shit, bread like Muhammad Ali Then, whoop a nigga ass like Muhammad Ali", "vault_lines": ["Let me tell you a little something bout me"], "meaning": "Muhammad Ali’s style was to stay away from his opponent and keep moving around so they couldn’t hit him. He would talk all that trash, so his opponent would come out mad and wanting to hit Ali as hard as he could. They were unable to do that though because of Ali’s style, and they would miss all their punches.\n\nT.I. would do the same thing to you.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VpWQEVkxABA", "annotation_id": "1789086", "url": "https://genius.com/1789086", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
