{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whoever You Like", "line": "Well, not actually, ’cause I make it rain (Whatever you like) Yeah, you can pick the weather you like", "vault_lines": ["Well, not actually, 'cause I make it rain"], "meaning": "Wayne continues on from the end of Jae Millz' verse where he says that his life is good, so the weather will always be sunny for him.\n\nWayne then assures us that it isn’t always sunny, since he makes it rain.", "annotation_id": "2780438", "url": "https://genius.com/2780438", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whoever You Like", "line": "Like you can’t touch this, like you can’t touch us with a pipe But we can touch whoever we like You could even do Lil’ Chuckee, Lil’ Twist, KY, Bobby V Lil’ Scrap, didn’t say me, ’cause I got a wife So, sorry, not tonight", "vault_lines": ["Mack Maine, Tyga Tyga, you can do whoever you like"], "meaning": "Wayne’s getting a little out of line here and says that he can even get girls to have sex with the younger members of YMCMB, like Lil Chuckee and Lil Twist.\n\nIt may not be that big of a deal to Wayne, however, as he lost his virginity when he was only 11 years old.\n\nWayne states that he is loyal to his wife, so he cannot participate in the same shenanigans that his clique is in. Strange thing is that Wayne was only ever married once (to his first baby mama and high school crush, Toya Wright), however they got divorced well before this song was released.\n\nHe is most likely referring to either singer Nivea or actress Lauren London; as he got both of them pregnant around the same time of this song’s release.\n\n\n\nToya, Lauren, and Nivea all pictured together. I guess Wayne really does have no baby mama drama.", "annotation_id": "2722413", "url": "https://genius.com/2722413", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
