{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whip Game Proper", "line": "Not from Georgia, I’m from Chicago but I got a Field Mob", "vault_lines": ["Not from Georgia, I'm from Chicago but I got a Field Mob"], "meaning": "Field Mob is a hip hop duo from Georgia. Twista is saying he may not be associated with the group but he has his own mob members.", "annotation_id": "19179237", "url": "https://genius.com/19179237", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whip Game Proper", "line": "Yes, human crack, Young Carter", "vault_lines": ["Yes, human crack, Young Carter"], "meaning": "“Crack” is the freebase form of cocaine usually produced for people with a lower income.\n\nTunechi uses the drug to describe himself as “dope”, which could refer to his lyrics, flow, etc.\n\n“Young Carter” of course refers to his real name – Dwayne Michael Carter, Jr.", "annotation_id": "8920326", "url": "https://genius.com/8920326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whip Game Proper", "line": "So much ice, I need the stick with the puck", "vault_lines": ["So much ice, I need the stick with the puck"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying that he have so much ice (Chain, bracelet etc)\nthat he can pass on as a hockey player, since they be around ice so much", "annotation_id": "2025915", "url": "https://genius.com/2025915", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whip Game Proper", "line": "Yeah, and my whip game straight", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, and my whip game straight"], "meaning": "A “whip” refers to a car, and usually, a nice car. If something (like a whip game) is straight, it means that it’s good. Meaning Wayne’s got some nice cars.\n\nOne of Wayne’s cars is a Bugatti which he spent $1.8 million on.\n\n\n\nDue to Wayne’s very nice Bugatti, I would agree that his whip game is straight.", "annotation_id": "1587760", "url": "https://genius.com/1587760", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whip Game Proper", "line": "Yosemite Sam, two holsters Two pistols, can’t be too cautious", "vault_lines": ["Yosemite Sam, two holsters"], "meaning": "Yosemite Sam is a character on the animated television series Looney Tunes. Yosemite Sam was often seen with his two pistols.\n\n\n\nMuch like Yosemite Sam, Wayne has two pistols of his own. These pistols are used to protect him from any danger he may encounter, and he has two because two is always better than one, right?", "annotation_id": "1563930", "url": "https://genius.com/1563930", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whip Game Proper", "line": "I perform better in hot water", "vault_lines": ["I perform better in hot water"], "meaning": "In this context, “hot water” refers to pressure. So Wayne performing better in hot water means that when things get rough and he needs to achieve a specific goal, he does.", "annotation_id": "1562050", "url": "https://genius.com/1562050", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whip Game Proper", "line": "And I’m physically fine, but my flow’s sick", "vault_lines": ["And I'm physically fine, but my flow's sick"], "meaning": "When something is “sick” that means that it is exceptional.\n\nWayne saying\n\nI’m physically fine\n\nCould mean 2 things:\n\n\nHe doesn’t have any health issues.\nHe thinks he is appealing/attractive (“fine” can often mean attractive)\n\n\n\n\n\nWayne the goes on to say\n\nbut my flow’s sick\n\nThis means that his flow (ability to ride the beat) is amazing, but Wayne makes it seem like sick means actually ill. This line makes it seem like he is contradicting himself, but it’s just common Wayne wordplay.", "annotation_id": "1562040", "url": "https://genius.com/1562040", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whip Game Proper", "line": "PETA", "vault_lines": ["Whip game proper, whip game proper"], "meaning": "PETA, the group that advocates for ethical treatment of animals", "annotation_id": "1311956", "url": "https://genius.com/1311956", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Whip Game Proper", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Twista-whip-game-proper-lyrics", "genius_title": "Whip Game Proper", "genius_id": 46508, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where da Cash At", "line": "I got ‘em creepin’ over;", "vault_lines": ["I got 'em creepin' over;"], "meaning": "Creepin’ just means to cheat [on your significant other]. It is called this because if you’re cheating on your loved one, you obviously don’t want them to find out. The true definition of creep is: “move slowly and carefully in order to avoid being heard or noticed,” i.e. to avoid being caught being unfaithful.\nCurrency is saying that he is such a player that she is willing to cheat on her man and will sneak over to copulate with Currency behind her man’s back.", "annotation_id": "30999773", "url": "https://genius.com/30999773", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where da Cash At", "line": "We doin’ dinner soda", "vault_lines": ["we doin' dinner soda"], "meaning": "I don’t think he is saying “we doin’ dinner soda,” but instead I believe he is actually saying “We do it, then it’s over,” which would make more sense in combination with the previous statement that he has her coming over to have sex. But, like the player that he claims to be, he ultimately sees her as nothing more than a sexual object so after the “deed” is done he wants nothing more to do with her: “then it’s over.” She’s gotta go.", "annotation_id": "30999702", "url": "https://genius.com/30999702", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where da Cash At", "line": "And if you smile at my bitch, I’ll make her smile back Don’t be surprised if she ask where the cash at", "vault_lines": ["Where the where the cash at, where the cash at"], "meaning": "When he is out in public with a girl he makes sure she smiles at people so that he can get more clients for her and continue to profit.", "annotation_id": "15655346", "url": "https://genius.com/15655346", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where da Cash At", "line": "I’m talkin’ burnin’ rubber, that melted Pirelli odor", "vault_lines": ["I'm talkin' burnin' rubber, that melted Pirelli odor"], "meaning": "Pirelli is a brand of tires and Curren$y uses the brand name to emphasize the burning rubber previously mentioned.", "annotation_id": "15655334", "url": "https://genius.com/15655334", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where da Cash At", "line": "You catch my girl legs open, better smash that Don’t be surprised if she ask where the cash at", "vault_lines": ["Where the where the cash at, where the cash at"], "meaning": "If you have relations with one of Lil Wayne girls, it’s going to cost, as he proclaimed on the song these lines were sampled from, his 2005 single “Fireman”:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/7xHV0coanGU?t=65", "annotation_id": "15655322", "url": "https://genius.com/15655322", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
