{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where You At", "line": "DL, you know?", "vault_lines": ["D what? DL, you know?"], "meaning": "DL means down low meaning to not tell people this information", "annotation_id": "35839922", "url": "https://genius.com/35839922", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where You At", "line": "Redbone in the shower, hello, Pocahontas", "vault_lines": ["Redbone in the shower, hello, Pocahontas"], "meaning": "Wayne could be stating that he, not quite literally, has a “red” (or Native American) woman in the shower, who he playfully refers to as Pocahontas, an influential Native American woman.\n\nMoreover, “redbone” is slang for a mixed-race or lightskin black woman who, upon exiting a hot shower, will have a slight pink or red tone to her skin. When Wayne sees this lightskin woman’s reddish skin, he comedically calls out to her by saying, “Hello, Pocahontas!”", "annotation_id": "33097599", "url": "https://genius.com/33097599", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where You At", "line": "This gotta be the last song on the album ‘Cause once nigga hear this, nigga don’t want hear no fuckin’ more", "vault_lines": ["This gotta be the last song on the album"], "meaning": "They didn’t listen to Lil Wayne and made this the tenth track on the album of 21 tracks", "annotation_id": "28764169", "url": "https://genius.com/28764169", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where You At", "line": "Sticky in my Swish, man, gasoline flow Fire spit, man, Weezy is about to blow", "vault_lines": ["Sticky in my Swish, man, gasoline flow"], "meaning": "Gasoline and sticky are both names for marajuana, a swisher is a type of cigar used to roll blunts, and the wordplay in that line perfectly compliments the fire spitting imagery in the next line, as well as the idea of his energy and flow being explosive. Wayne Inhales gasoline and spits fire like none other.", "annotation_id": "2744476", "url": "https://genius.com/2744476", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
