{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "I think he run with 12 and I think his whole squad linked", "vault_lines": ["I think he run with 12 and I think his whole squad linked"], "meaning": "Wayne suspects someone of working with the police (“Twelve”).\n\nAnd it’s not just the one snitch, his crew is tied up in it too.", "annotation_id": "8399461", "url": "https://genius.com/8399461", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Really ’bout to see a billion, I’m in arm’s reach", "vault_lines": ["Really 'bout to see a billion, I'm in arm's reach"], "meaning": "With an alleged net worth of $150 million, it’s not quite in arm’s reach. Considering he’s also suing Birdman for $52 million, and is currently unable to release his next solo LP, a billion is a mile away.", "annotation_id": "8546929", "url": "https://genius.com/8546929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Rrt, I’m taking off", "vault_lines": ["rrt, I'm taking off"], "meaning": "By using different meanings of the term “taking off”, Wayne makes a play on words where, he doesn’t take breaks from hustling – but he does blast off in one of his many exotic sports cars (that’s why he makes the sound of tires screeching on pavement).", "annotation_id": "8546892", "url": "https://genius.com/8546892", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "And the money coming godspeed", "vault_lines": ["And the money coming godspeed"], "meaning": "God speed-\nan expression of good wishes to a person starting a journey.\n\nHe playing on that word implying how fast the money comes is equivalent to the speed God produces.", "annotation_id": "8463608", "url": "https://genius.com/8463608", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "And I really kick my feet up, and that’s not karate Yeah, I really kick my feet up, let a thot massage ’em, yeah", "vault_lines": ["And I really kick my feet up, and that's not karate"], "meaning": "Wayne is a black belt in Chill-jitsu. So when he “kicks his feet up”, it’s not this kind:\n\n\n\nIt’s this kind:\n\n\n\nHe’s pimpin in chill mode with one of his many female friends rubbing his feet for him.", "annotation_id": "8416061", "url": "https://genius.com/8416061", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "I’m hittin’ notes with the pistol, ooh, I’m off-key", "vault_lines": ["I'm hittin' notes with the pistol, ooh, I'm off-key"], "meaning": "“Hit a note” as an idiom means to do something well consistently; obviously being Weezy, he takes this saying literally. Being off-key may imply he accidentally missed a target objectively or personally", "annotation_id": "8415629", "url": "https://genius.com/8415629", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "You know my MO, nigga, pit that A-M-M-O, nigga Blat", "vault_lines": ["You know my MO, nigga, pit that A-M-M-O, nigga"], "meaning": "M.O. stands for Modus Operandi which is Latin phrase that translates to “mode of operation.”\n\nWayne’s saying his M.O. is to go into the studio and spit bullets.\n\nHere is a video of Wayne ranting about how rappers need to come to the studio with ammo:\n\nhttps://m.youtube.com/watch?v=vU_y_JRJHo8", "annotation_id": "8305430", "url": "https://genius.com/8305430", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "I’m just sipped out and I’m way too tired to talk, please I’m just sipped out and I’m way too tired, I’m yawning Yeah", "vault_lines": ["I'm just sipped out and I'm way too tired to talk, please"], "meaning": "Wayne has been sipping codeine cough syrup, a drug he often mentions. A side effect of lean is severe drowsiness and slurred speech. He’s so high off lean, he can barely talk and is struggling to stay awake.", "annotation_id": "8284877", "url": "https://genius.com/8284877", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Been to Hell and back, came back in mint condition, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Been to Hell and back, came back in mint condition, nigga"], "meaning": "Saying you have been to hell and back usually means that you have experienced a lot in your life, good & bad.\n\nWeezy has been through a lot in his life, and 2015 was certainly one of his roughest years. Whether it was Getting sued by a t-shirt model or  his label getting sued things just weren’t going right for Weezy.\n\nIt didn’t help when Cash Money held his music back, while not paying him, and eventually suing him.", "annotation_id": "8282671", "url": "https://genius.com/8282671", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "I’m moving slow as hell but the money coming godspeed I’m moving slow as hell but the money coming godspeed", "vault_lines": ["And the money coming godspeed"], "meaning": "Weezy hasn’t released an album on iTunes since 2013, but he still appeared on Forbes Hip-Hop Cash Kings list in 2014 earning $23 million & 2015 around $15 million.\n\n\n\nHe’s also known for his prolific user of lean – a drug known for making things feel slower.", "annotation_id": "8282585", "url": "https://genius.com/8282585", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Where ya ass was at when I was fifteen in a Porsche?", "vault_lines": ["Where ya ass was at when I was fifteen in a Porsche?"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne earned $6500 when he was 14, that was his first rap paycheck, he went straight to Nissan and bought a Pathfinder.\n\nWhen he turned 15, he upgraded and got a Porsche.\n\nI got glasses like that white boy Scott Storch and a Porsche", "annotation_id": "8282507", "url": "https://genius.com/8282507", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "My neighbors can’t sleep, all they hearin’ is them cars screech My bitch can’t sleep, all she hearin’ is them car keys", "vault_lines": ["My neighbors can't sleep, all they hearin' is them cars screech"], "meaning": "Weezy stuntin' with the big collection of his cars at midnight.. How can you blame him with a collection as exotic as this?\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y0JqVuclB2E\n\nWeezy’s Miami mansion is pretty big, so the $2m Bugatti Veyron sure does have loud engines since it’s keeping his neighbors awake. They are a long way away.\n\nHe also claims to be the first rapper to have purchased the Bugatti Veyron, although Birdman has his own.", "annotation_id": "8282470", "url": "https://genius.com/8282470", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "I work too hard for taking off,", "vault_lines": ["I work too hard for taking off,"], "meaning": "Weezy lives in the studio, he never takes a break, he’s  been rapping for almost 20 years and has dropped a project or more  almost every year since his debut. In fact, this is the 3rd project he released this year.\n\nAs recently stated by one of his producers, Infamous:\n\nHis work ethic is crazier than anybody. He’s literally in the studio at least 6 days a week. And those six days, it’s a minimum of 8 to 10 hours a day. It’s not like another rap session where 6 of those hours are shooting the shit and just smoking weed.", "annotation_id": "8282448", "url": "https://genius.com/8282448", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "And we set a nigga up like eHarmony", "vault_lines": ["And we set a nigga up like eHarmony"], "meaning": "Wayne plays with the dual meaning of “setting up.”\n\neHarmony is dating site designed for singles to match with each other to form long-term relationships. Similar to how the couples are “set up,” Wayne performs a “setup” to trick his enemies into a corner.", "annotation_id": "8281514", "url": "https://genius.com/8281514", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "And he dumb as hell, and I swear his ass don’t think", "vault_lines": ["And he dumb as hell, and I swear his ass don't think"], "meaning": "A direct reference to this line from Fetty Wap’s My Way:\n\nAnd he dumb as hell and I swear his ass don’t think, aye", "annotation_id": "8279643", "url": "https://genius.com/8279643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "We had to stash and still balled, Steve Harvey We had to stash and still balled, Steve Harvey", "vault_lines": ["We had to stash and still balled, Steve Harvey"], "meaning": "Said “[stashing] and [stealing”] consequently earned “We” (presumably victims of Hurricane Katrina from New Orleans) a certain amount of affluence or wealth, or baller status.\n\nIn addition, both stash and balled, as used here, are a double entendres. Lil Wayne is referencing Steve Harvey’s famous bald head and distinctive ‘stache.", "annotation_id": "8279120", "url": "https://genius.com/8279120", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Hey now, you’re an all-star But the bitches you be with, they are sub-par", "vault_lines": ["Hey now, you're an all-star"], "meaning": "Weezy mimics Smash Mouth’s hit “All Star” in the opening line. He then contrasts this statement by saying even though you’re rich and famous, you still can’t get a good-looking girl.\n\nThe “all-star” line implies that this may be a subliminal to another rapper or someone in the industry.", "annotation_id": "8279001", "url": "https://genius.com/8279001", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Diamonds in my mouth, no Swarovski", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds in my mouth, no Swarovski"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne wants us to know that he’s grilled out in diamonds.\n\nHowever, said diamonds aren’t from Swarovski Kristall, a business that primarily works with luxury items, fashion design, crystals and high-end optics.", "annotation_id": "8278998", "url": "https://genius.com/8278998", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "And the purple rain right here in the soft drink Yeah, the purple rain right here in the soft drink And to fight the pain, nigga, like a horse tranq", "vault_lines": ["And the purple rain right here in the soft drink"], "meaning": "Purple rain is a euphemism for codeine – a key ingredient for one of Weezy’s favorite narcotics, Lean. Lean consists of codeine syrup with promethazine, a soda of choice, and Jolly Rancher candy for flavor.\n\nHe even has a song dedicated to Lean titled “Me And My Drank”.\n\n\n\nIt acts as a painkiller. Horse tranquilizers are incredibly strong medication, Wayne must have a lot of pain.", "annotation_id": "8278956", "url": "https://genius.com/8278956", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "No Ceilings", "vault_lines": ["Where ya ass was at when I was with the Hot Boys?"], "meaning": "The first No Ceilings went live in 2009, due to an album push back. Now its 2015 and Wayne drops the second part also due to his way over due album Tha Carter V.", "annotation_id": "8278856", "url": "https://genius.com/8278856", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Where ya ass was at when I was with the Hot Boys? Probably watchin’ Baller Blockin’, eatin’ popcorn, yeah Where ya ass was at? You was in the drought, boy I was probably at the fight bringin’ out Floyd", "vault_lines": ["Where ya ass was at when I was with the Hot Boys?"], "meaning": "Bitch I’m ballin' like a hot boy\n\nHot Boys was a group consisting of Wayne, Juvenile, B.G. and Turk back in 1996 to 2001. They regrouped in 2007 for a reunion. Weezy left the group and started working solo, and now that he is poppin everyone wants to flee to him.\n\n\n\nBaller Blockin was a film featuring Cash Money, it was released in 2000.\n\nAlso, he’s referencing the boxed Floyd Mayweather in the last line, as Wayne has accompanied him entering the ring before.", "annotation_id": "8278789", "url": "https://genius.com/8278789", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where Ya At", "status": "done", "targets": 21, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-where-ya-at-lyrics", "genius_title": "Where Ya At", "genius_id": 2378302, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where My Old Lady", "line": "Don’t I give you peace of mind, wa alaykum salaam", "vault_lines": ["Don't I give you peace of mind, wa alaykum salaam"], "meaning": "“Wa Alaykum Salaam” is an islamic greeting used by muslims which translates to “May peace be upon you”.", "annotation_id": "15688741", "url": "https://genius.com/15688741", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where My Old Lady", "line": "I had to seek with widened eyes", "vault_lines": ["I've gotten wise, I had to seek with widened eyes"], "meaning": "A commons phrase is: Seek with eyes wide open\n\nHere Wayne makes a wordplay, having just said “I had to put my pot aside”, this sentence gets a clever double meaning.. ( widened / whitened )\n\n\n\nWhen you smoke pot/weed you get red and low eyes.\nSo Wayne is basically saying that his eyes both widened and whitened as he put the pot aside.", "annotation_id": "15680320", "url": "https://genius.com/15680320", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
