{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Where I’m From", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-where-im-from-lyrics", "genius_title": "Where I’m From", "genius_id": 3434817, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "When You’re Gone", "line": "They kickin’ me outta Canada", "vault_lines": ["Blink again and they kickin' me outta Canada"], "meaning": "In July of 2018 G-Eazy was denied entry into Canada forcing him to cancel a performance at The Cowboys Music Festival in Calgary, Alberta.", "annotation_id": "24250063", "url": "https://genius.com/24250063", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "When You’re Gone", "line": "A black leather, slicked back, they want the old G “Things are happenin’ again,” that’s what they told me", "vault_lines": ["A black leather, slicked back, they want the old G"], "meaning": "G-Eazy is known for his slicked back hair and leather jacket look especially when touring for “These Things Happen” and “When It’s Dark Out” this line may be a direct reference to his look during the “These Things Happen” era where he was often seen wearing this custom painted leather jacket.", "annotation_id": "24250034", "url": "https://genius.com/24250034", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "When You’re Gone", "line": "With dreams so big, nobody understands us", "vault_lines": ["With dreams so big, nobody understands us"], "meaning": "This line is almost identical to and might be a reference to a line from G-Eazy’s song “For This” from his album “When It’s Dark Out”.", "annotation_id": "24024300", "url": "https://genius.com/24024300", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "When You’re Gone", "line": "’Cause these songs’ll beat longer than my heart will", "vault_lines": ["'Cause these songs'll beat longer than my heart will"], "meaning": "The song ends with the same line as “Never Listen To Adults” from G-Eazy’s early album “Big”\n\n“I want to be remembered so I grind like a barrel\nCuz my songs will beat longer than my heart will”\n\nand his debut  major-label studio album “These Things Happen” song “Just Believe”\n\n“Everyday I’m here I try to write songs\nCause I know the beat’ll longer than my heart will”\n\nG knows that his music will last longer than he will, and while the length of fame is uncertain he knows he has to make his music as perfect as possible because it will leave an impression on the world.", "annotation_id": "24024265", "url": "https://genius.com/24024265", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "When You’re Gone", "line": "They thinkin’ Kurt Cobain, but I’m thinkin’ living legend", "vault_lines": ["They thinkin' Kurt Cobain, but I'm thinkin' living legend"], "meaning": "Kurt Cobain was the frontman of the American alternative rock band Nirvana. Cobain unfortunately committed suicide in 1994 at only 27 years old. To this day, the “Smells Like Teen Spirit” vocalist is considered one of the most influential musicians in the history of music due to his angst-fueled songwriting and anti-establishment persona.\n\nWhile it’s common for artists to get their props after their death like Cobain, Weezy proudly labels himself a “living legend.”", "annotation_id": "24023014", "url": "https://genius.com/24023014", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "When You’re Gone", "line": "I’ma wear all my chains like some Olympic medals They think it’s all a game, so I’m thinkin’ winnin’ record", "vault_lines": ["I'ma wear all my chains like some Olympic medals"], "meaning": "Weezy’s jewelry is so extravagant that they are reminiscent of the medals awarded to Olympic winners. Since all of his competitors think they can go toe-to-toe with Wayne, he’s showing off his accomplishments proudly.\n\nLil Wayne actually skated with Yuto Horigome, who won the first ever skateboarding gold medal in the Olympics. Yuto let Weezy wear his 2020 Tokyo gold medal for a pic.", "annotation_id": "24022983", "url": "https://genius.com/24022983", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
