{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Wrong With Them", "line": "Money is the song Pockets on high note Do Re Mi Fa So", "vault_lines": ["Money is the song"], "meaning": "Weezy likens money to music, and his pockets are reaching a vocal range many musicians couldn’t fathom. This is another braggadacio about how rich he’s becoming…\n\nSolfège is a music education method used to teach pitch and sight singing. The seven syllables commonly used for this practice in English-speaking countries are: do, re, mi, fa, sol, la, and ti. Weezy’s flaunting his musical knowledge at this point.", "annotation_id": "8121861", "url": "https://genius.com/8121861", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Wrong With Them", "line": "Life on the rocks Too hard to swallow", "vault_lines": ["Life on the rocks"], "meaning": "Nice wordplay in these two lines.\n\nWhen an alcoholic drink is on the rocks, there is usually ice in it, as to keep it cold.\n\n\n\nIf a drink is full of ice blocks it would be really hard to swallow as ice blocks are usually quite large.\n\nThis metaphor for life portrays the rocky lifestyle that Wayne and many of his cohorts lead.\n\nToo Hard To Swallow is also an album by fellow southern hip hop duo – UGK\n\nFUN-FACT:\nWeezy has stated that he does not know where Hip Hop is at and that he  listens to a lot of UGK.\n\nI listen to a lot of UGK, a lot of 8Ball & MJG and that’s kind of it. As far as new, I listen to Future, to a lot of the older mixtape stuff [and] A$AP Ferg.\n\n\nRead the whole article and interview here!", "annotation_id": "2168404", "url": "https://genius.com/2168404", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Wrong With Them", "line": "And if you got beef, I turn it to a tenderloin", "vault_lines": ["And if you got beef, I turn it to a tenderloin"], "meaning": "If someone has issues with Wayne, he will be quick to get rid of the issue, and maybe completely eliminate his enemy (by killing them, or killing them on a song).\n\nSo if you have beef (issues) with Wayne.\n\n\n\nHe will put an end to it, or make it smaller, as if he turning the beef into a smaller item of beef, like beef tenderloin.", "annotation_id": "1461675", "url": "https://genius.com/1461675", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Wrong With Them", "line": "Big boss shit, Paul Castellano", "vault_lines": ["Big boss shit, Paul Castellano"], "meaning": "Castellano was a New York mob boss that was shot by the orders of rival mob boss John Gotti.", "annotation_id": "75885", "url": "https://genius.com/75885", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Wrong With Them", "line": "Disrespectful on the beat, Borat", "vault_lines": ["Disrespectful on the beat, Borat"], "meaning": "Borat sang the (fake) Kazakhstan National anthem in tune of the American Anthem, this caused a huge uproar and was considered extremely disrespectful. Wayne considers himself comparably (actually probably more) disrespectful when he raps", "annotation_id": "49478", "url": "https://genius.com/49478", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Wrong With Them", "line": "That’s that nine nigga ughh, Rondo", "vault_lines": ["That's that nine nigga ughh, Rondo"], "meaning": "Another one of Weezy’s wordplay references to basketball. This time Weezy is comparing his gun (9mm) to Boston Celtic Rajon Rondo’s jersey number (#9)\n\nWayne also expressed his Laker Pride/Anti-Celtic attitude similar to his documentary Carter and such songs such as Kobe Bryant 24", "annotation_id": "41650", "url": "https://genius.com/41650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Wrong With Them", "line": "Ya’ll boys just a bunch of pussy cats, Milo", "vault_lines": ["Ya'll boys just a bunch of pussy cats, Milo"], "meaning": "A reference to the 1986 Japanese film, The Adventures of Milo and Otis about an orange tabby cat named Milo and a fawn pug named Otis.\n\n\n\nHere Wayne compares his haters to Milo and calls them pussies.", "annotation_id": "41649", "url": "https://genius.com/41649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
