{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "Use protection when you fuck around", "vault_lines": ["Use protection when you fuck around"], "meaning": "Wayne is playing on “protection”, which has the double meaning of a firearm and a condom.. and “fuck around”, which has the double meaning of doing something foolish, such as dissing Wayne’s clique, and sleeping around with a bunch of people.\n\nIn either case you need a form of protection.", "annotation_id": "13785487", "url": "https://genius.com/13785487", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "A psycho, all I’m missin’ is the gown", "vault_lines": ["A psycho, all I'm missin' is the gown"], "meaning": "Wayne is a psychopath in every way except for the fact he’s not locked up in a mental institution, in which case he would wear a hospital gown.", "annotation_id": "13785472", "url": "https://genius.com/13785472", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "Don’t pay your bill, I’m power trippin’", "vault_lines": ["Don't pay your bill, I'm power trippin'"], "meaning": "If you don’t pay Wayne what you owe him then he will go on a power trip, meaning showcasing an ability to get what he wants. Power tripping is also a way to turn off electrical services, which happens when you don’t pay your electric bill. This perfectly describes the power struggle between Wayne and Birdman.", "annotation_id": "13785431", "url": "https://genius.com/13785431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "I’m the hottest out in my city, Bad Boy too, ask Diddy", "vault_lines": ["I'm the hottest out in my city, Bad Boy too, ask Diddy"], "meaning": "Diddy, founder of Bad Boy Records, jumped on an official remix of Zoey’s hit song Blow A Check, which ended up appearing on Diddy’s MMM album.\n\nHere Zoey explains how it came together\n\nhttps://genius.com/9184812", "annotation_id": "13696875", "url": "https://genius.com/13696875", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "Future put me on, he from Atlanta", "vault_lines": ["Future put me on, he from Atlanta"], "meaning": "Future, one of the biggest rappers of our generation, was an instrumental part in helping Zoey get signed to Epic Records through his imprint, Freebandz, after he caught his attention with his hit single Blow A Check\n\nhttps://www.bet.com/music/2017/08/30/prelude-zoey-dollaz.html", "annotation_id": "13696869", "url": "https://genius.com/13696869", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "She do the money count in just her drawers, yeah I make her count out loud, I listen hard", "vault_lines": ["She do the money count in just her drawers, yeah"], "meaning": "Wayne has girls in his house counting money in just their underwear.\n\nListen hard is a double entendre here, in which he could be using “hard” as another term for sexually aroused, which watching naked women count money will do to you. It could also mean he listens hard, as in very closely, to make sure that they don’t make a mistake or try to pull anything on him.", "annotation_id": "13696829", "url": "https://genius.com/13696829", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "I get them Ms a mile a minute", "vault_lines": ["I get them Ms a mile a minute"], "meaning": "Sayings “Ms,” is another way of saying millions. Just like how a speedometer measures speed by miles per hour. Wayne’s speed for getting money is a million(mile) a minute.\n\n\n\nThat’s still a lot of money!", "annotation_id": "13594522", "url": "https://genius.com/13594522", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "Miami ballin’, it’s a hobby, call a nigga Joe Robbie", "vault_lines": ["Miami ballin', it's a hobby, call a nigga Joe Robbie"], "meaning": "Joe Robbie was an American politician attorney and the founder of the Miami Dolphins football team. Since establishment in 1965, the team has gone on to win 2 Super Bowl championships, 5 conference championships and 13 Division championships.\n\nSince migrating from Haiti, Zoey Dollaz grew up in the Allapattah niehgbourhood of Miami. Putting on for his city, Zoey brags of making it and ‘balling’ like his city’s football team.", "annotation_id": "13521714", "url": "https://genius.com/13521714", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "BET, that’s how I’m livin’", "vault_lines": ["BET, that's how I'm livin'"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the BET telvevision network’s reality show “How I’m Livin'” that ran from 2001 to 2003 and showcased the lifestyle of various celebrities including Usher and Pitbull.", "annotation_id": "13521605", "url": "https://genius.com/13521605", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "You know my eyes nice and low, like I make egg rolls, oh", "vault_lines": ["You know my eyes nice and low, like I make egg rolls, oh"], "meaning": "Egg rolls refer to a deep fried appetizer served at Chinese restaurants, which is a savoury roll that usually  contains shredded cabbage, chopped pork among other ingredients.\n\n\n\nLil Wayne is comparing  being high has made his eyes ‘low’ to how a Chinese person’s eyes are also narrow.", "annotation_id": "13521559", "url": "https://genius.com/13521559", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "Going Krogers with the bags", "vault_lines": [", going Krogers with the bags"], "meaning": "Krogers is a supermarket located in the Southern and Midwestern USA. Krogers is actually the largest supermarket chain by revenue and the third largest retailer in the world, so Wayne is making a rather hyperbolized metaphorical bar here.\nWayne is from New Orleans, Louisiana; and a driver for Southern rap’s dominance, so it’s an apt reference.", "annotation_id": "13435674", "url": "https://genius.com/13435674", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "I been snorklin’ in the cash", "vault_lines": ["I been snorklin' in the cash"], "meaning": "A popular euphamism is that one can be so rich, they can swim in their money:\n\n\n\nWayne has so much money he can not only swim, but dive into his money; which could be true considering he was the 17th richest rapper of 2017", "annotation_id": "13435624", "url": "https://genius.com/13435624", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "Hello, I make her throw away her pussy toys, yeah Ain’t got a job, I make her look employed, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Hello, I make her throw away her pussy toys, yeah"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne brags about being generous to woman, how can can satisfy every of their lustful desires, here is narrows it down specifically down to satisfying them sexually and materially\n\n\n\n\nLil Wayne being on the Forbes List Richest Rappers indicates buying high fashion designer clothing and Expensive Jewellery is not an issue.", "annotation_id": "13410353", "url": "https://genius.com/13410353", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "I rob his ass like Robin Givens", "vault_lines": ["I rob his ass like Robin Givens"], "meaning": "Robin Givens is an actress and model who wed former boxer Mike Tyson on February 7th, 1988. The two divorced on February 14th, 1989 with Givens receiving a reported 10 million dollar divorce settlement.", "annotation_id": "13397888", "url": "https://genius.com/13397888", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "Chris Paul, we load the rocket", "vault_lines": ["Chris Paul, we load the rocket"], "meaning": "Chris Paul, a star basketball player, joined the Houston Rockets in 2017. His talent adds to an already impressive roster therefore making the rockets “loaded.”", "annotation_id": "13388924", "url": "https://genius.com/13388924", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "I done went blonde, goin’ Hulk Hogan on they ass", "vault_lines": ["I done went blonde, goin' Hulk Hogan on they ass"], "meaning": "Hulk Hogan is an American retired professional wrestler. He is regarded by many as the greatest professional wrestler of all time. He used to call himself “The Immortal.”", "annotation_id": "13366842", "url": "https://genius.com/13366842", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "Brrrt! Pull up like a taxi, stereo on maxi Nigga, bury your own casket Nigga, say hello to Rabbit", "vault_lines": ["Brrrt! Pull up like a taxi, stereo on maxi"], "meaning": "Weezy will pull up in his own car and kill you, which is not a strange scene to him. After he sends you to heaven, he wants you to say hello to his stepdad Reginald McDonald, aka Rabbit, who was murdered when Wayne was 13 years old. He considered him his real father.\n\nHe even made a song dedicated to him:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-mgnxBRGoeg", "annotation_id": "13366458", "url": "https://genius.com/13366458", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "What’s Next", "line": "My father ain’t been ’round, my heart ain’t missed a pound", "vault_lines": ["My father ain't been 'round, my heart ain't missed a pound"], "meaning": "Weezy refers to Birdman, who was his father figure before all the label issues happened. Wayne met Birdman when he was only 11, Baby then signed him to Cash Money Records. They had a father-son relationship until Wayne went on Twitter in 2014 and revealed that Birdman has not been paying for his music, so he had to sue him.\n\nWayne talked about how he felt about Birdman and Cash Money Records all over his 2015 mixtape Sorry 4 The Wait 2:\n\nNow I don’t want no problems, I just want my money\nAin’t gotta hold no conversation, nor my luggage\nTell whoever’s countin' that I’m on a hundred\nWoo, Birdman Junior – more like Ugly Duckling", "annotation_id": "13366376", "url": "https://genius.com/13366376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
