{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "Rest in peace, Jerry West", "vault_lines": ["Rest in peace, Jerry West"], "meaning": "Wayne wraps up this gospel with a tribute to the late Lakers Legend Jerry West, who passed away on June 12, 2024.", "annotation_id": "35812636", "url": "https://genius.com/35812636", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "I went from checkin’ niggas to the nigga who sign checks", "vault_lines": ["I went from checkin' niggas to the nigga who sign checks"], "meaning": "Instead on focusing on putting people in their place (“checking people”), Wayne is now focused at his success, which is proven by his financial prosper (a man who is able to “sign checks”).\n\nIt also plays a greater role of being able to sign checks as someone who came from the bottom – as he mentioned earlier in the verse he was a “two-dollar baby”.", "annotation_id": "35811909", "url": "https://genius.com/35811909", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "I made a million-dollar man from a two-dollar baby", "vault_lines": ["I made a million-dollar man from a two-dollar baby"], "meaning": "Wayne implies he came from nothing and raised into greatness, money wise.", "annotation_id": "35811897", "url": "https://genius.com/35811897", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "Smokin’ that bomb LA like I’m McVay", "vault_lines": ["Smokin' that bomb LA like I'm McVay"], "meaning": "“McVay”: Sean McVay, head coach of the Los Angeles Rams in the National Football League (NFL). McVay is known for his “air raid offense” (long-haul plays, commonly called “bombs” in American football, meaning long, spectacular passes).\n\nThis could also be a double entendre also referring to Timothy McVeigh who committed the Oklahoma City Bombing", "annotation_id": "35811882", "url": "https://genius.com/35811882", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "I check the Chopard, I got time today", "vault_lines": ["I check the Chopard, I got time today"], "meaning": "Chopard is a Swiss house specializing in very high-end watches and jewelry. When someone says “I check the Chopard”, it literally means “I look at my Chopard”,", "annotation_id": "35811830", "url": "https://genius.com/35811830", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "And if it’s beef, I turn the whole cow to leather", "vault_lines": ["And if it's beef, I turn the whole cow to leather"], "meaning": "Wayne uses a double entendre on the word “beef”:\n1. In slang, “beef” means having argument with another person\n2. Beef is also the culinary name for meat derived from cattle (cows) – reference\n\nWayne implies that if you have an altercation with him, he’s victory will be so predominant that it will be as he slaughtered a cattle and took out your skin (“leather”)", "annotation_id": "35811829", "url": "https://genius.com/35811829", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "Life a bitch, I’m ’bout to make her your ex", "vault_lines": ["Life a bitch, I'm 'bout to make her your ex"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying that he’s gonna\nmake life your ex.\n\nAs in he’s going to take your life", "annotation_id": "35810872", "url": "https://genius.com/35810872", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "Lay you down, Weezy F, the F for futon, baby", "vault_lines": ["Lay you down, Weezy F, the F for futon, baby"], "meaning": "A futon is a versatile piece of furniture that can serve as both a bed and a sofa. Typically, a futon will be used as a couch but can be “laid down” into a bed for sleeping.", "annotation_id": "35810858", "url": "https://genius.com/35810858", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "I still eat the rappers, I heard they appetizers", "vault_lines": ["I still eat the rappers, I heard they appetizers"], "meaning": "Wayne uses a metaphor of being a dominant force in rap by portraying other rappers as food, specifically appetizers, implying they’re small and easily consumed.\n\nThis calls back to his bars from “We Takin’ Over (Remix)”:\n\nIt’s me, the Rapper Eater. Haha! Feed me, feeeed me, feed me!", "annotation_id": "35810756", "url": "https://genius.com/35810756", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
