{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "Y’all get on my nerves, I get high and land like a bird", "vault_lines": ["Y'all get on my nerves, I get high and land like a bird"], "meaning": "Wayne gets “high” (as if he were a bird) on drugs and lands gracefully like a bird.", "annotation_id": "35810581", "url": "https://genius.com/35810581", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "Ayo, my sun’s gon’ shine forever And as long as we here, you might as well get your clouds together", "vault_lines": ["Ayo, my sun's gon' shine forever"], "meaning": "To barricade or block Wayne’s shine, you’re going to need to get “clouds together” but that’s ironic since the sun can still shine through clouds, defeating the purpose of blocking its light. In this line, Wayne also boasts about the fact that he’s never been out-shined.\n\nWayne also happens to Interpolates Diddy’s line from “Victory:”\n\nYo, the sun don’t shine forever\nBut as long as it’s here, then we might as well shine together", "annotation_id": "35810116", "url": "https://genius.com/35810116", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "You throw Weezy on a beat, you’re throwin’ gas on fire", "vault_lines": ["You throw Weezy on a beat, you're throwin' gas on fire"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying that if you put him on a beat, he will make the song better.\nHe uses a metaphor with gas and fire to represent that if you already have a fire, you are burning it brighter.", "annotation_id": "35810009", "url": "https://genius.com/35810009", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "While I eat lil’ mama backwards like mignon filet", "vault_lines": ["While I eat lil' mama backwards like mignon filet"], "meaning": "Oral sex performed by Lil Wayne on a woman from behind, hence filet mignon (a tender cut of meat) being stated in backward order.", "annotation_id": "35809993", "url": "https://genius.com/35809993", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Welcome to Tha Carter", "line": "Smokin’ on a pure L, no sanitizer", "vault_lines": ["Smokin' on a pure L, no sanitizer"], "meaning": "An “L” is used to refer to a blunt, so a pure L would mean it’s a potent strain of weed. Also, Purell is a brand of hand sanitizer that’s pronounced the same as “pure L.”", "annotation_id": "35809987", "url": "https://genius.com/35809987", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
