{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy’s Ambitions", "line": "Sim seemer", "vault_lines": ["Weezy Baby that crack, muthafucka get a fix"], "meaning": "a phrase used as a declaration or recognition of greatness by oneself or another person, most often used in a congratulatory nature\nan informal greeting between friends, replaces or adds on to “yo” to mean “hows it going”, or “whats up”\na response to a greeting, and depending on vocal tones, can be used to convey a wide variety of moods\nnonsensical lyrics used by Beanie Man at the beginning of the song Who Am I", "annotation_id": "15189716", "url": "https://genius.com/15189716", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy’s Ambitions", "line": "We done lost everything and you looking like a bargain", "vault_lines": ["Weezy Baby that crack, muthafucka get a fix"], "meaning": "After Hurricane Katrina passed southeast of New Orleans on August 29th 2005, a lot of people lost their houses, cars, friends, and some lost everything they had.", "annotation_id": "4948263", "url": "https://genius.com/4948263", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy’s Ambitions", "line": "All my brothers left the family", "vault_lines": ["All my brothers left the family"], "meaning": "He doesn’t have any brothers, but here he is referring to Turk, B.G., and Juvenile who used to be in a group called Hot Boys with Wayne back in 1996 to 2001, he considered them as his brothers, they were like a family.\n\nThey all left Cash Money Records and he is the only one who stayed.", "annotation_id": "4948169", "url": "https://genius.com/4948169", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
