{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy N Madonna", "line": "You can throw up peace", "vault_lines": ["You can throw up peace"], "meaning": "“Throwing up a piece” is a phrase used in the grafitti scene for quickly creating an artwork. Lil Wayne insinuades that the opposition’s “artworks” are done on the quick while he puts thought, time and work into his albums and mixtapes.", "annotation_id": "15280753", "url": "https://genius.com/15280753", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy N Madonna", "line": "I’ve been away, I’ve been around I’ve been busy doin’ business Mind your business ‘fore I shut your fuckin’ business down", "vault_lines": ["I've been away, I've been around"], "meaning": "Weezy creatively uses the song LOYALTY. to talk about his multiyear legal dispute with Birdman. Though he hasn’t been paid for his much anticipated Tha Carter V album, he won a Grammy in 2017 and was nominated in 2016. He also has remained in the Top 100 Artists on Spotify since 2015, bouncing between 50-60.", "annotation_id": "14215361", "url": "https://genius.com/14215361", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy N Madonna", "line": "Young Tune winnin’ now You know I been winnin’ then and now anyhow Anyway, don’t start no shit if you can’t finish loud", "vault_lines": ["Young Tune winnin' now"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne matches Kendrick Lamars flow on LOYALTY., similarly claiming he’s the best. Tunechi has been “winning then and now” since his first Platinum album in 1997 and the subsequent success of Tha Carter series.  This isn’t a shot at Kendrick Lamar, who agrees that Wayne is “the greatest”", "annotation_id": "14215342", "url": "https://genius.com/14215342", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy N Madonna", "line": "Had to get the dreads bleached, the James Blonde look", "vault_lines": ["Had to get the dreads bleached, the James Blonde look"], "meaning": "Wayne is playing off of the name “James Bond”, who is a spy that is referenced on numerous occasions for his extraordinary swag. Lil Wayne is referring to how good he looks with his new blonde dyed dreadlocks.", "annotation_id": "14196979", "url": "https://genius.com/14196979", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy N Madonna", "line": "You look priceless to me, I’ll rip your price tag off", "vault_lines": ["You look priceless to me, I'll rip your price tag off"], "meaning": "You look “priceless” to me…\n\nThis is complimenting her by saying she’s invaluable or extremely expensive. Wayne is complimenting himself by saying he can afford her, even though she’s priceless.\n\nThis is also extremely practical considering the fact that if you’re priceless you shouldn’t have a price tag on.", "annotation_id": "13876052", "url": "https://genius.com/13876052", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy N Madonna", "line": "I don’t usually do this unless I’m drunk or I’m high And right now I’m both, got me talking bout you hoe", "vault_lines": ["And right now I'm both, got me talking bout you hoe"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne interpolates his Young Money artist’s hook on Gucci Mane’s Both. Weezy rarely gets sentimental about the woman he’s seeing, but because he’s cross-faded he’s talking about her in this love duet.", "annotation_id": "13695614", "url": "https://genius.com/13695614", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy N Madonna", "line": "I’m ’bout to put my hands on her like E. Honda", "vault_lines": ["I'm 'bout to put my hands on her like E. Honda"], "meaning": "E. Honda is a Street Fighter character whose special attack was a hundred hand slap.\n\nBut Wayne isn’t going to assault her, he’s insinuating that he’s going to perform a sexual act on her since she’s not wearing any pants.", "annotation_id": "13645059", "url": "https://genius.com/13645059", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
