{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "Quick if I blow back, I (Yeah), got it, gone, Rabbit (Oh) Fast, my daddy Rabbit’s at home, what up, pa? (What up?)", "vault_lines": ["Quick if I blow back, I (Yeah), got it, gone, Rabbit (Oh)"], "meaning": "Rabbit was Wayne’s deceased stepfather, who Wayne has said to have considered his real father. Rabbit was murdered before Weezy became a star, and after his death, Wayne went to get “Rabbit” tatted, giving him his first tattoo at only 14. In the next lines he mentions deceased rappers, so “home” means Heaven here, where his father now is.", "annotation_id": "3927018", "url": "https://genius.com/3927018", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "As the streets get colder, I get chillier (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["As the streets get colder, I get chillier (Yeah)"], "meaning": "In this context the streets getting “colder” refer to them getting more dangerous, and when they get more dangerous, so does Wayne (he becomes “chillier”.", "annotation_id": "1576223", "url": "https://genius.com/1576223", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "Sick as a Prozac (Yeah), and Tha Carter I was the (Hah) Dick for you hoes’ trap, and (Ah) this is Tha Carter II and (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Sick as a Prozac (Yeah), and Tha Carter I was the (Hah)"], "meaning": "In this context “ya hoes trap” would refer to some girls mouth. Wayne is stating that if his albums were looked at from a sexual standpoint, Tha Carter would just be seen as foreplay, or would just be considered to get your girl warmed up.", "annotation_id": "309210", "url": "https://genius.com/309210", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "Like, oh, Nancy, the four’s plastic, automatic, I’m (Ow) More drastic, you’re no-names compared to me (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Like, oh, Nancy, the four's plastic, automatic, I'm (Ow)"], "meaning": "Weezy is so popular that almost everyone seems miniscule in comparison, but Wayne said on this exact album (Tha Carter II) that he is the Best Rapper Alive.\n\n\n\nAnother similar line where Wayne shows other rappers no compassion is on Stuntin' Like My Daddy\n\nBitch I’m paid, that’s all I gotta say; Can’t see you lil' niggas, the money in the way", "annotation_id": "309123", "url": "https://genius.com/309123", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "But no coward (Uh-uh) No, I am no Howard the Duck, duck (Baow)", "vault_lines": ["No, I am no Howard the Duck, duck (Baow)"], "meaning": "‘Howard the Duck’ is a movie released in 1986 about a cowardly duck who has to save the world from an alien invader.", "annotation_id": "309103", "url": "https://genius.com/309103", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "My dough tactics is so crafty (Yes)", "vault_lines": ["My dough tactics is so crafty (Yes)"], "meaning": "As a savvy businessman, Lil Wayne and his millionaire father have a whole bunch of different creative ways of gettin that money.", "annotation_id": "246001", "url": "https://genius.com/246001", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "I am Nino fuckin’ Brown and this is Tha Carter, ho (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["I am Nino fuckin' Brown and this is Tha Carter, ho (Woah)"], "meaning": "Nino Brown is a character from the movie New Jack City.\n\n\n\nLil Wayne references this movie all the time, he even had a documentary about himself called The Nino Brown Story.", "annotation_id": "138570", "url": "https://genius.com/138570", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "Hollygrove triggerman, guns in a knapsack, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Hollygrove triggerman, guns in a knapsack, yeah"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is sending a shout-out to his hometown, where he and other artists like Mack Maine grew up.\n\nWayne could also be referring to a song known as Drag Rap- The Showboys, but in this interview Wayne says people from New Olreans always referred to it as “Trigga Man”", "annotation_id": "138568", "url": "https://genius.com/138568", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "I’m fucking your sis, nigga, it’s Weezy (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm fucking your sis, nigga, it's Weezy (Yeah)"], "meaning": "At the time of the ‘Tha Cater II’ (2005), his alias as ‘Weezy’ was still fairly underground (compared to now-a-days)\n\n\n\nThis song certainly added fuel to propel this moniker into the mainstream.", "annotation_id": "85880", "url": "https://genius.com/85880", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "Lead showers (Yeah), black flowers (Yeah) Black dresses (Yeah), two hours (Yeah) Closed casket, uh (Aw)", "vault_lines": ["Lead showers (Yeah), black flowers (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Here Wayne is referring to a funeral. Black is commonly worn at funerals, and if the death is gruesome (which it would be from lead showers) the funeral will have a closed casket, which generally shortens the length of the funeral.", "annotation_id": "20425", "url": "https://genius.com/20425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Weezy Baby", "line": "So ’bout it (Yeah), like Master P (Who?)", "vault_lines": ["So 'bout it (Yeah), like Master P (Who?)"], "meaning": "Referencing the Master P and Cam'ron song “Bout It Bout It”\na fellow New Orleans Rapper.", "annotation_id": "20424", "url": "https://genius.com/20424", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
