{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Don’t", "line": "And even though I be the man with the milli’s When the shit go down, I be the man with the milli’s", "vault_lines": ["And even though I be the man with the milli's"], "meaning": "Wayne is a made man. He’s sitting on millions of dollars; he could hire people to do any dirt he needs or a security team to take care all his issues. But Wayne doesn’t play the game like that. When it’s go time, he handles his own with his 9 millimeter guns.", "annotation_id": "24102415", "url": "https://genius.com/24102415", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Don’t", "line": "Beef cranberry on the ceilin’", "vault_lines": ["Beef cranberry on the ceilin'"], "meaning": "this verse weezy keeps talking about guns and ‘shoot ya in ya head’ and beef cranberry is a metaphor of brains being splattered on the ceiling. as beef like grounded beef and cranberry having the dark colour of red similar to blood.", "annotation_id": "22258745", "url": "https://genius.com/22258745", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Don’t", "line": "I took over the circus ’Cause I’ma act a clown if you put your feet down on my surface I walk around, fo’ pound and surface To spin ya ass around in circles, you urkel", "vault_lines": ["I took over the circus"], "meaning": "Acting a clown is slang for going crazy. Wayne states that he has taken over the building (or the circus) and if you come anywhere near his territory he’ll go crazy and pop off as he keeps his gun on him. He also makes a reference to Steve Urkel off of the show Family Matters. When you get shot you will spin around in the same matter that Family Matters is a spin-off of Perfect Strangers.", "annotation_id": "20439306", "url": "https://genius.com/20439306", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Don’t", "line": "Because of that, mama, I’ll be gone ’till November", "vault_lines": ["Because of that, mama, I'll be gone 'till November"], "meaning": "“Gone ‘Til November” was a song that Wyclef Jean wrote about about a dealer going down south to sell drugs", "annotation_id": "20407898", "url": "https://genius.com/20407898", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Don’t", "line": "Yeah, life’s a bitch and death’s her husband", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, life's a bitch and death's her husband"], "meaning": "Another “life’s a bitch..” line by Weezy. He would later complete the family tree on his song “6 Foot 7 Foot” :\n\nLife is the bitch, and death is her sister\nSleep is the cousin, what a fuckin' family picture. You know Father Time, and we all know Mother Nature", "annotation_id": "3915943", "url": "https://genius.com/3915943", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
