{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Come and See About It", "line": "Yeah, yeah Too hot, too cold I’m, I’m Red hot, blue cold", "vault_lines": ["Red hot, blue cold"], "meaning": "Wayne’s personality is multifaceted and represents the extremes.\n\nWayne’s “hot\"ness represents the fire and passion in his music. His \"cold\"ness represents his calculating, rational side.\n\nAlthough these two poles of Wayne’s identity are opposite, they both imply a threat. He can switch gears without notice, whether he’s red-hot or blue-cold; wild and uncontrollable, or detached and unemotional.", "annotation_id": "6854288", "url": "https://genius.com/6854288", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Come and See About It", "line": "Well you can call me Scrooge Cause I’m swimming in bucks Bitch", "vault_lines": ["Well you can call me Scrooge"], "meaning": "Taking off from the previous reference to ducks, Wayne uses cartoon character Scrooge McDuck to create an image of his wealth based on an idea that’s already familiar to a large portion of the population due to the ongoing presence of variations on this image in popular culture.", "annotation_id": "6854154", "url": "https://genius.com/6854154", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
