{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Been On", "line": "I got the baddest chick in this bitch", "vault_lines": ["And I would take your girl but I got the baddest chick in this bitch"], "meaning": "knowing what this mf did he’s definitely referring to a child here", "annotation_id": "28202404", "url": "https://genius.com/28202404", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Been On", "line": "Italien on my shit", "vault_lines": ["Show niggas how to flip hundreds, Italien on my shit"], "meaning": "It’s no secret that rappers love their Versace, and that’s just what Birdman is wearing here, as is pictured in the song’s music video.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/ETfk-uDd6rY\n\nBirdman is no doubt a huge fan of the expensive clothing line, since he mentions it in some of his other songs, and is frequently seen sporting it.\n\n\n\nOn “Tapout,” he even talks about sleeping on Versace sheets.\n\nMillion dollar pussy, sleepin' on Versace", "annotation_id": "8353733", "url": "https://genius.com/8353733", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Been On", "line": "Okay, I’m getting high in this bitch, I’m O-mas in this bitch", "vault_lines": ["Okay, I'm getting high in this bitch, I'm O-mas in this bitch"], "meaning": "OMAS is an Italian manufacturer of writing instruments, fountain pens, ink and related luxury goods, founded in 1925. Their products are in the upper price range of writing instruments and are still manufactured in their factory located in Bologna Italy. (from Wikipedia)", "annotation_id": "1996519", "url": "https://genius.com/1996519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Been On", "line": "Got so many foreigns, you need a passport to walk in my garage", "vault_lines": ["Got so many foreigns, you need a passport to walk in my garage"], "meaning": "#Foreign Cars\nRich Gang has to many foreign cars in there garage that you need a passport to walk in. It’s one of the perks of being rich and famous. Here are some (not all) of there cars.\n\nBirdman owns a red Buggati Veyron. The Jozef Kaban designed car can go up to 267.856 mph and has a price of 2 million dollars.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&v=jAxSo7HyUek\n\nLil Wayne also owns a Bugatti Veyron – like father, like son. Actually, Birdman has bought most of Lil Wayne’s cars. He gave him a Bentley Mulsanne and an Aston Martin\n\n\n\nMo Money, Mo Problems", "annotation_id": "1995851", "url": "https://genius.com/1995851", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Been On", "line": "G5 for long trips", "vault_lines": ["That tall model is my bitch, G5 for long trips"], "meaning": "A G5 is a type of private jet.\n\n\n\nBirdman’s fellow Rich Gang member, Lil' Wayne, is no stranger to flying in these either.", "annotation_id": "1994314", "url": "https://genius.com/1994314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Been On", "line": "Livin’ on islands, caked up, uh", "vault_lines": ["From them red cups to them gold bottles, livin' on islands, caked up, uh"], "meaning": "For real though, he’s living on his own little island – Stunna Island, once featured in his “Fire Flame” music video.", "annotation_id": "1993631", "url": "https://genius.com/1993631", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
