{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Alright", "line": "And ever since I’m living life every night like it’s ’99", "vault_lines": ["And ever since I'm living life every night like it's '99"], "meaning": "This could mean that he’s living life now where he worries about nothing like he’s still being provided for and taken care of like he’s still young. He uses ‘99 as in 1999 just to rhyme, of which literally he was about 8 years old by then.", "annotation_id": "22715304", "url": "https://genius.com/22715304", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Alright", "line": "Like I’m new here but I’m nuclear, that’s a bomb threat, mothafucka, watch how I blow up", "vault_lines": ["Like I'm new here but I'm nuclear, that's a bomb threat, mothafucka, watch how I blow up"], "meaning": "Euro engages in bomb wordplay.\n“Watch how I blow up” (like a bomb)\n“Watch how I blow up” (Watch as he rises in the industry)", "annotation_id": "21030532", "url": "https://genius.com/21030532", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Alright", "line": "I’m way ahead of my time I think I was only 8 at that time", "vault_lines": ["I'm way ahead of my time I think I was only 8 at that time"], "meaning": "Referring tohe last line, which mentions the year 1999, this suggests that he was born in 1991.\n\nEuro was born in October, 1992; so he was actually 7 in 1999.", "annotation_id": "2846860", "url": "https://genius.com/2846860", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Alright", "line": "We make something out of nothing; what up 5?", "vault_lines": ["We make something out of nothing; what up 5?"], "meaning": "5 is a slang term that began on D5 in the mixtape Lil ‘Wayne called the Birdman of 5 because of its 5 star tattooed.\n\nBirdman is known to be Blood Triple OG. When a Blood calls himself “5\" he is infact reffering to himself as “BLOOD”. Here, Birdman greets another slime", "annotation_id": "2706296", "url": "https://genius.com/2706296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Alright", "line": "But loose lips sink ships, but I just let these hoes Worship", "vault_lines": ["But loose lips sink ships, but I just let these hoes Worship"], "meaning": "Letting your mouth go on about something that you are involved in criminally will eventually bring down the whole enterprise.\n\n\n\nAn ode to one of Wayne’s most famous lines…\n\n“Real G’s move in silence like lasagna”\n\n“Worship” is an obvious homophone for “war ship”.", "annotation_id": "2704464", "url": "https://genius.com/2704464", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Alright", "line": "Audemars and cigars in them new toys", "vault_lines": ["Audemars and cigars in them new toys"], "meaning": "Audemars-Piguet is a luxury brand watch. This isn’t the first time Birdman and Wayne enjoyed this combination", "annotation_id": "2703258", "url": "https://genius.com/2703258", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Alright", "line": "I’m working on that Carter V, I got this bitch in fifth gear", "vault_lines": ["I'm working on that Carter V, I got this bitch in fifth gear"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is working on the 5th (and final) sequence of Tha Carter series, “The Carter V”. It’s release was set for May 5, 2014, and it got pushed back to December 9, 2014.\n\nAs of 2017, Carter V was nowhere to be found. Tensions are higher than even with the beef that has been embroiling with Birdman and Wayne. These issues have led to lawsuits, family breakup, and violence. Finally, Lil Wayne released Carter V on September 28, 2018 after a 4 year hiatus.", "annotation_id": "2703067", "url": "https://genius.com/2703067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Alright", "line": "I’m a young stunna, young Wayne, I’m Young Money", "vault_lines": ["I'm a young stunna, young Wayne, I'm Young Money"], "meaning": "Just like how Lil Wayne was Birdman’s protégé in Cash Money Records (as a young stunna), Euro is being taken under both Birdman’s and Wayne’s wings of the YMCMB crew.", "annotation_id": "2702982", "url": "https://genius.com/2702982", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "We Alright", "line": "She think I’m a window of opportunity, close curtains", "vault_lines": ["She think I'm a window of opportunity, close curtains"], "meaning": "Clever pun by Weezy. By the saying that he’s a window of opportunity Wayne ment thay the girl thought that she had an opportunity to become rich by getting in Waynes wallet, in other words she was a gold diger, but since Wayne compared himself as a window he can close the curtains and “cut that bitch off”.\n\nAlso, by saying close curtains, he’s closing out his verse and/or the entire track altogether, like the end of a play or scene.", "annotation_id": "2702731", "url": "https://genius.com/2702731", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
