{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wayne’s World", "line": "I live it up, get rich or die tryin’ Like 50 Cent, many men (Huh) Wish death upon me, better wish again (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["I live it up, get rich or die tryin'"], "meaning": "Here we find Wayne interpolating the hook of “Many Men (Wish Death)” one of the hit singles of 50 Cent’s debut album:“Get Rich Or Die Tryin” which dropped back in 2003 under Shady/Aftermath the labels of Eminem and Dr. Dre, whom 50 was a protégée.\n\n\n\nIn fact, 50 rapped:“Many men, wish death upon me” at the beginning of the song’s hook.\n\nYou can read all the lyrics of Many Men here on Genius.\nhttps://genius.com/50-cent-many-men-wish-death-lyrics", "annotation_id": "18953217", "url": "https://genius.com/18953217", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
