{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Watch My Shoes", "line": "Before Tommy, Mac, and Nina debate around there, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Before Tommy, Mac, and Nina debate around there, yeah"], "meaning": "Hey, nice gun anthropomorphism!\n\n\n“Tommy” refers to either a Tommy Gun or a Tec-9 pistol\n“Mack” refers to a MAC-11\n“Nina” refers to a 9-millimeter\n\n\n\nIn hip hop slang, a gun firing is sometimes referred to as a gun “talking”. So if these 3 guns “debate”, there will be a lot of “talking” (i.e. shooting) going on", "annotation_id": "18502", "url": "https://genius.com/18502", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Watch My Shoes", "line": "I—I—I do me; no, I do three At a T... I-M-E", "vault_lines": ["I—I—I do me; no, I do three"], "meaning": "“I do me” means that he focuses on improving himself, rather than criticizing others (“You do you, I'mma do me” is a popular self-reliance philosophy among rappers)\n\n“I do 3” could either refer to, um, 3 things:\n\n\nThe 3 I’s on “I do me”\nA threesome (or even foursome, depending on interpretation / how many women Wayne can handle)\nWayne’s album: The Carter III\n\n\n\n“At A T-I-M-E” could also be heard as “at: A-T… I am me”, possibly referencing the hook from  “I’m Me”, a song on his 2007 EP The Leak", "annotation_id": "18499", "url": "https://genius.com/18499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Watch My Shoes", "line": "Smoking on that Bob Marley, listening to Pete Tosh", "vault_lines": ["Smoking on that Bob Marley, listening to Pete Tosh"], "meaning": "Marley and Tosh were both famous Jamaican reggae singers, and members of the Rastafari movement, and hence consumed a lot of marijuana.\n\n\n\nMarley in particular is so known for his smoking weed that Wayne refers to his weed as “Bob Marley”.", "annotation_id": "18497", "url": "https://genius.com/18497", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Watch My Shoes", "line": "We are not the same, I am a Martian, this is Space Jam", "vault_lines": ["We are not the same, I am a Martian, this is Space Jam"], "meaning": "Wayne often refers to himself as a Martian and/or a goblin; since he is obviously not human, he’s trying to find a species where he belongs (he says the same thing in his E.T.-based song “Phone Home”)\n\nSpace Jam was a movie that features, among others, Marvin the Martian\n\n\n\nHe’s saying there is no way you can even remotely compare yourself to him because he is not human. in other words, his flow is so amazing that it isn’t humanly possible to reach that level of awsomeness unless you are immortal, and since he is not a human being, he is the most amazing rapper", "annotation_id": "18488", "url": "https://genius.com/18488", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Watch My Shoes", "line": "You should see my eleven-year-old daughter do they dance I call it the Nae-Nae dance", "vault_lines": ["You should see my eleven-year-old daughter do they dance"], "meaning": "“Nae-Nae” refers to Reginae, Wayne’s first daughter, that he fathered at age 15.\n\n\n\nThe dance she’s doing is the “Crank That” dance (“Superman that ho!”) invented by the aforementioned Soulja Boy and Arab\n\nHe is actually trying to insult Soulja, Arab, and V.I.C. by saying that the dance is so juvenile that his daughter can do it. That’s why he made it a point to throw in her age.", "annotation_id": "18487", "url": "https://genius.com/18487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Watch My Shoes", "line": "Sillier than V.I.C. said, Soulja Boy and Arab", "vault_lines": ["Sillier than V.I.C. said, Soulja Boy and Arab"], "meaning": "Arab, Soulja Boy and V.I.C. – 3 up-and-coming Southern rappers – have a song together called “Get Silly”", "annotation_id": "18484", "url": "https://genius.com/18484", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Watch My Shoes", "line": "What’s the word around this ho? You get served around this ho Yeah, you get served like a fucking hors d’œuvre around this ho", "vault_lines": ["What's the word around this ho? You get served around this ho"], "meaning": "Hors d'oeuvres are fancy bite-sized appetizers. This implies that you will be “served” (out-done) multiple times, piece-by-piece", "annotation_id": "18477", "url": "https://genius.com/18477", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Watch My Shoes", "line": "Syrup got me slow like a turtle ’round this ho", "vault_lines": ["Syrup got me slow like a turtle 'round this ho"], "meaning": "Codeine syrup, aka “purple drank” or “lean”, was one of Wayne’s favorite drugs before he quit it circa October 2009\n\n\n\nDrinking it makes you slow down (contrasted with the “fast food” mentioned above)", "annotation_id": "18475", "url": "https://genius.com/18475", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Watch My Shoes", "line": "And I’m so unfit ’cause all I eat is rappers And these rappers ain’t shit, I like my fast food faster", "vault_lines": ["And I'm so unfit 'cause all I eat is rappers"], "meaning": "Wayne has repeatedly referred to himself as “The Rapper Eater”, meaning that he metaphorically ‘devours’ other rappers in battles\n\nChinese diet philosophy teaches that “you become what you eat”, so by eating bad rappers Wayne is damaging himself!\n\nAlso, Wayne, cut down on fast food! If you are in a rush, become a raw foodist, like Fabolous (better for your skin)", "annotation_id": "18473", "url": "https://genius.com/18473", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Watch My Shoes", "line": "On my Papa Bear shit, need hot porridge", "vault_lines": ["On my Papa Bear shit, need hot porridge"], "meaning": "Wayne is insinuating that he is the “Papa Bear” (patriarch) of rap\n\nIn the “Goldilocks” fairytale, a mischeivious girl breaks into the house of three bears, Papa Bear, Mama Bear, and Baby Bear while the family is away. In one part of the story, Goldilocks samples the porridge of each of the three family members, proclaiming Papa Bear’s to be “too hot”, Mama Bear’s to be “too cold”, and Baby Bear’s to be “just right”", "annotation_id": "18471", "url": "https://genius.com/18471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
