{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Panatela Dutchie", "vault_lines": ["Bugatti, matte black—\"Where they do that at?\""], "meaning": "A Panatela, or Panetela, cigar is a thin, long, and elegant cigar. The length ranges from between 5 to 7 ½ inches\n\nA dutchie is a blunt, in this case, a cigar emptied of tobacco, refilled with marijuana, and re-rolled… like mom’s boyfriend used to do in the kitchen when we were children, before playing Ready-2-Rumble with my brother, sister and I on Nintendo 64", "annotation_id": "33824503", "url": "https://genius.com/33824503", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "I make my girl cum first; then, I arrive later", "vault_lines": ["I make my girl cum first; then, I arrive later"], "meaning": "Lil wayne states he makes his girl cum first them he arrives later the word cum is also a homephone for “come”, hence the ‘arrive later\"  .Cum is an orgasm \\or the fluids that come out one the genitalia  when one ejaculates .In this line he states he makes his girl ejaculate firsts then he ejaculates after her.", "annotation_id": "26886971", "url": "https://genius.com/26886971", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Your flow never wet, like Grandma pussy I’m always good, like Grandma cookies", "vault_lines": ["Your flow never wet, like Grandma pussy"], "meaning": "During a woman’s childbearing years, estrogen helps keep vaginal tissue healthy by secreting vaginal lubrication. This moist environment helps maintain the elasticity of the tissue, the proper pH, and protects the tissues against damage and infection.\n\nAfter menopause, also known as post-menopause, hormone levels drop, decreasing the natural production of lubrication. Since grandmother’s are typically post-menopause, they’re “never wet.”\n\nWayne then parlays this into a clever line about grandma’s cookies, since they’re always tasty.", "annotation_id": "23745481", "url": "https://genius.com/23745481", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "You niggas bet’ not slip—Ice Road Truckers", "vault_lines": ["You niggas bet' not slip—Ice Road Truckers"], "meaning": "Ice road truckers is an american reality television series that premiered on History Channel\nIt features the activities of drivers who operate trucks on seasonal routes crossing frozen lakes and rivers, in remote Arctic territories in Canada and Alaska", "annotation_id": "21960283", "url": "https://genius.com/21960283", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "I’m always strapped—Vietnam, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm always strapped—Vietnam, nigga"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne compares his gun-toting tendencies to that of the soldiers in the Vietnam War.\n\nThe Vietnam War occurred from November 1, 1955, to April 30, 1975, between North Vietnam and South Vietnam, who had backing from the United States military. Soldiers carried around a variety of firearm weapons including rifles and machine guns.", "annotation_id": "18822289", "url": "https://genius.com/18822289", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "She going down like the hands on my time-ticker", "vault_lines": ["She going down like the hands on my time-ticker"], "meaning": "Most clocks measure the forward progression of time; if Wayne’s “time-ticker” is going down, it must represent a count-down of some kind. The fatalistic interpretation would be that his days are numbered, and just as his hours left on the earth are going down, so is a young lady on his genitals.", "annotation_id": "17582308", "url": "https://genius.com/17582308", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "President, got ’em in the White House naked", "vault_lines": ["President, got 'em in the White House naked"], "meaning": "A reference to Bill Clinton and his known sexual relations with intern Monica Lewinsky that occurred inside the West Wing of the White House", "annotation_id": "15778186", "url": "https://genius.com/15778186", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "We are fine, nigga, like Amber Rose", "vault_lines": ["We are fine, nigga, like Amber Rose"], "meaning": "Double entendre here:\n\nNine days before this mixtape officially dropped, Wayne pleaded guilty to charges of felony gun possession and was expected to go to jail. Here he’s reassuring his fans that him and his label, Young Money, are going to be ok or “fine” despite the charges.\n\n\n\nFine can also mean physically attractive; in the second part of the line, Wayne is paying a compliment to model and actress Amber Rose.", "annotation_id": "14957163", "url": "https://genius.com/14957163", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Get a pound, break it down, blow it like trial", "vault_lines": ["Get a pound, break it down, blow it like trial"], "meaning": "Tunechi didn’t feel like going to trial for his gun charges and risk going to jail for a long time, so he just took the plea-bargain and took his 8-month jail sentence like a man. He ‘blew’ trial; exactly what he does with his marijuana.\n\nAdditionally, he juxtaposes breaking down a pound with the word blow following, as if to reference cocaine.", "annotation_id": "2961005", "url": "https://genius.com/2961005", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Too many visions, completed missions", "vault_lines": ["Too many visions, completed missions"], "meaning": "Weezy has too many ideas to carry out, but on the other hand he’s accomplished more than he could have ever imagined. Wayne has one of the biggest discographies in music with almost 200 radio singles as of 2014.", "annotation_id": "2890553", "url": "https://genius.com/2890553", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Young Money, baby, big shit, like a horse ass", "vault_lines": ["Young Money, baby, big shit, like a horse ass"], "meaning": "#Simile:\n\nWayne is comparing Young Money, his record label, to big shit from a horse. He obviously doesn’t mean it in a negative connotation, rather he is stating his label is blowing up and becoming THE shit. His label is getting HUGE!\n\n\n\nWayne loves to shout out his label, and even does it another time on this song:\n\nIt’s Young Money baby, we the fucking greatest\n\nHe also references his label growing past everyones expectations on this song here.", "annotation_id": "2874996", "url": "https://genius.com/2874996", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "I’m laid up, I’m free-throwing Who rebounding? Who gives a shit?", "vault_lines": ["I'm laid up, I'm free-throwing"], "meaning": "Wayne cleverly paints an interesting picture with these two bars.\n\nIn basketball, a free throw is what you receive after the other team fouls. Members from both teams line up on either side of the paint and wait as the shooter takes his shit.\n\nWayne here says this is how every other rapper is whenever Wayne drops a new project. They line up and watch to see what happens when Wayne has the ball. He’s getting his free throw to earn his team (hip hop) a point or two more after the other rappers fouled with whack projects.\n\nA “rebound” is when the ball missed the net and bounces off the backboard, giving the players either a chance to steal the ball or the chance to try to make it again.\n\nWayne asks who is gonna take his place when he eventually fucks up, but then dismisses it with a “Who cares?”, cause he thinks that’ll never happen!", "annotation_id": "1255592", "url": "https://genius.com/1255592", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Oh, she a good girl? I got her transforming", "vault_lines": ["Oh, she a good girl? I got her transforming"], "meaning": "A reference to Chris Brown’s 2009 Lil Wayne-featuring single, “I Can Transform Ya”:\n\nSwizz Swizz on the beat, Chris move ya feet\nAnd Weezy transform a good girl to a freak", "annotation_id": "32954", "url": "https://genius.com/32954", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "It’s going down like the Catalina Wine Mixer", "vault_lines": ["It's going down like the Catalina Wine Mixer"], "meaning": "A double entendre:\n\n\nThe “Catalina Wine Mixer” was an integral part of the 3rd act of the Will Ferrell movie Step Brothers, where the brothers have to fill in for the missing band at the last minute (it’s a helicopter expo in the film, hence “going down”, I guess)\nA “Catalina Wine Mixer” is slang for the sexual act of inserting 3 or more red grapes into the pussy and using your penis to juice the grapes\n\n\n\nHence, because of the wine mixer’s location, it’s “going down”", "annotation_id": "19309", "url": "https://genius.com/19309", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Weezy F. Baby, the “F” is for “Forensics”", "vault_lines": ["Weezy F. Baby, the \"F\" is for \"Forensics\""], "meaning": "Weezy often calls himself “Weezy F Baby” but always changes what the “F” stands for (I’m guessing it’s actually “Francis”)\n\n“F is for Forensics” is a song by underground metal/rock band The Bled; Weezy had it on his mind because the rock band Fall Out Boy (which collaborated with him on Rebirth, his rock album) is deeply influenced by The Bled.\n\nA very little-known definition of Forensics is:  the art or study of argumentative discourse; There are actually many leagues around the country that debate in Dramatic Interpretation or Public Speaking called the Interscholastic Forensics Association.\n\nI’m pretty sure Wayne is talking about the “F” standing for his art of argumentative discourse.", "annotation_id": "19296", "url": "https://genius.com/19296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "South Beach Miami, ho, I’m probably with Tammy To’", "vault_lines": ["South Beach Miami, ho, I'm probably with Tammy To'"], "meaning": "Wayne has abandoned New Orleans, relocating to Miami’s decadent South Beach since Hurricane Katrina in 2005.\n\n\n\nTammy (real name Tammy Torres) is a model he’s friend with (she’s been in several of his music videos){Ex girlfriend now}\n\nShe is a typical “South Beach Girl”: Latin, busty, sexy, low-carb…\n\n\n\nHe might actually say “too”, but makes it sound like “toe” to rhyme with the previous line.\n\nHe eventually said she broke his heart in 6'7'", "annotation_id": "19288", "url": "https://genius.com/19288", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "You niggas Little League, call ’em Curaçao", "vault_lines": ["You niggas Little League, call 'em Curaçao"], "meaning": "Curaçao is a small island off the Venezuelan coast with one of the best Little League baseball teams\n\nLil Wayne is telling other rappers to go “play” with these guys", "annotation_id": "19285", "url": "https://genius.com/19285", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Rockstar lifestyle, might not make it", "vault_lines": ["Rockstar lifestyle, might not make it"], "meaning": "A paraphrase of the opening line of the original “Wasted”", "annotation_id": "18951", "url": "https://genius.com/18951", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "We ball, nigga, like Jalen Rose", "vault_lines": ["We ball, nigga, like Jalen Rose"], "meaning": "Jalen Rose is a retired NBA player who played for 6 teams (the Denver Nuggets, Indiana Pacers, Chicago Bulls, Toronto Raptors, New York Knicks, and the Phoenix Suns) during his 13-year career\n\n\n\nHe’s also said to be “Hip-Hops favourite DJ/basketball player”", "annotation_id": "18922", "url": "https://genius.com/18922", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "New Orleans nigga, I get super-dome", "vault_lines": ["New Orleans nigga, I get super-dome"], "meaning": "The Superdome is the stadium in New Orleans (Wayne’s hometown) that was used by refugees as shelter from Hurricane Katrina\n\n“Getting dome” is also slang for getting a blow job, but he gets really good head (super dome) from none other but his New Orleans girls.\n\n\n\nHere’s the Superdome all lit up for a Saints game and looking considerably like a spaceship to me, maybe it was Waynes idea", "annotation_id": "18851", "url": "https://genius.com/18851", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Bitch, I bring the noise where the lions sleep", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I bring the noise where the lions sleep"], "meaning": "According to The Tokens, the lion sleeps in the jungle, which is a crazy place (much like the ghetto, where Weezy makes a lot of noise.)\n\nIt could refer to the fact that Weezy takes lots of risks (and is in jail for one of them). To take it literally, no one in their right mind would to try to wake up a lion with noise.", "annotation_id": "18848", "url": "https://genius.com/18848", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Wasted", "line": "From start to finish, Usain Wayne", "vault_lines": ["From start to finish, Usain Wayne"], "meaning": "A reference to Jamaican sprinter Usain Bolt, Olympic gold medalist and current holder of the 100 meter and 200 meter world record.\n\nWayne is not as fast with his legs, but is quite swift with his tongue, note the homophone; Usain/ you sayin' Waynes' swift tongue has more than just the one use…", "annotation_id": "18840", "url": "https://genius.com/18840", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
