{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "I hope when we kiss, we make you sick to your stomach", "vault_lines": ["I hope when we kiss, we make you sick to your stomach"], "meaning": "Wayne is referring to when he and Baby kiss each other on the lips and how it might make a homophobe feel ill.", "annotation_id": "23112001", "url": "https://genius.com/23112001", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "The microphone wet ’cause my words like seduction", "vault_lines": ["The microphone wet 'cause my words like seduction"], "meaning": "Wayne’s words are so appealing and seductive that even a microphone, an inanimate object, would be sexually aroused and wet like a woman. What makes this line even more clever is that the microphone may literally be wet because Wayne is spitting. Spitting is another way of saying rapping.", "annotation_id": "17345994", "url": "https://genius.com/17345994", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "Switchin’ up my flows like a nigga do construction", "vault_lines": ["Switchin' up my flows like a nigga do construction"], "meaning": "This line is a double entendre.\n\nWayne switches his rap flows up quite regularly. “Flow” in this line means 2 different things. It means Flow and Floor. A lot of people pronounce floor as “Flo”. Flo and Flow sound the same. So Wayne is saying he switches up his rap flows as a construction worker would switch the floor of a building.", "annotation_id": "17345985", "url": "https://genius.com/17345985", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "Stuntin’ like my daddy", "vault_lines": ["I bought it out like Stunna"], "meaning": "A reference to the Birdman song Stuntin' Like My Daddy\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3EA1gh8XKGk", "annotation_id": "2559293", "url": "https://genius.com/2559293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "My house is a dungeon", "vault_lines": ["My house is a dungeon"], "meaning": "A dungeon from the olden days is a huge castle and sometimes designed to house prisoners. In this context, Lil wayne is basically letting us know that his house is big.", "annotation_id": "646165", "url": "https://genius.com/646165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "Only if I say that she can touch ya like Busta", "vault_lines": ["Only if I say that she can touch ya like Busta"], "meaning": "She needs Wayne’s permission to see someone like you. Also a reference to Busta Rhymes' song “Touch It”", "annotation_id": "475490", "url": "https://genius.com/475490", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "Two girls jump me like Double Dutches", "vault_lines": ["Two girls jump me like Double Dutches"], "meaning": "Double Dutch is a jump rope game where 1 or more people jump as a rope twirls around them. Wayne had a threesome with two girls who eagerly jumped on him.", "annotation_id": "257384", "url": "https://genius.com/257384", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "Explode in a bitch mouth like a Gusher", "vault_lines": ["Explode in a bitch mouth like a Gusher"], "meaning": "Here Wayne is referring to the snack called Fruit Gushers that explode in your mouth.\n\n\n\nFruit Gushers can explode in your mouth  because they have liquid centers.\n\nWhen Wayne is being given oral sex, he cums in the girls mouth, which could be referred to as exploding. He compares his orgasm to Fruit Gushers because receiving oral sex, and eating Fruit Gushers (not at the same time…) can both cause explosions.", "annotation_id": "257381", "url": "https://genius.com/257381", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "Me and my clique be in red like Russia", "vault_lines": ["Me and my clique be in red like Russia"], "meaning": "The color of the Soviet Union(Communist Russia) was red, as displayed on their flag. Wayne likes to rep the Bloods, also known for their red usage.", "annotation_id": "257380", "url": "https://genius.com/257380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "But she might cut ya and burn ya like Usher", "vault_lines": ["But she might cut ya and burn ya like Usher"], "meaning": "The girl that you’re trying to get with might give you an STD. Also a reference to the song “Burn” by Usher.", "annotation_id": "257377", "url": "https://genius.com/257377", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "Stand on my toes, you can call me Paul Bunyan", "vault_lines": ["Stand on my toes, you can call me Paul Bunyan"], "meaning": "Paul Bunyan was a mythical man in folklore who was mighty and unfearing, and Wayne, likewise, isn’t afraid and stands on his feet. Also, a play on the word ‘bunion’ which is a foot condition displayed as bumps in most cases.", "annotation_id": "257373", "url": "https://genius.com/257373", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "line": "Yellow diamond ring lookin’ like a little Funyun", "vault_lines": ["Yellow diamond ring lookin' like a little Funyun"], "meaning": "Funyuns are a brand name of onion rings, so yellow rings.  Gucci Mane later made a song dedicated to this type of jewelry", "annotation_id": "257371", "url": "https://genius.com/257371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Out", "status": "done", "targets": 17, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-walk-it-out-lyrics", "genius_title": "Walk It Out", "genius_id": 28659, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "‘Kay, put lil’ Drew on the map if he walk it off (Taz, what up?)", "vault_lines": ["'Kay, put lil' Drew on the map if he walk it off (Taz, what up?)"], "meaning": "This is likely about Drew ‘Lil Drew’ Correa, a producer whos two biggest hits went on to be Mr. Carter and I Am Not A Human Being, both by Wayne", "annotation_id": "40954773", "url": "https://genius.com/40954773", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "Say, put E.I. on the map if he walk it off", "vault_lines": ["Say, put E.I. on the map if he walk it off"], "meaning": "E.I. is Wayne’s long time road manager, making him a very close friend as they travel everywhere together.", "annotation_id": "40954762", "url": "https://genius.com/40954762", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "Say, put lil’ Fee on the map if he walk it off (Gangsta!", "vault_lines": ["Say, put lil' Fee on the map if he walk it off (Gangsta!"], "meaning": "Fee Banks, childhood friend of Wayne’s, member of Sqad Up and close personal business associate.\n\nHe eventually went on to form a management company and work with younger New Orleans rappers like NBA Youngboy and Kevin Gates.\n\n\n\n\"Rare\" throwback of Weezy and Fee", "annotation_id": "40954721", "url": "https://genius.com/40954721", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "Now, put lil’ Po on the map if he walk it off", "vault_lines": ["Now, put lil' Po on the map if he walk it off"], "meaning": "‘Tez Po’ is about Cortez ‘Tez’ Bryant, who was Wayne’s long time manager, and friend since childhood.\n\nHe usually calls him “Tez”, but on D2 and some earlier songs he calls him “Tez Po”\n\n\n\nThrowback photo of Wayne (left) and Tez (right) during the Sqad Up days\n\n\nAnd my nigga Tez Po been riding with me since pegs", "annotation_id": "40954662", "url": "https://genius.com/40954662", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "Ho, I’m a good-lookin’ rapper, I ain’t lyin’ to you I’m a good-lookin’ rapper, I ain’t lyin’ to you", "vault_lines": ["I'm a good-lookin' rapper, I ain't tryna stunt"], "meaning": "The “Good-Lookin' Rapper” Persona Refrain\n\nThese lines are a direct tribute to Yella Boy from U.N.L.V., serving as a melodic and lyrical interpolation rather than a moment of narcissistic introspection from Wayne.\n\nYella Boy, UNLV, Don’t U Be Greedy:\n\nIm a good lookin' rapper, I ain’t trynna stunt\n\nBy repeating the “good-lookin' rapper” mantra, Wayne is stepping into the persona of the late New Orleans legend to honor the specific swagger of the 3rd Ward. It isn’t about Wayne’s own vanity; it is a calculated nod to the local culture and the artists who laid the foundation for the bounce-heavy sound he is recreating.", "annotation_id": "39738081", "url": "https://genius.com/39738081", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "I can’t forget about my bitch named Eddie Boo", "vault_lines": ["I can't forget about my bitch named Eddie Boo"], "meaning": "Nominal Interpolation\n\n“Walk It Off” is a direct interpolation of a U.N.L.V. track, where Wayne flips the original lyric “Eddie Bow”—which is itself a reference to another U.N.L.V. song—into “Eddie Boo.”\n\nBy stretching the phonetic “E” and “oo” sounds, he recreates the exact cadence of the source material while shifting the reference to a female context. This wordplay allows Wayne to maintain the original bounce of the song.", "annotation_id": "39735876", "url": "https://genius.com/39735876", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "I’m a jalape-nuh boy, hot as", "vault_lines": ["I'm a jalape-nuh boy, hot as"], "meaning": "Wayne is using jalapeño boy as a clever play on his history with the Hot Boys.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GKEEvv-e_QM\n\nBy calling himself a “jalapeño boy” who is “hot as cayenne pepper,” he is signaling that he remains loyal to that original identity and is still succeeding in the same lane as the group that started it all.", "annotation_id": "39735775", "url": "https://genius.com/39735775", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "’Cause it’ll “rat-tat-tat-tat-tat-tat” on them dog hoes It’ll “rat-tat-tat-tat-tat-tat” on them dog hoes", "vault_lines": ["'Cause it'll \"rat-tat-tat-tat-tat-tat\" on them dog hoes"], "meaning": "A nod to the chorus in Wayne’s collab track, “Please Say The Baby” with Mack Maine and Curren$y—off the 2005 mixtape release, Dedication:\n\nRat-tat-tat-tat-ta-tat on you dog hoes\n\nhttps://youtu.be/vF5yPcbbk78?si=Q0x6QkzCoHJAAX8c&t=57", "annotation_id": "35637369", "url": "https://genius.com/35637369", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "I’m a good-lookin’ rapper, I ain’t tryna stunt I’m a good-lookin’ rapper, I ain’t tryna stunt Bitch, I’m a good-lookin’ rapper, I ain’t tryna front I’m a good-lookin’ rapper, I ain’t tryna front", "vault_lines": ["I'm a good-lookin' rapper, I ain't tryna stunt"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne considers himself to be a handsome rapper.\nhttps://i.genius.com/5eaf310f6587c4c9f17a3d1cf38950e674c3a79d?url=https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.gettyimages.com%2Fid%2F85392610%2Fphoto%2Fthe-2006-mtv-vma-forum.jpg%3Fs%3D594x594%26w%3D0%26k%3D20%26c%3DqqHsotm0Q5GcO-mEZ2la_r-3cI4FsX4N_3P6b637Bkk%3D\n\nThis is also a reference to the same lines from former Cash Money Records artists U.N.L.V.’s song “Don’t U Be Greedy” which this song samples. 6 years later, Lil Wayne would say this line again in T.I.’s song “Ball”", "annotation_id": "29230736", "url": "https://genius.com/29230736", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "You might see me in a Bentley painted royal blue", "vault_lines": ["You might see me in a Bentley painted royal blue"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne a.k.a. the Barack Obama of Bugatti, has been whippin' Bentley’s for over 20 years and has an extensive car collection. Lil Wayne in a black Bentley in 2012.", "annotation_id": "19960337", "url": "https://genius.com/19960337", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "Now, put lil’ Spitta on the map if he walk it off (This how it supposed to sound)", "vault_lines": ["Now, put lil' Spitta on the map if he walk it off (This how it supposed to sound)"], "meaning": "Wayne is referring to Curren$y here. At the time of this mixtapes release in 2006\n\n\n\nCurren$y was apart of the Young Money roster but eventually left in 2007 to “do him” and work on his own label, Jet Life Recordings.\n\nCurren$y’s nickname is The Hot Spitta, or simply, just Spitta (even his Twitter name is CurrenSy_Spitta).\n\nTo put someone on the map means to get them recognition, so by Wayne saying he’s gonna put Lil Spitta on the map, it means to give Curren$y recognition.", "annotation_id": "1465287", "url": "https://genius.com/1465287", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "I’m Mr. President, as they say", "vault_lines": ["I'm Mr. President, as they say"], "meaning": "Wayne was the president of Cash Money Records at the time of this song", "annotation_id": "1299746", "url": "https://genius.com/1299746", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "Cayenne pepper", "vault_lines": ["I'm a— (Gangsta!), I'm a— (Gangsta Grillz, you bastards!)"], "meaning": "A cayenne pepper is a very hot pepper, rated from 30,000-50,000 (6th tier) on the Scoville heat units.\n\n\n\nTo be hot in the rap game means to rap well. So if Wayne is hot like a cayenne pepper, then that means he raps really well.", "annotation_id": "97730", "url": "https://genius.com/97730", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk It Off", "line": "Now, put lil’ Mack on the map if he walk it off (Shout-out the East Bank! Shout-out the West Bank!)", "vault_lines": ["Now, put lil' Mack on the map if he walk it off (Shout-out the East Bank! Shout-out the West Bank!)"], "meaning": "Mack Maine, current member of Young Money Entertainment", "annotation_id": "23196", "url": "https://genius.com/23196", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
