{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "Mandarin V", "vault_lines": ["Handlin' streets in the Mandarin V"], "meaning": "A “mandarin V” is most likely referring to an orange-colored Cadillac CTS-V, a sports sedan which was released around the time Tha Carter was made.", "annotation_id": "32899575", "url": "https://genius.com/32899575", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "Hard as Malcolm,", "vault_lines": ["It's Tha Carter, motherfucker, I came back around"], "meaning": "A possible reference to Malcolm X.\n\n“Malcolm X was an African-American Muslim minister and human rights activist who was a prominent figure during the civil rights movement. A spokesman for the Nation of Islam until 1964, he was a vocal advocate for Black empowerment and the promotion of Islam within the Black community.”\n\nHe was also known for his ties with Martin Luther King Jr. aswell as the world heavy weight champion boxer, Muhammed Ali (Cassius Clay).", "annotation_id": "26480673", "url": "https://genius.com/26480673", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "Got Mannie hot with me ’cause I always beat his beat up", "vault_lines": ["Got Mannie hot with me 'cause I always beat his beat up"], "meaning": "Wayne mentions Mannie Fresh, a former affiliate of Cash Money Records. The duo have collaborated countless times up until 2005: Fresh produced hits such as “I Need A Hot Girl” and “Tha Block Is Hot” in addition to the majority of Tha Carter.\n\n\n\nWayne would later replicate the second part of this bar in his single with Cory Gunz, “6 Foot 7 Foot”:\n\nI beat the beat up; call it self-defense", "annotation_id": "15211222", "url": "https://genius.com/15211222", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "But I built this building from the ruts I own all the corners and the cuts in this motherfucker", "vault_lines": ["But I built this building from the ruts"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is the heart of Hollygrove, New Orleans, and at the time he was a drug dealer, it appears that he ruled pretty much the entire area.", "annotation_id": "4565034", "url": "https://genius.com/4565034", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "[Intro]", "vault_lines": ["It's Tha Carter, motherfucker, I came back around"], "meaning": "A young and very hungry Wayne welcomes everybody to the album. He treats it like his house aka “Tha Carter” which was inspired on the empire crack house from the movie “New Jack City” starring Wesley Snipes.\n\nThe album turned out to be one of his most important work as it is generally considered as Wayne’s “break out” album, due to the maturity in both his subject matter, and delivery compared to his first three albums.", "annotation_id": "3916130", "url": "https://genius.com/3916130", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "You do not want angus, USDA prime beef, you’re dead meat", "vault_lines": ["You do not want angus, USDA prime beef, you're dead meat"], "meaning": "Wordplay that connects “beef”, or conflict, with the result of the conflict– death or “dead meat”. Don’t mess with Wayne!\n\n“Angus” cattle (Aberdeen Angus) are a breed of cattle commonly used in beef production, while the USDA stands for “[United States Department of Agriculture](http://www.usda.gov/wps/portal/usda/usdahome", "annotation_id": "3915598", "url": "https://genius.com/3915598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "This is me, fourth solo album, baby, I came back around By myself this time, back off the wall", "vault_lines": ["This is me, fourth solo album, baby, I came back around"], "meaning": "Weezy’s follow-up to his 3rd solo album, 500 Degreez, is also his first album after a slew of collaboration mixtapes with his crew, Sqad Up.", "annotation_id": "2963831", "url": "https://genius.com/2963831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "I’m so ahead of these trendy rappers, speed up I’m already hot when another one startin’ to heat up", "vault_lines": ["I'm so ahead of these trendy rappers, speed up"], "meaning": "When Tha Carter was released, Wayne had been releasing albums for about 8 years. Around this same time, many one-hit wonder rappers (particularly from the south) started popping up who would maybe release a hit single or two and then fade into obscurity after one album (Jibbs, Mims, Dem Franchize Boyz, etc.)\n\n\n\nWayne feels that he has superior to these trend-following rappers and that his music will actually have longevity and go down in Hip Hop history (and now, 10 years after this song’s release, it seems like he was right).", "annotation_id": "2849089", "url": "https://genius.com/2849089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "Yeah, yeah, yeah It’s Tha Carter, motherfucker, I came back around It’s Tha Carter, motherfucker, I came back around It’s Tha Carter, motherfucker, yeah (Hah) I’ma show you all my building, man (Yeah), it’s Tha Carter", "vault_lines": ["It's Tha Carter, motherfucker, I came back around"], "meaning": "This is a reference to New Jack City, Nino Brown’s building in which he manufactured crack was called the Carter.\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to Lil Wayne’s last name and the name of the album in which this song comes from.", "annotation_id": "601034", "url": "https://genius.com/601034", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "Dark as The Falcon,", "vault_lines": ["dark as The Falcon,"], "meaning": "The Falcon is a fictional comic book superhero in comic books published by Marvel Comics, the first Black superhero.", "annotation_id": "384770", "url": "https://genius.com/384770", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "White bitch in the bathroom givin’ head for speed Boy, don’t you turn your head at me The president been doin’ it, then he tried to ruin it", "vault_lines": ["White bitch in the bathroom givin' head for speed"], "meaning": "This is a social criticism because no one would dare think of a precious white woman performing fellatio for drugs in a black owned drug house. Weezy is also saying that he doesn’t want to be judged when worse things happen. He used President Clinton’s White House scandal to try and put things into perspective.  Weezy belives he would have stood up and owned up to his actions, but he sees the President as weak stating “He tried to ruin it” by lying.", "annotation_id": "224077", "url": "https://genius.com/224077", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Walk In", "line": "Any drama, I pace it like Indiana I take your grandma pacemaker and just hand her the piece", "vault_lines": ["Any drama, I pace it like Indiana"], "meaning": "A play on words referencing the NBA basketball team the Indiana Pacers. Also Wayne meant he will take this persons pacemaker, which is keeping her (the grandmother) alive, and just give her the piece meaning gun so she can kill herself.", "annotation_id": "224074", "url": "https://genius.com/224074", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
