{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Waist of a Wasp", "line": "And if Wayne pass you on then he pass you to Mack Maine", "vault_lines": ["And if Wayne pass you on then he pass you to Mack Maine"], "meaning": "Mack Maine is a fellow New Orleans rapper of Weezy’s Young Money label. They have collaborated with each other on several songs. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_AHYewvwPA", "annotation_id": "11916786", "url": "https://genius.com/11916786", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Waist of a Wasp", "line": "And the plaid skirt you got on Lets a nigga know you just might have some class, girl", "vault_lines": ["And the plaid skirt you got on"], "meaning": "Pain makes a play on words regarding the girl’s class. He is calling her classy, relating to her style and sophistication, while playing on the connection to school classes because of her plaid skirt, commonly found on the often-sexualized schoolgirl outfit.", "annotation_id": "11865388", "url": "https://genius.com/11865388", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
