{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Dick in your mouth, fuck what you say", "vault_lines": ["Dick in your mouth, fuck what you say"], "meaning": "As in he is fucking what you say because he has his dick in your mouth", "annotation_id": "31574729", "url": "https://genius.com/31574729", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Car’s so cold, I parked in the house", "vault_lines": ["Car's so cold, I parked in the house"], "meaning": "Car engines are prone to weather damage, such as cold. Cars in this bar can be interpreted as Wayne’s bars, which are so cold he has to keep his car in a warm spot, like the house garage.", "annotation_id": "29292820", "url": "https://genius.com/29292820", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "I took over this rap shit These rappers are just my hostages", "vault_lines": ["I took over this rap shit"], "meaning": "Weezy’s solo career up until 2011 had summoned several top 20 singles as featured artist, three number one albums, and several other high charting albums, EPs, and Mixtapes. A rapper of such caliber is 100% capable of pummeling the competition and completely taking over the rap game. This braggadocious claim of rap being so easy to capture ties back to his hobby of eating rappers:\n\nRappers is what I eat for breakfast", "annotation_id": "29292793", "url": "https://genius.com/29292793", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Her mouth is like my house So I guess you can say I’m coming home", "vault_lines": ["Her mouth is like my house"], "meaning": "Earlier in the verse, Lil Wayne raps:\n\nIf she ain’t fucking, she can exit\n\nThe house is a common place of stay. A home is a tender synonym for house. Taking into consideration the earlier line, Weezy implies she and him are only with each other for sex and that they do it regularly. There is also light wordplay with “coming” (cumming).", "annotation_id": "29292559", "url": "https://genius.com/29292559", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Floating away like a leaf on the lake I’m gone, like delete and erase", "vault_lines": ["Up, up and away"], "meaning": "These lines are a double entendre.\n\n\nThe first is literal, indicating that he is indeed gone, as if he were a leaf on the lake. It can also be interpreted as gone like when graphite is erased from loose-leaf paper.\nThe second one is in the delivery of “gone, like delete and erase,” which can also be heard as “…gone, like the lead in the race.” Weezy is talented, and no rapper can catch up to him, nor can they see him coming like delete and erase.", "annotation_id": "29292514", "url": "https://genius.com/29292514", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Racks on deck, I’m rich as shit", "vault_lines": ["Racks on deck, I'm rich as shit"], "meaning": "He also said in a song that, standing on his money, he’d be 7 feet 8.", "annotation_id": "19544968", "url": "https://genius.com/19544968", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Up, up and away Up, up and away Man, I’m so high I’ll come down in a couple of days Up, up and away (Yeah) Up, up and away (Yeah) Man, I’m so high I’ll come down in a couple of days", "vault_lines": ["Up, up and away"], "meaning": "He also said in ‘No Love’ featuring Eminem that he’d ‘go up up and away’ and ‘come back in beast mode’. There surely is a reference here meant.", "annotation_id": "19544960", "url": "https://genius.com/19544960", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Talk that shit, I walk that shit", "vault_lines": ["Talk that shit, I walk that shit"], "meaning": "Reference to walk it like you talk it", "annotation_id": "19544952", "url": "https://genius.com/19544952", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "I’ll bust in ya face I ain’t got nothing to say", "vault_lines": ["I'll bust in ya face"], "meaning": "Play on words with “bust” and “nuttin” (nothin)", "annotation_id": "15793548", "url": "https://genius.com/15793548", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "40 cal’ with the extended clip", "vault_lines": ["40 cal' with the extended clip"], "meaning": "A reference to the 40 calibre glock. Glocks are common guns for drug dealers as well as gangsters due to their small size making them easier to conceal. An extended clip lets them hold more bullets.", "annotation_id": "11701583", "url": "https://genius.com/11701583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Flow so raw, this beat is pregnant Flow so tight, it’s yeast-infected", "vault_lines": ["Flow so raw, this beat is pregnant"], "meaning": "Wayne compares his music to a vagina (something he dearly loves).\nHis musical flow is so original (raw). Using the slang term raw as an allusion to unprotected sex, he gets the beat pregnant.\nWhen a female’s vagina has a yeast infection, it’s commonly understood that the vagina gets tight. Wayne compares the tightness of his music (how cool it is) to a tight vagina during a yeast infection.", "annotation_id": "11402026", "url": "https://genius.com/11402026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "What’s really good, five? I’m over here, smoking that really good fire", "vault_lines": ["What's really good, five?"], "meaning": "“Five” refers to Birdman, recently (as on D5) shouted out by Wayne as Five Stars. Wayne is asking him what’s up, as for Wayne himself he is smoking that really good kush.", "annotation_id": "3378512", "url": "https://genius.com/3378512", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Up, up and away Up, up and away Up, up, up and away", "vault_lines": ["Up, up and away"], "meaning": "The phrase “Up up and away” could mean various things.\n\n\nWayne could be saying he’s going to smoke weed and get high, or perhaps he is saying he will go away from everything and just chill out.\nWayne could be saying he’s going to go up as in above everyone’s head, and past all the other rappers as he raises higher in the ranks.\nAlso Superman is known to say this phrase:\n\n\n\n\n\nTherefore Wayne could be saying this track will be him eliminating the ones ruining the rap game as he flexes his lyrical prowess by killing this track.", "annotation_id": "3227423", "url": "https://genius.com/3227423", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "I don’t give a Hoover damn", "vault_lines": ["I don't give a Hoover damn"], "meaning": "I don’t give a damn is a common exclamation of disinterest. In this line, Lil Wayne plays-on a reference of the Hoover Dam – a well-known concrete gravity-arch dam on the border of Arizona and Nevada – to further reinforce his disinterest.", "annotation_id": "2568393", "url": "https://genius.com/2568393", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Walking around on my “Fuck it” shit", "vault_lines": ["Walking around on my \"Fuck it\" shit"], "meaning": "Wayne lives life like he doesn’t care, in the next line he talks about how he’s completed everything that he’s wanted to do. He doesn’t care about anything because he has achieved everything he’s ever wanted to, now he’s just having fun.", "annotation_id": "1021991", "url": "https://genius.com/1021991", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Man, I son all these niggas They should have a stupid tan", "vault_lines": ["Man, I son all these niggas"], "meaning": "Wordplay with son/sun. He owns all of these rappers. Also, if he “suns” them, then they would have a dark tan.", "annotation_id": "375314", "url": "https://genius.com/375314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Ha, President Carter Bote for Lil Wayne", "vault_lines": ["Bote for Lil Wayne"], "meaning": "Wayne is running for hip-hop president, I don’t think votes are necessary though. This is also an allusion to the track “President Carter”, also from Tha Carter IV", "annotation_id": "364512", "url": "https://genius.com/364512", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "I’m calling my bitch the shit", "vault_lines": ["I'm calling my bitch the shit"], "meaning": "Like Big Sean in “Marvin & Chardonnay”, Weezy calls his bitch the shit because she’s awesome.", "annotation_id": "364249", "url": "https://genius.com/364249", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Fuck that shit, I’m Superbad", "vault_lines": ["Fuck that shit, I'm Superbad"], "meaning": "A reference to some of the behaviors in the movie Superbad?", "annotation_id": "352926", "url": "https://genius.com/352926", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Leave you looking like lightning struck that nigga", "vault_lines": ["Leave you looking like lightning struck that nigga"], "meaning": "The previous line states that he’s strapped and won’t hesitate to strike you down. If you get struck by lightning, you’re probably laying on the ground half dead.", "annotation_id": "350996", "url": "https://genius.com/350996", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "You’re lucky I don’t kill your ass But you can still get pistol whipped", "vault_lines": ["You're lucky I don't kill your ass"], "meaning": "Hes not going to shoot the girl but he will pistol whip the girl kissing his girl. This might also be a pun referring to Eminem knocking out a bouncer for kissing his girl\n\nThe meaning of the last bitch of the top line could also be “a cowardly person” rather than “a woman”. That would mean that the phrase “pistol whip” would be in its more normal context of hitting someone with their gun", "annotation_id": "346392", "url": "https://genius.com/346392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Money tall, Lisa Leslie", "vault_lines": ["Money tall, Lisa Leslie"], "meaning": "He has stacks of money that are as tall as Lisa Leslie, a 6'5\" former WNBA player.", "annotation_id": "344733", "url": "https://genius.com/344733", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "Sit your five dollar ass down ’Fore I make change", "vault_lines": ["Sit your five dollar ass down"], "meaning": "Quote from Wesley Snipe’s Character in New Jack City:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uk6DAZ5LqaU\n\nWayne is saying that he will break you into pieces, like when you break a bill", "annotation_id": "344669", "url": "https://genius.com/344669", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Up Up and Away", "line": "I done did everything on my bucket list", "vault_lines": ["I done did everything on my bucket list"], "meaning": "Weezy has done everything he wanted to do before he died and he’s only 28. And by saying he’s done everything he’s wanted to do in his life, he’s saying he doesn’t care if he dies. So he lives like one wild-ass reckless motherfucker.", "annotation_id": "344583", "url": "https://genius.com/344583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
