{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Unstoppable", "line": "Ahem, my name is Weezy, I’m almost perfect", "vault_lines": ["Ahem, my name is Weezy, I'm almost perfect"], "meaning": "Ironically enough about five years prior he had said in the intro of his song “This Is The Carter”\n\nOkay, um, finally perfect", "annotation_id": "31913655", "url": "https://genius.com/31913655", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Unstoppable", "line": "I got a condo in Miami and my doormat is always sandy", "vault_lines": ["I got a condo in Miami and my doormat is always sandy"], "meaning": "Wayne has many different houses across the USA, one located in South Beach Miami. While in town, Weezy can usually be found at the beach.", "annotation_id": "18177411", "url": "https://genius.com/18177411", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Unstoppable", "line": "And I run Louisiana, but I’ve never pulled a hammy", "vault_lines": ["And I run Louisiana, but I've never pulled a hammy"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne was born in New Orleans, Louisiana, and since then has obviously managed to have a very successful career in rap music. Because of his success and fame, Wayne helped to put Louisiana on the map music-wise and quickly became one of the city’s biggest musical representations, especially in the hip-hop genre.\n\n\n\nWayne is comparing the way he represents New Orleans, or “runs” it, to the way a runner would injure themselves by pulling a hamstring. Hamstrings are muscles in a person’s legs that can get twisted the wrong way, which would cause pain and render someone temporarily unable to run.", "annotation_id": "17772273", "url": "https://genius.com/17772273", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Unstoppable", "line": "She say I get that pussy wetter than a Dasani shop", "vault_lines": ["She say I get that pussy wetter than a Dasani shop"], "meaning": "Dasani is a brand of bottled water that is owned by the Coca-Cola Company. Dasani is sold in many grocery and retail stores but does not have its own exclusive locations.", "annotation_id": "17772225", "url": "https://genius.com/17772225", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Unstoppable", "line": "Your girl singin’ to my shit, like, “a-la-la-lollipop”", "vault_lines": ["Your girl singin' to my shit, like, \"a-la-la-lollipop\""], "meaning": "This is a reference to Lil Wayne’s 2008 hit single “Lollipop.” The song first hit #1 on the Billboard Hot 100 on May 3, 2008 and spent five non-consecutive weeks in the chart’s top position. The song also helped Wayne’s blockbuster album Tha Carter III become the best-selling album of 2008 and propelled Wayne’s career for years to come.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2IH8tNQAzSs", "annotation_id": "17772165", "url": "https://genius.com/17772165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Unstoppable", "line": "And I belong, right where you see me Ain’t on the fence about it, I ain’t Mr. Feeny", "vault_lines": ["And I belong, right where you see me"], "meaning": "Drake claims that he earned his stardom and is confident that he belongs at the top of the rap game. Being on the fence about something means you struggle to make a decision, as you are torn between two choices. He alludes to the show Boy Meets World, as Mr. George Feeny was a character who frequently talked to his neighbor Cory Matthews over their backyard fence. Drake is clearly a fan of the sitcom, as he even named his 2017 international tour the Boy Meets World Tour.", "annotation_id": "16491257", "url": "https://genius.com/16491257", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Unstoppable", "line": "And I work harder than hard workin’", "vault_lines": ["And I work harder than hard workin'"], "meaning": "Weezy is famous for releasing more free music than most people can digest. In addition to 11 studio albums, 19 official mixtapes, and 192 singles, there are dozens of unofficial mixtapes consisting of verses that effortlessly flow out of Wayne’s brain like lava from a volcano.\n\nThe New York Times even wrote an extensive profile on him and titled it “The Trials of the Hardest-Working Man in Hip-Hop”.\n\nIn a TV interview with Katie Couric, he explained his day-to-day work ethic:\n\nI wake up every day and I go to work, I wake up every night and I go to work, I try not to sleep, When you’re young, you’re obligated to work.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gxKgxnRWWBQ", "annotation_id": "4203013", "url": "https://genius.com/4203013", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Unstoppable", "line": "And I fall in love with girls caught up in superficial glamour Who dress like Sarah Jessica and live like Princess Diana", "vault_lines": ["And I fall in love with girls caught up in superficial glamour"], "meaning": "Drake has a soft spot for girls who live a glamorous lifestyle like the late Princess Di. Drake’s also got an eye for you, if you dress like Sarah Jessica Parker of Sex In The City fame.\n\n\n\nNote how this bar is the opposite of the last where  he describes good things about himself, however in this line he states that he falls in love with materialistic girls, an unneeded trait.", "annotation_id": "1882024", "url": "https://genius.com/1882024", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Unstoppable", "line": "And I got a condo in Atlanta, and I always wear a bandana", "vault_lines": ["And I got a condo in Atlanta, and I always wear a bandana"], "meaning": "Wayne is a known member of the Blood gang so he reps them in Atlanta.", "annotation_id": "230136", "url": "https://genius.com/230136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
