{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Understatement", "line": "Dear I fear, we’re facing a problem You love me no longer, I know it", "vault_lines": ["Dear I fear, we're facing a problem"], "meaning": "Weezy F. starts “Understatement” directly interpolating the opening lines of the song heavily sampled throughout the track, The Cardigans‘ 1996 song “Lovefool.”\n\nThe original opening verse of the Cardigans' song is sampled at the end of “Understatement.” The full verse sung by frontwoman Nina Persson reads:\n\nDear, I fear we’re facing a problem\nYou love me no longer, I know and\nMaybe there is nothing that I can do\nTo make you do\nMama tells me I shouldn’t bother\nThat I ought just to stick to another man\nA man that surely deserves me\nBut I think you do", "annotation_id": "19187069", "url": "https://genius.com/19187069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
