{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "My woman a Queen like Coretta", "vault_lines": ["My woman a Queen like Coretta"], "meaning": "Coretta Scott King was married to Martin Luther King Jr. until his assassination in 1968. Wayne is cleverly referring to her as the female version of her last name.", "annotation_id": "27625328", "url": "https://genius.com/27625328", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "[Outro] Pop! Wait", "vault_lines": ["The instrumental is from U Guessed It by OG Maco. Produced by Brandon Thomas."], "meaning": "The “Pop” is Wayne bookending the track with the same gunshot onomatopoeia he kicked off his verse with.\n\nThe “Wait” is because Wayne doesn’t want you to switch up your music, he’s got another banger coming up for you.\nIt also plays on the Sorry 4 the Wait theme of the album.", "annotation_id": "6780007", "url": "https://genius.com/6780007", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "I get high, meditate like a monk Preposterous when I get drunk", "vault_lines": ["I get high, meditate like a monk"], "meaning": "The most famous Monks are Buddhists, who not only build their temples in high places, they also practice the art of meditation as part of their daily ritual.\n\nWayne uses the double meaning, saying when he gets high, he meditates, because it is his form of religious enlightment.", "annotation_id": "4772709", "url": "https://genius.com/4772709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "I’m sorry for the fucking wait Was busy, searching my calendar for better days I found ’em, you either turn the page or tear the page Y. M., Young Money; never age", "vault_lines": ["I'm Sorry 4 the Wait, apologetic"], "meaning": "This is the 2nd installment of his Sorry 4 The Wait mixtape series. He’s also apologetic fans have to wait for his new album, Tha Carter V. The album was expected to drop back in October of 2014, but issues with Cash Money forced album delays.", "annotation_id": "4770784", "url": "https://genius.com/4770784", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "Now the snow is just coming in Like I broke a window to an igloo", "vault_lines": ["Now the snow is just coming in"], "meaning": "This is a way of saying Wayne’s cocaine is coming in excessive amounts, metaphorically using the term snow because of it’s white color and that it usually comes in large quantities.", "annotation_id": "4763267", "url": "https://genius.com/4763267", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "Her pearl tongue like the pearly gates", "vault_lines": ["Her pearl tongue like the pearly gates"], "meaning": "Her tongue ring amplifies the feeling the blowjob is giving Wayne, making it feel heavenly.", "annotation_id": "4763084", "url": "https://genius.com/4763084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "Riding ’round like Pablo Still talking that blanco", "vault_lines": ["Riding 'round like Pablo"], "meaning": "Favorite subject was P.E – Pablo Escobar\n\nWayne is riding like the most wealthy drug lord, Pablo Escobar, who sold “that blanco” or cocaine. Escobar was regarded as the “King of Cocaine”. His empire was so massive that mostly everyone who was using cocaine in the 1980’s was using his product. By the end of his career, his net worth was 30 billion dollars.\n\nThis also isn’t the first time Wayne has mentioned a famous mobster in his music.", "annotation_id": "4762590", "url": "https://genius.com/4762590", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "Nigga I come with that heroin flow I come with that never before", "vault_lines": ["I come with that heroin flow"], "meaning": "Wayne is comparing his flow to heroin, one of the hardest and addictive drug there is. He’s saying he’s never come with a flow so hard before and that it’ll have you coming back for more.", "annotation_id": "4761188", "url": "https://genius.com/4761188", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "And my goons is wilder than Gronk", "vault_lines": ["And my goons is wilder than Gronk"], "meaning": "“Gronk” is the nickname of Rob Gronkowski, the star tight end for the New England Patriots. He goes wild both on and off the field – he’s known for his partying.", "annotation_id": "4760567", "url": "https://genius.com/4760567", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "My CMB days are dead I ain’t worried ’bout ghost I married the MOB, we divorced Hoo, and all that shit dead without me of course It’s nothing; a zombie, a corpse You burnt yourself and was supposed to pass me the torch Fuck it, I’ll see you in Forbes, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I got my shit right, it's just you and a tissue"], "meaning": "In early December of 2014, Weezy revealed on twitter that Birdman and Cash Money refused to release his anticipated upcoming album, Tha Carter V.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LilTunechi/status/540569858287493120\n\nBecause of Birdman opposing the release of the album, Weezy decided to cut ties with Cash money and has only repped his label, Young Money since.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LilTunechi/status/540570461772345344\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LilTunechi/status/543152195969904640\n\nCash Money is now dead without the star who made them rich, Weezy, and will probably make much less money without him as well.", "annotation_id": "4757190", "url": "https://genius.com/4757190", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "Make him change his name to John Doe", "vault_lines": ["Make him change his name to John Doe"], "meaning": "When a male body is unidentified the name used to refer to the corpse is John Doe, as the actual identity is unknown.\n\nWayne is saying that the body will be left unidentifiable.", "annotation_id": "4757094", "url": "https://genius.com/4757094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "Nigga! I’m sorry for the fucking wait Was busy Racing Ferraris with lil Reginae That’s gangsta You know I always come in second place You hatin’ It’s written all over your fuckin’ –", "vault_lines": ["It's written all over your fuckin' –"], "meaning": "His and hers Ferraris, nigga\nOne for me, one for my daughter, nigga\n\nReginae Carter is Lil Wayne’s daughter. For her 16th birthday, Weezy gave her a Ferrari. Now she’s really stuntin' like her daddy.\n\n\n\nHe makes the statement that he comes in second place not because he’s not winning, but because he’s putting his daughter first.", "annotation_id": "4757064", "url": "https://genius.com/4757064", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Guessed It", "line": "I couldn’t be Junior forever I don’t mean to ruffle your feathers But I had to spread my wings Ain’t trying to get lemon-peppered", "vault_lines": ["I couldn't be Junior forever"], "meaning": "Wayne can’t be Birdman Jr forever, especially after how Cash Money treated him. This might hurt or bother Birdman, thus ruffling his feathers, but he has no other choice.\n\n\n\nAlso, Wayne “flew away” from Birdman because he didn’t want to get killed and cooked like lemon pepper chicken. He probably also doesn’t want Rozay to eat him:\n\nhttps://genius.com/2850222/Rick-ross-thug-cry/Came-from-the-hood-aint-nothing-changed-still-lemon-pepper-on-my-mothafuckin-waaangs", "annotation_id": "4756964", "url": "https://genius.com/4756964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
