{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Gon Love Me", "line": "I shock her like Silk I Chaka like I’m managing a Ludacris", "vault_lines": ["I shock her like Silk"], "meaning": "Here he plays off of “shock her/Chaka” and references Ludacris' former manager and co-founder of Disturbing tha Peace Records, Chaka Zulu.", "annotation_id": "2955929", "url": "https://genius.com/2955929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Gon Love Me", "line": "Then I go and throw a party at Bungalow 8", "vault_lines": ["Then I go and throw a party at Bungalow 8"], "meaning": "Bungalow 8 was a nightclub in New York. It had been known to host celebrities but was eventually closed down after problems with liquor licenses and because they wanted strictly high-profile clientele as opposed to “the unwashed masses”.\n\nWayne’s gives no fucks so after he’s done nutting on your face figuratively and your girlfriend’s face literally he’s going to fly to New York and rent that club out. Actually Wayne is probably the reason that placed closed (jokes)", "annotation_id": "2938408", "url": "https://genius.com/2938408", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Gon Love Me", "line": "Shit make me bust a nut in yo face Tell ya girlfriend, ”Bitch Wipe the slut off yo face, ho”", "vault_lines": ["Shit make me bust a nut in yo face"], "meaning": "Wayne is drawing a connection that his Sig Sauer (which is positioned like his “dick, dawg”) will “bust a nut” or shoot you in the face.\n\n\n\nThen to take that connection and go in a more absurd route, he’s busting a nut in your girlfriend’s face as well, and that the semen he has ejaculated onto her face is what makes her a slut.", "annotation_id": "2938383", "url": "https://genius.com/2938383", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Gon Love Me", "line": "I gotta make it, Lil Layla’s six now My little brother J.E. wanna cop bricks now And little Marley, he just hold his chick down Get ’em a Benz so he can roll his chick round", "vault_lines": ["I gotta make it, Lil Layla's six now"], "meaning": "This is why Wayne wants to rob “the niggas that hate”. Wayne wants to take the money from the rich and in Robin Hood fashion give back to his people, maybe in the form of a Mercedes Benz. His family needs assistance; as Layla is getting older, J.E. wants to be involved in crime, and little Marley is reminiscent of Wayne in that he wants to be involved with the females. His responsibility for them is what drives him to do what he does.", "annotation_id": "2938340", "url": "https://genius.com/2938340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Gon Love Me", "line": "And you could probably get an ounce for eight Shit, if you spend eleven hundred you straight", "vault_lines": ["And you could probably get an ounce for eight"], "meaning": "Referring back to coke being 400 dollars, as the math goes 800 for an ounce now would be a hard bargain; but knowing the market for cocaine as being cutthroat and expensive, you’d be happy to get it for even $1100", "annotation_id": "2938316", "url": "https://genius.com/2938316", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Gon Love Me", "line": "I remember back in the day When an ounce of coke was four hundred", "vault_lines": ["I remember back in the day"], "meaning": "According to this website the average price of a kilo of cocaine is around 25,000 dollars. There are 35.274 ounces in a kilo. That makes the price of an ounce today around 700 dollars.\n\nIn other words: Wayne has been hustling for ages.", "annotation_id": "2938296", "url": "https://genius.com/2938296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Gon Love Me", "line": "Weezy F. Baby I don’t write shit, be on the hype shit", "vault_lines": ["I don't write shit, be on the hype shit"], "meaning": "Weezy has claimed he doesn’t write down his lyrics, that they are all in his head; in The Carter III documentary he states he “leaves no evidence”.\n\nIt has also been claimed by others (Gillie the Kid, et. al.) that he relies on ghostwriters, bringing new meaning to this line.\n\nEither way, Wayne is saying he doesn’t care about writing because he brings energy and excitement to his bars.", "annotation_id": "2938258", "url": "https://genius.com/2938258", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "U Gon Love Me", "line": "I’m so sick I go to the hospital When I don’t get fixed I get nicked by the brain surgeon", "vault_lines": ["I'm so sick I go to the hospital"], "meaning": "Wayne has so much swag he pulls at the hospital\nsimilar to The Notorious B.I.G.:\n\nThe doctor said I need about three weeks of recovery\nBut the nurses is lovin' me\nSayin' the best part of the day is my half\nFeedin' me breakfast and givin' me a sponge bath", "annotation_id": "1262569", "url": "https://genius.com/1262569", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
