{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Typa Way", "line": "You know me dog, so watch what you say (You better watch your mouth!)", "vault_lines": ["You know me dog, so watch what you say (You better watch your mouth!)"], "meaning": "You know T.I.\n\nHe won’t let you say whatever you want to say about him. He will definitely response. T.I.P’s not scared of beef and won’t stop until you stop.\n\nThis could also be a reference to the song “Better Watch What You Saying”, by Rich Homie Quan, who is also the man who did the original version to this song, “Type Of Way”. Both songs on his mixtape “Still Goin In: Reloaded”, which you can download right here.", "annotation_id": "3380435", "url": "https://genius.com/3380435", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Typa Way", "line": "(Hustle Gang my nigga!)", "vault_lines": ["This type of way, know you feel some type of way (Hustle Gang my nigga!)"], "meaning": "His record label.", "annotation_id": "2442463", "url": "https://genius.com/2442463", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Typa Way", "line": "(Bankrolls-R-Us!)", "vault_lines": ["The cash I gettin' make you feel some type of way (Bankrolls-R-Us!)"], "meaning": "Reference to the store Toys “R” Us, except instead of just having toys he has a whole lot of money", "annotation_id": "2249462", "url": "https://genius.com/2249462", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Typa Way", "line": "This shit might cost us our life, but that’s the price we pay", "vault_lines": ["This shit might cost us our life, but that's the price we pay"], "meaning": "As weed has no known negative side effects, he is most likely speaking of Purple Drank (codeine promethazine), which Wayne is known famously for drinking.\n\n Purple Drank slows down your heart rate, and when you drink too much of it, you can die, like the late great Pimp C. Wayne knows this can happen to him too, but this is the price he pays.", "annotation_id": "2194047", "url": "https://genius.com/2194047", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Typa Way", "line": "If you really gon’ be dramatic, we gon’ to need some music, they queuein’ the violin", "vault_lines": ["If you really gon' be dramatic, we gon' to need some music, they queuein' the violin"], "meaning": "T.I. refers to the fact that during sad/dramatic scenes in movies/television a violin plays to set the mood. Basically this is a play on the “world’s smallest violin” idea\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rasZzenuYxI", "annotation_id": "2178059", "url": "https://genius.com/2178059", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Typa Way", "line": "I pop up in that coupe ’bout to go back to the future", "vault_lines": ["I pop up in that coupe 'bout to go back to the future"], "meaning": "Wayne’s coupe is fast like the one in Back To The Future, which was a Delorean/time machine. “‘Bout to go back to the future” meaning he’s about to drive around fast (the car in Back to the Future had to be going 88 mph to go back)", "annotation_id": "2176326", "url": "https://genius.com/2176326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Typa Way", "line": "Monsters in my closet no more closet space", "vault_lines": ["Monsters in my closet no more closet space"], "meaning": "Wayne plays with the phrase “skeletons in my closet”, meaning having secrets from your past hidden away. Instead he’s got “monsters” in his closet, meaning other rappers in the game that describe themselves as “beasts” or “monsters” that he has killed on the track", "annotation_id": "2176144", "url": "https://genius.com/2176144", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Typa Way", "line": "Niggas want to be this fly, too many flights to take", "vault_lines": ["Niggas want to be this fly, too many flights to take"], "meaning": "Wayne is so “fly”, or cool, it’d take a lot for anyone to catch up to him. Play on words with fly and flights\n\nHe mentions how fly he is earlier in the mixtape as well\n\nSince all you nigga’s fly now, bugs all on my windshield", "annotation_id": "2174698", "url": "https://genius.com/2174698", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
