{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "If it’s not bright pink then it’s not my drink", "vault_lines": ["If it's not bright pink then it's not my drink"], "meaning": "Cough syrup (used in combination with soda to create “lean”) turns clear sprite a light pink color when combined. Lil Wayne is saying if color in the cup isn’t bright pink, meaning cough syrup was poured into the soda, then it isn’t his drink. Wayne is seen on many occasions drinking lean.", "annotation_id": "26768081", "url": "https://genius.com/26768081", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "That Nina work for me, that ho can get fired", "vault_lines": ["That Nina work for me, that ho can get fired"], "meaning": "This was one of Tyler the Creator’s favorite Wayne bars from one of his favorite Wayne songs.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jkjlr5lznVY", "annotation_id": "24254978", "url": "https://genius.com/24254978", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Bitch think we dated off a one-and-done", "vault_lines": ["Bitch think we dated off a one-and-done"], "meaning": "This refers not only to a likely “one night stand,” but also is a nod to Tyler Herro’s college playing career at Kentucky, which only lasted one year. When a NCAA player goes to the NBA after one year in college, it is commonly referred to as a “one and done.”", "annotation_id": "24128606", "url": "https://genius.com/24128606", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Upgraded, this ain’t even my final form", "vault_lines": ["Upgraded, this ain't even my final form"], "meaning": "Big Sean, a known fan of the anime series “DragonBall”, uses a DragonBall Z reference. The iconic villain Frieza is essentially a transforming character who wows his opponents through his transformations. While they’re all gasping at his second or third transformation, he laughs and taunts them, saying, “You fool, this isn’t even my final form!” before transforming himself yet again.", "annotation_id": "23035303", "url": "https://genius.com/23035303", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Need that double R when you go rags to riches Need some R&R but now we back to bid’ness, lil’ bitch", "vault_lines": ["Need that double R when you go rags to riches"], "meaning": "Big Sean plays with words that begin with 2 R’s.\n\n Double R which is the Roll’s Royce\n\n\n\nRags & Riches and R&R (Rest & Recuperation -military slang for rest and recuperation, is an acronym used for the free time of a soldier or international UN staff serving in unaccompanied duty stations)", "annotation_id": "21673557", "url": "https://genius.com/21673557", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Boy I goes in like outside was a storm", "vault_lines": ["Boy I goes in like outside was a storm"], "meaning": "Big Sean says he will go in on a song like it was raining outside. Eminem spits similar bars on “These Demons” on the B Side of Music to Be Murdered By.\n\n“Who attempt to diss Hailie (Hailie)\nBitch, I will go in like it’s raining”", "annotation_id": "21660213", "url": "https://genius.com/21660213", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Me and Weezy beat the beat like we Ken and Ryu and shit", "vault_lines": ["Me and Weezy beat the beat like we Ken and Ryu and shit"], "meaning": "Ken and Ryu are the two main characters from the Street Fighter beat-‘em-up video game franchise.\n\n\n\nJust as Ken & Ryu beat up enemies in the video games, Big Sean & Weezy “beat up” or killed the beat that they’re rapping over.", "annotation_id": "21656684", "url": "https://genius.com/21656684", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Everybody 5 like the FUBU company", "vault_lines": ["Everybody 5 like the FUBU company"], "meaning": "‘5’ refers to Wayne’s gang, the Bloods, so he’s saying everyone in his clique is a blood. FUBU is a clothing company known for putting ‘05’ on its clothes.", "annotation_id": "21655091", "url": "https://genius.com/21655091", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Five AKs and they pop, NSYNC", "vault_lines": ["Five AKs and they pop, NSYNC"], "meaning": "NSYNC was a pop group with five members.\nWayne’s saying he will shoot you with five AKs in sync, while making a play on words with NSYNC, which was a pop group with five members.\n\nWayne flipped Jack Harlow’s orignal bar “Five white boys but they not NSYNC”", "annotation_id": "21655017", "url": "https://genius.com/21655017", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "I’m in euphoria with a young thing and she poppin’ like Rue and shit", "vault_lines": ["I'm in euphoria with a young thing and she poppin' like Rue and shit"], "meaning": "Sean is implying he is over the moon with a pretty young thing, while referencing the critically acclaimed HBO series Euphoria and it’s star Rue, who is played by Zendaya.\n\n\n\nPoppin' is likely referring to taking pills, something that Rue is known to do in Euphoria.", "annotation_id": "21654412", "url": "https://genius.com/21654412", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "The ones that hate me the most look just like me You tatted up and say that they GOATs, just like me If I inspired you, that’s so inspirin’", "vault_lines": ["The ones that hate me the most look just like me"], "meaning": "Without a doubt, Lil Wayne is one of the most influential figures in hip-hop culture today. Weezy has been in the spotlight ever since releasing Get It How U Live!! with the Hot Boys in 1997. Nowadays it’s extremely common for rappers to be covered in tattoos and claim they’re the GOAT (Greatest Of All Time).\n\n\n\n“The ones that hate me the most look just like me” is taken straight from Jack Harlow’s chorus in the original “Tyler Herro” song:\n\nThe ones that hate me the most look just like me\nYou tell me what that means", "annotation_id": "21654257", "url": "https://genius.com/21654257", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Only smoke blunts, give the J to wifey Every now and then, I might hit the J like Kyrie", "vault_lines": ["Only smoke blunts, give the J to wifey"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne mostly smokes blunts, which are marijuana-filled cigars, but sometimes he’ll take a puff from his girl’s joint.\n\nWeezy uses his wordplay here on the word “J” which could refer to “Joint” as well as “Jump shot.” NBA player Kyrie Irving has one of the deadliest jumpshots in the league.", "annotation_id": "21654181", "url": "https://genius.com/21654181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Fuck everything that they say about me I done fucked every bad bitch that stay on South Beach", "vault_lines": ["Fuck everything that they say about me"], "meaning": "These lines interpolate two lines from Jack Harlow’s original “Tyler Herro” song:\n\n\nFuck what y'all think\nFuck everything that you say about me\n\nBut one thing they don’t do is play about me\nMy homeboy Tyler, he play in South Beach\n\n\nIn the original, Harlow mentions South Beach because NBA player Tyler Herro plays for the Miami Heat whose arena is located on South Beach. Weezy flips this to say he’s had many sexual experiences in Miami with numerous females.", "annotation_id": "21654130", "url": "https://genius.com/21654130", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Whole bunch of zeros like a new bag of Funyuns", "vault_lines": ["Whole bunch of zeros like a new bag of Funyuns"], "meaning": "When it comes to money, the number of zeros that follow the leading numbers indicates whether it’s hundreds, thousands, millions, billions, etc.\n\n\n\nIn Weezy’s case, he has a ton of zeros. He compares this to a new bag of Funyuns, which is a ring-shaped onion snack by Frito-Lay.", "annotation_id": "21654017", "url": "https://genius.com/21654017", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Just laid a bitch down like Laila Ali", "vault_lines": ["Just laid a bitch down like Laila Ali"], "meaning": "Laila Ali is the daughter of legendary boxer Muhammad Ali. Laila is a former professional boxer who competed from 1999 to 2007. She retired undefeated after 24 total career fights, 21 of which were by knock out.\n\n\n\nWhile Laila’s “laid a bitch down” refers to knocking out an opponent during a fight, Weezy uses the same phrase to refer to sex.", "annotation_id": "21653931", "url": "https://genius.com/21653931", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Tyler Herro, workin’ on my jumper", "vault_lines": ["Tyler Herro, workin' on my jumper"], "meaning": "Tyler Herro, who the original song is named after, is a professional NBA player who currently plays for the Miami Heat. Herro has been heavily scouted since high school due to his ability to constantly shoot and score, averaging 32.9 points during his senior year.\n\n\n\nThis line is similar to what Jack Harlow said in the original track:\n\nMy homeboy Tyler, he play in South Beach\nHe told me this summer he gon' fix my jumper", "annotation_id": "21653823", "url": "https://genius.com/21653823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Five white girls but they not Spice Girls Just some hot girls who like to snort white girl", "vault_lines": ["Five white girls but they not Spice Girls"], "meaning": "The Spice Girls are an English pop group consisting of five white girls (although Scary Spice is actually biracial).\n\nHowever, the females with Weezy are not the Spice Girls. They’re just some girls who like to “snort white,” meaning cocaine.\n\n\n\nThis line is similar to lines used in the original “Tyler Herro” track by Jack Harlow:\n\nI brought a gang to the party with me\nFive white boys, but they not NSYNC", "annotation_id": "21653755", "url": "https://genius.com/21653755", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "I’m in a all black coupe like Dark Knight, girl", "vault_lines": ["I'm in a all black coupe likе Dark Knight, girl"], "meaning": "Weezy is referring to Batman’s vehicle used in the superhero films Batman Begins & The Dark Knight. This specific Batmobile is called the “Tumbler” is an all black military prototype equipped with various weapons and gadgets.\n\nhttps://static.wikia.nocookie.net/batman/images/5/57/Thedarkknight17po4.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20120113141554\n\nAfter Bruce Wayne test drives the Batmobile in Batman Begins, he asks Lucius Fox “Does it come in black?”", "annotation_id": "21653717", "url": "https://genius.com/21653717", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Golf Wang Converse, I’m Lil Tyler Might skate in ’em, might not even rock ’em", "vault_lines": ["Golf Wang Converse, I'm Lil Tyler"], "meaning": "Golf Wang is an American clothing company founded by rapper and producer Tyler, The Creator, who has also established a partnership with footwear brand Converse in order to release a collection of sneakers.\n\n\n\nThroughout the years, Wayne has worked with the California-based artist on several songs, such as The Game’s “Martians Vs Goblins,” as well as Tyler’s own songs “SMUCKERS” and “Droppin' Seeds”.", "annotation_id": "21650962", "url": "https://genius.com/21650962", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Yeah, Young Money so raw, no condom", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, Young Money so raw, no condom"], "meaning": "Young Money Entertainment is Lil Wayne’s record label and includes artists such as Drake, Nicki Minaj, Lil Twist, Cory Gunz and more.\n\nBy raw, Weezy refers to the natural talent of his signees as compared to the growing number of record label-assisted “industry plant” artists. Meanwhile, “hitting it raw” is an expression used to describe unprotected sex, or intercourse without the use of condoms.", "annotation_id": "21650925", "url": "https://genius.com/21650925", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "I need a shero, fuckin’ Wonder Woman", "vault_lines": ["I need a shero, fuckin' Wonder Woman"], "meaning": "Wonder Woman is a heroic character, derived from the DC comics. Diana — her true name — was raised in Themyscira, an island hidden to the rest of the world. Diana grew up to become a superhero under the alias Wonder Woman, teaming up with fellow superheroes like Superman, Batman, and more, and even formed their own superhero team “Justice League”.\n\nBeing one of the few female heroes in the entire universe, Weezy makes a wordplay out of it, calling her a (She)ro instead of a (He)ro. Weezy also could be referencing her fit physique, which is what he might prefer his partner to look like.", "annotation_id": "21649856", "url": "https://genius.com/21649856", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tyler Herro", "line": "Nigga, I don’t fuck with you like Big Sean", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, I don't fuck with you like Big Sean"], "meaning": "Weezy closes his verse and introduces Big Sean by using wordplay to allude to Sean’s September 2014, six-time platinum track “I Don’t Fuck With You.”", "annotation_id": "21640416", "url": "https://genius.com/21640416", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
