{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Twist Made Me (Sure Thing)", "line": "Twist made me do this", "vault_lines": ["Twist made me do this"], "meaning": "Wayne is suggesting his Young Money signee Lil Twist recommended he remix singer Miguel’s 2010 hit “Sure Thing”.", "annotation_id": "30600496", "url": "https://genius.com/30600496", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Twist Made Me (Sure Thing)", "line": "While Miss Anita Baker sing “You Bringing Me Joy”", "vault_lines": ["While Miss Anita Baker sing \"You Bringing Me Joy\""], "meaning": "Wayne is listening to Anita Baker’s “You Bring Me Joy.” He’s a huge fan:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/liltunechi/status/85207531697348608", "annotation_id": "279983", "url": "https://genius.com/279983", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Twist Made Me (Sure Thing)", "line": "Girl, stop talking that shit Go on and suck a nigga dick for a new outfit, hahaha", "vault_lines": ["Girl, stop talking that shit"], "meaning": "Wayne shows his New Orleans roots here as he references one of the oldest chants in the city’s native hip-hop style, bounce music.  See perhaps the earliest recorded use of this phrase in bounce music here, on DJ Jimi’s seminal 1992 song “Where They At”, one of the first bounce tunes ever\n\nThis is hardly the first – or last – time that Wayne, who started out as a gangsta bounce artist on the most important bounce label and working with bounce’s most important producer, has used this chant", "annotation_id": "278421", "url": "https://genius.com/278421", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Twist Made Me (Sure Thing)", "line": "Hit your ass from the side like a screen pass", "vault_lines": ["Hit your ass from the side like a screen pass"], "meaning": "A screen pass is a type of play in American football. During a screen pass, many things are going on at the same time in order to fool the defense into thinking a long pass is being thrown, when in fact the pass is merely a short one thrown sideways, just beyond the defensive linemen.", "annotation_id": "277462", "url": "https://genius.com/277462", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Twist Made Me (Sure Thing)", "line": "Got a chopper and a trimmer, shooting like Jimmer", "vault_lines": ["Got a chopper and a trimmer, shooting like Jimmer"], "meaning": "He shoots guns with deadly accuracy like Jimmer Fredette does on the court.\n\n\n\nLil Wayne actually says he meant he was shooting for the stars just like Jimmer was in an interview on ESPN, but he may have just been trying to keep it clean for all the young fans that watch ESPN…\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&v=LjQUIbO5G9k#", "annotation_id": "277095", "url": "https://genius.com/277095", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
