{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tuxedo", "line": "Shout out the freak ho that I gave the lead role But didn’t deserve b-roll, lowkey had me emo, fuck", "vault_lines": ["Shout out the frеak ho that I gave the lead rolе"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne shouts out the hoe that he made his main girl (lead role which is also knows as a A-roll),\nbut the relationship ends up being over, making him sad, and makes him realize it was only a b-roll, which is the opposite of a lead roll.\nA b-roll supplements an A-roll, weezy uses this to explain that she was just another side piece not a main thang", "annotation_id": "29692826", "url": "https://genius.com/29692826", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tuxedo", "line": "On the d-low, she one, double zero", "vault_lines": ["On the d-low, she one, double zero"], "meaning": "After shouting out the CO that hooked him up with pussy in jail, lil wayne shouts her out with a double entendre, this line means that she gave him pussy on the down low, but also he’s saying she was on his dick on the low on the “d-low”, he finishes the lyric saying she kept it “100”", "annotation_id": "29692752", "url": "https://genius.com/29692752", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tuxedo", "line": "Whippin’ Aquafina ’til it’s Pellegrino", "vault_lines": ["Whippin' Aquafina 'til it's Pellegrino"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne uses water references with the words aquafina and pellegrino to describe him cooking up drugs in the kitchen. When you whip up crack in the kitchen, it sizzles, hence him saying he Aquafina, which is still water, and turns it into Pellegrino, which is sparking water\n\nhttps://www.aquafina.com/en-US/our-products.html#aquafina-bottle\n\nhttps://www.sanpellegrino.com/water/glass-range", "annotation_id": "29692719", "url": "https://genius.com/29692719", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tuxedo", "line": "Countin’ so much money I’ma need a hand massage", "vault_lines": ["Countin' so much money"], "meaning": "Weezy has so much money to count, his hands are tired from counting it and he needs a hand massage because of it.", "annotation_id": "29692685", "url": "https://genius.com/29692685", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tuxedo", "line": "I got a homie who stay in the field on the mound Had a hell of a splitter but now he inside and he totin’ a cutter", "vault_lines": ["I got a homie who stay in the field on the mound"], "meaning": "This is a baseball reference.  The “mountain” on a baseball field is the pitcher’s mound.  The pitcher in this reference (his homie), has a hell of a splitter (type of baseball pitch), but now he’s inside using a cutter (another type of baseball pitch).  This is a double-entendre with “cutter” also meaning “gun” or “weapon”", "annotation_id": "29688546", "url": "https://genius.com/29688546", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tuxedo", "line": "I ain’t a killer but you pushin’ me", "vault_lines": ["I ain't a killer but you pushin' me"], "meaning": "A brief twist on one of the most iconic and legendary starts to a verse or chorus.\n\n[Verse 1: 2Pac]\nI ain’t a killer, but don’t push me\n\nThe above line has been said numerous times by rappers of all generations and types. It is, sometimes, even used as a threat by real gangs.", "annotation_id": "29678414", "url": "https://genius.com/29678414", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tuxedo", "line": "I ain’t a killer but you pushin’ me", "vault_lines": ["I ain't a killer but you pushin' me"], "meaning": "A brief twist on one of the most iconic and legendary starts to a verse or chorus.\n\n[Verse 1: 2Pac]\nI ain’t a killer, but don’t push me\n\nThe above line has been said numerous times by rappers of all generations and types. It is, sometimes, even used as a threat by real gangs.", "annotation_id": "29678349", "url": "https://genius.com/29678349", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tuxedo", "line": "Shout out the C.O. that gave me some pussy in jail", "vault_lines": ["Shout out the C.O. that gave me some pussy in jail"], "meaning": "A C.O. is a prison officer (PO) or bluntly, a corrections officer (CO) responsible for the custody, supervision, safety, and regulation of prisoners.\n\nIn Gone ‘Til November, a handwritten journal by Lil Wayne himself, he recounts a time when two female officers were suspended for coming to see him during his eight-month stint at Rikers in 2010 for gun charges.", "annotation_id": "29678117", "url": "https://genius.com/29678117", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tuxedo", "line": "Came home from jail, they was tryna send me back, nigga I just called my nigga Donald Trump and that was that, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Came home from jail, they was tryna send me back, nigga"], "meaning": "In one of his final acts before leaving the oval office, Donald Trump issued a presidential pardon for Lil Wayne, keeping him out of prison over a firearms charge. Kodak Black was also pardoned the same day.\n\nWeezy was found to be carrying a gun and bullets when police searched a private plane in Miami in December 2019. He faced up to 10 years in prison due to his offending history", "annotation_id": "29667091", "url": "https://genius.com/29667091", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tuxedo", "line": "I ain’t Aaron Rodgers ’cause I’m still on that pack, nigga Still got 12 on my motherfuckin’ back, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I ain't Aaron Rodgers 'cause I'm still on that pack, nigga"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne kicks the song off with some wordplay as he says he’s still consuming a pack of dope while football fans were no longer consuming the play of Aaron Rodgers on the Green Bay Packers as he was traded to the New York Jets in April 2023, several months before this song was released.\n\nWeezy also talks about 12 being on his back with 12 being a nickname for the police, who are watching his every move. After Rodgers joined the Jets, he took 12 off his back in exchange for number 8.", "annotation_id": "29667022", "url": "https://genius.com/29667022", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
