{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tunechi Rollin’", "line": "I’ma do my thing, I put that on Nicki Minaj", "vault_lines": ["I'ma do my thing, I put that on Nicki Minaj"], "meaning": "Wayne gives a shoutout to fellow rapper and Young Money signee Nicki Minaj, who he helped mentor in her earlier years. The two have been open about their mutual appreciation for each other and have been close collaborators since meeting in the late 2000’s, appearing together on songs like “Only,” “High School,” and “I Get Crazy.” Wayne and Nicki have been rumored to have had a romantic relationship but it has never been publicly confirmed.", "annotation_id": "17995011", "url": "https://genius.com/17995011", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tunechi Rollin’", "line": "My Pa is the Birdman", "vault_lines": ["My Pa is the Birdman"], "meaning": "Birdman signed Wayne and took him under his wing (no pun intended) when he was just a teenager.\n\nNaturally, Baby became a father figure to Wayne after being abandoned by his biological father and his step-father passing away.", "annotation_id": "2667644", "url": "https://genius.com/2667644", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tunechi Rollin’", "line": "Mi casa, su casa;", "vault_lines": ["Mi casa, su casa;"], "meaning": "He’s referring to the movie Baby Boy, when P says “Mi casa es su casa, my house is your house” He’s playing on those words by saying “My house is a hoe house”.\n\n\n\nMy house is your house + my house is a hoe house\n∴ You’re a hoe", "annotation_id": "278173", "url": "https://genius.com/278173", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tunechi Rollin’", "line": "Razor blade under tongue", "vault_lines": [", razor blade under tongue"], "meaning": "In the movie “Above The Rim” the character Tupac played kept a blade under his tongue. Just another way of Lil Wayne saying he keeps it gangsta.\n\n\n\nACCEPTED COMMENT: This is also is a transition from the previous line, “T, roll another one[blunt]” Some people use razor blades to cut open blunts.\n\n\n\nHowever, it is interesting to note Tupac does not advise using a blade to cut a blunt. As he says so himself between 1:50-1:60\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=14a3JNCWsO0\n\nya hurr him riiiigh?", "annotation_id": "277900", "url": "https://genius.com/277900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tunechi Rollin’", "line": "Chopper with a drum, motherfucker, give the drummer some", "vault_lines": ["Chopper with a drum, motherfucker, give the drummer some"], "meaning": "In addition to referring to the previous line, this was also an allusion to the single “Can a Drummer get Some” by Travis Barker on which Wayne drops a verse. Also, Travis Barker’s album was titled Give the Drummer Some.", "annotation_id": "277621", "url": "https://genius.com/277621", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tunechi Rollin’", "line": "Wild as Ryu, I hit you with that “Hadouken”", "vault_lines": ["Wild as Ryu, I hit you with that \"Hadouken\""], "meaning": "Like the Street Fighter character Ryu he’ll hit you with his signature move, the Hadouken.", "annotation_id": "276549", "url": "https://genius.com/276549", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tunechi Rollin’", "line": "Polo, fuck that Hilfiger", "vault_lines": ["Only fuck with real niggas, Polo, fuck that Hilfiger"], "meaning": "Polo is much more preppy/stylish than Hilfiger; also could be a reaction to supposed racist remarks made by Tommy Hilfiger..\n\n\n\n“Polo, Fuck that Hilfiger!” is something Pimp C said a LOT, it has become a rallying cry for Pimp C fans.  Wayne said after Pimp died that he always listened to pimp’s instructions and also said he would change his name to Pimp C(arter) to help UGK continue.", "annotation_id": "276533", "url": "https://genius.com/276533", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
