{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "You done bought all of them guns and ain’t nobody dead yet", "vault_lines": ["You done bought all of them guns and ain't nobody dead yet"], "meaning": "The line closely mirrors Future’s lyric, and the suspected song being referenced—Future’s “Sh!t”—was also remixed by Wayne on the/this same mixtape (Sh!t by Lil Wayne).\n\nFuture (Sh!t):\n“Ayy, oh, you done go and get all them guns, and you ain’t killed nobody yet?”", "annotation_id": "38360087", "url": "https://genius.com/38360087", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Menace to society, menace to myself though", "vault_lines": ["Menace to society, menace to myself though"], "meaning": "Menace to Society continues from the last line’s imagery of holding the gun sideways, but also includes the implication of Wayne’s larger impact on culture as a whole.\n\nHe seems to freely accept his position in life, even if that means being villainized by some, and hated on by others.\n\nIn the second half of the line, Wayne relates the outward menace he is to others to the inward menace he is to himself; maybe realizing that his superstar lifestyle has taken a toll on him.", "annotation_id": "7201499", "url": "https://genius.com/7201499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Fuck fast, in slow motion", "vault_lines": ["Fuck fast, in slow motion"], "meaning": "By itself it means very little, but coupled with the other lines about paradoxical conundrums this is a clever play on words referring to the nature of the sex Mack and his girl are having.\n\nAlso a very obvious reference to Cash Money’s Juvenile and Soulja Slim’s number 1 classic New Orleans single “Slow Motion”. Mack Maine then mentions Soulja Slim on the next line.", "annotation_id": "4854626", "url": "https://genius.com/4854626", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Try to throw salt on my name and I’ll put pep in your step", "vault_lines": ["Try to throw salt on my name and I'll put pep in your step"], "meaning": "Salt is known to kill many plants, so by throwing salt on Mack Maine’s name, his enemies are stopping his growth.\n\nHe uses ‘salt and pepper’ to say that he will put ‘pep’ in your step if you try to salt his name, meaning he will slow you down, as pepper spray is a powerful tool to subdue unruly people.\n\nIt also links in with Wayne’s verse on U Guessed It, where he says he doesn’t want to get Lemon Peppered:\n\nhttps://genius.com/4756964/Lil-wayne-u-guessed-it/I-couldnt-be-jr-for-ever-i-dont-mean-to-ruffle-your-feathers-but-i-had-to-spread-my-wings-aint-trying-to-get-lemon-peppered", "annotation_id": "4778107", "url": "https://genius.com/4778107", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "My Chinese chick just want a blunt and some yaka mein", "vault_lines": ["My Chinese chick just want a blunt and some yaka mein"], "meaning": "Yaka Mein “is a type of beef noodle soup commonly found in many Creole and Chinese restaurants in New Orleans”", "annotation_id": "4778099", "url": "https://genius.com/4778099", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "I’m sedated and secluded", "vault_lines": ["I'm sedated and secluded"], "meaning": "As Wayne explores on No Type, he has a weakness for codeine, one of the side effects being sedation.\n\nAnother subtle shot at his label and the clique he mentioned earlier by claiming he is secluded, or on the out with those who he once was cool with.", "annotation_id": "4772810", "url": "https://genius.com/4772810", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Bitch I’m Tommy Gun Tunechi", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I'm Tommy Gun Tunechi"], "meaning": "A ‘tommy’ gun is a Thompson Submachine Gun, and is a popular way of expressing that you own a powerful weapon", "annotation_id": "4772807", "url": "https://genius.com/4772807", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Mama never bought me knockoffs Lord I need some wood to knock on", "vault_lines": ["Mama never bought me knockoffs"], "meaning": "Cortez Bryant said in an interview with XXL ““Wayne came in dressed to the tee: Gucci shoes on, his mom had him clean,””\n\nGucci sneaks were expensive back then, so Wayne’s mom held him down!\n\nTo knock on wood is a saying designed to avoid tempting fate. Wayne doesn’t want to be broke, and doesn’t want to go back to wearing knock offs", "annotation_id": "4772774", "url": "https://genius.com/4772774", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "If I see ’em in the streets I’ma have to treat ’em like a rival", "vault_lines": ["If I see 'em in the streets I'ma have to treat 'em like a rival"], "meaning": "Wayne takes his beef one step further, explaining that Cash Money, the clique he rides for, has disrespected him so much so that if he sees them in the street, he won’t hestiate to treat them like he treats his foes.", "annotation_id": "4772773", "url": "https://genius.com/4772773", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "On that Cognac and that loud pack, that loud pack", "vault_lines": ["On that Cognac and that loud pack, that loud pack"], "meaning": "Weezy’s drinking Cognac and smoking loud. A nickname for top-shelf marijuana.", "annotation_id": "4772693", "url": "https://genius.com/4772693", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Mack the thinker, I’m the Blood - Method Man, Redman", "vault_lines": ["Mack the thinker, I'm the Blood - Method Man, Redman"], "meaning": "The color of blood is red so, noting his affiliation with the Blood gang, it makes sense for Wayne to be Redman. By comparing Mack Maine, the president of Young Money, to Method Man, Wayne states how carefully Mack keeps things organized and gets shit done.\n\nMack Maine is the president of Young Money, so he gotta be the thinking man. Lil Wayne is Young Money, so he runs the whole thing.", "annotation_id": "4762964", "url": "https://genius.com/4762964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "My whole crew’ll skate on you like a hockey team It’s like Wayne Gretzky meets Jeremy Shockey", "vault_lines": ["My whole crew'll skate on you like a hockey team"], "meaning": "Wayne Gretzky is widely regarded as one of the greatest hockey players of all time. Jeremy Shockey, on the other hand, played as a tight end in the NFL.\n\nSince both players specialized in different sports, their playing styles are also different. Mack’s crew is similar – they all bring something unique to the table but can dominate regardless.", "annotation_id": "4762065", "url": "https://genius.com/4762065", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "I’m so sorry for the wait", "vault_lines": ["I'm so sorry for the wait"], "meaning": "This is the 2nd installment of his Sorry 4 The Wait mixtape series. He’s also apologetic fans have to wait for his new album, Tha Carter V. The album was expected to drop back in October of 2014, but issues with Cash Money forced album delays.", "annotation_id": "4761905", "url": "https://genius.com/4761905", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Catch me walkin’ on this mothafuckin’ water, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Catch me walkin' on this mothafuckin' water, nigga"], "meaning": "Wayne is comparing himself to Jesus, who walks on water according to the Bible. By comparing himself to Jesus, Wayne is saying that he is the savior of rap.", "annotation_id": "4761896", "url": "https://genius.com/4761896", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "I’m so fly I shop at Skymall", "vault_lines": ["I'm so fly I shop at Skymall"], "meaning": "SkyMall is a catalogue that is complementary on most flights and produces quarterly issues. It is full of things like 7-foot tall yeti statues and inflatable neck-tie pillows. On January 23, 2015, Skymall’s parent company filed for bankruptcy.", "annotation_id": "4761883", "url": "https://genius.com/4761883", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "When it comes to the drugs, boy we shop at Payless", "vault_lines": ["When it comes to the drugs, boy we shop at Payless"], "meaning": "Payless is a shoe store with a reputation for selling low quality shoes at a cheap price.\n\nEven though Wayne’s drugs are cheap, they are definitely high quality, considering he only smokes the good kush.", "annotation_id": "4761871", "url": "https://genius.com/4761871", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "My bitch in London said she’s a Mack Mainiac And her sister love Tune, she a Wayniac", "vault_lines": ["My bitch in London said she's a Mack Mainiac"], "meaning": "“Wayniac” is a play with Wayne and maniac, and is a term that devoted fans of Wayne use to refer to themselves.", "annotation_id": "4761834", "url": "https://genius.com/4761834", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Point guard with the bullets; you say Rájon, I say Rajon", "vault_lines": ["Point guard with the bullets; you say Rájon, I say Rajon"], "meaning": "In basketball, point guards are generally the quickest and fastest players on the court. Rajon Rondo, PG for the Dallas Mavericks, also excels at passing his teammates the ball – he led the NBA in assists per game in 2011-12 and 2012-13.\n\nWayne hits his enemies with bullets with the same precision that Rondo does when passing to his teammates.", "annotation_id": "4761809", "url": "https://genius.com/4761809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Tha Carter 5 a classic, sorry that it’s late And I ain’t apologetic, but, sorry for the wait Tha Carter 5 a classic, sorry that it’s late And I usually ain’t apologetic, but Sorry 4 The Wait", "vault_lines": ["I'm so sorry for the wait"], "meaning": "This is the 2nd installment of his Sorry 4 The Wait mixtape series. He’s also apologetic fans have to wait for his new album, Tha Carter V. The album was expected to drop back in October of 2014, but issues with Cash Money forced album delays.", "annotation_id": "4760382", "url": "https://genius.com/4760382", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "I’m a fiend for the bread, I want the whole Dej Loaf", "vault_lines": ["I'm a fiend for the bread, I want the whole Dej Loaf"], "meaning": "The instrumental they’re going over is Dej Loaf’s “Try Me.” Loaf is a type of bread, and bread is slang for money. Mack is not satisfied until he gets a lot of it.", "annotation_id": "4760103", "url": "https://genius.com/4760103", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Man I know Soulja proud of me (ya heard me?) Man, I know Soulja Slim proud of me (ya heard me?)", "vault_lines": ["Man I know Soulja proud of me (ya heard me?)"], "meaning": "Soulja Slim, who is also from New Orelans like Wayne and Mack, was a rapper who passed away in 2003. Mack wants to make his predecessor proud.", "annotation_id": "4760084", "url": "https://genius.com/4760084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "Brief moment of silence for Chris Wallace Soulja Slim, Pac, Pimp C, I hope they smilin’", "vault_lines": ["Brief moment of silence for Chris Wallace"], "meaning": "A “moment of silence” is done to show respect for the lost ones. Christopher Wallace (The Notorious B.I.G.), Soulja Slim, 2Pac and Pimp C are all rappers who have passed away.", "annotation_id": "4759854", "url": "https://genius.com/4759854", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "I represent my killers like Johnnie Cochran", "vault_lines": ["I represent my killers like Johnnie Cochran"], "meaning": "Johnnie Cochran is a lawyer, and much like how lawyers represent their clients in court, Wayne represents his killers. Johnnie is also most known for defending OJ Simpson for the murder of his former wife.", "annotation_id": "4757142", "url": "https://genius.com/4757142", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "And Weezy still hot as tamales", "vault_lines": ["And Weezy still hot as tamales"], "meaning": "“Hot Tamales” is a cinnamon candy which can be spicy. Wayne is still spitting hot fire.", "annotation_id": "4757119", "url": "https://genius.com/4757119", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Try Me", "line": "I hold a pistol sideways when I shoot, that’s for style points", "vault_lines": ["I hold a pistol sideways when I shoot, that's for style points"], "meaning": "Holding a gun sideways doesn’t have any practical benefits, and can even make aiming more difficult. The “side grip” was popularized through the opening scene in Menace 2 Society, a sure favorite of any gangster rapper, but Wayne might mess around and shoot himself. Hey, at least it looks cool!", "annotation_id": "4757036", "url": "https://genius.com/4757036", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
