{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trust Nobody", "line": "Two fingers, I keep ‘em crossed, I can’t be lookin’ for peace", "vault_lines": ["Two fingers, I keep 'em crossed, I can't be lookin' for peace"], "meaning": "If you cross your fingers, you can’t make the peace sign, which is made by extending the same two fingers. Also, people cross their fingers when they are lying, and lying would get in the way of looking for peace.", "annotation_id": "18958267", "url": "https://genius.com/18958267", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trust Nobody", "line": "If I die before I wake (Yeah) Pray the Lord, my soul to take (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["If I die before I wake (Yeah)"], "meaning": "“Now I lay me down to sleep” is a children’s Christian bedtime prayer, often used as a lullaby. It traces its roots to Joseph Addison’s 1711 essay, The Spectator, but Adam quotes the second half of the modern version of the prayer, originally published in 1750 by the New England Primer:\n\nNOW I lay me down to sleep,\nI pray the Lord my Soul to keep\nIf I should die before I ‘wake,\nI pray the Lord my Soul to take.", "annotation_id": "18956473", "url": "https://genius.com/18956473", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trust Nobody", "line": "I’ve been lookin’ at the cross and it just look like a “T”", "vault_lines": ["I've been lookin' at the cross and it just look like a \"T\""], "meaning": "Lil Wayne had a similar line on “Let It Fly” from Tha Carter V.\n\n“Take the T off Tunechi and look at it as the crucifix, bitch”", "annotation_id": "18956323", "url": "https://genius.com/18956323", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
