{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trouble Maker", "line": "Shoot you on the front porch And knock you to the backyard", "vault_lines": ["Shoot you on the front porch"], "meaning": "This means he is going to shoot you with a pump action shotgun. Which are well known for the force they exert on it’s receiver. Lil wayne is saying when his bullets hits you it will throw you from your front porch to the backyard. He can also be referring to his punchlines and metaphors, He is letting us know that he got mad punchlines that you can going to be blown away on hearing him spit bars.", "annotation_id": "8562192", "url": "https://genius.com/8562192", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
