{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trouble", "line": "Yeah, yeah, C3, yeah", "vault_lines": ["We eat like dogs"], "meaning": "This line is a reference to Wayne’s 2008 album, Tha Carter III. This track is one of the many songs that were supposed to be on C3 but got leaked early.", "annotation_id": "8209777", "url": "https://genius.com/8209777", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trouble", "line": "The coke smell just like a bunch of coffee beans", "vault_lines": ["The coke smell just like a bunch of coffee beans"], "meaning": "It was common among drug smugglers to hide their stashes in coffee beans during transport. The idea was that the strong smell of roasted coffee beans would throw off any drug-sniffing dog. Also, Cocaine bricks would be hard to intercept if hidden in coffee bags given the large volume of Coffee that is exported from South America.", "annotation_id": "3469039", "url": "https://genius.com/3469039", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trouble", "line": "Represent New Orleans like a fleur-de-lis", "vault_lines": ["Represent New Orleans like a fleur-de-lis"], "meaning": "In the US, the fleur-de-lis symbols tend to be along or near the Mississippi and Missouri rivers. New Orleans is one of the cities that have it in their flag. Following Hurricane Katrina, the fleur-de-lis has been widely used in New Orleans as a symbol of grassroots support for New Orleans' recovery.\n\nWeezy represents his hometown, as if he is a part of its flag.", "annotation_id": "3469023", "url": "https://genius.com/3469023", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trouble", "line": "Cut that tail off the rat He won’t rat no more", "vault_lines": ["Cut that tail off the rat"], "meaning": "He cut a snitch now he won’t snitch anymore.", "annotation_id": "618370", "url": "https://genius.com/618370", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trouble", "line": "Mama loved a drug dealer, straight quit her job", "vault_lines": ["Mama loved a drug dealer, straight quit her job"], "meaning": "He’s talkin' bout' his stepfather Rabbit who was drug dealer", "annotation_id": "171473", "url": "https://genius.com/171473", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trouble", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-trouble-lyrics", "genius_title": "Trouble", "genius_id": 28665, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trippy", "line": "Eyes rolling back, and keep blinking like hazards", "vault_lines": ["Eyes rolling back, and keep blinking like hazards"], "meaning": "Wayne shows himself as being so intoxicated that he feels almost zombie like. His rapidly blinking eyes are compared to hazard lights, making his face seem like it is signaling danger. The line suggests that his body is warning him he has gone too far, and that pushing it any further could become life threatening.", "annotation_id": "29876505", "url": "https://genius.com/29876505", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trippy", "line": "Tunechi", "vault_lines": ["We trippy mayne (Mayne, mayne, mayne, mayne, mayne)"], "meaning": "A nick name Wayne got from his grandma. He actually uses this nickname 25 times on this album.", "annotation_id": "2617547", "url": "https://genius.com/2617547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trippy", "line": "I don’t know if I’m coming or going, T, make my blunt a Samoan", "vault_lines": ["I don't know if I'm coming or going, T, make my blunt a Samoan"], "meaning": "Samoa is a small island country located in the Pacific Ocean. Due to the athletic culture of the country, it basically breeds athletes. For how they are raised and the conditions of the island, most of the Samoans grow to be very big and muscular.\n\nWayne uses this metaphor to illustrate  big how the blunt his buddy, T, is passing him. It has him high to the where he has lost all sense in life, and to the point he does not know left or right, front or back.", "annotation_id": "1615135", "url": "https://genius.com/1615135", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trippy", "line": "Don’t knock me off my high horse, what I do is my choice", "vault_lines": ["Don't knock me off my high horse, what I do is my choice"], "meaning": "When someone is on their high horse, they’re believing that they are superior to others.\n\nWayne doesn’t want to be bothered by haters who are trying to bring him down with their negativity. Wayne knows that’s he’s on top of game, and one of the best of all time.\n\n“High” horse could also be a reference to how high he is, and he doesn’t want people to kill his buzz. It’s his choice to do drugs.", "annotation_id": "1614060", "url": "https://genius.com/1614060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trippy", "line": "I said, ”King me”, king me with my mushroom crown on I graduated to better drugs, my cap and gown on", "vault_lines": ["I said, \"King me\", king me with my mushroom crown on"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne’s playing checkers here: he wants you to king him, and makes a reference to magic mushrooms.  In shrooms the most psychedelic ingredients are contained in the cap.  But he’s moved on from that or graduated to better and higher class drugs – Wayne is notoriously associated with Codeine and Promethezine syrup.\n\nThe phrase “graduated to better drugs” could also be a reference to Eminem’s “Drug Ballad”:\n\nBut I’m all grown up now and upgraded\nAnd graduated to better drugs and updated\n\nThere’s also some wordplay and association with his album covers as well.  When you graduate high school or college you wear a cap and gown, which refers to his album Tha Carter IV’s artwork:", "annotation_id": "1613672", "url": "https://genius.com/1613672", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trippy", "line": "Uh, blue skies, blue skies", "vault_lines": ["Uh, blue skies, blue skies"], "meaning": "“Blue Sky” (also known as Big Blue or Blue Magic) is the street name which has been coined for the notoriously potent and 99.1% chemically pure crystal methamphetamine", "annotation_id": "1612179", "url": "https://genius.com/1612179", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trippy", "line": "Juicy J with the Taylors,", "vault_lines": ["Juicy J with the Taylors,"], "meaning": "Juicy reps Taylor Gang. Wiz Khalifa, Chevy Woods, Lola Monroe, Berner and Tuki Carter are members of the gang.", "annotation_id": "1608767", "url": "https://genius.com/1608767", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trippy", "line": "Weed, pills and that drank, that’s my trippy kit, kit That’s my trippy kit, kit, that’s my trippy kit, kit Weed, pills and that drank, that’s my trippy kit, kit That’s my trippy kit, kit, that’s my trippy kit, kit Weed, pills and that drank, that’s my trippy kit, kit That’s my trippy kit, kit, that’s my trippy kit, kit Weed, pills and that drank, that’s my trippy kit, kit", "vault_lines": ["Weed, pills and that drank, that's my trippy kit, kit"], "meaning": "Juicy J’s hook references his own line on the 2012 Mac Miller song “Lucky Ass Bitch” :\n\nPaper planes rolled up I call them trippy sticks\nWeed, pills, and the drank (coedine)– she with it", "annotation_id": "1605224", "url": "https://genius.com/1605224", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trippy", "line": "I’m stoned, Mick Jagger", "vault_lines": ["I'm stoned, Mick Jagger"], "meaning": "Mick Jagger is the lead vocalist and a founder member of the Rolling Stones. Wayne’s playing on this and the fact that the Stones wrote the script for rock star debauchery (Keef Richards never fucked with the sizzurp though).\n\n\n\nOl' Mick has been enjoying a crazy new lease of popularity in pop culture in recent times. Just goes to show: swagger is timeless.", "annotation_id": "1603759", "url": "https://genius.com/1603759", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
