{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "And then a guard gave me some head, she felt guilty, nigga", "vault_lines": ["And then a guard gave me some head, she felt guilty, nigga"], "meaning": "This is a wordplay on “guilty,” as Wayne is saying the guard felt guilty that he was found guilty of a crime.\n\nAdditionally, by giving Wayne head, the guard literally felt (came into contact with) a guilty person.", "annotation_id": "37452088", "url": "https://genius.com/37452088", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "My bitch dyed her hair red for the set", "vault_lines": ["My bitch dyed her hair red for the set"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying that his girl dyed her hair red for the set (A group of people or gang)\n\nRead more: Set https://rapdictionary.com/meaning/set/)\n\nSpecifically red for the bloods, a street gang in Los Angeles, California, which Wayne is said to be affiliated with\n\nRead more: Bloods\nhttps://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloods", "annotation_id": "29767749", "url": "https://genius.com/29767749", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "Oh yeah, I feel like Neo on both pills", "vault_lines": ["Oh yeah, I feel like Neo on both pills"], "meaning": "Tunechi makes a reference to the matrix", "annotation_id": "14079583", "url": "https://genius.com/14079583", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "Plotting to ride for these niggas and it’s cold in the street", "vault_lines": ["Plotting to ride for these niggas and it's cold in the street"], "meaning": "One of the many reasons why YG is trill(true and real). As  his biggest hit song “My Niggas” also elaborates on this “I said that I’mma ride for my motherfuckin' niggas\nMost likely I’mma die with my finger on the trigger”  , he is loyal to his “niggas” and he would stand by them till the very end in the “cold” (i.e. dangerous) streets", "annotation_id": "11073671", "url": "https://genius.com/11073671", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "I know the stove like I worked at Piccadilly’s, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I know the stove like I worked at Piccadilly's, nigga"], "meaning": "Picadilly’s is a southern based chain of restaurants known for their freshly made baked goods all of which are made on site.\n\nLil Wayne makes it known that he knows how to cook something up, likely he means in the studio; Wayne’s income as made sure that he’ll never have to trap again.", "annotation_id": "11051619", "url": "https://genius.com/11051619", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "I done had a fucked up deal for my four plus years", "vault_lines": ["I done had a fucked up deal for my four plus years"], "meaning": "YG’s been having issues with his record label, Def Jam, just earlier this year. He recently vented out his frustrations after his new mixtape Red Friday leaked two days early, blaming the label for this administrative issue.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/YG/status/801891358508093440\n\nhttps://twitter.com/YG/status/801895028314415104\n\nHe repeated these sentiments a few more times for good measure.", "annotation_id": "11046958", "url": "https://genius.com/11046958", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "And your mama turn tricks and your homies turn state", "vault_lines": ["And your mama turn tricks and your homies turn state"], "meaning": "Creative repetition of the term “turn”, the first use referring to a crime (prostitution) and the second referring to the opposite, betraying your set in order to get time shaved off your sentence. Ironically, the crime committed by the mother isn’t respected any more than the homies' cooperation with the authorities.", "annotation_id": "10980258", "url": "https://genius.com/10980258", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "And my homies turn weight to some cake, for real", "vault_lines": ["And my homies turn weight to some cake, for real"], "meaning": "“Weight” is slang for large amounts of cocaine and cake is not only slang for a kilo of cocaine, it refers to large amounts of money. Cocaine looks like flour, which is an ingredient for cake.  Wayne and his homies are busy whipping soda in the kitchen so they can get money.\n\n\n\nThis line starts a series of references to consumables: cake, oatmeal, pills.", "annotation_id": "10975674", "url": "https://genius.com/10975674", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "I’m from west side California, we the realest state", "vault_lines": ["I'm from west side California, we the realest state"], "meaning": "YG cleverly uses wordplay and a double-entendre. He’s reppin' his home town, Compton, the birthplace for a lot of notable rappers such as himself, Kendrick Lamar, and Dr.Dre.\n\nCompton is also known for having a lot of houses closely cropped together, hence there’s a lot of real estate going on there.", "annotation_id": "10975606", "url": "https://genius.com/10975606", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "I wear a gold rope for old Mississippi niggas", "vault_lines": ["I wear a gold rope for old Mississippi niggas"], "meaning": "During the Civil Rights Era, Mississippi was thesite of several lynchings: racially-motivated hangings. Wayne shows solidarity with those tragically killed by wearing what’s known as a “gold rope chain.” It’s characterised by its yellow colour and thickness. It also signifies that the past injustice against African Americans still weighs heavy on his shoulders, and he carries it with him wherever he goes.", "annotation_id": "10975493", "url": "https://genius.com/10975493", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "I’m ’bout to bounce back on these niggas like Derrick Rose", "vault_lines": ["I'm 'bout to bounce back on these niggas like Derrick Rose"], "meaning": "D Rose has battled injuries his entire career.\nBut he seems to always seems to make his way back to the court.\n\nD Rose joined the New York Knicks in hopes to revitalize his new career. “Bounce back” is therefore also a pun, as you need to bounce a basketball to move it across the court.", "annotation_id": "10973250", "url": "https://genius.com/10973250", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "I’ll feel the holy ghost before I feel these niggas", "vault_lines": ["I'll feel the holy ghost before I feel these niggas"], "meaning": "Wayne will either die before he can relate to his competition, or transcend hip-hop and life itself before he understands them.\n\nThe “Holy Ghost” is the third part of the “Holy Trinity,” usually known as the “Holy Spirit.” The Holy Spirit is without a body, hence the connection to death.", "annotation_id": "10973209", "url": "https://genius.com/10973209", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "And I just walked up in the bank humming ”A Milli”, nigga Whoa, trill nigga just walked in the bank", "vault_lines": ["And I just walked up in the bank humming \"A Milli\", nigga"], "meaning": "Wayne deposits millions in his bank account, whilst humming his classic 2008 track “A Milli.” He’s immediately recognised as “trill” when he enters the bank, likely due to his many deposits and good credit score. “Trill” is pronounced slightly like “chill,” highlighting how familiar this situation is to him.", "annotation_id": "10972977", "url": "https://genius.com/10972977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trill", "line": "I got these bitches on they toes, no Achilles, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I got these bitches on they toes, no Achilles, nigga"], "meaning": "“Stay on your toes” is an idiom that urges you to be aware and “ready to act.” Women follow Wayne around, trying to remain a step ahead of his schedule.\n\nThe Achilles tendon is heavily used when you ascend onto your toes. By dismissing it, Wayne confirms he’s talking about the idiom, not the physical act of being on your toes.\n\n“Achilles” is also a figure in Greek Mythology. Whilst he was impervious everywhere else, his heel was not, hence the term for a perceived weakness is “Achilles.” Wayne does not have a weakness, in rap or for women.", "annotation_id": "10972960", "url": "https://genius.com/10972960", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
