{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "Rest in peace to the game ’cause I’m fresh to death", "vault_lines": ["Rest in peace to the game 'cause I'm fresh to death"], "meaning": "https://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5237520702001", "annotation_id": "1849685", "url": "https://genius.com/1849685", "state": "verified", "votes": -208, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "Bury me in fire and watch me phoenix", "vault_lines": ["Bury me in fire and watch me phoenix"], "meaning": "Possible reference to the ending of the song “Say Valley Maker” by Smog (Bill Callahan):\n\nBury me in fire\nAnd I’m gonna phoenix", "annotation_id": "33247899", "url": "https://genius.com/33247899", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "Hammer in my drawers but I nail your bitch", "vault_lines": ["Hammer in my drawers but I nail your bitch"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION:\n\nThis very well could be a triple entendre. The third meaning is that Tunechi has a hammer inside of the drawers, but instead of using the hammer, he nails your girl himself.", "annotation_id": "15558375", "url": "https://genius.com/15558375", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "These niggas buying Haterade by the twelve pack Like two stomachs", "vault_lines": ["These niggas buying Haterade by the twelve pack"], "meaning": "Haterade is a term meaning excessive negativity and drinking the haterade refers to partaking in critical and negative behaviour. Haterade is a blend of the words hater and Gatorade, Gatorade being a popular sports drink.\nA twelve-pack could either mean 12 bottles or cans of a certain drink, tying into the use of the term haterade, or it could mean two six-packs (two sets of well-developed abdominal muscles). Six-packs are found in between the pelvic bone and ribs, and this area is commonly called the stomach, even though the stomach is actually the name of an organ near this area.", "annotation_id": "22994994", "url": "https://genius.com/22994994", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "I bought me a double-R ’Cause I went from rags to riches", "vault_lines": ["I bought me a double-R"], "meaning": "As there is alliteration in the common phrase “rags to riches,” the double-R also refers to a Rolls Royce, which has two intertwined capital letter R’s in its insignia. After overcoming poverty, Weezy is now able to comfortably spend his money on luxury cars. One of Rolls-Royce’s most popular models, the Wraith, starts at $330,000.", "annotation_id": "22112059", "url": "https://genius.com/22112059", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "I don’t like to dream about gettin’ paid", "vault_lines": ["I don't like to dream about gettin' paid"], "meaning": "possibly a reference to Tha Dogg Pound track “I Don’t Like To Dream About Gettin' Paid” and to the Rakim line, that song was inspired by. Also to Warren G’s “This D.J.”", "annotation_id": "19374174", "url": "https://genius.com/19374174", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "One in ya dome One in ya dome, one in ya dome One in ya dome, one in ya dome One in ya dome, one in ya dome One in ya dome, one in ya dome", "vault_lines": ["One in ya dome"], "meaning": "“Dome” refers to someone’s head. Here, “one” refers to a bullet. Putting “one in your dome” refers to shooting someone in the head. The voice effect used for this part of the hook is very reminiscent of the background to Weezy’s 2008 hit, “A Milli.”", "annotation_id": "13983023", "url": "https://genius.com/13983023", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "And controlling my thoughts is like taming sharks", "vault_lines": ["And controlling my thoughts is like taming sharks"], "meaning": "Wayne’s thoughts aren’t influenced by the own thoughts or actions of others. This continues from the previous line, describing how his thought process is complex.\n\nHis thoughts being determined by other people is a difficult task to accomplish, comparing it to taming a shark. The great white shark is notable for being poor in conditions of captivity, the longest that one was held for only being six and a half months.", "annotation_id": "12894730", "url": "https://genius.com/12894730", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "Rest in peace to the game, tell them kill they self", "vault_lines": ["Rest in peace to the game, tell them kill they self"], "meaning": "RIP to the “rap” game, tell them (them rap game) to kill they self.\n\nMeaning I killed the game cuz im too fresh.", "annotation_id": "1849687", "url": "https://genius.com/1849687", "state": "verified", "votes": -212, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "Got green, New Orleans, St. Patrick, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Got green, New Orleans, St. Patrick, nigga"], "meaning": "Here, we experience a multifaceted play on words from Mr. Carter\n\nGreen refers to Wayne’s weed. He has as much weed around him as you see on Saint Patrick’s Day, a holiday that is celebrated by dressing up in heavily green clothes and accessories.\n\n\n\nNew Orleans comes into affect due to the fact that the city’s football team, the New Orleans Saints, was deemed the the name of the Saints by being founded on All Saints day.\n\n\n\nWayne is also a noted New Orleans native, and has even dubbed himself the New Orleans Nightmare", "annotation_id": "1619242", "url": "https://genius.com/1619242", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "Better turn to God ’fore I turn to Godzilla", "vault_lines": ["Better turn to God 'fore I turn to Godzilla"], "meaning": "This line partially refers to the previous one.\n\nTo try and save your life, you should start praying to survive.\n\n\n\nBecause Wayne is “turning into Godzilla”. By him turning into Godzilla he means he will destroy you and everything around you. Since he will destroy you, you have to pray for any hope of surviving.", "annotation_id": "1609714", "url": "https://genius.com/1609714", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "I like my blunt Nutty Professor", "vault_lines": ["I like my blunt Nutty Professor"], "meaning": "The Nutty Professor is a movie starring Eddie Murphy as a benevolent university professor called Sherman Klump, who is morbidly obese. Wayne likes his blunt (see here for a definition) as big as Sherman Klump", "annotation_id": "1608386", "url": "https://genius.com/1608386", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "You ain’t gon hurt nobody like Kid ’n Play", "vault_lines": ["You ain't gon hurt nobody like Kid 'n Play"], "meaning": "“Ain’t Gonna Hurt Nobody” is a song by rap group Kid ‘n Play\n\n\n\nThey don’t look like they’d hurt a fly", "annotation_id": "1603367", "url": "https://genius.com/1603367", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "And these hoes wanna kick it with me, I’m a sensei", "vault_lines": ["And these hoes wanna kick it with me, I'm a sensei"], "meaning": "To kick it means to chill/hang with someone. Lots of girls want to spend some time with Wayne, but he is way out of their league.\n\n\n\nWayne has used similar wordplay before, albeit in a different context", "annotation_id": "1603036", "url": "https://genius.com/1603036", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "[Verse 3: Soulja Boy]", "vault_lines": ["I ain't lookin' back, nigga"], "meaning": "One of the worst verses of all time.\n\n\n\nFor those of you who don’t have the time or intellectual capacity to read the complexities of Soulja Boy’s rhymes and vocabulary, I have shortened the verse into bite sized, simple phrases:\n\nI killed the game. I’m awesome forever.\nI killed the game. Tell the dead game to kill itself.\nI’m going to kill you because I’m too awesome.\nI’m awesome forever. I’m awesome forever.\nYou don’t have as much money as me. I’m awesome because of my money.\nThe game is dead. By the way, I killed it.\nI’m awesome forever. I’m awesome forever.\nYou’re saying things that I don’t understand. I’m a zombie.", "annotation_id": "1601861", "url": "https://genius.com/1601861", "state": "accepted", "votes": 316, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "line": "Ain’t nothin’ sweet but the codeine, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Ain't nothin' sweet but the codeine, nigga"], "meaning": "Codeine (methylmorphine) is cough/pain relief medication that will leave you leaning if you take enough. Two of the main ingredients in the mixture are the popular soda Sprite, and the sweet candy, Jolly Ranchers – leading to a wonderfully surgery concoction.", "annotation_id": "1601828", "url": "https://genius.com/1601828", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trigger Finger", "status": "done", "targets": 16, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-trigger-finger-lyrics", "genius_title": "Trigger Finger", "genius_id": 131919, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Triggaman", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-triggaman-lyrics", "genius_title": "Triggaman", "genius_id": 387734, "source": "api"}
