{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "That the truth is hard to swallow You got fake juice", "vault_lines": ["That the truth is hard to swallow"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying the truth is uncomfortable: by that time Actavis lean was no longer being made, so many claiming to have it were likely faking. “Fake juice” here literally means the prescription cough syrup isn’t authentic—at best counterfeit, at worst just corn/Karo syrup dressed up to look real—while also calling out a fake image built on pretending to have something that no longer/doesn’t exists.\n\nLil Wayne’s comrade 2 Chainz’s explaining:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o5wFaWTYZIE", "annotation_id": "38359898", "url": "https://genius.com/38359898", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Ooh, my bitch got a rack, Dolly Parton", "vault_lines": ["Ooh, my bitch got a rack, Dolly Parton"], "meaning": "“Rack” means large breasts and a lot of money. Wayne intentionally lets both meanings sit at once.\n\n\n\nDolly Parton is famously associated with an exaggerated bust (which she’s openly joked about), making her a cultural reference for a “rack.”", "annotation_id": "38359784", "url": "https://genius.com/38359784", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "My bitch ain’t got no love handles Boy, I’m clippin’ that toe on that camel", "vault_lines": ["My bitch ain't got no love handles"], "meaning": "Even though Wayne’s bitch doesn’t have love handles, he holds on to her love by clipping on to her camel toe, which is another word for pussy.\nAlso, he does a play on the word ‘clipping’, as it has two meanings: to hold on to something,\nand to cut something off, such as when you ‘clip’ your ‘toe’ nails.", "annotation_id": "17646803", "url": "https://genius.com/17646803", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "I don’t break records, I sets the records", "vault_lines": ["I don't break records, I sets the records"], "meaning": "Wayne is bragging about how he is one who sets the records for others to break.\n\nWayne actually has broken records before.\n\nIn 2011 when he released his Carter IV album, Wayne broke his first Guinness record when he garnered the most Facebook likes in one day with 588,243 in 24 hours.   Sadly for him the record was beaten a year after on the 7th of December 2012 by Barack Obama who made 3,868,253 in a day. Obama still holds this record.\n\nWayne currently holds the record for Most US Hot 100 hits by a rapper. He broke the record on the 30th of April, 2016.  As of December 2017 he has had 129 US Hot 100 hits.", "annotation_id": "13323224", "url": "https://genius.com/13323224", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Got the gas out shootin’ like Jordan", "vault_lines": ["Got the gas out shootin' like Jordan"], "meaning": "Wayne again uses Jordan’s shooting ability to signify his penchant for violence, this time namechecking gas-powered reloading which ties back in with his constant references to AK-47s", "annotation_id": "4772753", "url": "https://genius.com/4772753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Even Slick Rick the ruler know I break rules, ooh", "vault_lines": ["Even Slick Rick the ruler know I break rules, ooh"], "meaning": "Slick Rick is also known as Rick The Ruler. Here, Wayne namechecks him in order to explain that he doesn’t follow the rules, and that even Slick Rick knows and accepts that fact.", "annotation_id": "4772537", "url": "https://genius.com/4772537", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Niggas cooked crack on a Foreman While y’all boys was still sparrin’, uhh", "vault_lines": ["Niggas cooked crack on a Foreman"], "meaning": "Cocaine cooked with baking soda makes crack, and it is a popular method of crack preparation in the hood.\n\nGeorge Foreman is famous for his George Foreman Grill, and Wayne ties it in with the final word ‘sparring’ to complete the boxing analogy", "annotation_id": "4772529", "url": "https://genius.com/4772529", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Young nigga coming back like Jordan", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga coming back like Jordan"], "meaning": "Michael Jordan came back twice from retirement, once from deciding to return after committing to baseball, and the other to raise money for the 9/11 attacks. Wayne compares Jordan’s comebacks to the comeback he is trying to make. As he has appealed to have fallen off. Now, Wayne is prepared to full on comeback.", "annotation_id": "4772495", "url": "https://genius.com/4772495", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "She’s so down with this New World Order", "vault_lines": ["She's so down with this New World Order"], "meaning": "“New World Order” refers to a conspiracy theory orchestrated by a group of extremely powerful people. This is where the Illuminati is joked about. Like a lot of other celebrities, Lil Wayne is said to be in that group. Therefore, it has this girl interested in him.", "annotation_id": "4771809", "url": "https://genius.com/4771809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "So sorry for the wait, I’m sorry", "vault_lines": ["So sorry for the wait, I'm sorry"], "meaning": "This is the 2nd installment of his Sorry 4 The Wait mixtape series. He’s also apologetic fans have to wait for his new album, Tha Carter V. The album was expected to drop back in October of 2014, but issues with Cash Money forced album delays.", "annotation_id": "4769744", "url": "https://genius.com/4769744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Young nigga got guns, good luck Nina Ross say “Me so horny”", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga got guns, good luck"], "meaning": "A reference to the “Me So Horny” scene in the 1987 Vietnam War film, “Full Metal Jacket”. Wayne uses the “Nina Ross” slang throughout this mixtape several times, and it is slang for the 9MM handgun. Wayne’s gun wants some action, and is looking to shoot.", "annotation_id": "4769385", "url": "https://genius.com/4769385", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Going harder than my predecessor", "vault_lines": ["Going harder than my predecessor"], "meaning": "Being the best rapper alive holds a lot of weight. A predecessor is somebody who had a job or position before somebody else. So in all, Lil Wayne is still the shit. This serves as a shot at Birdman, who is the one who brought Weezy into the rap game, attaching him with Cash Money at a young age. Now, Wayne knows he’s going harder than Birdman.\n\n Which really cannot be that difficult…", "annotation_id": "4769340", "url": "https://genius.com/4769340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Yeah, a nigga had to go back in the stash But a nigga ’stache like James Harden", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, a nigga had to go back in the stash"], "meaning": "A “stash” is a secret spot where drugs are hidden, and “stache” is short for mustache. James Harden is an NBA player mainly recognized for his large beard. Therefore, he’s saying his stash (of rhymes) is huge.", "annotation_id": "4764410", "url": "https://genius.com/4764410", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "I knock your head off – Fumble", "vault_lines": ["I knock your head off – Fumble"], "meaning": "In American football, a fumble is when the player carrying the ball drops it, and it is usually caused by another player knocking it out. Wayne knocks off somebody’s head, just like a ball is knocked out of a persons hands.", "annotation_id": "4764387", "url": "https://genius.com/4764387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "House in the hills jumpin’ like Jordan", "vault_lines": ["House in the hills jumpin' like Jordan"], "meaning": "To be “jumping” means to be nice, and stylish. Michael Jordan is known for being Air Jordan, even making a shoe label for it. Wayne compares his houses, and the cops being “jumping” just like Jordan literally jumped, and was named the Jumpman.", "annotation_id": "4764336", "url": "https://genius.com/4764336", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Lil Tunechi coming back like Kobe", "vault_lines": ["Lil Tunechi coming back like Kobe"], "meaning": "Kobe Bryant suffered two major injuries (torn Achilles tendon and fractured tibial plateau) in 2013 that many thought spelled the end of his basketball career.\n\nBryant has since returned to the court, helping the Lakers out in 2014-15 with 22.6 PPG. Just like Kobe, Wayne doesn’t let setbacks deter his career – he’ll always come back.", "annotation_id": "4761310", "url": "https://genius.com/4761310", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Young nigga on the Moon like Warren", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga on the Moon like Warren"], "meaning": "A reference to Warren Moon who was a quarterback for the Houston Oilers in the 80s/90s. Wayne uses wordplay on his name stating he is so high off drugs, he’s up on the moon like Warren.", "annotation_id": "4760191", "url": "https://genius.com/4760191", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Bad bitch with a nice throat She ice cold and she like hoes Ooh, she just my type These other hoes just typos", "vault_lines": ["I got a bad bitch and she foreign"], "meaning": "She knows how to use her mouth, and she’s bisexual; that’s just what Wayne is into. Weezy also cleverly plays with “type” and “typo”. Some girls are the type for Wayne, while others are not of his interest, and are mistakes, just like “typos” are mistakes.", "annotation_id": "4757729", "url": "https://genius.com/4757729", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "My life like Bailey and Barnum’s", "vault_lines": ["My life like Bailey and Barnum's"], "meaning": "The proper name is “Barnum & Bailey”, but Wayne flips them around to fit the rhyme scheme. They combined forces with Ringling Bros. to make up a circus coined “The Greatest Show On Earth.” Wayne’s life is similarly spectacular.", "annotation_id": "4757564", "url": "https://genius.com/4757564", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Young nigga smoke weed like Marley", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga smoke weed like Marley"], "meaning": "Bob Marley is a well known reggae singer who is known a lot for smoking weed, and being very pro-cannabis.", "annotation_id": "4757437", "url": "https://genius.com/4757437", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "I’m mixing weed like gumbo", "vault_lines": ["I'm mixing weed like gumbo"], "meaning": "Gumbo is a dish which is a mixture of many ingredients, with roux, okra, filé powder, meat and/or shellfish, celery, bell pepper. Wayne likes to combine different types of weed when he smokes.\n\n\n\nGumbo is a famous dish in Louisiana, especially in New Orleans (Wayne’s hometown).", "annotation_id": "4757366", "url": "https://genius.com/4757366", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Young Money was my best investment", "vault_lines": ["Young Money was my best investment"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne founded Young Money Entertainment in 2005, his imprint of Cash Money Records. It turned out to be one of his smartest career moves as he birthed the successful careers of raps' biggest stars with Drake and Nicki Minaj.", "annotation_id": "4757309", "url": "https://genius.com/4757309", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Suck this thuggish ruggish bone, swallow that bone marrow", "vault_lines": ["Suck this thuggish ruggish bone, swallow that bone marrow"], "meaning": "Wayne compares his dick to a bone, relating that to the title of Bone Thugs-N-Harmony’s 1994 debut single, “Thuggish Ruggish Bone.” Bone marrow is found inside of bones, and this is Wayne’s way of telling her to swallow his semen.\n\nIt is common for people to suck the bone marrow out of bones after eating a meal, and it is seen by some as being a delicacy.", "annotation_id": "4757039", "url": "https://genius.com/4757039", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "These crooked ass cops still winnin’ Black man family still mournin’ Black President ain’t do nothin’ We need a real nigga up in that office", "vault_lines": ["Black man family still mournin'"], "meaning": "“Crooked cops” refers to dishonest police who murder people without proper cause or provocation, and the families who mourn their loved ones who fall victim to these “crooked-ass cops”.  The “crooked-ass cops” are winning because in Lil Wayne’s eyes, they always get away with murder.\n\nConsidering the time of this song’s release, this is likely a reference to the deaths of Eric Garner and Michael Brown, two black men who were both killed by police in 2014. These two incidences of cop-on-black-male violence caused a big stir in the news and on social media, and, as a result, police brutality was one of the year’s biggest hot-button issues. During this time, ‘black’ President Barack Obama was under pressure to respond to these incidents, thus Wayne shows some dislike for him or his actions during this time.", "annotation_id": "4756902", "url": "https://genius.com/4756902", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "But Tunechi bigger than Elvis Presley", "vault_lines": ["But Tunechi bigger than Elvis Presley"], "meaning": "Wayne likes to brag a lot, but this is a claim he can truly back up. In September 2012, Wayne surpassed Elvis' with the most appearances on the Billboard Hot 100 chart. He really is bigger than Elvis!", "annotation_id": "4756734", "url": "https://genius.com/4756734", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "Ooh! Yeah Lil Tunechi got it jumpin’ like Jordan These pussy ass niggas can’t guard me These rookie ass niggas still crawlin’", "vault_lines": ["Like \"ooh\" bedroom jumpin' like Jordan"], "meaning": "Michael Jordan is one of basketball’s biggest legends most notable for his impeccable jumping shot. Weezy is too fierce for any competition.\n\n\n\nJordan was notorious for trash talking to opponents on the court. Many players have told stories about him saying a variant of “You can’t guard me.”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wszhB7bQgnM\n\n“Rookie[s] still crawling” may refer to the younger rappers in the game, many of which started in their teens, which is not to far from “crawling” like a baby would. Fun fact: Weezy himself was only a teenager at the start of his career, joining the rap group Hot Boys at age 15.", "annotation_id": "4756699", "url": "https://genius.com/4756699", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trap House", "line": "I got bitches that’ll kill for me – Charles Manson", "vault_lines": ["I got bitches that'll kill for me – Charles Manson"], "meaning": "Simile in reference to Charles Manson, a serial killer who recruited people to his cult-like “family” and tasked them with murders, many of them being women.\n\nIn the way that these women would literally murder people for Manson, Weezy has girls so in love with him they would sacrifice anything for him. Additionally, Charles Manson is known for his proficiency in bed. He was said to be able to have sex nonstop all day long.", "annotation_id": "4756512", "url": "https://genius.com/4756512", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
