{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Trance", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lloyd-trance-lyrics", "genius_title": "Trance", "genius_id": 32919, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "Hallelujah, Hollygrove Hallelujah, Hollygrove", "vault_lines": ["How many times the merry-go-round goes around?"], "meaning": "Hollygrove is the neighbourhood of New Orleans in which Lil Wayne was born and raised. It was heavily damaged after Hurricane Katrina and the subsequent wake of government negligence.\n\nNot too long before the release of this song, Wayne dropped a collab album with 2 Chainz, called Collegrove, which combines Wayne’s home (Hollygrove) and 2 Chainz' home (College Park).\n\nThis lyric is similar to one on Kendrick Lamar’s “Money Trees”:\n\nIt go Halle Berry or hallelujah", "annotation_id": "10191173", "url": "https://genius.com/10191173", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "9 a.m. clockin’, 4 a.m. water whippin’", "vault_lines": ["9 a.m. clockin', 4 a.m. water whippin'"], "meaning": "“Water whippin'” is another name for cooking crack, which requires you to constantly stir a mixture of cocaine and baking soda in a pot of water.\n\nSince Travis isn’t known for dealing drugs, it’s likely this is a metaphor for him staying up late to cook up dope music.", "annotation_id": "10181166", "url": "https://genius.com/10181166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "Khaled, fuck with your boy", "vault_lines": ["Khaled, fuck with your boy"], "meaning": "DJ Khaled and Wayne have been homies since 2006 when Weezy was featured on Khaled’s first album. Wayne has never missed an appearance on Khaled’s albums since.", "annotation_id": "10175260", "url": "https://genius.com/10175260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "I pull out like skrrt in New Orleans I pull up her skirt and get gnarly", "vault_lines": ["I pull out like skrrt in New Orleans"], "meaning": "Wayne’s persona has evolved from being a thug to being a skater-dude since he left his home town New Orleans. A commonly used phrase among skaters and surfers is gnarly, which means extreme/radical, in either a positive or negative way.\n\nWayne also uses a homophone: skrrt (the sound someone makes when they pull out) and skirt.", "annotation_id": "10172699", "url": "https://genius.com/10172699", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "La Flame killin’ you niggas, damn, I’m sorry (Damn, I’m sorry)", "vault_lines": ["La Flame killin' you niggas, damn, I'm sorry (Damn, I'm sorry)"], "meaning": "La Flame is one of Travis Scott’s main aliases. He began using it early in his career and still uses it throughout his newer projects.\n\nKilling it refers to having great success. In 2015, Travis’s debut album Rodeo was met with positive critical reviews and solid sales, and its single “Antidote” went platinum.", "annotation_id": "10170345", "url": "https://genius.com/10170345", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "Moolah", "vault_lines": ["How many times the merry-go-round goes around?"], "meaning": "One of Wayne’s signature ad-libs, “moolah” means money, as in Young Money Entertainment, the label he founded.", "annotation_id": "10169598", "url": "https://genius.com/10169598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "That’s not my kid, call up my nigga Maury (Call up Maury) Drinkin’, drivin’, but I wore a condom, man I’m stickin’ to that story (Damn, damn)", "vault_lines": ["That's not my kid, call up my nigga Maury (Call up Maury)"], "meaning": "Maury is a popular daytime TV talk show. Maury Povich, the host of the show, offers people the opportunity to take a DNA paternity test to determine who the father of a child may be. The phrase, “You are NOT the father!” is frequently used on the show.\n\n\n\nTravis is telling the girl that isn’t his kid because he wore a condom when they had sex. He is so confident about it that he’ll go on Maury’s show to prove it.", "annotation_id": "10169264", "url": "https://genius.com/10169264", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "The weed got her lightheaded, red eyes I told her, “Don’t worry, we stay high”", "vault_lines": ["The weed got her lightheaded, red eyes"], "meaning": "Wayne is describing some of the common side effects of smoking marijuana; lightheadedness, red eyes, and paranoia. It’s all part of the lifestyle Wayne is introducing the girl too.", "annotation_id": "10167789", "url": "https://genius.com/10167789", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "We The Best Music", "vault_lines": ["How many times the merry-go-round goes around?"], "meaning": "DJ Khaled shouts out his record label, We the Best Music Group, as he does on many of his records.", "annotation_id": "10167586", "url": "https://genius.com/10167586", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "Wayne’s world – “Party time, excellent”", "vault_lines": ["Wayne's world – \"Party time, excellent\""], "meaning": "Wayne’s World is a 1992 comedy film featuring Mike Meyers and Dana Carvey. They were two knucklehead glam rock fanboys who filmed their own show in their basement.\n\nExcellent comes from their famous catchphrase “Wayne’s World! Wayne’s World! Party time! Excellent!” Similarly, in Lil Wayne’s world, it’s always party time.", "annotation_id": "10167182", "url": "https://genius.com/10167182", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "Had to bust a bitch I knew back from my old days Shawty held me down when a nigga had that bald fade (Straight up)", "vault_lines": ["Had to bust a bitch I knew back from my old days"], "meaning": "“To bust” is a slang term that means “to have sex”.  Travis had sex with a girl who used to support, or hold him down, when he had a bald fade–the type of haircut Travis had as a teenager.", "annotation_id": "10166400", "url": "https://genius.com/10166400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "But I pass it like I’m Robert Horry (Straight up)", "vault_lines": ["But I pass it like I'm Robert Horry (Straight up)"], "meaning": "Travis passes women to his buddy like former NBA Player Robert Horry would with the ball.\n\nThis is not the first time shouting Robert Horry, he has mentioned him in “Antidote”:\n\n I just hit a three peat\nFucked three hoes I met this week (Robert Horry!) I don’t do no old hoes (Oh, no, no!)\nMy nigga, that’s a no-no", "annotation_id": "10166214", "url": "https://genius.com/10166214", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "Bust a nigga like I bust a bitch", "vault_lines": ["Bust a nigga like I bust a bitch"], "meaning": "“Bust a nigga” refers to knocking out your opponents in a fight, while “bust a bitch” refers to having sex.", "annotation_id": "10166200", "url": "https://genius.com/10166200", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "She might be a tourist or a terrorist A Hell’s Angel actin’ like she Heaven-sent, Lord", "vault_lines": ["She might be a tourist or a terrorist"], "meaning": "As the story goes, the devil was an angel before he was pushed out of heaven by God. She is the devil in disguise–acting like an angel but actually a bad girl. This is further emphasized by alleging she might be a terrorist.\n\nWayne has used the devil comparison before, most prominently in “On Fire”, the second single from his rock-inspired album Rebirth.", "annotation_id": "10165782", "url": "https://genius.com/10165782", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "She come to Wayne’s world just to party And all of my tourists is foreign", "vault_lines": ["Wayne's world – \"Party time, excellent\""], "meaning": "Once again referring to the 1992 film Wayne’s World, when you take a drug-trip into Weezy’s world it’s all about partying with foreign women.\n\n\n\nWeezy used a very similar line to this on Tha Carter IV’s “It’s Good”", "annotation_id": "10165778", "url": "https://genius.com/10165778", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "Gin and tonic, pass that to my buddies (To my buddies) Only lean and soda, I’m not no alcoholic (Alcoholic)", "vault_lines": ["Gin and tonic, pass that to my buddies (To my buddies)"], "meaning": "Travis prefers drinking the concoction of cough syrup and soda known as lean instead of alcoholic beverages like Gin and Tonic water. Travis has previously mentioned that he drinks lean like others drink liquor:\n\nJust treat a pint like a handle", "annotation_id": "10164913", "url": "https://genius.com/10164913", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "Bust a trip, come and be my tourist Pretty bitches walkin’ ’round my forest How does it feel, my nigga? Damn, it feel great Bust a trip, come and be my tourist", "vault_lines": ["How does that feel, my nigga? I said it feel great (Woo, woo)"], "meaning": "Travis invites us to take a drug-induced trip into his fictional world.\n\nWhile Travis’s recent stage performances have a western aesthetic to tie into his first album Rodeo, he used woodland imagery earlier in his career— like the video for “Upper Echelon.”", "annotation_id": "10164594", "url": "https://genius.com/10164594", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "Just got to the mo’, while niggas still leanin’, tippin’", "vault_lines": ["Just got to the mo', while niggas still leanin', tippin'"], "meaning": "Mo is short for Missouri City, the part of Houston Travis grew up in. Tipping is Houston slang for riding in a car that uses hydraulics to tip to one side.", "annotation_id": "10164537", "url": "https://genius.com/10164537", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tourist", "line": "504, my nigga, shout my whodi", "vault_lines": ["504, my nigga, shout my whodi"], "meaning": "504 is the area code for New Orleans, LA and woadie is New Orleans slang for a friend or homie. Travis is likely referring to Lil Wayne as his woadie since Weezy is from New Orleans.", "annotation_id": "10164472", "url": "https://genius.com/10164472", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
