{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Took His Time", "line": "On a diet, on a diet from the fake beef", "vault_lines": ["On a diet, on a diet from the fake beef"], "meaning": "Wayne had all but disappeared for some time from the rap game, so this can be a line stating he is tired of the rap game. But, as in his FWA album on ‘Living Right’ ft Wiz Khalifa, he says he keeps his distance from trouble. So again he wants to avoid any trouble he can.", "annotation_id": "24275590", "url": "https://genius.com/24275590", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Took His Time", "line": "I’m speedin’ past in the newest soft top like the Jewish", "vault_lines": ["I'm speedin' past in the newest soft top like the Jewish"], "meaning": "Jewish people traditionally wear Yamakas, or Kippahs, which are a small, soft hat on the top of their head symbolizing God is with them. A “soft top” car is a convertible—a car without a roof.\n\nWayne would later use the same metaphor in 2020’s track “I Do It”:\n\nSoft top on my car like it’s Jewish (It’s Jewish)", "annotation_id": "19420636", "url": "https://genius.com/19420636", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Took His Time", "line": "Wake up and smell the azaleas sang her prayers like Mahalia", "vault_lines": ["Wake up and smell the azaleas sang her prayers like Mahalia"], "meaning": "Double entendre here, azaleas are a type of flower that are commonly found in Souther United States, as well as being the name of two famous women entertainers who many people think are beautiful (Iggy Azalea & Azealia Banks).\n\nWayne may be mixing the classic sayings “wake up and smell the coffee” and “stop and smell the roses”, or he could be talking about waking up with a variety of women.\n\n\n\nAzalea flowers\n\nMahalia Jackson is a renowned gospel singer who is a fellow New Orlean’s native, once dubbed “The Queen of Gospel.” As a gospel singer, much of her musical content related to God and praying, stating\n\nI sing gospel​ because it makes me feel free", "annotation_id": "15474094", "url": "https://genius.com/15474094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Took His Time", "line": "I been feelin’ like Galactus", "vault_lines": ["I been sippin' like the Dracula, I been feelin' like Galactus"], "meaning": "Galactus is a Marvel Comics supervillain who possesses godlike powers. He is a cosmic entity who consumes planets, has a plethora of abilities, and his space station is perhaps the greatest source of energy in their universe.\n\nWeezy feels that he is as important, and holds as much power to the rap game as Galactus does to the Marvel multiverse.", "annotation_id": "15474116", "url": "https://genius.com/15474116", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Took His Time", "line": "I put my pride to the side, off safety", "vault_lines": ["I put my pride to the side, off safety"], "meaning": "The first meaning is that Lil Wayne put his ego aside, but as Wayne made the gunshot backrap, this may also refer to the unfortunate time when he shot himself as a kid because of a gun with no safety.\n\nWeezy went to a TV show to explain himself, after saying in september 2016 that he never dealt with such thing as racism in an interview on Fox Sports 1 that was highliting the Colin Kaepernick’s feud.\nThe fact is that he shot himself because of a gun with no safety on and was seriously wounded, some cops broke his door to look for illegals guns and drugs possessions, and a white cop saved him, ever since, he always considered that racism doesn’t exist.\n\nDwayne Michael Carter Jr was heavily criticized at this time, and he had tu put his pride to the side to explain himself. Moreover, Lil Wayne also said that this event is a sign of a godly rescue, that makes sense as he explains God took his time when he made him.", "annotation_id": "15473454", "url": "https://genius.com/15473454", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Took His Time", "line": "Bickin’ back bein’ bool, trigger happiest goons", "vault_lines": ["Bickin' back bein' bool, trigger happiest goons"], "meaning": "A reference to fellow rapper and Blood gang affiliate, YG’s song: “Bicken Back Being Bool.”\n\nDue to the affiliation with the Blood gang, the C/K sounds at the beginning of words have been replaced with B’s, turning “Kickin' back bein' cool” into “Bickin' back bein' bool.”", "annotation_id": "15468968", "url": "https://genius.com/15468968", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
