{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "And I be OT with my bro T and Lil Hoody and Skateboard E And that’s my niggas, we fly niggas With shotguns under both wings", "vault_lines": ["And I be OT with my bro T and Lil Hoody and Skateboard E"], "meaning": "This part of the song mirrors the original rather well where he references skateboarding and uses letters in his flow. OT means overtime", "annotation_id": "15402683", "url": "https://genius.com/15402683", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "When shit got out of hand, my hands was full, I’m Going through some shit, yeah, but you know I ain’t broke up", "vault_lines": ["When shit got out of hand, my hands was full, I'm"], "meaning": "These lines are about the dispute between Young Money and Cash Money entertainment. He contemplated retirement as he was halted from releasing his music in what was a traumatic experience that likely reminded him of his childhood", "annotation_id": "15402642", "url": "https://genius.com/15402642", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Ain’t no peace, we chop off both fingers", "vault_lines": ["Ain't no peace, we chop off both fingers"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne and his crew are ruthless and don’t want no peace\n\nWayne isn’t interested in peace treaties or truces with his enemies:\n\n\n\nHim and his goons are gonna cut both those fingers off to send a message.", "annotation_id": "8504237", "url": "https://genius.com/8504237", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Gotta take out my pocket lint And make something out of it, like a scientist Be creative and confident;", "vault_lines": ["Gotta shake it like Iverson,"], "meaning": "Lint is merely tiny pieces of fabric left after washing a piece of clothing. To say you only have lint in your pocket means you’re broke. Wayne uses what some would find worthless, and turns it into a successful rap and business career.", "annotation_id": "8391568", "url": "https://genius.com/8391568", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "I pull up, I pull up, and I fade away That’s NBA, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I pull up, I pull up, I pull up, like \"ayy\""], "meaning": "Wayne could be referring to being “faded” from drugs/lean, he hits the fadeaway jump shot like a great in the NBA, or he pulls up on an enemy, does his business, then fades away, unseen.", "annotation_id": "8363592", "url": "https://genius.com/8363592", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Uh, I used to have braids but I still got the hoes, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Uh, I used to have braids but I still got the hoes, yeah"], "meaning": "Post Malone said “I got me some braids and I got me some hoes.” & Wayne is referencing that line but he doesn’t have braids anymore, so he’s saying I still got the hoes but I used to have braids.", "annotation_id": "8316274", "url": "https://genius.com/8316274", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Limo tint, limo tint 5 percent, Louie V moccasins", "vault_lines": ["Limo tint, limo tint 5 percent, Louie V moccasins"], "meaning": "Limo tint is very dark private tint; known as 5 percent when tinting windows that dark. And also the Louis Vuitton moccasin shoes for comfort, end of the day, relaxin'.", "annotation_id": "8308634", "url": "https://genius.com/8308634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Pour up, yeah I’m sipped out, I’m knocked out in my house all day", "vault_lines": ["I'm sipped out, I'm knocked out in my house all day"], "meaning": "Wayne lets us know that he’s usually sitting in his house all day in a stupor, “sipped out” presumably from popular drug combination of  promethazine and codeine.", "annotation_id": "8293628", "url": "https://genius.com/8293628", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Back when them hoes was wearing Juicy Couture, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Back when them hoes was wearing Juicy Couture, yeah"], "meaning": "Juicy Couture used to be very popular back in the day especially their velour tracksuits. I’m pretty sure he doesn’t say polo… He’s saying Juicy Couture isn’t in style anymore and neither are Velour jumpsuits", "annotation_id": "8290751", "url": "https://genius.com/8290751", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "I loosen my brakes and I still got control, err", "vault_lines": ["I loosen my brakes and I still got control, err"], "meaning": "Although Wayne has settled down a bit in the rap game, he still is confident and in control on the top of his game.", "annotation_id": "8290188", "url": "https://genius.com/8290188", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Staggerin’, I’m flaggin’, I’m reppin’ Suwu Yeah, Blood Gang", "vault_lines": ["Staggerin', I'm flaggin', I'm reppin' Suwu"], "meaning": "“SooWoo” is a calling card for the street gang “The Bloods.” “Flagging” also means he’s repping this gang.", "annotation_id": "8289530", "url": "https://genius.com/8289530", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Gotta shake it like Iverson,", "vault_lines": ["Gotta shake it like Iverson,"], "meaning": "Wayne is referring to the basketball move “The Shake N' Bake”\n\nHere’s a clip of Allen Iverson performing this move and crossing Michael Jordan:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y3X274lz3wY", "annotation_id": "8289497", "url": "https://genius.com/8289497", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "I pull up, I pull up, I pull up, like “ayy” I pull up, I pull up and I fade away", "vault_lines": ["I pull up, I pull up, I pull up, like \"ayy\""], "meaning": "Another smart word play by Wayne. He uses the basketball metaphor by saying he pull up in a car in the last line be then uses the pull up definition this line.", "annotation_id": "8287707", "url": "https://genius.com/8287707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Yeah, and I got that Flakka dick, them bitches be out of it", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, and I got that Flakka dick, them bitches be out of it"], "meaning": "“Flakka” is a drug that is emerging in the US, a designer drug similar in effect to bath salts. It’s an updated way of saying “dope dick,” implying he can have sex for long periods of time because he is high.\n\nThe drug is also described as a “zombie” drug because of how it makes people act.", "annotation_id": "8286520", "url": "https://genius.com/8286520", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "I got that dope dick, your bitch is a dope fiend", "vault_lines": ["I got that dope dick, your bitch is a dope fiend"], "meaning": "“Dope” is slang for a narcotic, usually cocaine, and a “dope fiend” is someone hooked on drugs. Wayne is comparing his dick game to cocaine, saying that if he gets with your girl once, then he’s going to have her hooked. Wayne has referenced having a “dope dick” before.\n\nThis is similar to Big Sean’s line on Lil Wayne’s “My Homies Still”.", "annotation_id": "8283475", "url": "https://genius.com/8283475", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Yeah, I’m saucy like pasta, bitch, I’m talking all kinda shit", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I'm saucy like pasta, bitch, I'm talking all kinda shit"], "meaning": "Being “saucy” is the equivalent to being “sassy” – Weezy seems to be on the edge for whatever reason, expressing quite the attitude. Pasta is often best served with sauce.", "annotation_id": "8281919", "url": "https://genius.com/8281919", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "No vacation, just power trips", "vault_lines": ["no vacation, just power trips"], "meaning": "When you’re “power tripping,” you’re aggressively waving your authority around. Wayne sees himself as one of the top people in the game, and isn’t afraid of showing it. That’s the only way he’ll go on a trip – “trip” being another word for “vacation” – because he grinds so much he doesn’t have time for vacations.", "annotation_id": "8281911", "url": "https://genius.com/8281911", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "And when I started fuckin’, I was young", "vault_lines": ["And when I started fuckin', I was young"], "meaning": "According to Wayne, he lost his virginity at the age of 11, which is a very early age. This line is mimics Post Malone’s original line.\n\nWhen I started ballin' I was young\n\nThis line is also similar to another one of Lil Wayne’s lines.", "annotation_id": "8281207", "url": "https://genius.com/8281207", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "Started out from nothin’, just some crumbs Started up from nothin’, just some crumbs And now I got a bakery, yum, yum", "vault_lines": ["Started out from nothin', just some crumbs"], "meaning": "Compared to the full pie, Wayne started as nothing but lil' crumbs, as he kept growing in his flow and talent. The “bakery” is likely referring to his record label, Young Money Entertainment, which has grown other crumbs, such as Drake, to the best pies you can find.\n\n\n\nBreaking out the likely double meaning, Wayne’s also talking about a different kind of pastry,  such as a laced pie or other treat. Now that Wayne has enough money to throw around, he decides to start cooking. Start cooking drug-laced treats that is.", "annotation_id": "8280340", "url": "https://genius.com/8280340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "When I started cussin’, I was one Mama put that soap on my tongue", "vault_lines": ["When I started cussin', I was one"], "meaning": "A common practice among parents is to wash a child’s mouth out with soap whenever they cuss. This is to try to deter them from cussing again. Like most children, Wayne started cussing young and his mother would wash his mouth out.\n\nWayne’s mother was against him cussing so much, that she even asked he refrain from cussing on his debut album Tha Block is Hot.", "annotation_id": "8279687", "url": "https://genius.com/8279687", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Too Young", "line": "And I’m a Martian, I’m marching on the stars and moon", "vault_lines": ["And I'm a Martian, I'm marching on the stars and moon"], "meaning": "Wayne often talks about not being a human being in his lyrics. Since martians are from outer space, they’re surrounded by stars and moons. This could be a double entendre, the second meaning being that he’s high enough to walk on the stars and moon, similar to another Wayne line.\n\nWayne has talked about being a martian before, however:\n\nOkay, hello it’s the Martian, Space Jam Jordans", "annotation_id": "8279685", "url": "https://genius.com/8279685", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
