{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "To The Bank", "line": "My pockets so fat, they hemorrhagin’", "vault_lines": ["My pockets so fat, they hemorrhagin'"], "meaning": "“Hemorrhaging” is a term often used in the context of bleeding or losing blood rapidly. In the lyrics, Lil Wayne uses it metaphorically to convey that his pockets are overflowing with money, akin to an excessive and uncontrollable flow of cash.", "annotation_id": "29866996", "url": "https://genius.com/29866996", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "To The Bank", "line": "Pockets pregnant, bitch tryna clip the umbilical", "vault_lines": ["Pockets pregnant, bitch tryna clip the umbilical"], "meaning": "In this line, Weezy compares getting money to getting pregnant and how his girl is trying to cut the umbilical cord to his pockets to have some money for herself.", "annotation_id": "29695082", "url": "https://genius.com/29695082", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
