{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "Let me get my Zsa Zsa Gabor on", "vault_lines": ["Let me get my Zsa Zsa Gabor on"], "meaning": "The slap heard around the world\n\nZsa Zsa Gabor was a Hungarian-American socialite and actress.\n\nIn 1989 Gabor was driving her $215,000 Rolls-Royce. Beverly Hills Police motorcycle Officer Paul Kramer stopped the actress for driving her car with expired registration tags. While Kramer was checking for other violations, Gabor drove off.\n\nWhen Kramer pulled her over the second time, Gabor slapped the officer. She claimed that she had acted in self-defense when Kramer pulled her out of her car roughly. Kramer insisted that the slap was unprovoked.\n\nGabor was fined $2,350 for slapping Kramer, $352 for driving without a license and $235 for possessing an open container of alcohol–a flask of Jack Daniels.", "annotation_id": "29840110", "url": "https://genius.com/29840110", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "She on tootsie, it’s pink and it’s pretty", "vault_lines": ["She on tootsie, it's pink and it's pretty"], "meaning": "‘Tusi’ is a phonetic translation of the drug ‘2C/2C-B’, a series of psychedelic phenethylamines. The concoction is also sometimes referred to as “pink cocaine” as it typically comes in the form of pink powder.", "annotation_id": "29770660", "url": "https://genius.com/29770660", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "Titties, titties, titties, titties Titties, titties, titties, titties Titties, titties, titties, titties, titties", "vault_lines": ["I smoke cookies, hate milk and love titties"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne loves titties.", "annotation_id": "29734141", "url": "https://genius.com/29734141", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "In a throne, I’m a king, I’m Mike Bibby", "vault_lines": ["In a throne, I'm a king, I'm Mike Bibby"], "meaning": "I’m Mike Bibby. Mike Bibby is a former NBA player for the Sacramento Kings.", "annotation_id": "29699778", "url": "https://genius.com/29699778", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "I don’t even work out, lil’ bitch, I just work hard I don’t even work out, lil’ bitch, I just work hard", "vault_lines": ["I don't even work out, lil' bitch, I just work hard"], "meaning": "During a February 2023 sit down with Zane Lowe for Apple Music, Lil Wayne openly talked about his lack of interest in working out. Instead of building his physique through weightlifting, Wayne stays fit by avoiding unhealthy foods. He also, substitutes regular gym sessions with skateboarding and an active lifestyle – His ability to consistently stay in shape year-round has been a talking point amongst fans for years.", "annotation_id": "29678006", "url": "https://genius.com/29678006", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "Shoot up your block and double back ’cause I got OCD", "vault_lines": ["Shoot up your block and double back 'cause I got OCD"], "meaning": "Here, Wayne implies he’s going to or can cause destruction in his opponent’s neighborhood while playing on the word OCD – a disorder that’s characterized by excessive thoughts (obsessions) that lead to repetitive behaviours (compulsions).", "annotation_id": "29677925", "url": "https://genius.com/29677925", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "It’s me and Mac, he like Shaq but I’m Kobe B", "vault_lines": ["It's me and Mac, he like Shaq but I'm Kobe B"], "meaning": "Wayne and Mac have been close friends since they were 8 years. Sharing the same birth year, they’ve worked together on a number of music projects. The standout move was in 2005 when they founded a record label, Young Money\n\nShaq & Kobe are former NBA Hall of Famers Shaquille O'Neal and Kobe Bryant — who played together from 1996 to 2004, winning three consecutive championships for the Los Angeles Lakers in the early 2000s — and also, famously feuded during their time as teammates.\n\nLil Wayne has always been a Kobe fan and has always shouted him out over his career, even naming one his songs on his 2009 Album, No Ceilings after him. Check it out below.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/IM7mMeUjX74", "annotation_id": "29677688", "url": "https://genius.com/29677688", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "[Verse 1: Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm on one, two, three, four Percs, light work though"], "meaning": "On this verse, Wayne begins the longest track on the album with a gradually increasing tempo accompanied by an electrifying synthesizer with no beat", "annotation_id": "29677570", "url": "https://genius.com/29677570", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "Ten toes down on the ground, no turf toe", "vault_lines": ["Ten toes down on the ground, no turf toe"], "meaning": "Being “ten toes down” means to be solid and never fold under pressure, adding “no turf toe” shows that there is no question as to how solid he is as having turf toe would inevitably make standing a struggle.", "annotation_id": "29677348", "url": "https://genius.com/29677348", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "Turn around, I hit it from the B-side, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Turn around, I hit it from the B-side, yeah"], "meaning": "The B side is the back of a traditional vinyl record. So “hit[ing] it from the B side” refers to having sex with a girl while behind her.", "annotation_id": "29677309", "url": "https://genius.com/29677309", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tity Boi", "line": "In a throne, I’m a king, I’m Mike Bibby", "vault_lines": ["In a throne, I'm a king, I'm Mike Bibby"], "meaning": "“Like Mike Bibby” who was a former NBA player for the Kings During his playing years in the league, former Sacramento Kings point guard Mike Bibby was known for his ability to score and set his teammates up", "annotation_id": "29667511", "url": "https://genius.com/29667511", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
