{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tina Turn Up Needs a Tune Up (Freestyle)", "line": "I could fix it I could fix it I could fix it I could fix it I could fix it I could fix it", "vault_lines": ["Well I could fix her, young blacksmith"], "meaning": "What does he wants to fix?\n\nBy saying in the hook that\n\nTina Turn Up need a tune up\n\nWayne is trying to say that she needs a better man, and no one is better than Lil Wayne. So he want to fix the problem, that she doesn’t have the right man, by giving her a “tune up”, what actually means, replacing her man with himself.", "annotation_id": "3350247", "url": "https://genius.com/3350247", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tina Turn Up Needs a Tune Up (Freestyle)", "line": "You a queen, not a princess You a queen, let’s have a princess", "vault_lines": ["You a queen, not a princess"], "meaning": "A queen is higher in ranking than a princess. There are two different kinds of queens:\n\n\nA queen who is the highest ranked, the female equivalent of a king, who does have the power to reign.\nA queen consort, the wife of the reigning king, who doesn’t have powers to reign\n\n\n\nI think Wayne is referring her to type 2 of a queen, seeing himself as the king of hip hop and her as the wife of the reigning king.\n\nA princess is the daughter of the queen and the king and because she’s a queen, Weezys queen, he wants to have a baby with her, so “let’s have a princess”.", "annotation_id": "3350169", "url": "https://genius.com/3350169", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tina Turn Up Needs a Tune Up (Freestyle)", "line": "Melt in your mouth not in your hand", "vault_lines": ["Melt in your mouth not in your hand"], "meaning": "A play of words with the previous line’s “M&M” which could refer to the colorful button-shaped candies.\n\n\n\n The M&M company’s slogan being “Melt in your mouth not in your hand”, Weezy is implying here that just like an M&M candy he’ll melt (another word used to say cum) in Tina’s mouth.", "annotation_id": "3260194", "url": "https://genius.com/3260194", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tina Turn Up Needs a Tune Up (Freestyle)", "line": "Tina Turn Up need a tune up Tina Turn Up need a tune up Tina Turn Up need a tune up Tina Turn Up need a tune up", "vault_lines": ["Need a king, need a king"], "meaning": "Basically saying that Tina Turn Up (Christina Milian) need’s a better man which he believes it’s him.\n\nTune is short for Tunechi which is Wayne.", "annotation_id": "3235557", "url": "https://genius.com/3235557", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
