{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "To multiply, I give it my undivided", "vault_lines": ["To multiply, I give it my undivided, you gotta move fast, think faster"], "meaning": "Here, Sean is playing off two words with opposite meaning, “multiply” and “divide”, at the same time, he is saying to multiply his wealth/success, he has to give his undivided attention and energy.", "annotation_id": "41315623", "url": "https://genius.com/41315623", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "What’s a king to a god, nigga? I’m gon’ live forever", "vault_lines": ["What's a king to a god, nigga? I'm gon' live forever"], "meaning": "This is possibly a reference to Kanye and Jay Z’s track “No Church in the Wild”, as Benny interpolates the line from the famous hook\n\n“Human beings in a mob\nWhat’s a mob to a king?\nWhat’s a king to a god?\nWhat’s a god to a non-believer\nWho don’t believe in anything?”\n\nNotably the producer of this song, Hit Boy, also produced the song N***as in Paris, Watch the throne’s 5th single and biggest song", "annotation_id": "33139346", "url": "https://genius.com/33139346", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "I treat the white girl like a wifey, treat her like Aphrodite Let a goddess satisfy me while I’m rollin’ the tighty", "vault_lines": ["I treat the white girl like a wifey, treat her like Aphrodite"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne compares “the white girl” (slang for cocaine) to Aphrodite, the Greek goddess of love, beauty and desire. By doing so, he highlights the drug’s irresistible appeal, likening the effects to being satisfied by a goddess.", "annotation_id": "32773072", "url": "https://genius.com/32773072", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "Swear it’s labels that’s up Bs that owe me Ms To them, that shit is like Gs, niggas ain’t G, greed’s a disease", "vault_lines": ["Swear it's labels that's up Bs that owe me Ms"], "meaning": "Big Sean is referencing the alleged $6 Million he’s owed by GOOD Music. He compares the mere $6 Million to the Billions that he says those who owe him are receiving.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/iHaj15gkrHc", "annotation_id": "24810453", "url": "https://genius.com/24810453", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "Watch me turn G.O.O.D. into great", "vault_lines": ["Watch me turn G.O.O.D. into great"], "meaning": "Word play on good and great. By definition great is better than good & Big Sean is also signed to G.O.O.D music.", "annotation_id": "22720410", "url": "https://genius.com/22720410", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "I got niggas on my team, they ain’t tryna swap jerseys with you", "vault_lines": ["I got niggas on my team, they ain't tryna swap jerseys with you"], "meaning": "Most sports teams wear jerseys, and they sometimes swap jerseys with the opposing team at the end of a game to show respect. Lil Wayne is showing the levels of his respect and his team’s disrespect to the other side at the same time", "annotation_id": "22720361", "url": "https://genius.com/22720361", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "When you don’t have a silver spoon, you gotta eat with your hands God walkin’ with me when I’m alone, two sets of feet in the sand", "vault_lines": ["When you don't have a silver spoon, you gotta eat with your hands"], "meaning": "A play on the phrase – “Born with a silver spoon” ,  which means to be born in a rich family. So here Big Sean is saying that if you are not fortunate enough to be born in a rich family, you have to do everything by yourself.\n\nIn the next bar he states that he will never be alone as he has god by his side, and he can see that god is walking besides him.", "annotation_id": "21434451", "url": "https://genius.com/21434451", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "A long way to the Presi’ from the Timex Classic", "vault_lines": ["A long way to the Presi' from the Timex Classic"], "meaning": "A reference to makes/models of watches. The Rolex Day-Date is known as ‘the president’s watch’, hence “presi”. The Rolex Day-Date has enjoyed a much sought-after status since its launch in 1956. Made only in gold or platinum, it was the first wristwatch to display both date and day of the week, spelt out in full in windows on the dial.  It costs in excess of 10k gbp/usd.\n\nThe timex classic is a budget bargain basement piece of shit that costs under 100 gbp/usd.\n\nBenny is saying he originally came from a low economic status, but now he has the funds to purchase the finer things in life.", "annotation_id": "21432393", "url": "https://genius.com/21432393", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "I thought small, then I grew, got to find out it was true Money change the people around quicker than it change you", "vault_lines": ["I thought small, then I grew, got to find out it was true"], "meaning": "Not my day ones, but definitely other people treat me different. Some of my friends, some of my relatives, some of the business partners that I have. I’ve been running around the industry for three years now. Everybody who opened their doors up to me, then seen my face, the doors was open.\n\nMy success changed them because I’m still me. If some people had an opportunity to interview me, but they didn’t want to back then, I’ll still do the interview. So it changed them. It changed what they think about me. I’m still the same person. I still got the same talent that they never gave a chance.", "annotation_id": "21077127", "url": "https://genius.com/21077127", "state": "verified", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "Like Pirelli tires on Chevy trucks, but still a Goodyear", "vault_lines": ["Like Pirelli tires on Chevy trucks, but still a Goodyear"], "meaning": "Pirelli and Goodyear are both famous brands of tyres. And tyres roll, a continued reference from last line “kush”.\nAnd the Chevy truck is a medium sized vehicle. Notice the wordplay on tyre and tire. Also, good year meaning his year so far has been pretty amazing with his album and his last four features are strong.", "annotation_id": "21028908", "url": "https://genius.com/21028908", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Timeless", "line": "Signed a slave deal, now a nigga up, ownin’ my masters", "vault_lines": ["Signed a slave deal, now a nigga up, ownin' my masters"], "meaning": "Big Sean, signed to Kanye West’s G.O.O.D Music under the Def Jam Label, references Kayne’s tweet after Kanye publicly claimed he was going to return 50% of his masters back to his artists.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/BigSean/status/1308848581315629056?s=20", "annotation_id": "21022610", "url": "https://genius.com/21022610", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
