{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thoughts", "line": "[Chorus: Tory Lanez]", "vault_lines": ["Movin' lowkey (Movin' lowkey on—)"], "meaning": "The chorus is interpolated from the third verse of “You” by Lloyd, which is also sampled in this song’s instrumental.\n\nThese just ain’t words, that I’m spitting\nIf you could see the thoughts that’s in my head", "annotation_id": "18793132", "url": "https://genius.com/18793132", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thoughts", "line": "Here (Ah) She’s fine too, but I want you (Ah)", "vault_lines": ["She's fine too, but I want you (Ah)"], "meaning": "This is sampled from Lloyd’s October 2006 song “You,” where he sings:\n\nLet’s dip up out of here\n(Ah) She’s fine too, but I want you\n\nhttps://youtu.be/UpD-56UqT14?t=78", "annotation_id": "18459095", "url": "https://genius.com/18459095", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thoughts", "line": "When I went and copped the Richard It was therapeutic, had to free my mind (Mind)", "vault_lines": ["When I went and copped the Richard"], "meaning": "Richard Mille is an expensive Swiss luxury watch brand that was founded in 1999. Their watches can range from $100,000 to  $1.7 million.", "annotation_id": "18458917", "url": "https://genius.com/18458917", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thoughts", "line": "Polly want a cracker, she said, “Please don’t call me Polly” She want me to call her bad words, these just ain’t words", "vault_lines": ["These just ain't words (Yeah)"], "meaning": "“Polly want a cracker” is a common saying to parrots as it’s often used in training a parrot to speak. The name Polly comes from the fact that it’s a variant of Poll as a female name for a parrot, according to the Oxford English Dictionary.", "annotation_id": "18458876", "url": "https://genius.com/18458876", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thoughts", "line": "You know you givin’ me good brain Like you graduated from a good school", "vault_lines": ["You know you givin' me good brain"], "meaning": "Wayne employs a double entendre on “brain” as he uses as slang for oral sex and in a literal matter. He similarily raps on 2009’s “Ice Cream”:\n\nShe give me good brain like she studied at Cambridge\n\nAdditionally, these lines, as well as the two lines above, are taken from Wayne’s verse on Lloyd’s October 2006 song “You,” which this song also samples.", "annotation_id": "18458848", "url": "https://genius.com/18458848", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thoughts", "line": "And you know I love you like good food You know you’re fuckin’ with a good dude", "vault_lines": ["And you know I love you like good food"], "meaning": "Wayne might be making an allusion to Jay-Z’s May 2002 song “Song Cry,” where he rapped:\n\nGood dude, I know you love me like cooked food", "annotation_id": "18458767", "url": "https://genius.com/18458767", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thoughts", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Tory-lanez-thoughts-lyrics", "genius_title": "Thoughts", "genius_id": 5004093, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thought It Was a Drought", "line": "I’m sipping that Houston like it’s communion", "vault_lines": ["I'm sipping that Houston like it's communion"], "meaning": "Sippin that Houston = Sippin Drank/Lean\n\nWhat it is, is a weak opioid in some liquid form -\n\nmodern\n- Promethazine and codeine\n- Chlorpheniramine and codeine (short existence)\n- Chlorpheniramine and Hydrocodone\n\n1960s – 1970s\n- Terpin Hydrate with Codeine\n- codeine with guaifenesin (Still exists not sought after due to side effects)\n\n Weak does not mean healthy \n\nHouston is where drank popularity started. Around the 1960s – 1970s it was used amongst the blues scenes in the third and fifth ward. Later on Houston rap was making way for a knew era. DJ Screw and the SUC became the stamp of the original drank sippers in Hip Hop during the 90s.\n\nsipin Houston, sippin H-Town, Texas in my cup, this is all referring to drank.", "annotation_id": "39958081", "url": "https://genius.com/39958081", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thought It Was a Drought", "line": "And I’d like to thank all the niggas that schooled me But I still might shoot up my class reunion", "vault_lines": ["And I'd like to thank all the niggas that schooled me"], "meaning": "Wayne is thankful for all of the people that schooled him in the past, because he learned from those experiences and became better. Even though he’s grateful, he still wants revenge on them so he can even the score. Note the word play: they “schooled” him and he might shoot up his “class reunion”", "annotation_id": "39003947", "url": "https://genius.com/39003947", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thought It Was a Drought", "line": "I’m quietly waiting, I’m trying to be patient But they want me to wait for Simon to say it", "vault_lines": ["I'm quietly waiting, I'm trying to be patient"], "meaning": "Wayne references the popular kid’s game ‘Simon Says’. In the game, players are only allowed to follow what the speaker says following the phrase Simon says.\n\nWayne is trying to be patient but he can’t just go by Simon (the rap game)’s rules. He goes by his own rules!", "annotation_id": "35840549", "url": "https://genius.com/35840549", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thought It Was a Drought", "line": "[Refrain: Lil Wayne] I just fucked your bitch in some Young Money flip flops I’m smoking on that loud and you can hear a pin drop (Hold up) I just kissed my bitch and I left codeine in her mouth (Yeah) Swimming in my money, I smell chlorine when I count (Get ’em)", "vault_lines": ["I just kissed my bitch and I left codeine in her mouth (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Interpolation of the hook on the OG Thought It Was A Drought by Future.\n\n‘'I just fucked your bitch in some Gucci flip flops\nI just had some bitches and I made them lip-lock\nI just took a piss and I seen codeine comin’ out\nWe got purple actavis I thought it was a  drought''", "annotation_id": "35840530", "url": "https://genius.com/35840530", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thought It Was a Drought", "line": "Shout to Mack Maine!", "vault_lines": ["Shout to Mack Maine!"], "meaning": "Mack Maine – member of Young Money", "annotation_id": "32555109", "url": "https://genius.com/32555109", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thought It Was a Drought", "line": "Big body on brabus, that’s all I know", "vault_lines": ["Big body on brabus, that's all I know"], "meaning": "This line is a reference to “Brabus” the automotive company. Known best for customizing and tuning Mercedes-Benz’s. Lil Wayne is the owner of a Brabus G-Wagon (also known as the 6 wheel G-Wagon). So to conclude Lil Wayne is saying the big body on his Brabus G-Wagon is all he knows. He rides around in his Chauffeured Brabus most of all his vehicles.", "annotation_id": "23084534", "url": "https://genius.com/23084534", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thought It Was a Drought", "line": "Like I’m the King, King of Zamunda", "vault_lines": ["Like I'm the King, King of Zamunda"], "meaning": "A reference to Eddie Murphy’s movie Coming to America. Zamunda is the fictional country where Eddie Murphy’s character Prince Akeem comes from. His father is King Jaffe Joffer, portrayed by James Earl Jones\n\n\n\nWayne previously referenced the movie in No Ceilings cut DOA:\nhttps://genius.com/15113", "annotation_id": "18621619", "url": "https://genius.com/18621619", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thought It Was a Drought", "line": "And if the bread get too low, kidnap John Doe (Hold up)", "vault_lines": ["And if the bread get too low, kidnap John Doe (Hold up)"], "meaning": "Bread = Money\nDoe “Dough” = Components to make Bread/Money.\nLil Wayne is going to kidnap John Doe if/when his money gets too low to make it more again.", "annotation_id": "17804580", "url": "https://genius.com/17804580", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thought It Was a Drought", "line": "Xanax and Adderall got me unparalleled", "vault_lines": ["Xanax and Adderall got me unparalleled"], "meaning": "His cozy drugs have him feeling great and unmatched by any other soul in the world (“unparalleled), but also a sort of double entendre / homophone for \"in parallel”. To explain: Xanax is considered a “downer” drug – like heroin or indica strains in weed – whereas Adderall is considered an “upper” drug – like meth or sativa strains in weed – he is “unparalleled” and “in parallel” because the down and up effect of the 2 drugs cancel one another out.", "annotation_id": "17160266", "url": "https://genius.com/17160266", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thought It Was a Drought", "line": "I ain’t got time for no rumors When I am not human, or you men, I’m booming", "vault_lines": ["I ain't got time for no rumors"], "meaning": "When you are as popular and as successful as Lil Wayne, people would create many rumors about you. Such as the time sites claimed he had HIV, or the time people thought he signed to ROC Nation.\n\nHowever, Weezy pays no mind to people who spend time creating rumors about him when he considers himself superior. He did tell us multiple times before that he is a Martian and not a human being.\n\nI thank God that I am not basic\n(I am not basic, I am not a human being)", "annotation_id": "13704802", "url": "https://genius.com/13704802", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
