{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "This Shit Right Here", "line": "I’m like Tyson, whisperin’ in your right-ear, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm like Tyson, whisperin' in your right-ear, nigga"], "meaning": "On June 28, 1997, one of the more bizarre moments in boxing history took place when Mike Tyson bit Evander Holyfield’s ear in the third round of their much-anticipated rematch. Tyson was disqualified from the bout and lost his boxing license. He was later reinstated.", "annotation_id": "28556901", "url": "https://genius.com/28556901", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "This Shit Right Here", "line": "Bloody red, bloody red, bloody red, bloody red Bloody red times five like a stop sign, gang", "vault_lines": ["Bloody red timеs five like a stop sign, gang"], "meaning": "“Bloody Mary, Bloody Mary, Bloody red, Bloody red, Bloody red times five like a stop sign, gang” is how I’m hearing it and with that said,\n\nThis would elude to the Bloody Mary curse where you can’t say it 3 times in the mirror without dying and relating it to the idea that you should keep the YSL bloods (who Wayne has been / still is affiliated with) name out your mouth. Saying stop talking as well as stopping himself from completing the Bloody Mary curse then saying ‘bloody red’ three times would relate to,\n1. Completing the curse would turn you blood red\n2.Speaking out of turn about YSL will turn you blood red (a simple repping his flag colour too)\n3. Obviously red lights and warning or danger signs are all also blood red tying into him stopping himself from the curse, telling people to don’t talk / stop talking and the face line saying stop signs are red.", "annotation_id": "28508644", "url": "https://genius.com/28508644", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "This Shit Right Here", "line": "I’m tryna talk to ’em, like Paul Finebaum", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryna talk to 'em, like Paul Finebaum"], "meaning": "Paul Finebaum is a well known sports commentator who produces a radio show from a regional base in Charlotte North Carolina. He primarily focuses on sports coming out of the south, which is also where Lil Wayne is from. In the line he’s comparing himself to a sports commentator in the manner and frequency of which he talks to them.", "annotation_id": "28359888", "url": "https://genius.com/28359888", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "This Shit Right Here", "line": "Mwah, “You on point, Tune’?” All the time, slime", "vault_lines": ["Mwah, \"You on point, Tune'?\" All the time, slime"], "meaning": "Reference to A Tribe Called Quest classic song Check the Rhime\n\nHeh, okay, you on point, Phife? All the time, Tip\nYou on point, Phife? All the time, Tip\nYou on point, Phife? All the time, Tip", "annotation_id": "28345235", "url": "https://genius.com/28345235", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "This Shit Right Here", "line": "You got a sharp fuse, bitch, I’m a live wire", "vault_lines": ["You got a sharp fuse, bitch, I'm a live wire"], "meaning": "“I’m a live wire” not hard wire\n\nA live wire is a wire carrying an electric current. Wayne is comparing himself to a live wire to say he’s energetic and dangerous.", "annotation_id": "28336928", "url": "https://genius.com/28336928", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
