{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "I eat that pussy ’cause it’s sweet, as sweet as one-six Sixteen bullets in a clip, but more than one clip", "vault_lines": ["I eat that pussy 'cause it's sweet, as sweet as one-six"], "meaning": "Mentions the underground producer, sixsixteen.", "annotation_id": "36021084", "url": "https://genius.com/36021084", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "Shoot a nigga sixteen times until I’m convinced", "vault_lines": ["Shoot a nigga sixteen times until I'm convinced"], "meaning": "Keeping the 16 theme going, Wayne says he’s not gonna stop shooting his target until he is convinced that he is dead.", "annotation_id": "7298478", "url": "https://genius.com/7298478", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "But I got one I really fuck with She makes my heart skip a beat She dropped her drum stick Sometimes we fuck forever, sometimes I cum quick", "vault_lines": ["She makes my heart skip a beat"], "meaning": "Although he doesn’t trust women anymore, he has this girl who has gained his trust. Lil Wayne is referring to the R&B songstress, Christina Milian.\n\nAdding a pun to his heart skipping a beat, Wayne’s girl must have dropped her metaphorical drumstick and missed a beat.  Someone’s heart skipping a beat is an idiom that refers to that special feeling people get with someone they really care about.", "annotation_id": "7261591", "url": "https://genius.com/7261591", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "That nigga Mack was chillin’, Po was home talkin’ on the phone", "vault_lines": ["That nigga Mack was chillin', Po was home talkin' on the phone"], "meaning": "Mack, also known as Mack Maine is Lil Wayne’s childhood friend. He is also the president of Young Money Entertainment. Mack has been working on his debut album, “Maine 4 President”, for a few years but has not been able to promote it, due to his focus and concentration on promoting the other artists of Young Money.\n\nAlso a reference to Cortez Bryant, Lil Wayne’s manager, and longtime friend. Bryant is one of the most influential and successful businessmen in the music industry today.\n\nNow my nigga Tez Po\nBeen ridin' with me since Keds", "annotation_id": "7231550", "url": "https://genius.com/7231550", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "Got my bitch with chinky eyes like that bitch Nia Long", "vault_lines": ["Got my bitch with chinky eyes like that bitch Nia Long"], "meaning": "Nia Long is an American actress, known for her roles in multiple television series', and the films Boyz n the Hood, and Friday.\n\nLil Wayne points out the similar physical appearance of his current girlfriend, Christina Milian, and Nia Long.\n\nThis is not the first time Wayne refers to Nia Long’s physical features. He mentioned her in “Novocane”, where he implies that his relationship was as short as Nia Long’s height:\n\nThe relationship was short and sweet, Nia Long", "annotation_id": "7226918", "url": "https://genius.com/7226918", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "Euro the future, fuck your future, like I’m reading palms", "vault_lines": ["Euro the future, fuck your future, like I'm reading palms"], "meaning": "Another reference to the latest Young Money signed artist, Euro. Lil Wayne announced that Euro is the newest member of Young Money on his Dedication 5 mixtape. Euro’s most notable feature was on “We Alright”, and “Ain’t Worried”. He is also featured in “Pull Up”, which is off the current album, FWA.\n\nLil Wayne metaphorically has the ability of reading ones lines in the palm to discover his true character of person and any future trends. He can easily tell that Euro has a shining future, unlike the future of Birdman’s lately signed artists.", "annotation_id": "7225270", "url": "https://genius.com/7225270", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "My goons waitin’ for you, to snap Like some photo bombers", "vault_lines": ["My goons waitin' for you, to snap"], "meaning": "Photo bombers wait until just before a picture is taken or snapped and then jump in the background at the last second. Weezy uses a modern simile to point out the impeccable timing of his goons is much like that of photo bombers. The difference being Weezy’s goons will ruin more then your picture.", "annotation_id": "7222558", "url": "https://genius.com/7222558", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "I got that Tec under my arm like Right Guard, Sure, Degree", "vault_lines": ["I got that Tec under my arm like Right Guard, Sure, Degree"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has a 9mm assault pistol under his arm, so he could use it whenever he want to.\n\nTunechi plays on words here by comparing how he has a gun under his arm, as usual as people put on deodorants under their arms. “Right Guard”, “Sure”, and “Degree” are all different brands of underarm deodorants.", "annotation_id": "7221067", "url": "https://genius.com/7221067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "Wayne Chong, chinky eyes like I’m from Vietnam", "vault_lines": ["Wayne Chong, chinky eyes like I'm from Vietnam"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne’s eyes are half-open at best, similarly to how Asians have not widely open eyes. He had a similar lyric on one of his recent songs D'usse, except now he compares the constriction of his eyes, from all the weed he smokes, to the eyes of Vietnamese people:\n\nEyes look Chinese, Wayne-chung to these niggas\n\nThis could also be a reference to Tommy Chong, a character from classic stoner comedy collection movies, Cheech and Chong.\n\nHe’s also phrased the line to sound like/reference Wang Chung, the 80’s band who’s notable for “Everybody have Fun Tonight”", "annotation_id": "7221024", "url": "https://genius.com/7221024", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "I got strawberry cocaine as sweet as Fun Dip", "vault_lines": ["I got strawberry cocaine as sweet as Fun Dip"], "meaning": "There has been some recent buzz in Hollywood about strawberry cocaine. Strawberry flavoring is added to the drug to give it its fruity flavor. Flavored cocaine is nothing new, people have been buying coke in all sorts of flavors, including rum and cherry.\n\nFun Dip is a candy powder, which is extremely sweet and contains of 89% sugar.", "annotation_id": "7220676", "url": "https://genius.com/7220676", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "Lord, just keep Lil Reginae away from birds and bees Let her be strong as the woman that gave birth to me", "vault_lines": ["Lord, just keep Lil Reginae away from birds and bees"], "meaning": "Reginae Carter, Lil Wayne’s daughter, is one of the latest music artists to sign with Young Money Entertainment.\n\nAlthough “Bird and bees” is an old term used to refer to adult relations between a man and a woman, Lil Wayne means drugs and gang violence that Wayne is involved in. “Birds”, meaning bricks of cocaine. “Bees” meaning the blood gang.\n\nBasically, Tunechi wishes his daughter to stay good, and wants her to be as strong as his mother.", "annotation_id": "7220634", "url": "https://genius.com/7220634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "That nigga Hoody on the set, he got his hoodie on", "vault_lines": ["That nigga Hoody on the set, he got his hoodie on"], "meaning": "Reference to Super Hood, a Texas rapper affiliated with Young Money. He teamed up for a cypher to put his individual talent on display with Lil Twist, Euro, Cory Gunz, Flow, and Gudda Gudda.\n\nHis most notable appearance was “Think I’m Lyin” featuring Lil Wayne, and Tyga. It was debuted on DJ Stevie J’s mixtape Appreciation 7.", "annotation_id": "7220600", "url": "https://genius.com/7220600", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "My nigga T got a 40, and he brought two cups", "vault_lines": ["My nigga T got a 40, and he brought two cups"], "meaning": "Reference to T-Streets, a rapper from New Orleans. Streets is one of the few original members of Young Money left as he is also a close friend of Weezy, who regards him more of a brother than his artist. His most notable appearance was his verse on Lil Wayne’s “Hold Up” track.\n\n40 is reference to 40 caliber pistol, Weezy adds then a pun to “40”, which could also be a slang for a 40 ounce alcoholic beverage.", "annotation_id": "7220538", "url": "https://genius.com/7220538", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "Uhh, bow-wow-wow, yippie-yo, yippie-yay Can’t trust these dog-ass hoes today I say bow-wow-wow, yippie-yo, yippie-yay Can’t trust these dog-ass hoes today", "vault_lines": ["Uhh, bow-wow-wow, yippie-yo, yippie-yay"], "meaning": "The “bawawa yupi yo yupi ya” comes from G-funk West Coast artists, particularly Snoop Dogg and Tha Dogg Pound.  Used to represent dogs, Wayne expresses his distaste for his former friends who have become unloyal, quite likely directed at Birdman.", "annotation_id": "7220105", "url": "https://genius.com/7220105", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinking Bout You", "line": "It go U-N-L-V It go, it go U-N-L-V It go U-N-L-V, U-N-L-V Uptown Nigga Living Violent Do I smell beef?", "vault_lines": ["It go, it go U-N-L-V"], "meaning": "Same lyrics from “6th & Baronne” which this song samples. U.N.L.V. was a trio signed to Cash Money from 1993-1997. U.N.L.V. stands for Uptown Niggas Livin Violent.\n\nU.N.L.V. was New Orleans-based rap group made up of the rappers Tec-9, Lil' Ya, and Yella Boy.", "annotation_id": "7220008", "url": "https://genius.com/7220008", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
