{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinkin About You", "line": "I’mma take it uptown, uptown", "vault_lines": ["I'mma take it uptown, uptown"], "meaning": "Uptown is an area in New Orleans, in which Weezy’s hometown of Hollygrove is a subdistrict\n\n\n\nIt is also a reference to Drake’s song “Uptown” that features Weezy and Bun B", "annotation_id": "2249359", "url": "https://genius.com/2249359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinkin About You", "line": "Oops upside your head I said oops upside your head", "vault_lines": ["Oops upside your head"], "meaning": "A nod to The Gap Band’s 1979 jam “Oops Upside Your Head”.  Snoop also paid tribute to this same tune with his classic “Snoop’s Upside Ya Head”", "annotation_id": "2165997", "url": "https://genius.com/2165997", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinkin About You", "line": "[Break]", "vault_lines": ["Come on, come on, come on, come"], "meaning": "The break here has a tuba bass line reminiscent of the oft-sampled (especially in bounce music) break in Rebirth Brass Band’s “Feel Like Funkin' It Up.”\n\nDa' Sha Ra, for example, used it on “Bootin' Up”\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fs10a2Ck38Q#t=0m12s", "annotation_id": "2165975", "url": "https://genius.com/2165975", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinkin About You", "line": "Shout for the 17, shout for the Hollygrove Shout for the 17", "vault_lines": ["Shout for the 17, shout for the Hollygrove"], "meaning": "Hollygrove, in New Orleans' 17th Ward, is the childhood home of Lil Wayne and Mack Maine and one of the areas ruined in Hurricane Katrina. Even though Wayne now lives in Miami, he fits a shout-out to the city in nearly every song, like “Kush” and “Mr. Carter.”\n\n\n\nHe even has his hometown tattooed on his stomach.", "annotation_id": "2161919", "url": "https://genius.com/2161919", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thinkin About You", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-thinkin-about-you-lyrics", "genius_title": "Thinkin About You", "genius_id": 212948, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Think I’m Lyin", "line": "Drop that coke in that hot water and tell that bitch to hold her nose", "vault_lines": ["Drop that coke in that hot water and tell that bitch to hold her nose"], "meaning": "Dropping coke in hot water is making crack:\n\nTo make crack, powder cocaine is dissolved in a mixture of water and either ammonia or sodium bicarbonate (baking soda). The mixture is boiled to separate out the solid, and then it’s cooled.\n\nHis advising of her to “hold her nose” is in order to avoid inhaling his crack.", "annotation_id": "3364125", "url": "https://genius.com/3364125", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Think I’m Lyin", "line": "I’m Bo Jack in Egypt, that Wraith smell like reefer", "vault_lines": ["I'm Bo Jack in Egypt, that Wraith smell like reefer"], "meaning": "BoJack is the main antagonist of the 1993 film Dragon Ball Z. He is the leader of the Galaxy Soldiers. This name means “arrogance” or “audacity” in Japanese.\n\n\n\nTyga as he claims to be: the leader in Egypt, and his Rolls Royce Wraith smells like marijuana, due to the highly usage of it.", "annotation_id": "3357763", "url": "https://genius.com/3357763", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Think I’m Lyin", "line": "Who that, nigga? I beat them, like Redman, I’ll be dat", "vault_lines": ["Who that, nigga? I beat them, like Redman, I'll be dat"], "meaning": "Paying Homage somewhat to the rapper Redman as red has a song named “I’ll Bee Dat”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Si186d57Ra4\n\nBeating a nigga can also be takin as a nod to redman as he was a playable character in the popular “Def Jam Fight For New York” game\n\n\n\nRedman said the very strange things in game too like\n\n “Imma rip your eyeballs out, and put em on my kneecaps, and call you Kneezy”!", "annotation_id": "3354958", "url": "https://genius.com/3354958", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Think I’m Lyin", "line": "LIV on Sundays", "vault_lines": ["Drop that coke in that hot water"], "meaning": "LIV nightclub in Miami has special events on Sundays, which Wayne frequently attends.", "annotation_id": "3353418", "url": "https://genius.com/3353418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Think I’m Lyin", "line": "I’m a dog like Rin Tin Tin, fuck y’all niggas, y’all some hoes", "vault_lines": ["I'm a dog like Rin Tin Tin, fuck y'all niggas, y'all some hoes"], "meaning": "Tune is a dog like the German Shepherd Rin Tin Tin, the dog featured in the American childrens television series The Adventures of Rin Tin Tin which aired from 1954-1959. Tune means that he is a dog and only cares about one thing, chasing that pussy!", "annotation_id": "3351610", "url": "https://genius.com/3351610", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
