{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Want My Blood", "line": "’Cause we deep as the mobb, so let Prodigy drink", "vault_lines": ["'Cause we deep as the mobb, so let Prodigy drink"], "meaning": "This line is a play on the hip hop duo Mobb Deep, which consists of rappers Prodigy and Havoc.\n\nProdigy of the Queensbridge New York rap duo had passed away in June of 2017, Wayne pours out his lean as a gesture/celebration towards his life.", "annotation_id": "16525137", "url": "https://genius.com/16525137", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Want My Blood", "line": "And I lean to the side and pour out a lil’ drank", "vault_lines": ["And I lean to the side and pour out a lil' drank"], "meaning": "This is a play on words as “drank” is another name for “lean.”", "annotation_id": "16525131", "url": "https://genius.com/16525131", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Want My Blood", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Dj-kay-slay-they-want-my-blood-lyrics", "genius_title": "They Want My Blood", "genius_id": 4238274, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "And my right wrist is looking like a cracked-open egg, that’s— White and yellow diamonds, adjust your lighting", "vault_lines": ["And my right wrist is looking like a cracked-open egg, that's—"], "meaning": "At this time, Wayne was known for his extensive and unique jewelry collection, which he’s always had an affinity for mixing colors and metals.\n\nHere’s an awesome close up pic of Wayne’s Breitling(?) watch with a yellow diamond bezel from June 2006 (1 month after this mixtape was released)\n\n\n\nAnd here’s another picture from two weeks earlier, showing him stacking gold and silver diamond bracelets.", "annotation_id": "40928090", "url": "https://genius.com/40928090", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "And my nigga Tez Po been riding with me since pegs", "vault_lines": ["And my nigga Tez Po been riding with me since pegs"], "meaning": "This is about Cortez ‘Tez’ Bryant, who was Wayne’s long time manager, and friend since childhood.\n\nThis line has a great double meaning, as Tez has been “riding with” or sticking with Wayne throughout his career, so long in fact that they were literally riding together on the pegs of a bike, as children do.\n\n\n\nThrowback photo of Wayne (left) and Tez (right) during the Sqad Up days\n\n\n\n\nTwo kids sharing a bike, the kid in the back is riding on the pegs", "annotation_id": "40927957", "url": "https://genius.com/40927957", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "I’m— The fireman, she just call me when she steamin", "vault_lines": ["The fireman, she just call me when she steamin"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Wayne’s hit song, Fireman off his album Tha Carter II, which had released about 6 months prior to this track.", "annotation_id": "40927909", "url": "https://genius.com/40927909", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "I got ’em so mad, but, “Oh, I think they like me” (Gangsta Gri-Zillz!)", "vault_lines": ["I got 'em so mad, but, \"Oh, I think they like me\" (Gangsta Gri-Zillz!)"], "meaning": "“Oh I Think They Like Me”\n\nWayne is quoting the 2005 hit “I Think They Like Me” by Dem Franchize Boyz. He’s pointing out the irony that his haters are so obsessed with his success that their “madness” actually looks like infatuation. By using their own jealousy to prove he is the center of attention, he’s suggesting that if you’re watching him that closely, you’re basically a fan in denial.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w5vxVuee5qA", "annotation_id": "39748466", "url": "https://genius.com/39748466", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "But I’m never doing nothing, ’cause I’m always getting money", "vault_lines": ["But I'm never doing nothing, 'cause I'm always getting money"], "meaning": "Wayne is known for his insane work ethic and dedication to the craft, so saying he does nothing is bold. Wayne plays on this by saying he’s never doing nothing, because if he was doing nothing, he’d still always be getting paid, which is something.", "annotation_id": "31872670", "url": "https://genius.com/31872670", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "Leave your whole head empty like a straight pumpkin", "vault_lines": ["Leave your whole head empty like a straight pumpkin"], "meaning": "“Leave your head empty” is in reference to shooting someone in the head. Wayne compares this persons’ head to a pumpkin in reference to the empty space inside of a pumpkin. Wayne headshot this person.", "annotation_id": "31872640", "url": "https://genius.com/31872640", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "OK, OK, OK. Mhm, mm, mhm. That’s what I’m talking ’bout, man. I killed that shit, man. Man, that right there—it’s easy, man. You know what I mean? Give me something else, man, Drama. I’m on fire, man, rock. Watch this, man!", "vault_lines": ["Track #3 off Dedication 2. Wayne raps over Dem Franchise Boyz' “Oh, I Think They Like Me”."], "meaning": "Wayne is referencing the previous track on the Dedication 2 –  ‘Get 'Em’. He did kill that shit.", "annotation_id": "20008189", "url": "https://genius.com/20008189", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "Let’s do this for Hollygrove!", "vault_lines": ["Let's do this for Hollygrove!"], "meaning": "Wayne grew up in Hollygrove", "annotation_id": "19320150", "url": "https://genius.com/19320150", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "I’m fresh, yeah, the Gucci sweats came with the creases", "vault_lines": ["I'm fresh, yeah, the Gucci sweats came with the creases"], "meaning": "The Gucci sweatpants he’s wearing came with creases in them which shows that Wayne wears his brand new clothes and gets new ones before the creases go away.", "annotation_id": "15655424", "url": "https://genius.com/15655424", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "Wayne’s getting money like Damon and Keenan", "vault_lines": ["Wayne's getting money like Damon and Keenan"], "meaning": "Brothers Damon and Keenen Wayans came to fame as co-creators of the sketch comedy series In Living Color before moving on to writing, directing, and acting in feature films.", "annotation_id": "14130835", "url": "https://genius.com/14130835", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "All the niggas tryna hate me, and them bitches tryna have me, I’m a—", "vault_lines": ["All the niggas tryna hate me, and them bitches tryna have me, I'm a—"], "meaning": "Men hate Weezy because they’re of his skills and accomplishments. Wayne is basically boasting that males are jealous of him and his success, which doesn’t matter because the girls lust him for it.\n\nWe see this idea eloquently illustrated for us by Lil Wayne’s protege Drake, who knows a thing or two about successful himself", "annotation_id": "2727875", "url": "https://genius.com/2727875", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "Sure, honey, I done heard what you said But if a nigga really cared, you’d already be dead", "vault_lines": ["Sure, honey, I done heard what you said"], "meaning": "He could be referring to either people talking shit in person, or on songs.\n\nIf Wayne actually cared enough about you, he’d already have dissed you back and ended your whole career. However, much like Drake said, responding to petty insults will only make them more relevant so it’s not even worth the time.", "annotation_id": "2725888", "url": "https://genius.com/2725888", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "Hollygrove my barrio", "vault_lines": ["Track #3 off Dedication 2. Wayne raps over Dem Franchise Boyz' “Oh, I Think They Like Me”."], "meaning": "Barrio is the Spanish word for neighborhood.\n\nWayne grew up in Hollygrove, an area in the 17th ward of New Orleans. Wayne represents his hood whenever he can and even has a “17” tattoo on his stomach dedicated to them.", "annotation_id": "2597799", "url": "https://genius.com/2597799", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "And boy, we can beef like Magnolia and Calliope", "vault_lines": ["And boy, we can beef like Magnolia and Calliope"], "meaning": "The “nolia” refers to the Magnolia Projects and the “calio” refers to the Calliope Projects – both traditional rivals in Lil Wayne’s hometown of New Orleans.\n\nBoth are extremely run-down and impoverished areas; especially after Hurricane Katrina.", "annotation_id": "2597792", "url": "https://genius.com/2597792", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "They Still Like Me", "line": "Came in a Corniche", "vault_lines": ["Left in a Porsche, came in a Corniche"], "meaning": "A Koenigsegg is a Swedish super car and one of the most expensive cars in the world.", "annotation_id": "306973", "url": "https://genius.com/306973", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
