{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "These Hoes", "line": "I stuck it, I stick it, I strike it, I struck it She suck it", "vault_lines": ["I stuck it, I stick it, I strike it, I struck it"], "meaning": "Incredible alliteration.", "annotation_id": "36084237", "url": "https://genius.com/36084237", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "These Hoes", "line": "With Mother Earth and that bitch told me I was adopted", "vault_lines": ["With Mother Earth and that bitch told me I was adopted"], "meaning": "Wayne has often referred to himself as a martian or as not a human being.\n\nHere he says that he has been staying on Earth despite not being from here just like how an adopted son stays with his mother even though he is not her biological son.\n\nIt’s interesting how Wayne refers to the Earth as his mother here because on several songs in the past, he has depicted himself as having sexual intercourse with the Earth. Then again, he is adopted so I guess it is excusable.\n\n‘'And Imma keep fuckin’ this world, ‘till you motherfuckers come for me’'", "annotation_id": "36084204", "url": "https://genius.com/36084204", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "These Hoes", "line": "I wore some Vans to a wedding (Oh) It was at the House of Versace, me and Kanye was spotted (Oh) He offered me some wings (Oh) I told him, “Don’t even bother, I’m already flyin’”", "vault_lines": ["I worе some Vans to a wedding (Oh)"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne references a viral video of him and Kanye West at 2Chainz’s wedding in 2018.\n\nhttps://m.youtube.com/watch?v=xNSrUTp5kxE\n\n“he offered me some wings, i told him don’t even bother, i’m already flying” is a metaphor for him being high already and don’t need wings to fly", "annotation_id": "30723808", "url": "https://genius.com/30723808", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "These Hoes", "line": "Gave me head like a marshmallow, then she dip low, go DJ", "vault_lines": ["Gave me head like a marshmallow, then she dip low, go DJ"], "meaning": "Marshmello is a DJ who wears a helmet on his head. dip low is worldplay for Diplo another DJ. go Dj is a single of the THa carter.", "annotation_id": "25224746", "url": "https://genius.com/25224746", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "These Hoes", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-these-hoes-lyrics", "genius_title": "These Hoes", "genius_id": 6289386, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Way I Are (Dance with Somebody)", "line": "Bloody noses, speeding cars (Ayy) Lethal doses, desperate hearts", "vault_lines": ["Bloody noses, speeding cars (Ayy)"], "meaning": "The whole song was based off the message to my old record label. Somebody met me and they were like, “B, you’re too much in the studio. You got to be out more. You got to be seen. You got to be in more paparazzi pictures. You got to have more famous friends. You got to be in the mix.”\n\nI was being sarcastic. The whole song is actually completely sarcastic. The verses are sarcastic. It’s all just me kind of laughing and not taking it too seriously. That’s what the bridge is, like, bloody noses, speeding cars, lethal doses, desperate hearts. Roll it up. Roll it up because we’re so ill. Heaven knows we love the thrill.\n\nIt’s like, no, I don’t want to play the part. I don’t want to go to your parties. I don’t want to get high just because it’s cool. If I want to get to get high it’s because I want to on my own dime or my own time. I’m going to do what I want and I’m not going to be following the pack. If I want to be in the studio and be a nerd and order pizza and watch, whatever, a cooking show, that’s what I’m going to do. I’m not going to be up all in the Hollywood scene. That’s not me and that’s not what I’m doing.", "annotation_id": "12294828", "url": "https://genius.com/12294828", "state": "verified", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Way I Are (Dance with Somebody)", "line": "Roll it up ’cause we so ill (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Roll it up 'cause we so ill (Ooh)"], "meaning": "You’re in Hollywood, you’re in LA. You know, roll up a joint. Everybody smokes some weed sometimes, and you write a song or something, but you don’t do it all the time. If that is what you do, go ahead and do it, but if it’s not what you do, don’t do it. I’m 27, so as you get older you make your own decisions and you should be smart. You shouldn’t follow the crowd and what the crowd’s doing. You do what you want.", "annotation_id": "12294823", "url": "https://genius.com/12294823", "state": "verified", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Way I Are (Dance with Somebody)", "line": "Don’t matter who you are Just love me the way I are", "vault_lines": ["Don't matter who you are"], "meaning": "I think the truest form of love is really accepting somebody for who they are and all their imperfections. I think that the goal in life is really to find people who just love you with all your problems and your imperfections and your flaws. I think that’s what that means. It’s just love me for who I am, except I want it to be grammatically incorrect because it’s fun. I like to irk people.\n\nEverybody’s like, “Why is it the way I are?” I have English teachers going on the YouTube, being like, “It’s the way I am.” It’s like, “Don’t matter who you are, just love me the way I am.” No. Don’t matter who are you, just love me the way I are. It’s just better, double ares. It’s art.", "annotation_id": "12294818", "url": "https://genius.com/12294818", "state": "verified", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Way I Are (Dance with Somebody)", "line": "So let’s let our hearts bleed, till they turn to rust Gonna live it up, ’cause it’s dangerous", "vault_lines": ["So let's let our hearts bleed, till they turn to rust"], "meaning": "I don’t know what I was thinking. I think I had those lyrics written somewhere in my computer or something. I just showed them to the other songwriters. I was like, “Hey, I have these lyrics written. Does this work for this?” They were like, “Yeah, it means just go live your life. Do you.” I was like, “Okay. Let’s put that in there.”\n\nI thought because the song is so simple in the verses and so simple in the hook, I thought that maybe it could use a poetic moment lyrically in the pre-choruses and the bridge so it wouldn’t be so simple throughout.", "annotation_id": "12294797", "url": "https://genius.com/12294797", "state": "verified", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Way I Are (Dance with Somebody)", "line": "Ooh-ooh, ooh-ooh, ooh But I still wanna dance with somebody (Tunechi)", "vault_lines": ["But I still wanna dance with somebody (Tunechi)"], "meaning": "I don’t know what happened, but we were in the studio, and we were trying to find some way to say “accept me for who I am,” but in a fun way.\n\nObviously, it’s dancing, but what we’re saying is basically, “I want to find somebody who accepts me for who I am. Just enjoy this moment with me.”\n\nIt was that moment we were like, “Oh, that is so good.” That is such an epic moment. We were like, “We have to keep this line. It’s too awesome.” When we went into the studio, we weren’t expecting to write a Whitney interpolation. It’s kind of like you’re remaking the song in your own way. It happened very naturally.", "annotation_id": "12294760", "url": "https://genius.com/12294760", "state": "verified", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Way I Are (Dance with Somebody)", "line": "I’m sorry, I’m not the most pretty", "vault_lines": ["I'm sorry, I'm not the most pretty"], "meaning": "I love myself. I do think I’m a pretty girl, but there will always be somebody more prettier than you. That’s just life. It’s me saying to the label, or anybody, “I am sorry that I’m not what you think is pretty. I don’t fit your standards of what pretty is.”", "annotation_id": "12294723", "url": "https://genius.com/12294723", "state": "verified", "votes": 86, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Way I Are (Dance with Somebody)", "line": "I’ll never ever sing like Whitney", "vault_lines": ["I'll never ever sing like Whitney"], "meaning": "Bebe Rexha references the late Whitney Houston, one of the best-selling music artists of all-time. Rexha’s song has “Dance With Somebody” in the title, as does Whitney Houston’s song, “I Wanna Dance With Somebody (Who Loves Me)”, which Rexha pays homage to in the chorus.\n\nThough both Rexha and Houston’s songs have that same line in both of their song titles, Rexha is saying that she knows her voice won’t compare with the powerful and exceptional vocal talent that Houston was known for.", "annotation_id": "11866839", "url": "https://genius.com/11866839", "state": "accepted", "votes": 192, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Way I Are (Dance with Somebody)", "line": "I just wanna dance with somebody (Hey) But I could never ever dance like Bobby (Hey)", "vault_lines": ["But I could never ever dance like Bobby (Hey)"], "meaning": "Wayne repeats the hook, which interpolates the  chorus from the Whitney Houston song “I Wanna Dance With Somebody (Who Loves Me).” In the next line, he references the late pop star’s former husband Bobby Brown, who was known for some fancy footwork back in the day.", "annotation_id": "11865976", "url": "https://genius.com/11865976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Way I Are (Dance with Somebody)", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Bebe-rexha-the-way-i-are-dance-with-somebody-lyrics", "genius_title": "The Way I Are (Dance with Somebody)", "genius_id": 2866364, "source": "api"}
