{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "Situation’s gettin’ fishy and I don’t eat anchovies", "vault_lines": ["Situation's gettin' fishy and I don't eat anchovies"], "meaning": "Clearly a play with the Anchovy, a type of fish which is used in various types of dishes around the word and “situation’s getting fishy” is an idiom for a difficult, awkward, or tricky problem that is hard to get out of.", "annotation_id": "40229647", "url": "https://genius.com/40229647", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "I hope this feelin’ last for fuckin’ ever I don’t wanna come back down, let me stay above the ground", "vault_lines": ["I hope this feelin' last for fuckin' ever"], "meaning": "Mac shares his feeling of wanting to stay high forever, alluding to when he comes out of his high, he feels down and has to confront his own issues.", "annotation_id": "32525296", "url": "https://genius.com/32525296", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "[Instrumental Outro]", "vault_lines": ["Sometimes I wonder who the fuck I am"], "meaning": "The outro from the mixtape/original version of “The Question” was altered for the remastered version that was added to streaming services in May 2018. Originally, it included an excerpt from the 2004 movie Eternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mind, one of Mac’s favorite movies:\n\nStop it\nI could die right now, Clem\nI’m just happy\nI’ve never felt that before\nI’m just exactly where I want to be\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tIT3kcZMgQ8&t=85s\n\nMac later collaborated with Jon Brion, who composed the soundtrack for the movie, on his albums Swimming and Circles. He also sampled a song from the movie on “The Quest,” which was released posthumously on the Watching Movies with the Sound Off 10th anniversary edition.", "annotation_id": "31643018", "url": "https://genius.com/31643018", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "Man, my voice probably sounds mad raspy right now", "vault_lines": ["Man, my voice probably sounds mad raspy right now"], "meaning": "opioids (probably lean in this case) cause your voice to become raspy", "annotation_id": "31297700", "url": "https://genius.com/31297700", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "I kill ’em like Nicole Simpson", "vault_lines": ["All I do is kill 'em, I kill 'em like Nicole"], "meaning": "Nicole Brown Simpson was the ex-wife of the former professional American football player, O. J. Simpson, to whom she was married from 1985 to 1992. Two years after her divorce from Simpson, Brown was stabbed to death at her Los Angeles home, on June 12, 1994, along with her friend, waiter Ron Goldman.", "annotation_id": "29254559", "url": "https://genius.com/29254559", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "Done so much in my short lifetime, but I haven’t done shit", "vault_lines": ["Done so much in my short lifetime, but I haven't done shit"], "meaning": "Miller shares his profound feeling that, although being already an accomplished artist at the time, he hasn’t done anything truly meaningful to himself.", "annotation_id": "28445957", "url": "https://genius.com/28445957", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "If that ho play with me, I whoop that chick like Terrence Howard", "vault_lines": ["If that ho play with me, I whoop that chick like Terrence Howard"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne could be refering here to the accusation of conjugal physical abuse the actor Terrence Howard faced from Michelle Ghent in 2011", "annotation_id": "28442709", "url": "https://genius.com/28442709", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "First, I shook a million hands, then I took a million pictures But I’m a hostage in my own world", "vault_lines": ["First, I shook a million hands, then I took a million pictures"], "meaning": "In this retrospective moment, Mac Miller refers to the fact that getting famous bring a lot of social relations by meeting a lot of “known” people on a regular basis.\n\nBut this popularity actually isolates the artist, because his social life is becoming more and more superficial. Thus the idea of being hostage of the celebrity", "annotation_id": "28442649", "url": "https://genius.com/28442649", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "Smoke ’em like Winstons", "vault_lines": [", flag crimson, smoke 'em like Winstons"], "meaning": "Winstons is a brand of cigarrets.", "annotation_id": "27601634", "url": "https://genius.com/27601634", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "I think they underestimate the grind I do to bring this dough, and I’m only twenty years old I wonder why I sip this devil juice, ’cause it feel incredible", "vault_lines": ["I think they underestimate the grind"], "meaning": "Mac Miller was introduced into the music industry at the age of 15 and now at 20, having to deal with the stressors of being famous from such a young age takes a toll. It is not surprising he turns to drugs and alcohol to numb his mental health problems. When working in the music industry there is a heightened normalcy with abusing drugs and alcohol; everyone does it which is why musicians have such high rates of alcohol problems.(Wilhelm et. al 2004).", "annotation_id": "27043474", "url": "https://genius.com/27043474", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "See, I come from a place where stars never shine And drama is accepted, credit cards are declined Everybody gotta die, but I ain’t everybody", "vault_lines": ["See, I come from a place where stars never shine"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne grew up in the impoverished 17th Ward of New Orleans, Louisiana. He liked rapping from a young age but his mother told him to give it up. Having the seemingly only way to make it out of his city and make a name for himself taken away from him, he was driven to a dark mental state where at age 12, he attempted suicide. Growing up in inner city communities fosters symptoms related to mental health disorders such as depression when it can be hard to seem like your life has purpose in such a stressful environment. (Horowitz et. al 2005)\nhttps://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/lil-wayne-on-attempted-suicide-age-12-9615310/", "annotation_id": "27043312", "url": "https://genius.com/27043312", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "’Cause everybody seems to have it, but to me, it seems they lack it", "vault_lines": ["'Cause everybody seems to have it, but to me, it seems they lack it"], "meaning": "Everybody on social media these days tries to appear to be “woke”, but mac knows that no one is really “woke”. Everyone is as lost as him.", "annotation_id": "24880841", "url": "https://genius.com/24880841", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Question", "line": "Show ’em what you got, tiger", "vault_lines": ["Show 'em what you got, tiger"], "meaning": "This was one of Mac’s first features by a top respected artist in the game. This could possibly be him hyping himself up to really drop hard but meaningful bars that Lil Wayne\nwas all about at the time of this release. At the time of this release Wayne also dropped his Dedication 4 mixtape. One of his most sought after mix tapes.", "annotation_id": "18665627", "url": "https://genius.com/18665627", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
