{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Profit", "line": "Joey the Mayor, I get Keys to the city", "vault_lines": ["Joey the Mayor, I get Keys to the city"], "meaning": "This is a pun & a play on words: he is the self-proclaimed Mayor of the City, since he runs it due to the large amount of money and power his drug control has garnered him, so therefore he gets the keys to the city meaning…\n\n1.) He can go anywhere in the city, as he literally holds the keys, alluding to the fact that he is respected through the city.\n\n2.) He is using keys, in the drug context, meaning he gets “keys of cocaine” to distribute to the city. ($_$)\n\n3.) Lastly, the Mayor bestows a reputable citizen with an award titled the “Key to the City,” Fat Joey gave himself this award hypothetically speaking due to the aforementioned reasons. He runs the city, he brings in money for the city, & he is a role model to the city.\n\nFun Fact: Juicy J has actually obtained a key to the city from Memphis, Tennessee.", "annotation_id": "1575683", "url": "https://genius.com/1575683", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Profit", "line": "I’m New York’s living legend", "vault_lines": ["I'm New York's living legend"], "meaning": "Fat Joe is not lying, he has a substantially relevant history in rap having rapped alongside legends like Big Pun, Big L, Lord Finesse, & even DJ Premier.", "annotation_id": "1575651", "url": "https://genius.com/1575651", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Profit", "line": "The sun even shines on dog shit", "vault_lines": ["The sun even shines on dog shit"], "meaning": "A better way of saying “Every dark cloud has a silver lining.” I mean, even dog shit can see sunshine sometimes. Right? That’s a positive. I believe.", "annotation_id": "788146", "url": "https://genius.com/788146", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Profit", "line": "I’m from New Orleans Homeless", "vault_lines": ["I'm from New Orleans"], "meaning": "Referring to how Hurricane Katrina left people who lived in New Orleans homeless.", "annotation_id": "788143", "url": "https://genius.com/788143", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Profit", "line": "I’m sitting in the coupe wit the titties outted The nipples chrome", "vault_lines": ["I'm sitting in the coupe wit the titties outted"], "meaning": "If the nipples are chrome, I’m guessing that refers to his rims. So the titties must be his wheels. Wayne likes his wheels 22’s or higher!\n\nWayne is sitting on Big Rims! Status Quo symbol.", "annotation_id": "787345", "url": "https://genius.com/787345", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Profit", "line": "The money knows me better than anybody", "vault_lines": ["The money knows me better than anybody"], "meaning": "A common rap theme where most rappers say that they can’t trust anyone except for their money.\n\nAlso, Wayne has been paid for so long, spent so much time with money, that it…the money…(yes, rappers do use personification as well) knows him better than his friends. That’s how ambitious he is.", "annotation_id": "787344", "url": "https://genius.com/787344", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Profit", "line": "Fuck the coach I keep shooting like Kobe", "vault_lines": ["Fuck the coach I keep shooting like Kobe"], "meaning": "He’s comparing the way that he keeps shooting his guns to the way Kobe Bryant shoots his basketball. Kobe shoots and doesn’t hold back, not even his coach can stop him.", "annotation_id": "787342", "url": "https://genius.com/787342", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
