{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "Them Spanish girls love me like I’m Aventura", "vault_lines": ["Type of money, everybody actin' like they knew ya"], "meaning": "Aventura is a popular Dominican bachata group featuring lead singer Romeo Santos, who Drake worked with in 2014 on the song ‘Odio’.", "annotation_id": "22455046", "url": "https://genius.com/22455046", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "I’m calling niggas out like the umpire", "vault_lines": ["I'm calling niggas out like the umpire"], "meaning": "In baseball and tennis, umpires call players out.\n\n\n\nSimilarly, Wayne’s not afraid to name names or get rid of anyone in his way.\n\nWeezy’s not the first to say this: Black Thought said it in “Web 20/20,” and the most intellectually gifted member of the Wu-Tang Clan said something similar.", "annotation_id": "8459630", "url": "https://genius.com/8459630", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "[Produced by T-Minus]", "vault_lines": ["Type of money, everybody actin' like they knew ya"], "meaning": "According to the liner notes, the track was produced by T-Minus, and the bass part was performed by Noah “40” Shebib. There are no samples credited, but there are two interpolations, both occurring at the end of a verse:\n\n\nOn Drake’s verse, he interpolates a line from “She Will” by Lil Wayne (which featured Drake and was also produced by T-Minus)\nOn Wayne’s verse, he interpolates a line from “Baby Got Back” by Sir Mix-a-Lot", "annotation_id": "8459609", "url": "https://genius.com/8459609", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "Tell Uncle Luke, “I’m out in Miami, too” Clubbin’ hard, fuckin’ women, there ain’t much to do", "vault_lines": ["Type of money, everybody actin' like they knew ya"], "meaning": "Southern rap pioneer, former 2 Live Crew impresario and former Miami mayoral candidate Luther “Luke” Campbell recently put a few hip-hop personalities on blast for living in Miami while not giving back to the community. If they don’t change their ways by January 2012, Luke threatens to have their “Miami cards” revoked. The Miami card is a free pass to all of Miami’s city-owned attractions. It became irrelevant however as Luke lost the election.\n\nThe open letter mentions “Lil Wayne, DJ Khaled, Puff Daddy, and all their boys”. Apparently Drake feels like he was worthy of inclusion by name as well.", "annotation_id": "8457536", "url": "https://genius.com/8457536", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "Go Uptown, New York City, bitch", "vault_lines": ["Type of money, everybody actin' like they knew ya"], "meaning": "Uptown NYC is a very fashion-minded neighborhood with little tourism. Being a fashion connoisseur himself, Drake must spend a lot of time in the Uptown area.\n\nThere is also a large Hispanic population in Upper Manhattan, specifically in Washington Heights or the upper-western side of Manhattan, which ties in with the next line about Spanish girls loving him.\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to Drizzy’s song “Uptown” off of So Far Gone.", "annotation_id": "8457341", "url": "https://genius.com/8457341", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "Type of money, everybody actin’ like they knew ya", "vault_lines": ["Type of money, everybody actin' like they knew ya"], "meaning": "Drake’s making sufficient sums of money for fake people to come out of the woodwork and act like they knew him back when he was up-and-coming.\n\nHe’s previously mentioned how people try to use himin the “Say What’s Real” freestyle:\n\nAnd don’t listen to anybody that knew me\nCause to have known me would\nMean that there’s a new me\nAnd if you think I changed in the slightest\nCould of fooled me", "annotation_id": "8457304", "url": "https://genius.com/8457304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "I’m the fuckin’ man, y’all don’t get it, do ya?", "vault_lines": ["Type of money, everybody actin' like they knew ya"], "meaning": "Drake’s rise to the top of the rap game has been a swift move. His relatively short career has spawned major success, such as getting rich off a mixtape and his debut album topping Billboard. Still after so much success he’s still slept on by hip hop heads who say Drake’s too soft.", "annotation_id": "8457295", "url": "https://genius.com/8457295", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "Real L.A. nigga, chucks with the gun drawn", "vault_lines": ["Real L.A. nigga, chucks with the gun drawn"], "meaning": "Chuck Taylor All Stars are commonly worn among gangsters in California, who are widely understood to not take any chances and therefore avoid using a holster for their weapons.", "annotation_id": "3370915", "url": "https://genius.com/3370915", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "Shout goes out to Niko, J and Chubbs, shouts to Gibbo", "vault_lines": ["Shout goes out to Niko, J and Chubbs, shouts to Gibbo"], "meaning": "Niko, J, and Chubbs are all part of Drake’s crew.\n\nNiko’s Drake’s good friend. Niko recommended a good barber to Drake when he was still just Jimmy on Degrassi. and the two have been BFFs ever since. In his lengthy Thank Me Later thank you’s, Drake calls Niko his “closest confidant.” He continued, “our friendship is what keeps me alive and focused, I always thought I was an only child buy my mother lied!! Haaa.” Aww. And when he’s not with Drake? He’s the father to a very cute daughter and apparently a decent fly fisherman. http://www.thefader.com/2013/10/03/fader-explains-drakes-boys/\n\nChubbs is Drake’s muscle. As he put it to Complex in 2011: “Everybody wants to poke and jab at Drake because they don’t feel like he will throw back. But nobody around here is going to let something happen to him at any time, especially me. I’m not ever going to let nothing happen to him. If it’s going to happen it’s going to happen to me first.” Maybe that’s why he’s the only OVO member to stay by Drake’s side during the Miami Vice style shoot-out at the end of the “Hold On We’re Going Home” video. He’s also Drake’s regular basketball buddy.\n\nRead more: http://www.thefader.com/2013/10/03", "annotation_id": "2463318", "url": "https://genius.com/2463318", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "Drawing on your face, you’re a clown, jack in the box", "vault_lines": ["Drawing on your face, you're a clown, jack in the box"], "meaning": "Another shot at Gucci Mane\n\n\nOnly clowns have drawings on their faces, so if you got  drawings/tattoos on your face then you’re a clown.\nif he pulls a gun to Gucci Mane’s face, he’s gonna shut up and pussy out, in other words, get back in his box, like a Jack in the box", "annotation_id": "448557", "url": "https://genius.com/448557", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Motto (Remix)", "line": "You funny little nigga, Duval", "vault_lines": ["You funny little nigga, Duval"], "meaning": "Tyga makes a reference to to Lil' Duval, a famous black comedian who has starred in films such as Meet the Blacks.", "annotation_id": "434343", "url": "https://genius.com/434343", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
