{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Leak", "line": "And I am Young Mula, and so is Twisty baby And you ever forget that", "vault_lines": ["Young mula baby, and yeah we so crazy"], "meaning": "Lil Twist is signed to Young Money, and Wayne created the label. Though it is tough to forget about them when Wayne brings it up in just about every one of his songs.", "annotation_id": "490145", "url": "https://genius.com/490145", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Leak", "line": "Ok Lil Twist I’m Kobe, but I’m shooting like Ginobli", "vault_lines": ["Ok Lil Twist I'm Kobe, but I'm shooting like Ginobli"], "meaning": "Weezy has dedicated a song to his friend Kobe Bryant in the past, but compares himself to the San Antonio Spurs' sharpshooter Manu Ginobili here.", "annotation_id": "490127", "url": "https://genius.com/490127", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Leak", "line": "I swear I’m a walking movie, you ain’t even gotta cue me", "vault_lines": ["I swear I'm a walking movie, you ain't even gotta cue me"], "meaning": "Cue, in theater or plays, is the signal for go or start. But Wayne’s life is like a never-ending movie, so he doesn’t have to worry about stopping and starting.", "annotation_id": "490116", "url": "https://genius.com/490116", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Leak", "line": "I’m the hip-hop rocka I’m the hip-hop doctor", "vault_lines": ["I'm the hip-hop rocka"], "meaning": "Wayne ventured into rock music on Rebirth, and played the role of hip-hop’s doctor on “Dr. Carter”.", "annotation_id": "490098", "url": "https://genius.com/490098", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Leak", "line": "It’s the microphone killa, microphone wrecker", "vault_lines": ["It's the microphone killa, microphone wrecker"], "meaning": "Literally killing the microphone is a long-running rap trope, meaning that your rhymes are so good the mic can’t handle them.", "annotation_id": "298514", "url": "https://genius.com/298514", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Leak", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-twist-the-leak-lyrics", "genius_title": "The Leak", "genius_id": 53143, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "I’m finna pop with the AK and dip I am just not feeling Nae Nae and Whip", "vault_lines": ["I'm finna pop with the AK and dip"], "meaning": "Watch Me (Whip/Nae Nae) is an nnoying dance that goes along with an equally annoying song. When they say “watch me whip” the hand and arm go to the front much like using a whip.\n\nLil Wayne shows up with an AK in one hand and syrup on the other because he’s not from the Nae Nae and Whip, and he doesn’t feel the dance even after popping a pill and eating a shroom.\n\nHe also plays it with ‘I am just not feeling Nae Nae weep’. Nae is Regina Carter, her daughter. Lil Wayne pops a pain pill to take away the pain of seeing her weep and sips syrup to numb the feeling", "annotation_id": "26230922", "url": "https://genius.com/26230922", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "And the pills have eyes, the pills have eyes And they peek-a-boo at us They seein’ through, through us It’s like pills have eyes, the pills have lives And they livin’ through, through us Livin’ through", "vault_lines": ["And the pills have eyes, the pills have eyes"], "meaning": "Wayne plays on the original bridge by The Weeknd:\n\nHills have eyes, the hills have eyes\n\nThe Weeknd was referencing the movie series The Hills Have Eyes to describe his predatory fans and paparazzis. However, Weezy knows the real killer and stalker is drug abuse: they possess him to the point where they seem to have a life of their own.\n\nHe even describes the pills to peek-a-boo over him, for they are so much bigger, yet control his emotions; reducing him to an infant. This also plays on the fact that drugs have raised him like a parent– which isn’t surprising, since he grew  up in a crime-ridden area of New Orleans.", "annotation_id": "8286284", "url": "https://genius.com/8286284", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "And we got that white girl if your nose runnin’", "vault_lines": ["And we got that white girl if your nose runnin'"], "meaning": "“White Girl” is slang for cocaine. Those on cocaine often have symptoms of a runny or red, irritated nose.", "annotation_id": "8283004", "url": "https://genius.com/8283004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "When I’m turnt up, that’s the real me When I’m turnt up, that’s the real me, yeah", "vault_lines": ["When I'm cupped up, that's the real me"], "meaning": "Much like The Weeknd, Wayne only feels like himself when he’s under the influence of some type of drug. This shouldn’t be surprising as drug use is often mentioned in Wayne’s lyrics.\n\nWayne has had some problems with addiction throughout his career, which he’s mentioned on multiple occasions.", "annotation_id": "8280803", "url": "https://genius.com/8280803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "Prescriptions got me feelin’ beaucoup shallow", "vault_lines": ["Prescriptions got me feelin' beaucoup shallow"], "meaning": "“Beaucoup” is French for very much or a lot, meaning that Wayne wants more for every pill he pops. He doesn’t mess around either; he goes straight to the strong prescription meds!", "annotation_id": "8280458", "url": "https://genius.com/8280458", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "You just tryna get me out my Polo", "vault_lines": ["You just tryna get me out my Polo"], "meaning": "“Polo” refers to Ralph Lauren brand clothing. The intentions of whatever girl Wayne is with are apparently obvious, she’s trying to get him out of his clothes. However, given the following verses, I’d say Tunechi is down with it.", "annotation_id": "8279691", "url": "https://genius.com/8279691", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "I know all my bitches is some homos", "vault_lines": ["I know all my bitches is some homos"], "meaning": "Technically speaking, if they’re into both Wayne and other women, they’re bisexual. Unless Wayne’s sex appeal is so grand that he’s got lesbians falling in love with only him, and no other guy.", "annotation_id": "8279328", "url": "https://genius.com/8279328", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "When I’m cupped up, that’s the real me When I’m cupped up, that’s the real me, yeah", "vault_lines": ["When I'm cupped up, that's the real me"], "meaning": "“Cupped up” means Wayne is double cupping, a traditional sign that he’s drinking Lean (Syrup). 2016 was full of think pieces about Wayne’s addiction to syrup, and how it may be slowly (or quickly) killing him.", "annotation_id": "8279054", "url": "https://genius.com/8279054", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "Sip so much a nigga need to relax How the fuck they expect me to relax? I got crocodile tears under this ski mask", "vault_lines": ["Pray so much a nigga need some kneepads"], "meaning": "Wayne is known to be an avid sipper of lean, a drug with side effects– such as irregular heartbeat and hallucinations– that would explain his mental state.\n\nFurthermore, he shows no remorse for those he slays. “Crocodile tears”, an expression used before in “Hello”, is defined by one who is only sad just for show, or displaying false guilt. This sprouted from the myth that crocodiles produce tears while eating and killing their prey.\n\nCriminals stereotypically wear ski masks while committing crimes that Wayne may display guilt from, though deep inside he is insincere.", "annotation_id": "8278902", "url": "https://genius.com/8278902", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "Me and all my goons in the bando Listenin’ to some old school Jay and Jaz-O Just got new cocaine before I saw you You gon’ have to take a fuckin’ sample Listenin’ to some old school Jay and Jaz-O And we still get the cocaine from Fernando", "vault_lines": ["Me and all my goons up in the bando"], "meaning": "A bando (syn. “trap house”) is slang for a house where illegal activity occurs (drug trade/use, prostitution), a place that Lil Wayne and co. frequent for leisure. This time around, they’re listening to Jay-Z and his mentor Jaz-O’s music and snorting cocaine, which Wayne “courteously” invites his addressee to use.\n\nPresumably, Wayne and co. are listening to “The Originator”, “Bring It On”, “Ain’t No Nigga”, “Rap Game / Crack Game” and/or “Let’s Go”. Listed are songs that Jay-Z and Jaz-O have collaborated on.\n\nLastly, Wayne is no stranger to this “Fernando” character. He references him on “Trap House”, a song from Sorry 4 the Wait 2:\n\nGot a goon named Fernando\nAt the front door your condo\nKnock knock, who’s there? He don’t care, he’s psycho", "annotation_id": "8278853", "url": "https://genius.com/8278853", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "I’m finna pop me a pain pill and sip I’m finna eat me a mushroom and trip", "vault_lines": ["I'm finna pop me a pain pill and sip"], "meaning": "Wayne has his trippy kit ready. After he pops a pill, he’s going to wash it down with some lean.\n\nMushrooms refer to the psychedelic drug “Psilocybin mushrooms”, which Wayne has dubbed himself the king of. Some effects include increased sensitivity towards light and feeling as if inanimate objects are “breathing”.", "annotation_id": "8278769", "url": "https://genius.com/8278769", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "Pray so much a nigga need some kneepads", "vault_lines": ["Pray so much a nigga need some kneepads"], "meaning": "Kneeling to pray is a very old practice. This tradition was a symbol of honor and humility when coming before someone of relative authority (f.e. king, master, God, etc.). Lil Wayne, a praying man, has been in this position so many times that it has harmed his knees, consequently seeking the help of knee pads, gear to provide padding for extended kneeling.\n\nAndré 3000 famously used a similar line in OutKast’s “Ms. Jackson”:\n\nI pray so much about it need some knee pads", "annotation_id": "8278684", "url": "https://genius.com/8278684", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "I already know you go commando", "vault_lines": ["I already know you go commando"], "meaning": "Lift up that mini-skirt, that’s my dinner desert\n\nGoing “commando” refers to not wearing any underwear. Wayne is letting her know he knows she doesn’t wear underwear and gets straight to the point. This way she knows he’s more than interested.", "annotation_id": "8278646", "url": "https://genius.com/8278646", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "You ridin’ me, my Magnum is your saddle Find out I was cummin’ and you swallow And let me stick my thumb up in your asshole", "vault_lines": ["You ridin' me, my Magnum is your saddle"], "meaning": "The girl is on top of Wayne’s “Magnum”, which is a popular condom line made by Trojan that is one of the biggest sizes, showing how large Wayne'e penis is. Because the girl is on top of his ‘Magnum\", she’s riding him during sex. He adds in the wordplay between riding and saddle by comparing himself to a horse.\n\nDuring the second line, Wayne makes a pun on the original lyrics from The Weeknd.\n\nFound out I was comin', sent your friends home\"\n\nWayne is about to finish, so the girl swallows for him, something Wayne is not shy about referencing.\n\nWhile the latter part of this verse is most likely a reference to Future’s line on Stick Talk. This isn’t the first time Wayne has mentioned sticking his thumb in a girl’s butt, as he’s known to be quite the freak in bed.", "annotation_id": "8278642", "url": "https://genius.com/8278642", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "I’m goin’ through some bullshit at the moment But all them mothafuckas know I’ll be back", "vault_lines": ["I'm goin' through some bullshit at the moment"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne’s label is refusing to release his highly anticipated album, Tha Carter V, but he wants to assure his fans that he’ll return, hopefully with the completed album.", "annotation_id": "8278622", "url": "https://genius.com/8278622", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "Xannies always send me off to dreamland Head startin’ to feelin’ like a bean bag", "vault_lines": ["Xannies always send me off to dreamland"], "meaning": "Xanax is a drug used to treat anxiety and panic disorder. It’s used by some people as a recreational drug due to it’s side effects like increased energy and hallucinations.\n\nBecause Weezy is on dreamland, he could be so fucked up to the point that could end up like Kevin Hart when he took ecstasy and started to fuck a bean bag as he told the audience on his stand-up show Let Me Explain.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/ii8ZwPv3FJA?t=2m18s", "annotation_id": "8278621", "url": "https://genius.com/8278621", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "In the middle of the summer sellin’ snow bunnies", "vault_lines": ["In the middle of the summer sellin' snow bunnies"], "meaning": "Snow bunny is slang that is used to refer to white women. Cocaine is often referred to as white girl, so Wayne is selling cocaine.\n\nNote that there isn’t any snow in summer but Wayne is still selling snow bunnies.", "annotation_id": "8278594", "url": "https://genius.com/8278594", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "[Verse 1]", "vault_lines": ["We still get them chickens for the low low"], "meaning": "These parts follow the exact same rhyme scheme as The Weeknd’s original, with plenty lines directly referencing the Toronto singer’s. The new superstar featured on the Dedication 5 cut, “I’m Good”.", "annotation_id": "8278579", "url": "https://genius.com/8278579", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "The sex look even better on the Go-Pro", "vault_lines": ["The sex look even better on the Go-Pro"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is not new to taping his sexual encounters and this night he’s making another movie.\n\nA Go-Pro is a popular brand of small action cameras, often used for extreme stunts. Weezy found another use however…", "annotation_id": "8278553", "url": "https://genius.com/8278553", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Hills", "line": "I just poured a 4, I’m moving slow-mo", "vault_lines": ["I just poured a 4, I'm moving slow-mo"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne just poured a 4oz bottle of codeine syrup, a key ingredient in lean, which is a drug frequently mentioned in Wayne’s lyrics.\n\n“Slow-mo” refers to one of its side effects, as it causes a “slowed” perception of time due to the drowsiness one feels.", "annotation_id": "8278552", "url": "https://genius.com/8278552", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
