{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Heat", "line": "Arm, leg, leg, arm, head", "vault_lines": ["I shoot your arm, leg, leg, arm, head"], "meaning": "According to the belief of the Nation of Gods and Earths, The first initials in “Arm, Leg, Leg, Arm, Head” creates the acronym, “A.L.L.A.H.” This represents the 360 degrees of man and man’s knowledge.", "annotation_id": "32932279", "url": "https://genius.com/32932279", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Heat", "line": "Murder my enemy, love thy brother And I ain’t never gave a shit about a motherfucker", "vault_lines": ["Murder my enemy, love thy brother"], "meaning": "Weezy makes use of the literary device known as an “Antithesis.” Inflicting violence upon an enemy while being peaceful to one’s brother, suggests gang affiliation, though Wayne and Birdman’s authenticity have been questioned before. While “love thy brother” is the famous Biblical “golden rule,” meaning to always be peaceful, Wayne rejects this command, claiming he never felt remorse for wrong doers (motherfuckers).", "annotation_id": "10878639", "url": "https://genius.com/10878639", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Heat", "line": "Me and my damn pistol Me and my girlfriend", "vault_lines": ["Me and my damn pistol"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Tupac’s song “Me And My Girl Friend,” where he juxtaposed his relationship with a handgun, to that of a ‘'ride or die’‘ girlfriend.\n\nI trust you dearly, I shoot blind", "annotation_id": "10878616", "url": "https://genius.com/10878616", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Heat", "line": "Shhh, the silence will speak to you", "vault_lines": ["Shhh, the silence will speak to you"], "meaning": "Weezy will kill these niggas with a silencer on his gun. He says practically the same thing 10 years later on a feature for Rick Ross on the song “Thug Cry”, among other times:\n\nI swear I got that silencer on that Mac 9 and I kill these niggas with silence\n\nWordplay:\n\nJuxtaposing words: silence and speak,", "annotation_id": "3042857", "url": "https://genius.com/3042857", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
