{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Days", "line": "The Fat Boys break up and Mike didn’t wake up", "vault_lines": ["The Fat Boys break up and Mike didn't wake up"], "meaning": "Possible interpolation of Jay-Z’s Ain’t No Love", "annotation_id": "38647493", "url": "https://genius.com/38647493", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Days", "line": "I also remember them days when I was layin’ on that hospital bed thinkin’ how many days I had left", "vault_lines": ["These are the days (Oh, RedOne"], "meaning": "It should be noted that “The Days” was originally recorded around 2013-2014 during the original recording sessions for Tha Carter V.\n\n2012 to 2013 was marked by health problems and hospitalizations for Lil Wayne, with him suffering multiple seizures in that time period.\n\nWayne reflects on the time he spent in the hospital and thinking about how much time he had left.", "annotation_id": "36880767", "url": "https://genius.com/36880767", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Days", "line": "(When I was behind them bars, just countin’ the days)", "vault_lines": ["These are the days (Oh, RedOne"], "meaning": "He was in the prison 8 months", "annotation_id": "36466481", "url": "https://genius.com/36466481", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Days", "line": "Based on a true story, I don’t need an editor", "vault_lines": ["Based on a true story, I don't need an editor"], "meaning": "Weezy’s music comes from completely genuine experiences he’s garnered throughout his life, and it’s undeniable. Unapologetically, he trusts in his ability to present his perspective honestly and with integrity.\n\nHe doesn’t see a need to sugarcoat his truths or spin his narrative to make it more palatable. He doesn’t need an editor because he’s already got a compelling true story to present.", "annotation_id": "36074098", "url": "https://genius.com/36074098", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Days", "line": "Oh, RedOne", "vault_lines": ["These are the days (Oh, RedOne"], "meaning": "RedOne’s producer tag. He is one of the two producers in this song, along with DVLP.\n\nThis particular tag is sampled from the intro of Lady Gaga’s Just Dance.", "annotation_id": "35816788", "url": "https://genius.com/35816788", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Days", "line": "And if you think I’m lyin’, hook me to the polygraph", "vault_lines": ["And if you think I'm lyin', hook me to the polygraph"], "meaning": "Polygraph is a machine designed to detect and record changes in physiological characteristics, such as a person’s pulse and breathing rates, used especially as a lie detector.\n\nDefinition from Oxford Languages", "annotation_id": "35812071", "url": "https://genius.com/35812071", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Days", "line": "Now I’m starin’ at the mirror lookin’ at my better half", "vault_lines": ["Now I'm starin' at the mirror lookin' at my better half"], "meaning": "Wayne reflects on his progress in life while referencing the state he was in when he recorded “Mirror”.\nWayne’s positive perspective on life comes in contrast to his old perspective, as he mentioned in “Mirror”:\n\n\n[Verse 1]\n…\nI see the pain hidden in your pride\nI see you’re not satisfied\nAnd I don’t see nobody else\nI see myself, I’m looking at the\n\n[Chorus]\nMirror on the wall,\n…", "annotation_id": "35812063", "url": "https://genius.com/35812063", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Days", "line": "Live like a soldier, die like a veteran", "vault_lines": ["Live like a soldier, die like a vetеran"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is saying he lives a tough, disciplined life, just like a soldier who’s always in the middle of a fight.\n\nBut when it’s his time to go, he wants to be remembered with respect, like a veteran who’s been through it all and earned honor.\n\nHe is saying that it’s about living strong and leaving a legacy.", "annotation_id": "35811989", "url": "https://genius.com/35811989", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Days", "line": "’Cause these are the days, anything can happen On 9/11, I was in Manhattan", "vault_lines": ["These are the days (Oh, RedOne"], "meaning": "The 9/11 attacks were a devastating act of terrorism targeting the Twin Towers in Manhattan on September 11, 2001, resulting in the deaths of 2,977 innocent people, in addition to the perpetrators.\n\n\n\nSimply being in Manhattan on that day would’ve had people in a state of extreme fear and panic, due to the unprecedented nature of attack. Many who witnessed the events firsthand developed PTSD from the traumatic experience. Wayne references being in Manhattan during the attacks to highlight the unpredictability of life.", "annotation_id": "35810904", "url": "https://genius.com/35810904", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Days", "line": "Take the highs with the lows, smell the concrete rose", "vault_lines": ["Take the highs with the lows, smell the concrete rose"], "meaning": "Here, Lil Wayne is saying to see the good even in the bad, the good being the rose and the bad being the concrete. Additionally, the mention of the “concrete rose” likely alludes to 2Pac’s poem, “The Rose That Grew From Concrete.”", "annotation_id": "35810875", "url": "https://genius.com/35810875", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
