{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "Joey, don’t do it, Joey done did it Joey keep doing it until you’re done with it", "vault_lines": ["Joey, don't do it, Joey done did it"], "meaning": "This self-referential line acknowledges Fat Joe’s continual involvement in risky actions. Despite warnings or doubts, he’s already deep in the game and committed to seeing it through until the end. Also it could be a commentary on Fat Joe pursuit of success, regardless of the dangers.", "annotation_id": "32903950", "url": "https://genius.com/32903950", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "I mean, I’m talking more pies than a frat house", "vault_lines": ["I mean, I'm talking more pies than a frat house"], "meaning": "“Pies” in this context is slang for drugs, specifically cocaine, referencing the selling and trafficking of large quantities.", "annotation_id": "32903934", "url": "https://genius.com/32903934", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
