{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "So much coke, a nigga change his government", "vault_lines": ["So much coke, a nigga change his government"], "meaning": "A reference to Gary Webb’s discovery of the CIA’s importation and distribution of vast quantities of cocaine in the United States to fund the Contras' failed coup (a nigga change his government) in Nicaragua. They’re keeping industrial amounts of cocaine like that.", "annotation_id": "16364979", "url": "https://genius.com/16364979", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "Even Reverend Al be like, “Joe’s that nigga!”", "vault_lines": ["Even Reverend Al be like, \"Joe's that nigga!\""], "meaning": "Alfred Charles Sharpton Jr. is an American civil rights activist, Baptist minister, television/radio talk show host and a trusted White House adviser who, according to 60 Minutes, has become President Barack Obama’s “go-to black leader.”", "annotation_id": "9283319", "url": "https://genius.com/9283319", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "Banana clips", "vault_lines": ["I'm sleeping on a billion dollars"], "meaning": "Banana’s have a strong resemblance to the ammo magazines used in automatic weapons and rifles, such as the AK-47.", "annotation_id": "9283027", "url": "https://genius.com/9283027", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "Hey, this is the crackhouse, welcome to the crackhouse", "vault_lines": ["Hey, this is the crackhouse, welcome to the crackhouse"], "meaning": "A crack house is a building where drug dealers and drug users buy, sell, produce, and use illegal drugs. This includes, but is not limited to, crack cocaine.", "annotation_id": "3170199", "url": "https://genius.com/3170199", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "Man I’m talkin’ more pies than a frat house", "vault_lines": ["Man I'm talkin' more pies than a frat house"], "meaning": "A pie is slang for a kilo of cocaine. This is a reference to the comedy film American Pie the Beta House.", "annotation_id": "2902678", "url": "https://genius.com/2902678", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "Yellow mustard Phantom car, it Grey Poupon", "vault_lines": ["Yellow mustard Phantom car, it Grey Poupon"], "meaning": "Try putting this on your sandwich!\n\n\n\nAlso, speaking of Kanye…", "annotation_id": "2666607", "url": "https://genius.com/2666607", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "These are the niggas you compare to Joe, hello", "vault_lines": ["These are the niggas you compare to Joe, hello"], "meaning": "You gotta compare Fat Joe with real people like Gotti and the Supreme Team members. Also, Joey is talking about selling drugs in the song, and Gotti and the Supreme Team were kind that.", "annotation_id": "2356338", "url": "https://genius.com/2356338", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "Supreme Team", "vault_lines": ["I'm sleeping on a billion dollars"], "meaning": "The Supreme Team was an African-American crack cocaine gang that operated throughout the 1980s in New York City. Their headquarters was in a South Jamaica, Queens housing project known as the Baisley Park Houses. However they controlled a huge chunk of the entire city itself, including Harlem. The leader was Kenneth “Supreme” McGriff and his nephew, Gerald “Prince” Miller.\n\nIn 1989, the Team was disbanded, and McGriff spent 10 years in a federal prison for a narcotics conviction. McGriff was depicted in 50 Cent’s film Get Rich or Die Tryin', as the character Majestic.", "annotation_id": "2356336", "url": "https://genius.com/2356336", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "John Gotti", "vault_lines": ["I'm sleeping on a billion dollars"], "meaning": "John Joseph Gotti, Jr. (October 27, 1940 – June 10, 2002) was an American mobster who became the Boss of the Gambino crime family in New York City.", "annotation_id": "2356324", "url": "https://genius.com/2356324", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "Pacman Jones", "vault_lines": ["I can make it Pacman Jones"], "meaning": "Adam Bernard Jones also know as Pacman Jones, is an American football cornerback for the Cincinnati Bengals of the National Football League. He was drafted in the first round with the sixth-overall pick in the 2005 NFL Draft by the Tennessee Titans. He played college football at West Virginia.\n\nJones has also played for the Dallas Cowboys. He was suspended from the NFL for the entire 2007 season and for part of the 2008 season for off-the-field conduct.\n\nBack in 2007, Pacman Jones started his career as a wrestler. He retired of wrestling in October of the same year.", "annotation_id": "2356296", "url": "https://genius.com/2356296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "The Crackhouse", "line": "And thier time’s tickin’ like an Audemars", "vault_lines": ["And thier time's tickin' like an Audemars"], "meaning": "Audemars is a manufacturer of Swiss watches.\nThey’re going to die (the clock is ticking).", "annotation_id": "2040951", "url": "https://genius.com/2040951", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
