{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s What They Call Me", "line": "Bitch, I’m a king no matter how the cards are dealt", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I’m a king no matter how the cards are dealt"], "meaning": "Wayne is basically referring to life as a game here, a card game, to be specific. Maybe a bit of a play on his “Life’s A Gamble” tattoo.\n\n\n\n(Tattoo located near Wayne’s left shoulder, or the viewers right)\n\nSo, even if Wayne isn’t dealt a card that has a king on it\n\n\n\nHe himself will still feel like a king.\n\n\n\nNot being dealt a king card probably refers to not always having things go as planned, but since Wayne still feels like a king, it obviously doesn’t bother him too much.", "annotation_id": "1700797", "url": "https://genius.com/1700797", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s What They Call Me", "line": "I ain’t never been a pussy, have you ever been in pussy?", "vault_lines": ["I ain't never been a pussy, have you ever been in pussy?"], "meaning": "It’s not good to be a pussy, but it’s good to be in pussy (shows how much semantic difference a tiny little preposition can make..)", "annotation_id": "161827", "url": "https://genius.com/161827", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
