{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s Not Love", "line": "[Verse 4: Fabolous]", "vault_lines": ["Snakes in the grass, so I stay in the pavement"], "meaning": "Fab first spitted this verse as a freestyle on a interview at Hot 97 with Funkmaster Flex and then decided to include it on the mixtape.\n\nCheck the video for the freestyle here :\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5rpDBFD2lrM", "annotation_id": "3955326", "url": "https://genius.com/3955326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s Not Love", "line": "Niggas pretend like they actually in But when it go down they fuck around and be them", "vault_lines": ["Niggas pretend like they actually in"], "meaning": "Wayne is referring to the “game” here.  Saying that people pretend to be with it, but when shit goes down they’re just “snitches” (back to the previous line) and look out only for themselves.", "annotation_id": "179850", "url": "https://genius.com/179850", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s Not Love", "line": "These niggas is snitching and still living", "vault_lines": ["These niggas is snitching and still living"], "meaning": "Somebody tells the authorities about somebody else’s bad deed to get themselves off the hook, “snitching” on someone.  Usually, this will lead to adverse consequences for the person being snitched on.  This is fixed, usually, by killing the snitch.\n\n\n\nRiley Freeman says “STOP SNITCHIN”", "annotation_id": "179747", "url": "https://genius.com/179747", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s Not Love", "line": "So you empty clip niggas ain’t got a shot", "vault_lines": ["So you empty clip niggas ain't got a shot"], "meaning": "Literally, if you don’t have a clip(container where bullets are stored) that means you don’t have a shot or a bullet to shoot\n\nThis is a diss to other rappers; they are lyrically vapid", "annotation_id": "178904", "url": "https://genius.com/178904", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s Not Love", "line": "Now I can sit and talk shit like Skip Bayless", "vault_lines": ["Now I can sit and talk shit like Skip Bayless"], "meaning": "Fab is at the top so he can say what he wants. Skip Bayless is on ESPN’s First Take, where he gives bullshit opinions (like this)\n\n\n\nAnother more rap-related opinion from Skip on the show.\n\nNote that Fab himself put in an appearance on First Take on May 18, 2011", "annotation_id": "178555", "url": "https://genius.com/178555", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s Not Love", "line": "Snakes in the grass, so I stay in the pavement", "vault_lines": ["Snakes in the grass, so I stay in the pavement"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has been a snakeophobe since the days of “Go DJ”:\n\nYou snakes: stop hiding in the grass\nSooner or later I’ll cut it, knock the blades in your ass\n\nThat’s why he keeps it street – “pavement” (skyscrapers are filled with snakes wearing suits..)", "annotation_id": "178498", "url": "https://genius.com/178498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s Not Love", "line": "Love spelt backwards is evol (evolve)", "vault_lines": ["Love spelt backwards is evol (evolve)"], "meaning": "A line with a multi-faceted hip-hop history; originated by Nas in “Everything is Everything”:\n\nNever play with love, love is evil spelled backwards\n\nMore recently quoted by Eminem on “Space Bound”:\n\nAnd love is evil, spell it backwards I’ll show ya\n\nWhy do all the rappers say it? Because it’s true! FUCK love", "annotation_id": "178392", "url": "https://genius.com/178392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s Not Love", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Fabolous-thats-not-love-lyrics", "genius_title": "That’s Not Love", "genius_id": 49344, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s My Nigga (Do It for the Boy)", "line": "We can do it real big, bigger than you’ve ever done it Everything you ever wanted, I can spend whatever on it", "vault_lines": ["We can do it real big, bigger than you've ever done it"], "meaning": "Speaking to the female, telling her they’ll be the biggest, most popular couple on earth.\n\n[Later to be sampled as Drake’s hook for “Best I Ever Had”]", "annotation_id": "2036747", "url": "https://genius.com/2036747", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s My Nigga (Do It for the Boy)", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Kidd-kidd-thats-my-nigga-do-it-for-the-boy-lyrics", "genius_title": "That’s My Nigga (Do It for the Boy)", "genius_id": 131009, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Pro-Black: pump they fist", "vault_lines": ["pro-Black: pump they fist"], "meaning": "Holding one fist in the air is a classic Black Power symbol, used by the Black Panthers in the 1980’s as a sign of solidarity and call for equality.", "annotation_id": "20729496", "url": "https://genius.com/20729496", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Money to the ceilings? Nigga, No Ceilings! I’m out!", "vault_lines": ["Money to the ceilings? Nigga, No Ceilings! I'm out!"], "meaning": "In here he refers to the fact that he owns a lot of money all the way to the ceiling.\n\nHe also uses the name of his album “No Ceilings” as a wordplay to mention his album and also to represent that there is no ceiling, therefore, his money just keeps growing.", "annotation_id": "20726164", "url": "https://genius.com/20726164", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Ugh! now let me start by sayin’ I don’t like this beat", "vault_lines": ["Ugh! now let me start by sayin' I don't like this beat"], "meaning": "Sometimes Wayne will still rap over a beat even if he dislikes it in which he states", "annotation_id": "14107518", "url": "https://genius.com/14107518", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Weezy F. Baby, I do it big—weigh me", "vault_lines": ["Weezy F. Baby, I do it big—weigh me"], "meaning": "To “do it big” means to do something in a major way and taking things to the next level. Wayne believes that when it comes to rap, he does it bigger than anyone else does.\n\nComing from the man that made a song titled “The Best Rapper Alive”, it’s not really shocking that Wayne said this.\n\nAlso, Wayne throws in some wordplay. If something is literally big, it probably weighs a lot. So Wayne using the literal definition claims you can come weigh him as in to test his skills as a rapper to prove that he has no fear.", "annotation_id": "4142696", "url": "https://genius.com/4142696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Open up your mouth, and catch a bomb, baby, haha!", "vault_lines": ["Open up your mouth, and catch a bomb, baby, haha!"], "meaning": "This line is continuing the football metaphor. A chick is performing oral sex on Weezy and he ejaculates in her mouth, thus catching the “bomb.” The bomb can be interpreted as either the football or the sperm.\n\n\n\nAs Wayne stated above, he is the quarterback (he’ll be providing the sperm), while the girl on the receiving end of the “pass” will be the receiver (she’ll be catching the sperm).", "annotation_id": "2875231", "url": "https://genius.com/2875231", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Spending time backwards,", "vault_lines": ["Nigga ain't let me catch my breath"], "meaning": "Tricky line right here…\n\nAs they say, time is money, and the opposite of “spending” is “buying”. So it could be an elaborate way to say that Wayne’s blowing money.", "annotation_id": "2744085", "url": "https://genius.com/2744085", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Quarterback Weezy, young Tom Brady", "vault_lines": ["Quarterback Weezy, young Tom Brady"], "meaning": "Instead of the usual comparisons to fellow rappers, this time Wayne compares himself to legendary Patriots Quarterback, Tom Brady.\n\n\n\n\n\nNotice the resemblance?", "annotation_id": "2739530", "url": "https://genius.com/2739530", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "That’s all I have!", "vault_lines": ["That's all I have!"], "meaning": "A rather ingenious way to finish off the song.\n\nUp until this point, the title, That’s All I Have doesn’t make too much sense. Not only is Shanell’s verse significantly shorter than Tyga and Wayne’s but she literally stops her verse in the middle of a line and states “That’s all I have” and cuts to the next song.\n\nI don’t know about you, but that made me laugh out loud…", "annotation_id": "2735916", "url": "https://genius.com/2735916", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "[Verse 3: Shanell]", "vault_lines": ["Nigga ain't let me catch my breath"], "meaning": "Shanell is an artist signed to YMCMB. She’s primarily a singer, and this is one of the only times she’s ever rapped on a song.", "annotation_id": "2735155", "url": "https://genius.com/2735155", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "But he’s more like platinum;", "vault_lines": ["But he's more like platinum;"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne’s less silver and way up on platinum status.\n- Platinum: Tha Block is Hot\n- Platinum: Tha Carter II\n- 3X Platinum: Tha Carter III\n- 2X Platinum: Tha Carter IV", "annotation_id": "1380768", "url": "https://genius.com/1380768", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "And he put them dreads in: Silver, John Long", "vault_lines": ["And he put them dreads in: Silver, John Long"], "meaning": "Wayne’s got dreads like a pirate (Long John Silver reference).", "annotation_id": "1380766", "url": "https://genius.com/1380766", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "And I juke it; for my future records y’all gon’ love to spin", "vault_lines": ["And I juke it; for my future records y'all gon' love to spin"], "meaning": "Shanell is a songwriter but also an exceptional dancer and started her career as a backup dancer for artists like Ciara & Ne-Yo who later signed her to his publishing company after noticing her songwriting skills. Juke means dance so through dancing she brings you her songs which apparently we’ll all love.", "annotation_id": "527736", "url": "https://genius.com/527736", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Ha! Boys-to-man business (Yes),", "vault_lines": ["Ha! Boys-to-man business (Yes),"], "meaning": "A reference to Boyz II Men, the R&B group from way back when.\n\n\n\nMan whatever happened to those dudes?\n\nIt also sounds like he says “voice command business” which could reference the voice command GPS in his car since he is such a baller and has a poor sense of direction.", "annotation_id": "513624", "url": "https://genius.com/513624", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Silence lambs, bitch (Yes), run through your land tripping (Hahaha)", "vault_lines": ["Silence lambs, bitch (Yes), run through your land tripping (Hahaha)"], "meaning": "In the movie Silence of the Lambs, the protagonist is caught by Hannibal Lecter when she trips while running from him.\n\n\n\nAlternatively: Tyga will take hallucinogens and sprint across your yard in some euphoric celebration of the fusion between reality and imagination (see next line).", "annotation_id": "513609", "url": "https://genius.com/513609", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Gorillas in the mist,", "vault_lines": ["Gorillas in the mist,"], "meaning": "Tyga is paying homage to the West Coast group Da Lench Mob, as he name drops their 1992 album, while also saying he has his unseen guerrillas (goons) to handle problems.", "annotation_id": "473616", "url": "https://genius.com/473616", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "I’m from the Planet of the Apes, King Kong clips (Blah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm from the Planet of the Apes, King Kong clips (Blah)"], "meaning": "Further homage to Da Lench Mob as Tyga drops a mention to their second album: Planet of da Apes, released two years post Guerrillas in da Mist.\n\n\n\nHis play on the album title proceeds to a description of his over sized handguns in which he uses King Kong to help depict their size.\nInferiority complex anyone??", "annotation_id": "282657", "url": "https://genius.com/282657", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "If shit hits the fan, I Ron Artest niggas (Ha)", "vault_lines": ["If shit hits the fan, I Ron Artest niggas (Ha)"], "meaning": "“Shit hit[ting] the fan” is a phrase meaning that things are out of control. When this happens, Tyga will repeatedly punch his opponents, much like basketball player Ron Artest infamously did during a 2004 game", "annotation_id": "107980", "url": "https://genius.com/107980", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "Long dough, no shortbread, no Lorna Doone", "vault_lines": ["Long dough, no shortbread, no Lorna Doone"], "meaning": "Weezy got endless money – he’s long on “bread” (money), not “short” (pun on shortbread, which is unhealthy both in the literal and metaphorical sense).", "annotation_id": "107487", "url": "https://genius.com/107487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That’s All I Have", "line": "I keep a house full, nigga—call me Bob Saget", "vault_lines": ["I keep a house full, nigga—call me Bob Saget"], "meaning": "Full House was a successful US sitcom that ran from the late 80’s to the mid 90’s. In the show Bob Saget ,who played the role of the widowed Father, was constantly surrounded by women as he had 3 daughters to raise AND was fresh on the dating scene. Hence why Wayne’s comparable to Bob\n\n\n\nACCEPTED COMMENT: Bob Saget even went on to aknowledge this reference and thank Weezy!", "annotation_id": "107485", "url": "https://genius.com/107485", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
