{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "Doctor’s patient", "vault_lines": ["Punch, shot, and stab; now you're the doctor's patient"], "meaning": "Dr. Carter was a song off of Tha Carter III which this lyric could be alluding to.", "annotation_id": "21191968", "url": "https://genius.com/21191968", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "And now I’m coming out the faders, no homo", "vault_lines": ["And now I'm coming out the faders, no homo"], "meaning": "Wayne is coming out of the faders, which is an audio system used for sound mixing as well as other things.\n\n\n\nHowever, Wayne says “no homo” to clarify that he isn’t talking about that kind of coming out.", "annotation_id": "2603680", "url": "https://genius.com/2603680", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "I’m in their conversations", "vault_lines": ["I'm in their conversations"], "meaning": "This means two things:\n\n– Wayne is what people are buzzing about.\n\n– Wayne is in people’s conversation for the greatest rappers of all time.", "annotation_id": "2603663", "url": "https://genius.com/2603663", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "Pullin’ the ladder from heaven, about to climb home", "vault_lines": ["Pullin' the ladder from heaven, about to climb home"], "meaning": "This could be a reference to the ladder that Jacob dreamed about in the Bible where he saw angels lined up like a ladder to heaven. Wayne is about to go home to heaven", "annotation_id": "201136", "url": "https://genius.com/201136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "Controlled by my two hands, they go tick tock Around the clock, yes, it’s my time, my throne", "vault_lines": ["It's my own throne"], "meaning": "The “two hands” are the two hands on a clock that show the hour and the time and basically control what most people do during the day. Wayne twists that to say that he is the one controlling time because it’s his time", "annotation_id": "201135", "url": "https://genius.com/201135", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "Yeah, I shall never leave Hip-Hop", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I shall never leave Hip-Hop"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne doesn’t want to retire from the rap game; in a interview with Angie Martinez on Hot 97 he said he’s planning on retiring at the age of 35! 7 more years of Weezy!", "annotation_id": "168572", "url": "https://genius.com/168572", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "Before that, it was a livin’ cesspool", "vault_lines": ["Before that, it was a livin' cesspool"], "meaning": "Lil' Wayne is referring to crime and poverty that ran rampant in New Orleans before the Hurricane.  Clearly, it’s still there seeing as most of the poor folk couldn’t afford to leave town.  But perhaps this is also a reference to the previous verse where he blamed others for not saving the city by fixing and improving the levees that resulted in the flooding of New Orleans.  Perhaps this is also referring to others not helping to fight crime and poverty in the impoverished communities for New Orleans.  But following this verse, he seems to also tell the people of those same communities that they need to get their shit together.  Perhaps because the faulty levees and the poor state of the city beforehand proved that no one else was gonna help them", "annotation_id": "78395", "url": "https://genius.com/78395", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "And I don’t go to church because the line long And the preacher, he be gettin’ his shine on", "vault_lines": ["And I don't go to church because the line long"], "meaning": "He doesn’t go to church because there are too many people trying to use the lord to save themselves\n\nAnd the preacher is apart of the scam by taking their money and being the one who is always the savior\n\nI feel you Weezy!!!", "annotation_id": "78391", "url": "https://genius.com/78391", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "Drop the top at the light, that’s when I be headed", "vault_lines": ["Drop the top at the light, that's when I be headed"], "meaning": "A double entendre:\n\nHe drops the top on the ride so it’s “beheaded.”\n\nWhere ever the road goes, that’s where he “be headed” or that’s where he’s going.", "annotation_id": "78188", "url": "https://genius.com/78188", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "When they turned my city into a swimmin’ pool", "vault_lines": ["When they turned my city into a swimmin' pool"], "meaning": "Hurricane Katrina the city of New Orleans\n\n\n\nInterestingly enough, Lil Wayne says that “they” turned his city into a swimming pool.  This refers to the fact that people knew that if the levees weren’t improved in New Orleans, then the city would literally drown whenever a major hurricane hit.  People warned the city of New Orleans for years but nobody listened.  Thus the city flooded massively and became like a giant swimming pool.  Weezy is blaming other people who could’ve fixed the problem and saved his beloved city.", "annotation_id": "75897", "url": "https://genius.com/75897", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "Never saved by the bell in a black school And I stay in trouble like Zack do", "vault_lines": ["Never saved by the bell in a black school"], "meaning": "He is Referring to the early 90’s TV show Saved by the Bell\nZack Morris was the name of the main character who always seemed to be in some sort of trouble each episode\n\n\n\nHis schooling experience wasn’t idyllic like that of the Saved By The Bell characters; their problems weren’t resolved neatly at the end of a 30 minute episode", "annotation_id": "68700", "url": "https://genius.com/68700", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "That Ain’t Me", "line": "But I feel electric like I’m Raiden Used to play Mortal Kombat when I was a couch potato", "vault_lines": ["But I feel electric like I'm Raiden"], "meaning": "The thunder god of the Mortal Kombat universe, also known as Lord Rayden, is a protector of Earthrealm. Raiden commands many supernatural abilities such as the ability to teleport, control over lightning, and flight.\n\nLil Wayne is describing Raiden and highlighting his power .", "annotation_id": "68461", "url": "https://genius.com/68461", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
