{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "[Verse 2: Q-Tip]", "vault_lines": ["Woo! Welcome to the bank"], "meaning": "Busta was (in the good old days) protege of Q-Tip and he also made some seriously good joints with ATCQ before he blew up. See Scenario. They are also good friends and they will be releasing a mixtape soon, named “The Abstract & The Dragon”\n\nhttps://twitter.com/BustaRhymes/statuses/403617142320689152\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n.", "annotation_id": "2479387", "url": "https://genius.com/2479387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "Not to mention, we veterans", "vault_lines": ["Not to mention, we veterans"], "meaning": "Bus' is a veteran of the rap game, killin' it since the 90’s when he was in Leaders of the New School;\n\n\n\nUp to the present with a newer styled rap songs like Coke Dope Crack Smack and Look at Me Now", "annotation_id": "2479099", "url": "https://genius.com/2479099", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "Flying United Emirates sized private plane, that kind of etiquette", "vault_lines": ["Flying United Emirates sized private plane, that kind of etiquette"], "meaning": "The airline is a subsidiary of The Emirates Group, which is wholly owned by the government of Dubai’s Investment Corporation of Dubai. It is the largest airline in the Middle East.\n\n\n\nThe punchline here takes five beats to get out, which is just great – the point is that his private jets are the size of commercial airliners.", "annotation_id": "2465185", "url": "https://genius.com/2465185", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "Kicking it in Pele Adidas", "vault_lines": ["Kicking it in Pele Adidas"], "meaning": "“Kickin' it in Pele' Adidas”. A play on “kickin' it” (chillin') vs. “kickin' it”, as in kicking a soccer ball like famous Brazilian soccer star Pele' did.  Ironically enough, Pele wore Pumas, Adidas' biggest rival at the time he played.", "annotation_id": "2448955", "url": "https://genius.com/2448955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "And live from the vault, is Bus-a-Bus (Yeah, yeah, yeah, yo)", "vault_lines": ["And live from the vault, is Bus-a-Bus"], "meaning": "AND, IN THE RED CORNER\n\n\nWeezy only introduces his artist on the track, as it is of course a Busta record, and this is the last we hear from him.\n\n\n\n“The Vault” is probably an allusion to how much money YMCMB make – they got stacks! Nicki, Drake and Wayne are all still moving records, hopefully Busta will go on to do the same.", "annotation_id": "2440974", "url": "https://genius.com/2440974", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "[Chorus: Alicia Myers & Kanye West]", "vault_lines": ["Woo! Welcome to the bank"], "meaning": "The closest thing we’ve seen to a feature since Yeezus, and it seems the only reasons he is on the track is to boost the hype, and to help squash beef between G.O.O.D Music and YMCMB.\n\nKanye also appears in the music video for this song.", "annotation_id": "2440906", "url": "https://genius.com/2440906", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "[Intro: Lil Wayne & Busta Rhymes]", "vault_lines": ["Woo! Welcome to the bank"], "meaning": "Although he doesn’t have a verse, Busta wanted Weezy on this track to try and kill the YMCMB/G.O.O.D Music beef. Q-Tip, the other rapper on the track, is a member of G.O.O.D, and Kanye, who has a similar job to Wayne on the track later in the song, is G.O.O.D Music’s leader.\n\n\n\nAlthough there is no personal beef between Weezy and Yeezy, and they have collaborated multiple times in the past, G.O.O.D Music member Pusha T has had something to say about the Young Money camp, and Wayne in particular, with this diss track:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-Evs0wwnuak", "annotation_id": "2440868", "url": "https://genius.com/2440868", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "See how we push sometimes a man fi get kuff? Beat him in the head", "vault_lines": ["See how we push sometimes a man fi get kuff?"], "meaning": "Busta is paying homage to his Jamaican ancestry, which he has previously done for the Neptunes produced “Kill Dem” and fellow-E.L.E. 2 single, “Twerk It”.\n\n\n\n“Man fi get kuff” is Jamaican patois basically for man getting hit (cuff/fisticuffs). It’s also a reference to an old Shelly Thunder Dancehall song called “Kuff”", "annotation_id": "2438401", "url": "https://genius.com/2438401", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "Gross when we give them a dose Got them O.D.’ing, leaning in each coast", "vault_lines": ["Keep the faculty close, gross when we give them a dose"], "meaning": "Busta is comparing in how his verse affects people like the drug syrup effects the consumers. He is saying he will give them a verse aka a dose and have then leaning aka slowed down from drinking too much syzzurp at once. So Bustas verses are the equivalent of drugs on both costs.\n\nLeaning could also refer to vertigo  (misbalance), causing them to lean. This is a side effect to overdosing on Busta’s verses, which are equivalent to a dose strength much higher than the therapeutic one.", "annotation_id": "2418123", "url": "https://genius.com/2418123", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "My niggas bite like Rin Tin Tin", "vault_lines": ["My niggas bite like Rin Tin Tin"], "meaning": "Rin Tin Tin was a German Shepherd who became a famous film star. Since he is a dog, he must have bit a lot of things.\n\nAlso a 20-year call back to the line from ATCQ’s “The Chase Pt. II,” which features Busta Rhymes:\n\nLyrically, we bite like we Rin Tin Tin\n\nThis song is on their album Midnight Marauders which features Busta on “Oh My God”.", "annotation_id": "2417432", "url": "https://genius.com/2417432", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "I’m Tunechi the boss", "vault_lines": ["I'm Tunechi the boss"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne the YM president\n\n\n\n“Tunechi”, as well being his Twitter name, is one of his many nicknames.\n\n“My nickname is Lil Tune — my grandmother named me that,” he explained. “She’s passed. My grandmother, her name was Mercedes Carter. She named me Lil Tune. We just threw the ‘Chi’ on there. Like Gucci, I say ‘Tunechi!’\"\n\nApparently, Lil Tune originally came from the nickname lil tuna fish, and the name grew from there.", "annotation_id": "2402765", "url": "https://genius.com/2402765", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "(And you listening to Q-Tip)", "vault_lines": ["Woo! Welcome to the bank"], "meaning": "Q-Tip and Kanye are frequent collaborators and peers. Standout material that the two have worked on together include “Lift Off” and “That’s My Bitch” (off Watch The Throne, Tip co-produced the tracks)\n\n\n\nTip is also signed to Kanye’s G.O.O.D Music imprint.", "annotation_id": "2402337", "url": "https://genius.com/2402337", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "Woo! Welcome to the bank Where you deposit Young Money And, and you get Cash Money", "vault_lines": ["Woo! Welcome to the bank"], "meaning": "Playing off of his label Young Money Entertainement under Birdman’s Cash Money Records AKA Young Money Cash Money (YMCMB):\n\n\nHe’s got freshly made ‘money in the bank’\n\nHis signees are pretty young rappers, though Nicki Minaj and Drake are the ones who bring the lion’s share.", "annotation_id": "2402301", "url": "https://genius.com/2402301", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "line": "Ahk see him, he puss", "vault_lines": ["Ahk see him, he puss"], "meaning": "Wordplay on word Oxypulse which is a measured value indicating the oxygen saturation level in a person. If he is beating the person to death in the previous line,  s/he is breathing their last breath. Busta is the taker of her/his life = taker of his breath = taker of his oxygen.\nBusta is high on oxycodone, therefore it’s in his bloodstream and he’s charging ie. in his pulse.", "annotation_id": "2402283", "url": "https://genius.com/2402283", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Thank You", "status": "done", "targets": 18, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Busta-rhymes-thank-you-lyrics", "genius_title": "Thank You", "genius_id": 256016, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "Told her gettin’ out the game is like coming out of a coma I’m trying,", "vault_lines": ["Told her gettin' out the game is like coming out of a coma"], "meaning": "In three ways, Wayne use a coma to describe his experience of living the street life (i.e., “the game”) and attempting to get out of it.\n\n(1) Wayne tells his mother that “coming out of the game is like coming out of a coma,” forming an analogy to underscore the low chances he has of escaping the street life. For reference, approximately 30-50% of medically diagnosed comatose persons “wake up.\"\n\n(2) Wayne explains he is “trying”; however, the simile of escaping the game and rising from a coma illustrates that his attempts are futile—Wayne “trying” to escape the game is like a person “trying” to wake up from a coma. A person unfortunately cannot “try,” in a traditional sense, to wake up from a coma.\n\n(3) This also demonstrates the principle of “mind over matter.” Despite lacking most of their faculties, people in comas oftentimes have limited forms of consciousness. By “trying” to wake up from a coma, the comatose person inherently has a positive/hopeful mindset, and that mindset might give them a greater chance of recovering. Similarly, even though Wayne’s literal “trying” won’t get him out of the game, his positive/hopeful mindset might.", "annotation_id": "37050530", "url": "https://genius.com/37050530", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "Nowadays, knowing life, ain’t no more road lights (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Nowadays, knowing life, ain't no more road lights (Woah)"], "meaning": "Getting this far in life, then 23 year old Lil Wayne he knows he is too old for ‘road lights’ or guidance in his life because he’s not a baby anymore.", "annotation_id": "35376182", "url": "https://genius.com/35376182", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "Start ’em, ignite ’em (Yeah), I walk through fire Watch the flames start multiplyin’, woo, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Start 'em, ignite 'em (Yeah), I walk through fire"], "meaning": "Wayne is gassed up, causing fire to spread when he’s walking through", "annotation_id": "31259134", "url": "https://genius.com/31259134", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "Take a chunk out your body like a shark bit a nigga (Damn)", "vault_lines": ["Take a chunk out your body like a shark bit a nigga (Damn)"], "meaning": "earlier in the song\n“It’s my ocean, baby, y'all niggas is tuna (Yeah)”\n\nTune is the shark of his ocean", "annotation_id": "31259119", "url": "https://genius.com/31259119", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "And what happens when the reaper come? (Huh?) I’m just hoping that he sends that elevator up (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["And what happens when the reaper come? (Huh?)"], "meaning": "The Grim Reaper represents death.  The elevator symbolizes the journey to either Heaven or Hell.  Weezy is saying that when he dies, he hopes the Grim Reaper will send his elevator up, therefore getting him into Heaven and avoiding the torture of Hell.", "annotation_id": "22448807", "url": "https://genius.com/22448807", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "When the jungle was open, I rolled in with the riders Stole food from the bears, and brought it back to the lions (Yeah) Hold court with the apes, I’m a gorilla, but lighter (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I put it down when the others was playin' (Yeah)"], "meaning": "The jungle is slang for the hood, or the streets. Wayne cleverly uses a metaphor comparing several different animals that you would typically see in the jungle to different types of people you see or face in the hood, reflecting situations he may have experienced or things he may have seen in his hood growing up. Stealing food from the bears may reference stealing from the rich and giving to the poor. Potentially saying he could have robbed houses for monetary gain. Gorilla or ape is slang for a killer or real gangster/hardened individual. Holding court may reference the code that people follow in the streets.", "annotation_id": "20439346", "url": "https://genius.com/20439346", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "It’s my ocean, baby, y’all niggas is tuna (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["It's my ocean, baby, y'all niggas is tuna (Yeah)"], "meaning": "This rap game is his and he is above almost everyone else is what this line is saying. “Yall niggas is tuna” is means he eats all these other rappers and gangsta’s for breakfast. Its also a play on words to his nickname tunechi (tuna fish)", "annotation_id": "16745967", "url": "https://genius.com/16745967", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "Semi nine fit me fine, hit a nigga twenty times (Bah-bah-bah-bah, bah) Damn, then one more to the face (Bah) Just so they close the casket like I pay to close the case (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Semi nine fit me fine, hit a nigga twenty times (Bah-bah-bah-bah, bah)"], "meaning": "Wayne is speaking hypothetically of course by storytelling which he does in many of his lyrics. Imagine him standing over his victim after already shooting him twenty times, and then shooting him once again in the face to finish him off.\n\n\n\nPeople who die so brutally usually have a close casket funeral, which Wayne wanted. And ironically, Wayne also paid a large amount of money so the crime he committed is no longer being investigated. Because that’s what gangsters do… close the casket and close the case.", "annotation_id": "6759654", "url": "https://genius.com/6759654", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "Flying ’round your city, tryna take a number two on ya (Hah)", "vault_lines": ["Flying 'round your city, tryna take a number two on ya (Hah)"], "meaning": "Junior is short for “Birdman Junior”, one of Wayne’s many nicknames. “Taking a number 2” is another way of saying he’s shitting on his competition.\n\nAlso a reference to birds shitting on people, which (unfortunately) happens often.", "annotation_id": "4722392", "url": "https://genius.com/4722392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "Palm trees, promethazine, but what’s new? (Tell ’em)", "vault_lines": ["Palm trees, promethazine, but what's new? (Tell 'em)"], "meaning": "At a certain point of his career Wayne was heavily addicted to promethazine also known as “Syrup” a highly addictive that led to the death of Houston music scene legend, DJ Screw (R.I.P!). He could always be seen with a white cup on his sand sipping the drink and even recorded a song for it Me and My Drank. It started to affect his health and his work ethic as he got into a argument on-stage with his DJ/long time friend and manager Cortez “Tez” Bryant. He was able to drop the habit and is now promethazine free.", "annotation_id": "3923992", "url": "https://genius.com/3923992", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "I’m awkward like Cartwright, fuck with a nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm awkward like Cartwright, fuck with a nigga"], "meaning": "This line (and the first part of the following line) refer to former New York Knick’s and Chicago Bull’s center Bill Cartwright, who had one of the ugliest free throw shooting forms ever seen.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xcqag8zPJmQ\n\nIn spite of his strange form, Cartwright still shot 77.1% from the free throw line, better than many of today’s All-Stars like Lebron James and Dwyane Wade.  So it sounds like Wayne’s saying that even if you hate on his style, you can’t hate on the results.", "annotation_id": "1644806", "url": "https://genius.com/1644806", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "Got the eye of a tiger, the heart of a fighter, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Got the eye of a tiger, the heart of a fighter, yeah"], "meaning": "The Survivor Eye. Survivor is a rock band. Their biggest hit is probably “Eye of the Tiger”. A song almost synonymous with the movie:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VgSMxY6asoE\n\n\n\nRocky may not have been as big physically as his opponents but he had a lot of heart. Weezy is also of small stature and has that Rocky heart.", "annotation_id": "1051138", "url": "https://genius.com/1051138", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "You pups can’t keep up with the pedigree (Get back)", "vault_lines": ["You pups can't keep up with the pedigree (Get back)"], "meaning": "Pedigree means line of decent. Those who are not in the same league as the “big dawgs” or are in over there head when entering the game an not keep up with Wayne, who could seen as way above them.\n\n\n\nPedigree is also a brand of dog food for puppies.", "annotation_id": "672803", "url": "https://genius.com/672803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "Cash Money, Young Money, motherfuck the other side", "vault_lines": ["Cash Money, Young Money, motherfuck the other side"], "meaning": "This line makes a similar point as Hov does in Izzo (H.O.V.A.)\n\nhe who does not feel me\nIs not real to me\n\nIf you’re not with Young Money Cash Money, Weezy F. Baby would not hesitate to give a nice little FUCK YOU.", "annotation_id": "494328", "url": "https://genius.com/494328", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "No beginner to the criminal activity (Come on) Fuck with them, they rushing in like Seminoles (Oh), Indians (Oh) No bow and arrows, Harold (No) Just Ninas, Gina (Damn) Just choppers, Robert (Damn)", "vault_lines": ["No beginner to the criminal activity (Come on)"], "meaning": "Breaking the law is nothing new, maybe even like difficulty setting…\n\n\nbeginner\nnormal\nhard <\n\n\n\nRushin' in like Florida State Seminoles, football reference also, The Powhatan Indian Attack of March 22, 1622. Where The Powhatan Tribe attacked colony of Virginia. It was a rush in kill everybody and everything 1 day massacre.\n\nInstead of using bows and arrows like they did now they are using guns mainly machine guns.", "annotation_id": "487613", "url": "https://genius.com/487613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "I’m in the lead, I could pop a wheelie (Got ’em)", "vault_lines": ["I'm in the lead, I could pop a wheelie (Got 'em)"], "meaning": "He’s so far ahead of everyone else he can take the time to do a trick and they still won’t catch up to him\n\nWayne means that his level is already high, so he can do what ever he wants and he’ll still be winning, no matter what he produces. Reminds me of someone:\n\n\n\nAgain, advice Wayne would eventually act upon by drowning in pussy, frying himself with sizzurp and making “Rebirth”.", "annotation_id": "361548", "url": "https://genius.com/361548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "I’m hungry like I didn’t eat (Yeah) I want it like I didn’t see a mil’ before seventeen (Boy)", "vault_lines": ["I'm hungry like I didn't eat (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Check the word “mill”. It is closely enunciated like the word, “meal”. Referencing to the last line about being hungry like he didn’t eat.\n\n\n\nMeaning he’s hungry as in his goal was to see $1 million dollars before 17.", "annotation_id": "191181", "url": "https://genius.com/191181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Mobb", "line": "And the beat keep crying, and I’ma keep beating her (Yeah) Fee, I’m fucking her, I’m deep in her, sleep in her (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["And the beat keep crying, and I'ma keep beating her (Yeah)"], "meaning": "A metaphorical explanation as to how he’s destroying the beat, lyrically. Wayne’s so immersed in it that it’s as if he’s mating with it and sleeping inside it, as if it’s a place of solace.\n\n\n\nThis wouldn’t be the last time Wayne mentions “beating the beat up”, he also uses it in this line off of 6 Foot 7 Foot.", "annotation_id": "89986", "url": "https://genius.com/89986", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
