{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Blues", "line": "And when you see me on the block, I come to give ’em the blues", "vault_lines": ["And when you see me on the block, I come to give 'em the blues"], "meaning": "“The blues” refers to blue opiate pills like like percs, oxys and more. This line means that when you see Lil' Wayne out on the streets he’s there selling drugs making money.", "annotation_id": "38532947", "url": "https://genius.com/38532947", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Blues", "line": "Believe this, my ninas got more shells than Adidas", "vault_lines": ["Believe this, my ninas got more shells than Adidas"], "meaning": "In essence, Wayne owns (and fires) more bullets than Adidas sells shoes.\n\n“Nina” is a slang or code term for a nine-millimeter handgun. Adidas famously sells a particular design of shoe that has been termed the “shell toe.”", "annotation_id": "33880297", "url": "https://genius.com/33880297", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
