{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Block Is Hot", "line": "No respect for no slut, and no money without power", "vault_lines": ["No respect for no slut, and no money without power"], "meaning": "This is a nod to The LOX’s 1998 song, “Money, Power & Respect” which features Lil’ Kim and DMX. It remains as the group’s most successful single. It peaked at #18 on Billboard Hot 100 and was certified gold in April 1998.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7suhKO9B50Q", "annotation_id": "18265719", "url": "https://genius.com/18265719", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Block Is Hot", "line": "And we’ll be ’round ya all day (Why?) ’til we “400 Degreez”", "vault_lines": ["And we'll be 'round ya all day (Why?) 'til we \"400 Degreez\""], "meaning": "400 Degreez is an album by fellow Hot Boys member Juvenile.", "annotation_id": "3231454", "url": "https://genius.com/3231454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tha Block Is Hot", "line": "Pile up in the Eddie Bauer and “blocka” at every hour", "vault_lines": ["Pile up in the Eddie Bauer and \"blocka\" at every hour"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has said he owned an Eddie Bauer edition Expedition around 1999/2000. When this song was released in the late 1990s, an Eddie Bauer edition Ford Expedition was a high profile car worth bragging about. “BLAKA” imitates the sound of a weapon firing. I.E., Wayne and his boys regularly crowd into expensive cars and do drive bys on their enemies.", "annotation_id": "768060", "url": "https://genius.com/768060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
