{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "I’m kicking out the weak and the timid", "vault_lines": ["I'm kicking out the weak and the timid"], "meaning": "Anyone that doesn’t exhibit strength, will be dominated by those who do have it.\n\nThe strong dominate the weak.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27273891", "url": "https://genius.com/27273891", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "Sometimes you need to take a step back and breathe for a minute Before you overreact to the heat and intenseness", "vault_lines": ["Sometimes you need to take a step back and breathe for a minute"], "meaning": "Instead of immediately responding to a situation & letting your emotions get the best of you, it’s better to take a moment to process the situation, & deliberate in a healthy manner.\n\nOverreacting to a situation that has a simple solution does nothing but bring more hurt, pain, & make the situation even worse than it was.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27273876", "url": "https://genius.com/27273876", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "Hopes man, I don’t even have ’em Burning ladders, bridges", "vault_lines": ["Hopes man, I don't even have 'em"], "meaning": "Hodgy is in such a mental distress, that he doesn’t even have hopes for a better life or future. (Ironic, considering in the next line he does)\n\nBurning bridges is an idiom. It means “To destroy one’s path, connections, reputation, opportunities, etc., particularly intentionally.”\n\nBurning a ladder could mean that he’s destroying his upward mobility, as well. This wordplay also means “latter”.\n\nThe terms former and latter are words used to distinguish between two things. Former directs us to the first of these two things, and latter directs us to the second (or last) of them. So, Hodgy is burning the latters (his hopes) bridges.\n\nThis could be a hint towards the bridge he burned with Tyler, The Creator during 2015 when he claimed the money changed Tyler & how Odd Future wasn’t what it was before.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27273849", "url": "https://genius.com/27273849", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "This liquor, nine months ago swear I’d make better decisions I would drink by the liter of kittens, my liver bleeds while I’m checking out instead of seeing the difference", "vault_lines": ["This liquor, nine months ago swear I'd make better decisions"], "meaning": "People who have issues or traumas, will often resort to drugs & alcohol to ease their pain.\n\nInstead of directly processing the issue, it’s easier to use escapism in those forms.\n\nHodgy, himself uses alcohol to deal with his issues. So much, that he gets blacked out drunk. Too much alcohol will damage your liver, which can cause alcohol poisoning & likely kill you.\n\nThe worst part about it all, is that even though you’ve escaped for a while, the issues still linger within your soul until you solve it. So, he’s not “seeing a difference”.\n\nHe also makes a clever play on words with “liter”. A liter is a volume amount of liquid. A litter of kittens is a group of animals born at one time. So in this sense, he’s drinking “liters” of alcohol from his “litter” of alcohol.\n\nUntil you build better habits, your life will stay the same.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27270032", "url": "https://genius.com/27270032", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "I’m whoopin’ at the deceased, horse leaving an imprint", "vault_lines": ["I'm whoopin' at the deceased, horse leaving an imprint"], "meaning": "Hodgy’s “beating a dead horse”, or continuing to waste energy on a situation that will not change or has already been solved.\n\nHe leaves an imprint by continuously talking about it till he feels satisfaction. This is a form of processing pain, although it doesn’t benefit you long term to continue beating a dead horse.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27270021", "url": "https://genius.com/27270021", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "You niggas snoring ’cause you sleep with the fishes", "vault_lines": ["You niggas snoring 'cause you sleep with the fishes"], "meaning": "The expression sleep with the fishes is a popular term used in media that portray the American Mafia or organized crime. The image is of a murdered person’s body being thrown into a body of water in order to escape detection.\n\nThis can also be a term on how a lot of musicians are “slept on”, or how their music isn’t listened to on a wider scale compared to mainstream artists.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27270010", "url": "https://genius.com/27270010", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "I’ma breeze to the finish and I’ma weep when I win it", "vault_lines": ["I'ma breeze to the finish and I'ma weep when I win it"], "meaning": "To “breeze” is to move so effortlessly through a challenge, that it might as well not be one. & even though he breeze to the finish line of his challenge, he still appreciates the challenge enough to “weep” tears of joys for winning it.\n\nIronic, considering that people often don’t appreciate things that are easy to obtain. It shows Lil Wayne’s humility in his occupation.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27269991", "url": "https://genius.com/27269991", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "Fuck the pigs all day, even the guineas", "vault_lines": ["Fuck the pigs all day, even the guineas"], "meaning": "“Pigs” is slang for police. The 12th letter in the alphabet is the letter “P”, which also refers to “police” or “pigs”.\n\nA clever play on words to say that the police are literally pigs, & to dismiss even Guinea pigs who associate with the police. The “pigs” line can also refer to how police officers often arrest, antagonize, or even kill black folks who do no wrong. Thus, making them disgusting pigs.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27269968", "url": "https://genius.com/27269968", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "Blood gang, creme de la creme is the Crimson", "vault_lines": ["Blood gang, creme de la creme is the Crimson"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne refers to himself as one of the best gang members to ever exist.\n\n“Crème de la crème” means to be the best of the best.\n\nA great way to view oneself when doing something very dangerous, or challenging.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27269960", "url": "https://genius.com/27269960", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "You say you’re gangsta I’ma need some convincing", "vault_lines": [", you say you're gangsta I'ma need some convincing"], "meaning": "Everyone wants to be a gangster & appear tougher than they actually are. However, when they come across someone who’s ACTUALLY tough & “about that life”, (participates in gang-related activities) they usually cower away in fear, get beat up, finessed, or killed.\n\nWayne is a well known gang member, so he wants to test the person who claims to be a gangsta to see if he’s willing to die for respect.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27269952", "url": "https://genius.com/27269952", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "Born in antagonism, at times I can’t even fathom", "vault_lines": ["Born in antagonism, at times I can't even fathom"], "meaning": "Hodgy displays how rough he had it growing up. In a recent interview, he expressed how he was homeless from 16, all the way until he was 20 years old when Odd Future first got signed.\n\nHe can’t even believe in his own imagination that it was really his reality.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27267800", "url": "https://genius.com/27267800", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "When the reaper come get me that’s when I reap what I’m knitting So", "vault_lines": ["When the reaper come get me that's when I reap what I'm knitting"], "meaning": "A clever play on words with the quote: “You reap what you sow.”\n\nMeaning: You’ll have to face the consequences of your actions eventually.\n\nThe Grim Reaper is the personification of death. He comes down to collect a person’s soul when it’s their time to die.\n\nLil Wayne takes the quote further by saying he’ll face his consequences ONLY when he dies. Till then, he’ll continue to do what he wants.\n\nAlso, the word “So”, is more wordplay that can also be used to display him “sowing” his the actions in the next line.\n\n\nMaãlík", "annotation_id": "27267759", "url": "https://genius.com/27267759", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "I don’t repeat I’m repentant", "vault_lines": ["But I'm saying, I don't repeat I'm repentant"], "meaning": "This line refer to his drama with Cash Money Records over the delay of his album Tha Carter V. He’s regretted of staying with Cash Money and as of now, he’s no longer connected to the label anymore (cut off the hand). Hand out a sentence alludes to his 51 million lawsuit with the label http://www.rollingstone.com/music/news/lil-wayne-sues-cash-money-for-51-million-20150128", "annotation_id": "11850315", "url": "https://genius.com/11850315", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "Started from a leak now we swimming", "vault_lines": ["Started from a leak now we swimming"], "meaning": "Wayne mentions how he started out by making albums and leaked music. But now he is swimming in the money/fame produced by these leaks and releases.\n\nThis could also be a nod to the hook from his label-mate Drake’s hit “Started From The Bottom”:\n\nStarted from the bottom now we here", "annotation_id": "11278854", "url": "https://genius.com/11278854", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "Niggas ain’t keepin’ it pimping, Weezy baby to an infant I’m growing", "vault_lines": ["Niggas ain't keepin' it pimping, Weezy baby to an infant"], "meaning": "Wayne is going through some problems with his record label Cash Money. Before he used to want to be called “Weezy Baby,” but now that he is past Cash Money, he denounces them by saying “I’m growing.”", "annotation_id": "11278741", "url": "https://genius.com/11278741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tape Beat", "line": "You’ll be like sheep to a grizzly, put my bare feet on them bitches", "vault_lines": ["You'll be like sheep to a grizzly, put my bare feet on them bitches"], "meaning": "Comparing other to Wayne is like comparing a sheep – herbivore to a grizzly – canivore. He plays on the homophone bare and bear to express how he’ll treat other rappers", "annotation_id": "11003143", "url": "https://genius.com/11003143", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
