{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "And I’m ballin’, no cushion", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "This could mean two things:\n\n1) Detail is having sex without a condom.\n\n2) Detail is spending money like he has no limit.", "annotation_id": "2021024", "url": "https://genius.com/2021024", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "(Rich girl)", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "You would think that given her presence on this song, Birdman is talking about Nicki Minaj, but no. “Rich Girl” is actually Birdman’s nickname for recent YMCMB signee Paris Hilton. (…don’t ask no ones entirely sure how that came about, save for Birdman saying YMCMB is “hustlers”).\n\nhttps://twitter.com/BIRDMAN5STAR/statuses/337283702855966721\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(Of course in the interest of fairness, one has to point out that Nicki did earn more than Birdman in 2013.) Then again, Birdman is still worth more overall, at $170M to Nicki’s $45M.", "annotation_id": "1993572", "url": "https://genius.com/1993572", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "I’m in love with your Egyptian skin", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "Egyptians are well known for their notoriously lighter skin than the rest of the African brothers and sisters, and the Rich Gang have fallen prey to the lust that one spontaneously finds their mind lost in when viewing a light-skinned female.\n\nHere are a few very attractive Egyptian women.\n\n\n\nEgypt’s Miss Universe contestant model Yara Naoum.\n\n\n\nEgyptian actress Nelly Karim.", "annotation_id": "1936565", "url": "https://genius.com/1936565", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "[Verse 3: Nicki Minaj & Birdman]", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "Nicki has often been blurring the lines between rapping and singing in her work, although here is one of the few instances where she switches instinctively between singing and rapping, in a style very similar to that popularised by her close friend and labelmate Drake.", "annotation_id": "1750611", "url": "https://genius.com/1750611", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "(Flossing while you’re shining, jumping out of Bugattis)", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "Birdman is referring to the automobile.\n\n\n\nBirdman is one of the first rappers to purchase a Bugatti.\n\nBirdman has also made a few references in his songs about the vehicle.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jAxSo7HyUek", "annotation_id": "1741041", "url": "https://genius.com/1741041", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "(Rich Gang)", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "Lately, Birdman has begun promoting some of his businesses with classy body (actually facial) art. The latest one he copped was for Rich Gang, his new mixtape which contains this song.", "annotation_id": "1624573", "url": "https://genius.com/1624573", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "Million dollar checks, don’t bounce on that ass", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "Nicki uses a quadruple reference here:\n\n1.) Nicki accepts million dollar checks, they will not bounce (a term that refers to checks that are rejected by the Bank when insufficient funds are associated between the check and respective account).\n\n2.) Anyone spending a million on Nicki’s ass will not regret it, because she can cash those checks, in other words deliver. Satisfied customers.\n\n3.) A million is nothing to Nicki, so a million dollar check will literally not MAKE her ASS BOUNCE in excitement for it.\n\n4.) Lastly, Nicki herself cashes million dollar checks acquired via her booty, remember sex sales in Hollywood. Hence, the next line where Nicki brags about her very expensive car.", "annotation_id": "1609926", "url": "https://genius.com/1609926", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "Bald head, yup, don’t want no Forrest, Gumps", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "#TRIM THOSE BUSHES!\n\n\n\n\nBald head pussy = no hair, wordplay on Forrest Gump.   So she wants no hairy “forest” on herself and is kept clean\nForest Gump is a fast runner and tends to run away from his problems in the movie. She knows men don’t like a backwoods snatch (well it depends on the guy) so she shaves it just as  precaution, to stop a man from doing a “forest gump” and running away like any pussy nigga would.\nGump himself, also is fond of cats in the film as well and is really soft for a man of his stature.\nCould be suggesting, that she only plays hardball with of men who are stripped, down there. She doesn’t want men who have a downstairs shrub themselves and is hygienic.\nAdditionally, Minaj loves it when her men are “brainy” (when they are performing oral sex). Forrest Gump isn’t entirely intelligent, and she wouldn’t want him near her “bald head”.\nIn the gif at the top, the Hanks character prematurely ejaculates very fast, for the first time, when he has sex with the love of his life, Jenny. I can’t imagine Nicki would want 2 pussies in the bedroom", "annotation_id": "1607967", "url": "https://genius.com/1607967", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "Alexander McQueen, rich in the paint", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "Alexander McQueen was a wealthy fashion designer who occasionally employed paint in his work.\n\nIt’s hard to see Stunnaman rockin' this though.\n\nCan also be heard as “rich in the pain”. McQueen was a tortured soul and eventually committed suicide.", "annotation_id": "1596875", "url": "https://genius.com/1596875", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "(Sexy Slim, I see you, paradise home, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "Ronald Williams also known as Slim is Cash Money Records Co-Founder with Birdman, he’s also his big brother.\n\nWilliams brothers (Birdman left, Slim right):", "annotation_id": "1594811", "url": "https://genius.com/1594811", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "Millions on the Maybach, glass top ceilings", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "Birdman spent $8 million on a Maybach Exelero:\n\n\n\nBaby also owns a $1.6 million Maybach 62S Landaulet which  ceiling is half convertible and half glass top.\n\nhttp://youtu.be/Xe6IVSwgWYI", "annotation_id": "1594715", "url": "https://genius.com/1594715", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "Married to the money, millions in the bank", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "Birdman has A LOT of money, literally millions in the bank. Forbes listed him as the 4th wealthiest Hip-Hop artist with a net worth of about $125 million. That’s a lot of money!", "annotation_id": "1580213", "url": "https://genius.com/1580213", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "Pussy jewelry make ’em say, “Burr man”", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "#FROZEN TURKEY\nReference to Gucci Mane’s coined term:\n\n\n\n\nBritish readers may find this implies Nicki’s had a “vajazzle” (a craze in certain areas of the UK where women put – often fake – jewels around their shaved pussies).\nShe refers to her hypothetical, “pussy jewelry”. Taking this into account she’s trying to say that she has enough a lot of diamonds around her’s to make guy want to stay warm.", "annotation_id": "1580060", "url": "https://genius.com/1580060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "Tell the pigs I say, “As-salamu alaykum,” uh", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "As-salamu alaykum is the greeting of Muslims, meaning “peace be upon you” Here Tunechi is saying that he doesn’t like the police – often colloquially known as “pigs”.\n\n\n\nEating pigs is forbidden in Islam. And although Wayne isn’t Muslim, he deals with the police (pigs) the same way Muslims would deal with actual pigs (ie. the animals in the bottom picture) – by avoiding them altogether.", "annotation_id": "1580015", "url": "https://genius.com/1580015", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "My bitch a choosy lover, never fuck without a rubber", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "This line interpolates Pimp C’s verse on UGK’s “International Player’s Anthem”:\n\nMy bitch a choosy lover, never fuck without a rubber\nNever in the sheets, like it on top of the cover", "annotation_id": "1577753", "url": "https://genius.com/1577753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "R-r-r-r-r-rubs hands like Birdman", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "One of Birdman’s signatures – rubbing his hands together. Despite, her rich ass verse about pulling up in cars we never can afford and being on Forbes list making millions her palms stay ichin' which many believes means that more money is on the way.\n\nMoney on the way It’s got both of my palms itching", "annotation_id": "1577722", "url": "https://genius.com/1577722", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Tap Out", "line": "Only rap bitch on the Forbes list", "vault_lines": ["Million dollar, oh, oh"], "meaning": "Nicki is the only female rapper that has made the Forbes list in recent years. No other female hip-hop artist even made the list…", "annotation_id": "1577717", "url": "https://genius.com/1577717", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
