{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Dressed in Balmain", "vault_lines": ["Young Moo–, Young Moolah, baby"], "meaning": "“Dressed in Balmain” Young Thug flexes that he’s boolin’ at the basketball game wearing Balmain, a high-end luxury fashion brand known for its bold, rockstar aesthetic and expensive pieces.\nThe “(Fresh)” ad-lib emphasizes how clean and stylish he looks. This fits perfectly into the song’s lavish, carefree Rich Gang lifestyle dropping racks on clothes while living extravagantly.", "annotation_id": "40302643", "url": "https://genius.com/40302643", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Young Moo–, Young Moolah, baby", "vault_lines": ["Young Moo–, Young Moolah, baby"], "meaning": "Trademark Weezeh", "annotation_id": "32952171", "url": "https://genius.com/32952171", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "(Rich Gang) Ooh! (Ahh!)", "vault_lines": ["Young Moo–, Young Moolah, baby"], "meaning": "You know what it is. Rich Gang, millions and billions. This tag is formerly and more known for the Rich Gang collectives music which consisted of Young Thug, Birdman, and Rich Homie Quan. This tag was more commonly used in the Rich Gang: Tha Tour Part 1 mixtape released in 2004.", "annotation_id": "19557842", "url": "https://genius.com/19557842", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Every time they hate, I throw them bands like a bouquet (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Every time they hate, I throw them bands like a bouquet (Woo)"], "meaning": "Young Thug is using his materialistic gains and his wealth to drown the hate. And he uses the simile of throwing his “bands” which represent his wealth, like that of a bouquet typically thrown in a wedding.", "annotation_id": "19557811", "url": "https://genius.com/19557811", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "We got London on da Track", "vault_lines": ["We got London on da Track"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag of Atlanta producer London Tyler Holmes. He has collaborated with Thugger on many occasions, including popular trap records such as “Lifestyle,” “Power,” and “With That.”", "annotation_id": "17378842", "url": "https://genius.com/17378842", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Take a trip to Peru Baby suck my dog like Snoop (Hey)", "vault_lines": ["Take a trip to Peru"], "meaning": "Thugger is out in Peru getting head. He refers to his dick as a “dog,” creating a play on Snoop Dogg’s name.", "annotation_id": "8102929", "url": "https://genius.com/8102929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "I’m really feelin’ super, like eight (Whew)", "vault_lines": ["I'm really feelin' super, like eight (Whew)"], "meaning": "A play on the J.J. Abrams-directed movie Super 8.\n\n\n\nCould also be referring to Super 8 motels, which ironically are far from super.\n\nCould also be referring to Super 8 cameras. Which is what the film is referring to.", "annotation_id": "4234634", "url": "https://genius.com/4234634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Ice inside my ring, you can skate (Skate)", "vault_lines": ["Ice inside my ring, you can skate (Skate)"], "meaning": "Thug describes his jewelry as ice to articulate that the diamonds are very clear and clean. Thugger’s ring being so “ice” that you can skate on it is a witty metaphor stressing how clean and clear the diamonds in the ring are.", "annotation_id": "4197105", "url": "https://genius.com/4197105", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Brand new Bentley, you could keep the ceiling (Skrrt skrrt, woo)", "vault_lines": ["Brand new Bentley, you could keep the ceiling (Skrrt skrrt, woo)"], "meaning": "Thugger is so rich that he can splash out his money on more premium items, he doesn’t really think about it anymore – he buys whatever he likes. Here he’s simply referring to a convertible version of the well known luxury car. ‘You can keep the ceiling of the car’ means Young Thug sees this as a minor thing, it doesn’t matter to him because of how wealthy he’s become.", "annotation_id": "4195972", "url": "https://genius.com/4195972", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Salutations to my old hoes And thank you for your participation", "vault_lines": ["Salutations to my old hoes"], "meaning": "Weezy’s been with a variety of girls in the past, from models to video vixens to athletes, and he would simply like to say hello and thank them for past experiences\n\n\n\nThe use of “thank you for your participation” is interesting, because awards for participation often are consolation prizes for those who didn’t win. Perhaps Wayne is thanking them for participation, because none of them have “won” his heart", "annotation_id": "4195240", "url": "https://genius.com/4195240", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "She so bad, I don’t know what to do with her I know just what to do in her", "vault_lines": ["She so bad, I don't know what to do with her"], "meaning": "Weezy is blinded by his female’s beauty to the point he can’t keep his head clear enough to figure out their future plans together and just wants to jump straight to bed with her, his area of expertise, so he knows exactly what to do!", "annotation_id": "4194871", "url": "https://genius.com/4194871", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "No chaser for my girl, though (Rich girl) She go harder than me on occasion Gettin’ wasted with my girl", "vault_lines": ["No chaser for my girl, though (Rich girl)"], "meaning": "A chaser is a drink people usually take right after a shot of hard alcohol to blunt the harsh feeling the shot can leave in your mouth. His girl (Christina Milian) doesn’t need a chaser; she takes the liquor straight. She even drinks more than Weezy some times – it’s their way of having fun.\n\nWeezy could also be referring to sex in this passage. “No Chaser”, his girl is enough for him, so he doesn’t need a “follow-up” ho. Similarly, “go(ing) hard” also may imply that she occasionally has more bed stamina than Weezy. These bars are basically emphasizing he has realized how compatible his girl is to him, fitting in with the theme of the song.", "annotation_id": "4194865", "url": "https://genius.com/4194865", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "On a million, goin’ to meet a billion (Chasin’, chasin’ racks!)", "vault_lines": ["On a million, goin' to meet a billion (Chasin', chasin' racks!)"], "meaning": "Thugger has made his first million already (net worth of 19 million to be exact), but he’s not done yet! His next motive is to make his first billion. Now that’s grinding.", "annotation_id": "4193486", "url": "https://genius.com/4193486", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "I’ll never believe what Lil’ Kim say (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["I'll never believe what Lil' Kim say (Ooh)"], "meaning": "It’s a reference to beef between Lil Kim & Nicki Minaj. Specifically, Kim claimed that Nicki (part of Rich Gang) copied her image. She also said that YMCMB stole her old demos. As a loyal member of the Cash Money family, Thug doesn’t believe this and supports Nicki.", "annotation_id": "4193433", "url": "https://genius.com/4193433", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "She don’t gangbang, she say she bang gangs (Bang)", "vault_lines": ["She don't gangbang, she say she bang gangs (Bang)"], "meaning": "The girl Thugger is with might not gang bang or take part in illegal activities but she has sex with straight up gangsters, and thus is “down to ride” in her own way…", "annotation_id": "4193416", "url": "https://genius.com/4193416", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "I just wanna nut, she say that’s easy like a baker (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["I just wanna nut, she say that's easy like a baker (Woo)"], "meaning": "Remember when Lil Wayne spit “It’s going down, it’s going down like there’s a whale in the boat” and made it work? This is Thug’s turn.\n\nWith a line about an Easy Bake Oven.", "annotation_id": "4193392", "url": "https://genius.com/4193392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Yeah she got Xans, she like, “Where Tar at?” (Geek)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah she got Xans, she like, \"Where Tar at?\" (Geek)"], "meaning": "Xan is short for Xanax – an anxiety/sleep disorder pill that is known to pair well with that lean. Thugger’s girl isn’t stopping there, though – she wants  tar (heroin) too.\n\nNote that combining benzodiazepines (Xanax) and opiates (heroin) can be extremely dangerous, even fatal.\n\n\n\nXanax on the left, heroin on the right\n\nThis is also a play off of Tarzan’s name, perhaps implying that the girl has a wild side.", "annotation_id": "4193372", "url": "https://genius.com/4193372", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Blood gang, big ups, suwoo (Blatt)", "vault_lines": ["Blood gang, big ups, suwoo (Blatt)"], "meaning": "Soo Woo is a phrase a Blood gang member says to get another Blood’s attention. Young Thug has always been open about his affiliation with Bloods, and mentions it in many songs, such as The Blanguage:\n\nTalkin shit, might drop, people listen to it\nI’m bangin’ blood, I could never flue it", "annotation_id": "4193338", "url": "https://genius.com/4193338", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Gotta open up the stores when they’re closed when we shoppin’ For my girl, wear the clothes that ain’t nobody rockin’", "vault_lines": ["Gotta open up the stores when they're closed when we shoppin'"], "meaning": "Weezy is so rich that he takes his girl to designer stores after they are closed so she can get private time to go through the store without people bothering her.\n\nThis is very familiar with a Kanye West line in Rick Ross’s song “Live Fast, Die Young”.\n\nAnd I know it’s superficial and you say it’s just clothes\nBut we shopping in that motherfucker and they just closed", "annotation_id": "4193313", "url": "https://genius.com/4193313", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Bought a castle with my last deal (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Bought a castle with my last deal (Woah)"], "meaning": "Thug’s finally getting meta on us – his signed-to-everybody-yet-not-signed-at-all status is well-documented and is highly responsible for the flood of music that we’ve seen come out in 2014 from him that may or may not have been recorded far in the past. Regardless of what that last deal was, nobody can deny that he’s always about those foreign homes.", "annotation_id": "4193305", "url": "https://genius.com/4193305", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "They be hatin’ on my girl, though And they wish they was the bitch they hatin’", "vault_lines": ["They be hatin' on my girl, though"], "meaning": "People envy Wayne’s current girlfriend Christina Milian, because they want to be her… they want to be in her place, but that’s never going to happen for them, so instead\n\nhaters gonna hate.", "annotation_id": "4193289", "url": "https://genius.com/4193289", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "Gotta open new accounts ’cause the others overcrowded", "vault_lines": ["Gotta open new accounts 'cause the others overcrowded"], "meaning": "I chase the bank, I don’t bank with Chase\n\nWe all know that Wayne has got money – in fact, so much that he has to set up separate bank accounts just to hold it all. Theoretically, he could have it all in one account, but it’s a much smarter move to divide it into several, more manageable accounts due to the FDIC insurance regulations, which only insure up to $250,000 per account in the event of bank failure, etc.", "annotation_id": "4193277", "url": "https://genius.com/4193277", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "line": "My homies hit me up, they said they’re goin’ out tonight I said, “I’m with my girl tonight, I can’t fuck with you niggas” I’ma take care of her", "vault_lines": ["Take care of her!"], "meaning": "Weezy is down with his girl, he spends quality time with her. He’s currently in a relationship with  Christina Milian, so whenveer his friends hit him up and say they are going out tonight, he gives them a raincheck because he wants to spend time with his girl. Wayne knows that he needs to make her feel special and take care of her.", "annotation_id": "4193263", "url": "https://genius.com/4193263", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take Kare", "status": "done", "targets": 23, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Young-thug-take-kare-lyrics", "genius_title": "Take Kare", "genius_id": 542248, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Another one DJ Khaled", "vault_lines": ["One shot, two shots, I'm gone (Ooh-ooh)"], "meaning": "These are DJ Khaled’s trademark slogans that he often proclaims in the intro of his songs since the 2000s.\n\n“Another One” is his way of saying that he has another hit on his hands.", "annotation_id": "17948820", "url": "https://genius.com/17948820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "I eat her ice cream, she eat my ice cream cone (Hahaha)", "vault_lines": ["I eat her ice cream, she eat my ice cream cone (Hahaha)"], "meaning": "Wayne uses “ice cream” and “ice cream cone” to represent the female and the male genitalia respectively. On his 2006 song “Feeling Myself,” Wayne also mentions ice cream but uses it to represent cocaine:\n\nFeds hear my cell ring\nPhone, we say ice cream\nHome, we say white", "annotation_id": "17948787", "url": "https://genius.com/17948787", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Big fat nigga, all that huffin’ and puffin’", "vault_lines": ["Big fat nigga, all that huffin' and puffin'"], "meaning": "Nicki calling her man a “big fat nigga” means he stacked with cash. This makes sense as Nicki talk about shopping in France in the following lines.\n\nAdditionally, this could be a shoutout to Rick Ross, who is also featured on this song and is famously overweight. Nicki also shouted out him on 2015’s “No Flex Zone (Remix)”:\n\nAss still fat, it’s on Rick Ross", "annotation_id": "17948727", "url": "https://genius.com/17948727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Reputation for G’s, that’s the role of a boss", "vault_lines": ["Reputation for G's, that's the role of a boss"], "meaning": "Ross first called himself a “boss” in 2006 and has since used the term frequently in his music. He even has a 2011 song called “You The Boss” with Nicki Minaj, who is also featured on this song.", "annotation_id": "17948611", "url": "https://genius.com/17948611", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Fuck with me, baby, it’s Tunechi, baby", "vault_lines": ["Fuck with me, baby, it's Tunechi, baby"], "meaning": "In a 2010 interview with MTV, Wayne explained the origin of his nickname, Tunechi:\n\nMy nickname is Lil Tune—my grandmother named me that […] We just threw the ‘Chi’ on there. Like Gucci, I say ‘Tunechi!’", "annotation_id": "17941820", "url": "https://genius.com/17941820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Girl, that pussy like medication to patients Got my eyes closed like Asian persuasion", "vault_lines": ["Girl, that pussy like medication to patients"], "meaning": "Wayne implies that sex with his girl is so intense that he ends up falling asleep after he’s done.\n\nIt’s stereotyped that Asians have small eyes due to the epicanthic fold of their upper eyelid—Wayne compares this to his eyes being closed.", "annotation_id": "17941791", "url": "https://genius.com/17941791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "I bet you Tunechi make her throw away that silver bullet, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I bet you Tunechi make her throw away that silver bullet, yeah"], "meaning": "A silver bullet is a vibrator—a sex toy that’s used to provide pleasurable sexual stimulation. Wayne notes here that his sex game is pleasurable enough for his girl and that she doesn’t need an alternative.\n\nWayne ends his verse with a sexual allusion as it cuts to Chris Brown singing “Take it to the head”—meaning in Wayne’s case, oral sex.", "annotation_id": "17941716", "url": "https://genius.com/17941716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "With all that pink on, bitch, I’m King Kong", "vault_lines": ["With all that pink on, bitch, I'm King Kong"], "meaning": "King Kong is a fictional monstrous ape that first appeared in the media in 1933, following its debut film that year. He’s one of the most famous movie icons in the world, inspiring numerous sequels, remakes, cartoons, and much more.\n\nWayne also has a 2007 song titled “King Kong,” however in a different context. Here, he’s talking about his ape-like behavior in bed.", "annotation_id": "17941531", "url": "https://genius.com/17941531", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Bust a nut, smoke a blunt, now I’m rejuvenated", "vault_lines": ["Bust a nut, smoke a blunt, now I'm rejuvenated"], "meaning": "“Buss a nut” means to ejaculate and “rejuvenated” means to feel fresh and younger.\n\nSex and weed is a common theme in Wayne’s music—he even has a song called “Pussy Money Weed,” which he released in 2007.", "annotation_id": "17941406", "url": "https://genius.com/17941406", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "I’m killin’ them hoes like Jason", "vault_lines": ["I'm killin' them hoes like Jason"], "meaning": "Jason Voorhees is the main character and antagonist of the American slasher horror film franchise, Friday the 13th. It focuses on Jason, who murders anyone residing at the fictional Camp Crystal Lake as revenge for his drowning as a little boy due to the camp staff’s negligence.", "annotation_id": "17941184", "url": "https://genius.com/17941184", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Uh, reputation for tastin’", "vault_lines": ["Uh, reputation for tastin'"], "meaning": "Wayne’s claim isn’t too far fetched—he even has a song called “Pussy Monster,” which is all about the female’s genitalia. It was released in 2008 and is featured on Tha Carter III.\n\nHi, I’m the\nPussy monster, the pussy monster\nThe pussy monster, the pussy monster\nAnd you gotta feed me\nPussy, pussy pussy, pussy pussy", "annotation_id": "17941170", "url": "https://genius.com/17941170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Competition, I don’t see any (Woo-hoo, ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Competition, I don't see any (Woo-hoo, ooh)"], "meaning": "During the late 2000s and early 2010s, other than Nicki, there wasn’t a big female presence in rap. Here, she boasts that her work ethic is no match for another female competitor.\n\nFor example, in 2011, she released her debut album, Pink Friday to massive success, topping the US Billboard charts. It was even nominated for Best Rap Album at the 54th Annual Grammy Awards, which Nicki attended two months before this verse. While she didn’t win, it was still a big deal as Pink Friday became the first female Grammy-nominated rap album since Missy Elliott’s Under Construction in 2004.", "annotation_id": "16892712", "url": "https://genius.com/16892712", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "I-I-I ride for him, DMV", "vault_lines": ["I-I-I ride for him, DMV"], "meaning": "DMV is an abbreviation for the Department of Motor Vehicles. It’s a US state-level government agency that manages vehicle registration and driver licensing.\n\nNicki plays on the word “ride,” meaning she’s a ride or die chick. She’ll stand by her man no matter what.", "annotation_id": "16892595", "url": "https://genius.com/16892595", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "I got a lot of figures (Yeah), I’m a father figure (Me)", "vault_lines": ["I got a lot of figures (Yeah), I'm a father figure (Me)"], "meaning": "In 2012, Rick Ross' net worth was estimated to be about $15 million. This, in part, came from his restaurant franchise Wingstop—which he first opened in 2011—and the success of his mixtape, Rich Forever and album, God Forgives, I Don’t, which he would later release three months later.\n\nA “father figure” is a person of power or influence who serves as an emotional substitute for a father. Ross is a father himself, who had two kids at the time of this song’s release.", "annotation_id": "16886085", "url": "https://genius.com/16886085", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "She know a lot of niggas, don’t know a hotter nigga (Ha!)", "vault_lines": ["She know a lot of niggas, don't know a hotter nigga (Ha!)"], "meaning": "Just 3 months before this verse, Ross released his second mixtape, titled Rich Forever. It became one of the most downloaded hip hop mixtapes of all time and was well-received from critics.\n\nAdditionally, Ross was named the “Hottest MC” of 2011 by MTV.", "annotation_id": "16885997", "url": "https://genius.com/16885997", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "She got all them purses, I say in my verses YSL and Hermès and barely scratch the surface (Ugh!)", "vault_lines": ["She got all them purses, I say in my verses"], "meaning": "YSL—Yves Saint Laurent—and Hermès are both French luxury fashion houses. YSL purses usually cost thousands of dollars while Hermès'  Birkin handbags can cost up to millions of dollars.\n\n“Barely scratch the surface” could mean buying these expensive items isn’t a big deal for Ross.", "annotation_id": "16885909", "url": "https://genius.com/16885909", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "So amazin’ to see, black baguettes in my watch", "vault_lines": ["So amazin' to see, black baguettes in my watch"], "meaning": "A baguette-cut is a square-cut diamond which seemingly resembles the shape of a baguette—a type of French bread.\n\nThey’re often used in rings, earrings, and bracelets but in Ross' case, a watch.\n\n\n\nA Caviar Tourbillon Collection Timepiece invisibly set with Black Baguette Diamonds", "annotation_id": "16885867", "url": "https://genius.com/16885867", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Stamina, GNC", "vault_lines": ["One shot, two shots, I'm gone (Ooh-ooh)"], "meaning": "GNC is a health company that also sells nutrition products. This line also follows from the previous, implying that, in the sack (and probably in every other aspect), Nicki has great stamina and resilience.", "annotation_id": "14336021", "url": "https://genius.com/14336021", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Take It to the Head", "line": "Three letters, CMB", "vault_lines": ["One shot, two shots, I'm gone (Ooh-ooh)"], "meaning": "It’s a word play line. She says CMB as in Cash Money Business (or Billionaires), but it is also the initials of Chris Brown (Christopher Maurice Brown) who sings the hook right after.", "annotation_id": "705707", "url": "https://genius.com/705707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
