{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "Out on these streets, when I get down on my knees", "vault_lines": ["Out on these streets, when I get down on my knees"], "meaning": "", "annotation_id": "23165981", "url": "https://genius.com/23165981", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "I’m being quiet, man, just waiting for these rappers to thank me, de nada", "vault_lines": ["I'm being quiet, man, just waiting for these rappers to thank me, de nada"], "meaning": "Wayne has inspired many rappers of the new generation, with his style of rapping, codeine drinking, styles of hair and clothing, and many more.\n\n“De nada” means “You’re welcome” in Spanish/Portuguese (brazil)", "annotation_id": "23160276", "url": "https://genius.com/23160276", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "Yeah, it been my turn, let me cut off these blinkers", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, it been my turn, let me cut off these blinkers"], "meaning": "Wayne compares his situation to that of a car trying to merge onto a highway. He keeps getting passed up by others, so he sees it as his time to cut off the fake people in his life. With newfound success, these fake supporters are left with their blinkers on, desperately trying to change lanes to get closer to Wayne and his money.", "annotation_id": "22888775", "url": "https://genius.com/22888775", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "[Intro: Choir & DJ Khaled]", "vault_lines": ["And I know that somebody been praying for me"], "meaning": "This intro samples the famous Kanye West produced Jay-Z song Heart of the City (Ain’t No Love) layering choir and horns in a very Kanye-esque way.", "annotation_id": "22888740", "url": "https://genius.com/22888740", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "(We The Best Music)", "vault_lines": ["And I know that somebody been praying for me"], "meaning": "Proclaimed before each track, this serves as DJ Khaled’s producer tag. An imprint of Epic Records, We the Best Music Group is also a record label founded by DJ Khaled in 2008.\n\nBy stating he’s released “another one,” he refers to him having produced yet another hit single.", "annotation_id": "22888297", "url": "https://genius.com/22888297", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "I never relinquish, I’m thanking Franklin as an acquaintance", "vault_lines": ["I never relinquish, I'm thanking Franklin as an acquaintance"], "meaning": "Wayne expresses his thankfulness for his wealth, in particular regularly receiving 100 dollar bills, which have the face of Founding Father Benjamin Franklin on them.\n\n\n\nIt also plays on the previous line by contrasting his acquaintane with Franklin – aka money – with the people he cut off.", "annotation_id": "22882501", "url": "https://genius.com/22882501", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "And I know that somebody been praying for me Head above ground and I could’ve been six feet deep", "vault_lines": ["And I know that somebody been praying for me"], "meaning": "In November 2020, Jeremih was diagnosed with COVID-19. He was on the ventilator and fighting for his life on November 14th, and many rappers like Chance the Rapper started praying for him.\n\nA week later, November 21st, he was off the ventilator and recovering. He left the hospital on December 4th.\n\nHe reminisces on this time in these 2 lines that he could’ve died if people didn’t pray for him.", "annotation_id": "22880920", "url": "https://genius.com/22880920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "Head above ground and I could’ve been six feet deep", "vault_lines": ["Head above ground and I could've been six feet deep"], "meaning": "Being buried six feet deep is common phrase used by many rappers. Coffins are commonly burried six feet deep, cause it helps farmers prevent from accidental plow of bodies.", "annotation_id": "22880578", "url": "https://genius.com/22880578", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "Sit down, be thankful", "vault_lines": ["Sit down, be thankful"], "meaning": "This line interprets the chorus of Kendrick Lamars HUMBLE.", "annotation_id": "22878902", "url": "https://genius.com/22878902", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "Seen white chalk make street angels", "vault_lines": ["Seen white chalk make street angels"], "meaning": "A dead body is often outlined in white chalk before it’s removed so investigators can evaluate the crime scene.  Wayne is comparing the outline of the body to the shape of a snow angel.  So in this situation it’s a “street angel”.", "annotation_id": "22878857", "url": "https://genius.com/22878857", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "THANKFUL", "line": "Nigga, that’s for the wankstas, 50 told me that, I say thank you", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, that's for the wankstas, 50 told me that, I say thank you"], "meaning": "This is a nod to 50 Cent’s November 2002 song, “Wanksta,” where on the chorus, 50 raps:\n\nYou say you a gangsta, but you never pop nothin'\nWe say you a wanksta and you need to stop frontin'", "annotation_id": "22878852", "url": "https://genius.com/22878852", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
