{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "TAlk tO Me (Remix)", "line": "Fuck it, might buy her a Bentley", "vault_lines": ["Fuck it, might buy her a Bentley"], "meaning": "A Bentley is a luxury car that can range from 165,000 dollars all the way up to over  2 million dollars. It is a subsidiary of Volkswagen AG, and is mentioned many times throughout Rich the Kid’s songs such as Plug Walk, Dead Friends, and Bring it Back .", "annotation_id": "16738512", "url": "https://genius.com/16738512", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "TAlk tO Me (Remix)", "line": "The Wraith red, Ben Frank, my friends dead (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["The Wraith red, Ben Frank, my friends dead (Yeah)"], "meaning": "A Wraith is a luxury car made by British automobile company Rolls-Royce. Benjamin Franklin was a leading author, politician, freemason, scientist, inventor, and Founding Father of the United States whose face appears on the $100 bill.\n\n\n\nRich also talks about being friends with the dead faces on his money on “Dead Friends”.", "annotation_id": "16577830", "url": "https://genius.com/16577830", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "TAlk tO Me (Remix)", "line": "Buzzing like I’m Lightyear Ain’t see me in a light-year", "vault_lines": ["Buzzing like I'm Lightyear"], "meaning": "Buzz Lightyear is a character from Pixar’s Toy Story. Tory carries the buzz with him even though you haven’t seen him in a light-year (which is actually a unit that measures distance not time).", "annotation_id": "16577748", "url": "https://genius.com/16577748", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
