{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "Extra clip, that’s my amenities", "vault_lines": ["Extra clip, that's my amenities"], "meaning": "Amenities are necessary things. An extra clip is not technically necessary, but he’s saying it is for him, implying he needs extra ammo.", "annotation_id": "37808599", "url": "https://genius.com/37808599", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "Wet your ass up with jacuzzi", "vault_lines": ["Wet your ass up with jacuzzi"], "meaning": "A Jacuzzi contains uzi, a sub-machine gun. A Jacuzzi gets you wet with water, and an uzi can make you wet from blood.", "annotation_id": "37808593", "url": "https://genius.com/37808593", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "Everything white, I got Bieber", "vault_lines": ["Everything white, I got Bieber"], "meaning": "In this context “white” refers to cocaine, for which  O.T. originally rose to popularity through his 2014 hit, “CoCo.” Here, Genasis compares the white color of the drug to the skin complexion of Justin Bieber,  continuing the practice of using the names of white celebrities as euphemisms for cocaine. A similar approach was used by NAV on Travis Scott’s 2016 track, “beibs in the trap”:\n\nWith a white bitch sniffin' on Bieber", "annotation_id": "19895253", "url": "https://genius.com/19895253", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "I’m in a DeLorean, nigga, I’m floorin’ it", "vault_lines": ["I'm in a DeLorean, nigga, I'm floorin' it"], "meaning": "The DeLorean is a car from the movie Back to the Future. If the car goes fast enough, as one would assume when you floor it, you will travel through time.", "annotation_id": "19000616", "url": "https://genius.com/19000616", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "Since Allen Iverson, I been like Eric with the snow", "vault_lines": ["Since Allen Iverson, I been like Eric with the snow"], "meaning": "Wayne is playing off the name Eric Snow in this line. Snow was a teammate of Allen Iverson’s while the duo were on the Philadelphia 76ers during the early 2000s. Weezy uses “Snow” as wordplay for cocaine in order to say he’s been selling cocaine since the days that AI was hooping with Eric.", "annotation_id": "18964615", "url": "https://genius.com/18964615", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "Free Base, bitch, I got Derek Jeter", "vault_lines": ["Free Base, bitch, I got Derek Jeter"], "meaning": "Here O.T. Genasis is talking about the freebase form of cocaine by comparing it to a base in baseball. Derek Jeter is a former professional baseball player.", "annotation_id": "18957537", "url": "https://genius.com/18957537", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "Walk around like I’m Yosemite (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Walk around like I'm Yosemite (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Here O.T. Genasis is referring to Looney Tunes' Yosemite Sam. Yosemite is always strapped with two pistols.", "annotation_id": "18957524", "url": "https://genius.com/18957524", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "Gun on Big Pun, and my clip on Notorious", "vault_lines": ["Gun on Big Pun, and my clip on Notorious"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying how he has a big gun with a big clip while referencing two bigger rappers named Big Pun as well as Notorious B.I.G..", "annotation_id": "18954959", "url": "https://genius.com/18954959", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "Bitch, I’m the man, no, the Mandalorian", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm the man, no, the Mandalorian"], "meaning": "Wayne compares himself to the Mandalorian, the protagonist in the new live-action Star Wars show of the same name released on Disney+ in late 2019.\n\nThe show has been a pop culture phenomenon, and is where the popular Baby Yoda meme originates from.", "annotation_id": "18954945", "url": "https://genius.com/18954945", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "Bezel it heavily, inspect it carefully I’m smokin’ like I’m in the Netherlands", "vault_lines": ["Bezel it heavily, inspect it carefully"], "meaning": "Although weed in the Netherlands is technically illegal, it has been decriminalized for personal use and is readily accessible in many arenas. The drug’s recreational usage is tolerated to the point where it is sold in “coffeeshops” (which are literally coffee shops combined with weed dispensaries) and pharmacies.\n\n\n\nA March 2014 article from CTV News outlines the nation’s policies regarding weed. Two notable remarks are that “the maximum amount of weed [that a person] can carry is five grams (0.2 ounces), and [that citizens] can grow no more than five cannabis plants.”", "annotation_id": "18951112", "url": "https://genius.com/18951112", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "T.O.", "line": "Every time I’m O.T., my bitch cry like T.O. (Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh)", "vault_lines": ["Every time I'm O.T., my bitch cry like T.O. (Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh)"], "meaning": "In January 2008, Terrell Owens, after losing a game in the NFL playoffs, cried during an interview while defending his teammate, Tony Romo. However, this was not a one-time occurrence, as Owens, often referred to as T.O., was known to “wear his emotions on his sleeve.”\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r43Rfh6Csjg Wayne compares Owens’ crying incidents to that of his significant other.", "annotation_id": "18951089", "url": "https://genius.com/18951089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
