{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "My girl, she get her Pam Grier on", "vault_lines": ["My girl, she get her Pam Grier on"], "meaning": "Pamela Suzette Grier (born May 26, 1949) is an American actress and singer. Described by Quentin Tarantino as cinema’s first female action star, she achieved fame for her starring roles in a string of 1970s action, blaxploitation and women in prison films for American International Pictures and New World Pictures. Her accolades include nominations for an Emmy Award, a Golden Globe Award, a Screen Actors Guild Award, a Satellite Award and a Saturn Award. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pam_Grier", "annotation_id": "30619476", "url": "https://genius.com/30619476", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "Keep a shotgun, yeah, I get my Jayson Will’ on", "vault_lines": ["Keep a shotgun, yeah, I get my Jayson Will' on"], "meaning": "Basketball star Jayson Williams shot his limo driver in 2002. https://www.mycentraljersey.com/story/news/history/2023/02/14/jayson-williams-costas-gus-christofi-limo-driver-shooting/69863809007/", "annotation_id": "30619471", "url": "https://genius.com/30619471", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "You niggas is sweeter than a box of Red Hots", "vault_lines": ["You niggas is sweeter than a box of Red Hots"], "meaning": "A powerful cinnamon kaboom in an itty-bitty bite! Red hots are a candy that comes in a box. Wayne’s haters/competitors are more sweeter (artificial) though.", "annotation_id": "30619462", "url": "https://genius.com/30619462", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "I ball and you just Erick Dampier, dog", "vault_lines": ["I ball and you just Erick Dampier, dog"], "meaning": "Erick Dampier was the Indiana Pacers' first-round pick in 1996 but turned out to have only a middling NBA career, much of it spent with the Golden State Warriors (in their pre-glory days).", "annotation_id": "14604682", "url": "https://genius.com/14604682", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "Only to talk models, yeah, I get my Seal on", "vault_lines": ["Only to talk models, yeah, I get my Seal on"], "meaning": "Soul/R&B singer Seal (AKA Henry Olusegun Adeola Samuel) was best know by the time of Da Drought 3 as the husband of German supermodel Heidi Klum, whom he married in 2005. (They divorced in 2014.)", "annotation_id": "14604582", "url": "https://genius.com/14604582", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "[Outro] I’m stuffed", "vault_lines": ["This the remix, baby, yeah"], "meaning": "Wayne often portrays his domination of potential competitors in the rap game to the imagery of the food chain; eat or be eaten. If you’re an apex predator, everything is a meal.\n\nTherefore, Wayne mentions at the end of the track that he’s “stuffed”, meaning he has satisfactorily gorged himself on the remnants of inferior artists.", "annotation_id": "7207708", "url": "https://genius.com/7207708", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "And they be lyin’ on wax like an earphone", "vault_lines": ["And they be lyin' on wax like an earphone"], "meaning": "Rappers tell lies on their songs (on wax) when they act tough or talk about their past.\nEarphone is a play on words. When other rappers are lying on their songs, you hear it through your earphones; which may or may not have ear wax on it (hopefully not).", "annotation_id": "2687535", "url": "https://genius.com/2687535", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "Just bought a Fleetwood And I’ma put some D’s on that bitch", "vault_lines": ["Just bought a Fleetwood"], "meaning": "Wayne wants to put Dayton Rims (D’s) on his Cadillac Fleetwood.\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to to Rich Boy’s Throw Some D’s which Wayne rapped over on this very mixtape.", "annotation_id": "2687523", "url": "https://genius.com/2687523", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "I’m cold, yeah, I get my Buffalo Bill on", "vault_lines": ["I'm cold, yeah, I get my Buffalo Bill on"], "meaning": "The Buffalo Bills frequently play in frigid temperatures.\n\nHe could also be saying he is as cold as the fictional serial killer Buffalo Bill from Silence of the Lambs. He wears womens skin as a suit and dances", "annotation_id": "2030050", "url": "https://genius.com/2030050", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "I’m a dog, you’re all a bunch of fleas on my dick", "vault_lines": ["I'm a dog, you're all a bunch of fleas on my dick"], "meaning": "Fleas are wingless insects usually ranging from 1.5 to 3.3 mm long, so they are very small.\n\n\n\nAnd dogs are much bigger. Especially the dog Wayne has associated himself with-a Great Dane. The current biggest Great Dane is 112 cm.\n\n\n\nSince the Great Dane (or just any dog in general) has a very big size advantage over a flea, well then a flea would not affect a dog at all-no matter what part of their body they are on.\n\nThe “fleas” in this line represent other rappers, and Wayne saying he is a dog and that fleas (other rappers) are on his dick shows his superiority. This shows his superiority in 2 ways:\n\n\nShows how other rappers are trying to be like Wayne (being on someone’s dick means to try and be like them)\nSince fleas are nothing compared to any part of a dog (that’s right, not even their penis), well then a flea being on a dog would mean the dog doesn’t even notice them. Meaning other rappers don’t get any attention from Wayne-they can’t even be compared to Wayne.\n\n\n\nThis line clearly shows Wayne’s confidence when it comes to the rap game, just as he has in other songs.", "annotation_id": "1544662", "url": "https://genius.com/1544662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "Fuck around, see a flock of red dots", "vault_lines": ["Fuck around, see a flock of red dots"], "meaning": "When using some guns, you will see a red dot while looking through the scope to make hitting your target an easier task\n\n\n\nAnd the red dots will appear on what you’re aiming at as well, which you can see in the picture above.\n\nSo if a gun with a red dot sight on the scope appears on the target, then Wayne’s enemies will have a bunch of red dots on them because of Wayne’s crew. Only if you mess with Wayne though…so don’t mess with him.", "annotation_id": "1469197", "url": "https://genius.com/1469197", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "Two girls, let ’em get they pill on Let ’em get they feel on, I get my tip drill on", "vault_lines": ["Two girls, let 'em get they pill on"], "meaning": "Wayne has two girls about to pop Ecstasy with him.\n\nEcstasy is said to make sex feel better. This is because, usually, the sense of being touched feels much better while on Ecstasy, so the sex would feel great.", "annotation_id": "1436229", "url": "https://genius.com/1436229", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "I’m dirty, I get my Bill Laimbeer on", "vault_lines": ["I'm dirty, I get my Bill Laimbeer on"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the Detroit basketball player Bill Laimbeer who was known for his aggressive, and sometimes dirty, style of play.", "annotation_id": "874678", "url": "https://genius.com/874678", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "Make that chick rock, get my Amil on", "vault_lines": ["Make that chick rock, get my Amil on"], "meaning": "A play on the word “rock”. He’s referring to Amil the female rapper who was once a part of the Roc-a-Fella family in the late 1990s.", "annotation_id": "874676", "url": "https://genius.com/874676", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "George Gervin, I’ma get my chill on", "vault_lines": ["George Gervin, I'ma get my chill on"], "meaning": "George Gervin is a retired professional basketball player who previously played for the Spurs and the Bulls. His nickname was “The Iceman” because of his cool demeanor on the basketball court.", "annotation_id": "874674", "url": "https://genius.com/874674", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "Gun is my bodyguard, call it Kevin Costner", "vault_lines": ["Gun is my bodyguard, call it Kevin Costner"], "meaning": "The Bodyguard is a film starring Whitney Houston and Kevin Costner in which he plays her bodyguard. In this case, however, Lil' Wayne’s bodyguard is a gun.", "annotation_id": "874673", "url": "https://genius.com/874673", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "You know me, I just be chillin’ in the Phantom, listenin’ to opera", "vault_lines": ["You know me, I just be chillin' in the Phantom, listenin' to opera"], "meaning": "The Phantom of the Opera is a musical done by Andrew Lloyd Weber in 1986 and still appears on playbill’s across the world.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Rolls Royce Phantom Coupé is a British, handmade luxury car.", "annotation_id": "874670", "url": "https://genius.com/874670", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "line": "Beatin’ up your block, yeah, I get my Emmett Till on", "vault_lines": ["Beatin' up your block, yeah, I get my Emmett Till on"], "meaning": "Emmett Till was an African-American boy that was murdered for flirting with a white woman in the 1950s.", "annotation_id": "240655", "url": "https://genius.com/240655", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swizzy", "status": "done", "targets": 20, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-swizzy-lyrics", "genius_title": "Swizzy", "genius_id": 28657, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Switch Up", "line": "New Ghost, new Wraith (New Ghost, new Wraith)", "vault_lines": ["New Ghost, new Wraith (New Ghost, new Wraith)"], "meaning": "The Rolls-Royce Ghost and Wraith are built on the same chassis. The Ghost is a four-door, and the Wraith is a coupe. Both have suicide doors.\n\n\n\n\n\nRolls Royce named its whole line after ethereal spirits: Ghost, Wraith, and Phantom.", "annotation_id": "8245184", "url": "https://genius.com/8245184", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Switch Up", "line": "I’ll disappear in that ’Lago Then reappear in that Ghost", "vault_lines": ["I'll disappear in that 'Lago"], "meaning": "Kelly switches up from a Lamborghini Murcielago to a Rolls-Royce Ghost.\n\n\n\n‘lago showing off its scissor doors\n\n\n\nGhost showing off its suicide doors\n\nLamborghini itself switched up from the Murcielago to the Aventador, which replaced the Mercy after 2010.\n\nRolls-Royce brought in the Ghost in 2009, as a more affordable version of the Phantom (the starting price is “only” around $300,000).", "annotation_id": "8245148", "url": "https://genius.com/8245148", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Switch Up", "line": "You know I make sure I hit her with the prenup", "vault_lines": ["You know I make sure I hit her with the prenup"], "meaning": "He quotes drake from “back to back” in this, and you can hear the similarity in his vocals when he says the line.\nhttps://genius.com/7466081", "annotation_id": "8066227", "url": "https://genius.com/8066227", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Switch Up", "line": "And then I let Uber get her home", "vault_lines": ["And then I let Uber get her home"], "meaning": "Since 2011, “Uber” has gradually increased its prevalence in lyrics. This has undoubtedly coincided with the company’s boom: it dwarfs its competitors' reach in major American cities.", "annotation_id": "8058287", "url": "https://genius.com/8058287", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
