{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "Go out there and make my bread", "vault_lines": [", go out there and make my bread"], "meaning": "Further riffing on “closed legs don’t get fed,” to “make my bread” is to earn a living and be able to feed herself.", "annotation_id": "38248207", "url": "https://genius.com/38248207", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "You move slow, you gettin’ pressure from cops You don’t know whether or not to lay low ’Cause 25 to life’s no joke To all my real guerillas thuggin’ (thuggin’) On top of corners every day strugglin’ (strugglin’) All the beautiful women’s gettin’ money (money, money)", "vault_lines": ["You move slow, you gettin' pressure from cops"], "meaning": "Sex workers approach their work strategically because the sentence for public prostitution is twenty five years to life; in this sense, sex workers are guerillas (untraditional and strategic)", "annotation_id": "38135204", "url": "https://genius.com/38135204", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "Closed legs don’t get fed", "vault_lines": ["Closed legs don't get fed"], "meaning": "A play on the saying “closed mouths don’t get fed,” meaning those who don’t advocate for their needs don’t get their needs met; she earns her living through sex work, or by “opening her legs\"", "annotation_id": "38135173", "url": "https://genius.com/38135173", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "Never thought that she would come and work for the president Mr. George Washington (where my money at?)", "vault_lines": ["He calls (where my money at?)"], "meaning": "There’s presidents on money. She works for money, so she works for the president. George Washinton is on the 1$ bill.\n\n\n\nSpecifially she became a prostitute.", "annotation_id": "17013949", "url": "https://genius.com/17013949", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "Some live for the bill, some kill for the bill (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Some live for the bill, some kill for the bill (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Some people live for the money, some people kill for it. Also a reference to The O'Jays hit single For The Love of Money, it says:\n\nSome people got to have it, some people really need it\"", "annotation_id": "8453609", "url": "https://genius.com/8453609", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "They got they mind on they money, money on they mind They got they finger on the trigger, hand on the 9", "vault_lines": ["They got they mind on they money, money on they mind"], "meaning": "This pays homage to a 2Pac line from MC Breed’s “Gotta Get Mine”.\n\n“I keep my mind on my money, money on my mind\nFinger on the trigger, nigga, hand on my nine”\n\nThis speaks to the pressures that come with gaining and maintaining money and power. If you want to rise up in the world, you have to always be aware of your surroundings and prepared for something to go wrong. This includes keeping a “9” (9mm gun) on you at all times.\n\nSnoop Dogg references this same line on “Gin and Juice”", "annotation_id": "1831202", "url": "https://genius.com/1831202", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "She whined for the bill,", "vault_lines": ["She whined for the bill,"], "meaning": "This is an intentional homophone. It can be heard as “whined” or “wind”. Winding would mean that she moved her body to dance and make money. Whined means that she begged or screwed some guys for money.", "annotation_id": "40394", "url": "https://genius.com/40394", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "And then she runs to the pastor And he tells her there will be a new chapter But she feels no different after And then she ask him: “Where my money at?”", "vault_lines": ["He calls (where my money at?)"], "meaning": "Mocking “televangelists” (like Pastor Kearny Thomas) – many of whom try to swindle their followers\n\n\n\nA pastor has requested the services of the poor woman whom both Wyclef and Wayne have been rapping about. However, she attempts to seek solace and counsel with the supposed Man of God. After sex instead of money or true guidance he gives her the same pastoral clichés i.e.\n\n“There will be a new chapter”\n\nUnlike the pastor, she then does her job and makes like Rick Ross", "annotation_id": "38153", "url": "https://genius.com/38153", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "Now she tricks on the track right by school", "vault_lines": ["Now she tricks on the track right by school"], "meaning": "Now she “tricks”, or trades her physical services with other men, in order for them to pay her bills. Notice that “trick” and “track” is an example of pararhyme.", "annotation_id": "38094", "url": "https://genius.com/38094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "She used to be the sweetest girl ever, whatever Now she like sour amaretto", "vault_lines": ["And she used to be the sweetest girl"], "meaning": "Sour Amaretto is a very bitter drink; definitely far from sweet.", "annotation_id": "38091", "url": "https://genius.com/38091", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "line": "See, I’ma tell you like Wu told me Cash Rules Everything Around Me", "vault_lines": ["See, I'ma tell you like Wu told me"], "meaning": "The hook is based on a line in “Notorious Thugs” by Biggie, which in turn referenced “C.R.E.A.M.” by the Wu-Tang Clan.\n\n“I'ma tell you like a nigga told me\nCash Rule Everything Around Me”\n\n\n\n\n\nThis song pays homage to the Wu-Tang Clan again on the remix, since it uses the “C.R.E.A.M.” instrumental and contains a verse from Wu-Tang rapper Raekwon", "annotation_id": "38081", "url": "https://genius.com/38081", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Wyclef-jean-sweetest-girl-dollar-bill-lyrics", "genius_title": "Sweetest Girl (Dollar Bill)", "genius_id": 1298, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "More head than a dread, my youte", "vault_lines": ["More head than a dread, my youte"], "meaning": "This line can mean two different things that make sense together. Nicki plays around with the “ head” and “dread” line, which refers to oral. “ My youte” is typically a caribbean way of greeting a man. Some Carribbean Men have dreads, which Nicki may know since she is Carribean gyal.", "annotation_id": "25476271", "url": "https://genius.com/25476271", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "You like balloon boy, mama, you was never there", "vault_lines": ["You like balloon boy, mama, you was never there"], "meaning": "Minaj references the infamous “Balloon Boy Hoax” of 2009. When parents of a 6 year old boy called a massive search party for their son who they claimed was trapped in a silver saucer that was flying in the air. When officials captured the saucer, the boy was never inside. The boy was hiding in the house. It turned out that the parents were lying about it to just get on television. https://g.co/kgs/mjwSgL", "annotation_id": "20917505", "url": "https://genius.com/20917505", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Get the pussy wet, Abita Springs", "vault_lines": ["get the pussy wet, Abita Springs"], "meaning": "Abita Springs is a town in Wayne’s home city of New Orleans, Louisiana. It was named this by its original Native American inhabitants for the nearby medicinal hot springs—which, of course, are wet.", "annotation_id": "20729716", "url": "https://genius.com/20729716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Kareem and the ring", "vault_lines": ["Kareem and the ring"], "meaning": "Another thing that goes together just as well as Weezy and Nicki: Kareem Abdul-Jabbar and an NBA Championship Ring.\n\nKareem was an American basketball player who won 6 NBA Championships in the span of his 20 year career. Like many other major sports leagues, the NBA gives out customized diamond ring to the players and staff of the winning franchise. 6 championships ties Kareem at 10th all time with 4 other players.", "annotation_id": "20729692", "url": "https://genius.com/20729692", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Go together like Ricky and his eye patch", "vault_lines": ["Go together like Ricky and his eye patch"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj and Lil Wayne are the perfect combination, and go together just as well as Slick Rick and his classic eye patch, which he’s never seen without. Rick’s patch is the result of an accident with glass that blinded him in his right eye when he was only 18 months old.", "annotation_id": "20729682", "url": "https://genius.com/20729682", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "That’s why I come through in a Barbie Bentley", "vault_lines": ["That's why I come through in a Barbie Bentley"], "meaning": "Connecting with the previous line, Nicki is rich and proves it by driving around in a hot pink Bentley GT", "annotation_id": "20729666", "url": "https://genius.com/20729666", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Get gas, then get at me, Texaco", "vault_lines": ["Get gas, then get at me, Texaco"], "meaning": "Texaco is a gas station company that was founded in Texas.", "annotation_id": "18456388", "url": "https://genius.com/18456388", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Cold like a white bear", "vault_lines": ["Cold like a white bear"], "meaning": "White bears are usually polar bears who live in the arctic, which is a very cold place\n\n\n\nAlso wheat beer (the drink) is known to look  white and called white beer when cold.", "annotation_id": "18456364", "url": "https://genius.com/18456364", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Bike gear, throw it up, no high chair", "vault_lines": ["Bike gear, throw it up, no high chair"], "meaning": "Nicki talks about throwing her bikes up which is like popping a wheelie.\n\n\n\nShe then compares it to a highchair which is a chair babies sit in and are known for throwing up in", "annotation_id": "18456353", "url": "https://genius.com/18456353", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Weezy and Nicki bring the A-game, high stats", "vault_lines": ["Weezy and Nicki bring the A-game, high stats"], "meaning": "To have an “A-Game” means to perform extremely well, and it could refer to anything, such as sports or music. Nicki here refers to her and Weezy having “high stats” which is Nicki bragging about all of hers and Wayne’s accomplishments, such as awards.\nLil Wayne has over 30 awards won\n\n\n\nWayne accepting Grammy Award\n\nNicki has over 20 awards won.\n\n\n\nNicki accepting award\n\n That’s a lot of awards for 2 people!. So yes, I’d say they are bringing their “A-Game”.", "annotation_id": "1483595", "url": "https://genius.com/1483595", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Weezy that nigga that you see in your dreams,", "vault_lines": ["Weezy that nigga that you see in your dreams,"], "meaning": "It seems as if Wayne may be making his own Freddie Krueger reference on this track.\n\n\n\nSince Freddie kills people in their dreams, and “Weezy is that nigga you see in your dreams”, then maybe Wayne is trying to express that he feels he kills everyone in the game and everyone in the rap game completely fears him (just as Freddie is feared)\n\nThis line could have another possible meaning, though, if people are dreaming about Wayne while they are sleeping, then they could be dreaming to be him, meaning instead of people fearing him, they envy him for everything he has (fame, money etc.) so they want want to be just like him.", "annotation_id": "1483562", "url": "https://genius.com/1483562", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "I’m so high, I need parachutes", "vault_lines": ["I'm so high, I need parachutes"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is comparing the level of his high (due to use of drugs).\n\n\n\nTo the altitude you are at when you jump out of a plane and use a parachute to come down at a slower rate.\n\n\n\nWhen you start to lose your high it is called coming down, so Wayne got so high and now is coming down from this massive high. Since Wayne is coming down from this crazy high, something to ease it would help-which parachutes do when you jump from planes.", "annotation_id": "1483524", "url": "https://genius.com/1483524", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "I’m terrible, be careful, you might want say a prayer or two", "vault_lines": ["I'm terrible, be careful, you might want say a prayer or two"], "meaning": "Weezy is giving you time to talk to God one last time, before he really does something drastic.\n\nWayne also had a similar line to this one on Trigger Finger he said\n\nBetter turn to God, ‘fore I turn to Godzilla", "annotation_id": "177312", "url": "https://genius.com/177312", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Kill bitches, leave they body in the Bayou", "vault_lines": ["Kill bitches, leave they body in the Bayou"], "meaning": "A “bayou” is an extremely slow-moving stream or river, which is typically found in flat, low-lying area. Louisiana is a place very famous for containing bayou’s, so maybe that’s her little shout-out to Wayne on this track since he’s from Louisiana. Wayne even has a map of Louisiana tatted on his back", "annotation_id": "81718", "url": "https://genius.com/81718", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "And my bank account ain’t hardly empty", "vault_lines": ["And my bank account ain't hardly empty"], "meaning": "Not hardly, considering her net worth is 22 million! Nicki’s Barbie gets so tired climbing money stacks that she apparently earned a free ride according to the following line.", "annotation_id": "66292", "url": "https://genius.com/66292", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "She be on her Barbie shit, and me? I’m on Tha Carter VI", "vault_lines": ["She be on her Barbie shit, and me? I'm on Tha Carter VI"], "meaning": "Even though only Tha Carter I, II and III had come out at the time, Weezy had it planned out all the way to VI, saying he’s already got the future on his mind and bragging about his legendary work ethic.\n\nInterestingly enough, Lil Wayne shared in an interview with Billboard that he wanted “Carter V” to be the last album of the series.", "annotation_id": "36859", "url": "https://genius.com/36859", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "You niggas gassed up, ’93 Supreme", "vault_lines": ["Anything we want we redeem, you niggas gassed up, '93 Supreme"], "meaning": "“93 Supreme” was a type of gasoline produced by Exxon. They were accused of unsubstantiated advertising claims after it was found the gas did not live up to the alleged benefits.", "annotation_id": "36851", "url": "https://genius.com/36851", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Good for the goose, then its good for the gander", "vault_lines": ["Good for the goose, then its good for the gander"], "meaning": "A pretty little double entendre:\n\n1) The idiom in the line says that what’s good for one person should be good for another – Nicki may be referring to criticism about her image and  style. More specifically this line addresses the notion of equality of the sexes (goose and gander are female and male geese).\nNicki often discusses her opinions on the disparity between men and women being allowed to express themselves sexually in the rap game.\n\n2) In the bedroom if the females getting some good action, it’s going to be good for the dude too!", "annotation_id": "36652", "url": "https://genius.com/36652", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "I ain’t Mike Jack but “This Is It”", "vault_lines": ["I ain't Mike Jack but \"This Is It\""], "meaning": "Michael Jackson’s posthumous concert film and soundtrack were titled This is It", "annotation_id": "36651", "url": "https://genius.com/36651", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Shoot yourself in the leg, Plaxico", "vault_lines": ["Shoot yourself in the leg, Plaxico"], "meaning": "Plaxico Burress, an American football player was infamously sentenced to two years in prison following an incident where he shot himself in the leg trying to stop his glock sliding down his sweatpants\n\n\n\nPlaxico was one of the best players on the New York Giants football team and was carrying an unlicensed gun in a club in New York City – there is a mandatory jail term for carrying an unlicensed gun in NYC.\n\nYoung Money affiliates are way smarter than that!", "annotation_id": "36649", "url": "https://genius.com/36649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "More brain than a IQ", "vault_lines": ["More brain than a IQ"], "meaning": "A not-so-imaginative oral sex pun.  Nicki gets more “brain” than a test of one’s Intelligence Quotient does.\n\nNicki made a very similar line on Roger That (which Wayne is also on), she said\n\nWhite girls tell me “Hey Nicki, your camp rules\nIs that why you get more head than shampoo’s?”", "annotation_id": "36644", "url": "https://genius.com/36644", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "Freddy Krueger, I’m a rap bitch nightmare", "vault_lines": ["Freddy Krueger, I'm a rap bitch nightmare"], "meaning": "Freddy Krueger is the main character in the movie series; A Nightmare On Elm Street. In the series Freddy kills people in their dreams, which results in their death in real life as well.\n\n\n\nNicki has the same affect on her competition in the rap game that Freddy had on his victims- she kills them (musically speaking, of course)", "annotation_id": "36643", "url": "https://genius.com/36643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sweet Dreams", "line": "So cold, I need theraflu,", "vault_lines": ["So cold, I need theraflu,"], "meaning": "Theraflu is a drink you have when you have a cold or flu, and to be “cold” in the rap game means to be dope/great, so Wayne is so cold (great) he needs Theraflu.", "annotation_id": "36375", "url": "https://genius.com/36375", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
