{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Kanyeezy for diversity", "vault_lines": ["No one on the corner has swagger like us"], "meaning": "Ironically, even though T.I. remarks that he’s the controversial one on this song, Kanye West would later go on to be arguably the most controversial artist in history.", "annotation_id": "30769981", "url": "https://genius.com/30769981", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Aye, you can go see Weezy for the wordplay,", "vault_lines": ["Aye, you can go see Weezy for the wordplay,"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne (Weezy) is known for his infectious flow and excellent wordplay, like in his verse above.", "annotation_id": "30545847", "url": "https://genius.com/30545847", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Ha! What the fuck you boys talkin’ ’bout? I know it’s us, ’cause we the only thing to talk about", "vault_lines": ["Ha! What the fuck you boys talkin' 'bout?"], "meaning": "In the late 2000s, Weezy, Yeezy, Jay, and T.I. were arguably the most prominent figures in hip hop. They were at times the only people talked about in major hip-hop publications.", "annotation_id": "30545827", "url": "https://genius.com/30545827", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Mami scream “¡Papí, no más!”", "vault_lines": ["Mami scream \"¡Papí, no más!\""], "meaning": "As Weezy gets down and dirty with his girl, she screams “Daddy, no more!” in Spanish because he’s pounding the punani. “¡No más!” was also famously said by boxer Roberto Duran to stop his second fight with Sugar Ray Leonard in 1980.", "annotation_id": "30545823", "url": "https://genius.com/30545823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "My swagger is Mick Jagger", "vault_lines": ["My swagger is Mick Jagger"], "meaning": "The Rolling Stones front man Mick Jagger is known for his eccentric yet fashionable outfits – which Kanye clearly takes inspiration from here.\n\n\n\nThis line is actually taken from Ghostface Killah’s The Champ.", "annotation_id": "30476213", "url": "https://genius.com/30476213", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Thanksgiving, do we even got a question?", "vault_lines": ["Thanksgiving, do we even got a question?"], "meaning": "The Pilgrims, as mentioned in the previous line, are widely credited to be the first to celebrate the Thanksgiving holiday.", "annotation_id": "30469550", "url": "https://genius.com/30469550", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "’Cause I slaved my whole life, now I’m the master", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I slaved my whole life, now I'm the master"], "meaning": "In his early days, Kanye would be no more than a slave producer to his rapper masters. Now, he’s the one able to boss producers around.", "annotation_id": "30461411", "url": "https://genius.com/30461411", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "How it feel to wake up and be the shit and the urine", "vault_lines": ["How it feel to wake up and be the shit and the urine"], "meaning": "Being “the shit” Kanye’s way of saying that he’s on top of the rap game. Nevertheless, he’s still “the piss” – regarded as a rather controversial figure with the more negative side of his character.\n\nTL;DR – He’s everything. The good, the bad and the Kanye West.", "annotation_id": "30461338", "url": "https://genius.com/30461338", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "My attitude is tattooed That mean it’s permanent", "vault_lines": ["That mean it's permanent"], "meaning": "Kanye’s character is largely defined by his… abrasive personality. To him, it’s like a tattoo – a permanent part of him and his character.", "annotation_id": "30461334", "url": "https://genius.com/30461334", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Ayo I know I got it first", "vault_lines": ["Ayo I know I got it first"], "meaning": "Ye has the first verse on the song, hence he’s “got it first”\nKanye is a leader in the rap industry with his influence, which truly shined with his 2008 album 808s and Heartbreak, which many prominent hip-hop figures have listed as a strong influence on their work. You could say he’s the first with the trends.", "annotation_id": "30461300", "url": "https://genius.com/30461300", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "I’m Christopher Columbus, y’all just the Pilgrims", "vault_lines": ["I'm Christopher Columbus, y'all just the Pilgrims"], "meaning": "Like how explorer Christopher Columbus led the European conquering of North America, Kanye is a leader in the rap industry with his influence. The mere peasants he influenced are like the Pilgrims, who later landed in the Americas, long after Columbus. They came far after Columbus. They didn’t discover anything.\n\nYe’s influence truly shined with his 2008 album 808s and Heartbreak, which many prominent hip-hop figures have listed as a strong influence on their work.\n\n\n\nAlso, when you’re on a song with the all-star lineup of heavy hitters like Wayne and Jay Z, you don’t want the first verse. Think Sheek Louch on Money, Power & Respect getting slaughtered by DMX or Diddy being bodied by Big on All About the Benjamins.\n\nKanye, who himself produced the song, is acknowledging he’s taking the first verse and does so like only Kanye West can.\n\nHe’s the Christopher Columbus of the track, the originator and the greatest. Y'all just the Pilgrims.", "annotation_id": "30461269", "url": "https://genius.com/30461269", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "You can pay for school, but you can’t buy class", "vault_lines": ["You can pay for school, but you can't buy class"], "meaning": "Kanye would later interpolate this line on his 2016 song 30 hours from The Life of Pablo.", "annotation_id": "30457339", "url": "https://genius.com/30457339", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "And my jewels blue and yellow The type of shit that make ’em call you Carmelo", "vault_lines": ["And my jewels blue and yellow"], "meaning": "When this song was released in 2008, Carmelo Anthony was the star player for the NBA’s Denver Nuggets, whose colors are the same blue and yellow that match Weezy’s diamonds.\n\n\n\nProbably coincidental but Allen Iverson was also on the Denver Nuggets at this time and he released the song “40 Bars” in 2000 under the name Jewelz.", "annotation_id": "24553603", "url": "https://genius.com/24553603", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Run up in your shit, just me, no mask", "vault_lines": ["Run up in your shit, just me, no mask"], "meaning": "Weezy is comparing running up in a woman in terms of sexual intercourse to running up in someone’s property solo to take their stuff and he lets them both know who did the damage by showing his face.", "annotation_id": "20912574", "url": "https://genius.com/20912574", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "No one on the corner has swagger like moi", "vault_lines": ["No one on the corner has swagger like moi"], "meaning": "“Moi” is french for me", "annotation_id": "19057694", "url": "https://genius.com/19057694", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Tryna get that Kobe number, one over Jordan", "vault_lines": ["Tryna get that Kobe number, one over Jordan"], "meaning": "There’s the literal meaning of Kobe’s jersey number (24) being one number higher than Jordan’s (23), but it’s also a reference to Kobe’s will to be the best basketball player of all time and to do that he needs one more championship than Jordan.", "annotation_id": "19057692", "url": "https://genius.com/19057692", "state": "pending", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Did you even have any doubt? After Doubt it was over", "vault_lines": ["Did you even have any doubt? After Doubt it was over"], "meaning": "People who used to doubt Hov when he was coming up after he dropped Reasonable Doubt (which is considered by many to be a CLASSIC) the doubt was over.\n\n“I went to every single record label, and they was like, ‘This guy is terrible. He’s nothing,’ ” Jay told MTV News prior to the release of The Blueprint in 2001. “I had to put [Reasonable Doubt] out myself, because nobody would sign me.”", "annotation_id": "18980710", "url": "https://genius.com/18980710", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "School of hard knocks, I’m a grad And that all-blue Yankee is my graduation cap", "vault_lines": ["School of hard knocks, I'm a grad"], "meaning": "The “School of Hard Knocks” is a classic idiom coined by Elbert Hubbard in 1902. It is used when one believes their [often difficult] life experiences are a form of education that cannot be taught formally.\n\nGraduated from the corner\nY'all can play me for a motherfuckin fool if you wanna\nStreet-smart and I’m book smart\n\nHov believes growing up in the Marcy Projects was his strongest form of schooling, where all of the classes happened to be held in the street.\n\nUpon graduation from the “School of Hard Knocks” Hov was capped with a Yankee fitted, a piece of sports merchandise that he claims to have made more famous than a Yankee player can.", "annotation_id": "10877985", "url": "https://genius.com/10877985", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Can’t wear skinny jeans, ’cause my knots don’t fit No one on the corner got a pocket like this So I rock Roc jeans, ’cause my knots so thick", "vault_lines": ["No one on the corner has swagger like us"], "meaning": "With his lexical ambiguity Jay pronounces “knots” in a way that also sounds like “nuts” – slang for male genitalia. Therefore, Hov doesn’t wear skinny jeans because:\n\n\nHis rubberbanded “knots,” which is slang for wads of cash, are far too thick to fit into the small pockets of a pair of skinny jeans.\nHis testicles are quite large too, so they won’t fit into the crotch area of a pair of skinny jeans.\n\n\n\nInstead, Hov wears a pair of his own Rocawear jeans, a company he had recently sold the rights of to the Iconix Brand Group for a $204 million knot. He retained his stake of Rocawear in the deal, and continues to oversee the brand’s marketing, licensing, and product development from the Roc Nation headquarters in New York.", "annotation_id": "10877979", "url": "https://genius.com/10877979", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "It’s Hooooovaaaa", "vault_lines": ["No one on the corner has swagger like us"], "meaning": "Hova is one of Jay’s nicknames, derived from JeHOVAh, meaning he’s the “God MC” of the rap game.\n\nJay’s use of the elongated enunciation is a callback to Kanye’s “naaaaaaaaa-na…” in the previous verse.\n\nHe could also be enunciating it this way to mean that this verse, my friends, is soon over.", "annotation_id": "1699938", "url": "https://genius.com/1699938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "[Verse 2: JAY-Z]", "vault_lines": ["No one on the corner has swagger like us"], "meaning": "This song is on T.I.’s 2008 album, Paper Trail. However, this song was supposed to be on Jay-Z’s 2009 album The Blueprint 3. Hova made a strict rule that songs with autotune will not be added on that album, which is what Kanye and Wayne used on this song (see D.O.A: Death of Autotune)", "annotation_id": "55615", "url": "https://genius.com/55615", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "And me for controversy", "vault_lines": [", and me for controversy"], "meaning": "TI’s career has been full of controversy and jail time. In 2007 at the Sunset Tower Hotel in West Hollywood, California he punched and choked  Ludacris' manager Chaka Zulu.  He also caused the 2008 Dirty Awards to be shut down when his and Shawty Lo’s entourages got in a fight during the ceremony forcing the police to use pepper-spray and evacuate the audience\n\nHe’s also had several significant legal issues including an arrest for assaulting a female officer in 2003, an arrest in 2006 for an outstanding probation violation warrant from Florida, and was convicted in 2009 of federal weapons charges which resulted in a 1 year and 1 day prison sentence.\n\nThat being said, all four rappers on this song, (except maybe Jay) seem to be very good at attracting controversy.", "annotation_id": "10532", "url": "https://genius.com/10532", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Whippin’ with the soda", "vault_lines": ["whippin' with the soda"], "meaning": "Hov is “whipping” cocaine, a method in which you add ice to a boiled cocaine and baking soda mixture and vigorously whip it to cool it quickly, so it coagulates into crack cocaine.\n\n\n\nJay has repeatedly referred to making rap music as “cooking crack.”", "annotation_id": "9999", "url": "https://genius.com/9999", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Hermès, Pastelle, I pass the dressin’", "vault_lines": ["Hermès, Pastelle, I pass the dressin'"], "meaning": "Here “dressin(g)” has a double meaning: The food turkey dressing that is traditionally served at Thanksgiving, and dressing as in clothes, since Hermes is a fashion company.\n\n\n\nPastelle was also a clothing brand that Kanye was starting, some of his clothing was worn by him at fashion shows and such, and even Rihanna wore a piece by him. A logo and website were started for it, but the line never went through for whatever reason.", "annotation_id": "9993", "url": "https://genius.com/9993", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Mr. West is in the buildin’ Swagger on a hundred thousand trillion", "vault_lines": ["Mr. West is in the buildin'"], "meaning": "(100,000,000,000,000)(1000) = One hundred thousand trillion, right?\n\nOne hundred thousand trillion = 1e+17 = 100,000,000,000,000,000 = 100 quadrillion, which is also the estimated US National Debt in ~88 years, assuming a $16.8T (principal) and that the annual rate of debt growth under Obama (10.4%) holds constant.\nYears = {log(total) -log(Principal)} ÷ log(1 + rate)", "annotation_id": "8750", "url": "https://genius.com/8750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Dippin’ different Rovers,", "vault_lines": ["No one on the corner has swagger like us"], "meaning": "Hova has been driving Rovers a long time. On 1997’s “Imaginary Player”, he berates someone for not knowing the difference between a Range Rover 4.0 and a 4.6", "annotation_id": "7608", "url": "https://genius.com/7608", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Jeezy for the bird play", "vault_lines": ["Jeezy for the bird play"], "meaning": "T.I. commented on this line saying:\n\nI’m definitely talking about Young (Jeezy), “Bird Play” could be a reference to ones [waves hands randomly] assumed distribution of some illegal substance, maybe? [T.I. shrugs intensely]\n\nhttps://youtu.be/rg8UT7IZTpU?t=43s", "annotation_id": "7359", "url": "https://genius.com/7359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "No one on the corner has swagger like us Swagger like us, swagger-swagger like us No one on the corner has swagger like us Swagger like us, swagger-swagger like us No one on the corner has swagger like us Swagger like us, swagger-swagger like us No one on the corner has swagger like us Swagger like us, swagger-swagger like us", "vault_lines": ["No one on the corner has swagger like us"], "meaning": "This is a sample of one minor line from M.I.A.’s huge hit “Paper Planes,” yet it perfectly encapsulates everything that these rappers and this song are all about.", "annotation_id": "6766", "url": "https://genius.com/6766", "state": "accepted", "votes": 94, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "status": "done", "targets": 30, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Jay-z-and-ti-swagga-like-us-lyrics", "genius_title": "Swagga Like Us", "genius_id": 182, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Now, get off my dick, I ain’t fuckin’ with you", "vault_lines": ["Now, get off my dick, I ain't fuckin' with you"], "meaning": "to be ‘on someone’s dick’ is to nag them or to forever be on their case. Wayne firstly tells the listener to stop that  and then tells he isn’t ‘fucking with them’, which could mean he isn’t feeling them or doesn’t like them, or could be taken literally as Wayne literally not wanting to engage in intercourse.", "annotation_id": "35860648", "url": "https://genius.com/35860648", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "I swear, I be the sickest nigga, you can ask the nurse", "vault_lines": ["I swear, I be the sickest nigga, you can ask the nurse"], "meaning": "‘Sick’ or ‘ill’ in hiphop slang means cool or tough. Wayne makes a double entendre with the term here:\n\n\nhe’s sick as in tough and even the guys at the clinic know.\nhe’s literally sick and you can ask the nurse at the hospital.", "annotation_id": "35860617", "url": "https://genius.com/35860617", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Mack, hold your head", "vault_lines": [", and Mack, hold your head"], "meaning": "A reference to Mack Maine, who is a lifelong friend and colleague of Lil Wayne and is the president of Young Money Entertainment.", "annotation_id": "30175714", "url": "https://genius.com/30175714", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Lost some real niggas I knew from a long time ago But Heaven or Hell, I’m hoping that they be where I’ma go", "vault_lines": ["Lost some real niggas I knew from a long time ago"], "meaning": "Wayne is stating that throughout his life, he has had  some people who were close to him pass away\n\nHe wishes that when he leaves this earth, regardless of where he ends up, either in Heaven or in Hell, the thing he wants most is to be reunited with those friends who are no longer on earth.", "annotation_id": "29140276", "url": "https://genius.com/29140276", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Watch me shoot to the bank, I’m a money pistol", "vault_lines": ["Watch me shoot to the bank, I'm a money pistol"], "meaning": "Wayne uses a similie to express how he quickly travels to the bank to deposit money.\n\nHe uses the slang shoot meaning to quickly travel.\n\nAnd the similie “Like a money pistol” provides a comparison of his actions to that of a Pistol, which rather than bullets, rapidly launches currency..", "annotation_id": "29140213", "url": "https://genius.com/29140213", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "You think we gon’ do our thing? Well, ain’t it sunny in the summer?", "vault_lines": ["You think we gon' do our thing? Well, ain't it sunny in the summer?"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is using a writing technique known as:\n\nAn asemphatic yes by way of an idiomatic, rhetorical question\"\n\nWhen he states:\n\nYou think we gon' do our thing?\n\nIt is comparable to asking “Is it sunny in the summer”\n\nHe is saying that it is obviously a fact, known to be true.\n\nA similar example is “Does a bear shit in the woods?\n\nAn obvious yes.", "annotation_id": "29140066", "url": "https://genius.com/29140066", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "I’m the shit, piss, nigga", "vault_lines": ["What's the matter? Check your bladder, I'm the shit, piss, nigga"], "meaning": "Another fecal joke from weezy", "annotation_id": "27548214", "url": "https://genius.com/27548214", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "The world is in my hands, and I keep my hands closed", "vault_lines": ["The world is in my hands, and I keep my hands closed"], "meaning": "The world is Tunechi’s oyster and he is unwilling to share. This line also implies that Wayne walks with both fists balled 24/7. He is ready to throw hands at a moment’s notice… possibly over ownership of the planet.", "annotation_id": "24165278", "url": "https://genius.com/24165278", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Bullet in you boys’ memory, now you act like you don’t know", "vault_lines": ["Bullet in you boys' memory, now you act like you don't know"], "meaning": "Being a witness to something in the hood isn’t always a good a thing. The witness always knows that they can also fall victim to the perpetrator if they say anything, so they act like they don’t know.", "annotation_id": "22565616", "url": "https://genius.com/22565616", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Behind that cash, get murked", "vault_lines": ["I'm on your ass, like dirt; behind that cash, get murked"], "meaning": "This is an analogy of “not getting your hands dirty”. Lil Wayne is rich enough to have you murked by his paid goons.", "annotation_id": "22565589", "url": "https://genius.com/22565589", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "I just tell my pilot to land it in my backyard", "vault_lines": ["I just tell my pilot to land it in my backyard"], "meaning": "His yard is so big, he can land his helicopter in his back yard.", "annotation_id": "20823162", "url": "https://genius.com/20823162", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "And even at the White House, we pull up at the back doors", "vault_lines": ["And even at the White House, we pull up at the back doors"], "meaning": "When you are famous, you need to avoid the crowds, so you enter through the back doors.", "annotation_id": "20823150", "url": "https://genius.com/20823150", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Stunt hard on these bitches, I ain’t promised tomorrow", "vault_lines": ["Stunt hard on these bitches, I ain't promised tomorrow"], "meaning": "Showing off his wealth to impress the ladies.", "annotation_id": "20823146", "url": "https://genius.com/20823146", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Ol’ dickless nigga", "vault_lines": ["A remix of the F.L.Y. “Swag Surfin” original."], "meaning": "Someone who is too afraid to step up.", "annotation_id": "20823143", "url": "https://genius.com/20823143", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "And we comin’ for the commas", "vault_lines": ["And we comin' for the commas"], "meaning": "That is, for money in large enough amounts to need commas to express the total (presumably millions, not thousands).", "annotation_id": "14512581", "url": "https://genius.com/14512581", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
