{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Take the brain off the whip, now it don’t make no sense", "vault_lines": ["Take the brain off the whip, now it don't make no sense"], "meaning": "He lets the top down on his convertible car.", "annotation_id": "13640162", "url": "https://genius.com/13640162", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Quarterback, shotgun, you don’t get any sack yards", "vault_lines": ["Quarterback, shotgun, you don’t get any sack yards"], "meaning": "Double entendre\n\n1.) The formation in a which a quarterback is further away from defensive pressure, effectively ruining a chance for a sack.\n\n2.) He’s telling you that if your try to run off on him with a quarter, he’ll use his shotgun to retrieve it. Oh, and you won’t get to buy estate with the money.", "annotation_id": "13483690", "url": "https://genius.com/13483690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Katrina wiped the city out but couldn’t fuck with Hollygrove", "vault_lines": ["Katrina wiped the city out but couldn't fuck with Hollygrove"], "meaning": "“The city” Wayne’s referring to is New Orleans, Louisiana. The center of Hurricane Katrina passed southeast of New Orleans on August 29, 2005, leaving behind $70 billion (2005 USD) in damages.\n\nHollygrove is a neighborhood in New Orleans, Louisiana, located in the city’s 17th Ward.", "annotation_id": "13194272", "url": "https://genius.com/13194272", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "[Verse]", "vault_lines": ["I smash this verse, and I swag and surf"], "meaning": "This song has no verses or hooks, just Lil Wayne spitting over this insanely hot beat with no breaks or assistance, as he alone takes the place of 4 other rappers.\n\nNotice how towards the beginning, Lil Wayne cleverly matches his flow to match the flow of the chorus from the original track.\n\nOriginal: (I’m swaggin, I’m surfin, I’m swaggin, I’m surfin)\nLil Wayne: (I’m bad, I’m worse, I’ll pass, the purp…I spazz, I curse)\n\nThe last bars of this song uses it, and even makes a direct allusion to the original.", "annotation_id": "2837659", "url": "https://genius.com/2837659", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "And if it costs to be the boss, oh well, I guess I gotta pay", "vault_lines": ["And if it costs to be the boss, oh well, I guess I gotta pay"], "meaning": "It takes a toll on someone if they want to be in charge because there’s so much stress, and Wayne’s saying that he accepts that.\n\nAlso a reference to the BB King track “Paying The Cost To Be The Boss”", "annotation_id": "294700", "url": "https://genius.com/294700", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Man, I’m too much for these niggas and three much for these hoes", "vault_lines": ["Man, I'm too much for these niggas and three much for these hoes"], "meaning": "This theme was later interpolated by Kendrick Lamar on his September 2010 single, “Michael Jordan,” where Kendrick gives Lil Wayne props for the idea:\n\nI’m two much for these niggas, I’m three much for these hoes\nWayne told me that and that’s just how it goes", "annotation_id": "114071", "url": "https://genius.com/114071", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "I smash this verse, and I swag and surf", "vault_lines": ["I smash this verse, and I swag and surf"], "meaning": "To “Swag Surf” is to surf (like on the Internet) trying to find “swagger” (style/confidence) to imitate\n\nIt was originally the name of a song by the Fast Life Youngstas that Lil Wayne is freestyling to", "annotation_id": "75348", "url": "https://genius.com/75348", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "I said, T.I., hold your head", "vault_lines": ["I said, T.I., hold your head"], "meaning": "A line that will seemingly forever be relevant, as T.I. is always in and out of jail", "annotation_id": "64287", "url": "https://genius.com/64287", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "No Ceilings", "vault_lines": ["A remix of the F.L.Y. “Swag Surfin” original."], "meaning": "Lil Wayne’s No Ceilings mixtape\n\n\n\nWayne is not only shouting out the mixtape name itself, with Swag Surfin' being the first song on the mixtape, he is once again reminding listeners just what they’re listening to, a common theme throughout, exemplified in the title track: No Ceilings.", "annotation_id": "47912", "url": "https://genius.com/47912", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "And if you throw it in a bag I bet I’ll snatch her purse", "vault_lines": ["And if you throw it in a bag I bet I'll snatch her purse"], "meaning": "The title of Fabolous' song about buying his bossy girlfriend whatever her little heart desires\n\nSimilarly, Lil Wayne would do anything for his purp – even snatch it a purse (umm.. Wayne.. I don’t think purple drank cares about material possessions the way us silly humans do!)\n\nThe Fabolous song is also remixed on the No Ceilings mixtape", "annotation_id": "18519", "url": "https://genius.com/18519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "And I live on an island, Atlantic in my backyard", "vault_lines": ["And I live on an island, Atlantic in my backyard"], "meaning": "A pun demonstrating Weezy’s dominance of the music industry. He is the master of his domain, which included an “island” (i.e. Island Records) and the “Atlantic” (i.e. Atlantic Records)\n\nAnd he lives on South Beach,which is an island in the Atlantic.", "annotation_id": "17509", "url": "https://genius.com/17509", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Eastside who I do it for, Eagle Street, right by the store", "vault_lines": ["Eastside who I do it for, Eagle Street, right by the store"], "meaning": "Wayne grew up on the corner of Eagle Street and Apple Street\n\nApparently there is in fact a cornerstore there (“Kim’s Supermarket”) but I’m not able to pull it up on Google Streetview..\n\nACCEPTED COMMENT: View Larger Map", "annotation_id": "14123", "url": "https://genius.com/14123", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Pretty Boy Floyd, step up, I will crack yours", "vault_lines": ["Pretty Boy Floyd, step up, I will crack yours"], "meaning": "“Pretty Boy” Floyd Mayweather Jr. was one of the most dominant boxers in the history of the sport, and one of the most lucrative sportsmen too.\n\nThe other “Pretty Boy” Floyd was an infamous 1930s bank robber.\n\nLike either Pretty Boy, Wayne says he will turn violent and crack your skull (and/or your safe) if he deems it necessary.", "annotation_id": "13384", "url": "https://genius.com/13384", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Man, I just be chillin’, I’m cool like Lou Rawls", "vault_lines": ["Man, I just be chillin', I'm cool like Lou Rawls"], "meaning": "Lou Rawls was a very chillaxed blues and jazz musician of yore. The simile connects chilling to being cool like Lou Rawls.", "annotation_id": "13381", "url": "https://genius.com/13381", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Weezy beat the beat up like Sonny Liston", "vault_lines": ["Weezy beat the beat up like Sonny Liston"], "meaning": "Charles L. “Sonny” Liston was a professional boxer who became world heavyweight champion in 1962 by knocking out Floyd Patterson in the first round. Liston was one of the most powerful punchers and jabbers in the history of boxing\n\nWeezy “beats up” the beat in the background (get it?) with his powerful jabby WORDS", "annotation_id": "13380", "url": "https://genius.com/13380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "In the Porsche 911, like emergency calls", "vault_lines": ["In the Porsche 911, like emergency calls"], "meaning": "Porsche 9-1-1 (like “Dial 911”)\n\n\n\nIronically named, the Porsche 911, in it’s early days especially, was well known as the “Grim Reaper” of cars. It’s heavy rear end, due to the posterior set engine, making round-a-bouts and U turns quite the challenge, was the culprit for many a road accident.\n\nOh sheeeeit, call 9-1-1 I hear a Porsche coming!", "annotation_id": "13317", "url": "https://genius.com/13317", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Still “long hair, don’t care” like a Navajo", "vault_lines": ["Still \"long hair, don't care\" like a Navajo"], "meaning": "Weezy is quite proud of his long hair (just like the Navajo Indians of the American southwest)\n\nOn “Don’t Get It,” he points out his hair’s resemblance to Jesus' hair:\n\nHe had hair like wool, He had hair like Wayne", "annotation_id": "13307", "url": "https://genius.com/13307", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Don’t fuck with me ’cause right now, I’m higher than Captain Kirk", "vault_lines": ["Don't fuck with me 'cause right now, I'm higher than Captain Kirk"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has smoked so much marijuana and has got so high that he feels like he’s in space, like Captain Kirk from television’s Star Trek:", "annotation_id": "13304", "url": "https://genius.com/13304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Shoot the witness, nigga Hold court in the streets and convict this nigga", "vault_lines": ["Shoot the witness, nigga"], "meaning": "If Lil Wayne were to commit a crime, he would be judge, jury and executioner to any eye witnesses\n\nNote Weezy’s tactical nous in terms of legal defense in knowing that an eye-witness is more likely to meet the requisite evidentiary standard for criminal prosecution", "annotation_id": "13290", "url": "https://genius.com/13290", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Nigga, take your Mrs. Officer and set some new laws", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, take your Mrs. Officer and set some new laws"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne advises his listeners to treat police officers like women: speak truth to power! As Weezy does in his guised revolutionary tract: “Mrs Officer”", "annotation_id": "13287", "url": "https://genius.com/13287", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Fuq’ roll them killer plants, the Little Shop of Horror", "vault_lines": ["Fuq' roll them killer plants, the Little Shop of Horror"], "meaning": "Flute seems to be Weezy’s designated blunt-roller (Lil Cease served this role for Notorious BIG); he rolls “killer plants” (marijuana) as if the crew is a musical rendition of the Little Shop of Horrors, a 1980s movie featuring a man-eating houseplant", "annotation_id": "13283", "url": "https://genius.com/13283", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Walk around like I’m 30 feet tall Tiger Woods, all these hoes tryna birdie these balls", "vault_lines": ["Walk around like I'm 30 feet tall"], "meaning": "Wayne treats women like objects – just like famed “blasian” golfer Tiger Woods – and tries to get the “birds” (girls) to massage his testicles (notice the golf pun; a “birdy” is a golf score one under par on a hole)\n\nThis song came out 3 months before Tigergate…Weezy is psychic\n\n“Birdy” also sounds a lot like “bury” – which enhances the sex pun", "annotation_id": "13281", "url": "https://genius.com/13281", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Man, I’m running with the blocka", "vault_lines": ["Man, I'm running with the blocka"], "meaning": "“The Blocka” is a nickname for The Bloods, who are Wayne’s gang\n\nWayne will be grateful for his Blucka runnings during his prison sentence, a time during which I suspect the Bloods will protect Weezy’s (otherwise-vulnerable) asshole", "annotation_id": "13280", "url": "https://genius.com/13280", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "And we roll them bitches thick, make ’em look like Toccara", "vault_lines": ["And we roll them bitches thick, make 'em look like Toccara"], "meaning": "The blunts (marijuana cigars) that Wayne rolls are fat, just like Toccara Jones, the Rubenesque black contestant on America’s Next Top Model", "annotation_id": "13279", "url": "https://genius.com/13279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Bitch, I ball hard, breakin’ all the backboards", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I ball hard, breakin' all the backboards"], "meaning": "To “ball” means to live extravagantly, but the adjective originates from a description of prowess in basketball\n\nAggressive basketball players (“ballers”) occasionally break the backboard when they slam dunk, while Lil Wayne “breaks backs” (roughly makes love to girls)", "annotation_id": "13278", "url": "https://genius.com/13278", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "And to my Bloods, code red", "vault_lines": ["And to my Bloods, code red"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is a member of the Bloods gang; his set is named “Code Red”, part of the elite Blood faction known as Vicelords", "annotation_id": "13277", "url": "https://genius.com/13277", "state": "accepted", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Gotta take care of them kids, man, I know you heard Obama", "vault_lines": ["Gotta take care of them kids, man, I know you heard Obama"], "meaning": "Obama mentioned Weezy in a speech, stating that kids in the ghetto have to realize they can’t all grow up to be “the next Lil Wayne or the next Lebron”.", "annotation_id": "13275", "url": "https://genius.com/13275", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "I got this chrome on this Bugatti, I’m strong in this Bugatti Two V8s, ain’t no such thing as driving calm in this Bugatti", "vault_lines": ["I got this chrome on this Bugatti, I'm strong in this Bugatti"], "meaning": "Picture Wayne, sitting a tall 5'6 in his Bugatti Veyron – chrome rims,  W16 quad-turbo engine, guzzling gas (I’m guessing the car has, errm, no ceiling).", "annotation_id": "13273", "url": "https://genius.com/13273", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "I’ll pass the purp", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I’m bad, I'm worse, I'll pass the purp"], "meaning": "Wayne offers to share his “purp” (purple marijuana) because he’s already smoked his fair share\n\nSome might think that “purp” is short for purple drank – a concoction of Codeine-based medications, alcohol and soda. But no…Wayne quit that stuff!", "annotation_id": "13272", "url": "https://genius.com/13272", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "I leave the pussy micro-soft like Windows Vista", "vault_lines": ["I leave the pussy micro-soft like Windows Vista"], "meaning": "Wayne’s penis is like fine-grained sandpaper, leaving his partner’s pussy silky smooth.\n\n\n\nMicrosoft is a technology company that created and sells Windows Vista, which was the latest version of the Windows operating system available when Weezy dropped this hot freestyle.", "annotation_id": "13271", "url": "https://genius.com/13271", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Redbone do me good, then her friend assist her", "vault_lines": ["Redbone do me good, then her friend assist her"], "meaning": "A “redbone” refers to a light-skinned black girl with ruddy hair and a freckled complexion (they are generally considered to be sexy)\n\nThis is wordplay because it can be interpreted as her friend assist her, or then her friend or sister, or I friend her sister. Weezy also uses the multiple interpretations to his advantage by using the same line twice since it can be interpreted differently from the first.", "annotation_id": "13270", "url": "https://genius.com/13270", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Swag Surf", "line": "Now, women kicking it with me like Nomar Garciaparra", "vault_lines": ["Now, women kicking it with me like Nomar Garciaparra"], "meaning": "Baseball player Nomar Garciaparra is married to soccer player Mia Hamm\n\nNowadays, when girls “kick it” (hang out) with Lil Wayne, they want to “kick it” the way that Mia Hamm – a soccer player (kick!) – “kicks it” with Nomar, i.e. they want to get married", "annotation_id": "13269", "url": "https://genius.com/13269", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
