{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sunshine", "line": "These niggas Stevie (What?) to the come up", "vault_lines": ["These niggas Stevie (What?) to the come up"], "meaning": "She is saying that they like Stevie (Wonder) to the come up bc they are blind to it (just like Stevie Wonder is a blind man & cannot see). This fits bc in the next line she makes a reference to wonder bread. Even though that is an actual brand of bread, it could also be seen as a clever play on Stevie’s last name.", "annotation_id": "28249995", "url": "https://genius.com/28249995", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sunshine", "line": "Went got my bread up, let ’em wonder", "vault_lines": ["Went got my bread up, let 'em wonder"], "meaning": "this bar is a play on words with the bread company “Wonder Bread”", "annotation_id": "25770152", "url": "https://genius.com/25770152", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sunshine", "line": "This Siggy get jiggy with niggas Don’t make me Will Smith me a nigga", "vault_lines": ["This Siggy get jiggy with niggas"], "meaning": "While more known for his Oscar winning acting, Will Smith also had a successful rap career in the 1990’s, with“Gettin’ Jiggy wit It” being his biggest hit.\n\nIn many of his iconic roles, Smith played no-nonsense tough guys. Wayne will approach his adversaries with the same attitude, using his “Siggy” (short for SIG Sauer – a fire-arms manufacturer) to make others dance/get jiggy.\n\nWayne appears to have also ‘predicated’ a case of life imitating art in these lyrics. At the 94th academy awards Will Smith walked on stage and slapped comedian Chris Rock for making a joke about his wife – Jada Pinkett-Smith – before returning to his seat and yelling:\n\nKeep my wife’s name out of your fucking mouth!", "annotation_id": "25454260", "url": "https://genius.com/25454260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sunshine", "line": "Smoke big tree, lil’ nigga, we too large to igg me, lil’ nigga", "vault_lines": ["Smoke big tree, lil' nigga, we too large to igg me, lil' nigga"], "meaning": "Slang for Tree is marijuana. If you know Wayne then you know he loves weed.\n“The smoke big three” is maybe a reference to happy 4/20 (episode 8 Weezy Wednesday). Where Wayne has a big blunt.\n\n\n\nTo Igg someone is to ignore someone. But Wayne is to large to Ignore him.", "annotation_id": "25432864", "url": "https://genius.com/25432864", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sunshine", "line": "They ain’t finna shoot, I’ma swish ’em", "vault_lines": ["They ain't finna shoot, I'ma swish 'em"], "meaning": "A basketball “shot” is  throwing the basketball toward the hoop. A “swish”is a shot that goes through the net without touching the rim of the basket.\nWayne plays with words “shoot” and “swish”.", "annotation_id": "25432831", "url": "https://genius.com/25432831", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sunshine", "line": "Sunshine on me, Devin Booker", "vault_lines": ["Sunshine on me, Devin Booker"], "meaning": "Devin Booker is an American professional basketball player. He plays for the Phoenix “Suns”.Wayne references Devin as sunshine because he plays for the “Suns”.", "annotation_id": "25432012", "url": "https://genius.com/25432012", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sunshine", "line": "The god of the sun and the light like Apollo Tunechi", "vault_lines": ["The god of the sun and the light like Apollo"], "meaning": "Apollo is the Olympian god of the sun and light, music and poetry, healing and plagues, prophecy and knowledge, order and beauty, archery and agriculture.", "annotation_id": "25432004", "url": "https://genius.com/25432004", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sunshine", "line": "I’m sweeter at rapping, like what the fuck happened? Came back and he’s snappin’, came back with a passion", "vault_lines": ["I'm sweeter at rapping, like what the fuck happened?"], "meaning": "Childish Gambino hasn’t had very many guest appearances in the past few years. His last rapping feature was in 2018, four years prior to this song on Monster by 21 Savage. He’s only had two features in those 4 years and neither were rap features.", "annotation_id": "25431951", "url": "https://genius.com/25431951", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sunshine", "line": "I’m hotter than Nelly, they say that I’m smelly Ain’t never smelled wealthy, I think", "vault_lines": ["I'm hotter than Nelly, they say that I'm smelly"], "meaning": "Donald Glover is often described as smelly. This is because of a few interviews he had around 2014 with Breakfast Club and it’s members, and admitted to not showering much and not wearing deodorant due to “being on some hippy shit.” https://youtu.be/9c5jjEcC-kA?t=150", "annotation_id": "25431937", "url": "https://genius.com/25431937", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
