{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stupid Wild", "line": "Young Money", "vault_lines": ["Weezy man, Young Money"], "meaning": "Shouts out to the label which Weezy is signed to!", "annotation_id": "3345517", "url": "https://genius.com/3345517", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stupid Wild", "line": "And every fuckin’ time I say soo woo it’s for the Bloods", "vault_lines": ["And every fuckin' time I say soo woo it's for the Bloods"], "meaning": "“Soo Woo” is a term Bloods use to greet each other.\n\nEver since Tha Carter III, Wayne has been repping the bloods on numerous songs as well as wearing their signature color red in public.", "annotation_id": "2597898", "url": "https://genius.com/2597898", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stupid Wild", "line": "And if she on my team I bet that bitch know who she playin’ for Mr. Coach Carter", "vault_lines": ["And if she on my team I bet that bitch know who she playin' for"], "meaning": "In the movie Coach Carter, Samuel L. Jackson plays the title character, who is a demanding coach who leads an inner city basketball team to success\n\n\n\nJust like in the movie, it’s no question who is in charge in Wayne’s relationship. Also, Weezy’s real name is Dwyane Carter, so he’s actually Coach Carter too", "annotation_id": "83465", "url": "https://genius.com/83465", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stupid Wild", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Gucci-mane-stupid-wild-lyrics", "genius_title": "Stupid Wild", "genius_id": 407, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stun’n (Remix)", "line": "The Hot Boy$ new album, Guerilla Warfare and it jumped of strong", "vault_lines": ["The Hot Boy$ new album, Guerilla Warfare and it jumped of strong"], "meaning": "Guerrilla Warfare is the second studio album by the New Orleans hip-hop group Hot Boys, released July 27, 1999 on Cash Money Records. The Hot Boys highly anticipated sophomore effort, Guerrilla Warfare, issued after Cash Money’s distribution deal with Universal Records, was an instant hit. It debuted at #5 on the Billboard 200 and #1 on the Top R&B/Hip Hop Albums selling 142,000 copies in its first week,[6] and remains their most successful album as a group and with Cash Money Records.\n\nProduced by Mannie Fresh, Guerrilla Warfare contains the lead single, “We On Fire”, which was placed at #49 on the Billboard’s Hot R&B/Hip-Hop Singles. Other charting tracks include “I Need A Hot Girl” which also peaked at #65 on the Billboard Hot 100.", "annotation_id": "9263329", "url": "https://genius.com/9263329", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stun’n (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Big-tymers-stunn-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Stun’n (Remix)", "genius_id": 10126, "source": "api"}
