{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "MoneyOverBitches dot com, check the domain", "vault_lines": ["MoneyOverBitches dot com, check the domain"], "meaning": "He’s saying that the business comes first, and the women come after. MoneyOverBitches is also a nod to his own MOB.  “Check the domain” is a double entendre, which can be said either as it’s stated, or “Check the dough, mayne”.", "annotation_id": "37238662", "url": "https://genius.com/37238662", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "Drop a four in it and appreciate the greatness, Drizzy", "vault_lines": ["Drop a four in it and appreciate the greatness, Drizzy"], "meaning": "“Four” is a reference to the ratio of codeine/syrup to soda. Lil Wayne popularizes the ratio in his song “Me and My Drank” where he says “Drop a four in a 20 ounce and call it 24’s.”", "annotation_id": "30831338", "url": "https://genius.com/30831338", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "People ask me if I pray, I say, “Yeah, once in a blue moon” Oops, I mean a red moon, I did it again, Tune", "vault_lines": ["People ask me if I pray, I say, \"Yeah, once in a blue moon\""], "meaning": "Drake is expressing he is not one to pray very often.  He uses a commonly used expression to even measure how rare it is. The moon is dubbed a “blue moon” if it is the second of two full moons within the same calendar month. This phenomena happens only once every few years. After Drake expresses his rarity, he realizes he made a mistake in speaking the color of the notorious gang the Crips. Wayne is affiliated with the Bloods, and the two aforementioned gangs are arch-rivals. The color of the Bloods is red, which makes Drake change the blue moon into a red moon. He then apologizes for making the mistake again like in their song Ransom. Drake said, “You ain’t heard of me then you should go and get a Blue’s Clue? Oops! I mean a red clue.\nWayne’s here, Soo-woo!”", "annotation_id": "13864299", "url": "https://genius.com/13864299", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "Stuntin’ is a habit, get it from my daddy", "vault_lines": ["Stuntin' is a habit, get it from my daddy"], "meaning": "Weezy is referencing one of his most iconic tracks “Stuntin' Like My Daddy” from his collaborative album with Birdman Like Father, Like Son. On the track, Wayne and Birdman detail their lavish lifestyles as pimps and rappers.", "annotation_id": "13571801", "url": "https://genius.com/13571801", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "The supplement I’ve taken got me feelin’ mighty", "vault_lines": ["The supplement I've taken got me feelin' mighty"], "meaning": "Double entendre: My Tee / Mighty\n\nMY Tee: “Promethazine codeine syrup weighs down your clothes, whatever you may be wearing and makes it feel heavy” -@Stasthagod\n\n\n\nMighty: also he could be referring to other drugs (Ex: MDMA, Weed) that has him feeling mighty(euphoria, endorphins).\n\n\n\na play on words…", "annotation_id": "3288219", "url": "https://genius.com/3288219", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "I’m just doin’", "vault_lines": ["I just listened back and now I'm sounding like a trumpet"], "meaning": "He’s just doing him, which means he is caring only about himself and doing what he wants. As he said in “Over”\n\nWhat am I doin'? Oh yeah, that’s right, I’m doin' me", "annotation_id": "3174620", "url": "https://genius.com/3174620", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "Just like Shaggy, I tote that boom-bastic", "vault_lines": ["Just like Shaggy, I tote that boom-bastic"], "meaning": "A reference to the song “Boombastic” by Jamaican musician Shaggy; Weezy gives his firearm another nickname.", "annotation_id": "3024551", "url": "https://genius.com/3024551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "Frostbite Drizzy, nigga, nobody as cold as Drake", "vault_lines": ["Frostbite Drizzy, nigga, nobody as cold as Drake"], "meaning": "Taking a page out of his mentor Lil Wayne’s book by giving himself a nickname, here Drake proclaims he’s the nicest on the track. Anytime he’s invited to do a guest verse, he’s coldblooded, giving the invitee no room to shine.", "annotation_id": "3024548", "url": "https://genius.com/3024548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "And homie’s scared, ’Cause his bitch like me", "vault_lines": ["And homie's scared, 'Cause his bitch like me"], "meaning": "The homie is scared ‘cause his girl is bout to leave him for weezy.\n\n\n\nWeezy is alluding to the original verse of Chris Brown on “Get Like Me\" by David Banner", "annotation_id": "1003599", "url": "https://genius.com/1003599", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "And 18 G’s is why the chicken crossed the street", "vault_lines": ["And 18 G's is why the chicken crossed the street"], "meaning": "A chicken is slang for a kilo of coke, which Wayne used to sell for 18G’s. So Weezy’s saying the chicken will only cross the street for 18000$.\n\nUsing a play on words with the expression “why did the chicken cross the road” and the chicken being “moved” or sold.", "annotation_id": "51656", "url": "https://genius.com/51656", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "I’m about to change the fucking game, pass the remote", "vault_lines": ["I'm about to change the fucking game, pass the remote"], "meaning": "When your team starts getting blown out you know you change to another game to avoid getting your heart stomped on anymore.\n\n\n\nYou change a channel with a remote, and Drake wants to change the rap game, therefore asking for a remote to make it more clever.", "annotation_id": "51653", "url": "https://genius.com/51653", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "All I hit is C-notes", "vault_lines": ["But I don't need my vocal cords, all I hit is C-notes"], "meaning": "“C-notes” refers to either hundred dollar bills or C-notes can be the first key on a piano, which is the lowest so  he could mean that he only sings in a low tone.", "annotation_id": "47191", "url": "https://genius.com/47191", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
