{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stunt Hard", "line": "You know I stunt shit ’cause I write all Stunna bars, haha", "vault_lines": ["You know I stunt shit 'cause I write all Stunna bars, haha"], "meaning": "If you hear a Birdman verse and think “hey this shit kinda fire”, Wayne wrote it.", "annotation_id": "23750149", "url": "https://genius.com/23750149", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stunt Hard", "line": "I’m a young rebel", "vault_lines": ["I'm a young rebel"], "meaning": "A setup for the next two lines: Wayne is saying he’s a young rebel, which sounds like “a young Rubble”, as in Barney (or in this case Bamm-Bamm) Rubble from The Flintstones.", "annotation_id": "1633184", "url": "https://genius.com/1633184", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stunt Hard", "line": "I need a young Pebbles,", "vault_lines": ["I need a young Pebbles,"], "meaning": "He needs a young female in his life.\n\nWayne is referencing the previous line where he says he’s a young Rubble (with a babyface). And if he’s a young Rubble, he’d need a young Pebbles (the daughter of Fred Flintstone).", "annotation_id": "1633126", "url": "https://genius.com/1633126", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stunt Hard", "line": "I’m wild, Drizzy tough, and the Kid vicious The three horseman, we just need Sid Vicious, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I'm wild, Drizzy tough, and the Kid vicious"], "meaning": "Despite Wayne’s questionable decisions on the mic as of late, he still gives us a good line here and there. And it just so happens this one’s alongside fellow Young Money member Drake and Kid-Kidd (aka Nut Da Kid). He compares his crew to the legendary wrestling faction, The Four Horsemen, which consisted of the 16-time World Champion Ric Flair, Barry Windham, and Ole Anderson during their 1990 – 1991 run in the south’s World Championship Wrestling. Not bad company to compare yourself to. Now all they need is a Sid Vicious, who was added to the actual Four Horsemen to fill the final spot in the group.\n\nGudda Gudda, maybe?", "annotation_id": "1462179", "url": "https://genius.com/1462179", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stunt Hard", "line": "I got a babyface", "vault_lines": ["and I got a babyface"], "meaning": "A setup between the young rebel/young Rubble line because Bamm-Bamm Rubble (a young Rubble) has a baby face.\n\nBirdman’s name also used to be baby. Birdman is considered to be “Weezy’s dad”, which is why he says he has a baby face.", "annotation_id": "169108", "url": "https://genius.com/169108", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stunt Hard", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-stunt-hard-lyrics", "genius_title": "Stunt Hard", "genius_id": 6011, "source": "api"}
