{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "I got my world in my pocket, cause I ain’ tryna drop it", "vault_lines": ["I got my world in my pocket, cause I ain' tryna drop it"], "meaning": "Actually, Lil Wayne tried Drop The World. But here’s Wizzy playin' on meanin “drop the world”, like a world is something, that he can REALLY drops. In literal sense.", "annotation_id": "137743", "url": "https://genius.com/137743", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "Steppin’ on the stars, she pause", "vault_lines": ["Steppin' on the stars, she pause"], "meaning": "Looks like they are on the Hollywood Walk of Fame in LA, stepping on the stars. Or the groupie is clearly stepping on stars to get to the top…or maybe they’re just high or as Wayne likes the state, that he is not a human being and that he is Right above it, [they are right above heaven] that they are just walking up there.", "annotation_id": "85165", "url": "https://genius.com/85165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "Cause my heart is out of service, my eyes turn black", "vault_lines": ["Cause my heart is out of service, my eyes turn black"], "meaning": "When Wayne’s heart is off, his eyes turn black ‘cause his heart is his inner-light", "annotation_id": "78846", "url": "https://genius.com/78846", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "Love create wars", "vault_lines": ["Love is the party, my heart is such a disco ball"], "meaning": "Way to go Helen of Troy.\n\nPeople who are in love often have fights.\n\nThis may also be a reference to “Love is a Battlefield” by Pat Benatar.", "annotation_id": "77080", "url": "https://genius.com/77080", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "I’m on a new way, tomorrow’s too late", "vault_lines": ["I'm on a new way, tomorrow's too late"], "meaning": "I thought the idiom was “better late than never.” Though I suppose Drake capped it off by stating “but never late is better.”", "annotation_id": "77076", "url": "https://genius.com/77076", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "When the sunlight falls down", "vault_lines": ["When the sunlight falls down"], "meaning": "It is often said of those in love that the sun sets and rises on the loved one. When the sun sets in this verse, the woman has left for good.", "annotation_id": "77073", "url": "https://genius.com/77073", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "Strobe lights dance with the stars", "vault_lines": ["Strobe lights dance with the stars"], "meaning": "The idea of strobe lights is the idea of a constantly flashing and confusing and overwhelming. Much like love, strobe lights can cause confusion and disorientation in those that experience it.", "annotation_id": "77069", "url": "https://genius.com/77069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "My world spin around her cause it’s a world without her", "vault_lines": ["My world spin around her cause it's a world without her"], "meaning": "Because this girl is no longer in his life, he thinks about her constantly. His world revolves around her (and getting her back).", "annotation_id": "77067", "url": "https://genius.com/77067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "I don’t see love anymore I’m blind to the fact", "vault_lines": ["I don't see love anymore I'm blind to the fact"], "meaning": "They say that love is blind, but in this instance Wayne is the one who has turned a blind eye to love.", "annotation_id": "77065", "url": "https://genius.com/77065", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "She question what we are, and I’ll drink to the answer", "vault_lines": ["She question what we are, and I'll drink to the answer"], "meaning": "In the tradition of toasting, Wayne says that whatever they are Wayne will drink in honor of that. Essentially, he’s just about having a good time with this girl.", "annotation_id": "77063", "url": "https://genius.com/77063", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "And I know that one day this show will end - applause", "vault_lines": ["And I know that one day this show will end - applause"], "meaning": "The “Supa Dupa” flow rears its ugly head early in Wayne’s verse, but he uses it cleverly. In this metaphor for love, Wayne creates that analogy that “love” is a theatre production, and when it’s over there will be applause. (Perhaps because the two lovers in this instance are not really meant for each other.)", "annotation_id": "77061", "url": "https://genius.com/77061", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "I told her I would love her, love her lasts forever Forever’s just a word, I put words together", "vault_lines": ["I told her I would love her, love her lasts forever"], "meaning": "Wayne told this girl he loved her, and then admitted that love lasts forever; Wayne goes on to dismiss the thought of love by dismissing the word “forever” by claiming “forever is only a word” and since Wayne makes a living off of “putting words” together he just does what he wants with the girl–essentially uses her.", "annotation_id": "77055", "url": "https://genius.com/77055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strobe Lights", "line": "Love is the party, my heart is such a disco ball She’s in line waitin’, my guest list too long", "vault_lines": ["Love is the party, my heart is such a disco ball"], "meaning": "Wayne likens the idea of love to a party, in this extended metaphor Wayne’s heart is the center of the party (the disco ball) and this song addresses one girl in particular who waited for a long time to feel his love–because there were too many groupie hoes that came before her.", "annotation_id": "77053", "url": "https://genius.com/77053", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
