{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Mining my own data", "vault_lines": ["mining my own data"], "meaning": "In relationship databases, you mine your own data. Also a double entendre of him saying he’s minding his own business", "annotation_id": "18828819", "url": "https://genius.com/18828819", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Hello world, I’m with a yellow girl, number two pencil", "vault_lines": ["Hello world, I'm with a yellow girl, number two pencil"], "meaning": "‘Hello World!’ is a common phrase used to do a sanity check when coding software. When Wayne says ‘yellow girl,’ he’s referring to being with a woman of Asian background.\n\nNot only is a number two pencil usually yellow, but there is a common stereotype with Asians being smart thus using a pencil more often.", "annotation_id": "18828786", "url": "https://genius.com/18828786", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "I’m top dog, you top ramen, I’m top dog", "vault_lines": ["I'm top dog, you top ramen, I'm top dog"], "meaning": "Like B.o.B.’s previous line “Bitch, I’m top chef, you Top Ramen, I’m top shelf”, Lil Wayne is reminding the listener how cool he is. Top dog is the leader of the pack. Lil Wayne also uses the “Top Ramen” line to refer to the listener as lame.", "annotation_id": "15774380", "url": "https://genius.com/15774380", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Bitch, I’m top chef, you top ramen, I’m top shelf", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm top chef, you top ramen, I'm top shelf"], "meaning": "B.o.B. refers to how top chefs cook very fancy food and he is comparing the listener to something cheap and basic, something he is above.\n\n“Top shelf” describes something as valuable, the term deriving from putting things you don’t want others to touch on the top shelf.", "annotation_id": "15774351", "url": "https://genius.com/15774351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "I do my job exceptionally,", "vault_lines": ["I do my job exceptionally,"], "meaning": "I would definitely say that this is the case for Bobby Ray.\nHis debut album,\nB.o.B Presents: The Adventures of Bobby Ray, has gone gold, and sold over 87,000 copies in the first week.\nHis second album, Strange Clouds, sold over 280,000 albums, and over 76,000 in the first week.\nHis most current album,\nUnderground Luxury, has also achieved a respective  level of success. Many Mixtapes of B.o.B’s mixed tapes have also received plenty of success", "annotation_id": "3388552", "url": "https://genius.com/3388552", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "You bitch, you, you hot as a igloo", "vault_lines": ["you bitch, you, you hot as a igloo"], "meaning": "An igloo, is a man-made ice home made out of tightly packed ice blocks. This line is a simile; meaning, he’s not hot at all.", "annotation_id": "505420", "url": "https://genius.com/505420", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "No last call to the bartender, “What you got left?”", "vault_lines": ["No last call to the bartender, \"What you got left?\""], "meaning": "Following on from the mentioning of the “top shelf” in the line prior to this.\n“Last call” being an indication made by a barwench to the  to grab some bottles before they stop serving, this rule came in in order to preserve some peace and prevent total sloppiness but they don’t apply to our high rollin' buddies here.\n\n\n\nTheir options are plentiful", "annotation_id": "433096", "url": "https://genius.com/433096", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Well, ain’t no question, yes, it’s B.o.B, yes, definitely", "vault_lines": ["Well, ain't no question, yes, it's B.o.B, yes, definitely"], "meaning": "Trending from the first line in verse 1\n\nThere’s obviously no need to question who this is.\nAs B.o.B. said himself “it’s B.o.B., yes definitely”", "annotation_id": "377865", "url": "https://genius.com/377865", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "You would swear I was an equestrian", "vault_lines": ["you would swear I was an equestrian"], "meaning": "Continuation from the horse theme; you would think he studied them because around one all the time.\n\nAlso, notice how, phonetically, “equestrian” and “question” are fairly similar, this follows on from the previous line where he mentions “guessing”.\nYou’d start to think he was a question with the way people were guessing him “B.o.B?…”.\n\n\n\nIt’s embarrassing that I thought of this immediately on 1st hearing this line but B.o.B ripped off a line spoken by Mary-Kate Olsen in It Takes Two\n\n“Are you asking me equestrian?”", "annotation_id": "376932", "url": "https://genius.com/376932", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "All you see is strange clouds (Strange clouds) Strange clouds", "vault_lines": ["All you see is strange clouds (Strange clouds)"], "meaning": "The clouds underline the statement of simultaneously being high and drinking, believe it or not, the clouds appear different from the norm when you part-take in such activities.\n\n\n\nDescribing yourself as being “up in the clouds” or “cloudy headed” are sayings which allude to feeling the effects of lighting up, the lingering and billowing smoke produced by smoking marijuana can, strangely, also resemble clouds.", "annotation_id": "376776", "url": "https://genius.com/376776", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Piru, gangsters, outlaws!", "vault_lines": ["I do my job exceptionally,"], "meaning": "The Pirus a.k.a Piru Street Boys are California based Bloods, the name “Piru” is derived from Piru Street in Compton which is where the California sector Bloods originated from.\n\n\n\nSoowoo if you bangin'!", "annotation_id": "375974", "url": "https://genius.com/375974", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "My nigga, all day, all night, half-pipe", "vault_lines": ["My nigga, all day, all night, half-pipe"], "meaning": "Wayne’s on weed and booze night and day, here he name drops the controversially titled 2001 song by Weezer: “Hash Pipe”.\nThe track was requested to be renamed “Half Pipe” in order to avoid the drug reference and appeal to boarders, the band refused only to have the track name censored wherever it was to appear.\n\nFUNFACT:\nRivers Cuomo was inspired to write this song after snorting some Ritalin followed by 3 Tequila shots.\n\n\n\nAfter he smoking half-pipe and drinks all day and night, Dwayne also attempts to skate board while on tour", "annotation_id": "375972", "url": "https://genius.com/375972", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "I dive in that pussy, ya, I belly flop, I jack knife", "vault_lines": ["I dive in that pussy, ya, I belly flop, I jack knife"], "meaning": "Wayne’s eager to get into that pussy\n\n\n\n“Belly flop” and “jack knife” are ways in which you can penetrate the waters surface, “jack knife” also being a sex position.", "annotation_id": "375744", "url": "https://genius.com/375744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Nigga, keep your nourishment first And your mind on my lyrics", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, keep your nourishment first"], "meaning": "This ties into the line before as Bobby Ray is addressing his haters.\n\n\n\nMomma always told you “never go to school on an empty stomach”, so he’s telling his haters to mull over his lyrics as their mind wakes up while eating their morning meal before they pass judgment.", "annotation_id": "375740", "url": "https://genius.com/375740", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "On point like a decimal is", "vault_lines": ["on point like a decimal is"], "meaning": "In math, when writing a number with a decimal, a period or point (.) is used.\n\n\n\nAlso a possible allusion to Naughty By Nature’s “Feel Me Flow” where they spat a similar simile:\n\nThat’s on point like decimals", "annotation_id": "375418", "url": "https://genius.com/375418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "I’m Decatur ’til I die (Yeah), yes, I rep that definitely", "vault_lines": ["I'm Decatur 'til I die (Yeah), yes, I rep that definitely"], "meaning": "Decatur is an intown suburb of Atlanta, where B.o.B hails from", "annotation_id": "375411", "url": "https://genius.com/375411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Yeah, got that TEC for technical difficulties", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, got that TEC for technical difficulties"], "meaning": "Tec is slang for the Tec 9mm gun that has been a favorite, historically, for rappers to mention.\n\nIf there are complex problems to deal with, he takes to them with his gun. Which is ironic, since he served almost a years time in Rikers Island for gun possession in New York City.\n\n\n\nMoral of the story: Tec 9s solve life’s hardest problems!", "annotation_id": "375289", "url": "https://genius.com/375289", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Uh, blue jeans, I’m faded,", "vault_lines": ["Uh, blue jeans, I'm faded,"], "meaning": "Weezy is as “faded” (slang for high) as the blue jeans he wears", "annotation_id": "375268", "url": "https://genius.com/375268", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Kick back on that Glock, call that Jiu Jitsu", "vault_lines": ["Kick back on that Glock, call that Jiu Jitsu"], "meaning": "His pistol kicks hard, as a counteract of it firing, much like a master of Jiu Jitsu, a form of martial arts, would counter-attack your strikes.\n\n\n\nUnfortunately kicking is an illegal move, it’s all about grappling. Tunechi Li needs to learn to follow the rules or he might end up in jail.", "annotation_id": "375264", "url": "https://genius.com/375264", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "It’s Tunechi Li,", "vault_lines": ["I do my job exceptionally,"], "meaning": "One of his MANY nicknames. Tunechi Li is a setup for later lines where he talks about fighting… Jet Li was also a fighter…\n\nHis Grandmother called him Lil' Tune, due to his love for music. He later changed it to Lil' Tunechi to make it sound cooler (like Gucci). He explains this in the documentary he shot before he went to jail, but he adds the ‘Li’ like he added ‘chi’ for Gucci but the ‘li’ is for ‘Jet Li’ maybe he was a great fan of him and his martial arts.", "annotation_id": "375238", "url": "https://genius.com/375238", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Smokin’ on that strong, that Arnold Schwarzenegger", "vault_lines": ["Smokin' on that strong, that Arnold Schwarzenegger"], "meaning": "Weezy is referencing the famous picture of Arnold smoking a joint, which caught him some flack years later during his career as governor of California. The pronunciation “Errlnold” is simply saying his name with an Austrian accent (where Arnold was born)\n\n\n\nAlso Arnold Schwarzenegger was a professional body builder, so this is a simile comparing Arnold’s strength to Lil Wayne’s high quality MJ.", "annotation_id": "375193", "url": "https://genius.com/375193", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "I just stay with a stallion,", "vault_lines": ["I just stay with a stallion,"], "meaning": "Stallion = A girl so wild, so beautiful, so aggressive, so fine, that’s thick in all the right places, strong physically and mentally\n\n\n\nNot to be confused with an uncastrated (male) horse", "annotation_id": "374689", "url": "https://genius.com/374689", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "And um, I’ma hit her with that pipe, call that Nancy Kerrigan", "vault_lines": ["And um, I'ma hit her with that pipe, call that Nancy Kerrigan"], "meaning": "Ice skater Nancy Kerrigan was famously attacked with a police baton during the 1994 US Figure Skating Championships. Her assailant was connected to Kerrigan’s skating rival Tonya Harding.\n\nVideo Interview with Ms. Kerrigan:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6T09XWRkq5M\n\nReminiscent of Cam'ron’s line:\n\nI stab a bitch over ice, Nancy Kerrigan\n\nB.o.B.’s not saying he’s going to beat up a woman, though. Pipe is another word for penis… so he’s giving her that.", "annotation_id": "374294", "url": "https://genius.com/374294", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Strange Clouds", "line": "Yeah, so these niggas can’t sleep on me There’s no Inception in this", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, so these niggas can't sleep on me"], "meaning": "Reference to the 2010 film, Inception, where people went into their dreams, and into dreams inside of dreams… As they were sleeping…\n\n\n\nInception is also confusing, and most people don’t understand it. Just like a rapper’s lyrics can get slept on.\n\nFun Fact: the music video for Wayne’s “6 Foot 7 Foot” was inspired by the 2010 film\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c7tOAGY59uQ", "annotation_id": "374187", "url": "https://genius.com/374187", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
