{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Straight To The Dance Floor", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Jamie-foxx-straight-to-the-dance-floor-lyrics", "genius_title": "Straight To The Dance Floor", "genius_id": 77723, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stop Playin With Me", "line": "’Cause when I was down, you all got lost on me like Bin Laden", "vault_lines": ["'Cause when I was down, you all got lost on me like Bin Laden"], "meaning": "Wayne is using a simile to compare his friends’ behavior to the disappearance of Osama Bin Laden after the 9/11 attacks. The first part of the line, “Cause when I was down,” refers to a time when Wayne was feeling low or depressed. This phrase evokes similarities to the Twin Towers being “downed” during 9/11. The second part of the line, “you all got lost on me like Bin Laden,” is a play on words that uses the name “Bin Laden” to describe the way his friends disappeared or were not there for him during his difficult time. The comparison to Bin Laden is significant because he was a notorious figure who was able to evade capture for a long time after the 9/11 attacks.", "annotation_id": "30611896", "url": "https://genius.com/30611896", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stop Playin With Me", "line": "They say to be or not to be, bitch, I’m indecisive", "vault_lines": ["They say to be or not to be, bitch, I'm indecisive"], "meaning": "Wayne quotes one of Shakespeare’s most famous examples of antithesis, which is one of the major themes of this song. See line 1 of verse 1 annotation.", "annotation_id": "28625029", "url": "https://genius.com/28625029", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stop Playin With Me", "line": "Ooh, I got a plus sized model But she my lil’ mama", "vault_lines": ["Ooh, I got a plus sized model"], "meaning": "Wayne uses the literary device of antithesis by contrasting two words and playing with their opposite meanings. He continues this theme throughout song.\n\nplus size – little\nspinning – the cure for spinning\nchange – don’t change\nrunning from – running into\ndream – wake\nlove – hate\nflames – cold\npay – receipt\ngetting tatted – orgasmic pleasure\nhospital attire – fashion week\nembarrassing – flattering\nbattle royale – 1 on 1 battle\nlong live – rest in peace\nA(dam) – Z\nflies – long\nto be – not to be\nlow – high\ncrawl – run\nlion (predator) – goat (prey)\ntoes – nose\ndown – up\nunfold (expand) – squeeze (contract)\n\nThis antithesis creates the sense that Wayne is playing mind games with the listener, which is fittingly the opposite of the song title. Wayne explicitly states that these opposing views are mind games in line 7 of verse 1.", "annotation_id": "28624857", "url": "https://genius.com/28624857", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stop Playin With Me", "line": "No car keys needed, button push, go", "vault_lines": ["No car keys needed, button push, go"], "meaning": "A reference to luxury cars many of which start up without turning an actual car key, instead by pushing a button.", "annotation_id": "23646562", "url": "https://genius.com/23646562", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stop Playin With Me", "line": "Long live my skateboard and rest in peace to Adam Z", "vault_lines": ["Long live my skateboard and rest in peace to Adam Z"], "meaning": "A tribute to Adam Ziegler AKA Adam Z, Wayne’s skateboard coach who passed away in 2016 of a heart attack.\n\nWayne broke the news on his twitter writing:\n\n “Rest in peace to my brother Adam Z…life is too short bro but real brotherhood is forever. U taught me that.”", "annotation_id": "23646480", "url": "https://genius.com/23646480", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stop Playin With Me", "line": "They’d rather battle royale, way before they battle me", "vault_lines": ["They'd rather battle royale, way before they battle me"], "meaning": "A battle royale is a large fight in which everyone is against one another. Wayne is saying that they’d rather fight amongst themselves than to fight him because he is a bigger threat.", "annotation_id": "19000566", "url": "https://genius.com/19000566", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stop Playin With Me", "line": "Stop playin’ with me, bitch, stop playin’ with me Stop playin’ with me, bitch,", "vault_lines": ["Motherfucker, stop playin' with me"], "meaning": "Wayne references one of the earliest hits by Cash Money Records, “Drag Em N Tha River” by UNLV, a New Orleans group consisting of Yella Boy, Tec-9, and Lil Ya.\n\nThe song was a diss record towards fellow New Orleans rapper Mystikal.\n\nThroughout the song, Yella Boy raps several times:\n\nDon’t forget about the U\nand the Cash Money clowns\nstop playing with me\nstop playing with me, bitch\nstop playing with me", "annotation_id": "18957194", "url": "https://genius.com/18957194", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Stop Playin With Me", "line": "Dwayne Carter, niggas wanna be the DC sniper", "vault_lines": ["Dwayne Carter, niggas wanna be the DC sniper"], "meaning": "This line is a play on the 2002 attacks which were credited the “D.C. Snipers”. In the attacks two men killed 10 people and wounded three others.", "annotation_id": "18955721", "url": "https://genius.com/18955721", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
