{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I spit these bars, this a uni-verse", "vault_lines": ["I spit these bars, this a uni-verse"], "meaning": "Clever wordplay from Tunechi here; he says that he is the one that spits the bars and the second part of the line: this a uni-verse. The second part describes the whole song just being a solo verse. Combined it just brings the initial train of thought that it is only him – Weezy- that does everything in the song.", "annotation_id": "18351847", "url": "https://genius.com/18351847", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Nigga I be hard on a ho ’cause a bitch ain’t shit And every ho I done fucked done sucked my dick", "vault_lines": ["Nigga I be hard on a ho 'cause a bitch ain't shit"], "meaning": "These lines came directly from Birdman on B.G.’s 1997 song “Stay ‘N’ Line Hoe”. https://genius.com/Bg-baby-gangsta-stay-n-line-hoe-lyrics\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_qWruomXTD0", "annotation_id": "13487217", "url": "https://genius.com/13487217", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I call my bitch Plane Jane ’cause she catch nut like a flight", "vault_lines": ["I call my bitch Plane Jane 'cause she catch nut like a flight"], "meaning": "Wordplay\n\nA woman who is a “Plain Jane” is a woman who is extremely average an unimpressive when it comes to being physically attractive.\n\n\n\nHowever, if you know anything about Wayne you know he always has good weed and bad bitches and is simply using his usual trademark, a clever play on words.\n\nWhile the world “plain” may mean unattractive or basic, it is a homophone for the word “plane” a large, flying machine.\n\nWeezy’s girl earned this nickname because the way she catches his nut (as in receive) is the same way in which someone may try to catch a plane (as in rushing to make it).", "annotation_id": "4029362", "url": "https://genius.com/4029362", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I can’t trust my iPhone, I think Siri the Feds", "vault_lines": ["I can't trust my iPhone, I think Siri the Feds"], "meaning": "Wayne doesn’t trust his iPhone, for believing that in some way Siri may be connected to the federal police. Even though it may seem a little paranoid at first, in view of the recent NSA scandal, Tune may be right in his suspicion.\n\n\n\nThe next year, Wayne recorded a song “Siri” featuring 2 Chainz based around this line, which found its official release in 2020.", "annotation_id": "3364183", "url": "https://genius.com/3364183", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "And my homie, he a sniper, we call him Wesley Snipes", "vault_lines": ["And my homie, he a sniper, we call him Wesley Snipes"], "meaning": "Not only a play-on of Wesley Snipe’s name, but a reference to his character, Joe, in the 2002 movie Liberty Stands Still, in which he plays a sniper.\n\nWeezy doesn’t even touch the work; he has goons for that.", "annotation_id": "2644817", "url": "https://genius.com/2644817", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Never say never, she might do her friend, you never know", "vault_lines": ["Never say never, she might do her friend, you never know"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne ironically contradicts himself by saying ‘you never know’ after saying the common phrase “Never say never”.\n\nThis is also a sneak-shout-out to Justin Bieber, who’s most popular for his track “Never Say Never”. Weezy has collaborated with the pop star on the song “Backpack”.", "annotation_id": "2625045", "url": "https://genius.com/2625045", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Your bitch leaking information, I just follow the drip", "vault_lines": ["Your bitch leaking information, I just follow the drip"], "meaning": "“Leaking information” refers to her snitching and telling the feds some compromising evidence.\n\nTherefore, Wayne follows the metaphorical “drip” from the “leak” to find her and, presumably, silence her for good.", "annotation_id": "2600285", "url": "https://genius.com/2600285", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I’m on them shrooms, my goons on alert", "vault_lines": ["I'm on them shrooms, my goons on alert"], "meaning": "Wayne’s high off mushrooms which causes intense hallucinations and disorientation.\n\n\n\nIt makes sense that he would need his goons to stay on alert while he is tripping off them.", "annotation_id": "2600276", "url": "https://genius.com/2600276", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I’m too young to die sober,", "vault_lines": ["I'm too young to die sober,"], "meaning": "At 31 years old, Wayne feels he is too young to stop drinking and smoking. He wants to enjoy his life while he can.\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to the hook of Wayne’s Bitch Don’t Kill My Vibe freestyle from earlier on this very mixtape.", "annotation_id": "2600259", "url": "https://genius.com/2600259", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Medication high", "vault_lines": ["Nigga I be hard on a ho 'cause a bitch ain't shit"], "meaning": "Could be referring to Wayne getting high off medical marijuana or prescription cough syrup.\n\n\n\n#AT THE SAME DAMN TIME!", "annotation_id": "2600233", "url": "https://genius.com/2600233", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I got the power, but a short fuse", "vault_lines": ["I got the power, but a short fuse"], "meaning": "He has power/authority due to his riches and influence.\nPower can also mean electrical power, in which fuses are used.\nA “short fuse” would shut off the power quickly. Having power and a short fuse might seem like a contradicting statement, but Wayne actually means he has a quick temper", "annotation_id": "2181819", "url": "https://genius.com/2181819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "My system solar", "vault_lines": ["In her throat like Ricola, my system solar"], "meaning": "Some people are fatigued by the sun, but Wayne is solar-powered (http://www.chicagobears.com/multimedia/videos/TE-Bennett-Im-solar-powered/510de2da-1bd3-4904-9cca-10c6714f1c02).\nHe is also the “hottest thing under the sun” so his body probably generates its own energy.\nLastly, by saying his system’s solar, he is saying he is big and the world revolves around him like the solar system.\nThere are two other astronomy references in this song: here and here", "annotation_id": "2181678", "url": "https://genius.com/2181678", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Shoot you up at the light", "vault_lines": ["Alright, fucking right, shoot you up at the light"], "meaning": "Rappers 2Pac and Notorious B.I.G. were both shot and killed in a drive-by while the cars they were in were stopped at a traffic light.\nWeezy will execute you in this same manner.", "annotation_id": "2181644", "url": "https://genius.com/2181644", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Soon as I get off paper, I’mma smack a nigga", "vault_lines": ["Soon as I get off paper, I'mma smack a nigga"], "meaning": "Getting off paper is a term used to describe when someone serves their time and pays their due for their crimes.\nTunechi is continuing his previous line about getting a ticket. And when he’s finished paying his dues:", "annotation_id": "2165563", "url": "https://genius.com/2165563", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I’m on a mission to get movie money, stick to the script", "vault_lines": ["I'm on a mission to get movie money, stick to the script"], "meaning": "He wants to get money like A-list actors receive from playing parts in movies.\n\n\n\nIn order to do this, he is going to “stick to the script”, which is a term used to describe actors simply reading the lines they’re given. Likewise, Lil Tunechi is saying that he is going to keep using his formula for success in order to keep making money.", "annotation_id": "2162860", "url": "https://genius.com/2162860", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "We geeked up, the revenge of the nerds", "vault_lines": ["We geeked up, the revenge of the nerds"], "meaning": "Geeked up is a term used to describe someone highly intoxicated off of drugs. Tunechi uses wordplay here to relate his “geeked up” state to actual geeks and nerds.\nRevenge of the Nerds is a 1984 comedy film where a group of persecuted outcasts try to fight back against fraternity jocks to gain some respect at their college.", "annotation_id": "2162852", "url": "https://genius.com/2162852", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I gotta clean up after these niggas ’cause they be wasting time", "vault_lines": ["I gotta clean up after these niggas 'cause they be wasting time"], "meaning": "The other rappers who Wayne works with tend to mess around and play on a song, causing it to become a bloated mess. It’s up to Wayne to clean up the aftermath, even if he does find it to be a waste of time correcting their work.", "annotation_id": "2161995", "url": "https://genius.com/2161995", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I’m shining on these hoes so hard they getting tan lines", "vault_lines": ["I'm shining on these hoes so hard they getting tan lines"], "meaning": "Being out in the sun for a long period of time (especially if the sun shining right down on you) will give you tan lines, which you can see if you remove your clothes. The parts of your body that are not exposed to sun will be lighter in color.\n\n\n\nThat’s how hard Wayne is shining AKA stunting on these hoes.", "annotation_id": "2161993", "url": "https://genius.com/2161993", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Still got that crack, maybe one day I’mma pass the rock", "vault_lines": ["Still got that crack, maybe one day I'mma pass the rock"], "meaning": "Double entendre.\n\nCould mean he literally still has crack on him, and he’ll sell it (pass the rock) eventually.\n\nCould mean he still has that crack (flow, skills, the game rap on lock etc) and one day he’ll pass the rock (let someone else have the rap game)", "annotation_id": "2161952", "url": "https://genius.com/2161952", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I swear to God, I put in work", "vault_lines": ["I swear to God, I put in work"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne indeed does put in work as he’s constantly put out a project every year.Just this year he’s put out IANAHB2 and D5, he could also be referring to kilos of cocaine which is also classified as work.\n\n\n\nThis is most likely a nod to A$AP Ferg’s single Work, as Wayne has admitted to being a avid listener of his music.", "annotation_id": "2161888", "url": "https://genius.com/2161888", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Pretty please don’t kill my vibe", "vault_lines": ["Pretty please don't kill my vibe"], "meaning": "A reference to Kendrick Lamar’s song Bitch, Don’t Kill My Vibe, which was also the beat used on the third track on this mixtape.", "annotation_id": "2161617", "url": "https://genius.com/2161617", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Shout out Turk It’s Hot Boys, bitch, the block is hot", "vault_lines": ["It's Hot Boys, bitch, the block is hot"], "meaning": "Wayne shows his gratitude to Turk, his close friend from Hot Boys (Wayne`s former hip-hop group).\n\n\n\nLil Wayne, Juvenile, B.G. and Turk.\n\nHe also mentions his debut album “The Block Is Hot”", "annotation_id": "2161129", "url": "https://genius.com/2161129", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "No broken mirrors, I can’t see myself broke", "vault_lines": ["No broken mirrors, I can't see myself broke"], "meaning": "A funny wordplay by Tune, he does not have any broken mirrors in the house, because he does not want to see himself broke(poor), or broken into pieces.", "annotation_id": "2161106", "url": "https://genius.com/2161106", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Straight take all your possessions, call that shit Poltergeist", "vault_lines": ["Straight take all your possessions, call that shit Poltergeist"], "meaning": "A poltergeist is a  supernatural being that can possess inanimate objects as well as sentient beings.\n\n\n\nWayne will take all of your “possessions” AKA material objects such as jewelry or money; much like how a ghost can “possess” someone.", "annotation_id": "2161070", "url": "https://genius.com/2161070", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Right back pocket, flag redder than a velvet rope", "vault_lines": ["Right back pocket, flag redder than a velvet rope"], "meaning": "A red bandana is as red as velvet rope and it’s in Weezy’s right pocket because he is Blood affiliated.", "annotation_id": "2160904", "url": "https://genius.com/2160904", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "And tell that bitch give me my space, like a telescope", "vault_lines": ["And tell that bitch give me my space, like a telescope"], "meaning": "Another example of clever wordplay by Tune, he is telling his girl to give him some space like a telescope, which you need to look in to space.", "annotation_id": "2160895", "url": "https://genius.com/2160895", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "Dirty money, no footprints in dirt", "vault_lines": ["Dirty money, no footprints in dirt"], "meaning": "Dirty money is defined as “profit from the sale of narcotics, prostitution, guns, or other illegal activities. Money that needs to be laundered.”\n\nThough he’s making money that’s “dirty”, he doesn’t physically step in dirt. He also leaves no trace of his activities, unlike a person who steps on the ground and leaves a footprint.", "annotation_id": "2160837", "url": "https://genius.com/2160837", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "It’s Dedication 5", "vault_lines": ["Nigga I be hard on a ho 'cause a bitch ain't shit"], "meaning": "Dedication 5 is the fifth mixtape in the Dedication/Gangsta Grillz Pentalogy", "annotation_id": "2160818", "url": "https://genius.com/2160818", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Still Got That Rock", "line": "I hope my weed ain’t too loud to hear the snakes hiss", "vault_lines": ["I hope my weed ain't too loud to hear the snakes hiss"], "meaning": "Clever wordplay by Wayne.\n\nWhen he says that he is smoking on that “loud”, that means weed he is smoking is really good.\n\nBut he hopes it’s not too loud so he can hear snitches snitching.", "annotation_id": "2160817", "url": "https://genius.com/2160817", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
