{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sticky", "line": "[Intro: Tyler, The Creator]", "vault_lines": ["Poppin' that shit get you hit quick fast (Mink, mink, mink)"], "meaning": "The “hey” chant that is heard sporadically throughout the song resembles the chants that is heard in the background of the song “Noid”.\n\nIn “Sticky”, the chant can be heard throughout the entire song, but it is most noticeable at the start of the song and the sixth verse.\n\nIn “Noid”, the chant can be heard in the background during the second verse.", "annotation_id": "36902153", "url": "https://genius.com/36902153", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sticky", "line": "[Chorus: Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": ["Poppin' that shit get you hit quick fast (Mink, mink, mink)"], "meaning": "Dwayne Michael Carter Jr., known professionally as Lil Wayne, is an American rapper and Grammy Award winner.", "annotation_id": "38467735", "url": "https://genius.com/38467735", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sticky", "line": "Uh, lit-ass bitch, steppin’, I be poppin’ shit", "vault_lines": ["Uh, lit-ass bitch, steppin', I be poppin' shit"], "meaning": "“Steppin'” is a term commonly used in AAVE (African American Vernacular English) to refer to fighting, ‘standing on business’ or just being ready for confrontation.\n\n“I be poppin' shit” implies that GloRilla fights well and wins fights.", "annotation_id": "38467591", "url": "https://genius.com/38467591", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sticky", "line": "Fah-fah-fah-fah, baby girl, I’m finna rock your shit", "vault_lines": ["Fah-fah-fah-fah, baby girl, I'm finna rock your shit"], "meaning": "In rap and in black circles in general, “I’m finna rock your shit” is a common saying. It means something along the lines of “mess you up” in one way or another.", "annotation_id": "38467487", "url": "https://genius.com/38467487", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
