{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Startrax", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-startrax-lyrics", "genius_title": "Startrax", "genius_id": 5108654, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "’Cause I got shooters on the roof like some fucking reindeer", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I got shooters on the roof like some fucking reindeer"], "meaning": "Wayne refers to Santa’s reindeer as a way of describing where his “shooters” (i.e., associates with firearms) can be found. Santa’s reindeer land on the roof of a home so Santa may enter the home’s chimney.\n\nAdditionally, as explained by Professor Kreston Kent on page 40 of The Literary Genius of Lil Wayne (2019), “any noun formed by the suffix ‘-er’ on a verb in the context of reindeers obviously plays on the names of Rudolph’s compatriots (Dasher, Dancer, Prancer, Donner).”\n\nEssentially, Wayne has “shooters” on the roof as if he was Santa and one of his reindeer was named “Shooter.”", "annotation_id": "38500779", "url": "https://genius.com/38500779", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Now I’ma keep a pill and a blunt I might pass the motherfucker but most likely I’ma flunk", "vault_lines": ["I might pass the motherfucker but most likely I'ma flunk"], "meaning": "Here the pun hinges on the word “pass,” which carries a double meaning. In one sense, it refers to the act of sharing a blunt in a traditional manner. However, “pass” is also used in the context of successfully completing a test, with its opposite being “flunk.” Wayne cleverly subverts this academic terminology, implying that while he might share (pass) the blunt, he is more inclined to keep it for himself (flunk). This pun is deepened by the potential metaphorical interpretation of the “pill and a blunt” as symbols of his lyrical talent, suggesting that he possesses unique insights and perspectives that he might choose not to share, thus ‘flunking’ in the conventional sense but excelling in his artistic domain.", "annotation_id": "30621872", "url": "https://genius.com/30621872", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "And we only selling what the boat bring here, nigga", "vault_lines": ["And we only selling what the boat bring here, nigga"], "meaning": "Wayne has a noted history of preferring foreign plugs. In this line he’s saying that he only sells foreign (quality) product.", "annotation_id": "26273328", "url": "https://genius.com/26273328", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Smoke like I fucking disappeared", "vault_lines": ["Smoke like I fucking disappeared"], "meaning": "Magicians often use smoke to blanket themselves while they hide. After the smoke clears, it seems like they disappeared that instant. Smoke appears and they “disappear.”\n\nWayne smokes so much weed, all that smoke can mask him like if he’s going to disappear.", "annotation_id": "13595104", "url": "https://genius.com/13595104", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Started from the bottom now my whole team here, nigga!", "vault_lines": ["Started from the bottom now my whole team here, nigga!"], "meaning": "Wayne is shouting out and referencing the hook of his close friend Drake’s 2013 song “Started From The Bottom”.\n\n> Started from the bottom, now we’re here\nStarted from the bottom, now my whole team fuckin' here\nStarted from the bottom, now we’re here\nStarted from the bottom, now the whole team here, nigga\n\nThis track is a remix of that song so he makes sure to shout out the original.\n\nIn the outro of this track, Wayne samples more lines from the second verse of “Started From The Bottom” but he puts his own twist on them.\n\nWorry bout me. give a fuck about you\nJust as a reminder to myself\nBust every single nut in her motherfucking mouth\n\nThe original lines being\n\nI'ma worry ‘bout me, give a fuck about you\nNigga, just as a reminder to myself\nI wear every single chain, even when I’m in the house", "annotation_id": "13314819", "url": "https://genius.com/13314819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Motherfucker, I’m like Y’all don’t want no problems up in here", "vault_lines": ["Y'all don't want no problems up in here"], "meaning": "Lord knows I’ll murk one of these niggas\n\nWayne is a “krazy” guy and he won’t back down from a fight. Also once through a concert Weezy made clear, that you don’t want no problem with him. http://youtu.be/Dain3zHzQR4?t=1m40s\n\nOr in other words\n\nHe ain’t no killer but don’t push him", "annotation_id": "3380374", "url": "https://genius.com/3380374", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Rather be judged by my jewelry, not a jury of my peers", "vault_lines": ["Rather be judged by my jewelry, not a jury of my peers"], "meaning": "Wayne would rather have people judge him based on his material possessions such as jewelry and chains rather than be literally judged in court by the jury and the prosecutor.\n\n\n\nWayne has had a lot of legal trouble in the past, so it’s no wonder he never wants to go back to court.", "annotation_id": "2600920", "url": "https://genius.com/2600920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Yeah, me, myself and I, the fucking Three Musketeers", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, me, myself and I, the fucking Three Musketeers"], "meaning": "An elaborate way for Wayne to say he only cares about himself.\n\nReference to the 1844 French novel The Three Musketeers.", "annotation_id": "2600899", "url": "https://genius.com/2600899", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Man, dreads hanging out the ski mask", "vault_lines": ["Man, dreads hanging out the ski mask"], "meaning": "Ski masks are often used during robberies, break-ins and other crimes to hide the perpetrators identity.\n\n\n\nThis may be a little more difficult for Wayne however, as his signature dreads would hang out and give people a better idea of who he actually is.", "annotation_id": "2600491", "url": "https://genius.com/2600491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Y’all don’t want no problems up in here Boy, I’m from New Orleans where the dope fiends kill niggas", "vault_lines": ["Y'all don't want no problems up in here"], "meaning": "Wayne is from Hollygrove, a dangerous area of New Orleans where dope fiends are willing to murder anybody in their way to get a fix.", "annotation_id": "2600475", "url": "https://genius.com/2600475", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Tattooed tears for my homies, it’s a cryin’ shame", "vault_lines": ["Tattooed tears for my homies, it's a cryin' shame"], "meaning": "Teardrop tattoos can represent multiple things, however in Wayne’s case, it represents his fallen homies.\n\nWayne has got three teardrop tattoos on his face.", "annotation_id": "2600452", "url": "https://genius.com/2600452", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Uh, lifestyles of the rich and famous", "vault_lines": ["Weezy goes over Drake’s highly popular Started From The Bottom."], "meaning": "Reference to the TV show Lifestyles of the Rich and Famous which aired from 1984 to 1995.\n\nEach week Robin Leach would highlight and report on someone who was rich and famous", "annotation_id": "2249489", "url": "https://genius.com/2249489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "Worry ’bout me, give a fuck about you", "vault_lines": ["Worry 'bout me, give a fuck about you"], "meaning": "This line was inspired by Drake’s original line on his hit Started From the Bottom\n\n“I’m a worry bout me, give a fuck about you”", "annotation_id": "2184309", "url": "https://genius.com/2184309", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Started", "line": "I check your pussy ass, and wait for it to clear, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I check your pussy ass, and wait for it to clear, nigga"], "meaning": "When depositing a check into a financial institution, the funds can take anywhere up to 2 weeks to clear. The bank can withhold funds until they have been paid by the bank whose check is being deposited.\n\n\n\nWayne uses another meaning of check:\n\nThe process by which someone puts another individual in their place verbally or physically either in a joking manner or a serious beatdown\n\n\n\nAfter he puts the pussy in their place, he waits for their ass to clear, or disappear.", "annotation_id": "2182688", "url": "https://genius.com/2182688", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
