{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Staring at the World", "line": "Left leg, right leg, segregation", "vault_lines": ["Left leg, right leg, segregation"], "meaning": "Segregation usually refers to the time in history when white and black people were kept separate from each other in public spaces – aka “separate but equal”, supposedly.\n\n\n\nHowever, Wayne is using the term to refer to his female’s legs, which are separated by Wayne just as the two races were. Same thing, right?", "annotation_id": "1419314", "url": "https://genius.com/1419314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Staring at the World", "line": "Got some makeup on my shirt when she gave me a hug", "vault_lines": ["Got some makeup on my shirt when she gave me a hug"], "meaning": "She must be even lil'er than Lil Wayne, who is 5-foot-6!", "annotation_id": "1419308", "url": "https://genius.com/1419308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Staring at the World", "line": "And she said “Encore”", "vault_lines": ["And she said \"Encore\""], "meaning": "She wants Wayne to work his magic just one more time, like when, after the curtains have closed, an artist comes back on stage for one last song at the end of his or her show.", "annotation_id": "1419231", "url": "https://genius.com/1419231", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Staring at the World", "line": "Who we is? Young Mooolah, baby!", "vault_lines": ["Who we is? Young Mooolah, baby!"], "meaning": "Say what you want about Wayne, but the one thing you can’t say is that he doesn’t rep his team.\n\nYoung Money Entertainment is a record label under the umbrellas of Cash Money Records and Universal Music Group. It was founded by Wayne in 2005, but is now run by Wayne’s labelmate and childhood friend Mack Maine.", "annotation_id": "1419191", "url": "https://genius.com/1419191", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Staring at the World", "line": "Bigg D on the track!", "vault_lines": ["Bigg D on the track!"], "meaning": "Bigg D is an up-and-coming music producer based in Miami, where Wayne currently lives. He also produced Best Rapper Alive on Tha Carter II, Jay-Z & Wayne’s Hello Brooklyn 2.0, and quite a few other hits.", "annotation_id": "1419159", "url": "https://genius.com/1419159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Staring at the World", "line": "I fuck her till she whine and then I drink a tall glass", "vault_lines": ["I fuck her till she whine and then I drink a tall glass"], "meaning": "Wayne uses a clever play on words (whine / wine) to refer both to the noises he’s making his girl produce and the drink he will sip thereafter.", "annotation_id": "1418250", "url": "https://genius.com/1418250", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Staring at the World", "line": "Pop that pussy like a cork and I’mma fuck you till you whine", "vault_lines": ["Pop that pussy like a cork and I'mma fuck you till you whine"], "meaning": "Coming back to that same homophone in the last line of the first verse (it was so good he had to use it twice in the same song), Wayne uses the same play on words (whine / wine), which he relates to a wine cork in this line.", "annotation_id": "1418247", "url": "https://genius.com/1418247", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Staring at the World", "line": "Remember me like this one time at band camp, yeah!", "vault_lines": ["Remember me like this one time at band camp, yeah!"], "meaning": "A reference to a classic repeated line in the hit movie American Pie.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uYWQAg12Ko0", "annotation_id": "1418244", "url": "https://genius.com/1418244", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
