{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SportsCenter Theme Remix", "line": "LA Laker fan,", "vault_lines": ["Okay, I don't, I don't give a football about what ya'll"], "meaning": "Just as wayne is a fan of the Packers for football, the LA Lakers is his basketball team of choice", "annotation_id": "4935561", "url": "https://genius.com/4935561", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SportsCenter Theme Remix", "line": "They say I’m taking over, I’m like where do I start at", "vault_lines": ["They say I'm taking over, I'm like where do I start at"], "meaning": "For a day ESPN asked Wayne to feature for an interview and highlight broadcasting. They said he could take over, willingly he did what he could.", "annotation_id": "4681533", "url": "https://genius.com/4681533", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SportsCenter Theme Remix", "line": "Live on TV, mama told me wear a dress shirt Instead I wore a t-shirt, Michael Jordan sneakers", "vault_lines": ["Live on TV, mama told me wear a dress shirt"], "meaning": "When you’re live on TV, you’re expected to dress nicely – usually in Sunday best.\n\nWayne disregards this expectation and instead dresses casually to his SportsCenter feature, but he does know how to clean up when it’s absolutely necessary.\n\n\n\n(Wayne on far right)", "annotation_id": "3927382", "url": "https://genius.com/3927382", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SportsCenter Theme Remix", "line": "I still think I’m fly, show me where the tarmac", "vault_lines": ["I still think I'm fly, show me where the tarmac"], "meaning": "“Tarmac” is another term for the airport apron, where planes at an airport are parked before being boarded. Note the correlation between the word fly, and the tarmac. Wayne references the tarmac to emphasize how fly he still is, and that he can be in style whenever he wants.\n\nWeezy could also be referencing how fly his outfit was on SportsCenter since he talks about the outfit in the lines above this one.\n\nInstead I wore a t-shirt, Michael Jordan sneakers\nRed Sox ballcap my dreadlocks fall back\n\n Despite being in the rap game since 14 years old, Weezy has managed to keep himself in style.", "annotation_id": "3916473", "url": "https://genius.com/3916473", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SportsCenter Theme Remix", "line": "Red Sox ballcap my dreadlocks fall back", "vault_lines": ["Red Sox ballcap my dreadlocks fall back"], "meaning": "Wayne admitted he was a Red Sox fan in a video he created for his fans a few years ago:\n\nI have my teams. I’m not sure if you can tell, but I’m a Green Bay Packers fan, I’m an LA Lakers fan, I’m a Boston Red Sox fan, I’m a Washington Capitals fan.\n\n\n\n(Tune with David Ortiz, the Red Sox DH)", "annotation_id": "3916465", "url": "https://genius.com/3916465", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SportsCenter Theme Remix", "line": "Yeah, entertainment sports on your network I love top 10 plays, yessir, best work", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, entertainment sports on your network"], "meaning": "ESPN, the channel that broadcasts SportsCenter, stands for “Entertainment and Sports Programming Network”.\n\nWayne’s giving a nod to that as well as the famous SportsCenter Top 10, a daily recap of the day’s best plays.\n\n\n\n“Best work” may also be referring to Wayne’s own career. We need to get a Weezy verified account so he can let us know what his personal Top 10 is!", "annotation_id": "3916435", "url": "https://genius.com/3916435", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SportsCenter Theme Remix", "line": "Let’s give Drake a hand For costing the Toronto Raptors 25 grand, I’m gone", "vault_lines": ["let's give Drake a hand"], "meaning": "During Drake’s fifth annual OVO Fest held in Toronto, Drake was accused and fined $25,000 by the NBA for violating their anti-tampering rules. With Kevin Durant in attendance, Drake gave him a shoutout and asked the crowd to show the MVP some love.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ECk4v7pSsZs\nDurant will be an unrestricted free agent in the summer of 2016, so a possible team he may go to could be the Toronto Raptors. But since Drake is now a team ambassador for them, he’s not allowed to interact with players in that manner and got fined.", "annotation_id": "3916055", "url": "https://genius.com/3916055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SportsCenter Theme Remix", "line": "Green Bay Packer but New Orleans where my heart at", "vault_lines": ["Green Bay Packer but New Orleans where my heart at"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is a Green Bay Packers fan. He even made a song called “Green and Yellow” to show his love for the team. But Wayne was born in the Hollygrove section of New Orleans, so he will always have a spot in his heart for the NO.\n\n\n\nhttp://rap.genius.com/36942", "annotation_id": "3915983", "url": "https://genius.com/3915983", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
