{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spitter", "line": "I been ready since eighty-one, and I was born in eighty-two", "vault_lines": ["I been ready since eighty-one, and I was born in eighty-two"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne was born September 27th, 1982. so he’s saying he has been ready before he was even born", "annotation_id": "27975064", "url": "https://genius.com/27975064", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spitter", "line": "Quarterback Weezy, baby: Shotgun, run, and shoot", "vault_lines": ["Quarterback Weezy, baby: Shotgun, run, and shoot"], "meaning": "In football, the “shotgun” is an offensive formation in which the quarterback takes the snap between four and seven yards back from the line of scrimmage rather than directly behind the center.\n\n\n\nWhile the shotgun formation is generally used for passing plays, Quarterback Weezy has a different shotgun in mind for his own play call of “run and shoot.”", "annotation_id": "14072203", "url": "https://genius.com/14072203", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spitter", "line": "Told you I’d be back—I’m comin’; I got that Tommy La-soda (Oh!)", "vault_lines": ["Told you I'd be back—I'm comin'; I got that Tommy La-soda (Oh!)"], "meaning": "Here in Verse 1, Weezy references his “Tommy gun” – i.e., a Thompson submachine gun, which became the signature weapon of both law enforcement and organized crime during Prohibition – by invoking famous L. A. Dodgers manager (1976-1996) Tommy Lasorda. He’ll name drop a different “Tommy” in the same context in Verse 2.", "annotation_id": "14072135", "url": "https://genius.com/14072135", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spitter", "line": "I told you I’m coming back—I got that Tommy Mottola", "vault_lines": ["I told you I'm coming back—I got that Tommy Mottola"], "meaning": "“Tommy gun” is a common informal name for the Thompson submachine gun commonly seen the in hands of members in organized crime gangs.\n\nTommy Mottola is an Italian-American music executive with rumored mob ties.", "annotation_id": "13000800", "url": "https://genius.com/13000800", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spitter", "line": "Spit yo’ game, talk yo’ shit (Big shout to Philly) Grab yo’ gat— (Yeah) Spit yo’ game, talk yo’ shit (Shout to everybody down in The Bottom) Grab yo’ gat— (Boo in here! Fee! Bridgewater, I see you) Spit yo game, talk yo’ shit (Shout to G-Town!) Grab yo’ gat, call yo’ clique (Spitta, Mack, Ju’, baby) Spit yo’ game, talk yo’ shit Grab yo’ gat, call your clique (Yeah! Can’t forget The Hollow!) Squeeze yo’ clip, hit the right one (Yeah) Pass the weed, I got to light one", "vault_lines": ["Spit yo' game, talk yo' shit (Big shout to Philly)"], "meaning": "This portion of the hook is sampled/interpolated from “Notorious Thugs” by The Notorious B.I.G., featuring Bone Thugs-n-Harmony.\n\nSpit your game, talk your shit\nGrab your gat, call your clique\nSqueeze your clip, hit the right one\nPass that weed, I got to light one\n\nYou can listen to the original below:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tfxvgi0i1nc", "annotation_id": "3133255", "url": "https://genius.com/3133255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spitter", "line": "Take that money from that bitch—she know what it be: M-O-B", "vault_lines": ["Take that money from that bitch—she know what it be: M-O-B"], "meaning": "M.O.B. stands for “Money Over Bitches”.\n\nWayne’s got a tattoo of it on his chest:\n\n\n\nWayne just loves using this line in his songs.", "annotation_id": "2597780", "url": "https://genius.com/2597780", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spitter", "line": "I’m in them S. Dots: That’s blood all over my Hovas—fuck!", "vault_lines": ["I'm in them S. Dots: That's blood all over my Hovas—fuck!"], "meaning": "Wayne is wearing Jay-Z’s S. Carter Reeboks; so when he shoots somebody he gets blood all over them.\n\n\n\nHova is simply another nickname for Jay.", "annotation_id": "2597774", "url": "https://genius.com/2597774", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
