{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spit In Your Face", "line": "And crazy’s what they’re calling me But crazy isn’t hardly what I am Try creatively retarded, I’m amazingly rewarded", "vault_lines": ["And crazy’s what they're calling me"], "meaning": "Wayne’s has always been stereotyped as a drugged out rapper who’s considered a little crazy too. Here, he’s not actually denying it, but confirming that he’s simply MORE than crazy.\n\n“Creatively retarded” -means his creatively is so good it’s “stupid”, he’s “stupid good”\n\namazingly rewarded-just a way of saying that he’s very grateful for what he has.", "annotation_id": "6521899", "url": "https://genius.com/6521899", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spit In Your Face", "line": "Young Tune", "vault_lines": ["This song was supposed to be on Lil Wayne’s Rebirth album but was eventually cut."], "meaning": "“Tune” is one of Lil Wayne’s nicknames, his grandmother gave it to him.", "annotation_id": "4155588", "url": "https://genius.com/4155588", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spit In Your Face", "line": "Uh, straight off the bat I come straight off my back with a gun like I’m in Iraq", "vault_lines": ["Uh, straight off the bat"], "meaning": "“Straight off the bat” is an idiom meaning first thing, or immediately. Wayne starts his verse off the only way he knows how, rapping like bullets whizzing past in a war zone. Think of something like Arnold Schwarzenegger.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6bTMQNIh4wA", "annotation_id": "4142654", "url": "https://genius.com/4142654", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Spit In Your Face", "line": "And I do whatever for the root of all evil", "vault_lines": ["And I do whatever for the root of all evil"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne does whatever he can for money which is “the root of all evil”, a misquote from 1 Timothy 6:10 which actually says “The love of money is a root of all kinds of evil.”", "annotation_id": "276233", "url": "https://genius.com/276233", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
