{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "South Muzik", "line": "Know he told the dealer, “Make sure there’s no equivalent” So that makes this a one-of-one That mean: none before it, none to come", "vault_lines": ["Sure he did, no kiddin', know he kitted it"], "meaning": "Limited editions of artworks, books, etc., are frequently numbered so as to indicate both the total number of items in the series and the particular number of each item within it; e.g., “25/100” or “Copy 69 of 100.”\n\n\n\nTunechi made sure to have his new Bentley tricked out is such a way as to make it unique (“one of one” – or 1/1) and unmatched.", "annotation_id": "14057328", "url": "https://genius.com/14057328", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "South Muzik", "line": "See, we did the first “Dedication” before disaster", "vault_lines": ["See, we did the first \"Dedication\" before disaster"], "meaning": "Though the first Dedication mixtape wasn’t released until December 2005, its tracks had been recorded earlier. The disaster in question was Hurricane Katrina, which struck New Orleans in August 2005. (Dedication 2 was released in September 2006.)", "annotation_id": "14053753", "url": "https://genius.com/14053753", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "South Muzik", "line": "I run better, like Corey Dillon for the New England Pats", "vault_lines": ["I run better, like Corey Dillon for the New England Pats"], "meaning": "Corey James Dillon (born October 24, 1974) is a former American football running back. He played his ten-season career for the Cincinnati Bengals and the New England Patriots, wearing jersey number 28 for both teams. Dillon played college football the University of Washington where he wore the number 4.", "annotation_id": "759448", "url": "https://genius.com/759448", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "South Muzik", "line": "That Desert Eagle ”New Workout Plan”: brain, then tummy", "vault_lines": ["That Desert Eagle \"New Workout Plan\": brain, then tummy"], "meaning": "The ‘workout plan’ for his gun is just where he’s going to shoot you. In the head and stomach, kind of like working out you’d work out your thighs and tummy or something.", "annotation_id": "306899", "url": "https://genius.com/306899", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "South Muzik", "line": "I call it “three the hard way,”", "vault_lines": ["I call it \"three the hard way,\""], "meaning": "Three the hard way is a basketball term for getting three points by getting fouled on a two, making it and making the free throw. It’s a play on ‘hard’ obviously, like his dick because he’s fuckin two girls.", "annotation_id": "306895", "url": "https://genius.com/306895", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
