{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Survivor", "line": "211 187, I’m on a mission", "vault_lines": ["211 187, I'm on a mission"], "meaning": "These are police codes, signifying what type of mission Wayne is on.\n\n211 = robbery\n187 = murder", "annotation_id": "35440943", "url": "https://genius.com/35440943", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Survivor", "line": "Mother fuck whoever higher, but I gotta get mine This time I’m going for the big climb And the boy about to incline, Jigga man I’m nearby", "vault_lines": ["Mother fuck whoever higher, but I gotta get mine"], "meaning": "It was around this time that Wayne began laying claims to the title of best rapper alive. And seeing as the Jigga Man had that title on lock at the time, that meant Wayne would have to go through him. To do so, Wayne put out a lot of quality music between 2005’s Tha Carter II and 2008’s Tha Carter III, which resulted in Hov eventually passing the torch to him on “Mr. Carter”.", "annotation_id": "3289423", "url": "https://genius.com/3289423", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Survivor", "line": "You’ll probably catch me and Weezy Baby on South Beach", "vault_lines": ["You'll probably catch me and Weezy Baby on South Beach"], "meaning": "In 2005 Lil Wayne moved to Miami, so he and the Young Money family spend alot of time on South Beach.", "annotation_id": "2993901", "url": "https://genius.com/2993901", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Survivor", "line": "Young Maine, Young Money, Cash Money, Fast Money", "vault_lines": ["Young Maine, Young Money, Cash Money, Fast Money"], "meaning": "Mack Maine was one of the first people to sign to Young Money with Curren$y in 2005.", "annotation_id": "2991030", "url": "https://genius.com/2991030", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Survivor", "line": "Chopper that I’m toting make me feel like Deebo", "vault_lines": ["Chopper that I'm toting make me feel like Deebo"], "meaning": "The weapon that Wayne is carrying makes him feel as intimidating as the hulking Deebo from the movie Friday, even though Wayne is only 5'6\".", "annotation_id": "1771032", "url": "https://genius.com/1771032", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Survivor", "line": "See all these new rappers got me missin’ Biggie and Pac", "vault_lines": ["See all these new rappers got me missin' Biggie and Pac"], "meaning": "The Notorious B.I.G. and 2Pac are considered two of the best to ever grab hold of a mic. The two were very close friends, but their friendship turned into quite the rivalry.\n\n\n\nA lot of rappers feel the same way as Mack Maine does, a lot of new rappers disgust hip-hod heads, and that makes them wish for the legends back, like Biggie and Pac.\n\nAs much as I and most others respect Big and Pac, this is a common message that people would like to send to people like Mack (people wishing for Biggie and Pac to come back):", "annotation_id": "1704510", "url": "https://genius.com/1704510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Survivor", "line": "Uptown his town, Hollygrove hizzound", "vault_lines": ["Uptown his town, Hollygrove hizzound"], "meaning": "Wayne is a “dog” (hizzound is a Snoopified version of hound) hailing from Hollygrove, New Orleans. Hollygrove is in the 17th Ward of NO which is considered uptown.", "annotation_id": "1697391", "url": "https://genius.com/1697391", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Survivor", "line": "Fuck with the little man, you will never get found", "vault_lines": ["Fuck with the little man, you will never get found"], "meaning": "Wayne’s a short dude – 5'6\" to be exact. But he has a crew full of enforcers that will guarantee the police never find your body after they kill you for coming at Weezy.\n\n\n\nWayne getting towered over by Hov", "annotation_id": "1697349", "url": "https://genius.com/1697349", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Survivor", "line": "Little ass niggas, stand tall like I’m 6'9\"", "vault_lines": ["Little ass niggas, stand tall like I'm 6'9\""], "meaning": "He’s saying that y'all are little ass niggas, and he stands like he’s 6'9\" tall. He’s explaining how small you are compared to him. Keep in mind Lil Wayne is 5'6\" tall", "annotation_id": "1697308", "url": "https://genius.com/1697308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Survivor", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-soul-survivor-lyrics", "genius_title": "Soul Survivor", "genius_id": 143161, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Child", "line": "New Orleans love me like Miami love Udonis", "vault_lines": ["New Orleans love me like Miami love Udonis"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne was born and raised in New Orleans, Louisiana. After making a name for himself as one of the biggest and rappers in the 2000s to 2010s era, his hometown began to acknowledge Wayne as a legend, and even gave the rapper his own day, as well as the keyes to the city of New Orleans. Additionally, fans idolize and love the rapper so much that there are even murals of the rapper scattered across the city.\n\n\n\n One of the most popular murals of Lil Wayne in the city of New Orleans, it’s located on Olive St, New Orleans.\n\nSimilarly, Wayne compares the love his city offers him to that of former Miami Heat basketball player, Udonis Haslem, who spent the entirety of his 20 seasons with the Heat. He is one of the three most longest tenured players to ever play for a singular team without getting traded. Due to this; fans and even the city of Miami revered the basketball player as a legend for the city, with even the team even giving Haslem his own Section 305 at the Miami Heat’s arena as part of his season-ending.. Additionally, during his last dance with his team, he dropped 24 points solidifying his legend status with the team.\n\n\n\nThe former NBA player even had his own documentary, which was dubbed, “The Asylum”. It released in 2022 and is one hour and 50 minutes long.", "annotation_id": "36471885", "url": "https://genius.com/36471885", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Child", "line": "Been a pro since a kid like the young Luka Dončić", "vault_lines": ["Been a pro since a kid like the young Luka Dončić"], "meaning": "Luka Dončič, is a professional basketball player for the Los Angeles Lakers.\n\n\n\nLuka began playing professional for the Real Madrid youth league at 13. Three years later, he then played basketball for Real Madrid in the Liga ACB at the age of 16 making him one of the youngest professional players in club history.\n\nSimilarly, Lil Wayne experienced the same rise as the generational hooper. Wayne started his rapping career at just the ripe age of eight, but three year slater, at just the age of 11, Lil Wayne signed a record deal with Cash Money Records. After signing his first deal, Wayne became the youngest signed rapper ever within the music industry. Similarly to how Luka became the youngest professional basketball player ever for Real Madrid.", "annotation_id": "36470961", "url": "https://genius.com/36470961", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Soul Child", "line": "The world cray", "vault_lines": ["Can't be the hottest in the city, I'm tryna take over the whole fuckin' world"], "meaning": "“The world, Craig”\nLil Wayne starts off his verse emphasizing the last line of Bleu’s verse with a quote from the movie “Friday After Next.” Wayne has also used this quote in a 2014 Interview at SXSW: (0:24)\nhttps://youtu.be/ZCLClOXHfQM\n\nUpdate 12/26/2022\nYung Bleu also confirms this lyric via an Instagram post:\nhttps://www.instagram.com/reel/CmpG-KCMqDd/?igshid=NTdlMDg3MTY=", "annotation_id": "27114745", "url": "https://genius.com/27114745", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
