{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "And the coupe transform, no Tyrese", "vault_lines": ["And the coupe transform, no Tyrese"], "meaning": "“Ejecto Seat-O Cuz”\n\nSorry 4 The 2 Fast 2 Furious Wait\n\nShout out to Tyrese Gibson\n\n#PocketsAintEmptyCuh\n#DontWorryAboutItCuh", "annotation_id": "33104966", "url": "https://genius.com/33104966", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "Yeah, Weezy go hard like Cialis", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, Weezy go hard like Cialis"], "meaning": "Cialis treats erectile dysfunction and high blood pressure in the lungs. In this case he is meaning that he’s going hard just like Cialis would do for erectile dysfunction", "annotation_id": "31644733", "url": "https://genius.com/31644733", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "And I just bought your girlfriend some kneepads, nigga Ha,", "vault_lines": ["And I just bought your girlfriend some kneepads, nigga"], "meaning": "Lil Wyane is a skater, he is taking YOUR girl skating with him. He also values safety as a result he purchases her a pair of knee pads in case she falls. While she’s down there she also may suck his d*ck, the knee pads would help.", "annotation_id": "29221385", "url": "https://genius.com/29221385", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "And then I gotta split, sorry, baby, sour grapes She whine, “Baby, don’t leave”", "vault_lines": ["And then I gotta split, sorry, baby, sour grapes"], "meaning": "A play on words between “sour grapes” and “whine”/wine, since grapes are used to make wine", "annotation_id": "18647994", "url": "https://genius.com/18647994", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "Tune gon’ ball, money tall, Paul Bunyan", "vault_lines": ["Tune gon' ball, money tall, Paul Bunyan"], "meaning": "Paul Bunyan is a legendary character in United States folklore, known to many as a giant lumberjack who symbolizes strength, toughness, and largeness in size. Bunyan became one of the most well-known tall-tales of the frontier era during the early 20th century. The original story of Paul Bunyan describes him wandering the Western US creating valleys, canyons, and other natural landforms.\n\n\n\nLil Wayne is saying that his money, when stacked together, rises to very tall heights because of his wealth. In 2011, Wayne had an estimated net worth of $32 million.", "annotation_id": "17989988", "url": "https://genius.com/17989988", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "And I reach for the stars, got stuck in the clouds", "vault_lines": ["And I reach for the stars, got stuck in the clouds"], "meaning": "Shooting For The Stars\n\nIn this lyric, Wayne writes about having high goals, therefore he is “reaching for the stars”, which is a high goal when it comes to altitude. But every journey goes through bumps and obstacles, in this case, the obstacles stopping him from reaching his goals are the clouds.", "annotation_id": "3034102", "url": "https://genius.com/3034102", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "Sorry 4 the Wait, man Album coming August 29th, though Tez made me do this song", "vault_lines": ["Sorry 4 the Wait, man"], "meaning": "Wayne’s much anticipated album, Tha Carter IV, suffered from multiple delays in the lead up to its release. The album was originally slated to drop on May 16th, then it was pushed back to June 21st, before it finally dropped on August 29th, 2011.\n\nCortez “Tez” Bryant is Lil Wayne’s longtime manager.", "annotation_id": "423770", "url": "https://genius.com/423770", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "I hit it from the back and make that bitch about-face", "vault_lines": ["I hit it from the back and make that bitch about-face"], "meaning": "To “hit it from the back” means to have sex in the doggy style position, and “about face” is a drill command used in the military in which the soldier makes a 180 degree turn.\n\n\n\n“Face” is also a slang term for receiving fellatio. Weezy implies that after he “hits it from the back”, he has her turn around and perform fellatio on him.", "annotation_id": "299102", "url": "https://genius.com/299102", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "Jumpin’ in the game, better read the rules", "vault_lines": ["Jumpin' in the game, better read the rules"], "meaning": "If you’re gonna come into rap, you better know what the fuck’s good", "annotation_id": "294794", "url": "https://genius.com/294794", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "Yeah, I was locked up, but like a bird, I’m free", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I was locked up, but like a bird, I'm free"], "meaning": "On July 22nd of 2007, Wayne was arrested after seen smoking weed with another man outside of his tour bus, he ended up being charged with possession of marijuana and a .40 caliber pistol.\n\nWayne was in jail from March 8th, 2010 – November 4th", "annotation_id": "281457", "url": "https://genius.com/281457", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "Eagle Street, where the real niggas hung", "vault_lines": ["Eagle Street, where the real niggas hung"], "meaning": "“Eagle street” is a street in the neighborhood of Hollygrove, the 17th ward in New Orleans, which Wayne is from.\n\nWayne has also mentioned Eagle street in La La La\n\nWayne even has a tattoo on his stomach that reads “Apple Eagle”\n\n\n\nCan be seen beside the “7” on Wayne’s stomach", "annotation_id": "279573", "url": "https://genius.com/279573", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "Ain’t nobody fuckin’ with me First-degree murder, you can get your degree, motherfucker", "vault_lines": ["Ain't nobody fuckin' with me"], "meaning": "A play on words of “first degree murder” and an educational degree. Paired with the previous line, he is suggesting that if you fuck with him, he is going to kill you.\n\nSpeaking of first degree murder, Flow (who is featured on this mixtape and is a close friend of Wayne’s) was arrested for first degree murder, as well as two counts of armed robbery.", "annotation_id": "277601", "url": "https://genius.com/277601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "And they can’t blindfold what my third eye see", "vault_lines": ["And they can't blindfold what my third eye see"], "meaning": "The third eye is a mystical and esoteric concept referring to inner realms and spaces of higher consciousness. Many say their third eye is opened after taking psychedelics such as mushrooms or LSD. Lil Wayne is using his third eye (a metaphorical eye) to view the world even if his other two are blind-folded.", "annotation_id": "277560", "url": "https://genius.com/277560", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sorry 4 the Wait", "line": "This shit is magic: Stan Van Gundy", "vault_lines": ["This shit is magic: Stan Van Gundy"], "meaning": "Stan Van Gundy used to be the head coach for the Orlando Magic.\n\n\n\n“This shit being magic” refers to the money/power he has at his disposal. They let him do ANYTHING he wants.", "annotation_id": "277465", "url": "https://genius.com/277465", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
