{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "I was her gangsta, she was my shoulder", "vault_lines": ["I was her gangsta, she was my shoulder"], "meaning": "Weezy has a tough side and a soft side.  He is a gangsta but he also needs a shoulder to cry on.", "annotation_id": "17896111", "url": "https://genius.com/17896111", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "Give me another chance I’m needin’ it like a kidney", "vault_lines": ["I'm needin' it like a kidney"], "meaning": "Most people are born with two kidneys as the functional components of what is called the renal system. In case you’ve lost a kidney, you can live with the another. Kidneys are so important in your body, for regulating the water in your body, or removing the wastes.\n\nNivea is as important for his life as his kidney, so apparently he can’t live without her.\n\nLil Wayne needs another chance to have her in his life, similarly to how life would give you another chance when you lose a kidney.", "annotation_id": "3144044", "url": "https://genius.com/3144044", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "And let me say: Please don’t worry ’bout the women I have been with No engagement can amount to your friendship", "vault_lines": ["Please don't worry 'bout the women I have been with"], "meaning": "After their relationship began to sour, rumors began surfacing that Lil Wayne had been seeing other women; some possibly during the time he was with Nivea.\nThese women include author Karrine Steffans, singer Solange Knowles, and rapper Katrina “Trina”, who he was briefly engaged to.", "annotation_id": "3143946", "url": "https://genius.com/3143946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "What she mean to me is what I mean to rap", "vault_lines": ["What she mean to me is what I mean to rap"], "meaning": "Lil Weezy is an extremely influential artist in the rap game. Dozens of rappers have cited Tunechi as an inspiration to their music, he’s signed dozens of rappers to his record label, and you can sense his influence in tons of other artists that may have not cited him as an influence.\n\nThis line also acts as a double entendre as Wayne “means to rap” about how much this woman “means to [him]”. He’s both espousing his heart and showing he’s Hip Hop’s heart.\n\nCheck out artists praising Weezy here!\n\nOf course he ties this metaphor into his love for his woman.", "annotation_id": "3013767", "url": "https://genius.com/3013767", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "[Hook] I’ve been lonely, I’ve been waiting for you I’m pretending, and that’s all I can do That’s all I can do mama The love I’m sending An’t making it through to your heart I hope you hear me", "vault_lines": ["I've been lonely, I've been waiting for you"], "meaning": "The hooks (and the core of the beat) come from “What About Love?” (1985) by Heart.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KE5GGMhmo-M", "annotation_id": "992436", "url": "https://genius.com/992436", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "And I hope that nigga know he got a queen And all I can do is dream", "vault_lines": ["I'm pretending, and that's all I can do"], "meaning": "Wayne and Nivea had an on-again, off-again relationship. After breaking up for the last time, Nivea met and began dating and eventually marrying music producer Terius “The Dream” Nash in 2004.\n\nThis last line is Wayne’s subtle acknowledgement of Nivea’s new relationship.", "annotation_id": "271779", "url": "https://genius.com/271779", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "I remember everything, I just wanna hear you sing", "vault_lines": ["I remember everything, I just wanna hear you sing"], "meaning": "Nivea is an R&B singer known for hit songs such as “Don’t Mess With My Man” and “Laundromat”.", "annotation_id": "271774", "url": "https://genius.com/271774", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "Pain! Since I’ve lost you, I’m lost too Nigga feelin’ like he at the bottom like a horseshoe", "vault_lines": ["Pain! Since I've lost you, I'm lost too"], "meaning": "Getting dumped feels like horses are trampling you to death.\n\n\n\nThis song has been rumored to be based on Wayne’s on-again, off-again relationship with R&B singer Nivea B. Nash.\n\nThe two were briefly engaged before separating for good, leading Nivea to meet and marry her now ex-husband Terius “The-Dream” Nash.", "annotation_id": "113559", "url": "https://genius.com/113559", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "Ma, you even went and got a teardrop like me", "vault_lines": ["Ma, you even went and got a teardrop like me"], "meaning": "Nivea, the woman this song is about, also has a teardrop tattoo.\n\n\n\nAccording to The Guardian, Wayne’s teardrop tats signify the death of friends.", "annotation_id": "94064", "url": "https://genius.com/94064", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "But I hope you haven’t forgot about me— Up in the living room, watchin’ SportsCenter", "vault_lines": ["You forgot about the house, you forgot about the ring"], "meaning": "Tunechi loves sports so much that he even hosted his own little sports show from his own house, called “Weezy’s Sports Corner.”", "annotation_id": "88472", "url": "https://genius.com/88472", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Something You Forgot", "line": "See, take away my title, take away my stripes You give me back my girl, and you give me back my life Give me back my girl, and you give me back my life", "vault_lines": ["See, take away my title, take away my stripes"], "meaning": "Stripes is a reference to the tear drop tattoo Lil Wayne has under his eyes.\n\nEven if you take away all of Wayne’s money and fame, if Nivea went back to him he would be great, because he considers her as his life.", "annotation_id": "88470", "url": "https://genius.com/88470", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
