{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "So Dedicated", "line": "She tell me, Tunechi, hit it raw, I tell her bitch you crazy Don’t want no HIV, don’t need that Honeymoon In Vegas", "vault_lines": ["She tell me, Tunechi, hit it raw, I tell her bitch you crazy"], "meaning": "He is using HIV as an abbreviation for Honeymoon In Vegas, a 90’s movie starring Nicholas Cage. A honeymoon would imply a marriage, something Wayne isn’t keen on.", "annotation_id": "1042861", "url": "https://genius.com/1042861", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "So Dedicated", "line": "Alright, let’s put it in perspective See 1, 1 makes you realize 2, that’s when the game became ours See 3, that’s when we showed you the future This here, it’s for the sport Some of you niggas mad the sport currently happens to be skateboarding But that gives us 4 wheels to roll over you niggas D4, and dedication!", "vault_lines": ["Alright, let's put it in perspective"], "meaning": "DJ Drama is going chronologically through each Dedication mixtape\n\n\n\nDedication 1 : An eye-opener, was what made you realize Wayne was the real deal\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDedication 2 : Was around the time Wayne had completely taken over the mixtape game and was murdering beats left and right\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDedication 3 : “that’s when we showed you the future” Dedication 3 was a mixtape showcasing the YM Crew and putting them out in the spotlight\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDedication 4 : “this here is for the sport” (Skateboarding), another showcase. Drama is letting you know that this mixtape is putting Wayne’s Skate line “Trukfit” out in the spotlight. Mad about skateboarding? Dedication 4 = 4 wheels to roll over the haters.", "annotation_id": "1041707", "url": "https://genius.com/1041707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "So Dedicated", "line": "The presidential double R, call that Ronald Reagan", "vault_lines": ["The presidential double R, call that Ronald Reagan"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is riding a Rolls Royce since his legendary album The Carter II. Right-wing politician and proponent of “trickle down” economics Ronald Reagan would have appreciated Lil' Wayne, both for his open celebration of wealth and success, and because he would have given Reagan the opportunity to go around scaring white people by telling them that without “law and order” conservatism every black man in America would be as dangerous as Lil' Wayne.\n\nA strapping young buck indeed", "annotation_id": "1041124", "url": "https://genius.com/1041124", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "So Dedicated", "line": "It’s YMCMB the fucking alpha and omega", "vault_lines": ["It's YMCMB the fucking alpha and omega"], "meaning": "Alpha (α or Α) and Omega (ω or Ω) are the first and last letters of the Greek alphabet. They represent “Christ” or “God” in the book of Revalation. Source\n\nChrist is described as the Alpha and Omega to signify that he is the Beginning and the End, He is all-encompassing and omni-present.\n\nWayne is saying his “Young Money Cash Money Billionaires” are on that status: on top of the world, the best label around.", "annotation_id": "1040206", "url": "https://genius.com/1040206", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "So Dedicated", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-so-dedicated-lyrics", "genius_title": "So Dedicated", "genius_id": 87077, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Snitch", "line": "Can’t no loose lips get on my yacht", "vault_lines": ["Can't no loose lips get on my yacht"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying that anyone invited onto his yacht needs to stay quiet afterward. He does not want people leaving and talking about what they saw or did while they were there.", "annotation_id": "29711201", "url": "https://genius.com/29711201", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Snitch", "line": "Real niggas takin’ falls like Niagara", "vault_lines": ["Real niggas takin' falls like Niagara"], "meaning": "Through the song Wayne criticizes friends who turn on each other and snitch on their partners upon incarceration aka “Snitches”. Real hustlers go down and serve their time without snitching. Niagra of course is a reference to the “Niagra Falls” which separates the U.S from Canada and have a total height of 167 ft.", "annotation_id": "3923813", "url": "https://genius.com/3923813", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Snitch", "line": "It ain’t no secret, I’m hotter than ether", "vault_lines": ["It ain't no secret, I'm hotter than ether"], "meaning": "Double meaning here :\n\n\n“Ether” is volatile liquid that is highly flammable. It is used as an anesthetic and as a solvent or intermediate in industrial processes.\n“Ether” was also a famous song by rapper Nas from his 2001 album “Stillmatic”; a response to Jay Z’s “The Takeover” (a diss song aimed at Nas), the song was very well received and Nas was dictated by many as the winner of the feud.", "annotation_id": "3923786", "url": "https://genius.com/3923786", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Snitch", "line": "Make no mistake, I’m a veteran at", "vault_lines": ["Make no mistake, I'm a veteran at"], "meaning": "Although being very young at the time (22 years old), Wayne had already been at the rap scene for years as “Get it how You Live!”, his group “The Hot Boyz” debut album was released in 1997 when he was only 15. At the time this album was released he was 7 years deep in the game and feeling like a veteran already.", "annotation_id": "3923753", "url": "https://genius.com/3923753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Snitch", "line": "Real-nigga shit, motherfucker, I’m Tune", "vault_lines": ["Real-nigga shit, motherfucker, I'm Tune"], "meaning": "Tune is the nickname Wayne’s grandmother gave him. Eventually this evolves into “Tunechi” combining “Tune” with “Gucci”, then eventually to “Lil Tunechi” which is where it is today", "annotation_id": "2160340", "url": "https://genius.com/2160340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
