{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Small Thing to a Giant", "line": "I’m a predator, when I prey I don’t mean meditation I mean vegetation, fuck the Feds and fuck the federation And every agent.", "vault_lines": ["I'm a predator, when I prey I don't mean meditation"], "meaning": "Lest you confuse him for a man of inaction, Wayne clarifies: he preys (not prays) on vegetation (“plants”) – federal authorities, the federal government itself and any other agent of the system", "annotation_id": "15052", "url": "https://genius.com/15052", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Small Thing to a Giant", "line": "Guess what? Streets off paper And me I’m praying for probation Like my ancestors prayed for segregation", "vault_lines": ["Guess what? Streets off paper"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne wrote this verse while awaiting sentencing for a weapons conviction. His opening line is sarcastically optimistic – “Guess What? There is a lot of money (\"paper”) to be made right now\"\n\nUnfortunately he’s caught up praying that he gets probation instead of jail time, a situation comparable to slaves praying for Jim crow style oppression – a bad, but better situation\n\nOR – is it “Streets OFF Paper”, as in his friend T-streets is off papers (probation)? Meanwhile, Wayne is begging for the papers because he was trying to avoid jail time..", "annotation_id": "15051", "url": "https://genius.com/15051", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Small Thing to a Giant", "line": "Take all his money then I take a shit on him", "vault_lines": ["Take all his money then I take a shit on him"], "meaning": "After the 1969 Woody Allen classic Take The Money and A Shit on Him\n\n“I have a Gudda Gudda”", "annotation_id": "15039", "url": "https://genius.com/15039", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Small Thing to a Giant", "line": "I’m serving niggas like my name was Pete Sampras", "vault_lines": ["I'm serving niggas like my name was Pete Sampras"], "meaning": "He’s defeating them (in the “you got served” sense) with the facility of Pete Sampras, who became a Nineties tennis legend by defeating competitors with fast and clean serves on grass courts…too bad he couldn’t play on clay\n\nInteresting that Gudda Gudda picks Pete Sampras, it’s a dated and milquetoast simile, kind of like Sampras himself", "annotation_id": "15038", "url": "https://genius.com/15038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
