{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "Came out at a hundred percent", "vault_lines": ["Came out at a hundred percent"], "meaning": "This double entendre follows from the previous line, showing that Wayne exited his prison stint in high spirits after substantial growth (“came out at a hundred percent”) as if he had been charging a phone battery to 100%.\n\nThe previous line plays on the words “cell” [prison cell | cell phone | battery cell] and “bars” [cell bars | battery bars].\n\nWayne was inside a jail cell staring at his cell bars as if he was staring at the digital bars indicating a phone’s battery level as it charges.", "annotation_id": "37952440", "url": "https://genius.com/37952440", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "And we feedin’ sharks on the yacht, throwin’ niggas off", "vault_lines": ["And we feedin' sharks on the yacht, throwin' niggas off"], "meaning": "This line is reminiscent of one found in Kendrick Lamar’s 2017 track, XXX.:\n\nThrow a steak off the yacht to a pool full of sharks, he’ll take it\n\nLamar has cited Lil Wayne as one of his major inspirations. Given Kendrick’s rising influence in hip-hop, Wayne may be paying him homage in return with this line, and with the “heavy is the head” line to follow.", "annotation_id": "32099239", "url": "https://genius.com/32099239", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "Head spinnin’ like “The Exorcist” on my dick", "vault_lines": ["Head spinnin' like \"The Exorcist\" on my dick"], "meaning": "Refers to a scene from the 1973 film in which a character’s head spins 360°.", "annotation_id": "32099191", "url": "https://genius.com/32099191", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "Go extra-terrestrial on my dick", "vault_lines": ["Go extra-terrestrial on my dick"], "meaning": "A self-reference to Wayne’s 2008 track “Phone Home” in which he compares himself to E.T.", "annotation_id": "32099141", "url": "https://genius.com/32099141", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "Chuggin’ the juice, my cup got a twin, this one is for Pimp This one is for Screw and this one is for Nip, pour out and sip", "vault_lines": ["Chuggin' the juice, my cup got a twin, this one is for Pimp"], "meaning": "A reference to lean—soda mixed with codeine cough syrup, famously drunk from two stacked styrofoam cups.\n\nWayne salutes three late hip-hop colleagues. Pimp C of UGK and DJ Screw passed away in the early 2000s from complications related to lean consumption. Rapper and activist Nipsey Hussle once stated he quit drinking lean due to health concerns. He was tragically murdered in 2019.", "annotation_id": "32099034", "url": "https://genius.com/32099034", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "Steady is the hand that whip around the pot, I’m kitchen smart", "vault_lines": ["Steady is the hand that whip around the pot, I'm kitchen smart"], "meaning": "Playing on the “heavy is the head” bar above, Wayne shifts focus from the bedroom to the kitchen. “Kitchen smart” is a double entendre—he brags about his culinary skills while referencing the cookware brand of the same name.", "annotation_id": "32098946", "url": "https://genius.com/32098946", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "Heavy is the head that wears the crown, and all my pillows soft", "vault_lines": ["Heavy is the head that wears the crown, and all my pillows soft"], "meaning": "Shakespeare’s Henry IV Part 2 originated the famous quote, “Uneasy lies the head that wears a crown.” Greatness in any field comes with extra responsibility and scrutiny. Despite the stress, Lil Wayne’s pillows allow him to sleep well.\n\nKendrick Lamar’s Crown (2022) refers to the same quote:\n“Heavy is the head that chose to wear the crown”. Wayne may be paying homage to his colleague here.", "annotation_id": "32098738", "url": "https://genius.com/32098738", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "Ultra green sparks", "vault_lines": ["Uh, South Beach, spring, California, autumn"], "meaning": "Probably a reference to Green Arrow who is a superhero in the DC comics.", "annotation_id": "30832627", "url": "https://genius.com/30832627", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "Out", "vault_lines": ["Uh, South Beach, spring, California, autumn"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying, “talking all that gangsta shit ‘out loud’ it sound like pillow talk”.", "annotation_id": "30566659", "url": "https://genius.com/30566659", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "When I ain’t talkin’ shit, I’m garglin’ the toilet water", "vault_lines": ["When I ain't talkin' shit, I'm garglin' the toilet water"], "meaning": "It sounds like ‘winter’ but Wayne is actually saying ‘When I’. This seems intentional because he says 2 seasons first and the brain expects more seasons. You can tell Wayne is saying ‘When I’ instead of ‘winter’ because Verse 2 rounds out the 4 seasons.", "annotation_id": "29770588", "url": "https://genius.com/29770588", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Slip", "line": "Uh, South Beach, spring, California, autumn", "vault_lines": ["Uh, South Beach, spring, California, autumn"], "meaning": "Wayne often uses complex structure in his rhymes. Verse one starts with spring and autumn while verse two starts with summer and winter. Additionally, the placement of opposite seasons together is consistent with the use of antithesis in Wayne’s body of work.", "annotation_id": "29770555", "url": "https://genius.com/29770555", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
