{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skit #1", "line": "And um, that’s that Guddaville playing in the background My nigga Gudda mixtape go get that shit", "vault_lines": ["And um, that's that Guddaville playing in the background"], "meaning": "The song playing in the background is “Always Love You” by then-Young Money signee Gudda Gudda. The song was released on Gudda Gudda’s debut mixtape, Guddaville, in February 2009.", "annotation_id": "35749324", "url": "https://genius.com/35749324", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skit #1", "line": "This is a big thank you for coming out to all the nights and days on tour, tours actually For coming to support me every single night", "vault_lines": ["This is a big thank you for coming out to all the nights and days on tour, tours actually"], "meaning": "After the tours, he did this mixtape to say thank you to the fans by giving away music for free. By talking of “tourS” he is talking about the “I Am Music Tour” and the “Americas Most Wanted Tour”. Here a short video about the tours and the recording of “http://rapgenius.com/albums/Lil-wayne/No-ceilings”.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P_1h4xwfNeg", "annotation_id": "2818941", "url": "https://genius.com/2818941", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
