{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "Everything that’s in my safe that’s for bail", "vault_lines": ["Everything that's in my safe that's for bail"], "meaning": "When high profile rappers are arrested, bail is usually set at a very large amount, for example Bobby Shmurda’s now withdrawn $2 Million bail. Weezy even had to bail out his own Young Money artist, Flow, for a tidy sum of $500,000.\n\nWayne was sentenced to a year in jail in 2010 for criminal possession of a firearm. Weezy’s net worth is estimated at $150 million, and given his past troubles with the law, if he’s ever convicted again it’s likely he’ll have to spend a handsome chunk of it bailing himself out, so it’s probably a wise move on Wayne’s part to reserve some in his safe for such an occasion.", "annotation_id": "9665726", "url": "https://genius.com/9665726", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "While I got more cards than a psychic, I’m good", "vault_lines": ["While I got more cards than a psychic, I'm good"], "meaning": "Self-proclaimed psychics often use tarot cards for divination, to tell fortunes and to communicate with spirits. Tarot cards often come in 78-card decks, Wayne probably has some seriously good credit if he has 78 credit and debit cards.\n\n\n\nInterestingly, in a 2012 deposition for a lawsuit Weezy filed against filmmaker and music producer Quincy Jones III (also known as QDIII), Wayne claimed to have psychic powers.", "annotation_id": "9664586", "url": "https://genius.com/9664586", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "She gon’ pop it off for a thug, yeah I just skated off on her love, deuces", "vault_lines": ["I just skated off on drugs, on drugs"], "meaning": "Just as Static Major sang on Wayne’s mega-hit “Lollipop”:\n\nShawty wanna thug\n\nAnd Wayne is entrenched in the thug life. To “pop it off” usually means to be violent against someone, but Wayne uses it to signify this girl’s desire to be with him. But, as he has before, he rejects her romantic advances in favour of a superficial sexual encounter, despite the girl leaving her husband.", "annotation_id": "9641873", "url": "https://genius.com/9641873", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "Treat a Rolls Royce like a Honda, bitch back up off me", "vault_lines": ["Treat a Rolls Royce like a Honda, bitch back up off me"], "meaning": "Wayne has an impressive car collection, and said during the song “Bounce”:\n\nGot a mansion, a condo, a cabin, I sleep in my Phantom\n\nA Honda (unless it’s the NSX) is a significant downgrade. Most people would treat a Rolls Royce with reverence and delicacy, but they’d think nothing of a few bumps and scrapes on a Honda. Wayne’s bank balance allows him to treat his RR like a regular vehicle.", "annotation_id": "9640966", "url": "https://genius.com/9640966", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I just skated off when I chop A gun in both hands, bitch I’m ’bout to do the Shaba, Shaba", "vault_lines": ["I just skated off on drugs, on drugs"], "meaning": "A “chopper” is an automatic weapon, and Wayne already introduced us to one earlier in the first verse. To “chop” means to shoot that weapon, making the traditional “doo-doo-doo” sound, that can sound like a helicopter (hence “chopper”).\n\nThe “Shaba” is a dance move created by youngsters Ruff N Smooth, with some of the arm movements similar to shooting a weapon.", "annotation_id": "9640633", "url": "https://genius.com/9640633", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I just skated off on twelve, fuck twelve bitch Bout to board slide a fucking handrail", "vault_lines": ["I just skated off on drugs, on drugs"], "meaning": "12 is slang for the police, usually shouted as a warning by spotters when a crime is being committed. It’s a slang term utilised by Atlanta rappers, such as Young Thug:\n\nHell nah, I ain’t Twelve, but if I like it I cop it\n\nA board slide is a basic skating move, one Wayne appears to have mastered:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/SITkrjLyP2s?t=22s", "annotation_id": "9636626", "url": "https://genius.com/9636626", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "And we just skateboard, we don’t dance in our Vans, nope", "vault_lines": ["And we just skateboard, we don't dance in our Vans, nope"], "meaning": "Vans are a shoe designed specifically for skating, but have achieved a cult fashion following in recent years. Wayne’s always promoted his vans as a skating aid, but Vans have become increasingly popular for hip-hop dancing.", "annotation_id": "9635826", "url": "https://genius.com/9635826", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "Think I need a cape like superman I just skated off on drugs, on drugs I just skated off sippin’ mud, sippin’ mud I just skated off on the Xan, on the Xan", "vault_lines": ["Think I need a cape like superman"], "meaning": "Wayne is feeling particularly omnipotent, name dropping famous friends like Nyjah Huston and Torey Pudwill, and by “skating off” on a bunch of substances he’s famous for abusing, he may just feel even more powerful.\n\nWayne’s recent drug use has been discussed at length, after he suffered two seizures in June 2016, with TMZ reporting they were due to Lean:\n\nWe’re told Weezy was cruising around with five 16 oz bottles of Promethazine/Codeine syrup during his club appearance in Milwaukee over the weekend … with one onlooker telling us Wayne downed 3 bottles just by himself.\n\n“Skate It Off” was released after his hospitalisation, and it’s possible he wrote these lyrics post-seizure.", "annotation_id": "9635417", "url": "https://genius.com/9635417", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I just touched down, what it do? What it do?", "vault_lines": ["I just touched down, what it do?"], "meaning": "Wayne’s referenced basketball, now he goes again for football, playing on “touch down,” a method of scoring in American Football (after which a place kick is taken to achieve an extra two points), with touching down after being incredibly high. Rarely does Wayne come back to planet Earth.", "annotation_id": "9635038", "url": "https://genius.com/9635038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I got eyeballs on the roof, on the roof I keep nigga’s skulls just for proof, nigga oh", "vault_lines": ["I got eyeballs on the roof, on the roof"], "meaning": "Wayne might be feeling slightly paranoid, after he was shot at in 2015 by a gang member associated with Young Thug. Thug also threatened Wayne over his Barter 6 record, which he was forced to change from Carter 6 due to Lil Wayne allegedly suing Thug.\n\nHe’s also no stranger to collecting skulls. During “CoCo” he rapped:\n\nI send my goons to kill somebody, I need head proof\nThen they come through and sit it on my coffee table", "annotation_id": "9634106", "url": "https://genius.com/9634106", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "Oh your bitch just want this D? Okay it’s D-Day", "vault_lines": ["Oh your bitch just want this D? Okay it's D-Day"], "meaning": "D refers to Lil Wayne’s genitals, and if a girl simply wants him for sexual reasons, he’s fine with giving her a one night (or day) stand.\n\nD-Day was the name of a famous battle in WW2, meaning the one night stand still has some significant even though it’s not the entire war, aka relationship.", "annotation_id": "9517637", "url": "https://genius.com/9517637", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I just skated off on a thot, thot bitch And left her thong wetter than my yacht, why not?", "vault_lines": ["I just skated off on drugs, on drugs"], "meaning": "A “thot” is a girl who sleeps around, and it gives Wayne another opportunity to add to his “wetter than” rhymes. One of the most famous being during his “Marvin’s Room” freestyle:\n\nYeah that’s my bitch\nPussy wetter than a wishing well, I wish\nI was in it right now instead of making this song\n\nDuring “We Takin' Over (Remix)” Wayne asked if he could borrow Scott Storch’s yacht. Based on the producers current financial status, Wayne may have bought it off him for cheap.", "annotation_id": "9517597", "url": "https://genius.com/9517597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "Nigga I’m the God, you Godiva", "vault_lines": ["Nigga I'm the God, you Godiva"], "meaning": "Godiva is a gourmet chocolate brand. Wayne is a God, his competition is “sweet.”", "annotation_id": "9517588", "url": "https://genius.com/9517588", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I just skated with some SB’s, got some SB’s bitch I just skated off with Theotis", "vault_lines": ["I just skated off on drugs, on drugs"], "meaning": "“SB’s” are Nike skate shoes, branded as Nike Skateboarding Shoes. Theotis Beasley is also a professional skater, one whom Wayne has been video’d skating with.", "annotation_id": "9517581", "url": "https://genius.com/9517581", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I just skated off with Chaz Ortiz, Chaz Ortiz bitch", "vault_lines": ["I just skated off with Chaz Ortiz, Chaz Ortiz bitch"], "meaning": "Chaz Ortiz is a pro skateboarder who has been known to skate with Lil Wayne.\n\nYeah, he’s my boy. I’ve been down to the studio to see him record. And when he was in Los Angeles, we skated a lot together. It’s sick. But I love how people hate on him for skateboarding, when in actuality, he’s way more passionate about skating than they are. I’ve seen that fool skate. He will try a trick for hours, nonstop, until he gets it.", "annotation_id": "9517573", "url": "https://genius.com/9517573", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "And I can eyeball work, fuck the scale, fuck the scale I got eyeballs on the roof, on the roof My slimer ollie off this fuckin’ roof, fuckin’ roof bitch I got eyeballs on your squad, pop, pop, pop", "vault_lines": ["I got eyeballs on the roof, on the roof"], "meaning": "A scale is typically used to calculate the weight of drugs for sale, although Wayne’s been confident in his estimations recently:\n\nNigga, we don’t need no scale\n\nHe’s so confident with the work he can eyeball it, i.e. estimate it’s weight by sight. He uses this to transition into his eyeballs on the roof line, and identifying them as “slimer” show’s they’re an integral part of his squad.", "annotation_id": "9517560", "url": "https://genius.com/9517560", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "Wait, I just skated off on the plug, skrr, skrr", "vault_lines": ["Wait, I just skated off on the plug, skrr, skrr"], "meaning": "This is reminiscent of the Plies track “Ran Off On Da Plug Twice” which became a meme briefly in 2016, specifically these lines:\n\nRan off on da plug twice\nHe’s steady callin', I ain’t callin' back\n\nDuring the video for the song, Plies can be seen running on the spot. Wayne doesn’t run, he skates.", "annotation_id": "9517535", "url": "https://genius.com/9517535", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I just skated off like T. Pud, skrr, skrr", "vault_lines": ["I just skated off like T. Pud, skrr, skrr"], "meaning": "Torey Pudwill a.k.a T-Puds, is an American professional street skateboarder. They often skate with each other, and Wayne helps to promote Grizzly, Pudwill’s own skateboarding company.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aWh5QZE8HFg", "annotation_id": "9490310", "url": "https://genius.com/9490310", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "Fuckboi you a hater, what the streets say These bullets turn your tomato to a v8", "vault_lines": ["Fuckboi you a hater, what the streets say"], "meaning": "Wayne looks at Fuckbois and haters the same.  He shoots them in the head til their noggin' starts oozing vegetable juice like V8, made from tomatos, the same color as blood spatter.\n\nTalk stupid? Off with your head!", "annotation_id": "9471647", "url": "https://genius.com/9471647", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I just skated off like El Chapo, Chapo", "vault_lines": ["I just skated off like El Chapo, Chapo"], "meaning": "Weezy will skate off on his skateboard or on drugs like El Chapo skated off from prison, twice last time escaping via a underground tunnel.", "annotation_id": "9471581", "url": "https://genius.com/9471581", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "Me and all my skaters in cahoots, in cahoots Bitch, I just skated off like Nyjah Huston, switch", "vault_lines": ["Me and all my skaters in cahoots, in cahoots"], "meaning": "Nyjah Houston is the highest paid professional skateboarder in the world. He also happens to be Wayne’s favorite skateboarder, and the two have even taken lessons together.\n\nWhenever Wheezy sees trouble coming his way, he just skates away like a pro, with all of his skaters in cahoot (partnership).", "annotation_id": "9471509", "url": "https://genius.com/9471509", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I just skated off in YSL", "vault_lines": ["I just skated off in YSL"], "meaning": "YSL is a designer fashion brand (Yves Saint Laurent), but it’s also an acronym attached to Young Thug, with his Young Stone Life apparel brand.", "annotation_id": "9471423", "url": "https://genius.com/9471423", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "You just hear AK, AK, AK, doo-doo-doo, doo-doo-doo-doo", "vault_lines": ["You just hear AK, AK, AK, doo-doo-doo, doo-doo-doo-doo"], "meaning": "An Ak-47 is a type of gun, one Wayne appears to be fond of:\n\nAnd AK-47 is my fucking address, huh\n\n“Doo-doo-doo” is the sound his weapon makes when he let’s fly.", "annotation_id": "9471412", "url": "https://genius.com/9471412", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "Yeah, I just touched down, what’s the scoop? What’s the scoop? I just hear blasé, blasé, blasé, whoop-de-whoop Whoop-de-whoop Yeah, i just touched down, I’m going for two", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I just touched down, what's the scoop?"], "meaning": "Wayne’s referenced basketball, now he goes again for football, playing on “touch down,” a method of scoring in American Football (after which a place kick is taken to achieve an extra two points), with touching down after being incredibly high. Rarely does Wayne come back to planet Earth.\n\nHe may be simply mentioning “Blasé” by Ty Dolla $ign, or he’s criticising how generic it sounds, “I just hear” implying all songs on the radio sound the same.", "annotation_id": "9471406", "url": "https://genius.com/9471406", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I’m high on my I.D, my IG and IQ", "vault_lines": ["I'm high on my I.D, my IG and IQ"], "meaning": "A clever line here. In literary terms, this is called a zeugma, when one single phrase or word joins different parts of a sentence.\n\n\nWayne is saying he looks high, aka intoxicated, on his identification card.\nAt the same time, he has a high amount of followers on his Instagram.\nAnd, he is saying he has a high IQ level.\n\n\n\nWayne gives us three entendres on “high” to let us know he’s intoxicated, famous, and smart.", "annotation_id": "9471398", "url": "https://genius.com/9471398", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "Money so tall it could hoop, money go", "vault_lines": ["Money so tall it could hoop, money go"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has a net worth of $150 million, if he were to stack up all those bills it’d surely be taller than even the most long-legged basketballer.", "annotation_id": "9471391", "url": "https://genius.com/9471391", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "I just skated off, on twelve With the work in one hand like Odell With the work, yeah", "vault_lines": ["With the work, yeah"], "meaning": "12 is slang for the police, usually shouted as a warning by spotters when a crime is being committed. It’s a slang term utilised by Atlanta rappers, such as Young Thug:\n\nHell nah, I ain’t Twelve, but if I like it I cop it\n\n“Work” is drugs, and he shouts out Odell Beckham, wide receiver, who made an incredible one handed catch that was replayed around the world.", "annotation_id": "9471386", "url": "https://genius.com/9471386", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Skate It Off", "line": "This the motherfuckin’ squad man", "vault_lines": ["This the motherfuckin' squad man"], "meaning": "Wayne’s introducing his squad, aka team, a group of people he skates with. During the video they can be seen dancing and skating with him. Also relates to his recent video game release, SQVAD UP!.", "annotation_id": "9471383", "url": "https://genius.com/9471383", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
