{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Situation", "line": "My body all over you body You body, all over my body, baby", "vault_lines": ["My body all over you body"], "meaning": "Wayne interpolates LSG’s chorus on “My Body” off their 1997 album, Levert.Sweat.Gill.\n\nhttps://m.youtube.com/watch?v=34BuV4QjtAM\n\nThe supergroup LSG consist of the 3 R&B legends: Gerald Levert, Keith Sweat and Johnny Gill.", "annotation_id": "17443727", "url": "https://genius.com/17443727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Situation", "line": "It’s gon’ jump right back up, do the jump man (Jump man) Jumpman, jumpman, jumpman", "vault_lines": ["It's gon' jump right back up, I'm a young man"], "meaning": "Wayne compares the way he is able to immediately regain an erection after sexual intercourse to the leaping ability of Michael Jordan. Jordan famously was nicknamed Jumpman for his high vertical and used the it for his logo for his brand.\n\nWayne also references his protege Drake’s September 2015 track, “Jumpman,” as he mimics the flow and delivery of the chorus:\n\nYeah, Jumpman, Jumpman, I don’t need no introduction\nJumpman, Jumpman, Metro Boomin on production, wow!\n\nIt is also important to note that Wayne released a freestyle over the track’s instrumental in November 2015.", "annotation_id": "17435113", "url": "https://genius.com/17435113", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
