{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sinister", "line": "Lil’ Tune flow sinister, I’ma finish ya", "vault_lines": ["Lil' Tune flow sinister, I'ma finish ya"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is also referred to as Tunechi, hence Lil' Tune", "annotation_id": "25019140", "url": "https://genius.com/25019140", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sinister", "line": "Call Hit-Boy for beats, ask for ten of ’em", "vault_lines": ["Call Hit-Boy for beats, ask for ten of 'em"], "meaning": "Here, Cordae name-drops the song’s co-producer: Hit-Boy, a Grammy-nominated producer and rapper that has produced for a wide range of popular artists, including Nas, Kanye West, Travis Scott, and Benny the Butcher.\n\n\n\nThe two have worked together on songs such as Nas‘ “Life is Like a Dice Game”.\n\nCordae’s statement is not that exaggerated, either, as Hit-Boy himself previously told Hot New HipHop that he has crafted “EP’s worth of music” with the Suitland native.", "annotation_id": "24881664", "url": "https://genius.com/24881664", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sinister", "line": "I ain’t going nowhere, twenty year career minimum", "vault_lines": ["I ain't going nowhere, twenty year career minimum"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne hopped in the chorus to emphasise his longevity in the rap game. Also in the music video, Cordae points at Lil Wayne while rapping the line as a sign of respect and recognition of Lil Waynes career.", "annotation_id": "24653253", "url": "https://genius.com/24653253", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sinister", "line": "My Siamese brother Benjamin, it’s how I stick to him", "vault_lines": ["My Siamese brother Benjamin, it's how I stick to him"], "meaning": "Conjoined twins, also commonly referred to as Siamese twins, are when two babies are conjoined at birth.\n\n\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: Benjamin also means $100 bills (Benjamin Franklin), and Wayne stays so close to his money, it’s like he’s siamese twins with his money.", "annotation_id": "24554173", "url": "https://genius.com/24554173", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
