{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sick", "line": "She a Crip ho but she a nympho And we color blind, and you know love is blind In each other’s eyes, we butterflies", "vault_lines": ["She a Crip ho but she a nympho"], "meaning": "Wayne has said many times that he is a blood, he even made a song about it. The woman with him is a crip, and it’s known that bloods and crips don’t go well together. However, since she’s a nympho, Wayne’s willing to look past it and calls the both of them color blind.\n\n\n\nWayne is referencing the infamous “Blood” & “Crip” gangs known for their distinctive colors red and blue respectively.", "annotation_id": "13869312", "url": "https://genius.com/13869312", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sick", "line": "Every night, any night, all night 6 hoes and they all dykes And all they need is one mic", "vault_lines": ["Every night, any night, all night"], "meaning": "Wayne prefers to sleep with multiple women at once, and even though it seems logical that the numbers wouldn’t add up, Wayne reassures us that the women are perfectly fine with the imbalance by referencing one of Nas' biggest commercial songs “One Mic”.", "annotation_id": "13641255", "url": "https://genius.com/13641255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
