{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shooter", "line": "Die, bitch nigga, die, I hope you bleed a lake", "vault_lines": ["Die, bitch nigga, die, I hope you bleed a lake"], "meaning": "Continuing on from the last line, Wayne hopes his lyrical ammunition kills you (or blows your mind) and forces you to lose substantial blood which is a figurative way of saying he hopes his great performance of lyrical ability destroys your ignorance.\n\nHead shots are likely to make someone open up.", "annotation_id": "3463412", "url": "https://genius.com/3463412", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shooter", "line": "Lil Wayne, just call me Lord, hard Take pain like Tylenols, raw", "vault_lines": ["Lil Wayne, just call me Lord, hard"], "meaning": "Tylenol is a brand of painkillers.\n\n\n\nWayne stays persistent when running from the cops and can take the pain from running and getting shot at like some painkiller pills.", "annotation_id": "2703497", "url": "https://genius.com/2703497", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shooter", "line": "Socks soakin’ wet, I been running, y’all, I reload Every hundred yards, I’m comin’ forward You better know me", "vault_lines": ["Socks soakin' wet, I been running, y'all, I reload"], "meaning": "In this last verse, Wayne stops addressing the Southern Hip Hop criticism and instead picks up on the story of the bank-robbers that Robin has been telling so far.\n\nAfter alerting the police in the previous lines, Wayne is now running from the police; getting his socks sweaty and reloading his gun as he runs to fire back.", "annotation_id": "2703447", "url": "https://genius.com/2703447", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shooter", "line": "But this is Southern, face it If we too simple, then y’all don’t get the basics", "vault_lines": ["But this is Southern, face it"], "meaning": "People criticize southern rap (and southern culture in general) for being shallow and simple-minded, so Wayne retorts that if they don’t understand and appreciate what he’s doing then they don’t understand the fundamental basics of Hip Hop.\n\nHis music is more complex than critics think, and he claims that critics straw-man his art without even a basic understanding of how it works.", "annotation_id": "2703426", "url": "https://genius.com/2703426", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shooter", "line": "You don’t know how sick you make us I wanna throw it up like chips in Vegas", "vault_lines": ["You don't know how sick you make us"], "meaning": "The discrimination and bias in Hip Hop is making Wayne so physically sick that he wants to throw up.\n\nLas Vegas is infamous for its casinos, which are known to “throw up” a large amount of chips when hitting the jackpot.", "annotation_id": "2703402", "url": "https://genius.com/2703402", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shooter", "line": "With all these riches and all these riches (Yeah) But ain’t no loaners around (What you say?) They thinkin’ ’bout shooters, they, shooters, they (Okay) Guns, girls (Okay), ladies, get the guns (Okay), get the Shoot, shoot, shoot, shoot, shooters (Okay, come on)", "vault_lines": ["With all these riches and all these riches (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Robin Thicke and Wayne talk about two different kinds of “shooters” on this song. Here, Robin continues his concept from the intro, talking about a bank robbery conducted by literal “shooters”.\n\nHowever, Wayne’s verses are about him trying to prove to the world that he could earn the title of “best rapper alive” despite all the criticism southern rappers were facing at the time. Wayne is a lyrical “shooter”.", "annotation_id": "2703316", "url": "https://genius.com/2703316", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shooter", "line": "I take you to the shootout, baby, win, lose, or draw, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I take you to the shootout, baby, win, lose, or draw, yeah"], "meaning": "Penalty shots (AKA “shootouts”) is what happens in a sports game, whenever there is a draw or a tie.\n\nNo matter whether Wayne loses, wins, or draws, he’s going to be firing.\n\nAlso, a play on the word “draw”, which can also mean to pull out a gun.", "annotation_id": "569871", "url": "https://genius.com/569871", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shooter", "line": "I’m just tryna be the great, tryna get a piece of cake Take it off of your plate, eat it right in your face (Hah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm just tryna be the great, tryna get a piece of cake"], "meaning": "Double meaning. Figuratively wayne is going to take his opponents profits or ‘cake\" and spend them in their face. Literally, he’s gonna eat their cake right in their face\n\n\n\nEither way it sucks to be “them”", "annotation_id": "50700", "url": "https://genius.com/50700", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shooter", "line": "And to the radio stations, I’m tired of bein’ patient Stop being rapper racists, region haters Spectators, dictators, behind door dick takers, it’s outrageous", "vault_lines": ["And to the radio stations, I'm tired of bein' patient"], "meaning": "Wayne speaking directly to radio stations who find his music to be subpar purely because it comes from the south.\n\nIt’s rumored that this was especially directed towards Hot 97 and Funk Flex, who slept on the South heavy feeling that the southern/crunk pop movement was killing hip-hop, and never gave Wayne much attention due to being from New Orleans.", "annotation_id": "50698", "url": "https://genius.com/50698", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shooter", "line": "They got a whole lot to say, but I don’t listen Call me Automatic Weezy, bitch, I keep spittin’, pow", "vault_lines": ["They got a whole lot to say, but I don't listen"], "meaning": "Wayne isn’t concerned with others, he’s just busy doing him.\n\n“Automatic Weezy” means that he continuously generates rhymes with a succession similar to that of an automatic fire arm. Wayne simply keeps “spitting” to prove himself as a capable rapper and destroy the stereotype against southern rappers in general.", "annotation_id": "38680", "url": "https://genius.com/38680", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
