{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "But your bullets don’t reach Mars", "vault_lines": ["But your bullets don't reach Mars"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is saying that he’s so far ahead of the rap game, that anyone who tries taking a shot at him won’t even reach him.", "annotation_id": "36076671", "url": "https://genius.com/36076671", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "This is history in the making Now shut the fuck up and let me make it", "vault_lines": ["This is history in the making"], "meaning": "Wayne was right, Tha Carter 3 really was a historical moment in music. After selling one million copies first week, it’s become one of the most iconic albums of all time.", "annotation_id": "28884182", "url": "https://genius.com/28884182", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "Ride for hours, supply the flowers", "vault_lines": ["Ride for hours, supply the flowers"], "meaning": "Wayne supplies the flower cuz Wayne is the biggest pimp.", "annotation_id": "26593783", "url": "https://genius.com/26593783", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "And I would die for ours", "vault_lines": ["And I would die for ours"], "meaning": "This also sounds like “die for hours”", "annotation_id": "22761002", "url": "https://genius.com/22761002", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "And if you shootin’ for the stars, then just shoot me", "vault_lines": ["And if you shootin' for the stars, then just shoot me"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is implying that he’s a star.", "annotation_id": "22549643", "url": "https://genius.com/22549643", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "My picture should be in the dictionary Next to the definition of definition Because repetition is the father of learnin’", "vault_lines": ["my picture should be in the dictionary"], "meaning": "In Tha Carter Documentary, it’s revealed that Wayne uses the phrase “because repetition is the father of learnin'” often. This is akin to age-old proverb “practice makes perfect”. Wayne lives it as evidenced by his legendary work ethic that resulted in 7 albums between 2004-2011 and 21 mixtapes between 2002-2013.\nHe also alludes to repetition as a literal life-or-death necessity for Hip-Hop in his song “Dr. Carter”. Rap often utilizes homages, allusions, and samples to add a historical layer to the culture.", "annotation_id": "14774171", "url": "https://genius.com/14774171", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "Bitch, see, it gets me how nothin’ gets me or get to me", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, see, it gets me how nothin' gets me or get to me"], "meaning": "This is a packed line:\n1.  He affirms the concept that he is set apart from everyone else and subsequently explores the layers of this distance.\n2. It gets [him] how nothing bothers him. As Chance the Rapper explains “Wayne remade the whole Carter III after it got stolen and leaked. So it’s two [albums]. Both versions are my favorite album”. So while this may have ruined other rappers, Wayne kept his cool.\n3. It “gets [him]” how nothing understands him. This connects to “DontGetIt” the outro of Tha Carter III through the theme of being misunderstood. Wayne employs the martian metaphor to symbolize how his unparalleled, “out of this world” success.\n4. It “gets [him]” how nothing can challenge him or “get to him” Since 2000, 50 cent and Wayne are the only two African-American rappers to sell over 3 million albums (as of June 2018). Although the height of the Recession, over 1,000,000 people bought Tha Carter III in the first week; a feat not even DAMN accomplished in an age of streaming. His success is truly legendary as he put rap, Southern Rap no less, at the forefront of mainstream music.\n5. This also connects with the next quatrain “I’ll getcha”. He highlights the irony that though nobody understands him, he understands everybody as he solidified his “Best Rapper Alive” claim with Tha Carter III’s commercial and critical success, (Wayne took home 4 Grammys in 2008.\n6. When examined from a perspective on drug use, he could also be commenting on his controversial codeine use at the time. The first half of the line could be referencing how he’s misunderstood as other artists have abused drugs while that rarely becomes their media image. The second half would then refer to how drugs never “get to [him]” or how he never overwhelmed by his drug use and has been quite successful. As he said in regards to balancing his drug use with creative success “a junkie can’t do what the fuck I do”.", "annotation_id": "14774089", "url": "https://genius.com/14774089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "I spit Alcatraz bars, I know", "vault_lines": ["I spit Alcatraz bars, I know"], "meaning": "Wayne uses wordplay and compares his skillful bars and ability to rap to the high maximum security bars of the famous Alcatraz Federal Penitentary located in San Francisco, California.", "annotation_id": "13936172", "url": "https://genius.com/13936172", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "And I’ma do it again, like, nigga, backwards", "vault_lines": ["And I'ma do it again, like, nigga, backwards"], "meaning": "This is a bit of clever wordplay. If one was to say the word “nigga” backwards, “aggin”, it would sound like they were saying the word, “again.”", "annotation_id": "12951641", "url": "https://genius.com/12951641", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "I swear this tea is at a real good temperature right now So am I, yeah, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I swear this tea is at a real good temperature right now"], "meaning": "As D. Smith explained to XXL:\n\n[Wayne] heard the beat and kicked everybody out except for like two people, the engineer, and myself. He smoked two blunts, asked for a cup of hot tea and just went in.", "annotation_id": "4185270", "url": "https://genius.com/4185270", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "I see your boys hatin’, and I see your girls naked", "vault_lines": ["I see your boys hatin', and I see your girls naked"], "meaning": "Wayne gets a lot hate for his position in life, with all the success and having the finer things; but that doesn’t matter to Wayne.\n\nBecause you can love him or hate him, it doesn’t matter because nothing will stop Lil Wayne getting any girl he wants.", "annotation_id": "3288964", "url": "https://genius.com/3288964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "Paws, claws because I’m a beast, I’m a dog I’ll get you,", "vault_lines": ["Paws, claws because I'm a beast, I'm a dog"], "meaning": "Wayne is not only mentioning the paws and claws of a beast or dog which he compares himself to in the next line, but is also making a double entendre. A clause (“claws”) is a connection of two thoughts or a group of words containing a subject and predicate, forming part of a compound or complex sentence. This requires a conjunction, such as “because”. A comma is used when a conjuction is present in a sentence. You pause (“paws”) when reading a comma.\n\nSo the line can also be read as: “Your bullets can’t reach Mars, (comma “Paws, claws”) because I’m a beast, I’m a dog.”  Very clever.", "annotation_id": "1913236", "url": "https://genius.com/1913236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "Nah, D., bring the drums back", "vault_lines": ["Nah, D., bring the drums back"], "meaning": "D. Smith produced the song as well as sung the hook. The drums stop right after “time’s up” … but Wayne instructs the producer to bring them back – he isn’t finished", "annotation_id": "147031", "url": "https://genius.com/147031", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "Now, watch me get high, like, time’s up", "vault_lines": ["Now, watch me get high, like, time's up"], "meaning": "When your time’s up, you die and your angel gets high as it floats to heaven. Watch him get high as if he was floating to heaven.\n\nAlso note the wordplay: “watch/time” and “high/up.”", "annotation_id": "66872", "url": "https://genius.com/66872", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "These niggas backwards, but they behind us", "vault_lines": ["These niggas backwards, but they behind us"], "meaning": "To be backwards is to be behind in something, but Wayne says that they are behind him – meaning that not only are they behind on the times, they are also literally behind Wayne because they aren’t his competition.\nThis line comes pretty close to the elusive triple entendre\n\nBackwards=fucked up (Mentally)\nBackwards=Moving backwards(doing shit thats aready done)\nBackwards=behind him (lil wayne)\n\nTriple Entendre", "annotation_id": "61664", "url": "https://genius.com/61664", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "I’m drinkin’ hot tea, bitch Feel me", "vault_lines": ["I'm drinkin' hot tea, bitch"], "meaning": "As D. Smith explained to XXL:\n\n[Wayne] heard the beat and kicked everybody out except for like two people, the engineer, and myself. He smoked two blunts, asked for a cup of hot tea and just went in.", "annotation_id": "61641", "url": "https://genius.com/61641", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "Drum sound like a naked gun, switch clips with my thumb Then, I pop another clip in and aim at his vision ’Cause Wayne is his vision, ’cause Wayne is the mission I’m aimin’ at a mirror", "vault_lines": ["Drum sound like a naked gun, switch clips with my thumb"], "meaning": "This links back to when, as a child, he accidentally shot himself while looking at a mirror. He’s so great that the only one who can shoot him down is himself.\n\n\nIn other words, he’s his best friend, yet his worst enemy.", "annotation_id": "61636", "url": "https://genius.com/61636", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "Got a .380 on my waist and Rambo back home", "vault_lines": ["Got a .380 on my waist and Rambo back home"], "meaning": "He’s “always strapped” and he’s got more weapons back home.\n\nRambo, a popular movie series, depicted the main character having very powerful weapons.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/sfMnshSFt1o?t=128", "annotation_id": "61625", "url": "https://genius.com/61625", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "And D-boys is the only Alphabet Boys I know", "vault_lines": ["And D-boys is the only Alphabet Boys I know"], "meaning": "Alphabet boys are considered as police or affiliations to the police; DEA the drug enforcement administration; the FBI, federal bureau of investigation; the ATF, bureau of alcohol, tobacco, firearms or explosives etc. So basically he doesn’t talk to the police. D-boys is also short for “dope-boys”, highlighting his affiliation with drug-dealers as well", "annotation_id": "61624", "url": "https://genius.com/61624", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "No more bandana ’round my dome, bandana in my right pocket Bitch, I’m grown, fuck what you on", "vault_lines": ["No more bandana 'round my dome, bandana in my right pocket"], "meaning": "Lil wayne was commonly seen wearing bandannas on his head during his Hot Boys days.\n\n\n\nBut now he is all grown up and reps the Bloods! Is that a blue bandanna?\n\nAlso a play on the previous use of ‘Rambo’ in the previous line since he is known for wearing a bandana", "annotation_id": "37225", "url": "https://genius.com/37225", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shoot Me Down", "line": "I ain’t kinda hot, I’m sauna I sweat money and the bank is my shower Haha, and that pistol is my towel Haha, so stop sweatin’ me, coward", "vault_lines": ["Haha, and that pistol is my towel"], "meaning": "He’s hot, as one would be in a sauna, but actually meaning popular in the rap game, and that heat makes him money, just as literal heat makes sweat. Just as a shower would take much sweat, he has much money (sweat) in the bank (shower). A towel also gets rid of sweat, and his pistol serves as his towel, getting rid of haters who “sweat” him, with sweat being hassling in this scenario", "annotation_id": "36635", "url": "https://genius.com/36635", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
