{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shit Stains", "line": "And everybody’s on edge ’til you push ’em", "vault_lines": ["And everybody's on edge 'til you push 'em"], "meaning": "Wayne plays with the ideas of being on the edge of something and the idiom to be on edge. What is amusing is that we have two opposite effects on each option. If you are on the edge of something and someone pushes you, most likely you are going to fall. On the other hand, if you claim to be on your own edge and somebody pushes you, it is very probable that you’ll find out that you could be doing more than you thought.", "annotation_id": "3376886", "url": "https://genius.com/3376886", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shit Stains", "line": "Bad bitches, I get at you like “sinus” (God bless you)", "vault_lines": ["Bad bitches, I get at you like \"sinus\" (God bless you)"], "meaning": "A clever play on words. Wayne makes use of the homophones at you and achoo to create a pun in here. Simply put, he is saying that he is going to get at bad bitches, that is, to hook up with them. But the more elaborate part is that “at you” and “achoo” are homophones, and just like sinus fatally makes you sneeze, this is the manner in which Weezy is going to hook up with bad bitches.", "annotation_id": "3376860", "url": "https://genius.com/3376860", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shit Stains", "line": "Got money on my mind,", "vault_lines": ["Got money on my mind,"], "meaning": "Reminiscent of his legendary Carter 2 days, from where he coins the phrase in his popular song Money on My Mind\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=avtLR_Mzngo", "annotation_id": "1638202", "url": "https://genius.com/1638202", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shit Stains", "line": "I’m in this bitch throwin’ up Blood, like a ulcer (Suu whoop)", "vault_lines": ["I'm in this bitch throwin' up Blood, like a ulcer (Suu whoop)"], "meaning": "Wayne is reppin' and “throwing up” his gang’s signs.\nAn ulcer in your stomach can cause you to vomit blood.", "annotation_id": "1624617", "url": "https://genius.com/1624617", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shit Stains", "line": "I’m from Hollygrove (Yeah), I used to hang with ’El (’El) I make them bitches (*gasp*), they waitin’ to exhale (Yeah) I’m on some gangsta shit (Yeah), knock your head off (Yeah) Bark up my tree, that’s a dead dog (Ugh) Where them hoes at? (”Right there”) Tell ’em I say, “What’s up?” (What’s up?) I like a shaved pussy, no razor bumps (Okay)", "vault_lines": ["I brung my AK, I'm on my \"A\" game"], "meaning": "Wayne takes verse/line recycling to a whole ‘nother level.\n\nThis whole section is repeated word-for-word from Wayne’s verse on Bow Wow’s Sweat. Watch the video for proof. http://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&v=E4z_FH2wiCg#t=136s\n\nThere is a slight but important difference between this section and the similar section in Bow Wow’s Sweat. He says here that he “used to hang” with Elz. In Sweat he said “I still hang” with Elz. Presumably him and Juelz Santana have had some sort of breakup.", "annotation_id": "1622914", "url": "https://genius.com/1622914", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shit Stains", "line": "I’m ’bout to shoot a porn; I’m castin’: broken arm", "vault_lines": ["I'm 'bout to shoot a porn; I'm castin': broken arm"], "meaning": "He’s having auditions for the pornographic movie that he’s about to shoot.\n\n\n\nThe word “castin'” also refers to a cast that you have to get on your arm when you break it, hence “broken arm”", "annotation_id": "1621181", "url": "https://genius.com/1621181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shit Stains", "line": "Dr. Carter, M.D., that’s mur-der (Whoa)", "vault_lines": ["Dr. Carter, M.D., that's mur-der (Whoa)"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is also a Doctor of Hip-Hop, as he let us know in his famous song off Tha Carter 3. “MD”, derived from the Latin phrase “Medicinae Doctor”, means “Doctor of Medicine”. He is also saying that MD stands for murder\n\nIt could also stand for Michael Dwayne, the first two words of his name", "annotation_id": "1621117", "url": "https://genius.com/1621117", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shit Stains", "line": "Bitch I’m from New Orleans, everybody ain’t saints (Ugh)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I'm from New Orleans, everybody ain't saints (Ugh)"], "meaning": "Double Entendre:\n\nHe’s from New Orleans, where people can do some shady stuff. Don’t be misled by the name of their football team (Saints)\n\nNot everyone from New Orleans is in fact a Saints fan since Lil Wayne is known as a diehard Packers fan.", "annotation_id": "1620671", "url": "https://genius.com/1620671", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
