{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "She Don’t Put It Down", "line": "But you know love is nothing; ask Stan Smith", "vault_lines": ["But you know love is nothing; ask Stan Smith"], "meaning": "Stan Smith is a former World No. 1 American tennis player who (with his partner Bob Lutz) formed one of the most successful doubles teams of all time, winning 54 titles worldwide. The duo also hold the record for the most appearances in doubles finals matches.\n\nSo the two of them really do well together…\n\n\n\nThe wordplay behind this line is that, in the context of tennis, a score of zero (“nothing”) is called “love”.\n\n*FUN FACT: Additionally, in tennis, “Game” is 4.", "annotation_id": "1134862", "url": "https://genius.com/1134862", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "She Don’t Put It Down", "line": "I mean it’s working out, so we’re staying fit", "vault_lines": ["I mean it’s working out, so we’re staying fit"], "meaning": "double entendre:\n\n\nYou stay fit by working out\n\nIf a relationship is working out, means its going good.\nAlso a healthy relationship one where you have a lot of sex", "annotation_id": "1130970", "url": "https://genius.com/1130970", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "She Don’t Put It Down", "line": "Ass so mean that I’m always on her bad side", "vault_lines": ["Ass so mean that I’m always on her bad side"], "meaning": "He’s using wordplay to say that he likes looking at her from behind.\n\n\n\nTo be on someone’s “bad side” is an idiom for when someone is criticizing you harshly.\nIn this case, her bad side is her “backside”.\n\nAlso, when someone is mean you are likely to get mad, a possible wordplay from the prior line.", "annotation_id": "1127293", "url": "https://genius.com/1127293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
