{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sharks", "line": "Sweet comes before bitter", "vault_lines": ["Sweet comes before bitter"], "meaning": "This refers to how the tongue has the sweet, sour, salty and bitter spot, and is indicating that the sweet part of the tongue is towards the tip while the bitter is towards the back of the tongue poasibly alluding to the reverse of “with pain come ease” where Weezy expects rainy days ahead after seeing too much sunshine.", "annotation_id": "35889891", "url": "https://genius.com/35889891", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
