{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sharks", "line": "Just a menace to society", "vault_lines": ["Just a menace to society"], "meaning": "Wayne references the 1993 film Menace II Society, a seminal portrayal of violence and systemic despair in South Central Los Angeles. Coming right after he asks, “Where was everybody at when I was just nobody?,” the line speaks to being cast out or ignored until success arrives. The film’s title becomes a way for Wayne to own the label society gives him — not just as a rebel, but as someone shaped by neglect, betrayal, and survival in a world where trust is rare.", "annotation_id": "35815622", "url": "https://genius.com/35815622", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
