{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sharks", "line": "Thieves in the night move cool like a breeze in the night", "vault_lines": ["Thieves in the night move cool like a breeze in the night"], "meaning": "Woah! That’s Tunechi I know he never misses, look how he mended two ideas of the same kind. Semicolon simile. Lil Wayne just took the very same idiom we all familiar with;\n\n“thief in the night” (http://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thief_in_the_night)\nEtymology And he knotted it with the coolness that descend down on earth during the night hours mostly, around midnight, so literally he says, “Thieves will never make you arlet when they make counterattack upon you.” They’ll come at you with such a cool approach as the breeze in the night does. And by the time you get a wake-up call it’ll will be too late for you to act against them.", "annotation_id": "35812013", "url": "https://genius.com/35812013", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sharks", "line": "You goin’ Bobby Brown, I’m a new addiction", "vault_lines": ["You goin' Bobby Brown, I'm a new addiction"], "meaning": "Bobby Brown is an R&B singer with well-known substance abuse problems. Big Sean is saying that he and his music is something you can get addicted to, just like drugs. Also, Brown rose to fame as founding member of the R&B group New Edition, which sounds a lot like “new addiction.”\n\nhttps://s.yimg.com/ny/api/res/1.2/3MqQsAQbxeUweifopvDd7g--/YXBwaWQ9aGlnaGxhbmRlcjt3PTEyMDA7aD03OTg-/https://s.yimg.com/os/creatr-uploaded-images/2022-05/5f127e20-db8a-11ec-8ba7-14a67e463c95", "annotation_id": "35811487", "url": "https://genius.com/35811487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
