{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shades", "line": "Let me have my way, I’ma have my way, Carlito", "vault_lines": ["Let me have my way, I'ma have my way, Carlito"], "meaning": "Reference to the 1996 movie Carlito’s Way, sometimes considered to be a sort of sequel to the much more famous film Scarface (a remake of a 1932 movie released in 1983).\n\n\n\nBoth works, directed by Brian De Palma and starring Al Pacino, are widely referred to in hip hop.", "annotation_id": "18479259", "url": "https://genius.com/18479259", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shades", "line": "Flashing lights come from everywhere", "vault_lines": ["Flashing lights come from everywhere"], "meaning": "Timberlake Interpolates his own 2007 song “LoveStoned/I Think She Knows”\n“Those flashing lights come from everywhere\nThe way they hit her, I had to stop and stare\nShe’s got me love stoned, man, I swear\nShe’s bad and she knows, I think that she knows.”", "annotation_id": "18479169", "url": "https://genius.com/18479169", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
