{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Shades", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Diddy-dirty-money-shades-lyrics", "genius_title": "Shades", "genius_id": 2879, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "I don’t twerk, but I tweak For that purple, that pink Yeah you see what I’m saying Like you heard what you see I’m a verbal disease", "vault_lines": ["\"Tune, I heard you don't sleep\""], "meaning": "Weezy is saying that he doesn’t twerk but when he’s on that drank/lean, (“that purple that pink”) he tweaks from the effects of the promethazine.\n\nHe then uses clever word play and almost interpolates a double entendre… “See what I’m sayin'” , is similar to the phrase, “you know what I mean?”. Therefore, you can’t physically “see” what Weezy is “saying” but he twists the meaning by then adding “like you heard what you see”.\n\n“I’m a verbal disease” alludes to the fact that Wayne spits bars that are fire and like he says later on in this song, “…keep my name out yo mouth, I hope it tastes like cayenne”, his name is enough to give you disease ridden symptoms\n\nProbably one of the most hardest lines from Tunechi during this time,  when his songs were slowly declining from bad to worse. SFTW2 was his “revival” to some, considering it dropped around his infamous beef with Birdman.", "annotation_id": "22721693", "url": "https://genius.com/22721693", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "I’m a nerd, I’m a geek I’m absurd, I’m unique", "vault_lines": ["I'm a nerd, I'm a geek"], "meaning": "Wayne came out on the scene with his unique style, voice, punchlines that separated him from other rappers. He was outstanding because he was different, if you see a person who doesn’t look like the most people you remember him, so being unique is a big plus for Weezy.\n\nAlso note the internal rhyme scheme used here – Nerd/Absurd, Geek/Unique – one syllable words that rhythmically balance out over the course of the bar very nicely. However, Nerd and Geek are two different words that in fact describe the same thing..academically smart / intellectual / passionate about learning.", "annotation_id": "4716741", "url": "https://genius.com/4716741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "Been a turd on these streets Since my curtains was sheets", "vault_lines": ["Been a turd on these streets"], "meaning": "Wayne’s been “the shit” on the streets since “The Block Was Hot”. Sheets are used in households that can’t afford proper curtains. This also ties in nicely with the title of the song.", "annotation_id": "4709562", "url": "https://genius.com/4709562", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "I’m just serving these fiends Sell birds to the bees I sell birds to the trees", "vault_lines": ["I'm just serving these fiends"], "meaning": "A bird is a kilo of cocaine – Wayne services his fans with great punchlines like a drug dealer peddles dope to an addict.\n\n“The Birds and the Bees” is also a common way of teaching the ins and outs of sex to young children.\n\n“I sell birds to the trees”  is Wayne’s reinterpretation of the “selling snow to Eskimos.”", "annotation_id": "4709329", "url": "https://genius.com/4709329", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "I’ll kill a nigga right now I’ll put a nigga lights out Then put his body in a ice box With holes in his body like socks These niggas softer than These niggas softer than nylon So keep my name out your mouth I hope it taste like cayenne", "vault_lines": ["I'll kill a nigga right now"], "meaning": "Wayne doesn’t want to be associated with soft rappers, so similar to boxer, James Toney, Weezy will knock ya “lights out.” Good thing a pair of socks only have two holes, so not too much to worry about.\n\nWeezy is hot like the cayenne pepper so don’t play with fire. Keep his name out of your mouth, but don’t keep cayenne out – it has health benefits!", "annotation_id": "4709291", "url": "https://genius.com/4709291", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "I sleep on a crucifix I wake up cranky and turn into a lunatic Then shoot my bitch Behind orange juice and grits", "vault_lines": ["I sleep on a crucifix"], "meaning": "Comparing himself to Jesus, Wayne describes his death on the cross and subsequent rebirth. His 2010 album was even titled Rebirth.\n\n“Crank” and “lunatic” both refer to his crazy rhymes, one of which is uttered immediately after – shooting his girl at breakfast.", "annotation_id": "4709267", "url": "https://genius.com/4709267", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "Now don’t, I mean don’t Don’t question me Let me breathe", "vault_lines": ["Now don't, I mean don't"], "meaning": "This line could reference the death of New York resident Eric Garner who was choked to death by police after expressing he couldn’t breathe 11 times.\n\nWayne is exercising his right and telling law enforcement to not question him if he hasn’t done anything wrong and to let him “breathe” meaning to not get in his way.", "annotation_id": "4709242", "url": "https://genius.com/4709242", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "Like that blunt between my two fingers I’m at peace Word", "vault_lines": ["Like that blunt between my two fingers"], "meaning": "Wordplay!\n\nWeezy is holding a blunt between his middle and index fingers. Forming a peace sign around the blunt. Weezy is “at peace” like the blunt between his two fingers which is literally at peace.", "annotation_id": "4709030", "url": "https://genius.com/4709030", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "I’m so sorry, so sorry... woo This-this that Sorry 4 the Wait 2 And I’m so sorry", "vault_lines": ["But this is that Sorry 4 the Wait, nigga"], "meaning": "In 2011, Wayne released a mixtape titled Sorry 4 The Wait to keep fans content until Tha Carter IV arrived. Once again it seems Birdman & Slim got the better of him, and Weezy’s been forced to release a follow up to his 2011 mixtape.\n\n“Bad bitch in mi casa, no mi casa su casa” is Spanish for bad bitch in my home, my home is not your home, implying the chick is only there for fun, and not for a relationship. It’s also not the first time Wayne has used that line. So regardless of Wayne’s album issues, he still parties, and enjoys a woman’s company, like he always has.\n\nLastly, “My Choppa go doom da da. Di da di da da” seems to be a reference to Boyz 2 men’s Motown philly.", "annotation_id": "4708721", "url": "https://genius.com/4708721", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "And motherfuck you if you fight crime I’m from a place with a high crime rate, like Iran We put your ass on Nightline I’m on the grass like a python", "vault_lines": ["And motherfuck you if you fight crime"], "meaning": "Wayne didn’t grow up in the most affluent place in the world – New Orleans. It’s safe to compare these kind of death scenarios to the strict anarchist country of Iran, although Iran’s is substantially higher'.\n\nConsidering Wayne grew up in the area, he knows a thing or two about getting away with rash crimes, thus them appearing on Nightline television and escaping like a python in the grass.\n\n\n\n“On the grass” is also a reference to being high off marijuana, something Weezy’s known to partake in.", "annotation_id": "4708680", "url": "https://genius.com/4708680", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sh!t", "line": "Did my time at Cash Money Time served and released But this agent ain’t free Word That’s the word on these streets But that shit is old news That shit’s so yesterweek I’m just focused Focused on my expertise", "vault_lines": ["And I'm so sorry, I'm so sorry"], "meaning": "Wayne went on a twitter rant back in December where he explained his problems with his long time label Cash Money.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LilTunechi/status/540571271927300096\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWayne has done his time and released multiple albums under the label, yet he is still being held prisoner by it and isn’t being let out of his contract. In relation to prison, his sentence is over yet they won’t set him free. However, that’s behind him, and he just wants to make good music.", "annotation_id": "4708415", "url": "https://genius.com/4708415", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
