{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "I could sell salt and equalize it, wait I said I could sell salt and equalize it", "vault_lines": ["I could sell salt and equalize it, wait"], "meaning": "Equal is an artificial sweetener that shares the same color and consistency as salt.  Through this line, Lil Wayne is saying that he can take something unpleasant and make it better.", "annotation_id": "31440504", "url": "https://genius.com/31440504", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Man if this was baseball, I ain’t let ’em slide once", "vault_lines": ["Man if this was baseball, I ain't let 'em slide once"], "meaning": "When you let someone “slide” you’re basically ignoring or tolerating mistake they made.\nNicki also uses a sports reference here – as she often does – by using the baseball term “sliding” which is used when an opposing player tries to touch a base faster by sliding toward it.\nIt is common for baseball infielders to try and prevent this by blocking the base. Thus she’s basically saying that she’s not gonna make it easy for the other rappers.\n\n\n\nShe might also be saying that she’ll never let another dude slide in her DM’s.", "annotation_id": "17984320", "url": "https://genius.com/17984320", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "All these rappers is my sons, and I’m always nine months", "vault_lines": ["All these rappers is my sons, and I'm always nine months"], "meaning": "Nicki coined the phrase “all these bitches is my sons,” as she’s used the phrase countless times throughout her career. The phrase alludes to all other rappers are her children and thus inferior to her.\n\nTypically when you have a baby, it takes eight to nine months before going into labor and having your baby. Nicki has a similar lyric on her 2012 track “The Boys”:\n\nGirls is my sons, carried them for 8 months (ouh)\nAnd yes, you’re premature", "annotation_id": "17984296", "url": "https://genius.com/17984296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "All you niggas lame, tooly on me, got killers on speed dial", "vault_lines": ["All you niggas lame, tooly on me, got killers on speed dial"], "meaning": "Wordplaying off of both definitions of “lame”\n\n\nIn Rap, it means you’re whack ass hell, boring af, uncool, etc.\nLame, adj. – (of a person or animal) unable to walk normally because of an injury or illness affecting the leg or foot. So the other meaning is you’re weak and crippled\n\n\n\nAs a side allusion: He keep be using more wordplay to say he rolls with Bloods like the Game and not “cripped” ass gangbangers, while he has style in his lyricism and rapping. (Gangsta MC’s are NOT renowned for not being lyrical or technical)\n\nHis gang will take out his enemies faster than having them called on speed dial.", "annotation_id": "3326689", "url": "https://genius.com/3326689", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Infrared blam if a nigga shout Don’t get packed out,", "vault_lines": ["Infrared blam if a nigga shout"], "meaning": "He’s using dual wordplay with “infrared”. He’s punning the fact that, the blood from the gunshot wound will be the same color, as his gun’s red beam.\n\n\nShooters, typically use lasersight at night time for executing stealth hits. The “blam” from the barrel flash, is “snapshot” as fast as one from a camera. He’s looking through a scope (like binoculars) and scanning his target like an IR surveillance camera\nHe implies if a rat (snitch), rats out to the cops “packs out” he will get laser-targeted and blood over all him.\nIf the rat, somehow manages to outlive the shooting, to go back to his “ratpack” Tyga is not reluctant. He will still get him, even if the group has his back. Wayne says this later in another line to confirm it.\nThe snitches' death will make T-Raw famous and will be reported on the news and media, overnight. When hundreds of cameras flash (if he goes to court for murder) in your eyes, they look like infrared sensors.", "annotation_id": "3326228", "url": "https://genius.com/3326228", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "[Verse 2: Nicki Minaj]", "vault_lines": ["High in the video, fuck with me, hella raw"], "meaning": "If you pay attention RIGHT before the her verse comes in, the bass drops “growls” like a panther to let you know she’s next in the song. Felines often are associated with feminine characteristics (such as scratching, fighting, being nosy, loud, sneaking, etc).\n\n\n\n\nShe continues her “killer mood” demeanor in her tone. The 1st couple of lines sounds like she described an execution job she just got done and is picking up paycheck for “killing verses”.\nPersonification is used here (as her money is representing her status). It’s Nicki’s version of “Talk to the hand” with the following lines:\n\n\n\nMoney talks, guess I got I the gift of gab, don’t interject, don’t intercept, you ain’t on a jet, you ain’t meet a bitch (her) with this kind of money yet\n\n\n\nThen she goes delves into “Nicki The Boss” alter ego to say exactly why “money talks for her” and begins dropping her usual anvil-sized bars.", "annotation_id": "3042324", "url": "https://genius.com/3042324", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "[Produced by d.a. got that dope]", "vault_lines": ["High in the video, fuck with me, hella raw"], "meaning": "This instrumental is notable for its tempo [snail’s pace, only slightly faster than “All Gold Everything” and its sparse texture, otherworldly synth pad sounds accompanying an ominous humming kick drum and snappy snares. In times, such as the beginning of Nicki Minaj’s verse, the bass becomes more distorted as the purr turns to a growl.", "annotation_id": "2931243", "url": "https://genius.com/2931243", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "[Verse 1: Tyga]", "vault_lines": ["High in the video, fuck with me, hella raw"], "meaning": "According to an interview “Senile” was going to be a Tyga single off his album, but his album is not coming out until the summer. He was playing part of his album for Nicki and Nicki went nuts over it. She wanted to get on it, so he gave it to her. She really spazzed on her verse and was like, “We should put Wayne on this.” So then they put Wayne on it. Then everyone was like, “Man, this should be the Young Money single.” So it went from a Tyga single to a Young Money single.", "annotation_id": "2901093", "url": "https://genius.com/2901093", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Man I’m a good guy, turned to a vill-i-an", "vault_lines": ["Man I'm a good guy, turned to a vill-i-an"], "meaning": "Tyga is flippin Jay Z’s line from so appalled\n“ Dark knight feeling die and be a hero or live long enough to see yourself being become a villian”\n\nhttp://rapgenius.com/39888/Kanye-west-so-appalled/Dark-knight-feeling-die-and-be-a-hero-or-live-long-enough-to-see-yourself-become-a-villain", "annotation_id": "2846087", "url": "https://genius.com/2846087", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Raw got a little riddle, riddle, twerk for a star", "vault_lines": ["Raw got a little riddle, riddle, twerk for a star"], "meaning": "Tyga or T-Raw, a play on the last line as he humbly calls himself that (he is the rawest), is going illiterate or RECKLESS STUPID DUMB and getting the ladies to twerk for him, the Young Money king.\n\nBecause really, who else dishes out club bangers like Tyga?", "annotation_id": "2844015", "url": "https://genius.com/2844015", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "High in the video, fuck with me, hella raw", "vault_lines": ["High in the video, fuck with me, hella raw"], "meaning": "He’s high in the video probably off rolling one of his joints using “Raw” papers.\n“Fuck with me, hella raw”-Intercourse without a condom is “Raw-dogging”\nGood use of the word raw.\n\n\n\nACCEPTED COMMENT: His nickname is also T-Raw or “Tyga Raw”.", "annotation_id": "2843704", "url": "https://genius.com/2843704", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Ride with the heat, trunk full of beat", "vault_lines": ["Ride with the heat, trunk full of beat"], "meaning": "Tyga’s ridin' dirty in his car with a gun while bumping loud music.\n\nCould it be a reference to a popular song by Lil Wayne’s friend and fellow rapper Tech N9ne?\n\nJ’s on my feet, car full of beat\nTrunk full of heat, Caribou in the seat", "annotation_id": "2843626", "url": "https://genius.com/2843626", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Gingerbread man run while you can", "vault_lines": ["Gingerbread man run while you can"], "meaning": "This line is a reference to The Gingerbread man which is a story about a gingerbread man who runs away from all the danger that faces him until his tragic death at the end. The most famous phrase from the story is “Run, run as fast as you can. You can’t catch me, I’m the gingerbread man .”\n\n\n\nHe’s calling other niggas “candy ass (pussy) rappers” (notice the Gingerbread Man has the same exact complexion as them) and has them running like the sweetened fuck away from the “oven” (Tyga’s heat = his gun, crew and music)", "annotation_id": "2843004", "url": "https://genius.com/2843004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Oh, you wanna beat me, how?", "vault_lines": ["Oh, you wanna beat me, how?"], "meaning": "Clearly from looking at the Forbes list Nicki Minaj is at the top of her game earning big dollars amongst the likes of Jay-z and Diddy.\n\n\n\nNow everybody wants to be at the top clearly because everybody wants to win, and the way to do that is beat the people who are at the top, and because of the fact that Nicki is amongst the people at the top these other rappers have to beat her.\n\nHaving said all of that Nicki Minaj realizes this. And in this bar “oh you wanna beat me? How?” Nicki is asking exactly how are you going to beat her as she believes she is the baddest bitch in the game!\n\nBecause of the next bar “Oh you the number one draft in the game now” she could again be responding to Kendrick’s control verse as he called out all of the best rappers in the game stating that he was coming for them, he wanted to ‘beat’ them. Even though Nicki’s name wasn’t mentioned she recognizes that she is one of the best and so knows that Kendrick wants to ‘beat’ her. (as she states in her Power 105 interview) but because as she has stated “all these bitches is her sons” that’s not going to happen. and so is asking exactly how? is he going to do that considering she is the  Mother!\nPOWER 105 INTERVIEW\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EyM_3GIiSJA", "annotation_id": "2842915", "url": "https://genius.com/2842915", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Tunechi!", "vault_lines": ["High in the video, fuck with me, hella raw"], "meaning": "This is one of Lil Wayne’s nicknames, it was given to him by his grandmother and he has been using it quite a bit lately.", "annotation_id": "2842731", "url": "https://genius.com/2842731", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Bombs in L.A., bombs in the Bay", "vault_lines": ["Bombs in L.A., bombs in the Bay"], "meaning": "Parallel to the Outkast song Bombs Over Baghdad\n\n\n\nThe hook states\n\nDon’t pull the thang out, unless you plan to bang\nBombs over Baghdad!\nDon’t even bang unless you plan to hit something\nBombs over Baghdad!\n\nThe hook compares the music industry with the 90’s Iraq campaign, suggesting we should not have started war or in this case rap unless we planned to bang KILL SADDAM who represents the rap game.\n\nHe and other rappers, from his hometown area of California, are dropping bombs (hot verses) and no rapper is safe. Maybe this is a shoutout to other California based artists like TDE and Nipsey Hussle.", "annotation_id": "2842719", "url": "https://genius.com/2842719", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Started from the, like Christina, got a million", "vault_lines": ["Started from the, like Christina, got a million"], "meaning": "The words “Started from the” is a reference to Drake’s well known 2013 anthem Started From The Bottom. However Tyga now has millions, which is a homophone to actress Christina Milian’s last name.", "annotation_id": "2842649", "url": "https://genius.com/2842649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Nigga you ain’t safe, I run with niggas like O-Dog", "vault_lines": ["Nigga you ain't safe, I run with niggas like O-Dog"], "meaning": "O Dog is an extremely violent character from the movie Menace II Society\n\nA quote from O Dog that exemplifies his violent mentality\n\nHey, you know what, nigga? You acting like a little bitch right now. You acting real paranoid and shit. Now, these motherfuckers smoked your goddam cousin in front of you, nigga! Blew his head off in front of your face, and you ain’t gonna do shit? You acting like a little bitch right now, nigga. Man, fuck that. I ain’t letting that shit ride. We gonna go in and smoke all these motherfuckers. I don’t care who the fuck out there. Goddamn it, is you down, nigga?\n\nACCEPTED COMMENT: This is the video where he said that:\nhttp://youtu.be/j-FkkpLOyOg\nIf Tyga has friends like O Dog think twice before crossing him.", "annotation_id": "2842571", "url": "https://genius.com/2842571", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Oh, you the number one draft in the league now?", "vault_lines": ["Oh, you the number one draft in the league now?"], "meaning": "Nicki goes after other female rappers…\n\nTo raise a child, it might take a village\nBut I wouldn’t know cause these bitches my sons; yes, they was, and they still is\n\n… and industry dudes…\n\nSo all you niggas toast cause all you deep throat word/Fuck fuck your Lambo, fuck fuck your Murcie\n/I got more money, in in my fucking purse\n\nNow she’s going after ANYONE who claims they’re the GOAT.\n\nThis is definitely not the first time Nicki has made sports metaphors to display her prowess. The draft is the annual selection process where NFL teams pick college football players to join and play in the subsequent season. Nicki’s rivals think they’re #1 because they’re getting picked, but they’re forgetting that Nicki is a veteran pro baller.\n\n\n\nI call the play, now do you see why / These bitches calling me Manning Eli?", "annotation_id": "2842519", "url": "https://genius.com/2842519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Lean in the drop, ice in the watch Nigga, that’s Ben & Jerry dollars, watch a nigga make a stack house", "vault_lines": ["Lean in the drop, ice in the watch"], "meaning": "Tyga’s actual watch.\n\nTyga makes a few clever references here.\n\n1) He calls the   ice  in his watch Ben & Jerry dollars. Ben & Jerry’s is an Ice Cream company with a Net Income of over $3,926,000.00.\n\n2) There is also a play on words with  “Jerry” and “Stackhouse”. Tyga is referencing the former NBA player Jerry Stackhouse.\n\n3) Indeed, if he really has “Ben & Jerry dollars”, he just might be able to build a house out of stacks. His “stackhouse” is either made of stacks (of cash), ice (columns) or could be as tough as a gingerbread house (drugs/trapping). Could be likely that he’s referring to being a gingerbread (rich drug dealer) in the next line.\n\n4) Lean is a purple drank that is commonly served with Sprite & ice. The word play in this line is a double entendre referring him “leaning” in the drop (in his whip), while he has lean, with dropped “ice” in the cup.\n\n5) His also uses “watch” twice as a homograph, referring to his ice (bling) and for his haters to watch him as he’s cruises on by. Stunting 101.", "annotation_id": "2842504", "url": "https://genius.com/2842504", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Boy, I got every award but a Heisman", "vault_lines": ["Boy, I got every award but a Heisman"], "meaning": "Wayne has been in the game for a minute, and has had a very successful career so far. He got a deal at 11 years old, and since then, he’s earned a total of 59 awards!\n\n\n\nSo I guess it is true, he’s won about every award except the Heisman. But then again, he never played NCAA Football which leaves him not applicable.", "annotation_id": "2842480", "url": "https://genius.com/2842480", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Got the coupe on Yokohamas, got the super soaker chopper", "vault_lines": ["Got the coupe on Yokohamas, got the super soaker chopper"], "meaning": "Yokohoma is a renowned Japanese tire company\n\n\n\nWayne is in the custom coupe with the guns on deck", "annotation_id": "2842477", "url": "https://genius.com/2842477", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "I can make a lion say “Meow”", "vault_lines": ["I can make a lion say \"Meow\""], "meaning": "Wayne will make the vagina sing. His girls are much wilder, so “Lion” is used as an alternative to the overused and much too tame “pussy”\nLions are known to be “Big Cats” and by saying this Lil Wayne is saying that he is a statue of person that can make a big cat do something that ordinary/small cats do. This is metaphor for a well respected person, as in he can make someone who is “Big” do something that is uncharacteristic of them. Even if that person is at the top of the food chain as a Lion is.\nCats/Pussys say meow. Lions are at the top of the cat family. Making a lion to say meow will reduce it from the top and bring him down, turning him to a pussy.", "annotation_id": "2842445", "url": "https://genius.com/2842445", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Do you see now? You playin’ D now?", "vault_lines": ["Do you see now? You playin' D now?"], "meaning": "Rappers didn’t know Nicki was ill like that. Now they are backing off. ‘Playing D’ = playing defence…ALSO ‘playing D now’, sounds like playing DENIAL, alluding to the earlier question about how these rappers didn’t know that Nicki was coming with it.\n\nTo be “In denial” is a symptom of a mental patient or “whacked out mofo” who’s on the verge of being “senile” it’s a defense mechanism that is alluded to the title of the song.", "annotation_id": "2842431", "url": "https://genius.com/2842431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Yeah, I got an Audemar, I ain’t set the time once", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I got an Audemar, I ain't set the time once"], "meaning": "An Audemar Piguet is a company that manufactures luxury swiss watches. These watches can be VERY expensive. Nicki is saying that she doesn’t use the watch for what its intended to be used for – time, instead she wears the Audemar watch to show off her immense wealth. Nicki also refers to another type of watch in the beginning of this verse called the Sky dweller.", "annotation_id": "2842427", "url": "https://genius.com/2842427", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Neighborhood nice and quiet, thought I saw Mr. Rogers, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Neighborhood nice and quiet, thought I saw Mr. Rogers, nigga"], "meaning": "Mr. Rogers was the main character from the television series  Mister Rogers' Neighborhood\".\n\nIn the beginning of each episode he sung:\n\n It’s a beautiful day in this neighborhood,\nA beautiful day for a neighbor \n\nWeezy’s neighborhood is so beautiful that it could have been the same neighborhood Mr. Rodgers was in.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gh2MSiU7gDU", "annotation_id": "2842424", "url": "https://genius.com/2842424", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Money talk, guess I got the gift of gab Don’t interject, don’t intercept", "vault_lines": ["Money talk, guess I got the gift of gab"], "meaning": "The gift of gab is an idiom meaning eloquence, the ability to talk convincingly. If we’re following the figure of speech – money talks – this means that Nicki talks well: she’s got a lot of money.\n\n\n\nAnd don’t you dare interrupt when her money is speaking!", "annotation_id": "2842412", "url": "https://genius.com/2842412", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Ride down ya block, doors 12 o’clock", "vault_lines": ["Ride down ya block, doors 12 o'clock"], "meaning": "“Twelve o'clock” is a phrase used to compare the hands on a clock at 12 to the position of motorcycles or, in this case, Lamborghini doors when they are straight in the air.\n\nNicki’s Pink Lamborghini Aventador has scissor doors (they open upward).\n\n\n\nShe actually likes to drive with the doors up, but she may not encourage this because you can get pulled over by cops like she did…\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u9eU_Zr5cLs#t=3m30", "annotation_id": "2842384", "url": "https://genius.com/2842384", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Senile", "line": "Sky dweller check, helicopter pad", "vault_lines": ["Sky dweller check, helicopter pad"], "meaning": "Sky Dweller is a model of Rolex watches that sells for about $45k. It’s not the first time Nicki invokes this piece as a prime example of her icy wrists.\n\n\n\nYou know what else dwells in the sky? Helicopters. And Nicki has her own air ride landing on a private helipad.", "annotation_id": "2842364", "url": "https://genius.com/2842364", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
