{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "Tell everybody, everybody that you know Tell everybody that you know That I don’t love you no more And that’s one thing that you know, that you know", "vault_lines": ["And that you know"], "meaning": "Kanye has accepted the fact that they have broke knows she will tell everyone. What he means by “And that’s one thing that you know” Is that they both know they are broken up, but only one will announce it to everyone (being the girl)", "annotation_id": "37685691", "url": "https://genius.com/37685691", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "But this is farewell, yeah", "vault_lines": ["But this is farewell, yeah"], "meaning": "Just like Jay-Z on “Diamonds From Sierra Leonne (Remix)” Wayne ends his verse off with a Good-bye to the listener.", "annotation_id": "37300415", "url": "https://genius.com/37300415", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "And it’s all because of you, girl, we through", "vault_lines": ["And it's all because of you, girl, we through"], "meaning": "Ye blames his ex for the end of their relationship. This is pretty consistent throughout the album.", "annotation_id": "35534480", "url": "https://genius.com/35534480", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "Okay, I’m back up on my grind You do you and I’m just gon’ do mine You do you ‘cause I’m just gon’ be fine Okay, I got you out my mind", "vault_lines": ["Okay, I'm back up on my grind"], "meaning": "As we move through the album Ye seems to be finding some closure. In this line he feels like he’s finally moving on, back to doing his own thing, finally not obsessing over his ex.\nEven though we see a glimpse of Ye improving going back to the chorus it’s obvious that at night, things aren’t going so well for him", "annotation_id": "35534466", "url": "https://genius.com/35534466", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "The clouds is in my vision, look how high that I be getting", "vault_lines": ["The clouds is in my vision, look how high that I be getting"], "meaning": "double entrende: the “cloud” image of simply being vertically high, and his vision clouding up because of how high he is off of drugs.", "annotation_id": "34804098", "url": "https://genius.com/34804098", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "I thought we were committed I thought we were cemented, I really thought we meant it", "vault_lines": ["Babygirl, I'm finished, I thought we were committed"], "meaning": "Kanye and Alexis Phifer were planning to get engaged but it was then cancelled and they broke apart.", "annotation_id": "32797957", "url": "https://genius.com/32797957", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "Well, how did you get there?", "vault_lines": ["Well, how did you get there?"], "meaning": "He wonders how she ended up in his nightmare, implying that he didn’t expect to see her there or that he wishes she wasn’t there.", "annotation_id": "29952839", "url": "https://genius.com/29952839", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "I got my life and it’s my only one I got the night, I’m running from the sun", "vault_lines": ["I got the night, I'm running from the sun"], "meaning": "Kanye is telling the person that he’s gonna break up with her. Saying “I got my life and it’s only one” Which means that he only has one life and he dosen’t want to waste it on her. “running from the sun” means that he is running away from this lady and never wants to meet them again.", "annotation_id": "29732651", "url": "https://genius.com/29732651", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "So good night, I’m headed out the door Door, door, door, door After tonight, there will be no return", "vault_lines": ["So good night, I'm headed out the door"], "meaning": "He is breaking up with this person. He is getting out of their apartment and he will never come back to this lady because of the heartbreak that she caused.", "annotation_id": "29732647", "url": "https://genius.com/29732647", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "That you know Tell everybody that you know That I don’t love you no more And that’s one thing that you know, that you know", "vault_lines": ["And that you know"], "meaning": "Kanye has accepted the fact that they have broke knows she will tell everyone. What he means by “And that’s one you know” Is that they both know they are broken up, but only one will announce it to everyone (being the girl)", "annotation_id": "29732642", "url": "https://genius.com/29732642", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "After tonight, I’m taking off on the road I’m taking off on the road And that you know", "vault_lines": ["After tonight, I'm taking off on the road"], "meaning": "Kanye is finally deciding to leave this person.\n\nThis could be a slight reference to something he said on “Heartless”:\n\nAnd you can’t make it right\nI’m gonna take off tonight into the night", "annotation_id": "3022714", "url": "https://genius.com/3022714", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "You always thought I was always wrong Well, now, you know", "vault_lines": ["You always thought I was always wrong"], "meaning": "A moment ago he said the person was off his mind. Now here he is, thinking again about how they always thought and/or told him he was wrong. A la fake it ‘til you make it, he’s outwardly trying to say and show he’s over it, but he’s sort of not because it’s still about trying to prove something to the other person.\n\n‘Ye is also making sure that the person knows it was THEIR fault:\n\nYeah, you always thought I was wrong, well guess what? I wasn’t! And now you know… So tell all your friends how it was your fault that we ended and I don’t love you no more. Not mine.", "annotation_id": "759139", "url": "https://genius.com/759139", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "I’m cold (Yeah) I’m cold (Yeah) I’m cold (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I got the night, I'm running from the sun"], "meaning": "The whole album has a very cold and distant feeling to it. Hearing Wayne’s voice on Auto-Tune only furthers that effect. Nightmares can often be seen as cold places to be.\n\nCold also means heartless and is another way of saying awesome, so it might have a triple meaning to it. Heartless, awesome, and actually cold.\n\nCold is also a reference to winter, which he’s just been through/going through. See: Coldest Winter", "annotation_id": "217165", "url": "https://genius.com/217165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "You think your **** don’t stank, but you are Mrs. Pee-yew", "vault_lines": ["You think your **** don't stank, but you are Mrs. Pee-yew"], "meaning": "He is saying that she thinks she can do no wrong but in reality she is the one who is causing their problems.\nAnd, “pee-yew” is a noise people make when things stink, so she thinks she doesn’t stink although other people say differently.\n\nThis is also a reference to OutKast’s song “Roses”\n\nAlong with this being one of only 2 explicit lyrics on the entire album, the final release of the album saw the word “shit” taken out of the track.", "annotation_id": "100429", "url": "https://genius.com/100429", "state": "accepted", "votes": 114, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "And the night is young, the drinks is cold The stars is out, I’m ready to go", "vault_lines": ["And the night is young, the drinks is cold"], "meaning": "After such a quick rebound, he’s ready to hit the clubs and find somebody else.\n\n#Double Entendre\n1. “The stars is out”: “Stars” refer to stars in the sky (distant suns). Nights when stars are visible are much colder than cloudy nights, as the clouds insulate the Earth.\n2. The stars is out: “Stars” refer to famous folks that are always in the clubs that Ye frequents.\n\nStars\n\n\n\nAlso Stars", "annotation_id": "79811", "url": "https://genius.com/79811", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "line": "’Cause we were once a fairy tale", "vault_lines": ["'Cause we were once a fairy tale"], "meaning": "A lot of relationships can seem like a fairytale at first, usually because there isn’t anything to argue about yet.\n\nAlso, Kanye West was in a short film entitled We Were Once A Fairytale in which this song was played.", "annotation_id": "79809", "url": "https://genius.com/79809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "See You In My Nightmares", "status": "done", "targets": 16, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Kanye-west-see-you-in-my-nightmares-lyrics", "genius_title": "See You in My Nightmares", "genius_id": 2319, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Section", "line": "I got a scale, I’m ducking from 12, eat Benihana’s like McDonald’s", "vault_lines": ["I got a scale, I'm ducking from 12, eat Benihana’s like McDonald's"], "meaning": "Chainz has rapped extensively about his history dealing drugs throughout his career, and the scale he talks about here is what he weighs his product with. Also, a drug dealer needs to stay away from the police, and a slang term for the police is “12”. Chainz has had run-ins with the police before, as detailed previously in his music.\n\nTwelve came through and we had for the fishes\nGot locked up in school, we ain’t worried ‘bout detention\n\nAlso, as the title of his latest mixtape, Hibachi for Lunch, suggests, 2 Chainz eats at the hibachi restaurant Benihana as casually as a normal human may eat at McDonald’s; this is probably because he has sufficient income to eat at this rather expensive restaurant with such frequency.", "annotation_id": "11618729", "url": "https://genius.com/11618729", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Section", "line": "I got the loud of course", "vault_lines": ["I got the loud of course"], "meaning": "“Loud” is slang for high quality marijuana that gives off a strong smell. Chainz must have a whole lot of it if he smokes as much as he claims to in his song “100 Joints.”\n\nNo matter what they say I smoke 100 joints a day\nLaying by my chopper, chopper laying by my safe\nNo matter what they say I smoke 100 joints a day", "annotation_id": "11293038", "url": "https://genius.com/11293038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Section", "line": "Fuck my girl with no protection", "vault_lines": ["Fuck my girl with no protection"], "meaning": "Chainz doesn’t use a condom when he has sex with his girl. It doesn’t look like he’s learned to wrap it up from his baby mama woes.\n\nI said I take care of my kids but I’m flexin' on my baby mama\nI’m like, “Damn, I shoulda wore a condom!”", "annotation_id": "11293025", "url": "https://genius.com/11293025", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Section", "line": "I went to jail, I might go to Hell, I used to sell drugs to my momma", "vault_lines": ["I went to jail, I might go to Hell, I used to sell drugs to my momma"], "meaning": "It’s reality. And that’s a reality for half the hood.", "annotation_id": "8975888", "url": "https://genius.com/8975888", "state": "verified", "votes": 109, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Section", "line": "I went to jail, I might go to Hell, I used to sell drugs to my momma", "vault_lines": ["I went to jail, I might go to Hell, I used to sell drugs to my momma"], "meaning": "For me, music is very therapeutic. I like getting into a booth. I never been into talking to a psychiatrist or counselor. I handle my stuff a different way.\n\nI’m going to give you a scenario. You live in a trap; you don’t come visit. You live in a trap where it’s a drug infested neighborhood where people can actually go up the street and get dope.\n\nSo imagine you stay in this neighborhood, and you’re dealing with somebody in your family that you love very much, having a habit that you or they can’t control. They make dope, some of it clean, some of it fucked up. Do you send them down the street to do something?\n\nYou can look at a nigga like, “you ain’t shit. You fucking evil devil” or you can look at a nigga like, “I understand.” If you haven’t been there before… It’s stuff that niggas’ll never fucking understand.\n\nI’m still not comfortable talking about this shit because it some fucked up shit that a lot of you niggas wouldn’t even understand.", "annotation_id": "8975193", "url": "https://genius.com/8975193", "state": "verified", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Section", "line": "I got them commas on commas", "vault_lines": ["I got them commas on commas"], "meaning": "2 Chainz’s net worth is reportedly $6 million.", "annotation_id": "8932795", "url": "https://genius.com/8932795", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Section", "line": "I got that money, money’s not a problem", "vault_lines": ["I got that money, money’s not a problem"], "meaning": "Weezy uses two allusions to his own works to express one of the more common sentiments in Hip-Hop: wealth.\n\nThe first segment references an earlier track off of The Carter III entitled “Got Money”, while the following segment references a more recent work.", "annotation_id": "8768538", "url": "https://genius.com/8768538", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Section", "line": "My favorite rapper is me", "vault_lines": ["My favorite rapper is me"], "meaning": "Chainz channels his inner Kanye, revealing an egotistic side to himself.\n\nStraight from the Book of Ye:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/kanyewset/status/563798479349104641", "annotation_id": "8768503", "url": "https://genius.com/8768503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Section", "line": "Shawty said she wanted Houston’s, so I flew her to Texas", "vault_lines": ["Shawty said she wanted Houston's, so I flew her to Texas"], "meaning": "Houston’s is an upscale American casual dining restaurant chain, owned by Hillstone Restaurant Group, whose main corporate headquarters is based in Beverly Hills, California.\n\nIn Atlanta, Houston’s is prevalent in the affluent Buckhead neighborhood, where 2 Chainz frequents.\n\nOverall, this is a play on words where the rapper is saying he’s more than capable of taking her out to enjoy fine dining, but he also has the ability fly her out to Houston, Texas (where there are also two Houston’s restaurants).", "annotation_id": "8766510", "url": "https://genius.com/8766510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
