{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "I am just a Martian, ain’t nobody else on this Planet, I know, see, I live by my only", "vault_lines": ["I am just a Martian, ain't nobody else on this"], "meaning": "A popular Wayne trope that began with the line “We are not the same, I’m a Martian” in his “Show Me What You Got” freestyle from 2006. (That line would subsequently inspire the Cool & Dre number “Phone Home” on 2008’s Tha Carter III.)", "annotation_id": "14512502", "url": "https://genius.com/14512502", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "Mannie got this fuckin’ beat poundin’, it’s poundin’ But it was just lost until I found it, I found it Stole it like a scoundrel, Hollygrove hound it Put this bitch to sleep, fuckin’ right, I nightgowned it", "vault_lines": ["Mannie got this fuckin' beat poundin', it's poundin'"], "meaning": "Weezy may have hijacked this particular Mannie Fresh beat from T.I.’s “Top Back,” but he makes it clear (compliments to T.I. in the intro notwithstanding) that only his own freestyling here finally does the beat justice. (This song is further confirmation of the claim Weezy made in Da Drought 3’s opening song, “Intro” to the effect that “[he] can jump on any n***a song and make a part two.”)", "annotation_id": "14512443", "url": "https://genius.com/14512443", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "And that white widow weed out the jar is a must", "vault_lines": ["And that white widow weed out the jar is a must"], "meaning": "White Widow is a strain of cannabis whose popularity in the US soared around the time of Da Drought 3 in part due to frequent mentions on the Showtime comedy-drama Weeds.", "annotation_id": "14511628", "url": "https://genius.com/14511628", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "Yeah, baby, we ballin’ like Rawlings and Spalding", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, baby, we ballin' like Rawlings and Spalding"], "meaning": "Tunechi spends his money carelessly, because he knows he’s going to make more of it. In this simile, he compares the metaphorical ‘ballin’ to the literal basketball Spalding, and the baseball equipment company Rawlings.", "annotation_id": "2880113", "url": "https://genius.com/2880113", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "Young Money, motherfucker, know you worried ’bout us Cash Money, motherfucker, CMR, I trust", "vault_lines": ["Young Money, motherfucker, know you worried 'bout us"], "meaning": "Young Money is the label Wayne himself founded in 2006.\n\n\n\nCash Money is the label Birdman and his brother Ronald “Slim” Williams founded in 1991. They signed Wayne back when he was just a teenager.", "annotation_id": "2644803", "url": "https://genius.com/2644803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "I be with Jim Jones and we be ballin’, ballin’?", "vault_lines": ["I be with Jim Jones and we be ballin', ballin'?"], "meaning": "“BALLIN'!” is Jim Jones' frequently-used ad-lib that was popularized with his song We Fly High.", "annotation_id": "2644793", "url": "https://genius.com/2644793", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "Got a black-and-gold soul with a fresh New Orleans fitted And a collar Polo and a pair of Bally bucks", "vault_lines": ["Got a black-and-gold soul with a fresh New Orleans fitted"], "meaning": "Wayne lists off his wardrobe here.\n\nA fitted hat with the colors of the New Orleans Saints:\n\n\n\nA collared Polo Ralph Lauren shirt:\n\n\n\nAnd a pair of Bally Shoes:", "annotation_id": "2644779", "url": "https://genius.com/2644779", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "Niggas talkin’ cheap, tell ’em niggas, “Pipe down, bitch”", "vault_lines": ["Niggas talkin' cheap, tell 'em niggas, \"Pipe down, bitch\""], "meaning": "“Pipe down” is another way of saying “shut up”. It was originally a naval expression, as the Pipe Down was the last signal from the Bosun’s pipe each day which meant “lights out” and “silence”.", "annotation_id": "66826", "url": "https://genius.com/66826", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "Ayy, that is my brothers, ladies and gentlemen, T.I., and he is the king, bitch", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, that is my brothers, ladies and gentlemen, T.I., and he is the king, bitch"], "meaning": "T.I.’s nickname is The King, and his original song “Top Back,” which Wayne is rapping over, is off of the album, King", "annotation_id": "30937", "url": "https://genius.com/30937", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "This is Da Drought 3 And it’s been a minute since I’ve rapped on a Mannie Fresh beat, but uh", "vault_lines": ["This is Da Drought 3"], "meaning": "This track comes from the mixtape Da Drought 3. The beat is T.I.’s song “Top Back” which was produced by former Cash Money Records in-house producer Mannie Fresh. Wayne hadn’t collaborated with Mannie since Tha Carter.", "annotation_id": "21149", "url": "https://genius.com/21149", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "I am so, so New Orleans Like 1825 Tulane", "vault_lines": ["I am so, so New Orleans"], "meaning": "1825 Tulane was the address of Rosenberg’s, a New Orleans furniture store famous for its commercials, which pretty much became an in-joke among residents of the town\n\nThe Rosenbergs literally bought up all the radio commercial time in New Orleans for a while, and the ads always end the same way: a very creepy little girl’s voice singing their address (1825 Tulane) and then giggling –the melody (and creepiness) of which Lil Wayne mimics with surprising accuracy here (even the giggle!). See an ad here", "annotation_id": "18911", "url": "https://genius.com/18911", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "Pint of DJ Screw and that Hawaiian, I am", "vault_lines": ["Pint of DJ Screw and that Hawaiian, I am"], "meaning": "DJ Screw was a DJ from Texas that died from an overdose of syrup (Wayne’s favorite drug); hence, Wayne named his syrup after him (he does the same thing in “Watch My Shoes,” calling his weed “Bob Marley”.\n\nSyrup is usually mixed into another drink, and Wayne’s mixer of choice is Hawaiian Punch.", "annotation_id": "18854", "url": "https://genius.com/18854", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "T.I.P.", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, that is my brothers, ladies and gentlemen, T.I., and he is the king, bitch"], "meaning": "T.I.’s alter ego, and his original stage name. He dropped the P to avoid confusion with Q-Tip.", "annotation_id": "18734", "url": "https://genius.com/18734", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Seat Down Low", "line": "What happens on my bus stays on my bus", "vault_lines": ["What happens on my bus stays on my bus"], "meaning": "Actually, Wayne has been arrested multiple times for incidents occurring on or near his bus. This is also a play on the famous phrase, “What happens in Vegas, stays in Vegas”.", "annotation_id": "18731", "url": "https://genius.com/18731", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
