{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scottie", "line": "Just pass that weed like flyin’ colors", "vault_lines": ["Just pass that weed like flyin' colors"], "meaning": "When someone passes a test in school very well, they’re said to have ‘passed with flying colors’. Wayne wants his blunt to be passed to him like a student passes tests.", "annotation_id": "36102599", "url": "https://genius.com/36102599", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scottie", "line": "Smoking on Cee-Lo Green, lighting up a big gift", "vault_lines": ["Smoking on Cee-Lo Green, lighting up a big gift"], "meaning": "I think he’s saying “lighting up a Big Gipp” referencing the group Goodie Mob who both Cee-Lo and Gipp were members", "annotation_id": "20915842", "url": "https://genius.com/20915842", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scottie", "line": "When I’m in a room, if these walls could talk I’m sure they’d prefer to be non-verbal", "vault_lines": ["When I'm in a room, if these walls could talk"], "meaning": "Wayne has used this Phrase before to express his presence and energy in a room\nIn  https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-i-like-the-view-lyrics He states, “If these walls could talk, they probably won’t shut up.”", "annotation_id": "20902795", "url": "https://genius.com/20902795", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scottie", "line": "Might cut off my hair ’cause these hoes is Delilah’s", "vault_lines": ["Might cut off my hair 'cause these hoes is Delilah's"], "meaning": "Wayne references the biblical story of Samson and Delilah. Samson’s secret to his great strength was his long hair and Delilah was sent to seduce him and cut off his hair in order to lose his strength and power.", "annotation_id": "18099314", "url": "https://genius.com/18099314", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scottie", "line": "That’s why I got a ice box where My heart used to be in this cold world I’m a monster, a cold blooded monster I’m colder than fuckin’ Moscow, kilos, ounces, GRAMMYs, Oscars Knock you off your fuckin’ high horse Like a cold-blooded jouster, fightin’ for my life", "vault_lines": ["That's why I got a ice box where"], "meaning": "Wayne’s hometown, New Orleans, is infamous for its high levels of wretchedness; High crime rates, gangs, drugs, poverty, insecurity, all have been the reality for many of its citizens (especially minorities) for decades now. Wayne experienced a similar situation during his childhood.\n\nHe was fortunate enough though to break out of the misery thanks to his rap skills that he had started developing at a young age. The rap mogul, Birdman, and his brother, Slim, took Wayne under their wings when the latter was just 9 years old; he was touring nationwide by the time he hit 15.\n\nFrom rags to riches, from dealing with drugs (=“kilos,ounces”) to achieving humongous success and fame (=“Grammies, Oscars”), this whole time he’s been fighting like “a cold-blooded monster” to sustain some sort of security of his and his children’s, inside the hood as well as outside of it.", "annotation_id": "18039881", "url": "https://genius.com/18039881", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scottie", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-scottie-lyrics", "genius_title": "Scottie", "genius_id": 3088569, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "Ah, I got a question, where was protection? How did this happen? Can we go backwards? (Can we go backwards?) [Outro: XXXTENTACION] I got a question I got a question, I got a question, shooter School shooter, I taught ’em a lesson Yeah", "vault_lines": ["Ah, I got a question, where was protection?"], "meaning": "X is troubeled by the fact that there was no protection and because of that one of the students had to protect the other kids by shielding his classmates while he was getting shot at. The student’s name is Anthony Borges, the young man is credited with saving up to 20 lives during the Parkland, Florida, school rampage.\n\n\n\nThis question is aimet at the Broward County Sheriff’s Office due to their response, or lack thereof, to the Marjory Stoneman Douglas High shooting that killed 17 and injured 17 on Valentine’s Day 2018 in Parkland, Florida.\n\nThe sheriff’s deputies as well as local police officers stayed outside the scene of the tragedy as it was occurring, leading to several resignations and the removal of Sheriff Scott Israel. The Sheriff’s Office was also criticized for allowing the perpetrator to purchase firearms even after several incidents of threatening behaviour.", "annotation_id": "22106736", "url": "https://genius.com/22106736", "state": "pending", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "The innocent, who the fuck’s protectin’ us?", "vault_lines": ["The innocent, who the fuck's protectin' us?"], "meaning": "The line is directed to the Broward County Sheriff’s Office due to their response, or lack thereof, to the Marjory Stoneman Douglas High shooting that killed 17 and injured 17 on Valentine’s Day 2018 in Parkland, Florida.\n\nThe sheriff’s deputies as well as local police officers stayed outside the scene of the tragedy as it was occurring, leading to several resignations and the removal of Sheriff Scott Israel. The Sheriff’s Office was also criticized for allowing the perpetrator to purchase firearms even after several incidents of threatening behaviour.", "annotation_id": "18843748", "url": "https://genius.com/18843748", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "Get in front of my classmates and kill myself", "vault_lines": ["Get in front of my classmates and kill myself"], "meaning": "Jeremy Wade Delle was a 15-year-old high school student from Richardson, Texas.\n\n\n\nOn January 8th, 1991, Jeremy left his second-period English class after being told by the teacher to get a late slip. He returned with a .357 Magnum revolver and committed suicide in front of his classmates at Richardson High School. This tragedy would become the inspiration for Pearl Jam’s song “Jeremy”.", "annotation_id": "18838292", "url": "https://genius.com/18838292", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "Kids at school callin’ me different, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Kids at school callin' me different, yeah"], "meaning": "A school shooter reference guide posted by the Federal Bureau of Investigation notes that 75% of school shooters are motivated by the fact that they feel bullied or persecuted by others.", "annotation_id": "18792749", "url": "https://genius.com/18792749", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "I don’t need no school, I got internet, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I don't need no school, I got internet, yeah"], "meaning": "There is a large population of students today who believe that you can learn much more from the internet than you can learn at school, as explained in this Quora discussion.  Internet access is becoming increasingly common and accessible among the youth each year, and a study shows that screen time affects mental health.", "annotation_id": "18792732", "url": "https://genius.com/18792732", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "A school shooter, I just need attention, yeah, uh", "vault_lines": ["A school shooter, I just need attention, yeah, uh"], "meaning": "A school shooter reference guide posted by the Federal Bureau of Investigation notes that 24% of school shootings are motivated by the desire for attention or recognition.  In this verse, Wayne steps into the shoes of a school shooter to explain common motives for their attacks.", "annotation_id": "18790992", "url": "https://genius.com/18790992", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "Or the semi-TEC at school, what’s the bigger threat?", "vault_lines": ["Or the semi-TEC at school, what's the bigger threat?"], "meaning": "A “semi-TEC” refers to the Intratec TEC-9 semi-automatic pistol. The gun gained infamy after it was used by one of the two perpetrators of the Columbine High School Massacre that occurred on April 20th, 1999 that killed 15, including the shooters, and wounded 24 as well as the 101 California Street Shooting on July 1st, 1993 that killed 9, including the shooter, and wounded 6.\n\nThe gun was discontinued in 2001 after the manufacturer, Intratec, went out of business.", "annotation_id": "18622093", "url": "https://genius.com/18622093", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "Boy, you better buckle up ’cause I got questions for you fucks, I’ve had enough", "vault_lines": ["Boy, you better buckle up 'cause I got questions for you fucks, I've had enough"], "meaning": "This line is structured similarily to another line on X’s February 2016 song, “#ImSippinTeaInYoHood,” where he says:\n\nHow these pussy niggas moving day to day? I’ve had enough (Yeah)", "annotation_id": "18608081", "url": "https://genius.com/18608081", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "Saved by the bell, I couldn’t hear the bell", "vault_lines": ["Saved by the bell, I couldn't hear the bell"], "meaning": "“Saved by the bell” is an idiom that expresses the idea that someone is ‘saved’ from experiencing a bad outcome of something at the last minute. It came from the popular NBC series of the same name, which ran from 1989 from 1993.\n\nWayne uses it as a way to say he never got out of these bad outcomes, hence “I can’t hear the bell.”", "annotation_id": "18601117", "url": "https://genius.com/18601117", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "Give me bad grades, I don’t give a F", "vault_lines": ["Give me bad grades, I don't give a F"], "meaning": "Wayne uses a clever double entendre describing the grading system and his wild tendencies. The common grading scale is a system of recognition for performance in a class, with the best results being an A+ grade and the worst result being a Fail (F). At most schools, an F is earned after a student gets scores from 0% to 59% in a class, equivalent to a 0 GPA.\n\n\n\nWayne relates this to his attitude, as “don’t give a F” is an abbreviated slang of “Don’t give a fuck,” meaning Wayne does not care about his poor grades or the consequences that come with failing.\n\nWayne dropped out of school at age 14 to focus on creating music, although he was an honors student before abandoning his education.", "annotation_id": "18592929", "url": "https://genius.com/18592929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "School Shooters", "line": "Triple X, I just popped a triple X, uh", "vault_lines": ["Triple X, I just popped a triple X, uh"], "meaning": "Wayne puns XXXTENTACION’s name to the taking of MDMA, or ecstasy pills. Coincidentally, Wayne was arrested for the suspicion of possessing drug paraphernalia, cocaine, and ecstasy back in 2008.\n\nWayne has contorted X’s name in music before, specifically on their September 2018 posthumous collaboration, “Don’t Cry”:\n\nBut if heaven’s as good as advertised\nI want a triple extension on my motherfuckin' afterlife\nRest in paradise", "annotation_id": "18519519", "url": "https://genius.com/18519519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
