{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "Scarface with diamond teeth, haha!", "vault_lines": ["Scarface with diamond teeth, haha!"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has got bling on his teeth, hence “Scarface with diamond teeth”.", "annotation_id": "20961874", "url": "https://genius.com/20961874", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "On the for reala, my nigga, just call me Scarface On the for reala, my nigga, just call me Scarface (All I have in this world, all I have in this world) On the for reala, my nigga, just call me Scarface Nobody know my name, they only know my face (All I have in this world, all I have in this world) On the for reala, my nigga, just call me Scarface (All I have in this world, all I have in this world) Nobody know my name, they only know my face (All I have in this world, all I have in this world) On the for reala, my nigga, just call me Scarface", "vault_lines": ["All I have in this world, all I have in this world (What up, Blood?)"], "meaning": "Wayne wants people to call him Scarface.\n\nScarface was the name of a 1983 film about a powerful drug kingpin named Tony Montana. Wayne thinks his drug dealing game is as good as Tony Montana so he wants to be respected like him.\n\nWayne has even said before that one of the songs on his Rebirth album was inspired by the movie Scarface. On the track “On Fire”, Wayne samples the song “She’s On Fire” which was part of the Scarface soundtrack.\n\nhttp://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/scarface/images/5/5c/Scarface.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20120324032345&path-prefix=en", "annotation_id": "13332427", "url": "https://genius.com/13332427", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "A devil in the flesh, a rebel at its best, no complainin’ We live in Hell and I’m blessed, Scarface", "vault_lines": ["A devil in the flesh, a rebel at its best, no complainin'"], "meaning": "Life is hell, and Lil Wayne claims that he is the devil so he’s blessed to be living in hell (earth).\n\n\n\nQuote from Tony Montana (Scarface):\n“You think you can take me? You need a fuckin' army if you’re gonna take me! You hear?! C'mon! I’ll take you all to fuckin' Hell!”", "annotation_id": "9190528", "url": "https://genius.com/9190528", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "All I have in this world, all I have in this world (What up, Blood?) All I have in this world, all I have in this world", "vault_lines": ["All I have in this world, all I have in this world (What up, Blood?)"], "meaning": "… is my balls and my word.\n\nOnly right to start off a track called “Scarface” with a Scarface reference.\n\nhttp://youtu.be/zIRwd1S26Ik?t=7s", "annotation_id": "3342211", "url": "https://genius.com/3342211", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "Let me bloom, let me boom", "vault_lines": ["M.O.B, let me bloom, let me boom"], "meaning": "Blooming and booming are two completely different processes in life: one is creating it and the other is taking it.\n\n\n\nAlthough they may seem radically different, the attribute of starting small and going big is shared by both and is how Wayne has traversed his career: starting small and gaining popularity over time", "annotation_id": "2989423", "url": "https://genius.com/2989423", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "Tough as Bamm-Bamm from Bedrock I’m tied to the game like wedlock", "vault_lines": ["Tough as Bamm-Bamm from Bedrock"], "meaning": "Reference to the Flintstones strong infant character Bamm-Bamm, living in the town of Bedrock.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AOWR0CfMUZE\n\nWayne’s dedicated to the rap game as if they were married.", "annotation_id": "2649299", "url": "https://genius.com/2649299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "These motherfuckers the prey; I’m the Predator, see me dreadlocks", "vault_lines": ["These motherfuckers the prey; I'm the Predator, see me dreadlocks"], "meaning": "Wayne bragging about his mic skills yet again. Here he’s saying other rappers are his prey while he’s the predator.\n\nThis is also a reference to the 1987 film Predator.\n\nThe titular monster from the film appears to sport a set of dreads, much like Wayne’s.", "annotation_id": "2590913", "url": "https://genius.com/2590913", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "Lord, protect me from my friends, I can take care of my enemies", "vault_lines": ["Lord, protect me from my friends, I can take care of my enemies"], "meaning": "He can take care of the blunt enemies, but he needs a little help with the backstabbers.\n\nThis is similar to a quote attributed to Jean Hérault, sieur de Gourville (1625 – 1703)\n\nDefend me from my friends; I can defend myself from my enemies”", "annotation_id": "47639", "url": "https://genius.com/47639", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "Say “Hello red dot” Say “Goodbye life” and say “Hello Satan”", "vault_lines": [", say \"Hello red dot\""], "meaning": "Weezy will kill you with a sniper rifle with a laser sight and send you to hell\n\nAlso a reference to the Predator two lines ago, who rocked laser sights", "annotation_id": "33376", "url": "https://genius.com/33376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "Six degrees, leanin’ on that prometha-tha-tha-thazine", "vault_lines": ["Six degrees, leanin' on that prometha-tha-tha-thazine"], "meaning": "Promethazine is one of the main ingredients of cough syrup (which Wayne had an addiction to).\n\nTo “lean” is to be high on cough syrup. Weezy quantifies his lean at 6°", "annotation_id": "33373", "url": "https://genius.com/33373", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "Go to Iraq And get a car with gas and tell them crackers, “War with that”", "vault_lines": ["And get a car with gas and tell them crackers, \"War with that\""], "meaning": "At the time this song was recorded (2007), gas prices were extremely high. Weezy, who blasted Bush in a track off his mixtape Dedication 2, further scolds the government due to war and gas prices", "annotation_id": "33371", "url": "https://genius.com/33371", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "I am soon to get all my chips and doubloons", "vault_lines": ["I am soon to get all my chips and doubloons"], "meaning": "Money.\n\nChips comes from poker chips, of course, while doubloons is a bit more complex.\n\nThe doubloon was a Spanish coin worth two escudos, derived from “doblón,” the Spanish word for “double”\n\nWayne, from New Orleans, may be familiar with them as fake doubloons are typically thrown around as part of the Mardi Gras celebration there.", "annotation_id": "33370", "url": "https://genius.com/33370", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "line": "They know where Carter at, straight off the launchin’ pad", "vault_lines": ["They know where Carter at, straight off the launchin' pad"], "meaning": "Weezy’s fame (and money) just keep going higher and higher, just like a rocket taking off from a launching pad\n\nAlso, it sets up the reference to the Moon and Mars in the next line", "annotation_id": "32167", "url": "https://genius.com/32167", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scarface", "status": "done", "targets": 14, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-scarface-lyrics", "genius_title": "Scarface", "genius_id": 833, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scared of the Dark", "line": "[Bridge: XXXTENTACION]", "vault_lines": ["I'm not scared of the dark"], "meaning": "This bridge was a scrapped verse, originally a part of “Fuck Love” featuring Trippie Redd. Another one of X’s previous songs, a part of his project 17. It was scrapped because, X didn’t like the verse.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/uFpBmVpWmmI?si=2yY7T6KZH5rXdEs7", "annotation_id": "30797433", "url": "https://genius.com/30797433", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scared of the Dark", "line": "I’m behind the trigger, what if I am the target? Deep sigh, a sayōnara, I ain’t afraid to die It’s either goodbye or good mornin’, and the skies start to fallin’ And I’ma shine in the darkness", "vault_lines": ["I'm behind the trigger, what if I am the target?"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is referring to his suicide attempt when he was 12 years old and that he isn’t afraid of leaving this world if he has to, using the word “sayōnara”, which means goodbye.\nHe’ll shine in the darkness of his death because of his cemented status in hip-hop and the legacy he’s already left behind.", "annotation_id": "25554167", "url": "https://genius.com/25554167", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scared of the Dark", "line": "In my feelings, ****, let’s ride", "vault_lines": ["In my feelings, ****, let's ride"], "meaning": "In the scrapped version of Bhad Bhabie’s “Trust Me,” X says, “In my feelings, ho, let’s ride.”\n\nThe decision to censor “ho” was likely made due to the movie’s target demographic.", "annotation_id": "16095691", "url": "https://genius.com/16095691", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scared of the Dark", "line": "Tunechi", "vault_lines": ["I'm not scared of the dark"], "meaning": "Tunechi is a nickname Lil Wayne made for himself based on the words Gucci (an Italian luxury fashion brand) and “Tune”, a nickname given to Wayne by his grandmother. He uses the nickname Tune more often nowadays due to the passing of his grandmother.\n\nOn previous songs, the name “Tunechi” was changed to Lil Tunechi based on the Lil in Lil Wayne:\n\nIt’s Lil Tunechi\nI don’t rap, I film movies", "annotation_id": "16045865", "url": "https://genius.com/16045865", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scared of the Dark", "line": "Big MAC to the side", "vault_lines": ["Big MAC to the side"], "meaning": "The MAC-11 is subcompact automatic sub-machine gun. The gun was created in 1970 by Gordon Ingram. They have a rate of fire of 1200 rounds per minute (around 20 rounds per second). It is lethal to around 50 meters for a .45 ACP round and 70 meters for a 9x19mm Parabellum.", "annotation_id": "16010673", "url": "https://genius.com/16010673", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scared of the Dark", "line": "I ain’t never terrified, I ain’t never petrified You know I see dead people, I just tell ’em get a life", "vault_lines": ["I ain't never terrified, I ain't never petrified"], "meaning": "“I see dead people” is an iconic quotable from the mystery movie The Sixth Sense by prolific director M. Night Shyamalan:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZSNyiSetZ8Y\nWayne claims that while he sees dead people, he is so used to them that he shrugs them off and tells them to “get a life” in jest of their dead state.", "annotation_id": "16010514", "url": "https://genius.com/16010514", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scared of the Dark", "line": "I’m not scared of the dark I’m not running, running, running No, I’m not afraid of the fall I’m not scared, not at all Why would a star, a star ever be afraid of the dark? I’m not scared I’m not scared, neither are the stars I’m not scared of the dark Of the dark, mmm", "vault_lines": ["I'm not scared of the dark"], "meaning": "In this chorus, Ty uses “darkness” as a metaphor for the unknown and “falling” as one for death. After his life experiences and time as a celebrity, he has “outgrown” his fear of them, similar to the way a young child would outgrow their literal fear of falling in the dark.\n\n\n\nThese lyrics help contribute to the theme of evolution and growing which is portrayed throughout the song and movie.", "annotation_id": "16010453", "url": "https://genius.com/16010453", "state": "accepted", "votes": 127, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scared of the Dark", "line": "If I could count the tears I’ve cried So many times, I swear I’ve died I’m trying, but it’s still not right The only time I want her is night", "vault_lines": ["I'm not running, running, running"], "meaning": "X reflects on the pain he endured in his life. He had a very troubled past dealing with violence, heartbreaks, and a traumatic childhood.\n\n“A million times, I swear I’ve died” is X’s way of saying he’s gone through so much pain he feels like he has already died many times over.\n\nThese lyrics also draw a parallel to “NUMB,” where X also sang about his pain and the tears he has shed:\n\nAnd every single year\nI’m drowning in my tears, I’m drowning in my tears again\nI can’t seem to forget the pain you seem to give\nThe pain you seem to give, my friend", "annotation_id": "16008255", "url": "https://genius.com/16008255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 189, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scared of the Dark", "line": "[Verse 2: XXXTENTACION]", "vault_lines": ["I'm not scared of the dark"], "meaning": "The first part of X’s verse was originally recorded for Bhad Bhabie’s “Trust Me,” which she revealed during an Instagram livestream. It was instead replaced with Ty Dolla $ign.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mP096fcj4ug\n\nThe second part is an original recording, which has only been heard on “Scared of the Dark.”", "annotation_id": "16006927", "url": "https://genius.com/16006927", "state": "accepted", "votes": 76, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Scared of the Dark", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-and-ty-dolla-sign-scared-of-the-dark-lyrics", "genius_title": "Scared of the Dark", "genius_id": 4150963, "source": "api"}
