{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Young Carter", "vault_lines": ["I rеally got my own sneaker, used to shop at Sears"], "meaning": "Lil Waynes full name is Dwayne Michael Carter. His “Tha Carter” album series is a prime example of him using his last name in his music.", "annotation_id": "34877399", "url": "https://genius.com/34877399", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "I reminisce on the daily, my penmanship which had pay me", "vault_lines": ["I reminisce on the daily, my penmanship which had pay me"], "meaning": "Cordea  uses buy using penmanship which is a combination of pen and membership of subscription meaning he gets paid for writing good tracks", "annotation_id": "34357930", "url": "https://genius.com/34357930", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Lord", "vault_lines": ["Lord knows it's crazy how I can just text Hov"], "meaning": "Jesus Christ, also known as Jesus of Nazareth, is the central figure of Christianity. Born in Bethlehem around 4 BC, Jesus was a Jewish preacher, teacher, and healer who proclaimed the kingdom of God. According to the New Testament, he was born of a virgin, performed miracles, and was crucified on a cross for the sins of humanity. On the third day, he resurrected, demonstrating his power over death and sin. Jesus' teachings emphasize love, forgiveness, and compassion, inspiring millions worldwide to follow his example and seek salvation through faith in him. His life, teachings, death, and resurrection form the foundation of Christian theology and continue to shape world history.", "annotation_id": "33384286", "url": "https://genius.com/33384286", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Need less yes-men and more amens", "vault_lines": ["Need less yes-men and more amens"], "meaning": "Wayne relates back to Cordae’s Jim Carrey bar, saying he needs less “yes-men” (pushovers) and more people praying for him.", "annotation_id": "33252458", "url": "https://genius.com/33252458", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "You sweet as jelly-jam, honey glazed deli ham Bubblegum candy yams", "vault_lines": ["You sweet as jelly-jam, honey glazed deli ham"], "meaning": "Carrying on from the previous bar, Wayne is mocking whoever he is referring to by calling them a teddy bear and “sweet” by likening them to various sweet foods.\n\nThis is most likely not a Drake diss considering their long history of friendship and respect for one-another.", "annotation_id": "33239206", "url": "https://genius.com/33239206", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Hov", "vault_lines": ["Lord knows it's crazy how I can just text Hov"], "meaning": "shoulda said hoes, then the XOs in the next line woulda been a double. X’s and O’s as in running plays on the field and xoxoxo", "annotation_id": "33053086", "url": "https://genius.com/33053086", "state": "pending", "votes": -12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Take some drugs then take off, take some when I land", "vault_lines": ["Take some drugs then take off, take some when I land"], "meaning": "By saying that he “take[s] off” after taking drugs, Wayne likens himself while high to an airplane. When he “lands” (or his high wears off), he takes more drugs to ‘get back in the air.’\n\nMoreover, it is widely illegal to take drugs onto an aircraft. As a result, drug users oftentimes must consume their drugs before and after, rather than during, their flights.\n\nWayne, himself, has had run-ins with federal law enforcement officers over this particular issue:\n\nhttps://www.tampabay.com/news/florida/2019/12/24/guns-drugs-found-on-plane-with-rapper-lil-wayne-on-board-sources-say/\n\nWhile drugs were found on his airplane, the prosecution focused its efforts on a more serious weapons charge, attempting to place Tunechi in federal prison for up to 10 years.  Mr. Carter later received a Presidential Pardon from President Donald Trump, officially forgiving The Best Rapper Alive for his illegal acts.", "annotation_id": "32869259", "url": "https://genius.com/32869259", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "The most effective leaders have closed mouths and open ears", "vault_lines": ["The most effective leaders have closed mouths and open ears"], "meaning": "Cordae demonstrates that effective leadership stems from mindful communication—talking less and listening more. By using “closed mouths” to represent silence and “open ears” for attentiveness, he emphasizes this balance.\n\nA strong leader demonstrates humility by speaking scarcely, giving the team room to express their ideas. This approach encourages teamwork and innovation. Just as crucial is active listening, as it enables leaders to learn from their team’s experiences.", "annotation_id": "32721438", "url": "https://genius.com/32721438", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Carrying water, chopping the wood But you gon’ always have motion if the product is good", "vault_lines": ["Carrying water, chopping the wood"], "meaning": "Cordae refers to a famous Zen Buddhist saying:\n\n“Before enlightenment, chop wood, carry water.\nAfter enlightenment, chop wood, carry water.”\n\nIn a similar vein, he is likely stating that regardless of where you may be spiritually, if you keep doing good, good things will come to you.", "annotation_id": "32556132", "url": "https://genius.com/32556132", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "I need more real love and less fake laughs, huh", "vault_lines": ["I need more real love and less fake laughs, huh"], "meaning": "This is Corade saying he would prefer his friends/associates to give him loyalty and love rather than just be around him for fame", "annotation_id": "32524453", "url": "https://genius.com/32524453", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Am I talking to the martians when I pray, man? I need to know is there a heaven or just Space Jam?", "vault_lines": ["Am I talking to the martians when I pray, man?"], "meaning": "Wayne nods at the 1998 movie “Space Jam”, asking if his prayers are heard by someone or something (represented by “Martians”), or if there’s a true heaven. Marvin the Martian, a character from the Looney Tunes, is featured in the Space Jam movie. This also ties in with the Saturday Morning theme of cartoons.", "annotation_id": "32509686", "url": "https://genius.com/32509686", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Wish a nigga would like Timmy, bro, send ’em to Fairy World", "vault_lines": ["Wish a nigga would like Timmy, bro, send 'em to Fairy World"], "meaning": "This line is a reference to the show “The Fairly OddParents”, where the main character, Timmy Turner, has fairy godparents who grant his wishes.\n\n“Wish a nigga would like Timmy”\n\nimplies a challenge or a dare, using the slang “wish a nigga would,” which means daring someone to challenge them.\n\n“Send ’em to Fairy World”\n\nmeans that if someone does challenge Cordae, he’ll send them to heaven, or in this case Fairy World.", "annotation_id": "32509625", "url": "https://genius.com/32509625", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "The chopper’s singin’ like Justin Bieber", "vault_lines": ["The chopper's singin' like Justin Bieber"], "meaning": "Back when Justin Bieber was 14, he sang a parody song of his “One Less Lonely Girl” in which he switched up the word “Girl” with a certain derogatory term for black people and sang about killing them\n\nhttps://youtu.be/HYuIoFai3Sw?si=pDXJB14NbFaMQpqw\n\nCordae raps here that the guns out here are killing black people", "annotation_id": "32507279", "url": "https://genius.com/32507279", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Bubba Dub, nigga, straight trash", "vault_lines": ["You smokin' Bubba Dub, nigga, straight trash"], "meaning": "Bubba Dub is Jerry “Bubba Dub” Morgan, a professional standup comedian and sports analyst. He had a series called “Bubba Dub’s Trashh Talk Podcast”.\n\nAdditionally, there is a strain of weed called Bubba Kush from Florida that has become infamous for its extreme sedative effects.\n\nLil Wayne is using wordplay to claim that the person who he’s talking to is smoking “Bubba Dub” and that’s why he’s speaking trash.", "annotation_id": "32497785", "url": "https://genius.com/32497785", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "It’s time to get the bacon, this shit is biscuits and gravy Time to break fast", "vault_lines": ["It's time to get the bacon, this shit is biscuits and gravy"], "meaning": "Bacon, biscuits, gravy = all breakfast foods\n\nbreak + fast = breakfast\n\nAnd with all of this food he’s breaking a fast, fasting meaning going without food for an extended period of time.", "annotation_id": "32490443", "url": "https://genius.com/32490443", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "If I post it, I own it No cap for me, we get money like athletes", "vault_lines": ["No cap for me, we get money like athletes"], "meaning": "This bar has 3 meanings (third one could be a stretch but it makes sense to me):\n\nCap (lie): “cap” can translate to “lie” so you know if he’s posting something he’s not lying about it or putting up a front\n\nSalary cap: in basketball specifically, which he references in the next bar, there is a defined salary limit, also known as a cap, for each player and a maximum value that can be given per contract, (a max contract). This cap doesn’t exist for rappers or their contracts on record labels, but Cordae still earns money similar to the amounts a professional athlete makes.\n\nCaption: People who use captions excessively in their posts can be seen as fake and Cordae would rather have what he posts speak for itself.", "annotation_id": "32490365", "url": "https://genius.com/32490365", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "She deep throat the whole dick, but couldn’t take half", "vault_lines": ["She deep throat the whole dick, but couldn't take half"], "meaning": "He implies that despite her ability to perform oral sex, he will not consider her for marriage.\n\n“but couldn’t take half” suggests that despite her sexual abilities, she may not be capable of handling the broader responsibilities of a relationship, or it could imply a reluctance to commit due to the potential financial implications of divorce, where a spouse might claim half of one’s assets.\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: Also could be a double entendre – Waynes saying that although she can deep throat him his dick is too big for her to take it vaginally", "annotation_id": "32477729", "url": "https://genius.com/32477729", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "I need the astronaut pack with asteroid buds", "vault_lines": ["I need the astronaut pack with asteroid buds"], "meaning": "Wayne is referring to the popular marijuana brand “MOON ROCKS” when he says he needs the astronaut pack. The cannabis buds are dipped in resin and covered in powdered cannabis dust. The moon rocks induce a powerful high, which some would say is “out of this world”.", "annotation_id": "32470140", "url": "https://genius.com/32470140", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Plans gon’ be executed like niggas on death row", "vault_lines": ["Plans gon' be executed like niggas on death row"], "meaning": "Wordplay on executed and Death Row. Saying he’s going to execute and follow through with his plans.\n\nDeath Row inmates get executed due to the sentencing of the crime they committed.", "annotation_id": "32468219", "url": "https://genius.com/32468219", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
