{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "[Intro: Cordae]", "vault_lines": ["I rеally got my own sneaker, used to shop at Sears"], "meaning": "This song uses a sample from “I Really, Really Love You” by Father’s Children.\n\n\n\nOther songs that use this sample are “Weight” by redveil & “Breath Control” by Logic (ft. Wiz Khalifa).", "annotation_id": "32467842", "url": "https://genius.com/32467842", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "And if it ain’t Mula Baby, then I ain’t the dad", "vault_lines": ["And if it ain't Mula Baby, then I ain't the dad"], "meaning": "This could possibly be a reference to Young Money Entertainment, a record label founded by Lil Wayne himself which has produced some of the best selling artists of the late 2000s and 2010s such as Drake, Nicki Minaj and Tyga.\n\n“(Young) Mula Baby” is an ad-lib that has been used by Wayne several times, so this line implies that he only claims responsibility for anything related to his success or wealth, which has come from his timeless music.", "annotation_id": "32466652", "url": "https://genius.com/32466652", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "I thank Elohim that I woke up this morning", "vault_lines": ["To my fellow kings, keep the hope, I thank Elohim that I woke up this morning"], "meaning": "“Elohim” is a Hebrew word used in the Bible to describe God and how mighty and supreme he is.", "annotation_id": "32465896", "url": "https://genius.com/32465896", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "Like the Nile, I can flow for years", "vault_lines": ["Likе the Nile, I can flow for years"], "meaning": "The Nile, known for being the longest river, also represents one of the oldest continuously flowing rivers in the world.\n\nSo by comparing Nile’s longevity of flowing and also flowing in musical terms, Cordae shows his confidence in his career, and its longevity.", "annotation_id": "32465723", "url": "https://genius.com/32465723", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Saturday Mornings", "line": "And run plays on the weekend, it’s more than just XOs", "vault_lines": ["And run plays on the weekend, it's more than just XOs"], "meaning": "Cordae references Canadian singer The Weeknd and his label XO.\n\nAdditionally, X’s and O’s are the play calling that happens in football, which happens on the weekend.", "annotation_id": "32465187", "url": "https://genius.com/32465187", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
