{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Same Damn Tune", "line": "I’m so short, yellow bus retarded", "vault_lines": ["I'm so short, yellow bus retarded"], "meaning": "This is a double entendre.\nTalking about a short school bus, which usually carries SWE (Student With Exceptionalities) students. But against Weezy’s claims, not everyone who rides the short bus is retarded.\nWayne is also 5'5\", below the average height of an American male, which is 5'9\".", "annotation_id": "38658116", "url": "https://genius.com/38658116", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Same Damn Tune", "line": "I said I might retire, but y’all know I be high", "vault_lines": ["I said I might retire, but y'all know I be high"], "meaning": "Around this time leading to the Carter 5. Wayne said he was planning to retire once the fifth installment in the series was released. On Jimmy Kimmel in 2013 Wayne hinted that he wanted C5 to be his last album. ““I want to retire after Tha Carter 5, which I hope will be my last album”.\n\nShortly after  as we know he got into problems with his label which probably sparked inspiration and motivation because in fact he did not stop and eventually released the album in 2018. Wayne is far from retiring has he is planning to drop tha Carter VI in June, 2025.", "annotation_id": "34601246", "url": "https://genius.com/34601246", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Same Damn Tune", "line": "I did that time, I paid that fine", "vault_lines": ["I did that time, I paid that fine"], "meaning": "In 2010, Lil Wayne was sentenced to a year in prison for gun possession, but was released after serving eight months of the sentence.", "annotation_id": "1053810", "url": "https://genius.com/1053810", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Same Damn Tune", "line": "Tunechi, Drama, same time Can only be Dedication", "vault_lines": ["Tunechi, Drama, same time"], "meaning": "DJ Drama has worked with Wayne on all four installments of the Dedication mixtape series. It’s Tunechi and Drama, so you know without looking that it has to be another dedication mixtape.\n\nFurthermore, it shows a lot of dedication to their work, their relationship, and their spirit to make four mixtapes for their fans – it “can only be dedication”.", "annotation_id": "1047759", "url": "https://genius.com/1047759", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Same Damn Tune", "line": "Church - with the priest", "vault_lines": ["Church - with the priest"], "meaning": "“Church” is a popular exclamation that is meant to underscore the truth or significance of the statement preceding or following.\n\n\n\nThis is based on the idea that statements made in church are thought to be both truthful and important.\n\nHe adds the prepositional phrase “with the priest” to create a double entendre. Now it means that his statement true and he was ostensibly in an actual church with an actual priest.\n\nThe irony here is that priests have been under fire over the last decade for acting in opposition to some of the principles that lend strength to the exclamation of the word “Church” in this sense.", "annotation_id": "1042690", "url": "https://genius.com/1042690", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Same Damn Tune", "line": "Future fuck with me!", "vault_lines": ["Sampled beat of “Future – Same Damn Time”"], "meaning": "The instrumental to this song is from “Same Damn Time” by Future.\n\n\n\nTurns out Future did fuck with him, since soon after D4 was dropped, Future let Lil Wayne feature on the remix to “Turn on the Lights”.", "annotation_id": "1042067", "url": "https://genius.com/1042067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Same Damn Tune", "line": "Bitch I am not a human", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I am not a human"], "meaning": "A reference to I Am Not A Human Being, which is the eighth studio album by Lil Wayne. He in recent years has come to refer to himself as a martian, clearly not human.", "annotation_id": "1040254", "url": "https://genius.com/1040254", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
