{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Salute", "line": "At second thought I got the heart of a S-s-s-s-solider", "vault_lines": ["At second thought I got the heart of a S-s-s-s-solider"], "meaning": "The Purple Heart is awarded in the name of the President of the United States to any member of the Armed Forces of the United States who, while serving under competent authority in any capacity with one of the U.S. Armed Services after April 5, 1917, has been wounded or killed.\nFab been through war.", "annotation_id": "1005080", "url": "https://genius.com/1005080", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Salute", "line": "Nick got the cannon, yeah that nigga be Wild-N-Out", "vault_lines": ["Nick got the cannon, yeah that nigga be Wild-N-Out"], "meaning": "Nick Cannon was the host of an improvisation television game show on MTV in the mid 2000s with the name Wild-N'-Out.", "annotation_id": "662911", "url": "https://genius.com/662911", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Salute", "line": "Were on top I will put you underneath niggas We the TAKE-YA-HO tribe and I’m the chief nigga", "vault_lines": ["Were on top I will put you underneath niggas"], "meaning": "He’s on “top” of the game but with no hesitation he’ll put you underneath, six feet underneath that is.\n\n\n\nHe also uses opposite wordplay with “top” and “underneath”.\n\nThe second part he’s trying to say, his team take peoples' girls and he’s the chief of all of them, so imagine how much he gets.\n\nNOTE:TAKE-YA-HO, sounds like a actual Indian tribe name.\n\n\n\nCould he be talking about these girls?\n\nTheres is a rumor Fabolous might of been dating both Kanye West’s ex, Amber Rose, and Rob Kardashian’s ex, Adrienne Bailon.", "annotation_id": "395176", "url": "https://genius.com/395176", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Salute", "line": "I’m a rapping Ray Charles (I don’t see nobody)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a rapping Ray Charles (I don't see nobody)"], "meaning": "Ray Charles was a famous artist who pretty much invented and pioneered Blues, R&B, Rock N Roll, Soul, Gospel and a lot of other genres. He was one of the first black artists who was given artistic control by a major mainstream record company. Fabolous says he is the Hip-Hop/Rap version of Ray Charles.\n\nThe phrase I Dont See Nobody is used a lot by Fabolous especially on his mixtape There Is No Competition 2: The Funeral Service.\n\nRay Charles is also blind. Reference to the “I don’t see nobody” line. He’s saying he’s so high up in the rap game that he can’t see anyone below him.", "annotation_id": "129905", "url": "https://genius.com/129905", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Salute", "line": "In this chopper I will p - p - p - p - pop ’em Make it sound like a helicopters land on top of this bitch", "vault_lines": ["In this chopper I will p - p - p - p - pop 'em"], "meaning": "Using a simile to connect the two most common ways rappers use the word, “chopper”:\nWhen the chopper (slang for the AK-47 gun) lets off rounds, it does sound similar to the sound of the propellers when a helicopter lands.", "annotation_id": "129902", "url": "https://genius.com/129902", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Salute", "line": "S-S-S-S-Sendin’ champagne to my enemies", "vault_lines": ["S-S-S-S-Sendin' champagne to my enemies"], "meaning": "Frank Lucas, drug king pin of brooklyn in the 60’s would send champagne to his enemies as seen in the movie.", "annotation_id": "129900", "url": "https://genius.com/129900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Salute", "line": "I’m not that little pregnant white girl but Juno", "vault_lines": ["I'm not that little pregnant white girl but Juno"], "meaning": "A refference to the movie Juno. The movie is about a 16-year old pregnant white girl named Juno.\n\n\n\nHe always make Juno sound like “you know” when he repeats in the next line.", "annotation_id": "129883", "url": "https://genius.com/129883", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Salute", "line": "I was once told by my nigga Meech", "vault_lines": ["I was once told by my nigga Meech"], "meaning": "He was once told by his nigga Meech A.K.A. Big Meech from BMF (Black Maffia Family). Fabolous is known that he was associated with the BMF.\n\nBig Meech (on the right, in green)", "annotation_id": "129874", "url": "https://genius.com/129874", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
