{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sacrifice", "line": "Young cannibal, cut you like a cantaloupe", "vault_lines": ["Young cannibal, cut you like a cantaloupe"], "meaning": "The repeated first syllables in “cantaloupe” and “cannibal” reinforce the rhythm of these bars.  The two phonetically resonant terms have been used together by a number of artist since Eminem paired them in a similar simile in “The Real Slim Shady”, including Earl Sweatshirt, JUNGLEPUSSY,\n Wakizashi and Lord Infamous.", "annotation_id": "14118492", "url": "https://genius.com/14118492", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sacrifice", "line": "You a danish, you need glazing", "vault_lines": ["You a danish, you need glazing"], "meaning": "Holland is known for their pastries. Glazing means to cum on someone’s face. (the pasties are known to be glazed as well)", "annotation_id": "2902701", "url": "https://genius.com/2902701", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
