{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sacrifice", "line": "Ha! I’m evil like three sixes, nigga, minus the “Mafia”", "vault_lines": ["Ha! I'm evil like three sixes, nigga, minus the \"Mafia\""], "meaning": "Three 6’s (666) is often used as the number that invokes Satan.\n\nHe also cites rap group Three 6 Mafia afterwards.", "annotation_id": "1123998", "url": "https://genius.com/1123998", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Sacrifice", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Gudda-gudda-sacrifice-lyrics", "genius_title": "Sacrifice", "genius_id": 64307, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SUWU", "line": "And she don’t mind fuckin’ with girls As long as Tiffany’s first", "vault_lines": ["And she don't mind fuckin' with girls as long as Tiffany's first"], "meaning": "Clever wordplay. Wayne’s girl doesn’t mind having threesomes with other women, as long as he takes her shopping first at the store Tiffany’s (which is also a popular girl name).", "annotation_id": "36071931", "url": "https://genius.com/36071931", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SUWU", "line": "Let’s go off to space, the way stars do, (Pewm) We gone, it’s all in our heads, and our hearts too, (Vroom) I’m gone, she waitin’ in bed for that part two, (Skrt) I’m back, and we argue all mornin’, fuck all noon, (Err-Ehh)", "vault_lines": ["Let's go off to space, the way stars do, (Pewm)"], "meaning": "This is giving a detailed cicle about what Wayne and the groupie go through when they see each other. At first they start off by “going to space” which indicated they are getting high together, he is also stating that that is they way “starts do it”, basically saying that getting high with groupie is a everyday thing for him.\n\nThe third line in this is saying, while he is still high she is still waiting for him to come down so they can have a part two, a second sex session. But when he is come down and normal again (which is in the next morning), all they do  is argue all day and once they are ready to tolerate each other again they conjugate the rest of the day.", "annotation_id": "13376056", "url": "https://genius.com/13376056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SUWU", "line": "Damn, I’m changin’ her life, her ringtone too Cut that shit down, you’ll hear old Tune", "vault_lines": ["Cut the shit down, you'll hear old Tune, brrp"], "meaning": "A nice play of words by Weezy. He is saying, that he is changing the life of his current lover/groupie, this relates to the money, he could provide for her.\n\nBy her ringtone, he is basically making a “I am back!” statement and saying that his new music, relating to the mixtape you are just listening to, Dedication 6 and to end his point he plays with the word “tune”. Saying that he is hearing old Tune(chi), which is one of his many infamous nicknames.", "annotation_id": "13376014", "url": "https://genius.com/13376014", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SUWU", "line": "She said, “Fuck that nigga, Baby, I’m your real baby.”", "vault_lines": ["She said, \"Fuck that nigga, Baby, I'm your real baby.\""], "meaning": "Here, Weezy’s girl refers to Birdman, who goes by the nickname “Baby.”\n\nHim and Wayne have had a father-son relationship for over 2 decades, Wayne even called himself “Weezy F Baby” for many years, and he made sure we did not forget to say the Baby. However, in 2014 Weezy revealed that Birdman was not paying him for his music and he had to sue him.", "annotation_id": "13373837", "url": "https://genius.com/13373837", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SUWU", "line": "Suwu", "vault_lines": ["She get a little brazy, but she still wavy (Suwu"], "meaning": "“Suwu” which is commonly spelled “Suwoo” is a call used by members of the Blood gang to acknowledge each other. It is speculated by some that it is an onomatopoeia mimicking the sound of a police siren.", "annotation_id": "13355479", "url": "https://genius.com/13355479", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SUWU", "line": "So easy to pick up, and they so hard to put down Gift and a curse", "vault_lines": ["So easy to pick up, and they so hard to put down"], "meaning": "Drugs are addictive. In fact, prescription medication can be more addictive than heroin, and while it’s easy to start using them, it’s definitely hard to stop.\nFor some, the euphoria felt while high can be a gift, but, the withdrawals and pain caused by using drugs is a curse.", "annotation_id": "13355438", "url": "https://genius.com/13355438", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SUWU", "line": "I cross my heart, I won’t cross you, damn", "vault_lines": ["I cross my heart, I won't cross you, damn"], "meaning": "Cross my heart is an expression used when making a promise that is unbreakable. Wayne employs repetition to say that their connection, like his word, is forever.", "annotation_id": "13355429", "url": "https://genius.com/13355429", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
