{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "And I gave you all I got, you still want extra from me (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["And I gave you all I got, you still want extra from me (Woo)"], "meaning": "Kanye refers to the concept of people never being satisfied with what you give them, especially fake friends and acquaintances who entertain an air of camraderie purely in the hopes of benefitting financially and materialistically.", "annotation_id": "29717180", "url": "https://genius.com/29717180", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Don’t speak to me, nigga, you not important", "vault_lines": ["Don't speak to me, nigga, you not important"], "meaning": "This line is about how Tyler views himself as above his peers, when factoring in his tone when say this it almost sounds like he is saying it so aggressively that he is almost slurring up spit, contrasting the tone Kanye West has when his verse comes in creating a highlight to the term “Smuckers” as it’s a contrast between peanut butter and jelly but in one container or in this context, one song", "annotation_id": "29507344", "url": "https://genius.com/29507344", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Got too much drive, need like ten lanes", "vault_lines": ["Got too much drive, need like ten lanes"], "meaning": "Tyler is known to talk about his love for cars. In this line he is implying that to bring out his collection of vehicles, he would need 10 lanes on a road.", "annotation_id": "29482682", "url": "https://genius.com/29482682", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I mean, you can even dress extra bummy", "vault_lines": ["I mean, you can even dress extra bummy"], "meaning": "This lyric sees Ye poking fun at the people criticizing his fashion sense, which some may consider to look ‘homeless’ or, in this case, bummy.\n\nHe adopted the style during the era of his 2013 album, Yeezus.\n\nKanye has addressed these negative opinions before and after Smuckers came out, seeing as he tweeted in March 2016: “yes I believe in my ripped homeless sweaters!!!”.", "annotation_id": "28844451", "url": "https://genius.com/28844451", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "It’s funny, when you get extra money", "vault_lines": ["It's funny, when you get extra money"], "meaning": "This line means that when you have lots of money people will laugh at your jokes- or just generally suck up to you- with the hopes of receiving some of that money.", "annotation_id": "28274426", "url": "https://genius.com/28274426", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I am the free nigga archetype (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["I am the free nigga archetype (Woo)"], "meaning": "referring to slavery he is saying he is free and living how he wants. Also he is saying he is a ‘free'mason, as in the next lines he talks about the light and religious figures.", "annotation_id": "27554424", "url": "https://genius.com/27554424", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Why, oh, why, why, why don’t they like me?", "vault_lines": ["Why, oh, why, why, why don't they like me?"], "meaning": "Kanye is one of the most controversial musicians ever, he’s even called the most hated person in 2009, so the general public don’t like him due to his opinions and actions.", "annotation_id": "27488124", "url": "https://genius.com/27488124", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Bring in the horns", "vault_lines": ["Bring in the horns"], "meaning": "This may be a reference to the song “Sam (Is Dead)”, wherein Tyler says to “bring in the horns.” https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0axbemV5Fnc&ab_channel=OddFuture-Topic", "annotation_id": "27405890", "url": "https://genius.com/27405890", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
