{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Life is a broad, and she give brain", "vault_lines": ["Life is a broad, and she give brain"], "meaning": "This is a double entendre.\n\n1) Tyler is saying life is abroad and as life is going by, you gain knowledge (life giving brain).\n2) Tyler is saying life is a bitch, another word for “broad”.", "annotation_id": "26288633", "url": "https://genius.com/26288633", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "But it’s the two-thou’ (Yeah) And the one-four and the one-five, yo, what up, Wayne?", "vault_lines": [", but it's the two-thou' (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Building off the last two lines, Tyler, The Creator compares his Golf Wang clique to that of the Hot Boys whom Wayne was a part of from 1997-2001. Back in the that era, Juvenile would proudly say “Cash Money Record takin' over for the ‘99 and the 2000’s.”\n\nThe “two-thousand” and the “one-four/one-five” are referring to the years 2014 and 2015, the era in which Tyler was working on the release of his 2015 album, “Cherry Bomb”. Tyler is paying homage to the Hot Boys, implying that they will take over even in the present day/no matter the circumstances.", "annotation_id": "23957571", "url": "https://genius.com/23957571", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Middle finger blind, so it’s fuck A-N-Y-one (Um) Fuck, skate, and die, son, a hundred ways to die, son", "vault_lines": ["Middle finger blind, so it's fuck A-N-Y-one (Um)"], "meaning": "Since Wayne’s middle finger is blind, it can’t pick who it’s pointed to and that’s why he points it to anyone.\n\n“Skate or die” is a really popular saying among skaters. It comes from an old skateboarding video game by EA with the same name. Even popular skater brands like Thrasher have used it in several occasions.", "annotation_id": "23695152", "url": "https://genius.com/23695152", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Got a full tank of that same year I was born That’s that one-nine-nine-one", "vault_lines": ["Got a full tank of that same year I was born"], "meaning": "The car Tyler frequently raps about on Cherry Bomb is a BMW M3, specifically the 1991 Model. In this line he is stating that the 1991 modelled car has a full tank.", "annotation_id": "23269487", "url": "https://genius.com/23269487", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "And you pussies prayin’ that we squash the beef like zucchini, I know", "vault_lines": ["And you pussies prayin' that we squash the beef like zucchini, I know"], "meaning": "For the culinarily uninclined, zucchinis are a type of summer squash.\n\n\n\nAlso as far as this contributor is aware, Kanye and Weezy have never had public beef. However Kanye/Drake as well as Jay-Z/Wayne feuds (Roc-A-Fella vs. Young Money) have happened in the past, so this may be referencing the general rivalry of the two labels.", "annotation_id": "19051671", "url": "https://genius.com/19051671", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I’m starin’ at a tramp on lean, make my eye jump", "vault_lines": ["I'm starin' at a tramp on lean, make my eye jump"], "meaning": "Wayne shows his lyricism through this line. He says that he’s “starin' at a tramp on lean” which sounds like “trampoline”, and follows up with “make my eye jump.”\n\nThis line works because seeing a shaggy person (a tramp) on drugs really stands out and could “make your eye jump”. The double meaning is that viewing a trampoline (used for jumping) could make your eyes jump.", "annotation_id": "18762681", "url": "https://genius.com/18762681", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Been exhausted, I been workin’ While y’all silly bros smoke like broken exhaust tips", "vault_lines": [", been exhausted, I been workin'"], "meaning": "When used in combination with an upgraded exhaust system, including wider pipes and/or an performance muffler, exhaust tips can amplify the new tones coming from your exhaust. The shape and width of the exhaust tip can slightly change the sound to be either more throaty (larger tips) or raspy (smaller tips).\n\nBroken exaust tips, however, Release massive amount of smoke, But in this line, With his clever wordplay of him being “exausted” and “exaust tips, Tyler compares his old freinds smoking and being lazy, to broken exaust tips, releaseing massive amounts of smoke. But on the other hand he has been putting in massive amounts of work.", "annotation_id": "18668174", "url": "https://genius.com/18668174", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Hold your fuckin’ ponies, my homie I’ll whip your donkey by my lonely, I eat pussy like Shoney’s, yeah (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Hold your fuckin' horses"], "meaning": "A donkey is an ass. An ass/donkey/burro being a beast of burden, it isn’t uncommon for them to get a taste of the whip to keep them working. However, to whip/whoop someone’s ass means to physically pummel them.\n\n“Donkey” can also refer to a female’s ass so Wayne is saying that he won’t invite other guys to have sex with this girl.  He is also calling the competition pussy (scared or soft) and threatens eat them (do them harm). Shoney’s is a Tennessee-based casual restaurant.\n\nThese lyrics may be inspired by Naughty by Nature’s “Let the Ho’s Go”:\n\nYou don’t know me homey, from a peach or a pony\nI’m the Only, now your lyrics look lonely", "annotation_id": "7961098", "url": "https://genius.com/7961098", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "These niggas colder than Tommy buddy", "vault_lines": ["Wayne, them bitches ugly, these niggas colder than Tommy buddy"], "meaning": "Continuing the Martin references, Tyler invokes Tommy’s buddy Cole.", "annotation_id": "6259118", "url": "https://genius.com/6259118", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Bitch, I’m goin’ harder than yellow cabbies stoppin’ for Lionel (Black ass nigga)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm goin' harder than yellow cabbies stoppin' for Lionel (Black ass nigga)"], "meaning": "In this line Tyler is referring to his flow. The harder the flow the better.\n\n\n\nLionel is a cast member on Cartoon Network’s show ‘Loiter Squad’. Tyler is showing us what would happen in the situation that Lionel was trying to hail a cab. Stereotypically, the joke goes that cab drivers don’t stop for people of color, implying that this cabby isn’t stopping at all.\n\nTyler connects the two lines by saying that his flow is harder than how hard the cabby is trying to not stop for Lionel.", "annotation_id": "5212370", "url": "https://genius.com/5212370", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Use Adderall like alarm clocks, wake my high up", "vault_lines": ["Use Adderall like alarm clocks, wake my high up"], "meaning": "Adderall is a drug used mainly to put the user into better focus, and in this case, Wayne takes Adderall to wake him up (hence the play on of alarm clocks). While Wayne may be high off of another drug, the Adderall helps him maintain the high he already has.", "annotation_id": "5210828", "url": "https://genius.com/5210828", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "They be duckin’ us niggas, shout out to Donald Sterling", "vault_lines": ["They be duckin' us niggas, shout out to Donald Sterling"], "meaning": "Bring the nooses as in the rope to tie a “noose knot”, and the trees to hang on them.\n\nFor a long time, black men for made up reasons were hung by groups of racist bigots in the south. (The KKK was blamed for many of these)\n\nThe idea of hanging nooses from the tree in Jena was a way of telling the black students that they weren’t wanted sitting under the ‘white only’ tree.\n\nAs a matter of fact, the noose is a sign of bigotry, and ignorance.", "annotation_id": "5210022", "url": "https://genius.com/5210022", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Ye, we hittin’ models like Tony Parker be hittin’ bottles", "vault_lines": ["Ye, we hittin' models like Tony Parker be hittin' bottles"], "meaning": "Former San Antonio Spurs point guard Tony Parker suffered an eye injury from thrown bottles during the 2013 Chris Brown-Drake nightclub brawl. Ye and Tyler aren’t in a brawl; they’re mingling with beautiful women at the club.\n\nTyler previously referenced Parker in “Tamale.”", "annotation_id": "5208714", "url": "https://genius.com/5208714", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Son, you need Jesus But I heard he left Sunset to go on tour with Yeezus, well (That’s too harsh) I’m prayin’ for the new Yeezys", "vault_lines": ["Son, you need Jesus"], "meaning": "“Y'all motherfuckers need Jesus” is said when somebody thinks another person REALLY needs help. Wayne is trying to help out Tyler by continuing this conversation.\n\nWayne plays on Jesus' exorcism at sunset, to (humorously) say that Jesus left all of that behind, and goes on tour with Kanye instead. We already know that Ye' and Jesus are quite close. Wayne may also be poking fun at “pray the gay away”- type Christians who would tell someone they need Jesus in response to someone indicating that they’re gay.\n\n\n\nAnd of course, Wayne’s joining the fight for a pair of the newest Adidas Yeezys.\n\n20 Gs for the Yeezys off of eBay", "annotation_id": "5208259", "url": "https://genius.com/5208259", "state": "accepted", "votes": 154, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "My new music’s all over the street like Erick Sermon was", "vault_lines": ["My new music's all over the street like Erick Sermon was"], "meaning": "Erick Sermon attempted suicide in 2001 by jumping out of a building and landing on the street.\n\nHe has since claimed he didn’t attempt suicide after all, but just “fell”.\n\nTyler has previously been fascinated by the idea of suicide, and at the end of his video for “Yonkers” he commits suicide.", "annotation_id": "5208195", "url": "https://genius.com/5208195", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "They say I’m nutty, I’m picnic basket I’m short of a sandwich, I’m peanut butter Boyce Watkins a faggot,", "vault_lines": ["I'm short of a sandwich, I'm peanut butter"], "meaning": "Tyler is pretty “nuts” – he’s playing with various food-related euphemisms for insanity. If you’re one sandwich short of a picnic basket, you’re nearly a basket-case, ready for the nut-house, etc.\n\n\n\nTyler’s particular brand of crazy was on full display in his recent Mountain Dew commercial. It also featured a goat charged with assault. The commercial faced a lot of backlash, and was banned due in part to Dr. Boyce Watkins calling it “arguably the most racist commercial in history”. Clearly, Tyler learned his lesson, and is never going to say or do anything controversial again.\n\nBoyce Watkins actually responded to this line on his YouTube channel.", "annotation_id": "5207753", "url": "https://genius.com/5207753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 116, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "’nother nigga like I, you won’t find one ’Cause, nigga, I’m a god, a divine one", "vault_lines": [", 'nother nigga like I, you won't find one"], "meaning": "Tyler has the most vocal religious claimaint in rap history on this track, so this statement is less about himself as an individual, and more about black people in general. Rather than say “you won’t find one” he says ‘You gon’ find one\", implying that black people, like himself, are gods, which is a reference to the teachings of the Five-Percent Nation.\n\nTune, is of course, Lil Wayne’s nickname.", "annotation_id": "5207266", "url": "https://genius.com/5207266", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I studied the proportions Emotions runnin’ at a Autobahn speed-level", "vault_lines": ["I studied the proportions"], "meaning": "Kanye’s rise was not meteoric nor was it an overnight success. As he explained to MTV in 2002 he had spent his life studying the art of hip hop, working out how to create beats from samples, and finding his own unique voice as a rapper.\n\nEver since his first record – Kanye has traded on emotion. Arguably, in recent times, he has been the most emotional rapper in the game. An Autobahn has no speed limit, so Kanye is saying he has no control over where his emotions take him, and at what speed.\n\nKanye has a direct line with God, and this ties back in with his car crash reference in saying that whilst he was driving, out of control (drunk from his drink with fear), he was texting God, implying that that act was the thing that birthed his career.\n\nKanye also talked in an interview about the importance of the knowledge and art of proportions and how it had inspired his album Yeezus:\n\nIn school’s moving forward, beauty needs to be understood. Of course, we can learn about Picasso, but we need to learn about proportion. Proportion is the luxury. Everything is inside of proportions. Proportions are so important that in ancient times they would hide the information of proportions and now it’s happening again. Picture a Gucci jacket, just a guy’s Gucci jacket, he doesn’t have proper proportions in my opinion. And you think about all the artists: Dürer, Da Vinci, everyone studied these proportions, and there can be proportions of sound as there are visual.", "annotation_id": "5207190", "url": "https://genius.com/5207190", "state": "accepted", "votes": 76, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "And the Lexus pull up, errr, like hop, I hopped out, like wassup? Err-err-err, step back, hold up, my nigga, you suck Hold up (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["And the Lexus pull up, errr, like hop, I hopped out, like wassup?"], "meaning": "Kanye’s infamous car crash occurred in a Lexus, and he hasn’t been seen in one since.\n\nHe acknowledges that the car accident may just be one of his definitive moments, as it spawned his breakthrough hit, “Through The Wire.”\n\nThis kind of onomatopoeia isn’t new for Ye, as he toyed with it on “Live Fast, Die Young” in 2010", "annotation_id": "5207181", "url": "https://genius.com/5207181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 127, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I’m a liar, I’m a faggot, ugh", "vault_lines": ["I'm a liar, I'm a faggot, ugh"], "meaning": "This line is probably related to the previous line. Tyler calls himself a liar because he still enjoys his music and feel accomplishment in the rap game. He actually fucks with himself, which sarcastically makes him a faggot.\n\nNow, when he says “faggot”, a slang also used for someone that’s a loser or stupid, he could be calling himself “stupid” for being a liar.\n\nIt can also be related to tweets Tyler made the day before the release of Cherry Bomb.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/587461037395349504\n\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/587459235706900480\n\nThis line has since been made more interesting, raising questions about the balance of honesty and shock value in the lyric as Tyler has shared more clearly earnest thoughts about being gay on his 2017 album Flower Boy.", "annotation_id": "5207157", "url": "https://genius.com/5207157", "state": "accepted", "votes": 73, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Nobody can tell me where I’m headin’", "vault_lines": ["Nobody can tell me where I'm headin'"], "meaning": "As Kanye’s consistently shown over the years, each album and venture is more unpredictable than the last. But while no one knows exactly where he’s going next, he feels that he’s on the path to become the Michael Jordan of rap; in other words, the greatest ever.\n\n\n\nThis isn’t just because he and MJ are the best at their respective crafts; the fact that Michael’s most famous teammate Scottie Pippen got an invite to the Kanye-Kardashian wedding must make Yeezy feel pretty Jordanesque as well.", "annotation_id": "5207032", "url": "https://genius.com/5207032", "state": "accepted", "votes": 104, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Hold your fuckin’ horses Niggas really fuckin’ thought that T lost it Like I bet it at a auction", "vault_lines": ["Hold your fuckin' horses"], "meaning": "Hold your horses is a common idiom which means to “hold on” or wait. The phrase is historically related to horse riding, or driving a horse-drawn vehicle.\n\nTyler is reminding everyone to hold on and hang tight as he alluded earlier.\n\nThere have been whisperings that Tyler was over music and was spending more time focused on film career. He makes fun of his detractors who claim he “lost it”, as if “it” is a material possession that he can put up for auction with no reserve.", "annotation_id": "5206949", "url": "https://genius.com/5206949", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "My trigger finger wise, but my .9 dumb (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["My trigger finger wise, but my .9 dumb (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Wayne’s Trigger Finger is both itchy and intelligent, but his weapon is a follower, not a leader, so he allows his finger to do the thinking, and his gun to do the talking. Not to mention, with Wayne’s trigger finger busy his nine other fingers have gone dumb.\n\nHe also refers to his 9mm weapon as “dumb” because it is silenced, or mute. He furthers the meaning by claiming that whilst his trigger finger is the wise one, his other 9 aren’t as intelligent, and won’t hesitate to use violence against you.", "annotation_id": "5206936", "url": "https://genius.com/5206936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 142, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Please come and get me", "vault_lines": ["please come and get me"], "meaning": "Tyler refers to two well known risks of sexual encounters, though one is far more serious than the other. HIV is one of the most difficult to treat STDs on the planet; hickeys are sometimes a nuisance but popular among young lovers.\n\nTyler’s raps are “sick” and no one’s “fucking with him\"—it’s too risky.", "annotation_id": "5206885", "url": "https://genius.com/5206885", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "We ain’t lyin’, we the truth, call him Simba, beast is loose", "vault_lines": ["We ain't lyin', we the truth, call him Simba, beast is loose"], "meaning": "Simba is the main character in The Lion King film series. Tyler’s claims of success and his ability to overcome obstacles are truth – he isn’t lion.", "annotation_id": "5206843", "url": "https://genius.com/5206843", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Damn, ’bout to drop, gas ’em up, thick exhaust (Woo) Young T, came quick, hard to beat, dick is soft", "vault_lines": ["Damn, 'bout to drop, gas 'em up, thick exhaust (Woo)"], "meaning": "A thick exhaust pipe leads to a deeper exhaust note when a car is driven hard. Tyler compares this to the strong nature of his record, as seen in his “DEATHCAMP” assertions.\n\nYoung T is a new nickname Tyler has created, similar to his diabolical alter ego Young N—. He comes quick, making him “hard to beat” – a soft dick is hard to beat.", "annotation_id": "5206823", "url": "https://genius.com/5206823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I got banned from New Zealand, whitey called me a demon (Yeah) And a terrorist? Goddamn it, I couldn’t believe it", "vault_lines": ["I got banned from New Zealand, whitey called me a demon (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Odd Future was set to replace Kendrick Lamar in the lineup for Eminem’s early 2014 Rapture festival in New Zealand. The authorities in NZ denied them access at the last minute, citing “potential threat to public order and the public interest.”\n\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/statuses/433798469312974849\n\nAlthough New Zealand is known as Aotearoa, which translates in English to “the land of the long white cloud”, Tyler is most likely poking fun at the predominately Caucasian population.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/596446826951245824", "annotation_id": "5206585", "url": "https://genius.com/5206585", "state": "accepted", "votes": 119, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Or some niggas from Alabama, Birmingham", "vault_lines": ["Or some niggas from Alabama, Birmingham"], "meaning": "Birmingham is a city in the Deep South. Lynchings were common in Alabama. Birmingham has historical significance when examining the civil rights movement. Martin Luther King Jr. was confined in the Birmingham city jail and wrote a letter describing the city as “most thoroughly segregated city in the United States.” MLK would lead the peaceful Birmingham campaign to integrate blacks and whites. This campaign was met with a large resistance from the whites in the city. Governor Bull Conor infamously used force against the peaceful protestors, sending attack dogs and firehoses.", "annotation_id": "5206444", "url": "https://genius.com/5206444", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I stick my Rollie in her mouth, let the time come", "vault_lines": ["I stick my Rollie in her mouth, let the time come"], "meaning": "“Rollie” is a nickname given to a Rolex watch. The “rollie” in this case, is Wayne’s penis. And to “let the time come” is a common phrase, but here he uses the “cum” – “come” homonym to refer to when he climaxes in her mouth.", "annotation_id": "5206433", "url": "https://genius.com/5206433", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "[Verse: Tyler, The Creator & Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": ["I'm short of a sandwich, I'm peanut butter"], "meaning": "Here, the beat changes to a sample from the the song Metrolpolis Notte by Gabriele Ducros.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ko5yjwihpCc\n\nLil Wayne has always been a friend of Tyler’s and has even shouted him out before.\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/587526321544151040\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/587662763503173633\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/587662873683345408", "annotation_id": "5206426", "url": "https://genius.com/5206426", "state": "accepted", "votes": 84, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Anti-Golf boys ’cause I don’t fuck with me either", "vault_lines": ["Anti-Golf boys 'cause I don't fuck with me either"], "meaning": "This line is open to a few interpretations:\n\n\nOdd Future was banned from entering New Zealand. After hearing the news, group members started tweeting “Anti Golf Boyz”, and putting it in their Twitter and Instagram bios. He might be saying that he doesn’t fuck with himself, just how New Zealand doesn’t fuck with him.\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/419521752570408960\n\n\nThis also could mean that he’s not interested in rapping anymore; he wants to take an approach on other things, such as directing films, music videos, and the list goes on.", "annotation_id": "5206366", "url": "https://genius.com/5206366", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "[Verse 2: Kanye West & Tyler, The Creator]", "vault_lines": ["I'm short of a sandwich, I'm peanut butter"], "meaning": "Tyler said that Kanye scrapped the original verse he wrote for his feature after he heard Wayne and Tyler’s verses and then wrote a better one. Kanye even said that it made him want to rap again.\n\n\n\nOn the opening track to Goblin, Tyler bragged about Kanye tweeting praise for his “Yonkers” video. He’s come a long way since then, performing with Kanye at the Camp Flog Gnaw in 2013 and now landing a guest verse.", "annotation_id": "5206352", "url": "https://genius.com/5206352", "state": "accepted", "votes": 113, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "She got hair like Sheneneh, and eyes like Wanda, oh my goodness", "vault_lines": ["She got hair like Sheneneh, and eyes like Wanda, oh my goodness"], "meaning": "Sheneneh and Wanda are two characters from the heist film Skank Robbers. Both women are played by male actors Martin Lawrence and Jamie Foxx.\n\nWayne is so bombed-out, the girl he is with has facial features similar to Sheneneh and Wanda.\n\n“Oh my goodness” was Shanaynay’s catchphrase in Martin.", "annotation_id": "5206347", "url": "https://genius.com/5206347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "For your boy I’m watching “Freaks and Geeks” with the trampoline on the floor I’m tryna cop the new McLaren with the vertical doors Nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm prayin' for the new Yeezys"], "meaning": "Tyler has a trampoline in his bedroom. He told The Fader he thinks of it as a symbol of success. The trampoline also appeared in the music video for “Tamale”.\n\nFreaks and Geeks was a critically acclaimed 2000 TV show with a then-unknown cast and crew: James Franco, Seth Rogen, Jason Segel and Judd Apatow among them. Tyler mentioned in his interview with Seth Rogen on the GOLF Media app that he had recently finished watching Freaks and Geeks. Tyler may identify with the spirit of the show and its makers—they started as outsiders but now they’re huge, and they succeeded on their own terms.\n\nNow that Tyler has his trampoline and Netflix game on lock, he’s set his sights on a McLaren sports car – a new symbol of success.", "annotation_id": "5206341", "url": "https://genius.com/5206341", "state": "accepted", "votes": 170, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "’Cause I’m tryna hang like I’m Mr. Cooper or Jews in Berlin", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I'm tryna hang like I'm Mr. Cooper or Jews in Berlin"], "meaning": "Wordplay:\n\nDuring the Holocaust, Jews were hanged by the Nazis. During 1940 and 1941, the murder of large numbers of Jews in Berlin continued, and the deportation of Jews to the General Government was undertaken.\n\nOn a much lighter note, Hangin' with Mr. Cooper is an American television sitcom that originally aired on ABC from 1992 to 1997, starring Mark Curry and Holly Robinson.", "annotation_id": "5206301", "url": "https://genius.com/5206301", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I am the light and the beacon; you can ask the deacon (Ask the deacon)", "vault_lines": ["I am the light and the beacon; you can ask the deacon (Ask the deacon)"], "meaning": "As it states in Matthew 5:14: “You are the light of the world.”\n\nA deacon is a ministerial office in the Christian Church that is in charge of presiding over religious services. The “Deacon’s Office” is seen as the pastor’s place to prepare sermons. Kanye reprises his role as Jesus.\n\nHis claims of holy status are much cleaner in nature in this verse, promoting positivity rather than highlighting oppression.", "annotation_id": "5206297", "url": "https://genius.com/5206297", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "What up, Slime? Nigga, go hard", "vault_lines": ["What up, Slime? Nigga, go hard"], "meaning": "The word Slime has two possible definitions that pertain to this line:\n\n\nS.L.I.M.E is an acronym for “Street Life Intelligence and Money is Everything.”\nSlime is also another word used when addressing a friend or accomplice and is specifically associated with Blood gangs.", "annotation_id": "5206197", "url": "https://genius.com/5206197", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I wanna turn the tanks to playgrounds", "vault_lines": ["I wanna turn the tanks to playgrounds"], "meaning": "Since he’s become a father, Kanye’s adopted a different outlook on life. Rather than “taking the bullet” and risking his pubic perception, he’d rather be more positive.\n\nThis also relates to his native Chicago. Gun violence and murder rates in his hometown are some of the highest in the U.S, Kanye wants his vision to transcend beyond music – see DONDA.", "annotation_id": "5206163", "url": "https://genius.com/5206163", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "It’s Tunechi, homie, Master of Ceremonies I knock ’em down, Domino effect, no pepperoni, I swear", "vault_lines": ["It's Tunechi, homie, Master of Ceremonies"], "meaning": "Wayne is renown for his… unique sounds. His lyrics definitely make one think! “Master of Ceremonies” also stands for “MC”.\n\nWeezy also says that he kills every thing, or knocks them down like dominoes.\n\nHe also plays with the word dominos by comparing the once popular game to the pizza company.", "annotation_id": "5206154", "url": "https://genius.com/5206154", "state": "accepted", "votes": 103, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I dreamt of 2Pac, he asked me “Are you still down?”", "vault_lines": ["I dreamt of 2Pac, he asked me \"Are you still down?\""], "meaning": "Apparently Yeezy had a dream where Pac quoted his track “R U Still Down?” – asking Ye if he was ready to carry on his legacy, to which Kanye responded yes.", "annotation_id": "5206145", "url": "https://genius.com/5206145", "state": "accepted", "votes": 127, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Scarier than black people with ideas", "vault_lines": ["Scarier than black people with ideas"], "meaning": "As Paul Mooney once said:\n\n“I have a Stephen King horror movie, A Nigga With a Brain”.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/-_2iBE-QVqk?t=6m46s\n\nIt’s a widely-held sentiment that America is terrified of educated black men and women. This relates to the Willie Lynch theory in that America (European Settlers and their descendants) tried desperately to keep African American slaves deaf, dumb, and blind.", "annotation_id": "5206129", "url": "https://genius.com/5206129", "state": "accepted", "votes": 172, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "You can’t lynch Marshawn if Tom Brady throwin’ to me", "vault_lines": ["You can't lynch Marshawn if Tom Brady throwin' to me"], "meaning": "Kanye uses a metaphor to describe his success. His career can’t be killed (lynched) if he has white money (Tom Brady) supporting him. Kanye has previously alluded to lynching in songs like “Blood On The Leaves”.\n\n\n\nIt should also be noted the trio share some of the same characteristics – Marshawn Lynch, and Kanye both share a disdain for the media, and all three are considered experts of their chosen craft.", "annotation_id": "5206126", "url": "https://genius.com/5206126", "state": "accepted", "votes": 135, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Oxford want a full-blown lecture from me", "vault_lines": ["Oxford want a full-blown lecture from me"], "meaning": "While in London for fashion week in 2015, Kanye stopped by Oxford’s University society called “The Guild” to deliver a lecture to students.\n\nThe Guild Society is devoted to business and networking and Kanye’s lecture was based on the issues in today’s world involving separatism.", "annotation_id": "5206124", "url": "https://genius.com/5206124", "state": "accepted", "votes": 83, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Cherry Bomb the greatest fuckin’ album since the days of sound", "vault_lines": ["Cherry Bomb the greatest fuckin' album since the days of sound"], "meaning": "Tyler’s confident that Cherry Bomb is the greatest music composition in a good long while. The “days of sound” is likely a reference to “the Wall of Sound” popularized by record producer Phil Spector in the 1960s. Spector’s albums with The Ronettes, the Beatles and others are considered one of the great moments in pop music production, and Tyler’s picking up where Spector and others left off. He further claims his album is going to “pop”, like his absent father.\n\nAlso note the wordplay with “rounds” (of ammunition) and “pop” (slang for “shoot a gun”).\n\nThroughout the song Tyler pronounces “Cherry Bomb” like “Chur Bum.” This saying was influenced by a toon account Tyler stumbled upon last summer, known as “Tylar, Teh Creatur.”\n\n https://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/587352568541478912", "annotation_id": "5206102", "url": "https://genius.com/5206102", "state": "accepted", "votes": 97, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "For the nine-nine and two-thousand", "vault_lines": ["For the nine-nine and two-thousand"], "meaning": "Back in the “Hot Boys” era Juvenile would proudly say “Cash Money Record takin' over for the ‘99 and the 2000’s.” Tyler pays homage to the Hot Boys with another reference to them.", "annotation_id": "5206095", "url": "https://genius.com/5206095", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Ban a kid from a country, I never fall, never timber", "vault_lines": ["Ban a kid from a country, I never fall, never timber"], "meaning": "Tyler compares timber falling to parents “failing” to raise their children. While his fans' parents may have kept him out of New Zealand, he jokes that they “failed” as a parent since he’s their kid’s idol.\n\nTyler has a similar line on “Nightmare”:\n\nAll because a nigga just don’t give a fuck\nParents wanna blame me all because their kid is fucking up\nBut fuck that, you’re a shitty parent, face it, suck it up\n\nhttps://twitter.com/tylerthecreator/status/606663536845004802?lang=en-gb", "annotation_id": "5206086", "url": "https://genius.com/5206086", "state": "accepted", "votes": 119, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "And fuck your loud pack, and fuck your Snapchat (Man)", "vault_lines": ["And fuck your loud pack, and fuck your Snapchat (Man)"], "meaning": "Tyler dislikes loud pack (good marijuana) and when people use social media apps like Snapchat. He believes instead of being themselves, people put on an act just to get likes and comments.\n\nBoth Tyler and Earl Sweatshirt have been known to insult fans at their shows if they catch them watching the show from behind a phone, rather than living in and enjoying the moment.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/587431970872803328\n\nhttp://imgur.com/akMsXU4\n\nHe also raps this line in the same meter as this line Lil Wayne used on “Barry Bonds.”", "annotation_id": "5206082", "url": "https://genius.com/5206082", "state": "accepted", "votes": 116, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "It’s them Golf boys, like them Hot Boys (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["It's them Golf boys, like them Hot Boys (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Tyler compares his Golf Wang clique to that of the Hot Boys whom Wayne was a part of from 1997-2001.", "annotation_id": "5206080", "url": "https://genius.com/5206080", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Boy, let’s get a scrimmage and cut some niggas, I’ll bring the Clippers And a couple owners that’s kinda German", "vault_lines": ["Boy, let's get a scrimmage and cut some niggas, I'll bring the Clippers"], "meaning": "Donald Sterling was the famously racist owner of the L.A. Clippers. Tyler’s playing on the fact that he’ll “cut some niggas,” using the team (clippers are another word for scissors).\n\nFurthermore, when Donald was going to be ousted for his racism scandal, it was rumored that a few wealthy German investors would purchase the team. The reference to Germany plays into Tyler’s mention of Jews in Berlin a few lines later, an allusion to Nazi Germany, and a thread to the tapestry of racial tension that Tyler weaves in this verse.\n\nNote the duck/Donald wordplay.", "annotation_id": "5206078", "url": "https://genius.com/5206078", "state": "accepted", "votes": 96, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Put that fuckin’ cow on my level, ’cause I’m raising the stakes", "vault_lines": ["Put that fuckin' cow on my level, 'cause I'm raising the stakes"], "meaning": "Tyler refers to his level of success and his newly elevated socio-economic status with a play on “stakes” & “steaks”.\n\nSince risking it all and moving out of Section 8 government housing, Tyler and his family have become much better off.\n\nHe’s at such a high level, even two of his idols, Kanye West & Lil Wayne are featured on his album.\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/596446923336380417", "annotation_id": "5206059", "url": "https://genius.com/5206059", "state": "accepted", "votes": 177, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I made a million mistakes, but I’m successful in spite of ’em", "vault_lines": ["I made a million mistakes, but I'm successful in spite of 'em"], "meaning": "Kanye’s no stranger to mistakes. From politically incorrect interviews, to rude interruptions, he’s done some things he’s not so proud of.\n\nHe compares his mistakes to a fitness trainer eating “junk food” – they’re still at the top of their game, but not everyone’s perfect.", "annotation_id": "5206046", "url": "https://genius.com/5206046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Money, money, money, money, money ain’t the motive What’s your name again? Nobody knows it", "vault_lines": ["Money, money, money, money, money ain't the motive"], "meaning": "As Tyler raps in “Yonkers”:\n\nGreen paper, gold teeth and pregnant golden retrievers\nAll I want, fuck money, diamonds and bitches, don’t need them\n\nHe isn’t in the game for the fat checks, but sometimes he claims he doesn’t even like rapping. So what’s he in it for?! Part of Tyler’s charm is we’re never quite sure.\n\n\n\nThe delivery of “money, money, money” is similar to Kanye West’s in “Gotta Have It” from Watch The Throne.\n\nHe also says “Money ain’t the motive” the way Lil Wayne said “The money is the motive” on We Be Steady Mobbin' featuring Gucci Mane who Tyler is a known fan of.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/fucktyler/status/596446232937136128", "annotation_id": "5206042", "url": "https://genius.com/5206042", "state": "accepted", "votes": 101, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "They say I’m crazy, but that’s the best thing goin’ for me", "vault_lines": ["They say I'm crazy, but that's the best thing goin' for me"], "meaning": "Kanye’s been called crazy his whole career,  but it’s his singular individuality that makes him impossible to imitate or replace. He mentioned being crazy during his lecture at Oxford earlier in 2015.\n\nAnd as he rapped on “Otis”:\n\nThey say I’m crazy, but I’m about to go dumb again", "annotation_id": "5206019", "url": "https://genius.com/5206019", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "He said, ”I gave you a big dick, so go extra hard”, uh (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["He said, \"I gave you a big dick, so go extra hard\", uh (Woo)"], "meaning": "Kanye ends the verse in typical Yeezus fashion, as he rapped in “Breathe In Breathe Out”:\n\nI always had a Ph.D.: a Pretty Huge Dick\n\n\n\nAlso note the worldplay on dick/hard.", "annotation_id": "5206009", "url": "https://genius.com/5206009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 295, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Tyler, The Creator sweatin’ Jesus juice", "vault_lines": ["Tyler, The Creator sweatin' Jesus juice"], "meaning": "Just like Jesus, Tyler turns water into wine. Blessed wine used for Holy Communion can be crudely referred to “Jesus Juice” – Tyler’s sweat is God like.", "annotation_id": "5205986", "url": "https://genius.com/5205986", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Cocaine, bathroom break, nose extra runny", "vault_lines": ["Cocaine, bathroom break, nose extra runny"], "meaning": "Cocaine deteriorates the nasal membrane, causing the user’s nose to consistently run. Since Yeezy’s rich it’s appropriate for him to do drugs in the bathroom. Kanye has referenced cocaine use before.", "annotation_id": "5205984", "url": "https://genius.com/5205984", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "I know they told they white daughters, “Don’t bring home Jerome”", "vault_lines": ["I know they told they white daughters, \"Don't bring home Jerome\""], "meaning": "Jerome was in fact a character on the hit 1990s sitcom “Martin.” Nicknamed Romey Rome, the character a grimy ladies' man played by Martin Lawrence in multiple episodes.\n\n\n\nYe has also mentioned Jerome multiple times in previous songs “Bound 2” and “Illest Motherfucker Alive”:\n\n\n“Jerome is in the house, watch your mouth”\n“I mean damn, what would Jeromey Romey Romey Rome think?”\n“And I swear to God they so cold / Got a nigga in Miami wearing winter clothes / I got my fur on feelin' like Jerome”\n\n\n\nAs Kanye also mentioned in “Gorgeous”, Jerome is a popular black male name. Kanye talks about white parents that don’t want their daughters to hang out with black guys, while in the next line, says he’s a “free nigga archetype” – Jerome is a black male archetype too, scaring white parents.", "annotation_id": "5205973", "url": "https://genius.com/5205973", "state": "accepted", "votes": 120, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Richer than white people with black kids", "vault_lines": ["Richer than white people with black kids"], "meaning": "“White people with black kids” refers to the tendency of wealthy Caucasians to adopt African children from third world countries, like Brad Pitt and Angelina Jolie have.\n\nBig Sean rapped a similar line on “Outro (Dark Sky Paradise)”:\n\nBut I’m tryna get that real real money, like um\nWhite people with a black son\n\n\n\nThis may also be a reference to an episode that took place in the second season of the Loiter Squad, Lionel plays a young blind man taken in forcibly by a rich white woman. Despite protesting his independence and desire to be at home, the woman refuses to realize that she is in no way helping “Big Mike”.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PU254F0stE0", "annotation_id": "5205970", "url": "https://genius.com/5205970", "state": "accepted", "votes": 166, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "Nah, faggot, it’s Golf Wang", "vault_lines": ["Or lame, nor strange, nah, faggot, it's Golf Wang"], "meaning": "A spoonerism of Tyler’s group Odd Future Wolf Gang Kill Them All", "annotation_id": "5205956", "url": "https://genius.com/5205956", "state": "accepted", "votes": 327, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "line": "’Cause Nike gave a lot of niggas checks", "vault_lines": ["'Cause Nike gave a lot of niggas checks"], "meaning": "While many black athletes receive cheques from Nike as endorsement deals, Kanye’s the only one to “check them” per-se – he has aggressively challenged Nike’s approach to doing business since signing with Adidas in late 2013.\n\nThe Nike Swoosh is sometimes referred to as a “check”.", "annotation_id": "5205946", "url": "https://genius.com/5205946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 369, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "SMUCKERS", "status": "done", "targets": 72, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Tyler-the-creator-smuckers-lyrics", "genius_title": "SMUCKERS", "genius_id": 748243, "source": "api"}
