{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "line": "The world’s screwed and niggas pourin’ drinks like Bill Huxtable (Ha)", "vault_lines": ["The world's screwed and niggas pourin’ drinks like Bill Huxtable (Ha)"], "meaning": "Luda opens the track with a reflection on the state of the world by mentioning “Bill Huxtable”–a mix of Bill Cosby and his character Dr. Cliff Huxtable from his hit 1980s sitcom The Cosby Show.\n\n\n\nIn 2014, talk of Bill Cosby’s past incidents of sexual assault resurfaced. After a public outcry and subsequent investigation, it was uncovered that he had used Quaaludes in the past to sedate women who he wanted to have sex with during various encounters. He was subsequently arrested, convicted in 2018 on sexual assault charges and sentenced to 10 years in prison but his conviction was overturned after three years when it was discovered that his due process rights were violated.\n\nLuda points out the dichotomy of arguably the most popular TV dad in history being played by a man with this type of Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde past, showing that many may put on a friendly front while engaging in devious acts. He also alludes to “lean,” a drugged drink where cough syrup is “poured up” into a cup with soda. The drink is associated with Houston’s DJ Screw, who died in 2000 from an overdose of codeine, an ingredient in the cough syrup.", "annotation_id": "28055223", "url": "https://genius.com/28055223", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "line": "Damn, shit ’bout to get ugly Like Shabba Ranks, Mr. Lover Man", "vault_lines": ["Damn, shit 'bout to get ugly"], "meaning": "To prelude a potentially unattractive situation, Lil Wayne alludes to the 1992 In Living Color sketch “Mr. Ugly Man,” which was a Marlon Wayans parody of the 1991 Shabba Ranks hit “Mr. Loverman”:\nhttps://youtu.be/FXXWF8tC3t8", "annotation_id": "23644406", "url": "https://genius.com/23644406", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "line": ".45 tucked away in the gut (Uh) ain’t a killer but don’t test me", "vault_lines": [".45 tucked away in the gut (Uh) ain't a killer but don't test me"], "meaning": "Reference to 2Pac’s classic bar from “Hail Mary”:\n\nI ain’t a killer, but don’t push me", "annotation_id": "23644274", "url": "https://genius.com/23644274", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "line": "But Mayweather told me blow my change on the shopping spree", "vault_lines": ["But Mayweather told me blow my change on the shopping spree"], "meaning": "Floyd Mayweather is a former professional boxer who was active and an undefeated defensive specialist between 1996 and 2017 while fighting in occasional exhibitions in the years since his retirement. In 2017, he amassed more than $1 billion in career earnings, and as the leader of The Money Team, Mayweather is also known for his lavish spending, once spending $5.3 million on a shopping spree in 2018. While Gandhi inspired Ludacris to lead by example, Money Mayweather inspired Luda’s ludicrously lavish living.", "annotation_id": "19937376", "url": "https://genius.com/19937376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "line": "Stand for what you believe in like Kaepernick You either in control or you gettin’ fucked, no abstinence Huh, it’s not enough blacks in the drivin’ seat like a Nascar Why? Cause most racist people still drinkin’ what’s at Roseanne’s bar", "vault_lines": ["Stand for what you believe in like Kaepernick"], "meaning": "With these lines, Ludacris refers to perceived racial inequality and police brutality against black people.\n\nFirst, a reference is made to Colin Kaepernick, a quarterback who played American football for the San Francisco 49ers. In 2016, Kaepernick protested racial injustice and inequality by kneeling during the U.S. national anthem which was played before the games. As is customary, NFL players normally stand up during the national anthem. His actions led to further protests. Ludacris contrasts Kaepernick’s kneeling with him standing up for his beliefs.\n\nSecondly, Ludacris states that black people are not in control of their own situation. He asserts that if you are not in control in the U.S., you are likely to be screwed over, most likely by the oppressors he believes to be systematically maintaining racial inequality in the U.S.. Abstinence means one refrains from sexual activities for a variety of reasons. Ludacris then states that many black people are not in control of their own situation; not in the drivin' seat of their own lives. In contrast, a NASCAR driver usually has excquisite control over his vehicle.\n\nLastly, Ludacris asserts that the reason black people are not in control is because of the spread of racism against black minorities in the United States. As an illustration, he makes a reference to Roseanne Barr, best known for her eponymous sitcom Roseanne, which ran from 1988 to 1997. In 2018, Barr was heavily criticised for a tweet about Valerie Jarrett, former advisor to former U.S. president Barack Obama. The tweet sparked allegations of racism against black people and Muslims. By making a play on her last name, Ludacris concludes that American people are still drinking from Roseanne’s bar, meaning that racism is still widespread among the U.S. population.", "annotation_id": "19937258", "url": "https://genius.com/19937258", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "line": "I love R. Kelly but around my daughters, I’m not comfortable (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["I love R. Kelly but around my daughters, I'm not comfortable (Uh)"], "meaning": "R. Kelly and Ludacris have worked on several songs together, including R. Kelly’s “Legs Shakin'” and “Rock Star,” Luda’s “Woozy” and Lil Jon & The East Side Boyz’s “In Da Club.”\n\n\n\nIn 2019, R. Kelly was arrested for his alleged involvement in child pornography, kidnapping and forced labor, among other charges. He is currently imprisoned in Chicago. At the time of this song’s release, Luda had three daughters, aged 18, 6, and 4 years old. While he still expressed some support for Kellz, he would still be wary of leaving his daughters alone with him based on his alleged extracurricular activities with young girls.", "annotation_id": "19937185", "url": "https://genius.com/19937185", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "line": "Woah, they say between love and hate there’s a thin line (Yeah) I say love or hate, still no snitchin’, that’s a 6ix9ine (No)", "vault_lines": ["Woah, they say between love and hate there's a thin line (Yeah)"], "meaning": "While alluding to the 1971 song “Thin Line Between Love and Hate” by Persuaders, Luda suggests that whether he loves or hates somebody, he would never snitch on them like rapper Tekashi 6ix9ine, who testified in court in 2019 against members of the Nine Trey Gangsta Bloods while also implicating rappers Jim Jones and Cardi B as gang members in order to reduce his jail time.", "annotation_id": "19928297", "url": "https://genius.com/19928297", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "line": "Oh, watch me pass on that ass like Kendall Jenner (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Oh, watch me pass on that ass like Kendall Jenner (Woah)"], "meaning": "This could have two meanings;\n\n(1) Kendall Jenner is famously one of the only Kardashian members to not have a surgically enhanced ass. Luda is saying like Kendall, he’s going to ‘pass on that ass,’ suggesting that he is going to pass up having sex with a girl.\n\n(2) Kendall was recently slammed in the media for dating different NBA players. She responded to some tweets about her being passed around, and clarified that she was the one doing the passing.", "annotation_id": "19917360", "url": "https://genius.com/19917360", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "line": "What the world needs now (What’s that?) Is love sweet love (Is love sweet love)", "vault_lines": ["What the world needs now (What's that?)"], "meaning": "Luda uses lyrics from “What the World Needs Now Is Love”, a 1965 song first recorded and made popular by Jackie DeShannon. The song was originally offered to Dionne Warwick, who turned it down at the time, saying she felt it was “too country” for her tastes  but she later recorded it for her album Here Where There Is Love.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PdzR8oO2KhY", "annotation_id": "19917274", "url": "https://genius.com/19917274", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "line": "Hah, Gandhi told me to be the change that I wanna see", "vault_lines": ["Hah, Gandhi told me to be the change that I wanna see"], "meaning": "Mahatma Gandhi (originally Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi) was an Indian political figure known for his philosophies of non-violence.\n\nLuda here refers to one of his famous quotes:\n\nYou must be the change you want to see in the world.", "annotation_id": "19912325", "url": "https://genius.com/19912325", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Ludacris-sotl-silence-of-the-lambs-lyrics", "genius_title": "S.O.T.L. (Silence of the Lambs)", "genius_id": 5584559, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Now let me see ya kickflip, kickflip, kickflip, kickflip, kickflip, kickflip", "vault_lines": ["Now let me see ya kickflip, kickflip, kickflip, kickflip, kickflip, kickflip"], "meaning": "The Kickflip is a skateboarding trick where the rider ollies and kicks his/her foot out and flips the board 360 degrees along its long axis with his/her toes, allows the board to spin all of the way around, and then catches it and lands.", "annotation_id": "2673508", "url": "https://genius.com/2673508", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "[Verse 1: Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": ["S.A.S.A.R.A.F. = Skate and Smoke and Rap and Fuck"], "meaning": "This verse and the hook are rapped acapella by Wayne as a freestyle on the track before SASARAF (this song) on the DJ Stevie J Appreciation Vol. 4 mixtape they both exclusively appeared on.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ndCFJLHRMHw", "annotation_id": "1670667", "url": "https://genius.com/1670667", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Back on my bullshit, I’m back on my bullshit", "vault_lines": ["Back on my bullshit, I'm back on my bullshit"], "meaning": "Wayne’s saying he’s back to his old rapping self quality-wise despite what some/many/all of his fans think.\n\nAlso possibly referencing the 2009 Busta Rhymes album titled Back on My B.S.", "annotation_id": "1670648", "url": "https://genius.com/1670648", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "We go Bozo", "vault_lines": [", we go Bozo"], "meaning": "Bozo is a famous clown originating in the 60’s. by saying going Bozo, mean’s to start acting like a clown. “Going crazy and stupid”", "annotation_id": "803668", "url": "https://genius.com/803668", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "5Boro", "vault_lines": ["S.A.S.A.R.A.F. = Skate and Smoke and Rap and Fuck"], "meaning": "5Boro NYC is Lil Wayne’s skate entourage/crew, to which he has been sending a lot of shout outs and also got a tattoo of its logo.", "annotation_id": "803282", "url": "https://genius.com/803282", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "If you don’t want beef milk the cow cowboy", "vault_lines": ["If you don't want beef milk the cow cowboy"], "meaning": "You can either kill the cow and get beef (usually as in meat but Wayne makes a play on beefing/battling) or keep it alive and milk the cow…the line would work better the other way around, though.\n\nAlso if you don’t want “beef” or a conflict with him, you’re going to have to “milk” him or get him off.  Which probably should require a “nohomo”.", "annotation_id": "803165", "url": "https://genius.com/803165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "If you scared go to church, I shoot at the pulpit", "vault_lines": ["If you scared go to church, I shoot at the pulpit"], "meaning": "Wayne will take over the priest’s speech to make it more “fun”.\n\n\n\n:If you scared go to church\" is onne of Lil Wayne’s quotes mentioned on the songs “Two Shots” from Tha Carter IV and “Gucci Gucci” from Sorry 4 The Wait, amongst others", "annotation_id": "803161", "url": "https://genius.com/803161", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Glock with the magazine do you want the cover nigga huh?", "vault_lines": ["Glock with the magazine do you want the cover nigga huh?"], "meaning": "A gun must be packed with a magazine (the container for bullets). Therefore, this is a wordplay: It suggests that the gun’s magazine is in reality a readable magazine, so then he questions if one wants the cover (bullet/s)", "annotation_id": "803156", "url": "https://genius.com/803156", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Bitch better have my money", "vault_lines": ["Bitch better have my money"], "meaning": "What a pimp says (to himself and others) when he’s on his way to collect money from his hookers. This is also a reference to the 1992 song by AMG, “Bitch Betta Have My Money”.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dKBUUXm0eow", "annotation_id": "803153", "url": "https://genius.com/803153", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Kidnap his mom, and fuck her like Stifflers", "vault_lines": ["Kidnap his mom, and fuck her like Stifflers"], "meaning": "In the movie American Pie the mother of Stifler gets fucked by Finch at the end of the movie. This moment is known for originating the term “MILF” (Mom I’d Like to Fuck)", "annotation_id": "803117", "url": "https://genius.com/803117", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Fuck around and get stuck like gum down here", "vault_lines": ["Fuck around and get stuck like gum down here"], "meaning": "A play on gum being sticky and stick ups. A stick up is an armed robbery in which a gun is used to threaten people.", "annotation_id": "803107", "url": "https://genius.com/803107", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Punch him in the kisser", "vault_lines": ["punch him in the kisser"], "meaning": "Punch him in the face. Kisser = mouth, which is usually regarded as the face’s centred point. For the case of a swisher, punching will mean taking a deep puff, one that will therefore screw you!!", "annotation_id": "803092", "url": "https://genius.com/803092", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Man light up that Swisher,", "vault_lines": ["Man light up that Swisher,"], "meaning": "Swisher as in a “Swisher” brand cigar. Filled with the worst tobacco you could possibly smoke. But the manufacturer knows that. They know that folks don’t actually smoke their shit. The purpose of the Swisher is to roll a blunt and smoke weed.", "annotation_id": "803084", "url": "https://genius.com/803084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "My girl pussy sweeter than a whatchamacallit", "vault_lines": ["My girl pussy sweeter than a whatchamacallit"], "meaning": "A Watchamacallit is a candy bar by the Hershey Company.\n\n\n\nIt also gives the sense of Wayne questioning: what Imma call it?\n\nWayne has compared his girl’s/s' vagina to a lot of stuff on his lyrics, therefore, he does not even know what to compare it to anymore. Or these girl’s cookie is so sweet that there’s nothing compared to!", "annotation_id": "803053", "url": "https://genius.com/803053", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Um, I’m in that Trukfit", "vault_lines": ["Um, I'm in that Trukfit"], "meaning": "Wayne is wearing his own clothing line; “Trukfit”.", "annotation_id": "803043", "url": "https://genius.com/803043", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "I ain’t worried bout ’em, I say “Hi hater” I throw you off the top of a skyscraper", "vault_lines": ["I ain't worried bout 'em, I say \"Hi hater\""], "meaning": "Wayne doesn’t care for haters, because they can’t hurt him. He just “kills” them by simply throwing them of a skyscraper, which are relatively high.\n\n\n\nLil Wayne is the rapper on top at the moment (not as an opinion, but as a fact for the awards he won on the 2012 BET Awards). He is so high, higher than a scryscaber (which he might consider something avarage), so he will have the generosity to go down to these rappers level and send em down (kill their carrer)!", "annotation_id": "802962", "url": "https://genius.com/802962", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "And I ain’t no magician so I never love a trick", "vault_lines": ["And I ain't no magician so I never love a trick"], "meaning": "A play on how magicians perform tricks, and how he will never love a trick.\n\nTrick is slang for describing women who are either teases, hoes, or one of the above pretending to be the other. Calling a woman a trick shows you are not impressed/convinced by their shit.\n\nOR\n\nWeezy specially loves a female who does tricks, who “hop up on that dick and do a full split”! But he got so used to it that females can’t really surprise him with anything they try for him in bed", "annotation_id": "802955", "url": "https://genius.com/802955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Don’t test me, motherfucker I study", "vault_lines": ["Don't test me, motherfucker I study"], "meaning": "Pusha doesn’t even need to study for his tests…\n\n\n\nThe meaning of this wordplay is that Weezy is a confident person (“study”), he is ready for any situation and anyone fronting him (“test”), therefore he is not afraid of it", "annotation_id": "802950", "url": "https://genius.com/802950", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "S.A.S.A.R.A.F.", "line": "Yeah, my gun “pow” like Gasol", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, my gun \"pow\" like Gasol"], "meaning": "Pau Gasol is a spanish NBA player for the LA Lakers\n\nHe uses the name of the player as an onomatopoeia for ‘shooting’. Pau Gasol currently holds the Memphis Grizzlies franchise records for a lot of stuff, of which one of them is being a good shooter.\n\nBasically, Weezy created a pun for Los Angeles Lakers' power forward/center, Pau Gasol.", "annotation_id": "802935", "url": "https://genius.com/802935", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
