{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "These bitches sellin’ they soul Well, I want my money back", "vault_lines": ["Bitches want money stacks, I just want my percent"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION:\n\nWayne is saying he sold his soul and now wants a money back because he already got everything he wanted and at this point there’s nothing much else to gain.", "annotation_id": "11496190", "url": "https://genius.com/11496190", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "They only wish is for a new chain But they stuck up in the ankle bracelet", "vault_lines": ["They only wish is for a new chain"], "meaning": "Killers rob and steal hoping for an upgrade in the street game. As they continue to thieve, they get in trouble by the law.\nWale uses ‘ankle bracelet’ as a means to refer to ankle monitors issued by parole officers while also keeping the jewelry theme introduced in the previous line.", "annotation_id": "15586155", "url": "https://genius.com/15586155", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "And I move where the realest be And the quickest, see, baby, you gettin’ lapped", "vault_lines": ["And I move where the realest be"], "meaning": "He “moves” or operates with whom he claims to be the realest – Maybach Music Group.\n\nGoing along with the word “moving” as well as the sports theme of the song, he says moves so much faster that he’s lapping people, as seen in track.", "annotation_id": "11375823", "url": "https://genius.com/11375823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "All of this fog like the weather change", "vault_lines": ["All of this fog like the weather change"], "meaning": "Use of weather imagery and the play on words that Wayne implies one thing while saying another is well done. The fog from his weed smoke, then the hurricane from making it rain money, and finally the snow flurry of cocaine ties up the triplet with class and style. Weezy man.", "annotation_id": "11252485", "url": "https://genius.com/11252485", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "You niggas be fumbling, don’t you give ’em no gun again", "vault_lines": ["You niggas be fumbling, don't you give 'em no gun again"], "meaning": "Continuing with the football wordplay, “fumbling” here essentially means messing up.\n\n\n\nThese people keep “dropping the ball” when it’s in their hands, so they definitely can’t be trusted with an opportunity to do some harm.", "annotation_id": "11249508", "url": "https://genius.com/11249508", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "I get the money stacked See the moon’s where it’s sunny at", "vault_lines": ["I get the money stacked"], "meaning": "This is an oxymoron of sorts, seeing as the moon is best seen when the sun is not visible.\n\nHowever, Wale’s creative company, EBM (Every Blue Moon), which consists of designers, artists & videographers, has a bright and sunny future.", "annotation_id": "11246587", "url": "https://genius.com/11246587", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "Yeah, I used to play running back I turned that football to a money bag,", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I used to play running back"], "meaning": "A good running back doesn’t fumble the football once it is in their possession. Therefore, Lil Wayne doesn’t lose his money once he’s got his hands on it.\n\nTurning the football to a money bag could also refer to the money he made while making runs selling dope, including Football Xanax.", "annotation_id": "11224993", "url": "https://genius.com/11224993", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "Look what them booty shots done to that That bitch need her money back, Lord", "vault_lines": ["Look what them booty shots done to that"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne joins the list of rappers  unamused with butt injections. On “Back On The Bullshyt” by 2 Chainz, a song in which Wayne is featured, 2 Chainz states his disdain for butt injections:\n\nBad booty shots got you lopsided\n\nWale also declares he isn’t all for girls getting butt injections in his song “Lacefrontin.”\n\nBooty shots, fake eyes, fake bitches, fake broads\nAnd you ask twitter why you getting fake guys", "annotation_id": "11224773", "url": "https://genius.com/11224773", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "We got that cocaine, snow flurry gang", "vault_lines": ["We got that cocaine, snow flurry gang"], "meaning": "Young Jeezy popularized using the word “snow” as slang for cocaine in rap music, by referring to himself as “The Snowman.” Wayne uses this slang also to describe the drugs in his possession.", "annotation_id": "11224742", "url": "https://genius.com/11224742", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "Turn the strip club to a hurricane", "vault_lines": ["Turn the strip club to a hurricane"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has gloated about the money he tosses around at strip clubs throughout his career. Songs like “Make it Rain” and “Got Money” go into further detail about how much Lil Wayne enjoys facilitating his wealth. However, while normal people make it rain in the strip club, Wayne brings the whole storm. His catalog is jam packed with hurricane references after Hurricane Katrina devastated his home town of New Orleans.", "annotation_id": "11224707", "url": "https://genius.com/11224707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "Yeah, the DMV on the map That’s a city, two states if you can count", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the DMV on the map"], "meaning": "“DMV” is an acronym for DC (from where Wale originates), Maryland & Virginia.", "annotation_id": "11206459", "url": "https://genius.com/11206459", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "I be with killers just coming home They only hope is me and the Quran", "vault_lines": ["I be with killers just coming home"], "meaning": "Wale compares himself to The Quran which is a holy book of Islam. He gives motivation and inspiration to his friends on the streets, similar to the way the Quran gives hope to Muslims.\n\nAlthough Wale has not identified as being Muslim, he has made several references to Islam on tracks such as “Self Made” and “By Any Means,”", "annotation_id": "11204180", "url": "https://genius.com/11204180", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "Since Jesus of Nazareth The realest you’ve come across", "vault_lines": ["Since Jesus of Nazareth"], "meaning": "Here, Wale states that he is the realest person known since biblical times when Jesus was alive.\n\nJesus is believed to be one of the most righteous beings in many religions—living a life purely in God’s will and abiding by the truth at all times; hence, being the “realest”.\n\nIn addition, he uses wordplay within the word “across” as Jesus died on the cross for the sins of his people.", "annotation_id": "11202680", "url": "https://genius.com/11202680", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "She like the finer things She said I sent her a diamond ring She say I buy her all kinds of things She lie about everything I put her on time out and everything", "vault_lines": ["She like the finer things"], "meaning": "In early January 2016, there was rumors that Lil Wayne bought @ErikaFBaby a diamond ring after she posted on Instagram pictures of a diamond ring that was sent to her in a package with a card reading “from Wayne,” as in Lil Wayne. But Lil Wayne tweeted, “I don’t send rings thru the mail people I’m much more romantic than that stop it.”", "annotation_id": "11200634", "url": "https://genius.com/11200634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "line": "She told me to hit the hole, I used to play running back", "vault_lines": ["She told me to hit the hole, I used to play running back"], "meaning": "A skilled football player in high school, Wale earned scholarships to both Robert Morris University and Virginia State University. He later transferred to Bowie State University prior to dropping out for academic reasons.\n\nHe’s well qualified, then, to make the “hit the hole” double entendre here. Running backs use that lingo to mean looking for breaks in the defensive line.", "annotation_id": "11198083", "url": "https://genius.com/11198083", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Running Back", "status": "done", "targets": 15, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Wale-running-back-lyrics", "genius_title": "Running Back", "genius_id": 2947324, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Runnin Circles", "line": "I’m on two-eighty five around these square ass niggas", "vault_lines": ["I'm on two-eighty five around these square ass niggas"], "meaning": "Gucci calls himself the King of Atlanta. Interstate 285 (I-285) is an interstate highway loop encircling Atlanta, Georgia. It is 64 miles long and literally creates a circle around Atlanta. Gucci uses a play on words in this line saying he’s running circles around some square ass niggas.", "annotation_id": "1831227", "url": "https://genius.com/1831227", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Runnin Circles", "line": "I ball like Kobe, you know I’m shootin’", "vault_lines": ["I ball like Kobe, you know I'm shootin'"], "meaning": "Kobe Bryant is known for taking an insane amount of shots in the NBA and not passing the ball. Like Kobe, Gucci shoots a lot too, but he shoots with a gun.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vYm6i3JPK5Y", "annotation_id": "1517865", "url": "https://genius.com/1517865", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
