{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "I look in the flames and see a hotter me", "vault_lines": ["I look in the flames and see a hotter me"], "meaning": "Reference to his 2002 album 500 Degreez, which itself is a reference to Juvenile’s album 400 Degreez.  Juvenile also responded to Wayne’s 500 Degreez with 600 Degreez.", "annotation_id": "29172965", "url": "https://genius.com/29172965", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "Now, I’m off that “super” shit, fuck that shit, I super-quit", "vault_lines": ["Now, I'm off that \"super\" shit, fuck that shit, I super-quit"], "meaning": "Wayne decides to mess with his listeners here and shows how he loves to have fun on his mixtapes. Right when listeners think Weezy is finished with the “super” repetition, he hits them with “super quit”", "annotation_id": "26226522", "url": "https://genius.com/26226522", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "Perfection is the goal, and I’m headed to the pylon", "vault_lines": ["Perfection is the goal, and I'm headed to the pylon"], "meaning": "The goal refers to the endzone in American football, and the pylon is the orange cone-like object that marks the corner of the endzone. Lil Wayne is saying here he is heading towards perfection", "annotation_id": "20721741", "url": "https://genius.com/20721741", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "Put the beat in ER", "vault_lines": ["put the beat in ER"], "meaning": "The ER can be known as the emergency room. Wayne is “killing the beat” by putting it in the ER.", "annotation_id": "18205224", "url": "https://genius.com/18205224", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "I’m proud of me", "vault_lines": ["Young Mula, baby; I'm proud of me"], "meaning": "Wayne is one of the most successful rappers in the game, he has been nominated for 179 awards, and has been awarded 64 times.He has also sold a lot of copies.", "annotation_id": "17028893", "url": "https://genius.com/17028893", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "Riding this track like a motherfucking streetcar", "vault_lines": ["Riding this track like a motherfucking streetcar"], "meaning": "A “streetcar” is a reference to the book, “A Streetcar Named Desire.” This book takes place in Wayne’s city of New Orleans, which he goes on to mention in the next line.\n\nIn the book, the car is called “desire”, and the car drives you to your luxury in life. The car is later called “Cemetery” and it drives you to the Elysian Fields, which is used to represent heaven or an afterlife. Wayne has numerously talked about how well his afterlife will be.", "annotation_id": "15788483", "url": "https://genius.com/15788483", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "Super-Millz, Mack, Tyga, Streets, ‘Nelly, Super Nick’ Super-Drizzy, Gudda, Chuckee, Twist, that’s the super-clique", "vault_lines": ["Super-Millz, Mack, Tyga, Streets, 'Nelly, Super Nick'"], "meaning": "The Young Money roster at the time of this recording.", "annotation_id": "13126916", "url": "https://genius.com/13126916", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "Running circles ’round the game, like a hula hoop and shit You gon’ have to loop this shit, there won’t be a duplicate", "vault_lines": ["Running circles 'round the game, like a hula hoop and shit"], "meaning": "A hula-hoop is a toy that you put around your waist, and then you begin to move your waist back and forth to the left and right of you, eventually creating a circular motion for the hula hoop to revolve around.\n\nTo “run circles” around something is to be ahead of everyone, so Lil Wayne is easily ahead of everyone else in the game.\n\n\n\nWeezy also lets us know that he will never stop running circles around the rap game and there will never be anyone like him, which is hard to argue.", "annotation_id": "998771", "url": "https://genius.com/998771", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "And my blunts be super-thick, I’m higher than a Supra kick", "vault_lines": ["And my blunts be super-thick, I'm higher than a Supra kick"], "meaning": "The super kick is employed by using the heel of one’s foot to deliver a headshot to an opponent. This obviously requires serious leg elevation either by jumping or remarkable flexiblity.\n\nShawn Michaels, aka “The Heartbreak Kid”, of the bygone era of WWF/WWE wrestling was famous for his version of the SuperKick, called Sweet Chin Music.", "annotation_id": "37592", "url": "https://genius.com/37592", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "Tunechi be the wildest, let’s run the metropolis", "vault_lines": ["Tunechi be the wildest, let's run the metropolis"], "meaning": "Wayne, as he does just a few lines later, intentionally mispronounces this word. He says it as “metro-POLIS” in order to slant rhyme with “wildest”", "annotation_id": "11272", "url": "https://genius.com/11272", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "Do you roger me?", "vault_lines": ["I'm the prodigy—do you roger me?"], "meaning": "On walkie-talkies, people say “Roger” to indicate they got your message\n\nDid you get Wayne’s message, over-and-out?", "annotation_id": "10467", "url": "https://genius.com/10467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "I’m colder than “B-R,” add another three Rs", "vault_lines": ["I'm colder than \"B-R,\" add another three Rs"], "meaning": "By “cold” he means “icy” (covered in diamonds)\n\n“B-R” either is short for Baskin Robbins – the ice cream chain – or the spelling of “Brr! It’s cold in here!”", "annotation_id": "10460", "url": "https://genius.com/10460", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "C-A-R-T-E-R,", "vault_lines": ["Weezy’s “super”-freestyle uses the beat from Jay-Z’s Grammy-winning sensation!"], "meaning": "A spelling of “Lil” (D)wayne Carter’s last name, as well as the last name of Jay-Z (Shawn Carter), who recorded the original song.", "annotation_id": "10459", "url": "https://genius.com/10459", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "Anybody beat, I’m gon’ go Archie Bunkers", "vault_lines": ["Anybody beat, I'm gon' go Archie Bunkers"], "meaning": "Wayne is conbining “going bonkers” (going crazy) with the last name of All in the Family character Archie Bunker, known for being racist and ill-spirited", "annotation_id": "10374", "url": "https://genius.com/10374", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Run This Town", "line": "Man, I kicks it, bitch, get your shinguard! Ugh", "vault_lines": ["Man, I kicks it, bitch, get your shinguard! Ugh"], "meaning": "A reference to ATCQ’s seminal rap song “Can I Kick It”\n\nOf course, one wears shin guards while playing soccer, which involves kicking", "annotation_id": "10373", "url": "https://genius.com/10373", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
