{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Round Here", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-round-here-lyrics", "genius_title": "Round Here", "genius_id": 3434821, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "You out of work, I know it’s tough", "vault_lines": ["You out of work, I know it's tough"], "meaning": "In 2008 due to a lawsuit with Brookland Ent. more popularly known as, (Trackmasters) a judge ruled that Lil' Kim could not make new music. It remains unclear how long Lil' Kim was contractually barred from making new music, but it’s widely speculated that it lasted from 2008-2016. During this time Lil' Kim did a track with Birdman which also featured Nicki Minaj and she accused them of using the track to stamp Nicki Minaj’s career and discard her as old news. After the track’s official release Lil' Kim would fall out with her contacts at Cash Money. While she alleges shady business on their end, it’s speculated that her failure to disclose her legal woes (being barred from making new music) are the true cause of the fallout. Here with “You out of work, I know it’s tough” Nicki Minaj leans into the idea that her and the rest of the Cash Money team became privy to Lil' Kim’s legal troubles. At this time Lil' Kim , a contestant on “Dancing With The Stars” would still drop mixtapes and tracks dissing Minaj but did not have any commercial music release until 2019.", "annotation_id": "40382622", "url": "https://genius.com/40382622", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "I like a big, wet pussy with a fork and a spoon", "vault_lines": ["I like a big, wet pussy with a fork and a spoon"], "meaning": "", "annotation_id": "35206823", "url": "https://genius.com/35206823", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "I hear them mumblin’, I hear the cacklin’ I got ‘em scared, shook, panickin’", "vault_lines": ["I—I—I—I hear them mumblin', I hear the cacklin'"], "meaning": "During the nicki and lil Kim beef a lot of artists were asked to speak on it a lot of artists say back and played the fence\n\nThis bar now connects to how she felt about missy as well as why we don’t have sufficient enough photographed interactions or lack there of\n\nIt’s been confirmed by a tweet nicki Minaj tweeted for her video vanguard award announcement. Missy Elliot tweeted a congratulatory message and nicki replied with mumbling and cackling\n\nThe connection between the bar and today is that lil Kim’s die hard fans stuck by her side missy always played sides.\n\nCheck supporting bar\n“I see them dusty ass filas", "annotation_id": "26460144", "url": "https://genius.com/26460144", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "I got bars: sentencin", "vault_lines": ["I got bars: sentencin"], "meaning": "Minaj likens her lyrical “bars” to the bars of a jail cell — she included similar wordplay on August 2018’s “Barbie Dreams”:\n\n“I got them bars, I’m indicted”\n\nAlbeit a subtle one, this could be Minaj’s continuation of subliminal jabs toward Lil' Kim. In 2006, Kim was sentenced to a year and a day in prison on three counts of perjury and one count of conspiracy. Since her release the “Queen Bee” hasn’t seen too much success and Minaj has the “bars” to keep Kim’s career on lockdown.\n\nMinaj confirmed this lyric via Twitter.", "annotation_id": "26322969", "url": "https://genius.com/26322969", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "Plasma", "vault_lines": ["I am not Jasmine, I am Aladdin"], "meaning": "Plasma refers to the kind of flat screen TV she’s hanging up.\n\nLike the rest of the Young Money crew and many other rappers these days, Nicki Minaj is known for using what’s called hashtag rap. This song is probably her most obvious and famous display of the technique.\n\nThe concept is simple: you follow a line with a one-word or short-phrase hashtag, then build your rhyme off of it.\n\nStylized with the hashtags, here is what these few lines would look like:\n\nSo fuck I look like getting back to a hasAnnotate-been?\nYeah, I said it, has-been, hang it up #flatscreen #plasma\n“Hey Nicki, hey Nicki,” #asthma\nI got the pumps, it ain’t got medicine\nI got bars #sentencing\nI’m a bad bitch, I’m a cunt\nAnd I’ll kick that ho #punt\nForced trauma #blunt\nYou play the back, bitch, I’m in the front", "annotation_id": "26322889", "url": "https://genius.com/26322889", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "Look at my show footage, how these girls be spazzin’ So fuck I look like gettin’ back to a has-been? Yeah, I said it—”has-been” Hang it up: flatscreen, ha", "vault_lines": ["Look at my show footage, how these girls be spazzin'"], "meaning": "This is one of Nicki’s first direct responses (if technically subliminal – Kim’s name is never mentioned) to Lil' Kim’s provocations\n\nKim spent most of 2010 claiming that Nicki ripped off her style. Nicki has not responded this directly on record, at least until now\n\nNote also that there is an emphasis on the “BEE” in “has-been” in reference to Lil' Kim, who calls herself the “Queen Bee” (cf. Kim’s song “Can’t Fuck With Queen Bee”)\n\nhttp://rarebasedswag.tumblr.com/post/3431287466", "annotation_id": "26322881", "url": "https://genius.com/26322881", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "Raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon", "vault_lines": ["Raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon"], "meaning": "“Rah, rah, like a dungeon dragon” is a phrase that has long been associated with Busta Rhymes. He first used it in his verse on A Tribe Called Quest’s classic “Scenario” and has periodically come back to it since.\n\nMinaj went on to reference these lines on her April 2012 track “Roman Holiday”:\n\n“I'mma put her in a dungeon under, under", "annotation_id": "26322871", "url": "https://genius.com/26322871", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "Raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon Raah, raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon Raah, raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon Like a dungeon dragon, like a dungeon dragon", "vault_lines": ["Raah, raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon"], "meaning": "“Rah, rah, like a dungeon dragon” is a phrase that has long been associated with Busta Rhymes. He first used it in his verse on A Tribe Called Quest’s classic “Scenario” and has periodically come back to it since.\n\nMinaj went on to reference these lines on her April 2012 track “Roman Holiday”:\n\n“I'mma put her in a dungeon under, under", "annotation_id": "26322861", "url": "https://genius.com/26322861", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "I’m startin’ to feel like a dungeon dragon Raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon I’m startin’ to feel like a dungeon dragon", "vault_lines": ["Raah, raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon"], "meaning": "“Rah, rah, like a dungeon dragon” is a phrase that has long been associated with Busta Rhymes. He first used it in his verse on A Tribe Called Quest’s classic “Scenario” and has periodically come back to it since.\n\nMinaj went on to reference these lines on her April 2012 track “Roman Holiday”:\n\n“I'mma put her in a dungeon under, under", "annotation_id": "26322854", "url": "https://genius.com/26322854", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "Raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon Raah, raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon Raah, raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon Like a dungeon dragon, like a dungeon dragon", "vault_lines": ["Raah, raah, raah, like a dungeon dragon"], "meaning": "“Rah, rah, like a dungeon dragon” is a phrase that has long been associated with Busta Rhymes. He first used it in his verse on A Tribe Called Quest’s classic “Scenario” and has periodically come back to it since.\n\nMinaj went on to reference these lines on her April 2012 track “Roman Holiday”:\n\n“I'mma put her in a dungeon under, under", "annotation_id": "26322849", "url": "https://genius.com/26322849", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "So far ahead, these bums is laggin’ See me in that new thing, bums is gaggin’", "vault_lines": ["So far ahead, these bums is laggin'"], "meaning": "Nicki’s use of the word “bums” here is not accidental. It is aimed at rapper Keys. See their history of fighting here. In her verse on DJ Khaled’s “All I Do Is Win (Remix)”, Minaj spits lines that were generally thought to be aimed at Keys:\n\n“I ain’t mad, ma – see you on your bummy swag\nI’m in that money-green Jag, lotta money bags…\nYou could talk slick all the way down to the welfare\nAsk the IRS, bitch, I’m paying for your health care", "annotation_id": "26322824", "url": "https://genius.com/26322824", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "I am not Jasmine, I am Aladdin", "vault_lines": ["I am not Jasmine, I am Aladdin"], "meaning": "This reference to the female love interest and male prince in Disney’s Aladdin movie has several possible interpretations. First, that despite being female, Nicki is playing the part of the aggressive protagonist in the rap game – which certainly fits with the tone and subject matter of this song\n\nSecondly, the “Roman Zolanski” character who raps this number, who Nicki refers to as her twin sister, is sometimes referred to in masculine terms (including in the outro of this song) – thus, she may be emphasizing the playing-with-gender done by her alter ego.\n\nThirdly, in the movie Aladdin, Aladdin sings that he is “one jump ahead,” so Nicki is saying that she is too", "annotation_id": "26322819", "url": "https://genius.com/26322819", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "I got the pumps, it ain’t got medicine", "vault_lines": ["I got the pumps, it ain't got medicine"], "meaning": "This is a follow up to her previous line as “pumps” are also known as Ventolin inhalers. This could mean one of two things, or both even.\n\n\nPumps as in high-healed footwear. This could be an allusion to her multifaceted and extensive shoe collection.\nPumps as in a shotgun. Once fired, you pump the shotgun again to eject the discharged cartridge and to load the next round in a single “pump.” So, “to pump a shotgun” is technically to chamber a cartridge, and/or to eject a spent cartridge.", "annotation_id": "23060487", "url": "https://genius.com/23060487", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "All I do is win, my name should be “Victor”", "vault_lines": ["All I do is win, my name should be \"Victor\""], "meaning": "This is a reference to All I Do is Win by DJ Khaled, a song from his album Victory.\n\nVictor (aside from being a name) means “winner” in English, and since he always wins, he’s considering a name change.", "annotation_id": "99081", "url": "https://genius.com/99081", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "line": "Haha! Old-ass rappers", "vault_lines": ["I am not Jasmine, I am Aladdin"], "meaning": "Subliminal directed at Jay-Z (Cam'ron pioneered Jay-Z age disses – and that was years ago!)\n\nThe line also refers to the multitudes of old-school rappers who have thrown shade at the Young Money camp, most notably Lil' Kim, at whom the rest of the song is directed. Young Money has been positioning itself as the new school: performative, experimental, not necessarily street-credible. Here, Wayne’s mocking the old guard for thinking that they’re still relevant in the changing world of hip-hop.", "annotation_id": "98909", "url": "https://genius.com/98909", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 15, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Nicki-minaj-romans-revenge-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Roman’s Revenge (Remix)", "genius_id": 3480, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Romance", "line": "Send me cards, make me read", "vault_lines": ["Send me cards, make me read"], "meaning": "This might be the only reading Wayne is doing.  From an XXL interview in 2008:\n\n\n I don’t read, other than [for college courses].\n\n But we talking about books for leisure.\n\n Nah, I’ve done that like once or twice. It’s just not my thing. I’m not into made-up stories.\n\n You know how people get together and they like, “Yo, you read…”\n\n I’m not even in that conversation circle. That would be crazy, I can’t answer nothing so why would I sit there and talk? I ain’t read no books. I sit and watch ESPN all day.", "annotation_id": "1621190", "url": "https://genius.com/1621190", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Romance", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-romance-lyrics", "genius_title": "Romance", "genius_id": 132055, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "And the ad is global; your ad was local", "vault_lines": ["And the ad is global; your ad was local"], "meaning": "Nicki is saying that her ad that was produced for her was globally reconized, while “yours” (in refrence to either her haters or as in the media), was not globally reconized. It was “local” saying that you aren’t as famous or known as Nicki.", "annotation_id": "36193996", "url": "https://genius.com/36193996", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Only thing that’s pop is my endorsement, akh", "vault_lines": ["Only thing that’s pop is my endorsement, akh"], "meaning": "She was being endorsed by Pepsi around this time.", "annotation_id": "35625554", "url": "https://genius.com/35625554", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "More knots than Eric on Basketball Wives", "vault_lines": ["More knots than Eric on Basketball Wives"], "meaning": "In this context, “knot” likely refers to the bump on the head of Eric Williams, who appears on the show Basketball Wives. The highlight is that the person being mentioned has more issues or problems in their life than the physical knot on Eric’s head.", "annotation_id": "29946225", "url": "https://genius.com/29946225", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "My ex wanna work it out, bitch, try yoga", "vault_lines": ["My ex wanna work it out, bitch, try yoga"], "meaning": "Wayne A.K.A Weezy is using a metaphor as his ex wants to get back together(work it out) , YOGA is a workout exercise , so he is telling her no go try yoga .", "annotation_id": "27684436", "url": "https://genius.com/27684436", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Raggedy Ann, could never be a Barbie, bitch", "vault_lines": ["Raggedy Ann, could never be a Barbie, bitch"], "meaning": "Nicki told nothing but facts!\n\nA Raggedy Ann doll could never be a Barbie.\n\n\n\nLittle girls aren’t walking with dolls like that in their hands expect for Barbies.\n\n\n\nIf you would put these two dolls in a toy store, which one will outsell the other?\n\nThis might be a subliminal diss to a certain female rapper but we already know who that is.", "annotation_id": "26833628", "url": "https://genius.com/26833628", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "I’m chillin’ at the top, I got ample time", "vault_lines": ["I’m chillin’ at the top, I got ample time"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj is having the time of her life with a shining crown on her head.\n\n\n\nWhen someone has ample time, they have the time needed to finish that task. Sometimes, it means that you have enough time to finish it.", "annotation_id": "26833594", "url": "https://genius.com/26833594", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Yo, is it me, or did I put these rap bitches on the map again?", "vault_lines": ["Yo, is it me, or did I put these rap bitches on the map again?"], "meaning": "Nicki feels that since her career has been taking off she’s provided female rappers with much-needed attention that hasn’t been there for a long time. She spoke about the topic in a 2017 interview with XXL:\n\nMy role in hip-hop has been super unique because when my first album came out, there had been so much time where there wasn’t a female rap album out that went platinum. There wasn’t a big female rap presence right before I got in. So, my role was reintroducing the female rapper to pop culture. \n\nShortly after the interview, Nicki clarified her thoughts after hearing confusion from fans in an Instagram post:\n\nWhen I came out, there had been a drought of a few years where NO female rap album had gone platinum, females weren’t getting budgets, the industry did NOT believe in the female rapper anymore. They had stopped generating MONEY for labels. Ask any rap historian or just anyone with a brain. These are facts and nothing but the facts. So I “REINTRODUCED” the “successful” female rapper back to POP CULTURE. Showed big business we were major players in the game just like the boys were.\n\nOnce her career took off, Nicki became the first female rapper to top the Billboard 200 in nine years, the first female to chart at #1 on the Hot Rap Songs for seven years, and her first album broke the first-week sales for a female rap album, certainly bringing female rappers on the “map again.”\n\nNicki spoke about a similar issue on her 2010 track “Roman’s Revenge:”\n\nIs this the thanks that I get for puttin' you bitches on?\nIs it my fault that all of you bitches gone?", "annotation_id": "19610232", "url": "https://genius.com/19610232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Bite me, Apple sign Ha-ha", "vault_lines": ["Bite me, Apple sign"], "meaning": "A reference to the logo for Apple, which is an apple with a bite taken out of it. Despite her reference to Apple, she performed at Nokia’s Lumia 9000 Phone Launch the same year this was released. She released the song at the end of February 2012 and performed at the launch in early April.", "annotation_id": "13113787", "url": "https://genius.com/13113787", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "[Refrain: Nicki Minaj]", "vault_lines": ["Bang, my shit bang, it bang-bang"], "meaning": "This song is actually a Conceptual one by use of extended metaphor, based on the symbolism of her “firing blanks” on her album people thought she was gonna flop on and not Rap on, doing only Dance and Pop. It’s based on the phrase “Jumpin' The Gun”\n\n\nHear the sound of the hammer being pulled in the background, before the hook starts. A magnum revolver has 6 chamber slots. Count the number of times she uses the “B” sound. It’s said 5 times, before each of her 4 verses. She reloads (the hook) a total of 4 times, aiming the last shot (verse), directly at Lil' Kim. Therefore the verses are actually the REMAINING SHOTS being fired as a diss. 20 blanks (all the b sounds) + 4 shots (verses) = 24 calibers of 357 ammo.\nThe 5 other genres on that album, people thought she sold out with (Pop, R&B, Dance, Reggae/Dancehall and Electro). Coincidentally, all her parts were done using Hardcore Rap. This choice of rapping, perfectly fits the theme of the album and title track. She backfired shots at all her naysayers, the old-fashioned way.\nThere is a multitude of “Pop/Shot” puns in her verses and countless references to gun activity: (The Columbine Massacre, glock, bang, popping off, etc.). People claimed she was gonna “jam the barrel” with her new direction on her 2nd studio album. RR’s 1st half has 9 total Rap/R&B tracks, more than enough for the Hip-Hop Head (mostly males). The 2nd half is for her female fanbase.\nShe also paraphrased E-40’s classic hook in his song. For circumstantial proof, they did perform at Wild Jam together In May, after the album was released in Apr. in 2012. It’s located in San Francisco which is his hometown in the Bay Area, “Hyphy Scene”", "annotation_id": "3165690", "url": "https://genius.com/3165690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Word, middle finger on the trigger", "vault_lines": ["Word, middle finger on the trigger"], "meaning": "A reference to Lil Wayne’s “Sky is the Limit” off Da Drought 3 where he says:\n\n“Most likely I'mma die with my finger on the trigger”\n\nThe middle finger just adds to the defiance and irreverence.", "annotation_id": "2858187", "url": "https://genius.com/2858187", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "I say, shout out Mack Maine,", "vault_lines": ["I say, shout out Mack Maine,"], "meaning": "Mack Maine is one of the closest Wayne friends from the label Young Money. Tune took his time just to salute him.", "annotation_id": "2858170", "url": "https://genius.com/2858170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "I hear the slick shit, bitch, you washed", "vault_lines": ["I hear the slick shit, bitch, you washed"], "meaning": "Nicki hears the trash talk other people have given her. She fires back by simply reminding them the state of their careers.\n\nAlso a reference to the outro in her song Womp Womp (track 19 on her Sucka Free Mixtape):\n\nThese bitches so washed up\nI’m walking around with them drier sheets\nLike you know the sheets you put in the drier\nYeah Im walking around with them sheets now\nCause like when I see these washed up ass bitches\nI’m just throwing them on bitches like\nBitch hit the drier, you washed!", "annotation_id": "2417878", "url": "https://genius.com/2417878", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Give that shit to a wash-up, bitch, I’m winnin’", "vault_lines": ["Give that shit to a wash-up, bitch, I’m winnin’"], "meaning": "#You’re WASHED UP, BITCH!\n\n\n\nIf you’re not giving Nicki enough money than she’s not taking the deal. The middleman would be better off, giving it to a chick (such as Kim or really any other rap bitch rn who became irrelevant) who is worth that little bit of money.\n\nShe usually says this, in conjunction with one her words/phrases from the “Nicktionary” (which is hilarity at its finest) such as “Tumble dry”\n\n\n\nV., Tumble Dry, : \\təm-bəl-drī\\ – Used when speaking to any WASHED UP bitches. Ex. “Tumble Dry bitch! Tumble Dry!”", "annotation_id": "2417873", "url": "https://genius.com/2417873", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "You at the bottom of the barrel, scrapin’", "vault_lines": ["You at the bottom of the barrel, scrapin’"], "meaning": "The meaning of being at “the bottom of the barrel” means to be of the lowest of all the social classes, extremely poor: trying to make money anyway a person knows how.\n\nThis line may also be a reference to the children’s game, Monkeys in a Barrel to how Nicki has been referring to her nemesis as Bubbles.", "annotation_id": "606888", "url": "https://genius.com/606888", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Ugh, I couldn’t do your TV show, I needed ten more mil’", "vault_lines": ["Ugh, I couldn’t do your TV show, I needed ten more mil'"], "meaning": "It was rumored that Simon Cowell wanted to recruit Nicki as a judge on the upcoming season of Xfactor.\n\nNicki is taking shots at Bravo’s “Watch What Happens Live”, where Lil' Kim appeared and referred to Nicki as a “Stupid Hoe”. She’s saying that Bravo couldn’t pay her enough to appear on the show and that it’s more appropriate for a washed up rapper ergo, Lil' Kim.", "annotation_id": "605310", "url": "https://genius.com/605310", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Hottest MCs, top five", "vault_lines": ["Hottest MCs, top five"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj was named #5 Hottest MC in the game on MTV, later being switched with Lil Wayne and nabbing the #4 spot.", "annotation_id": "605308", "url": "https://genius.com/605308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "All you hoes cryin’—Christopher Bosh", "vault_lines": ["All you hoes cryin’—Christopher Bosh"], "meaning": "Referring to Chris Bosh, who cried after losing the NBA Finals\n\n\n\n\nHe also cried at a Press Conference on March 3rd after a mide-season loss to Orlando.\nShe’s talking about Christopher Bosh crying after Lil Wayne had sex with his wife.", "annotation_id": "605299", "url": "https://genius.com/605299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Bang, my shit bang, it bang-bang B-B-B-Bang, my shit bang, it bang-bang", "vault_lines": ["Bang, my shit bang, it bang-bang"], "meaning": "A reference to “My Shit Bang” by E-40:\n\nTurn my music up, turn my music up\nMy shit bang, my shit bang\nMy shit bang, my-my shit bang\nNigga my shit bang, bang, bang, bang", "annotation_id": "605291", "url": "https://genius.com/605291", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "You in the booth, but I’m who you be channelin’", "vault_lines": ["You in the booth, but I'm who you be channelin’"], "meaning": "One can assume that Nicki is talking about Lil Kim. Lil Kim recently put out the mixtape Black Friday, featuring many disses to Nicki Minaj.\n\nNicki is saying that she is the influence for why Lil Kim is in the booth.\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to the catholic church. you go to confession in a booth and say your sins to the priest. Through him you reach God. Nicki is God who “normal people” channel through prayer.", "annotation_id": "605208", "url": "https://genius.com/605208", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "You mad ’cause I’m at the Grammys with the Vatican", "vault_lines": ["You mad ’cause I’m at the Grammys with the Vatican"], "meaning": "Many people were upset when Nicki performed “Roman Holiday” at the Grammy Awards using a church-like setting and acting possessed using her alter-ego Roman Zolanski. It was a performance that not many have seen from the “Super Bass” rapper so because of it they criticized her (were angry). She is mocking the people who thought negatively about her performance. .", "annotation_id": "605207", "url": "https://genius.com/605207", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "I’m out in LA at the Ice Age tapin’", "vault_lines": ["I’m out in LA at the Ice Age tapin’"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj was featured in the animated movie Ice Age: Continental Drift as Steffie, a woolly mammoth.", "annotation_id": "605205", "url": "https://genius.com/605205", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Yo, I guess I went commercial, just shot a commercial When I flew to the set, though, I ain’t fly commercial", "vault_lines": ["Yo, I guess I went commercial, just shot a commercial"], "meaning": "People say that Nicki’s new music is more poppy than her previous work, or in other words, commercial.\n\nNicki shrugs off this notion by taunting them and saying she shot a commercial (for Pepsi in Argentina) and flew without a commercial airline, meaning she flew in a private jet.", "annotation_id": "605197", "url": "https://genius.com/605197", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Take bitches to school, then I Columbine these hoes", "vault_lines": ["Take bitches to school, then I Columbine these hoes"], "meaning": "Columbine is a reference to the infamous Columbine High School Massacre. Causing the deaths of one teacher and twelve students. Nicki is playing off of the common phrase of “schoolin' someone” and is basically saying she is killing these bitches.", "annotation_id": "605190", "url": "https://genius.com/605190", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "line": "Yes, I really do mean that it’s Barbie, bitch Ask Mattel, they auctioned my Barbie, bitch", "vault_lines": ["Yes, I really do mean that it’s Barbie, bitch"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj allowed Mattel to use her likeness from the Pink Friday album cover to make a one-of-a-kind Barbie doll of herself—the Harajuku Barbie finally became a real Barbie.\n\nThe doll was auctioned off for charity, believed to have been bought for somewhere around $15,000.", "annotation_id": "605126", "url": "https://genius.com/605126", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Roman Reloaded", "status": "done", "targets": 24, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Nicki-minaj-roman-reloaded-lyrics", "genius_title": "Roman Reloaded", "genius_id": 66564, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "Bitches, hoes, and women, I don’t know the difference", "vault_lines": ["Bitches, hoes, and women, I don’t know the difference"], "meaning": "By claiming this ignorance, Wayne turns a hyper-explicit brag into a confession of complete emotional detachment: fame has made everyone equally transactional to him.", "annotation_id": "40729831", "url": "https://genius.com/40729831", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "Eyes chink like Chinese niggas", "vault_lines": ["Eyes chink like Chinese niggas"], "meaning": "Weezy is a heavy marijuana smoker, and smokers' eyes tend to squint when they are high on weed. People from China, along with other Asian countries, typically have eyelids that display much less of the eyeball. Because Wayne is squinting due to smoking, he is also showing less eyeball, so he compares his high eyes to that of a Chinese person.", "annotation_id": "11616980", "url": "https://genius.com/11616980", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "Bring your best friend, you don’t need nobody else", "vault_lines": ["Bring your best friend, you don't need nobody else"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is seeking a threesome, informing his girl to bring one of her friends to join in on the sexual fun. Instead of seeking sexual partners for himself, he makes it clear that he prefers to let his current sexual partners choose for him.\n\nMy new bitch gon' pull me a new bitch\nThen pull me a new bitch\nSee that is a snowball effect", "annotation_id": "11616941", "url": "https://genius.com/11616941", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "I just got a text message from wifey, nigga I scroll down, the next message from Nike, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I just got a text message from wifey, nigga"], "meaning": "I thought this line was too plain. People like Mack Maine and Hood, they tell me, “you think it’s plain, but it’s actually nothing nobody would say.”\n\nSo I left it.", "annotation_id": "8975904", "url": "https://genius.com/8975904", "state": "verified", "votes": 127, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "First lick I made, I bought five pairs of Jordans", "vault_lines": ["First lick I made, I bought five pairs of Jordans"], "meaning": "I bought the Olympic ones. The ones with the number 9 on the back. The 7’s. Had the blue and gray on the back. I bought two pair of those.\n\nI bought the Bugs Bunny 8s, white with the gray joints. I had bought damn near two of each pair.\n\nI had too many shoes. I was buying two pair of J’s for no reason! Still got a pair! Still got the motherfuckers with the 9 on them!\n\nBut at this time, I had a lot of dope money and it was a lot of trash, meaning no hundreds. 5’s, 10’s, 20’s, a lot of trash, so you couldn’t wait ‘till the lady say “800” and you pull out some 5’s and 10’s. You go to licking the cash!", "annotation_id": "8975436", "url": "https://genius.com/8975436", "state": "verified", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "I just got a text message from wifey, nigga I scroll down, the next message from Nike, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I just got a text message from wifey, nigga"], "meaning": "Whoa! He could’ve stopped right there! I hit him like “what the fuck, man?” And then he was going to change the line.\n\nGuess what I told him? I’ll use that motherfucker.\n\nYou can see that line. It’s dope when you can see the raps. I think that’s important.", "annotation_id": "8975366", "url": "https://genius.com/8975366", "state": "verified", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "Mama only child we stayed in a one bedroom (tru) Used to ride MARTA ‘cause it had more leg room", "vault_lines": ["Mama only child we stayed in a one bedroom (tru)"], "meaning": "I had a girl over to the apartment. I’m kicking shit. I’m finna hit her. I’m finna try her on the sofa. She going to tell me, “Yo mama in the other room.”\n\nBecause, it’s just a living room, and a bedroom. Her door closed, but you can hear the TV.\n\nBut my mama cool. Is just me and my mama. I ain’t got no brothers and sisters. My mama know I’m hitting. My mama know I’m selling dope. My mama know I’m cooking. I get locked up in high school twice, my mama already know what’s up with this campaign.\n\nSo I’m finna hit her and she say “Noooo. I don’t feel comfortable. Yo mama in there.”", "annotation_id": "8975340", "url": "https://genius.com/8975340", "state": "verified", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "Pockets deep and I’mma get in depth like like Johnny nigga", "vault_lines": ["Pockets deep and I’mma get in depth like like Johnny nigga"], "meaning": "Tunechi isn’t only known for his big bank account (his net worth is at $150 million), but also for his clever and intricate lines.\n\nHe creates a wordplay on depth/Depp, which is the second name of actor Johnny (Depp), who’s net worth is at $400 million.", "annotation_id": "8762118", "url": "https://genius.com/8762118", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "Bitches know my name and I don’t have to wear a necklace (2 Chainz)", "vault_lines": ["Bitches know my name and I don’t have to wear a necklace (2 Chainz)"], "meaning": "Born Tauheed Epps, 2 Chainz is better known by his stage name which he changed from Tity boy in early 2011. He’s known for yelling “2 CHAINZ” to introduce himself on verses. “If y'all don’t see [him] with jewelry on [he’s] still 2 Chainz” — 2 Chainz on Fuse’s Hip Hop Shop Dec. 2011.", "annotation_id": "8683487", "url": "https://genius.com/8683487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "I’m a ghetto boy, I came up on Brad Jordan", "vault_lines": ["I'm a ghetto boy, I came up on Brad Jordan"], "meaning": "Brad Terrence Jordan is the real name of Geto Boys member and southern rap legend Scarface.\n\nTity Boi might express his love for him as well as state his origin, by using the term “ghetto boy”.\n\nBoth collaborated already on his solo debut album Based on a T.R.U. Story on the record “Ghetto Dreams” together with John Legend.", "annotation_id": "8682464", "url": "https://genius.com/8682464", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "I keep that Maggie on me, I think I’m Homer Simpson", "vault_lines": ["I keep that Maggie on me, I think I'm Homer Simpson"], "meaning": "Maggie is the youngest daughter on “The Simpsons”. Wayne uses this play, by meaning he keeps the Mag (Gun) on him at ALL times.", "annotation_id": "8682113", "url": "https://genius.com/8682113", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "Money over bitches, should be a Bible scripture", "vault_lines": ["Money over bitches, should be a Bible scripture"], "meaning": "M.O.B! Something Weezy will always stand by, he will take money over any woman, any day..\n\nHe even has it tattooed on his chest!\n\n\n\nMoney over bitches, I’m yelling it to the grave", "annotation_id": "8681997", "url": "https://genius.com/8681997", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "line": "I’m just doing it too big on these tiny niggas I been lost my fuckin’ mind, I never mind these niggas", "vault_lines": ["I’m just doing it too big on these tiny niggas"], "meaning": "We all know by now that Wayne is crazy, no artist in the rap game scares him.\n\nHe obviously isn’t talking about height when he calls other rappers tiny because he himself is only 5'5, but he is one of the biggest and most successful artists of all time, whether you are a new or an old artist, you ain’t got nothing on him.\n\nHe has surpassed Elvis Presley with most Billboard Hot 100 entries, maintains a wide lead for the most entries among all artists as a lead solo act. He is also 1 of the only 3 rappers to go platinum in 1 week. His legacy is cemented and he got no worries!", "annotation_id": "8681879", "url": "https://genius.com/8681879", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/2-chainz-rolls-royce-weather-every-day-lyrics", "genius_title": "Rolls Royce Weather Every Day", "genius_id": 2423713, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rollers & Riders", "line": "When I was 14 I told my ma we will see better days And sure enough I got Ms. Cita in a better place", "vault_lines": ["When I was 14 I told my ma we will see better days"], "meaning": "The same line as the one below from Tha Carter 3’s “Three Peat” from 2008, which itself is very similar to (and perhaps a re-working of) the (reportedly) original album-opener “I’m Me”, which leaked in 2007 and was put out officially on The Leak EP:\n\nYeah, when I was 14, I told my mom we will see better days\nAnd sure enough, I got Miss Cita in a better place", "annotation_id": "16761466", "url": "https://genius.com/16761466", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
