{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "Got no time to seduce a Superhead type of seducer", "vault_lines": ["Got no time to seduce a Superhead type of seducer"], "meaning": "“Superhead” is the nickname of Karrine Steffans who was know for seducing rappers and sleeping with them to become famous.\n\n\n\nFunny enough, Lil Wayne, who is featured on this song, has been seen with Karrine multiple times.", "annotation_id": "19144914", "url": "https://genius.com/19144914", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "Chamillitary, man! Young Money We the new Red Hot Chili Peppers", "vault_lines": ["Chamillitary, man! Young Money"], "meaning": "This line is a shout out to Chamillionaire himself and Lil Wayne.\nChamillitairy Mayne is one of Chamillionaires nicknames. Chamillitairy is also the name of his record label.\n\n\n\nYoung Money is referring to Lil Waynes record label named Young Money Entertainment.\n\n\n\nThe Red Hot Chilli Peppers are one of the best selling rock bands worldwide. Chamillionaire and Lil Wayne are comparing themselves to RHCP because Cham, Wayne and the members of RHCP are rock stars.", "annotation_id": "3396342", "url": "https://genius.com/3396342", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "Groupies trying to snake me, but Koopa denying Medusas (Ha-ha!)", "vault_lines": ["Groupies trying to snake me, but Koopa denying Medusas (Ha-ha!)"], "meaning": "The groupies are snaking Chamillionaire up. But that is not Chamillionaires style so he denies them.\nMedusa is generally described as a monster that has the face of a hideous human female with living venomous snakes in place of hair. Gazing directly into her eyes would turn you to stone.", "annotation_id": "3396331", "url": "https://genius.com/3396331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "You try sniffin’ ’round me, then I’ma clean your nose", "vault_lines": ["You try sniffin' 'round me, then I'ma clean your nose"], "meaning": "If you don’t act like yourself around Lil Wayne he will tell you to act like yourself and not like a little kid who needs its nose cleaned.", "annotation_id": "3396324", "url": "https://genius.com/3396324", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "She’s saying she’s in love with me, and she is probably your lady", "vault_lines": ["She's saying she's in love with me, and she is probably your lady"], "meaning": "In other words she is a groupie.", "annotation_id": "3396319", "url": "https://genius.com/3396319", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "See how we rippin’ up tickets that police be writin’ us Do like Michael Jackson’s complexion, mister, and lighten up (Ha-ha!)", "vault_lines": ["See how we rippin' up tickets that police be writin' us"], "meaning": "As a rock star you don’t care about police tickets so you can just rip those up.\nSo don’t be so tight about the little things and lighten up!\n\nAlso, Michael Jacksons skin did lighten up. It began to bleach after a while.", "annotation_id": "3396314", "url": "https://genius.com/3396314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "How I’m a rapper with revenue like a rockstar? If I’m near, you can believe the black card is not far", "vault_lines": ["How I'm a rapper with revenue like a rockstar?"], "meaning": "Cham makes so much money of rapping that he earns as much as rock stars do.\nAnd with earning a lot of money comes a special black credit card.", "annotation_id": "3396312", "url": "https://genius.com/3396312", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "Take it off and you lost, the tough talk get tuned off Keep the four-iron near, keep on thinking that it’s for golf (What)", "vault_lines": ["Take it off and you lost, the tough talk get tuned off"], "meaning": "Haters that call Chamillionaire out for a fight are more talk than action. So when Cham takes of his jewels and gets his golf club they are quiet all of a sudden.", "annotation_id": "3396302", "url": "https://genius.com/3396302", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "Teen spirit ain’t what they smelling; they yelling, “Where that Nirvana?”", "vault_lines": ["Teen spirit ain't what they smelling; they yelling, \"Where that Nirvana?\""], "meaning": "Chamillionaire is making a marijuana reference by referring to the song by Nirvana “Smells Like Teen Spirit”\n\nHowever what the people are smelling in this case is some grade-A reefer. Marijuana is given many ‘Enlightening’ names:\n\nBuddha, Satori, Nirvana, etc…", "annotation_id": "3272384", "url": "https://genius.com/3272384", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "Famous look right at me and said, “Know why I got my lighter up?” (Why?) Just like the throwback P. Diddy alias (I’ma puff)", "vault_lines": ["Famous look right at me and said, “Know why I got my lighter up?\" (Why?)"], "meaning": "Chamillionaire is saying that hes going to “Puff” on some herb, like the throwback (old) P. Diddy. Back in the day, P. Diddy changed his name multiple times from “P. Diddy Puff Daddy” to just\n“P. Diddy” and eventually “Diddy”. Diddy’s oldest name had the word puff in it which is Chamillionaire’s intended reference.\n\nPuff can also mean to get bigger, and Diddy did get ridiculously rich…", "annotation_id": "2018071", "url": "https://genius.com/2018071", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "They judging me like your honor", "vault_lines": ["They judging me like your honor"], "meaning": "A Judge is usually called “Your Honor' out of respect because that is the official title of their occupation.\n\nExample: “Your Honorable Judge Joe Brown”", "annotation_id": "2018064", "url": "https://genius.com/2018064", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "I’m a Hot Boy (Hey), I’m on my hot shit (Rock, rock)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a Hot Boy (Hey), I'm on my hot shit (Rock, rock)"], "meaning": "The Hot Boys (Often styled Hot Boy$) was the group of rappers that included Lil' Wayne as well as Juvenile, B.G. and Turk. They released 3 albums and had 5 singles together before splitting up. Lil' Wayne is saying he’s a hot boy until he dies and still reps it and ends the line being conceited as usual.", "annotation_id": "2018046", "url": "https://genius.com/2018046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "Reporting to you live from the moshpit", "vault_lines": ["Reporting to you live from the moshpit"], "meaning": "Moshing, in a strict sense, is a style of dance whose participants push or slam into each other. It is most associated with “aggressive” music genres, such as hardcore punk, rock and heavy metal. It is primarily done to live music, although it can be done to recorded music.\n\nClearly, Lil' Wayne is smack in the middle of one, after being thrown across the audience via Stagedive.", "annotation_id": "1268652", "url": "https://genius.com/1268652", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "On the red carpet so much, they mistake me for Aladdin (Wow)", "vault_lines": ["On the red carpet so much, they mistake me for Aladdin (Wow)"], "meaning": "Although Aladdin’s carpet wasn’t known for being red… Aladdin is the only person that comes to mind who rides a carpet.", "annotation_id": "1112375", "url": "https://genius.com/1112375", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "Rock on! They see the jewels is so sick, like flu spit and flu cough", "vault_lines": ["Rock on! They see the jewels is so sick, like flu spit and flu cough"], "meaning": "He’s got his “rocks on” meaning that he is wearing a lot of jewelry, and it’s Sick… I wish it was contagious.\n\nMany rappers like Gucci Mane and Migos have  used the same type of wordplay:\n\nhttp://rapgenius.com/3128827", "annotation_id": "1103452", "url": "https://genius.com/1103452", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rock Star", "line": "We gonna keep on rocking and rolling until the wheels fall off, know what I’m talking about?", "vault_lines": ["We gonna keep on rocking and rolling until the wheels fall off, know what I'm talking about?"], "meaning": "Get it? He’s calling the Rock & Roll game as if it were a car, rocking and rolling it until it’s tires pop right off, which is a very improper way to change a tire.", "annotation_id": "1103427", "url": "https://genius.com/1103427", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
