{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "But the tourists come down and spend too many dollars And no matter how you change it, it’ll still be ours", "vault_lines": ["But the tourists come down and spend too many dollars"], "meaning": "After Katrina, the economy reemerged with tourists and developers. Weezy is saying no matter how the city changes, it’ll still belong to the native New Orleaners.", "annotation_id": "26116050", "url": "https://genius.com/26116050", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "Relying on rap, but in the kitchen, I’m a chemist", "vault_lines": ["Relying on rap, but in the kitchen, I'm a chemist"], "meaning": "Weezy’s kitchen chemistry consists of mixing various elements to manufacture drugs to sell.", "annotation_id": "26116040", "url": "https://genius.com/26116040", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "My eyes get so wide as it rise in the skillet I let my bitch bag it, if she stealin’, I’ma kill her", "vault_lines": ["My eyes get so wide as it rise in the skillet"], "meaning": "Wayne is referencing the art of turning cocaine into crack by cooking it. Cocaine, heat, baking soda and water are each needed. If each componernt is present and in their correct ratio then sufficient heat should be supplied long enough for the soda to remove the HCL Hydrochloride acid from the cocaine using a base (soda). Cooking crack is an acid-base reaction. His girl puts it into bags to be ready for distribution; if she steals the crack she will die", "annotation_id": "23481195", "url": "https://genius.com/23481195", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "And you ain’t got to know the alphabets to see", "vault_lines": ["And you ain't got to know the alphabets to see"], "meaning": "Homophone.\n\n“See” sounds like the third alphabet “C”", "annotation_id": "23152075", "url": "https://genius.com/23152075", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "I bulletproofed the ride, now I feel like armadillos", "vault_lines": ["I bulletproofed the ride, now I feel like armadillos"], "meaning": "Armadillos have a tough exterior shell, much like an automobile that’s been bulletproofed.", "annotation_id": "15235580", "url": "https://genius.com/15235580", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "And when I was five, my favorite movie was The Gremlins Ain’t got shit to do with this, but I just thought that I should mention", "vault_lines": ["And when I was five, my favorite movie was The Gremlins"], "meaning": "The 1984 movie Gremlins premiered when Wayne was two years old. Maybe it’s because he sees a little bit of himself in those wily creatures?", "annotation_id": "11858349", "url": "https://genius.com/11858349", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "Self-made G", "vault_lines": ["I bulletproofed the ride, now I feel like armadillos"], "meaning": "A “G” is a slang term for a gangster, so because Wayne crafted himself into what he is by his own power, He is a Self-made Gangster.", "annotation_id": "11496819", "url": "https://genius.com/11496819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "You know I ride for my motherfucking niggas Most likely, I’ma die with my finger on the trigger", "vault_lines": ["And you know that I'ma ride with my motherfucking niggas"], "meaning": "As the saying goes: Live by the sword, die by the sword.  Therefore, Wayne figures he’ll die in a shootout.\n\nThis couplet was later interpolated on YG’s “My Nigga.”", "annotation_id": "8275958", "url": "https://genius.com/8275958", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "They tell me, “Don’t get high” and I should try to make a living I tell ’em I’m a hustler and I’d rather make a killing", "vault_lines": ["Tell a bitch, \"Don't talk to me"], "meaning": "Media and adversaries criticize him for using drugs or making references about them in his songs, and often say that he should look for a more “proper” career instead of rapping.\n\nWayne responds by saying that he is a hustler and he’d rather keep doing what he does and die, than to “make a living” by being a regular person in a nine-to-five (regular job).", "annotation_id": "2332835", "url": "https://genius.com/2332835", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "The only thing on a mind of a shark is ”Eat By any means,” and you just sardines", "vault_lines": ["The only thing on a mind of a shark is \"Eat"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is always using water as a metaphor for the ghetto. This is very appropriate since after Katrina, his childhood neighborhood was effectively in the ocean for a while\n\nHe is devouring his competition as a shark would do a sardine", "annotation_id": "7126", "url": "https://genius.com/7126", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "Switching lanes faster than she switch subjects", "vault_lines": ["Switching lanes faster than she switch subjects"], "meaning": "Fun simile sets up the following line’s insult by introducing the girl as chatty and perhaps scatterbrained\n\nAnother reading of “subjects” is “male suitors.” In other words, Li'l Wayne informs his target that the lady in question engages in sexual activity not only with him, but also with Li'l Wayne and a slew of other men (subjects).", "annotation_id": "5924", "url": "https://genius.com/5924", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "They tried to make a brand-new map without us", "vault_lines": ["They tried to make a brand-new map without us"], "meaning": "After the great storm coming the US map will not look the same. Check out the NAFTA superhighway map. New Orleans tore down most of the housing projects after Katrina and began ‘mixed-income’ projects.", "annotation_id": "1717", "url": "https://genius.com/1717", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "Tucked in my P-R-Ps", "vault_lines": ["I got the forty-cal' tucked in my P-R-Ps"], "meaning": "P.R.P.s are a luxury denim brand", "annotation_id": "1716", "url": "https://genius.com/1716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "See, my world is different like Dwayne Wayne", "vault_lines": ["See, my world is different like Dwayne Wayne"], "meaning": "A reference to the early Nineties sitcom A Different World, whose main character is a college student named Dwayne Wayne\n\nWayne’s given name is Dwayne but he dropped the D because his father, Dwayne Sr., left him and Wayne didn’t want to carry his name", "annotation_id": "1712", "url": "https://genius.com/1712", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "I’m probably in the sky, flying with the fishes Or maybe in the ocean, swimming with the pigeons", "vault_lines": ["I'm probably in the sky, flying with the fishes"], "meaning": "Wayne does things differently, he flys and swims with things that ordinarily do not. He is an alien\n\nMight be a stretch but this line could be a subtle reference to M.C. Escher’s famous Sky and Water I. Even if he doesn’t know who Escher is, lots of people have seen this – definitely fits the image of flying fish and swimming birds.\n\n\n\nIn addition to the previous line, “and them birds don’t fly without my permission”, speaking about commanding the sale of cocaine, Wayne may also be suggesting that he is using airplanes to “fly” and transport Fishscale cocaine and boats to “swim” the pigeons, also slang for a kilo of cocaine.", "annotation_id": "1709", "url": "https://genius.com/1709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "And them birds don’t fly without my permission", "vault_lines": ["And them birds don't fly without my permission"], "meaning": "A “bird” is a kilo of cocaine. Coke doesn’t get sold unless Weezy allows it\n\nAlso an expression of frustration with man’s lack of control over nature, similar to the sentiment expressed in Blood Meridian: “The existence of birds offends me”\n\nThe former reading is more in line with the previous lines, but the latter reading makes sense as a transition to the next lines about Wayne’s place in nature", "annotation_id": "1707", "url": "https://genius.com/1707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ride 4 My Niggas (Sky is the Limit)", "line": "My flow is nasty, like C-Y-philis", "vault_lines": ["My flow is nasty, like C-Y-philis"], "meaning": "I think he’s trying to spell out syphilis here and doing incorrectly (S Y Phyllis wouldn’t have the same ring to it)\n\nC also equals see, so it’s literally translated as:\n\nMy flow is nasty like. See why? Feel this.", "annotation_id": "1704", "url": "https://genius.com/1704", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
