{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "All rats gotta die, even Master Splinter", "vault_lines": ["All rats gotta die, even Master Splinter"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying because of principle all snitches or rats have to die no matter how deep the relationship was because snitching is unforgivable.\n\nMaster splinter was the father figure of the teenage mutant ninja turtles and was a giant mutated rat.", "annotation_id": "27222443", "url": "https://genius.com/27222443", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Nigga, you get beat the crap out, but that’s just how the dice roll", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, you get beat the crap out, but that's just how the dice roll"], "meaning": "Craps is a dice game in which players bet on the outcomes of a pair of dice.\n\nThis line is a play on the word ‘crap’ which is a reference to the game craps, and the phrase ‘that’s how the dice rolls’.", "annotation_id": "25093575", "url": "https://genius.com/25093575", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "I turned a penny to a motherfuckin Janet Jackson", "vault_lines": ["I turned a penny to a motherfuckin Janet Jackson"], "meaning": "Janet Jackson played the character Penny Gordon Woods in the show “Good Times.”\nWith this bar, Wayne is saying that he can turn a low-value object like a penny into something grand and expensive, like the famous singer Janet Jackson.", "annotation_id": "23705558", "url": "https://genius.com/23705558", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
