{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "And I see your girl when I want I got that ho TiVo’d, ugh", "vault_lines": ["And I see your girl when I want"], "meaning": "Television In, Video Out Computing or TiVo  is a digital video recorder (DVR) developed and marketed by Xperi (previously by TiVo Corporation and TiVo Inc.) and introduced in 1999. TiVo provides an on-screen guide of scheduled broadcast programming television programs, whose features include “Season Pass” schedules which record every new episode of a series, and “WishList” searches which allow the user to find and record shows that match their interests by title, actor, director, category, or keyword.\n\n\n\nWayne says here that he can your girl when he wants, just like TiVo programming as he uses the DVR as a metaphor next.", "annotation_id": "20365830", "url": "https://genius.com/20365830", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "I be killing them bitches, I hope all dogs go to heaven", "vault_lines": ["I be killing them bitches, I hope all dogs go to heaven"], "meaning": "At least he wishes the best for women he’s bragging about killing.\n\nBitch is also a term for a female dog.\n\nAll Dogs Go to Heaven is a 1989 animated movie.", "annotation_id": "20288518", "url": "https://genius.com/20288518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Yeah, murder, one-eighty-seven", "vault_lines": ["Ugh, AK on my nightstand, right next to that Bible"], "meaning": "The term “187” is slang for murder. It refers to section 187 of the California Penal Code.", "annotation_id": "20288499", "url": "https://genius.com/20288499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "And I’m spraying at these rusty niggas like WD-40", "vault_lines": ["And I'm spraying at these rusty niggas like WD-40"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne creates a simile that compares the spray fire of his guns and WD-40, a water displacement spray bottle, which serves as a lubricant and rust remover.", "annotation_id": "18810153", "url": "https://genius.com/18810153", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Pockets gettin’ too fat, no Weight Watchers, no lipo", "vault_lines": ["Pockets gettin' too fat, no Weight Watchers, no lipo"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Lil Wayne references his “fat” stacks of cash which he stores in his pockets. To further the analogy between the size of his cash stacks and the word “fat”, Wayne references Weight Watchers and Liposuction. Both of these references are ways of dealing with being overweight, one being an exercise program and the other being an actual surgical process.", "annotation_id": "18810113", "url": "https://genius.com/18810113", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Tell the bitches that be hatin’ I ain’t got no worries", "vault_lines": ["Tell the bitches that be hatin' I ain't got no worries"], "meaning": "This lyric likely references another song on I Am Not A Human Being II, “No Worries”.", "annotation_id": "18810082", "url": "https://genius.com/18810082", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "And I make that pussy tap out", "vault_lines": ["And I make that pussy tap out"], "meaning": "This is a likely reference to the Rich Gang song “Tapout,” on which Wayne is featured, along with Future, Nicki Minaj, Mack Maine, Detail, and Birdman", "annotation_id": "18227640", "url": "https://genius.com/18227640", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Light that shit, then pass that shit", "vault_lines": ["Light that shit, then pass that shit"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is a heavy marijuana smoker, as he has mentioned tirelessly throughout his career. He wants whoever is lighting the weed to pass it his way.\n\nPass me the dutchy with ya left hand", "annotation_id": "11647034", "url": "https://genius.com/11647034", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Got a red-ass bitch with a red-ass pussy", "vault_lines": ["Got a red-ass bitch with a red-ass pussy"], "meaning": "“Red,” short for redbone is a term used in the African American culture dating back to 60’s. This termed is used often in today’s culture to reference a light-skinned woman that is in shape and has a nice figure.", "annotation_id": "1783379", "url": "https://genius.com/1783379", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Look at you (Aw), now look at us All my niggas look rich as fuck (Yeah) All my niggas live rich as fuck (Yeah) All—All my niggas look rich as fuck (Yeah) Look at you (Look at you), now look at us (Now look at us) All my niggas look rich as fuck (Bitch) All my—All my niggas live rich as fuck (You hoe-ass bi—) All my—All—All my ni—", "vault_lines": ["Look at you (Aw), now look at us"], "meaning": "A very simple chorus. 2 Chainz instructs you to look at yourself and then compare yourself to him and his crew.\n\nLil Wayne is estimated to be worth $110  Million\n2 Chainz is estimated to be worth $2 Million\n\nOnce you add in the networths of people in their crews—YMCMB and GOOD Music—you’d end up with a whole lot of money!\n\nWhat’s the difference between you and them? They’re just richer.", "annotation_id": "1775125", "url": "https://genius.com/1775125", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Bitch niggas go behind your back like nunchucks, and that’s fucked up", "vault_lines": ["Bitch niggas go behind your back like nunchucks, and that's fucked up"], "meaning": "If one is to “go behind your back”, well then that person is saying negative things about you while you aren’t there to defend yourself. Usually when someone does this, they are completely nice to you while you share one-another’s company. When one does this, they are considered two-faced.\nNun-chucks (also know as Nunchaku) are a weapon that consist of two sticks and are connected by a rope or chain.\n\n\n\n\n\nIn this line Wayne could either be referring to:\n\n\nSomeone specific who has friends who speak negatively about them when they aren’t around\nOr people who go behind someone’s back are considered “bitch niggas”.\n\n\n\n#Regardless\nWayne made a clever comparison of people placing nun-chucks behind their back\n\n\n\nTo people who talk behind one-another’s back to show that people run their mouths.", "annotation_id": "1584069", "url": "https://genius.com/1584069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "But I swear, with these fifty shots, I’ll shoot it out with Five-O", "vault_lines": ["But I swear, with these fifty shots, I'll shoot it out with Five-O"], "meaning": "“5-0” refers to police officers.\n\n\n\nWayne is willing to have a shoot-out with police officers.\n\nWeezy has expressed his disapproval for police officers before, more recently with the line\n\nNumbers don’t lie\nExcept 5-0\n\nOn his song titled “Get Smoked” off of his Dedication 4 mixtape\n\n\n\nThis is also a double entendre, Weezy F. will not only shoot it out with 5-0 as in police officers, but he will literally shoot it because 50 Shots Set’s it Off. “I’ll shoot it out with 5-0” also means he has 50 shots to shoot.", "annotation_id": "1579283", "url": "https://genius.com/1579283", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Ugh, AK on my nightstand, right next to that Bible", "vault_lines": ["Ugh, AK on my nightstand, right next to that Bible"], "meaning": "He has is AK47 by his bedside to symbolize the street life that he used to live, and the Bible to represent his faith in God. This also references his verse from Tyga’s “I’m On It”\n\nStill go to sleep with my Bible on my nightstand\n\nThe addition of the AK47 to that night stand provides a visualization of Wayne’s internal conflict between his spiritual self and more violent lifestyle.\n\nHe shows a similar sentiment via another bible juxtaposition in “No Love” when he says\n\nThat’s why my bars are full of broken bottles\nAnd my night stands are full of open Bibles", "annotation_id": "1579268", "url": "https://genius.com/1579268", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Call me Mr. Sandman, I’m sellin’ all these hoes dreams", "vault_lines": ["Call me Mr. Sandman, I'm sellin' all these hoes dreams"], "meaning": "A nod here to the 1954 song by the Chordettes called “Mr. Sandman,\" the opening words of which are,\n\n“Mr. Sandman, bring me a dream”\n\nThe legend of the sandman is that he sprinkles sleeping dust on children to help them fall asleep, and thus letting them have dream. Wayne is sharing his (crushed up) xanax, percs, and purple drank with his hoes. His hoes then have crazy-ass trips. Just like the Sandman does with his sand, Wayne is having these hoes trip on his “sand” that he supplies.", "annotation_id": "1375322", "url": "https://genius.com/1375322", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "I’m killing these hoes like Michael Myers", "vault_lines": ["I'm killing these hoes like Michael Myers"], "meaning": "Michael Myers = fictional character from the Halloween series of slasher films.\n\n\n\nMichael Myers, in the Halloween films, is famous for killing hoes while they’re banging some dude, or after they’ve banged some dude, and they tend to be naked when he does so.", "annotation_id": "1374727", "url": "https://genius.com/1374727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "And I got Xanax, Percocet, promethazine with codeine", "vault_lines": ["And I got Xanax, Percocet, promethazine with codeine"], "meaning": "Xanax is an antianxiety drug that is frequently abused, and percocet is a painkiller. The two actually interact, so mixing these drugs is a very bad idea.\n\n…And if you’re topping that off with promethazine-codeine cough syrup (otherwise known as lean), you’re just begging to end up like DJ Screw (R.I.P.)", "annotation_id": "1374650", "url": "https://genius.com/1374650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "What’s your name? What’s your sign? Zodiac Killer", "vault_lines": ["What's your name? What's your sign? Zodiac Killer"], "meaning": "The Zodiac Killer was an infamous serial killer in Northern Cali during the 1960’s and 1970’s. His identity has only been speculated on, but this is his sign:\n\n\n\nTunechi probably goes around “killing” hoes in sucession just like the Zodiac.\n\nAlso: the “What’s your name, what’s your sign?” is a direct line from B.I.G.’s “Big Poppa”", "annotation_id": "1374611", "url": "https://genius.com/1374611", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "One time for them pussy niggas—that’s that shit I don’t like", "vault_lines": ["One time for them pussy niggas—that's that shit I don't like"], "meaning": "Reference to Chief Keef’s hit: “I Don’t Like”; “One Time” is referring to the police.\n\n\n\nWayne remixed this song on his latest mixtape Dedication 4.", "annotation_id": "1373384", "url": "https://genius.com/1373384", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As Fuck", "line": "Ugh, never talk to the cops, I don’t speak Pig Latin", "vault_lines": ["Ugh, never talk to the cops, I don't speak Pig Latin"], "meaning": "Wayne doesn’t associate with cops – “Pigs” is mocking slang for cops, and Pig Latin is a “language” made by taking English words, moving the first letter to the end of the word, and adding an “-ay” sound.\n\nHowever, Wayne’s claim of never talking to police is, in a literal sense, false. Per nola.com, Wayne called the cops once when he was 12 after he accidentally shot himself. Then years later in a restaurant, he recognized the cop who saved his life and called him over to thank him.\n\nLudacris expressed a similar sentiment back in 2003.", "annotation_id": "1372556", "url": "https://genius.com/1372556", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
