{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rich As F#ck", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/2-chainz-rich-as-fck-lyrics", "genius_title": "Rich As F#ck", "genius_id": 1857786, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "I know what’s at the store cause I go more, I go forth and so forth", "vault_lines": ["I know what's at the store cause I go more, I go forth and so forth"], "meaning": "Wayne loves pushing the boundaries of literary devices in hip hop and the limits of words within the confines of a beat. Wayne just finishes using the word “whores” in many different contexts in a repeating yet dynamic flow.\n\nI love reading “I know whats at the store cause I go more” as a metaphor for how Wayne can play with words better than anyone else because he practices more than anyone else.\n\nIn the unofficial documentary about Lil Wayne around Tha Carter III he says “repetition is the father of learning.” Wayne also frequently states on his mixtapes that they are practice. On Lamar from No Ceilings 3, Wayne states:\n“Get my cleats ‘cause I’m running this rap shit\nY'all know me, this ain’t nothing but practice”.", "annotation_id": "30832141", "url": "https://genius.com/30832141", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "What more can I say? I can’t feel my face", "vault_lines": ["What more can I say? I can't feel my face"], "meaning": "This line works on multiple levels: the literal physical numbness (possibly from substance use or intense experience) and a metaphorical sense of being overwhelmed. The inter-textual reference to Jay Z’s “What More Can I Say” adds a layer of humor and irony, making it a sylleptic pun that plays on the ambiguity of sensation and expression.", "annotation_id": "30604572", "url": "https://genius.com/30604572", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "I’m a kick to the snare, I’m a boom to the bass", "vault_lines": ["I'm a kick to the snare, I'm a boom to the bass"], "meaning": "This line artfully uses musical terms (“kick,” “snare,” “boom”) in a dual capacity: as literal drum sounds and metaphorically representing Lil Wayne’s impact and presence in music. The dual usage makes it a sylleptic pun, showcasing his integral role akin to essential elements of a rhythm. The double entendre here not only highlights his dominance in music but also cleverly aligns his personal influence with fundamental elements of sound.", "annotation_id": "30604472", "url": "https://genius.com/30604472", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "Bitch get lost in the current how the dough flows", "vault_lines": ["Bitch get lost in the current how the dough flows"], "meaning": "The term “current” cleverly refers to both the movement of water and the flow of money. This homographic pun intertwines natural phenomena with economic concepts, highlighting the pervasive influence of money.", "annotation_id": "30604358", "url": "https://genius.com/30604358", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "Try me and I’m coming out my coat arm with somethin’", "vault_lines": ["Try me and I'm coming out my coat arm with somethin'"], "meaning": "Initially suggesting the drawing of a weapon, the phrase “coat arm” may also play on “coat of arms,” symbolizing identity and allegiance. This homographic pun merges the physical action with a metaphorical gesture of revealing one’s true colors or affiliations, especially in light of Lil Wayne’s self-identification as a soldier and references to gang culture.", "annotation_id": "30604333", "url": "https://genius.com/30604333", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "Watch out Ms. Sylvia, I’m kinda feelin’ ya, ha", "vault_lines": ["Watch out Ms. Sylvia, I'm kinda feelin' ya, ha"], "meaning": "Sylvia Rhone was executive vice president of Universal Records from 2006 to 2011. Universal was parent and distributor of Cash Money Records.", "annotation_id": "30603907", "url": "https://genius.com/30603907", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "“gimme those” (gimme) Gimme those (those) Gimme those (those) Matter fact gimme those whole three rows", "vault_lines": ["Gimme those (those) Gimme those (those)"], "meaning": "I love the symmetry here. “Gimme those” repeats 4 times. “Gimme that” then repeats 4 times. Juelz starts this numeration with “two words”, inserts a 3 between the repeated 4’s and ends with a 4. Multi level Jazziness.", "annotation_id": "30598209", "url": "https://genius.com/30598209", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "You can’t get the cash then pay me in yayo", "vault_lines": ["You can't get the cash then pay me in yayo"], "meaning": "If you can’t pay him in cash, give him drugs.", "annotation_id": "28346403", "url": "https://genius.com/28346403", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "Nigga mouth slow-leakin’, air him out, no charge", "vault_lines": ["Nigga mouth slow-leakin', air him out, no charge"], "meaning": "‘mouth slow leakin’: Someone is snitching, little by little (most likely for jail privileges) .\n\n‘Air him out no charge’: nobody needs to get paid to take out a snitch, that’s for free.", "annotation_id": "18198687", "url": "https://genius.com/18198687", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "That coke, that hard, that crack, oh God", "vault_lines": ["That coke, that hard, that crack, oh God"], "meaning": "Coke, hard, crack. Referring to the three types of commonly trafficked cocaine. Powder coke, hard-packed bricks, and and rock crack.", "annotation_id": "18198682", "url": "https://genius.com/18198682", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
