{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "I hit the Saks like gimme that (that) gimme that (that) Gimme that, matter fact gimme that rack", "vault_lines": ["I hit the Saks like gimme that (that) gimme that (that)"], "meaning": "Saks Fifth Avenue is an expensive, designer clothing store originally on Fifth Ave. in New York City. The fact that Juelz can buy a whole rack of clothing there shows how much money he has.", "annotation_id": "11498427", "url": "https://genius.com/11498427", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "In the crib playin EA sports", "vault_lines": ["In the crib playin EA sports"], "meaning": "EA Sports is a video game company that dominates sports video games, making Madden, 2K, FIFA and many others.", "annotation_id": "11498419", "url": "https://genius.com/11498419", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "Uptown, Uptown’s where I rose", "vault_lines": ["Uptown, Uptown's where I rose"], "meaning": "Uptown is a neighborhood in Wayne’s home city New Orleans, which can be heard being frequently mentioned by him and Birdman.\n\nAs you can see in this picture, Hollygrove, where Wayne is really from, is a part of Uptown.\n\nhttps://www.google.com/maps?client=safari&rls=en&q=uptown+new+orleans&bav=on.2,or.r_cp.&bvm=bv.149397726,d.eWE&biw=1240&bih=680&um=1&ie=UTF-8&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiWgtHx49LSAhWEKCYKHbYdD68Q_AUIBigB", "annotation_id": "11498410", "url": "https://genius.com/11498410", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "Shout to my stompin’ ground, Hollygrove", "vault_lines": ["Shout to my stompin' ground, Hollygrove"], "meaning": "Hollygrove is the neighborhood Lil Wayne grew up in. It’s located in New Orleans, LA.", "annotation_id": "2890538", "url": "https://genius.com/2890538", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "Ice Cream hoodie, Bathing Ape tennis shoes", "vault_lines": ["Yea, Ice Cream hoodie, Bathing Ape tennis shoes"], "meaning": "Wayne’s talking about his outfit. He’s wearing a white hooded sweatshirt and ‘Bathing Ape’ sneaks. Bathing Ape is a Japanese company that was very popular at the release of this song.", "annotation_id": "2890524", "url": "https://genius.com/2890524", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "Niggas call Maybachs lo-lo’s", "vault_lines": ["Niggas call Maybachs lo-lo's"], "meaning": "A grand old car company initial founded by Wilhelm Maybach in 1920 (Maybach himself was one of the founding engineers of Diamler Benz).", "annotation_id": "1311255", "url": "https://genius.com/1311255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rewind", "line": "They know they gotta buy more, they head hurt they eyes sore You’re selling that cheap rock, sheet rock, dry wall They don’t want that, they come back for more But they come back to me, they don’t come back to y’all", "vault_lines": ["They know they gotta buy more, they head hurt they eyes sore"], "meaning": "Juelz is “rewinding” for the listener.  The addicts are going back to work to get more money, because Juelz’s rivals' inferior product fails to give them a quality high.  The crack Juelz is selling is actually quality, and not cut with anything – therefore the crack rocks are actually hard rocks, and not soft powder.  Competitors cut their crack to try and stretch it, possibly through “water-whipping”.  The fiends realize this, and knowing that the crack Juelz sells is better, return to him with their money.", "annotation_id": "554274", "url": "https://genius.com/554274", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
