{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renegades", "line": "And if she’s as late as yours", "vault_lines": ["And if she's as late as yours"], "meaning": "Misquoted lyric\n\n“And if she’s late it’s yours”\n\nWayne is referring to the previous bar about “going up in your lady raw and making your lady roar”\n\nWhen Wayne says “if she’s late, it’s yours” he’s saying after he busts inside your girl, if she’s late on her period because she’s pregnant, then the kid is yours", "annotation_id": "41763095", "url": "https://genius.com/41763095", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renegades", "line": "You know the boy from the damb streets, respect and expect me, I pack that heat", "vault_lines": ["You know the boy from the damb streets, respect and expect me, I pack that heat"], "meaning": "You know the boy from the MAZANT street, respect ME or expect BEEF, YOU CATS KNOW WHERE THE TEC BE", "annotation_id": "30690958", "url": "https://genius.com/30690958", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renegades", "line": "I’m younger than kobe, vet like rob horry", "vault_lines": ["I'm younger than kobe, vet like rob horry"], "meaning": "Kobe has been an object of Wayne’s admiration for a long time. He was 19 when he wrote this. 7 years later, he would go on to write a classic song about him, titled “Kobe Bryant”.\n\nWayne names 2 teammates on the Lakers at the time to help articulate that although he is younger than ‘02 Kobe, he has veteran status like Rob Horry due to how long he has been putting in work, despite his youth.", "annotation_id": "27307209", "url": "https://genius.com/27307209", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renegades", "line": "I’m bundlin up a ton, i’m pumpin it by that bump in the road I’ll leave you slumped in the road, if ever pumpin by my bump in the road", "vault_lines": ["I'm bundlin up a ton, i'm pumpin it by that bump in the road"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying hes bundling up a ton meaning he has a lot of drugs to sell and pumpin by the bump in the road means hes selling them by the road and he will kill you if he ever sees you selling by his spot In the road", "annotation_id": "13840551", "url": "https://genius.com/13840551", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renegades", "line": "Honey say her hubby gettin boring So honey be by money when you snoring", "vault_lines": ["Honey say her hubby gettin boring"], "meaning": "Wayne is indicating that he will take your bitch, you’re boring to her.\n\nAs soon as you fall asleep she’ll flock to Wayne (or “money”, as he refers to himself in this instance – which he clearly has more than enough to do so!)", "annotation_id": "3196910", "url": "https://genius.com/3196910", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renegades", "line": "I ain’t just jumped off the porch, i been that boy", "vault_lines": ["I ain't just jumped off the porch, i been that boy"], "meaning": "Wayne’s isn’t new to the game, having started his career in 1997 with the Hot Boys he’s a veteran in the game and has looked upon as one the best rappers in mainstream for quite some time now.\n\n\n\nHe has even claimed to be the best rapper alive.", "annotation_id": "3196901", "url": "https://genius.com/3196901", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
