{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "Back with hazardous weathers and blizzards As I spit, stickin’ out my tongue like an iguana lizard", "vault_lines": ["Back with hazardous weathers and blizzards"], "meaning": "back in the days when he used to perform in the street of East Flatbush, New York where it rains bullets and crack cocaine is been sold left to right none stop all day every day…", "annotation_id": "28417799", "url": "https://genius.com/28417799", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "Farmers Boulevard", "vault_lines": ["Right there, on Farmers Boulevard"], "meaning": "Farmer’s Boulevard is a a street in Saint Alban’s, Queens, where Q-Tip grew up. LL Cool J also, famously, rapped about it.", "annotation_id": "27511582", "url": "https://genius.com/27511582", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "We be runnin’ out of rhymes, never bullets", "vault_lines": ["We be runnin' out of rhymes, never bullets"], "meaning": "Raekwon is a true OG in the game at this point, he must have to start running out of rhymes to spit eventually, but he assures us, he’ll never run out of bullets to spit no matter how old he gets.", "annotation_id": "2669570", "url": "https://genius.com/2669570", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "Poison medals on my neck wrists and arms", "vault_lines": ["Poison medals on my neck wrists and arms"], "meaning": "Rae rocks his jewelry like medals of honour from his wars on the streets. The way he references them as ‘poison’ shows that The Chef acknowledges that what he’s done to earn them may not have been exactly saintly (Drug dealing, gang banging, shooting it out)", "annotation_id": "2669566", "url": "https://genius.com/2669566", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "Ayo, ayo, squeezing Johnny Walker neck up in the Benzo freezing", "vault_lines": ["Ayo, ayo, squeezing Johnny Walker neck up in the Benzo freezing"], "meaning": "Raekwon is holding his bottle of Johnny Walker (Hopefully nothing  less than Blue Label) by the neck so he can start drinking in his ‘ice cold’ Benz.", "annotation_id": "2669564", "url": "https://genius.com/2669564", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "Yo, yo, Godbody, wise intelligence", "vault_lines": ["Yo, yo, Godbody, wise intelligence"], "meaning": "God body in some areas is slang for the Five percent nation, the organization founded in Harlem that believe that they are the 5% of the total population of the earth who know the truth of existence and are determined to enlighten the rest of the uninformed masses. Busta Rhymes used to be part of the Five percent nation but he converted to traditional Islam.", "annotation_id": "2594207", "url": "https://genius.com/2594207", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "Night of the living MC’s, the weak ones fled; c’mon Bus…", "vault_lines": ["Night of the living MC's, the weak ones fled; c'mon Bus…"], "meaning": "Playing off the ‘dead’ reference in the previous line, ‘Night of the living MC’s’ is a spin on the horror film, “Night of the living dead”. In the movie people are trapped in a farmhouse killing off zombies and trying to survive. Tip and BussaBuss are killing off rappers like the people in the movie.", "annotation_id": "2594170", "url": "https://genius.com/2594170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "Get it in your head, we gon’ rock the dead", "vault_lines": ["Get it in your head, we gon' rock the dead"], "meaning": "He wants the people to believe that he will accomplish the seemingly impossible with this new music he is putting out.", "annotation_id": "2594159", "url": "https://genius.com/2594159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "At you corny niggas (ha!), Animal Planet rap, Wildlife", "vault_lines": ["At you corny niggas (ha!), Animal Planet rap, Wildlife"], "meaning": "Notice the use of all kinds of animal metaphors throughout the verse. Elephants, Iguana, Buffalo, Gorillas.", "annotation_id": "2594152", "url": "https://genius.com/2594152", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "My beloved, respect my benevolence", "vault_lines": ["My beloved, respect my benevolence"], "meaning": "Benevolence – ‘an act intending or showing kindness and good will’. Busta wants the people to be thankful for blessing us with these BARS.", "annotation_id": "2594121", "url": "https://genius.com/2594121", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "Weezy Baby, straight out the Caesarean, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Weezy Baby, straight out the Caesarean, nigga"], "meaning": "Another strange play on his nickname “Weezy F Baby”.\n\nHere, he implies the baby is being birthed by C-Section.\n\nMan, Wayne is just crazy.", "annotation_id": "2562384", "url": "https://genius.com/2562384", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "So ahead of my time with my next-week ass", "vault_lines": ["So ahead of my time with my next-week ass"], "meaning": "Wayne is just saying that his style is so far ahead of it’s time (he’s doing now what people in a year will be doing) that he’s living in next week.\n\nHe’s a trendsetter…", "annotation_id": "2416388", "url": "https://genius.com/2416388", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "And then my legend would grow on the A-train line", "vault_lines": ["And then my legend would grow on the A-train line"], "meaning": "The A-train line is a subway route in New York City that goes through part of Queens, much of Brooklyn, and Harlem. Q-Tip was likely battling other rappers on the train, growing his reputation and legend from borough to borough with each victory.", "annotation_id": "2407637", "url": "https://genius.com/2407637", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "[Intro: Q-Tip (imitating Marley Marl)] I don’t care who first or who last I just know y’all betta rock dis at da drop of a dime, baby! (Renaissance…) I don’t care what y’all say or what y’all do But you got to be finished before the music is through", "vault_lines": ["I don't care who first or who last"], "meaning": "The intro, interlude and outro are all references to Marley Marl’s song “The Symphony”, a posse cut consisting of four Juice Crew members: Masta Ace, Craig G, Kool G Rap and Big Daddy Kane. It is often referred to as one of the greatest posse cuts of all time.", "annotation_id": "2406429", "url": "https://genius.com/2406429", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "And I do it for the killers and the hundred dollar billas", "vault_lines": ["And I do it for the killers and the hundred dollar billas"], "meaning": "An allusion to: Shook One’s Pt II by Mobb Deep http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0NUX4tW5pps", "annotation_id": "561307", "url": "https://genius.com/561307", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "You got a bullet and a shank, I got a bullet and a tank", "vault_lines": ["You got a bullet and a shank, I got a bullet and a tank"], "meaning": "What he has is ten times better than what you have.", "annotation_id": "452231", "url": "https://genius.com/452231", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "Though they call me Weezy F., you gon let me pass", "vault_lines": ["Though they call me Weezy F., you gon let me pass"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne calls himself Weezy F, and although the F stands for a failing grade, you’re still going to let him pass (because he has mucho dinero)\n\n\n\nPeep Lil'Wayne’s many nicknames", "annotation_id": "452229", "url": "https://genius.com/452229", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Renaissance Rap (Remix)", "line": "When in the heat of the cypher, I was not liable For all the casualties of the dutty MCs", "vault_lines": ["When in the heat of the cypher, I was not liable"], "meaning": "He couldn’t control his fatal rhyming skills, when it gets down at cyphers he was like a Uzi to the other wack rappers…\n\n\n\nYou can see it in his eyes….", "annotation_id": "452225", "url": "https://genius.com/452225", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
