{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Rum", "line": "If her religion is true, I’m ’bout to visit the moon Is you coming?", "vault_lines": ["If her religion is true, I'm 'bout to visit the moon"], "meaning": "This does refer to True Religion Jeans. He’s saying he’s about to take a trip to her ass if she’s wearing those jeans.", "annotation_id": "629918", "url": "https://genius.com/629918", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Rum", "line": "And yea, I be on that ass like a horse’s shoe", "vault_lines": ["And yea, I be on that ass like a horse's shoe"], "meaning": "True religion jeans have a horse shoe on backside.", "annotation_id": "629917", "url": "https://genius.com/629917", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Rum", "line": "And since day one, I look forward to Three, four, five bitches in my Porsche coupe", "vault_lines": ["And since day one, I look forward to"], "meaning": "Wayne has always expected to be fucking bad bitches in his luxury Porsche Coupe! Damn wayne, look where that ambition got you. a fucking Bugatti!", "annotation_id": "629916", "url": "https://genius.com/629916", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Rum", "line": "That’s what they be yellin’ I’m a pimp by blood, not relation Ya’ll be chasin, and I replace em’.. huh?", "vault_lines": ["Ya'll be chasin, and I replace em'.. huh?"], "meaning": "POWERFUL! Being a pimp is in HIS DNA specifically, its not something that runs through his family. While other pimps are chasing hoes he’s already replacing them.", "annotation_id": "629907", "url": "https://genius.com/629907", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Rum", "line": "When they Remy’s in the system Ain’t no tellin’ will I fuck em’, will I diss em’", "vault_lines": ["When the Remy's in the system"], "meaning": "This is referring to Biggie’s classic lines, also used by Jay-Z on “I Just Wanna Love U“  in the song ”The World Is Filled\"", "annotation_id": "629906", "url": "https://genius.com/629906", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Rum", "line": "My nigga I think we got one, well, another one Theres so much of these mo’fuckers, Weezy", "vault_lines": ["My nigga I think we got one, well, another one"], "meaning": "Wayne has so many hits, you could have the radio jammed up with his songs.\n\nLil Wayne is the only artist to have 6 Billboard hits in a year.", "annotation_id": "629900", "url": "https://genius.com/629900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Rum", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-red-rum-lyrics", "genius_title": "Red Rum", "genius_id": 62443, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Louisville slugger, Yogi Berra in my new era", "vault_lines": ["Louisville slugger, Yogi Berra in my new era"], "meaning": "Double entendre … the Game is one of the best in this ‘new era’ of rap, akin to Yogi Berra being one of the best catchers of all time in the MLB from the 40s and 50s.\n\nAlso, New Era is a brand of baseball hats. Game probably feels like like a baller (like Yogi Berra) in his New Era hat.", "annotation_id": "24057192", "url": "https://genius.com/24057192", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Where my nigga Jim Jones at?", "vault_lines": ["Where my nigga Jim Jones at?"], "meaning": "Double entendre. Jim Jones is an american rapper who has collaborated with The Game on several ocassions however The Game could also be referencing the infamous cult leader Jim Jones founder of “The People´s Temple” a religious congregation that mixed Christianism and Communism. In 1978 he forced all of his followers to perform a mass suicide to prevent his arrest and repatriation from Guyana back to the US.\n The Game is referencing where is his fellow due to the fact that they are both players of the “red team” so to say, as Game is a Blood gang member and Jones was a firm believer of Communism a political doctrine identified by the color red.\n\n\n\nJones in 1977", "annotation_id": "19537132", "url": "https://genius.com/19537132", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "And we gon’ fuck the world ’til that bitch bust nuts", "vault_lines": ["And we gon' fuck the world 'til that bitch bust nuts"], "meaning": "“Fuck” means to have sex with and “busting a nut” is slang for ejaculating, So Lil Wayne is saying that he will have sex with the world until it ejacuates", "annotation_id": "19522932", "url": "https://genius.com/19522932", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Niggas’ll trade they soul to be Drake or J. Cole Live and die for this shit, word to 2Pac Shakur’s halo", "vault_lines": ["Niggas’ll trade they soul to be Drake or J. Cole"], "meaning": "The Game gives shoutouts to two very popular and successful rappers who were some of the most talked-about fresh faces at the time, Drake and J. Cole.\n\nWith his mixtapes The Warm Up and Friday Night Lights, Cole established himself as one of the most prominent lyrical rappers in the game at the start of the 2010’s.\n\nThe prodigy of Lil Wayne, Drake broke out with the release of his 2009 single “Best I Ever Had” and quickly became a huge superstar. The Game would go on to collaborate with Cole on his 2012 track “Pray,” and with Drake on the 2015 hit single “100.”\n\n\n\nHailing from Compton, California, The Game has paid respect to other legendary rappers from the area over the years. Here, he references 2Pac, one of the most celebrated hip-hop artists who represented Los Angeles. Unfortunately, 2Pac was shot and killed on September 13, 1996 in a Las Vegas drive-by. It is also worth noting that Pac made a song called “To Live and Die in L.A.”", "annotation_id": "18878340", "url": "https://genius.com/18878340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Now we hittin’ switches ’til the Spring Break, Cancun", "vault_lines": ["Now we hittin’ switches 'til the Spring Break, Cancun"], "meaning": "Lowriders can be customized with hydraulic switches to bounce the right way. It would be pretty hard to go all the way to Cancun (the popular Spring Break destination on the EAST Coast of Mexico) in one of those cars though.\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso, if you “hit switches” too much in a car with hydraulics the “springs” might “break.” Spring Break is a play on words, in this case referencing the springs of a car which make hydraulics possible.", "annotation_id": "202950", "url": "https://genius.com/202950", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Got my red Dre Beats on, tryna put my peeps on", "vault_lines": ["Got my red Dre Beats on, tryna put my peeps on"], "meaning": "Reference to Dre’s “Beats” headphones. Game has been endorsing the product and trying to put his friends on to them, the headphones sporting a red b logo on the sides (perfect for Game and the Blood gang, which rock all red everything.)\n\n\n\nWhen Game says this line in the video, it shows Kid Red wearing red Beats headphones. At the time, Kid Red was signed to Black Wall Street. Game was tryna make Kid Red hot, when he literally put him on his video with Young Money.", "annotation_id": "202922", "url": "https://genius.com/202922", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Walk in the club saggin’ with a .38 Magnum", "vault_lines": ["Walk in the club saggin’ with a .38 Magnum"], "meaning": "His pants are sagging from the weight of the Mangnum, in this case the gun\n\nFYI: .38 special (a type of gun) can fire out of any revolver chambered for .357 magnum (another gun). So he effectively combines the two; hence .38 magnum.", "annotation_id": "202895", "url": "https://genius.com/202895", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Got that natty on, tighter than a magnum", "vault_lines": ["Got that natty on, tighter than a magnum"], "meaning": "He wears a Cincinnati cap on his head tighter than a magnum condom\n\n\n\nThis line is also a subtle brag about Game’s penis size, since magnum condoms are made for larger members.", "annotation_id": "202893", "url": "https://genius.com/202893", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Of the New Era, test me", "vault_lines": ["of the New Era, test me"], "meaning": "Game claims to be the force to be reckoned with in this era.\n\nAlso a reference to New Era, the maker of popular baseball caps such as the Cincinnati cap mentioned in the first line..\n\n\n\nThe juxtaposition of the name of a well-known socialist revolutionary with a corporate brand also serves to parody both while allowing Game to paint himself, in Warholesque fashion, as a figure above both revolution and profit–much to his own benefit", "annotation_id": "202886", "url": "https://genius.com/202886", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Che Guevara", "vault_lines": ["Throw your muthafucking Cincinnati hats in the sky,"], "meaning": "Argentinian communist revolutionary who entered U.S. popular culture with ubiquitous Red T-shirts that were popular about ten years ago.\n\n\n\nHe was part of the “Red Army” of communism, thus the blood tie-in.", "annotation_id": "202884", "url": "https://genius.com/202884", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "And stick my red flag in the ground it’s Red Nation", "vault_lines": ["And stick my red flag in the ground it’s Red Nation"], "meaning": "Game will also continue to rep for the Bloods. In fact, he took to twitter to protest the decision of MTV and BET not to play the Red Nation video due to its unsubtle gang-related content.", "annotation_id": "202870", "url": "https://genius.com/202870", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Dre called, told my baby momma “won’t you decide”", "vault_lines": ["Dre called, told my baby momma “won’t you decide”"], "meaning": "Game has said that his first mixtape reached the hands of Sean Combs, who was on the on the verge of signing him to Bad Boy. Dr. Dre had also listened to the mixtape and convinced him to join Aftermath in 2003.", "annotation_id": "202844", "url": "https://genius.com/202844", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "98 degrees on Christmas,", "vault_lines": ["98 degrees on Christmas,"], "meaning": "Game’s hometown of Los Angeles is known to be warm year-round, yes, even on Christmas.\n\nThis is also a reference to the boy band 98 Degrees who released an album This Christmas, released on Christmas of 1999.", "annotation_id": "202791", "url": "https://genius.com/202791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Get thrown in the backwoods, Los Angeles", "vault_lines": ["Get thrown in the backwoods, Los Angeles"], "meaning": "A play on words from the previous line. Backwoods usually refer to remote, thinly settled areas, but here The Game just uses it to emphasize the dangers of Los Angeles.", "annotation_id": "202778", "url": "https://genius.com/202778", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "One blood,", "vault_lines": ["Throw your muthafucking Cincinnati hats in the sky,"], "meaning": "Plural refers to both the “one blood” and “Euros”.\n\nOne Blood just means Bloods are united as one even though they have many members (i.e. they are plural). Sort of like when the army replaced “Be All You Can Be” with the “Army of One” slogan. It was quickly abandoned when the paradox between individual choice and group coherence became apparent. Too bad they hadn’t read up much on social choice theory.\n\n\n\nBig up to Kenneth Arrow.\n\n“One blood” is also a reference to “One love,” a phrase which expresses unity. In this case that unity would be among blood gang members, but there is even deeper meaning here. Nas has a song called “One Love”, and in the song “The Kill”, Game states the following:\n\n“Nas, we forever since you helped me get a deal son”", "annotation_id": "202768", "url": "https://genius.com/202768", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "That’s my Chi-lingo, yeah I’m bi-lingual", "vault_lines": ["That’s my Chi-lingo, yeah I’m bi-lingual"], "meaning": "Game states the last few lines were an example of his ‘Chicago language’, or ‘lingo’. That means he can talk like gang members from Chicago, so he speaks two languages; Chicago gang and the gang where he’s from", "annotation_id": "202738", "url": "https://genius.com/202738", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Plural, nigga I’m spending Euros", "vault_lines": ["plural, nigga I’m spending Euros"], "meaning": "Euro, as in the currency used in much of West Europe (the UK, Norway, and Switzerland being notable exceptions). The Game is either implying that he is spending money overseas or that he is somehow hedging his currency exposure.\n\nIn most of Europe, the plural of Euro is still Euro as in “even the cheapest hotel in Monaco cost us too many Euro.” But maybe Game learned from Jay-Z from whom he “borrowed” the line:\n\n I see Euros, that’s right: plural", "annotation_id": "202735", "url": "https://genius.com/202735", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Bullets and fast cars", "vault_lines": ["bullets and fast cars"], "meaning": "Surrealist portrait of Los Angeles: Hollywood celebrities dance while people in the hood dodge bullets and drive fast cars.", "annotation_id": "185992", "url": "https://genius.com/185992", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "So many bloods in Compton had to get a NYC song", "vault_lines": ["So many bloods in Compton had to get a NYC song"], "meaning": "The Bloods started in Compton as the Pirus Street gang of the Crips and broke off during an internal gang war (hence the rivalry). They have since expanded as a somewhat loosely bound organization of affiliated groups.\n\nGame may be alluding to this fact by referencing the song We Keep It Rocking which features Jim Jones and uses the famous “California Love” beat to celebrate New York.", "annotation_id": "178230", "url": "https://genius.com/178230", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "But that was suicide, I don’t live in Judas’ eyes", "vault_lines": ["But that was suicide, I don’t live in Judas’ eyes"], "meaning": "Judas Iscariot was one of the twelve disciples of Jesus. He is best known for betraying Jesus for “thirty pieces of silver.” According to Matthew, he later felt remorse and committed suicide.", "annotation_id": "161794", "url": "https://genius.com/161794", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Nigga we rollin’ cannabis", "vault_lines": ["nigga we rollin’ cannabis"], "meaning": "They smoke marijuana", "annotation_id": "155094", "url": "https://genius.com/155094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Blood, I’m a dog, call me a blood hound", "vault_lines": ["Blood, I’m a dog, call me a blood hound"], "meaning": "He’s a blood, and a friend of Game’s, and he’s a “dog” and so are bloodhound’s.", "annotation_id": "152885", "url": "https://genius.com/152885", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Lookin’ in the mirror, I’m nowhere to be found", "vault_lines": ["Lookin’ in the mirror, I’m nowhere to be found"], "meaning": "This is a line connecting vampires to the gang; vampires can’t be seen in a mirror. He metaphorically calls himself a vampire (a mu'fucking monster who likes blood).", "annotation_id": "152822", "url": "https://genius.com/152822", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Dancing with the stars,", "vault_lines": ["Dancing with the stars,"], "meaning": "A reference to the previous line. Chad Ochocinco was featured on a recent season of “Dancing With The Stars.”", "annotation_id": "144148", "url": "https://genius.com/144148", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "I told her I’m Charles Louboutin", "vault_lines": ["Swisha sweet ain't it, I told her I’m Charles Louboutin"], "meaning": "One of Game’s pseudonyms. Also the name that appears on his Twitter account. In other words his “alias.”", "annotation_id": "144147", "url": "https://genius.com/144147", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Home of the scandalous,", "vault_lines": ["Home of the scandalous,"], "meaning": "Possible reference to Los Angeles native Tupac’s “Skandalouz”", "annotation_id": "143130", "url": "https://genius.com/143130", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Ferrari got an ice cream paint job, Dorrough", "vault_lines": ["Ferrari got an ice cream paint job, Dorrough"], "meaning": "A shout out to Dorrough, who came out with a single in 2009 called “Ice Cream Paint Job”", "annotation_id": "143100", "url": "https://genius.com/143100", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Ball by myself, nigga, Ochocinco", "vault_lines": ["Ball by myself, nigga, Ochocinco"], "meaning": "Chad Johnson (Ochocinco) is a football player known for putting himself before the team. He is a talented player, but only does it for himself, which is frowned upon in football, but earns respect in the hood if you can do it all on your own.", "annotation_id": "142704", "url": "https://genius.com/142704", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "I, walk on the moon,", "vault_lines": ["I, walk on the moon,"], "meaning": "Much as Neil Armstrong was the first man on the moon, The Game was the first rapper to claim Blood Piru.\n\n\n\n“One small step for man, one giant leap for thugs”\n\n\n(Actually Game was the second to claim. DJ Quik, who’s first album (Quik Is the Name) came out in 1991, was the first mainstream artist to claim to be apart of the Bloods. He was one of the few if not only to do so with the the only other “fellow gang members” in the rap community being Crips (Eazy-E, MC Ren, Snoop Dogg, Dogg Pound etc.) A decade later, Game would be the 2nd) RG Facts", "annotation_id": "142249", "url": "https://genius.com/142249", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "On a hill like Lauren", "vault_lines": ["On a hill like Lauren"], "meaning": "Lauryn Hill: one of the most profound female hip-hop artists in the history of the game; no pun intended.", "annotation_id": "141909", "url": "https://genius.com/141909", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "And that’s, B’s up, hoes down", "vault_lines": ["And that’s, B’s up, hoes down"], "meaning": "He holds his Bloods gang members in higher esteem than women (how does Ms. Cita feel about this line?)\n\nThis can also mean putting “B’s up” with your hands for the “blood” symbol, and “hoes down” means girls get down on their knees, if you know what I mean.\n\nThis is also a reference to Snoop Dogg’s, “G’s Up, Hoes Down”(which is odd, because Snoop is a Crip). Here’s a better explanation of this connection.\n\nThis also references to the line before it, “I can’t tell you whats good, but I can tell you whats what”\n\nWhats good – Hoes\nWhats up? – B’s up.\n\nBloods before hoes.", "annotation_id": "141908", "url": "https://genius.com/141908", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "I can’t tell you what’s good, but I can tell you what’s what", "vault_lines": ["I can’t tell you what's good, but I can tell you what's what"], "meaning": "Moral relativism/ambiguity as conveyed by Lil Wayne.\n\n“What’s good” is usually used in the sense of “What’s up,” but here Wayne seems to be taking it more literally (i.e. good as “right” or “morally just”). In other words, he is not sure what is right, but he is aware of what’s happening around him.", "annotation_id": "141907", "url": "https://genius.com/141907", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Russia got a red flag, US got red stripes", "vault_lines": ["Russia got a red flag, US got red stripes"], "meaning": "United States and USSR – both implicitly support the Bloods\n\n\n\n\n\nFACT: Russians switched to a red, white, and blue flag in the 22th August, 1991.", "annotation_id": "141335", "url": "https://genius.com/141335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Any nigga want drama I kick up a sand dune", "vault_lines": ["Any nigga want drama I kick up a sand dune"], "meaning": "This is Game’s wordplay on “kickin' up dust” phrase. He suggests that he will cause much much more problems to anyone who wants to cause him trouble. He’s not just kickin' up “dust” but the whole “sand dune”!\n\nThis desert imagery ties in well with the previous line’s heated seasonal metaphor", "annotation_id": "141325", "url": "https://genius.com/141325", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Suge had me in,", "vault_lines": ["Suge had me in,"], "meaning": "Suge Knight, the producer, helped him start his career as a rapper.", "annotation_id": "141218", "url": "https://genius.com/141218", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "I went Puffy like Zab Judah eye", "vault_lines": ["I went Puffy like Zab Judah eye"], "meaning": "He worked with Puffy after he worked with Suge Knight, despite the famous rivalry\n\n\n\nZab Judah – top tier boxer, with his eye got swollen or “Puffy”", "annotation_id": "140929", "url": "https://genius.com/140929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Cause I’m Malcolm X before he turned Muslim, Red", "vault_lines": ["Cause I’m Malcolm X before he turned Muslim, Red"], "meaning": "Prior to converting to Islam, Malcolm X was known as “Detroit Red” due to his ruddy hair color\n\n\n\nThe Game is most likely refering to Malcolm X’s early days of drug dealing and pimping. Malcolm Little soon moved on to more elaborate larcenies of wealthy families in Boston, for which he was incarcerated. It was during this incarceration he converted to Islam.", "annotation_id": "140582", "url": "https://genius.com/140582", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "The double R sittin’", "vault_lines": ["Red Ralph Laurens, the double R sittin’"], "meaning": "Referencing the Range Rover\n\n\n\nOr possibly the Rolls Royce (a UK-made car, which could present a double interpretation of the word “foreign” in the next line)", "annotation_id": "140569", "url": "https://genius.com/140569", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Made the letter B more famous than a Red Sox fitted", "vault_lines": ["Made the letter B more famous than a Red Sox fitted"], "meaning": "Boston? Blood? You decide!\n\nPossibly inspired by the Jay-Z line “I made the Yankee hat more famous than a Yankee can.”\n\nThis could also be the “B” in the Black Wall Street logo.", "annotation_id": "140562", "url": "https://genius.com/140562", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Get it? Nah forget it, Soo Woo I live it", "vault_lines": ["Get it? Nah forget it, Soo Woo I live it"], "meaning": "First, Game asks us if we get the previous line (which I’m not sure that I do). He implies that it is an insider Blood reference which most us wouldn’t know (i.e. “forget it”).\n\nSoo Woo is a common saying by Bloods to greet one another (some rappers talk about it; Game B’s about it)\n\n\n\n“Soo Woo” is also a song by The Game and Lil Wayne off of Purp & Patron.", "annotation_id": "140560", "url": "https://genius.com/140560", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Peace to my man Tune for giving his man room", "vault_lines": ["Peace to my man Tune for giving his man room"], "meaning": "‘Tune is short for Lil Tunchi which is another name for lil wayne\n\nThe Game is thanking Lil Wayne for waiting a little longer to put out his forthcoming album – Carter 4 – since it makes 2011 a R.E.D. album year (go Bloods!)", "annotation_id": "140559", "url": "https://genius.com/140559", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Nation", "line": "Throw your muthafucking Cincinnati hats in the sky,", "vault_lines": ["Throw your muthafucking Cincinnati hats in the sky,"], "meaning": "The song is about the Bloods – The Game wears Cincinnati hats because they represent “Red” (which is the bloods color), and also have a C to represent his set: Cedar Block Pirus…\n\nIt’s ironic though, as their main rivals are the Crips, and they use the C to represent their gang.\n\n\n\nThe C on the hat also stands for Compton, Game’s hometown", "annotation_id": "140558", "url": "https://genius.com/140558", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
