{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Magic", "line": "And this time, I’m gon’ shine like the chrome on Dayton’s", "vault_lines": ["And this time I'm gon' shine like the chrome on Dayton's"], "meaning": "Dayton’s are rims for a car that do tend to shine.\n\n\n\nTo shine means to do well, so if Game is going to shine like Dayton’s then he is going to do his best to reach goals.", "annotation_id": "1458936", "url": "https://genius.com/1458936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Magic", "line": "But Weezy go this hard, like pussy right in front me", "vault_lines": ["But Weezy go this hard, like pussy right in front me"], "meaning": "To “go hard” in rap means to rap strongly or rap well. Wayne compares him going hard on a song (making a good song) to getting hard (getting an erection) if a naked woman was in front of him. Wayne is pretty much trying to express he will constantly make good songs, and used the whole hard wordplay to be clever.", "annotation_id": "1458917", "url": "https://genius.com/1458917", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Magic", "line": "Before S dot Carter was Brooklyn’s stepfather", "vault_lines": ["Before S dot Carter was Brooklyn's step-father"], "meaning": "Here Game is referring to Jay-Z. Jay-Z’s name is Shawn Carter, and he was raised in Brooklyn. Since he was raised in Brooklyn, Game is just paying homage to Jay by saying he the big man from New York.\n\nJay-Z first became known to a wide audience in 1994 when he was featured on the posse cut of Show and Prove by Big Daddy Kane. Meaning Jay-Z became Brooklyn’s “stepfather” around the time of 1994. Game is referring to how he was doing gang related things before Jay-Z became widely known. That goes to show that Game has been gang banging for a long time.", "annotation_id": "1458890", "url": "https://genius.com/1458890", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Red Magic", "line": "Nigga, so you know what I mean When I say I get the money like a money machine, yeah I’m in L.A. Gasol-in’", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, so you know what I mean"], "meaning": "When he’s in Los Angeles he’s cheering for Pau Gasol", "annotation_id": "146233", "url": "https://genius.com/146233", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
