{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Real As They Come", "line": "Like Excedrin cause it’s this big", "vault_lines": ["Like Excedrin cause it’s this big"], "meaning": "Excedrin is a headache medicine,\nTheir commercials would say “I’ve got a headache THIS BIG!”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DT4Q5bLg6Qw", "annotation_id": "587069", "url": "https://genius.com/587069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Real As They Come", "line": "I looked in the mirror and I said what’s happening? The mirror said “you are, you conceited bastard!”", "vault_lines": ["I looked in the mirror and I said what’s happening?"], "meaning": "He looked in the mirror and asked himself what’s happening, then suddenly realised that he is! In other words, he’s “doing it” with his music.\n\nSomewhat Mirroring Maleficent asking who is the fairest lady in the land.", "annotation_id": "587046", "url": "https://genius.com/587046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Real As They Come", "line": "D-R.﻿ C-A-R-T-E… R Or, R-I-P hahaha", "vault_lines": ["Or I-C-U N I-T, D-R.﻿ C-A-R-T-E… R"], "meaning": "Dr. Carter, an alias Wayne often associates himself with. Carter is of course his surname. “r.i.p” could refer to the state you’d be in if you cross him… (dead), either way Wayne is going on a S-P-E-L-L-I-N-G  S-P-R-E-E", "annotation_id": "587009", "url": "https://genius.com/587009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Real As They Come", "line": "Yeah without my street, and that’s Apple & Eagle bitch", "vault_lines": ["Yeah without my street, and that’s Apple & Eagle bitch"], "meaning": "Continuation from previous line, as well as drugs, Wayne’s life revolves heavily around his “hood”, where he grew up. Apple and Eagle is the name of the street on which his “corner” was (where he sold crack from) in 17th Ward of Hollygrove, New Orleans, Louisiana.", "annotation_id": "587004", "url": "https://genius.com/587004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Real As They Come", "line": "Red flag, red hat", "vault_lines": ["Red flag, red hat"], "meaning": "reference to weezy’s affiliation with the Blood Gang. Bloods (and Wayne) wear all red to show their loyalty.", "annotation_id": "586989", "url": "https://genius.com/586989", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
