{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "She want the green light, let the bitch go", "vault_lines": ["She want the green light, let the bitch go"], "meaning": "A reference to “Red Light Green Light”, an ‘03 Limp Bizkit track with Snoop Dogg.", "annotation_id": "1618026", "url": "https://genius.com/1618026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "I’m a fuckin’ outlaw (Fucked up), packin’ me a chainsaw (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a fuckin' outlaw (Fucked up), packin' me a chainsaw (Yeah)"], "meaning": "A callback to “Break Stuff”, where Fred first made us aware of his proud chainsaw ownership.", "annotation_id": "1618011", "url": "https://genius.com/1618011", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "Everything I touch turn to gold, she a gold digger", "vault_lines": ["Everything I touch turn to gold, she a gold digger"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne apparently has the “midas touch”. Since everything he touches turns to gold his chick must be a gold digger.\n\n\n\nThis line could also mean that since Lil Wayne has a lot of expensive (gold) things, then his girl just want him for his money.", "annotation_id": "1616162", "url": "https://genius.com/1616162", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "They say that rock-shit doesn’t rock anymo’ They say the whole game done went pop, so I’m back in this ho", "vault_lines": ["They say that rock-shit doesn't rock anymo'"], "meaning": "Despite having several charting singles, Limp Bizkit’s image has always been anti-pop. Now that popular music has grown so stagnant and boring, they’re bringing some crazy back into this motherfucker.\n\nAlthough despite the fact that Bizkit is anti-pop, they are on the same label as:\nLil Wayne\n\n\n\nDrake\n\n\n\nNicki Minaj\n\n\n\nParis Hilton", "annotation_id": "1615138", "url": "https://genius.com/1615138", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "You know, the one to have Britney droppin’ to her knees (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["You know, the one to have Britney droppin' to her knees (Oh)"], "meaning": "LIMP BIZKIT frontman FRED DURST has boasted how he had rampant sex with BRITNEY SPEARS after she wore a see-through blouse to seduce him.\n\n-The Sun", "annotation_id": "1614653", "url": "https://genius.com/1614653", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "It’s ashes to ashes, dust to dust, come on", "vault_lines": ["It's ashes to ashes, dust to dust, come on"], "meaning": "This is a phrase from the Anglican burial service that has worked its way into popular culture\n\nFor as much as it hath pleased Almighty God of his great mercy to take unto himself the soul of our dear brother here departed, we therefore commit his body to the ground; earth to earth, ashes to ashes, dust to dust; in sure and certain hope of the Resurrection to eternal life, through our Lord Jesus Christ; who shall change our vile body, that it may be like unto his glorious body, according to the mighty working, whereby he is able to subdue all things to himself.\n\nInterestingly enough, Pusha T, a longtime rival of Wayne, dropped a similar line", "annotation_id": "1614561", "url": "https://genius.com/1614561", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "That’s right, it’s Freddy D (Yeah), the public enemy (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["That's right, it's Freddy D (Yeah), the public enemy (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Likely meant to be a comparison between Durst and Chuck D of Public Enemy fame…ironic as one is famous for making conscious afro-centric hip hop and the other is so symbolic of the archetypal “White rapper”", "annotation_id": "1614528", "url": "https://genius.com/1614528", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "Rock, rock, rock with a real nigga", "vault_lines": ["Rock, rock, rock with a real nigga"], "meaning": "Double entendre:\n\n\nRock as in you can chill with him —  a “real nigga”\nTo rock could also mean to play music with him, as “Rock” is a genre of music, one that this song falls under.\n\n\n\nLil Wayne is no stranger to the Rock genre, he once crossed over a bit with his heavy Rock influenced album, Rebirth. Plus, he plays the guitar so he can sorta rock:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Smb8tMeRTQQ\n\n…I never said he was any good.", "annotation_id": "1614436", "url": "https://genius.com/1614436", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "Forty million records later, I am still the fuckin’ man", "vault_lines": ["Forty million records later, I am still the fuckin' man"], "meaning": "Limp Bizkit have released six studio albums, been nominated for 3 Grammy’s and have sold over 35 million records worldwide. (According to Wikipedia) but Fred says 40, either way it’s a lot. With a new album coming in 2013 and all these facts in check anyone saying LB fell off needs to check the numbers.", "annotation_id": "1614301", "url": "https://genius.com/1614301", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "Shots, shots, shots, have a lil’ liquor", "vault_lines": ["Shots, shots, shots, have a lil' liquor"], "meaning": "Strangely reminiscent of the smash LMFAO single “Shots”", "annotation_id": "1614261", "url": "https://genius.com/1614261", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "And now they wanna copy me like ten-fo’", "vault_lines": ["And now they wanna copy me like ten-fo'"], "meaning": "10-4 is code for “copy” on radio CB, basically meaning “message received”.", "annotation_id": "1614251", "url": "https://genius.com/1614251", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "Red hat to the back like Fred Durst, uh", "vault_lines": ["Red hat to the back like Fred Durst, uh"], "meaning": "As part of his “signature” look he always had the omniprescent red New York Yankees Fitted hat turned backwards in performances, videos, tours, etc\n\nThis is also a reference to Wayne’s supposed Blood affiliations.\n\nWeezy also used this reference on his cover of D.O.A\n\nFlip your fitted cap back like Fred Durst", "annotation_id": "1614250", "url": "https://genius.com/1614250", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Ready to Go", "line": "Got the bitch takin’ shots like Reggie Miller", "vault_lines": ["Got the bitch takin' shots like Reggie Miller"], "meaning": "Reggie Miller was a Shooting Guard for the Indiana Pacers, who would go on to be inducted into the NBA Hall Of Fame.\n\nThe girl in this line is taking shots of strong alcohol, which are small glasses.\n\n\n\nJust like Reggie Miller took basketball shots on the court, which are attempts to score.", "annotation_id": "1614235", "url": "https://genius.com/1614235", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
