{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rax", "line": "Guns clap like patty-cake, Blood gang red bandana face Make them pussies pop they self, you can call that masturbate", "vault_lines": ["Guns clap like patty-cake, Blood gang red bandana face"], "meaning": "Another word for a wimp or punk, is a scaredy-cat, also known as a pussy. Since Wayne has guns and gang ties, his reputation alone might be enough to frighten his opps. They might even pop themselves because they are too afraid of Wayne.", "annotation_id": "35492528", "url": "https://genius.com/35492528", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rax", "line": "She let me into her jungle, I’m gonna hit her with that rattlesnake", "vault_lines": ["She let me into her jungle, I'm gonna hit her with that rattlesnake"], "meaning": "In this context, her jungle and that rattlesnake are euphemisms for female and male private parts.", "annotation_id": "35492485", "url": "https://genius.com/35492485", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rax", "line": "Hatin’-ass niggas be baller blockin’, actin’ like some goalkeepers", "vault_lines": ["Hatin'-ass niggas be baller blockin', actin' like some goalkeepers"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is a successful artist whose lifestyle could be compared to that of a ballplayer. Not everyone is happy about Wayne’s success and may prevent him from scoring more successes, much like a goalkeeper (goalie).", "annotation_id": "35492389", "url": "https://genius.com/35492389", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rax", "line": "I can’t fuck with ho niggas; I can’t trust these hoes, neither", "vault_lines": ["I can't fuck with ho niggas; I can't trust these hoes, neither"], "meaning": "In the way the words are used and expressed here, “fuck with” and “trust” are one in the same.", "annotation_id": "35492369", "url": "https://genius.com/35492369", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rax", "line": "Throw that pussy at me, bitch, I think I’m Babe Ruth", "vault_lines": ["Throw that pussy at me, bitch, I think I'm Babe Ruth"], "meaning": "Babe Ruth is regarded as America’s greatest baseball player of all time. In this line, Lil Wayne likens the way he hits pus*y to the way Babe Ruth hits the baseball.", "annotation_id": "25742372", "url": "https://genius.com/25742372", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rax", "line": "What’s up, redbone? What’s up, caramel?", "vault_lines": ["What's up, redbone? What's up, caramel?"], "meaning": "Red bone and Caramel are nicknames for his light-skinned ladies.\n\nRedbone is a light skinned black female. They are usually just a little bit darker than Yellow Bones (which are the lightest of black females and usually mixed with white) aka Caramel\n\n\n\nWayne loves his red bones", "annotation_id": "277026", "url": "https://genius.com/277026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rax", "line": "All my niggas strapped and ready to set it off: Queen Latifah", "vault_lines": ["All my niggas strapped and ready to set it off: Queen Latifah"], "meaning": "Set It Off is a 1996 movie with Queen Latifah.\n“Set it off” is a phrase that refers to making a splash/impact.\n\n\n\nThis is also a recycled line from his protégé. Drake’s line in in his 2010 single, “Over” is as follows:\n\nAbout to set it off in this bitch: Jada Pinkett", "annotation_id": "276499", "url": "https://genius.com/276499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rax", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-rax-lyrics", "genius_title": "Rax", "genius_id": 52247, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Raw", "line": "Y’all takin’ life and judgin’ Nick Cannon—that feel wrong", "vault_lines": ["Y'all takin' life and judgin' Nick Cannon—that feel wrong"], "meaning": "Rapsody points out the hypocrisy of people who partake in taking lives (which could be figurative) and yet judge Nick Cannon for having so many kids – twelve to be exact.", "annotation_id": "31791805", "url": "https://genius.com/31791805", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Raw", "line": "You a queen to me like Bohemian Rhapsody It’s Weezy and Rapsody—we runnin’ this shit, baby", "vault_lines": ["You a queen to me like Bohemian Rhapsody"], "meaning": "An easy one over here: Weezy plays with the names of the band that composed Bohemian Rhapsody, Queen, and the name of the rapper he is collaborating with.", "annotation_id": "31779787", "url": "https://genius.com/31779787", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Raw", "line": "Broke phone like Lamar—ooh, baby, I like it raw", "vault_lines": ["Broke phone like Lamar—ooh, baby, I like it raw"], "meaning": "Here Rapsody refers to the song “Rich Spirit” by Kendrick Lamar, the hook says:\n\n“Rich n***a, broke phone (Ah)\nTryna keep the balance, I’m stayin' strong (Ooh)”\n\nIt is also well known that Kendrick Lamar is someone who’s against smartphones and all the time they take up. To promote this lifestyle without distractions, he launched a cell phone with pgLang that’s “only a phone”, it has calls, alarms and messages without images, designed to be used as little as possible.\n\nRapsody and Kendrick Lamar have shown to have a good relationship, they first linked up on “Rock the Bells” from Rapsody’s 2011 mixtape For Everything. Almost 4 years later, Rapsody appeared on “Complexion (A Zulu Love)” from Kendrick’s critically acclaimed third studio album To Pimp a Butterfly, and then two years later in Laila’s Wisdom with “Power”.", "annotation_id": "31779693", "url": "https://genius.com/31779693", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Raw", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rapsody-raw-lyrics", "genius_title": "Raw", "genius_id": 10163764, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rari", "line": "She ask for the number and I told her, “Deuces”", "vault_lines": ["Shе ask for the number and I told her, \"Dеuces\""], "meaning": "“Deuces” is a another way of saying “goodbye”, referring to the two fingers held up when making the peace sign.\n\nAfter the hook-up expressed in the previous line, Weezy’s not interested in pursuing further relations.", "annotation_id": "36062418", "url": "https://genius.com/36062418", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rari", "line": "Like I’m Cochran", "vault_lines": ["All eyes on me like I'm the new Makaveli"], "meaning": "Johnnie Cochran is the lawyer that defended OJ Simpson. “Smoking Glove” much like the term “show me the smoking gun” means show me the proof of the murder because Cochran brought the Glove used to murder Nicole Brown to the trial saying “If it doesnt fit, you must aquit!\nThat ties in with the bar \"Smoking on that Gary Payton” which is a strain of marijuana by the brand Cookies followed by his nickname and the murder weapon The Glove.", "annotation_id": "35911770", "url": "https://genius.com/35911770", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rari", "line": "We family, nigga, Weezy F. for fine and dandy, nigga, been ballin’ Before Kobe went to prom with Brandy, nigga", "vault_lines": ["We family, nigga, Weezy F. for fine and dandy, nigga, been ballin'"], "meaning": "Weezy wee is stating that although Kross is not his son they still family, and he has him for life just as he has Cameron . He’s also stating he’s been getting to the money before 1996 which is the year Kobe took brandy to prom.", "annotation_id": "35832095", "url": "https://genius.com/35832095", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
