{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rap City Freestyle [2002]", "line": "Mommy like Wayne so she show a lean body We blow a lil’ blunt... and", "vault_lines": ["Mommy like Wayne so she show a lean body"], "meaning": "Mommy like Wayne so she show a lil' body\nWe blow a lil' Marley, got it in my pockets man\n\nMarley is bleeped out, but we can infer that a woman gets naked for Wayne and they smoke weed together", "annotation_id": "26766287", "url": "https://genius.com/26766287", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rap City Freestyle [2002]", "line": "You see me with my mob [?] posture I don’t play ball I play guard every dollar", "vault_lines": ["You see me with my mob [?] posture"], "meaning": "You see me with my Marbury posture\nI don’t play ball, I point guard every dollar\n\nWayne is posturing like Stephen Marbury, a prolific NBA point guard who played in the league from 1996 to 2009. Unlike Marbury, however, Wayne doesn’t play ball—he gets money and guards it.", "annotation_id": "26766274", "url": "https://genius.com/26766274", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rap City Freestyle [2002]", "line": "With the .40 Cal’ Ripken boy, rip a boy", "vault_lines": ["With the .40 Cal' Ripken boy, rip a boy"], "meaning": "The .40 Cal Ripken is a double entendre; .40 Cal is referring to a .40 Cal gun, and Cal Ripken is referencing the ex-MLB player from before. Wayne uses a .40 cal to “rip a boy” to shreds", "annotation_id": "26764225", "url": "https://genius.com/26764225", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Rap City Freestyle [2002]", "line": "I play the corner like Ripken boy", "vault_lines": ["I ain't trippin' boy, I play the corner like Ripken boy"], "meaning": "Wayne plays the street corner the same way that Cal Ripken Jr., an MLB hall-of-famer, played 3rd base (aka “the corner” in baseball).", "annotation_id": "26764200", "url": "https://genius.com/26764200", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
