{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "I’m flyer then a butterfly doing the tootsie roll", "vault_lines": ["I'm flyer then a butterfly doing the tootsie roll"], "meaning": "Tootsie Roll is a dance from the 90’s created by the 69 Boyz. Butterfly is a similar dance move, but the Tootsie Roll is where it’s at!", "annotation_id": "2803053", "url": "https://genius.com/2803053", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "Stunna man said kill em all, so still and all I’m a kill em all, murder them pussy hoes", "vault_lines": ["Stunna man said kill em all, so still and all"], "meaning": "#Kill ‘em\n\nBirdman (aka Stunna) told Wayne to kill everyone on the track. “Kill ‘em” is a figurative way of praising someone’s actions.", "annotation_id": "2481844", "url": "https://genius.com/2481844", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "All my niggas red flagging you could see we soo woo’n", "vault_lines": ["All my niggas red flagging you could see we soo woo'n"], "meaning": "Reference to the Bloods street gang. Their call is “soo woo”, a way to acknowledge each other. It’s a shoutout to his boss Lil Wayne, who often claims that he is a member of the gang (though actual bloods say otherwise)\n\nRed flagging refers to:\n\n\nThe red color of the Bloods, and flying their flag\nThe term “red flagging” means signaling danger, which Gudda implies is coming from the Young Money crew", "annotation_id": "2295187", "url": "https://genius.com/2295187", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "Young nigga, got my money running like Barry", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga, got my money running like Barry"], "meaning": "Having his money “running” is just a way of saying he has a lot of cash.\n\nReference to the great Barry Sanders, a Hall of Fame running back who played for the Detroit Lions in the 1990’s", "annotation_id": "2289367", "url": "https://genius.com/2289367", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "I’m who they’re looking to and who they’re looking for And numbers don’t lie, lieeeeee And numbers don’t lie, yeah Yea better hope your math is right", "vault_lines": ["I'm who they're looking to and who they're looking for"], "meaning": "People look to Wayne as a leader and many fans/paparazzi constantly look for him.\n\nPlay on words of “to” and “for” which represent the numbers 2 and 4. Wayne points out that numbers don’t lie, which supposedly validates the previous line.\n\nBut since numbers don’t lie, you better have the math right", "annotation_id": "2289363", "url": "https://genius.com/2289363", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "Haha, I got chips like the cookie dough", "vault_lines": ["Haha, I got chips like the cookie dough"], "meaning": "Referring to the chocolate chip variety of cookie dough which is baked into a delicious cookie\n\nChips and dough are also slang terms for money.", "annotation_id": "2289362", "url": "https://genius.com/2289362", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "And then we eat some chicken, you get no piece bitch", "vault_lines": ["And then we eat some chicken, you get no piece bitch"], "meaning": "Double Entendre:\n\n\nThey are not chicken (cowards/scared) and if you try them you will not get peace as a response.\nThey are eating chicken (the food) and you can’t have a piece of it because it is theirs.\n\n\n\nWayne and crew are getting their fair share of protein in this verse. First rappers, now chicken.", "annotation_id": "2289361", "url": "https://genius.com/2289361", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "Skipped class only class I knew, was S-Benz", "vault_lines": ["Skipped class only class I knew, was S-Benz"], "meaning": "Instead of going to his school classes he was worrying about was the Mercedes-Benz S-Class, a series of luxury cars\n\n\n\nTyga’s Mercedes-Benz SLS", "annotation_id": "2289360", "url": "https://genius.com/2289360", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "I am living the game, hitting the fades, quick cash", "vault_lines": ["I am living the game, hitting the fades, quick cash"], "meaning": "Double Entendre\n\n\n\n“The game” refers to both the rap game and the game of basketball, which he claims to be getting “quick cash” in both\n\n“Hitting the fades” refers to being high/drunk (getting faded) and the fadeaway jumper in basketball in which you shoot as you’re falling away from the basket", "annotation_id": "2289359", "url": "https://genius.com/2289359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "All brown maybach, you could say I’m yoohoo’n", "vault_lines": ["All brown maybach, you could say I'm yoohoo'n"], "meaning": "His brown Maybach\n\n\n\nIs a similar color to the chocolate drink Yoo-hoo", "annotation_id": "1504625", "url": "https://genius.com/1504625", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put on for the Game", "line": "And it takes a lot of paper to book a show You wouldn’t know cause you couldn’t know", "vault_lines": ["And it takes a lot of paper to book a show"], "meaning": "It costs a lot of money to not only book Wayne for a concert, but to spend on the actual production of the show. He also mentions that the average person would not know anything about that because he isn’t as famous/talented as Weezy\n\nThis is also a play on words with “paper” and “book” as a book has a lot of pages of paper that contain the story.", "annotation_id": "1094178", "url": "https://genius.com/1094178", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
