{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "And in that Lamborghini, I do donuts like Dunkins", "vault_lines": ["And in that Lamborghini, I do donuts like Dunkins"], "meaning": "Doing donuts in a car is when you swerve around in a circular motion leaving skid marks on the pavement. Dunkin' Donuts is a chain restaurant that sells donuts.", "annotation_id": "20452631", "url": "https://genius.com/20452631", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "I’m strapped like a bookbag So anyone of y’all can come on and get a foot tag", "vault_lines": ["I'm strapped like a bookbag"], "meaning": "To be “strapped” is slang for keeping a gun on you. A bookbag, or a backpack, is held up by straps that go around your shoulders keeping it on to you. Wayne is saying that he has his gun and is ready to kill anyone that wants problems with him. A foot tag is a piece of paper that goes on a corpse’s toe in a morgue when someone has died.", "annotation_id": "20439471", "url": "https://genius.com/20439471", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "Real talk, you niggas can’t guard me Two niggas can’t guard me, you looking at Jordan From the side, like Spike at the Garden I got the hardest bars, call me the warden", "vault_lines": ["Real talk, you niggas can't guard me"], "meaning": "Wayne compares himself to basketball player Michael Jordan, who is believed by some to be the greatest player of all time. Jordan was frequently guarded by more than one player and couldn’t be stopped from scoring. Spike Lee is a film director who is famously known for being a New York Knicks fan. Weezy says that people are watching him from the sidelines like Spike watches games at the Madison Square Garden which is the Knicks' home arena. A bar is a rap line. Wayne executes a double entendre in saying he has the hardest bars like how a prison has bars, stating that he is like the Warden.", "annotation_id": "20439458", "url": "https://genius.com/20439458", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "You know I’m out this world, I just bought a space shuttle I’ma put some D’s on that bitch", "vault_lines": ["You know I'm out this world, I just bought a space shuttle"], "meaning": "Wayne is so good that his skills are out of this world. He compares his skills to literally leaving Earth, as you would need a space shuttle to leave our world.", "annotation_id": "20439454", "url": "https://genius.com/20439454", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "Peyton Manning flow, I just go, no huddle", "vault_lines": ["Peyton Manning flow, I just go, no huddle"], "meaning": "Peyton Manning is an NFL quarterback considered to be one of the greatest quarterbacks of all time. He is known for running a play on the fly with no huddle or preparation time. Wayne is saying his flow is like Peyton Manning because he just goes in and starts spitting without any preparation.", "annotation_id": "20439441", "url": "https://genius.com/20439441", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "Make the homies say, “Ho,” and make all the girlies scream", "vault_lines": ["Make the homies say, \"Ho,\" and make all the girlies scream"], "meaning": "This line may have been influenced by Schoolly D’s Aqua Teen Hunger Force Theme. Its closing refrain:\n\nCause we are the Aqua Teens\nMake the homies say “ho” and the girlies wanna scream", "annotation_id": "18955483", "url": "https://genius.com/18955483", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "Pockets just fat like the Klumps and Norbit", "vault_lines": ["Pockets just fat like the Klumps and Norbit"], "meaning": "Weezy, even at the time of this song’s releasing, was already a multi-millionaire. Trying to fit that much cash in your pockets would no doubt stuff them to their max capacity, making them appear fat.\n\nWayne relates the fatness of pockets to morbidly obese Eddie Murphy characters the Klumps and Rasputia from Nutty Professor II: The Klumps (2000) and Norbit (2007), respectively.", "annotation_id": "17796967", "url": "https://genius.com/17796967", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "That’s my car, yup, vroom, errr", "vault_lines": ["That's my car, yup, vroom, errr"], "meaning": "He’s saying that cough syrup is his motivation or inspiration, or basically his drive when he’s rapping. Then he uses onomatopoeia to show that he is “driving” or currently being motivated.\n\nThe “urghhh” symbolizes him crashing, and the drugs losing their effect.", "annotation_id": "3485121", "url": "https://genius.com/3485121", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "Listen how my words are poetic like Langston", "vault_lines": ["Listen how my words are poetic like Langston"], "meaning": "Reference to the American Poet Langston Hughes. Wayne’s raps are as beautiful as Mr. Hughes' poetry.", "annotation_id": "2992961", "url": "https://genius.com/2992961", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "Just some Swishers and a whole bunch of cans of whoop-ass, haha", "vault_lines": ["Just some Swishers and a whole bunch of cans of whoop-ass, haha"], "meaning": "At the grocery store, he got some swishers to roll up his “greens”.\n\n\n\nAs well as some cans of whoop ass to hand out to other rappers.", "annotation_id": "2644739", "url": "https://genius.com/2644739", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "I break a bitch down like Tonya Harding", "vault_lines": ["I break a bitch down like Tonya Harding"], "meaning": "Harding is a notorious ice skater charged with conspiring to have her chief competitor, Nancy Kerrigan, hit on the knee with a crowbar. Later, in the Olympics, Harding placed 8th, while Kerrigan healed and earned a silver medal.", "annotation_id": "70814", "url": "https://genius.com/70814", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "I am a vegetarian, man, I only eat beats Wear a lot of carats and I smoke the best greens", "vault_lines": ["I am a vegetarian, man, I only eat beats"], "meaning": "Carrots means both carrot as in vegetable, and carat as in diamonds. 1 carat=200mg. Greens is also vegetable, and also weed.", "annotation_id": "68999", "url": "https://genius.com/68999", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Put Some Keys On That", "line": "Okay, I’m not a rookie, I’m a promethazine fiend", "vault_lines": ["Okay, I'm not a rookie, I'm a promethazine fiend"], "meaning": "Wordplay on the rookie-pro part. He actually says promethazine fiend, only the -methazine fiend is in the line under. Promethazine is a substance found in coughsirup that lil wayne used to be addicted to. fiend means addict.", "annotation_id": "63234", "url": "https://genius.com/63234", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
