{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "And if you on fire, you know the fireman can put out the fire, baby, baby", "vault_lines": ["And if you on fire, you know the fireman can put out the fire, baby, baby"], "meaning": "This is presumably a reference to his deleted track “Playing with Fire”.", "annotation_id": "41050226", "url": "https://genius.com/41050226", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "And I just stood over my stew and just blew And when there is no more you in the soup I remove my spoon and drink your juice", "vault_lines": ["And I just stood over my stew and just blew"], "meaning": "This extended metaphor likens the act of performing oral sex on a woman to eating a bowl of hot stew or soup.\n\nThe “stew” or “soup” represents the woman’s vagina, with the heat symbolizing her physical attractiveness and warmth.\n\nAnd I just stood over my stew and just blew\n\nStarting with preparation, a person blows on hot food to cool it down so it’s safe and comfortable to eat. Sexually, this is a euphemism for blowing air gently as a form of teasing or stimulation.\n\nAnd when there is no more you in the soup\n\nHere, the metaphor shifts to the consumption process. Once the soup’s main ingredients have been eaten, only the soup’s liquid base remains. Sexually, this is a euphemism for performing oral sex on a woman until she climaxes.\n\n I remove my spoon and drink your juice\n\nThe “spoon” symbolizes his tongue used as a tool for eating the “stew.” Removing the spoon means setting aside that method and switching to drinking directly from the bowl—consuming the remaining “juice” to finish off the “meal.”", "annotation_id": "38060928", "url": "https://genius.com/38060928", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "Pussy, pussy-pussy, pussy-pussy Pussy, pussy-pussy, pussy-pussy", "vault_lines": ["Put that pussy in my face every time I face you"], "meaning": "This is actually a nod to an obscure song!\n\nBefore he was in the Geto Boys, Willie D was already signed to Rap-A-Lot records and had put out his first solo LP, Controversy. The album’s 11th track, I Need Some Pussy has an eerily similar chorus.\n\nHear it for yourself:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_eKA9MO92xQ\n\nCoincidence? Nah. Weezy knows his Southern classics.", "annotation_id": "23751699", "url": "https://genius.com/23751699", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "Girl, you cold, let me suck out your flu", "vault_lines": ["Girl, you cold, let me suck out your flu"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne’s altruism really shows in this line, here he offers a rather dark imagery of sucking the flu ( “the illness” ) out of a girl, who is presumably his significant other. This can be compared to Kurt Cobain’s lyric in Heart Shaped Box “I wish I could eat your cancer when you turn black”.", "annotation_id": "17514487", "url": "https://genius.com/17514487", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "Lil’ Chris said ‘Run It’", "vault_lines": ["Lil' Chris said 'Run It'"], "meaning": "Reference to Chris Brown’s 2005 Billboard chart topper, Run It!\nWeezy is basically creating a football analogy, except the girl has been tackled for his night of fun", "annotation_id": "14555410", "url": "https://genius.com/14555410", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "Imagine if I did that with your pearl on my tongue", "vault_lines": ["Imagine if I did that with your pearl on my tongue"], "meaning": "“Pussy pearl” is slang for the female clitoris. (Cp., for example, 2 Live Crew’s “Pop That Pussy” from 1991).", "annotation_id": "14274076", "url": "https://genius.com/14274076", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "You heard of Salt N’ Pepa? Well, girl, you food", "vault_lines": ["You heard of Salt N' Pepa? Well, girl, you food"], "meaning": "Salt N' Pepa is a famous rap group.\n\n\n\nLil Wayne uses a play on their stage name.\nThis girl is “food” because he’s gonna eat her out.", "annotation_id": "6488778", "url": "https://genius.com/6488778", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "And I could make it rain, I’m the hurricane, son", "vault_lines": ["And I could make it rain, I'm the hurricane, son"], "meaning": "Triple Entendre\n\n\nWeezy makes enough money to ‘make it rain’ by throwing cash.\nTo go along with the fact that he’s “the hurricane, son”, he can make his girl’s vagina wet.\nHe also references his home town, New Orleans, which got hit with one of the most destructive hurricanes ever: Hurricane Katrina. If you read the line “I’m the hurricane(’s) son”, you can interpret it as Wayne saying the hurricane made him the person he is today, like a mother would. Very subtle seeing as what the whole idea of the song is much simpler than that.", "annotation_id": "2624411", "url": "https://genius.com/2624411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "P-L-A-Y because I don’t have a clue", "vault_lines": ["P-L-A-Y because I don't have a clue"], "meaning": "Wayne is referencing the commonly used method of performing oral sex on a woman by licking the alphabet on her clitoris with one’s tongue. If his methods weren’t working he goes back to that basic method.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Pt0WkGe6-oY", "annotation_id": "355658", "url": "https://genius.com/355658", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "And I’m a urban legend like a black Acura", "vault_lines": ["And I'm a urban legend like a black Acura"], "meaning": "As a celebrity from the inner city, Lil Wayne is an “urban legend.” Since there is an Acura model called a Legend, and “urban” is very often used as a euphemism for “black,” the two things he’s comparing mean the same thing in this context.", "annotation_id": "223089", "url": "https://genius.com/223089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "Because it’s the reason I am alive", "vault_lines": ["Because it's the reason I am alive"], "meaning": "Wayne admits to being a hedonist, i.e. he lives life in search of pleasure, which in this case comes in the form of oral sex.\n\n“P-U-S-S-Y” is also literally the reason he is alive, ie. vaginal birth.", "annotation_id": "75613", "url": "https://genius.com/75613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pussy Monster", "line": "Girl, you hot like a bowl of hot stew", "vault_lines": ["Girl, you hot like a bowl of hot stew"], "meaning": "A simile is a comparison using ‘like’ or ‘as.’  In this case Mr. Wayne is implying that this girl is hot (slang for attractive) in the same way that a bowl of warm stew is hot.  This topic sentence prepares the listener for the rest of the stanza.", "annotation_id": "65783", "url": "https://genius.com/65783", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
