{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Push", "line": "Okay, so after you back it up, just stop Now drop it like it’s hot, and pop it like a Glock", "vault_lines": ["Okay, so after you back it up, just stop"], "meaning": "These lines are referencing Lil Wayne’s classic outro on Juvenile’s “Back That Azz Up”\n\n“Now-now-now-now-now after you back it up then stop\nThen wha-wha-what, drop-drop it like it’s hot”\n\nLil Wayne has used this flow with similar lyrics many times throughout his career, even making an entire song based around this outro.\n\nhttps://genius.com/Lil-wayne-drop-it-like-its-hot-lyrics", "annotation_id": "19143543", "url": "https://genius.com/19143543", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Push", "line": "She said she wanna do it to the new Enrique I pop the disc in and put the song on replay", "vault_lines": ["I pop the disc in and put the song on replay"], "meaning": "Wayne’s girl said that she wants to have sex with him while they are playing Enrique Iglesias‘ album Insomniac, so he put the album on repeat.", "annotation_id": "4164573", "url": "https://genius.com/4164573", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Push", "line": "Mamma, I could help you get off, like the weekend", "vault_lines": ["Mamma, I could help you get off, like the weekend"], "meaning": "As Rebecca Black has stated in her infamous song, “gotta get down on Friday.” The weekend is a good time to just let lose. Except Lil' Wayne is suggesting that he and this woman he’s attracted to “let lose” in a sexual manor.\n\nIf you haven’t heard the song check it out! It’s an Illuminati cult classic!", "annotation_id": "2622538", "url": "https://genius.com/2622538", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Push", "line": "Hey mamma, they call me Weezy", "vault_lines": ["Hey mamma, they call me Weezy"], "meaning": "Lil' Wayne calls himself “Weezy” sometimes.\n\n\n\nThe nickname Weezy comes from a name for a drink that consists of ecstasy dissolved in wine. The ecstasy gets someone more passionate and the wine gets them looser, making a great drink before having sex.", "annotation_id": "2622534", "url": "https://genius.com/2622534", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Push", "line": "Baby, I could bless you when you ain’t even sneezing", "vault_lines": ["Baby, I could bless you when you ain't even sneezing"], "meaning": "It is common for people to say “Bless you” when someone sneezes. Lil Wayne is saying that he could bless here when she isn’t even sneezing. He exudes the presence of a holy man and just being around him could greatly benefit your well being.", "annotation_id": "2402857", "url": "https://genius.com/2402857", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
