{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "Tell the beef I mean business, suit and tie nigga", "vault_lines": ["Tell the beef I mean business, suit and tie nigga"], "meaning": "“I mean business” in figurative terms means that you are serious and aren’t playing around\nIn literal business, a suit and tie is often worn by people conducting business\nhttps://s3.amazonaws.com/filepicker-images-rapgenius/KIC4C2SWSaOLDQr0sx1d_images", "annotation_id": "25258487", "url": "https://genius.com/25258487", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "Thank God I’m fly, I had to thank my pilot", "vault_lines": ["Thank God I'm fly, I had to thank my pilot"], "meaning": "To be “fly” is to be cool or stylish. Planes literally fly and they have someone that steers the plane also known as the pilot.", "annotation_id": "20439515", "url": "https://genius.com/20439515", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "Trigger happy nigga, I just can’t stop smiling", "vault_lines": ["Trigger happy nigga, I just can't stop smiling"], "meaning": "To be “trigger happy” is to shoot your gun at the slightest reaction, or to be anxious to pull the trigger. Wayne compares being “trigger happy” to smiling and literally being happy.", "annotation_id": "20439514", "url": "https://genius.com/20439514", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "All these bitches think they dimes, watch me flip a coin", "vault_lines": ["All these bitches think they dimes, watch me flip a coin"], "meaning": "One of Weezy’s many metaphors. A “dime” is slang for an attractive woman. Weezy takes the “dime” slang and puts it together with the act of flipping a literal coin.", "annotation_id": "20439508", "url": "https://genius.com/20439508", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "Bring me his head, so I can make sure it’s him", "vault_lines": ["Bring me his head, so I can make sure it's him"], "meaning": "In ancient times, when rulers would place a bounty on someone’s head, bounty hunters sometimes decapitated the person’s head to bring back as evidence of the identity to claim their prize.\n\nWayne put a hit out on people who are sending threats, and he wants the head as confirmation.", "annotation_id": "13595055", "url": "https://genius.com/13595055", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "You see, I’m armed like a fucking short sleeve shirt!", "vault_lines": ["You see, I'm armed like a fucking short sleeve shirt!"], "meaning": "“Arms” is slang for weaponry such as guns.\n\n\n\nWhen wearing a short sleeve shirt your arms can be seen, just like how you can see that Wayne is “armed”.\n\nThis is very similar to a certain classic Jay-Z line.", "annotation_id": "2812004", "url": "https://genius.com/2812004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "They tell me “Go to Hell,” Okay, I know the owner", "vault_lines": ["They tell me \"Go to Hell,\" Okay, I know the owner"], "meaning": "People are always hating on Wayne, even to extremes such as wishing death on him.\n\nWeezy just brushes this off by saying he’s got family everywhere. This could also be a reference to fellow friend and rapper Lil B’s song I Am The Devil.", "annotation_id": "2615324", "url": "https://genius.com/2615324", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "It’s loaded, so I just let her jump the gun", "vault_lines": ["It's loaded, so I just let her jump the gun"], "meaning": "Metaphor:\n\nAt a track meet, the runners start the race at the sound of the gun. To “jump the gun” is to false start and leave before the gun has sounded.\n\nTrack starting gun = Weezy’s weenie\nThe gun (his dick) is “loaded” (uhh…ready) so he lets her jump the gun (start early)", "annotation_id": "2231869", "url": "https://genius.com/2231869", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "You and all your dogs could get euthanize, nigga", "vault_lines": ["You and all your dogs could get euthanize, nigga"], "meaning": "Euthanizing animals means killing them. Word play on killing you and your crew.\n\n\n\nTies into the previous line references his dogs being off the leashes.", "annotation_id": "2196536", "url": "https://genius.com/2196536", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "I’m a movie motherfucker, camera man, are you getting this?", "vault_lines": ["I'm a movie motherfucker, camera man, are you getting this?"], "meaning": "Rappers with insane amounts of money often compare their life to an actual movie. They usually start with the phrase “my life is a movie”. Wayne adopts this phrase, and cleverly changes it up to a personification of a metaphorical cameraman.", "annotation_id": "2179918", "url": "https://genius.com/2179918", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "We be passing blunts, they be passing judgement", "vault_lines": ["We be passing blunts, they be passing judgement"], "meaning": "In this case, the word “passing” has two completely different meanings.\n\nWayne and his homies are passing blunts, physically.\nThe haters are passing judgement (talking shit about them).", "annotation_id": "2179911", "url": "https://genius.com/2179911", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "D5, what up five?", "vault_lines": ["D5, what up five?"], "meaning": "D5 = Dedication 5\n\nWhen he says “What up five?”, he’s talking about the man he treats like his father, Birdman aka Stunnaman aka Brrrman", "annotation_id": "2172069", "url": "https://genius.com/2172069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "Mac so paid we ’bout to start calling him Macintosh", "vault_lines": ["Mac so paid we 'bout to start calling him Macintosh"], "meaning": "Weezy is saying that his homie Mack Maine is getting so much money that he’s going to start calling him “Macintosh”.\n\nThe Macintosh is a personal computer made by Apple (a very well-known and wealthy company, obviously).", "annotation_id": "2172045", "url": "https://genius.com/2172045", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "This change of face on my Rollie, shout out Lil Kim", "vault_lines": ["This change of face on my Rollie, shout out Lil Kim"], "meaning": "Lil Kim got a lot of plastic surgery on her face, hence “changing the face” of his Rollie. Lil Kim and Tiffany Foxx (Lil Kim’s new artist) were not impressed to hear this line.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LilKim/statuses/374324454698254336\n\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/1tiffanyfoxx/statuses/374230485607907329", "annotation_id": "2171452", "url": "https://genius.com/2171452", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "Burning blunts like bridges, turn up, missing", "vault_lines": ["Burning blunts like bridges, turn up, missing"], "meaning": "Tunechi adds a different look on the phrase “don’t burn bridges” by comparing his burning of blunts to people’s burning of bridges. He continues by saying the hype phrase “turn up” but switches by explaining the only turning up you’ll be doing is missing.", "annotation_id": "2171300", "url": "https://genius.com/2171300", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "She said she trying to see me, bitch that’s Stevie Wonderful", "vault_lines": ["She said she trying to see me, bitch that's Stevie Wonderful"], "meaning": "Clever word play. Weezy’s thinks that the act of the woman wanting to see him is “wonderful” but he doesn’t want to see her the same way Stevie Wonderful aka Stevie Wonder can’t see due to the fact he’s blind.\n\nEven Stevie notices the wordplay.\n\n\n\nNot the first time Wayne has used Stevie Wonder in his wordplay", "annotation_id": "2171249", "url": "https://genius.com/2171249", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "I think I’m ’bout to jump, niggas phony as a prop", "vault_lines": ["I think I'm 'bout to jump, niggas phony as a prop"], "meaning": "Props are objects used in movies or plays and are generally fake, ie. a bowl of fruits used for decoration. Tunechi wants to get away from the phony people around him so he might jump from the top.", "annotation_id": "2171226", "url": "https://genius.com/2171226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "YMCMB, the world is ours, seconds, minutes", "vault_lines": ["YMCMB, the world is ours, seconds, minutes"], "meaning": "Wayne uses the words “ours” and “hours” as homophones here. He’s saying that the world belongs to his team, every second and every minute of the day.", "annotation_id": "2171216", "url": "https://genius.com/2171216", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pure Colombia", "line": "It’s just us, fuck the rest, we got insomnia", "vault_lines": ["It's just us, fuck the rest, we got insomnia"], "meaning": "Play on words, Weezy uses both definitions of the word rest. “Fuck the rest,” meaning forget everyone else and “fuck the rest,” meaning forget sleep. Someone who has insomnia can’t sleep, so they practically say “fuck rest.”\n\n\n\nUsing coke will also give you insomnia which ties into the line above this.", "annotation_id": "2171211", "url": "https://genius.com/2171211", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
