{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "You the always-call-your-brother type", "vault_lines": ["You the always-call-your-brother type"], "meaning": "They are saying anyone they come up against is too scared to handle things on their own. They are too scared to fight them so they have to call backup.", "annotation_id": "24270994", "url": "https://genius.com/24270994", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Read a scripture out your movie, get a picture, I’m a-zoomin", "vault_lines": ["Read a scripture out your movie, get a picture, I'm a-zoomin"], "meaning": "Clever word play here, a scripture is a holy text but when used here with the use of movie Wayne flips it to mean a script which is used to write out the plot of a movie first. He then follows it by saying “get a picture” a movie being a motion picture as well as meaning get an idea “get the big picture”. He finishes with saying “I’m a-zoomin” meaning hes going off but also zooming as in zooming in a picture finishing off the scheme.", "annotation_id": "20283540", "url": "https://genius.com/20283540", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "With “Pull Up to My Bumper” playin’", "vault_lines": ["With \"Pull Up to My Bumper\" playin'"], "meaning": "“Pull Up to the Bumper” is a 1981 single by Jamaican singer Grace Jones. It was released as the third single from her fifth album, Nightclubbing.\n\n“Pull Up to the Bumper” was also covered by Jamaican reggae singer Patra in 1995 for her second album Scent of Attraction.\n\nCoolio sampled the song on his 1997 single “Ooh La La”, from the album My Soul.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Tc1IphRx1pk\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xSEGmIrR_xY\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yX60WIkXDio", "annotation_id": "20254565", "url": "https://genius.com/20254565", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Everything I’m driving is new, improved", "vault_lines": ["Everything I'm driving is new, improved"], "meaning": "Taking a trick from his mentor, Euro brags about his cars. “New and improved” is usually to describe an upgrade of something, in this case a car.\n\nEuro also plays on the title of the song…“Pull Up”. It’s usually to describe a shooting, but you can also pull up in a car.", "annotation_id": "7451732", "url": "https://genius.com/7451732", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Shifty eyes, I see four", "vault_lines": ["Shifty eyes, I see four"], "meaning": "“Shifty eyes” is having the appearance of being dishonest, especially as signified by a lack of eye. It could also simply imply a sign of disinterest.\n\nSince Euro has shifty eyes, he adds a pun of seeing four, which sounds the same as C4. He is referencing to C4, Tha Carter IV, which is the 9th studio album of Lil Wayne.\n\n\n\nThis line is also a continuation to the last line. While the gun is in the person’s mouth, if they get shifty eyes, he will C4. That means he will cause the gun to explode.", "annotation_id": "7241605", "url": "https://genius.com/7241605", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "But fuck it man, like what you sayin’? Look, I’m not sayin’, but I’m just sayin’", "vault_lines": ["You do you, I'ma do what it do"], "meaning": "A reference to naturally aggressive warriors in the anime, Dragon Ball Z.\n\nA quite clever use of homophone, “Saiyan/sayin'”, Wayne is not a “Saiyan”, but he’s just saying as to make the point he shouldn’t be messed with.", "annotation_id": "7238623", "url": "https://genius.com/7238623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Flip them pies like D. Dawes", "vault_lines": [", flip them pies like D. Dawes"], "meaning": "Reference to Dominique Dawes, a retired American artistic gymnast.\n\nEuro plays on words here. Pie is a kilo of coke, and flipping them is making a profit out of them. Similarly to how D. Dawes flip, or do acrobatic moves to make a profit, Euro flips kilos of cocaine.", "annotation_id": "7232401", "url": "https://genius.com/7232401", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "So if you wanna meet, nigga, I’m a butcher If you wanna beef, nigga, I’m a butcher", "vault_lines": ["So if you wanna meet, nigga, I'm a butcher"], "meaning": "A butcher is a person who may slaughter animals, dress their flesh, sell their meat or do any combination of these three tasks.\n\nOnce again Wayne uses homophones “meet” and “meat” to let his foes know that he will meet up and treat the beef like a butcher. On the other hand, Wayne lets his foes know that if you have beef with him? The beef he brings is like a butcher’s.", "annotation_id": "7228133", "url": "https://genius.com/7228133", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "I been Piru, I’m in my mood So you know what you can do?", "vault_lines": ["You do you, I'ma do what it do"], "meaning": "Wayne affiliates himself with the Piru Blood gang in Compton. Flow, mentioned previously, is allegedly a full blown Piru member, and is not too impressed with Thug’s Instagram posturing.", "annotation_id": "7225496", "url": "https://genius.com/7225496", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Police find you in the bayou With your friends by you and your shit knocked loose", "vault_lines": ["Police find you in the bayou"], "meaning": "A classic throwback to Wayne’s “Get ‘Em” off his much lauded Dedication 2 mixtape.\n\n“I think they sipping on that ‘I Can Fuck With Him Juice’\nTest me if ya wanna bet, man I knock a limb loose”.", "annotation_id": "7225488", "url": "https://genius.com/7225488", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Hear you niggas talking about what you gon’ do or might do I invite you, I entice you, but I advise you not to God bless you like “Achoo”", "vault_lines": ["You do you, I'ma do what it do"], "meaning": "The whole song is a not so subliminal diss towards Young Thug and Rich Gang, who had a track on their Tha Tour Part 1 mixtape entitled “Pull Up”.\n\nDeeper than that, Thug threatened Wayne in a series of instagram posts and concert appearances, brandishing weapons, which culminated in the shooting of Wayne’s tour bus.\n\nWayne’s penchant for hair triggers means him and his goons have itchy fingers, and even the slightest provocation, a sneeze for example, can set them off.", "annotation_id": "7225462", "url": "https://genius.com/7225462", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Light blue Michael Jordans, my shoe get checks like “Swoosh”", "vault_lines": ["Light blue Michael Jordans, my shoe get checks like \"Swoosh\""], "meaning": "In December 2014, Nike caused a stir when they released their Air Jordan 11 Retro Legend Blue, throwing back to the mid 90s when the colour was first introduced.\n\nMere mortals would have to pay $200 for the privilege of owning a pair, but Wayne gets his own Jordan’s. Wearing shoes for him is just another revenue stream.\n\nHis shoe game is wicked enough that those around him are always checking on his style.", "annotation_id": "7225446", "url": "https://genius.com/7225446", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Young nigga ridin’ in a V-1-2", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga ridin' in a V-1-2"], "meaning": "V-12 is an engine with twelve cylinders and pistons arranged in a v formation. As he explained on “Trigger Finger”, he bought himself an “R and R”: a Rolls Royce Phantom, which has a V12 engine. He allegedly also owns an Aston Martin Vanquish, another V12 powered vehicle.", "annotation_id": "7225369", "url": "https://genius.com/7225369", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Smoking nothing but Irene", "vault_lines": ["Smoking nothing but Irene"], "meaning": "Irene is a strain of kush (high grade marijuana) that has a particularly sour smell, and was made famous by Soulja Boy.", "annotation_id": "7225337", "url": "https://genius.com/7225337", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "I got Jays at my door I got shooters on my team", "vault_lines": ["I got bitches on my dick"], "meaning": "“J’s at my door” refers to junkies, implying Euro lives in the trap house. In fact, the trap house is the studio, and the cocaine he is cooking up is music.\n\nEuro can further claim shooters on his team after labelmate Flow was arrested for a double homocide in which he allegedly shot and killed two brothers.", "annotation_id": "7225310", "url": "https://genius.com/7225310", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Got a big house with a green lawn Got a cigar full of neon Like my ho cold and my tea warm", "vault_lines": ["Got a big house with a green lawn"], "meaning": "Wayne’s mansion is vast, and his “green lawn” also helps him keep his blunt full of “neon”: hallucinogenic substances.\n\n\n\nAn avid tea drinker, he is also referring to dinner, as no-one likes cold tea. A cold girl though? That’s a challenge.", "annotation_id": "7225279", "url": "https://genius.com/7225279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "My dead Presidents reborn", "vault_lines": ["My dead Presidents reborn"], "meaning": "Wayne uses some interesting wordplay, calling his money “dead presidents” and saying they are “reborn”. He implies that the dead president is reborn because his face appears on money and he still is useful and lives on through it. Wayne is bragging about his money and this is definitely not the first time.", "annotation_id": "7223736", "url": "https://genius.com/7223736", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Got a bitch with good hygiene I’m sick with it, no vaccine", "vault_lines": ["Got a bitch with good hygiene"], "meaning": "Vaccine are used to fight against illness. Yet another variation on the “sick” brag that hip hop does so well.\n\nHis girl is clean and healthy, so he isn’t getting it from her. It must be coming from within, and since he isn’t vaccinated, it makes it even worse.", "annotation_id": "7222721", "url": "https://genius.com/7222721", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Nigga, that’s what you’ll get like Ken and Ryu", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, that's what you'll get like Ken and Ryu"], "meaning": "It is a reference to the original animated street fighter in which Ken and Ryu (“with your friends by you”) were fighting Bison in the bayou (“find you in the bayou”) and while losing were tossed on the ground together in defeat (“with your shit knocked loose”).\n\nKen and Ryu are also 2 characters from fighting game series “Street Fighter”, and “What you’ll get” sounds similar to the “Hadouken” fireball that has become a staple of the Street Fighter franchise.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I056MPrakoQ", "annotation_id": "7222503", "url": "https://genius.com/7222503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "All my goons be too enthused So don’t open your mouth like you’re chewing glue", "vault_lines": ["All my goons be too enthused"], "meaning": "Wayne’s goons are all eager to kill you, so Wayne advises you to not talk.\n\nHe refers to chewing glue, as glue is sticky and if one were to chew glue, they wouldn’t be able to open their mouth.", "annotation_id": "7222063", "url": "https://genius.com/7222063", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "D-boy, D-boy, D-boy My pockets look Keloid", "vault_lines": ["My pockets look Keloid"], "meaning": "D-boy is a possible reference to his 13th track off Tha Carter II, featuring Birdman. D-boy is a street slang for dope boy or drug dealer.\n\nKeloid scar is a result of an overgrowth of granulation tissue, and looks like a bubble. Lil Wayne depicts how excessive his pockets look like, as an abnormal scar.", "annotation_id": "7220849", "url": "https://genius.com/7220849", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Bout it, bout it, bout it like hoody-hoo", "vault_lines": ["Bout it, bout it, bout it like hoody-hoo"], "meaning": "Following Lil Wayne’s reference to “Bout it Bout it”, Euro adds another reference to TRU’s track, “Hoody Hoo”.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A3yLiTEkDaI", "annotation_id": "7220135", "url": "https://genius.com/7220135", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "’Bout it, ’bout it, ’bout it like T-R-U", "vault_lines": ["'Bout it, 'bout it, 'bout it like T-R-U"], "meaning": "A reference to “Bout it, Bout it”, which is a song by Tru from No Limit.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jxi0VIEjP78", "annotation_id": "7220130", "url": "https://genius.com/7220130", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "Chop bricks like karate, judo, kung fu Like jiu-jitsu, split a brick in two", "vault_lines": ["Chop bricks like karate, judo, kung fu"], "meaning": "Wayne makes a simile on how he cuts cocaine bricks to the multiple types of bricks that the martial arts trainers use as a training method.\n\nJiu Jitso is another martial art that uses the least amount of effort to cause the most amount of pain. It is one of the best forms of self defense as it is as effective from someone not as physically capable as someone who is in prime condition.\n\nAlso a reference to Future’s standout banger, “Karate Chop”, with Wayne also being a remix of the track.\n\nChoppin' bricks like karate", "annotation_id": "7220069", "url": "https://genius.com/7220069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "line": "I been out here since P had the hook up", "vault_lines": ["I been out here since P had the hook up"], "meaning": "Reference to Master P’s movie and soundtrack, I Got The Hook Up, which came out in 1998. In 98' Wayne was still a Hot Boy on Cash Money, decades later Wayne is still here and standing strong.", "annotation_id": "7220056", "url": "https://genius.com/7220056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pull Up", "status": "done", "targets": 25, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-pull-up-lyrics", "genius_title": "Pull Up", "genius_id": 2164332, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Public Announcement", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-public-announcement-lyrics", "genius_title": "Public Announcement", "genius_id": 3434819, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Psycho", "line": "I go hard for my baby Psycho ward for my baby", "vault_lines": ["Bodyguard for my baby"], "meaning": "Weezy uses a basic “hard” double entendre. Not only does he go hard on the mic, but Wayne also goes hard in the bed.\n\nPsychiatric hospitals (psych wards) are used for serious, hard patients. Wayne’s lust is so strong, that he could be placed in one of these facilities.\n\nThis may also be a subliminal reference to his “Krazy” music video which took place in a mental institution.", "annotation_id": "7434644", "url": "https://genius.com/7434644", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Psycho", "line": "Lock it down for my baby I knock that pussy out and then I growl for my baby", "vault_lines": ["Swipe that card for my baby"], "meaning": "Borrowing from his single “Rich As Fuck”, rappers seem to have gotten the idea in their head that “beating up pussy”, or being so aggressive that sex actually hurts, is an enjoyable, pleasurable experience.\n\nClumsy wordplay on the word “pussy”, Wayne likens himself to an animal to further deepen the attraction between the two, adding a primal aspect to their relationship.", "annotation_id": "7343016", "url": "https://genius.com/7343016", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Psycho", "line": "Jump without a parachute, I’m crazy", "vault_lines": ["Jump without a parachute, I'm crazy"], "meaning": "Throughout this song, Wayne believes love is a drug that drives people crazy, which could be scientifically true. Relating to the song title, Psycho, Weezy relates jumping without a parachute to how crazy he is about her.\n\nParachutes basically aid a person from having a hard hit onto the ground when jumping from something usually high up in the sky.", "annotation_id": "7227326", "url": "https://genius.com/7227326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Psycho", "line": "Girl, I’m so crazy for you I left my old lady for you Now she done went crazy You know she be hatin’ on you Say she gon’ be waitin’ for me Well, she gon’ be waitin’ ’Cause she know I’m crazy ’bout you", "vault_lines": ["Girl, I'm so crazy for you"], "meaning": "Waynes not so rumoured girlfriend Christina Milian has provoked the ire of his “fiancée” Dhea recently, and the two have engaged in a subliminal Instagram battle, with Dhea turning up to Wayne concerts unaccompanied and posting photos of the evening.", "annotation_id": "7225178", "url": "https://genius.com/7225178", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Psycho", "line": "Even psychos need love too I save all her text messages I smell her panties while she in the bathroom And taste whatever she left in them I take pictures of her when she not lookin’ Study ’em microscopically Marry me and then bury me And then bury her on top of me, I’m", "vault_lines": ["Even psychos need love too"], "meaning": "It’s normally women tainted with the psycho tag, but Wayne flips it and describes a series of uncomfortable actions that a normal person would consider unhealthy.\n\nWayne lists a number of slightly excessive actions, including panty sniffing (and, apparently, panty tasting), and taking pictures whilst his girl is asleep so he can view them at his leisure.\n\nThe antithesis of his song “Single,” which described the actions of a girlfriend who had become way too attached.", "annotation_id": "7225168", "url": "https://genius.com/7225168", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Psycho", "line": "I’m just tryna kick it wit’ ya And I don’t even know karate But I know cr-azy", "vault_lines": ["I'm just tryna kick it wit' ya"], "meaning": "Weezy is trying to kick it with her (hang out) but he doesn’t even know karate, the art of self defense which relies heavily on kicking.\n\nHe is such a psycho he is unable to chill properly with his girl, always ruining things and getting worked up. Also, karate can be violent as can psychos.\n\n“I don’t even know karate, but I know crazy” is a reference to the James Brown song named “The Payback”. Also, another reference to “Krazy”.", "annotation_id": "7221927", "url": "https://genius.com/7221927", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Psycho", "line": "I fell asleep in it like Whitney", "vault_lines": ["I fell asleep in it like Whitney"], "meaning": "A reference to Whitney Houston’s death on February 11, 2012 in Beverly Hills. She was found dead, submerged in a bathtub.\n\nCompleting the reference, Bobby Brown has been referred to as crazy, meaning Wayne is “crazy” for his girl. The two were married.", "annotation_id": "7219923", "url": "https://genius.com/7219923", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
