{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Prostitute 2", "line": "[Chorus] I wouldn’t care if you was a prostitute And that you hit every man that you ever knew See, it wouldn’t make a difference if that was way before me and you, girl And you don’t never have to worry about me, long as you keep it real Whatever’s on your mind, speak on how you feel Stay truthful to me and never lie to me And don’t you ever keep no secrets, no matter whatever", "vault_lines": ["Um, I wouldn't care if you was a prostitute"], "meaning": "The hook is lyrics from Musiq Soulchild’s ‘'You and Me\" (2000) where he sings about his undying love for a woman regardless of what people think about her.", "annotation_id": "32104616", "url": "https://genius.com/32104616", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Prostitute 2", "line": "Um, I wouldn’t care if you was a prostitute And that you hit every man that you ever knew You see, it wouldn’t make a difference if that was way before me and you, girl", "vault_lines": ["Um, I wouldn't care if you was a prostitute"], "meaning": "This line is borrowed from Musiq Soulchild’s song “You And Me\n\nBasically he’s being as forgiving as a man could be towards a girl with a sordid past.", "annotation_id": "218643", "url": "https://genius.com/218643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
