{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Prostitute", "line": "[Chorus: Lil Wayne] I wouldn’t care if you were a prostitute And that you hit every man that you ever knew See it wouldn’t make a difference If that was way before me and you girl See you don’t ever have to worry about me As long as you keep it real Whatever is on your mind, speak on how you feel Stay true to me and never lie to me And don’t ever keep no secrets no matter whatever Girl you know what I mean (yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I wouldn't care if you were a prostitute"], "meaning": "The hook is lyrics from Musiq Soulchild’s ‘'You and Me\" (2000) where he sings about his undying love for a woman regardless of what people think about her.", "annotation_id": "2718601", "url": "https://genius.com/2718601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Prostitute", "line": "I’ll give up the game At the top of the arena there’s my jersey wit my name", "vault_lines": ["At the top of the arena there's my jersey wit my name"], "meaning": "Wayne is using this line to state that he would quit rap for this girl; however, at the same time he is boasting about his rap skills by making the jersey reference.\n\nWhen particularly talented athletes retire, the team they played for hangs a banner or jersey (depending on the sport) and retires their number from future use to acknowledge their unique skill. By retiring their number, the athlete is being recognized as an unmatchable talent; no one else deserves their number.\n\nWayne is making the claim that he is such a uniquely talented rapper that he would receive a similar honour if he ever retired.  It also serves as a claim that no one else will ever be able to match his particular talents (or even try to).", "annotation_id": "1023058", "url": "https://genius.com/1023058", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
