{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Project Bitch", "line": "[Verse 3: Juvenile]", "vault_lines": ["This is for Deshawn, Eshlawn, Lil Mama, an her friends"], "meaning": "In the edited and music video version Juvenile’s verse is replaced with a verse by B.G.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b6CpYP4cfC0&t=124s", "annotation_id": "29347107", "url": "https://genius.com/29347107", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Project Bitch", "line": "[Chorus: Juvenile]", "vault_lines": ["This is for Deshawn, Eshlawn, Lil Mama, an her friends"], "meaning": "Turk was originally supposed to do the chorus as it comes from his line in the Hot Boy$ song “I Need A Hot Girl”.\n\nIn September 2014, Mannie Fresh told Complex:\n\nThe ‘Project Chick’ line, we got that from ‘I Need a Hot Girl.’ Whenever Turk said that line, the crowd went crazy. I’m like, ‘I don’t know what it is about that line, but we need to turn that into a hook.’\n\nHe also said:\n\nWhen we did ‘Project Chick’ the hook was supposed to be Turk, the line came from him. But he didn’t show up and Juvi was like, ‘I got that. Don’t worry about it.’ [Laughs.]", "annotation_id": "29347005", "url": "https://genius.com/29347005", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Project Bitch", "line": "I bought them shoes, them tattoos, and even fixed yo breasts I put you inside the flyest rides and put a “S” on yo’ chest", "vault_lines": ["I bought them shoes, them tattoos, and even fixed yo breasts"], "meaning": "Mannie Fresh would often try to make his music portray a positive outlook on his life as opposed to the references to violence and gang activity that the other artists of “Cash Money Records” mentioned. He would rap about how well he treated the women he liked and about all of the stuff he would buy them. In this case, he’s giving a woman the full “Cash Money” treatment, consisting of new shoes, tattoos, breast implants, and Cash Money’s signature “S on yo chest.” This refers to the big and expensive looking pendants that the Cash Money crew wore in many of their videos. Mannie giving one to a girl symbolizes allowing her into the Cash Money clique. The name also pays homage to Superman’s costume, which had a large “S” printed across the chest.", "annotation_id": "6716030", "url": "https://genius.com/6716030", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Project Bitch", "line": "She was still-un, I spared her because her chil-drun", "vault_lines": ["She was still-un, I spared her because her chil-drun"], "meaning": "She was going through Juve’s wallet when he was passed out after they had sex. He let it slide on account of her being a single mother.", "annotation_id": "2195668", "url": "https://genius.com/2195668", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Project Bitch", "line": "Give me three minutes, maybe four she be wantin to marry a nigga", "vault_lines": ["Give me three minutes, maybe four she be wantin to marry a nigga"], "meaning": "This is a line from Smokey in Friday that Wayne borrowed here\n\nSmokey: Man, man, MAN. Her momma got an ass too. Just give me three and a half minutes… maybe even four. She’ll be wantin’ to marry a nigga!\nCraig: Who, her momma?\nSmokey: Yeah! Older the berry, the sweeter the juice.\nCraig: I think it’s the blacker the berry, the sweeter the juice.\nSmokey: Yeah, yeah, well she blacker than a motherfucka too.", "annotation_id": "386863", "url": "https://genius.com/386863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Project Bitch", "line": "My mama send me by my grandma, my grandma flipped out And said we ain’t gone have no evil in this house", "vault_lines": ["My mama send me by my grandma, my grandma flipped out"], "meaning": "Juv’s mom sent him off to live with his nana. Presumably because he was living too wild. Grandma told him to tone down his scandalous ways or he’d have to leave.", "annotation_id": "247405", "url": "https://genius.com/247405", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
