{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Problems", "line": "Better get up and stand up like Bob Marley", "vault_lines": ["Better get up and stand up like Bob Marley"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Bob Marley & the Wailers‘ 1975 song “Get up, stand up.” This is not the first time Wayne has mentioned Marley in his music, with the line:\n\nLegendary like Bob Marley\n\non the song “Not Like Me” off of his 1999 debut album Tha Block is Hot.", "annotation_id": "15467978", "url": "https://genius.com/15467978", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
