{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pretty Lil’ Heart", "line": "Don’t need a rocket scientist to see that you and I are meant", "vault_lines": ["Don’t need a rocket scientist to see that you and I are meant"], "meaning": "The exclamation “it’s not rocket science” is often used to say that something isn’t difficult. Lil Wayne knows that it’s clear as day that him and this person should be together but he goes further making it a double entendre by pronouncing “are meant” like “emit” as in “to throw or give off or out” such as rockets emitting downward force in order to take off, something a rocket scientist would know all about.", "annotation_id": "27815704", "url": "https://genius.com/27815704", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
