{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "Okay, we see you in your Phantom acting cocky with your misses Yeah, you balling till you see us pull up in nine of them bitches, putting", "vault_lines": ["Okay, we see you in your Phantom acting cocky with your misses"], "meaning": "The Rolls-Royce Phantom is a model of an expensive luxury car.  Busta Rhymes is insinuating that a lesser rapper than himself would feel proud and accomplished driving such a car with a beautiful woman at his side.  Furthermore, such a rapper would start acting cocky and arrogant.\n\nWhile such a feat may initially seem impressive, it pales when compared to the accomplishments of one of the greatest rappers, such as Busta Rhymes.  He and his crew pull up in nine of said vehicle all with beautiful womem in them, making the lesser rapper’s accomplishment seem petty and quaint.\n\nThus putting pressure upon the lesser rapper and demonstrating their inferiority.", "annotation_id": "4094869", "url": "https://genius.com/4094869", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "Pressure bust pipes, but Weezy bust twice", "vault_lines": ["Pressure bust pipes, but Weezy bust twice"], "meaning": "This line references a rather popular sports quote often attributed to now retired basketball player Robert Horry.\n\n\n\n“Pressure can burst a pipe or pressure can make a diamond”\n\nContinuing his string of double entendres, Lil' Wayne is using some clever wordplay to insinuate two meanings:\n\n1) The literal pressure bursting a pipe, as referenced by the above quote.  This also has connotations of greatness since in the above quote Lil' Wayne would be likening himself to the diamond.  Meaning he is something exceptional and of great value.\n\n2) “Pipe” used as slang for a man’s penis.  “Pressure” would be the pressure a woman’s vaginal walls put upon a man’s penis during intercourse.  Finally “bust” as a shorted form of the phrase “bust a nut”, meaning to ejaculate.\n\nIn essence he is saying that he has such great sexual prowess he is capable of ejaculating twice before he is finished with sex.", "annotation_id": "4094558", "url": "https://genius.com/4094558", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "Young Casanova, I bend their asses over", "vault_lines": ["Young Casanova, I bend their asses over"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is likening himself to Giacomo Casanova.  An adventurer and author of the 18th century.  He became so famous for his elaborate and often complicated affairs with women that his name has become synonymous with “womanizer”.", "annotation_id": "4094042", "url": "https://genius.com/4094042", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "She say my dick stronger than a six-pack of Cola", "vault_lines": ["She say my dick stronger than a six-pack of Cola"], "meaning": "Double meaning:\n\n\nIf you drink a 6-pack of cola really fast, it will most likely affect you and be a very strong change of feel.\nOr the 6-pack of a man is tend to be seen as a strong buff person, where a 6-pack of cola is hard because it’s canned. The wordplay is all about being a hard 6-pack.\n\n\n\nEither way he means his dick is hard and strong.", "annotation_id": "1013593", "url": "https://genius.com/1013593", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "Quicker than a leopard on ’em", "vault_lines": ["Swag with no effort on 'em, quicker than a leopard on 'em"], "meaning": "Leopards are known to go fast as hell to kill and hunt.\n\nNot as fast as a cheetah… but still faster than you.", "annotation_id": "1013592", "url": "https://genius.com/1013592", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "Young Money the special team, we so Devin Hester on ’em", "vault_lines": ["Young Money the special team, we so Devin Hester on 'em"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying that his team (young money) is special. Devin Hester is a special teams player for the Chicago Bears.\n\n\n\nCurrently Atlanta Falcons.", "annotation_id": "1013090", "url": "https://genius.com/1013090", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "Man, I’m so fly I got arachnophobia", "vault_lines": ["Man, I'm so fly I got arachnophobia"], "meaning": "Arachnaphobia is a fear of spiders, Spiders eat flies so he is insinuating he is ‘so Fly’ that he is scared of Spiders. And why not? They’re scary as shit!\n\n\n\nThat guy is insane!", "annotation_id": "1011705", "url": "https://genius.com/1011705", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "Real shit, we hold the bread, the hoes hold the toasters", "vault_lines": ["Real shit, we hold the bread, the hoes hold the toasters"], "meaning": "This could either mean:\n\n\nHe is carrying the money on him and his women holds the guns.\n\n\n\nor\n\n\nWayne and his crew have so much money compared to their contemporaries that, metaphorically, YMCMB is eating while everyone else is serving them and starving – no bread.", "annotation_id": "1011499", "url": "https://genius.com/1011499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "Blood gang 6 flags niggas, no rollercoaster", "vault_lines": ["Blood gang 6 flags niggas, no rollercoaster"], "meaning": "Wayne and all his homies are bloods. Theyre are carrying six flags on them, but not like the amusment park Six Flags.", "annotation_id": "1011493", "url": "https://genius.com/1011493", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "Smoking on that G13 and everything funny", "vault_lines": ["Smoking on that G13 and everything funny"], "meaning": "Wayne is smoking on a strong stand of Haze, which makes situations that are normal when he is sober, funny when he is high.", "annotation_id": "1011483", "url": "https://genius.com/1011483", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "Semi settle everything for me and everything for me", "vault_lines": ["Semi settle everything for me and everything for me"], "meaning": "Wayne doesnt like to beef with people, he has better things to do. So he lets his weapons do the talking.", "annotation_id": "1011477", "url": "https://genius.com/1011477", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "No Spinderella, just plenty metal for any fellow", "vault_lines": ["No Spinderella, just plenty metal for any fellow"], "meaning": "Playing off the line above; Spinderella is a member of the band Salt ‘n’ Pepa. But hes saying I got guns for anybody. No matter who it is.", "annotation_id": "1011472", "url": "https://genius.com/1011472", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pressure", "line": "If he got beef, watch me sprinkle salt and pepper on ’em", "vault_lines": ["If he got beef, watch me sprinkle salt and pepper on 'em"], "meaning": "If you have beef with someone, that means you have some sort of disagreement with them. If someone is throwing salt on you it means they’re turning your good situation into a bad one. And pepper is another word for bullets. So Wayne is saying if somebody got beef he will shoot them multiple times and “eat the beef”. In other words, finish you.", "annotation_id": "1011459", "url": "https://genius.com/1011459", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
