{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "Have niggas in ya yard like a yard sale", "vault_lines": ["Have niggas in ya yard like a yard sale"], "meaning": "During a yard sale people are in your yard to check out the merchandise that is available to buy.\n\nLil' Wayne is saying that he’ll send so many goons to your house the neighbors might think you’re having a yard sale.", "annotation_id": "12809802", "url": "https://genius.com/12809802", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "[Produced by Angel “Onhel” Aponte and Infamous]", "vault_lines": ["I do this for my Uptown politicians"], "meaning": "The haunting riff repeated throughout this song is from “Les Dunes D'Ostende” by François De Roubaix. The intro and hook are sampled from President Jimmy Carter’s 1977 Oath of Office.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/trimBK-h79E?t=43s", "annotation_id": "8893523", "url": "https://genius.com/8893523", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "Uh, appetite for disaster I want a full plate then another plate after", "vault_lines": ["Uh, appetite for disaster"], "meaning": "Seeing as just a year before this album he dropped his experimental rock album, Rebirth; this could be an ode to classic rock band Guns N' Roses‘ debut album Appetite For Destruction.\n\nHere Weezy unintentionally starts a controversy!\n\nWayne is expressing his punk attitude by using wordplay to describe his ‘hunger’.", "annotation_id": "3024587", "url": "https://genius.com/3024587", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "I’m beneficial, I’ve been official", "vault_lines": ["I'm beneficial, I've been official"], "meaning": "Ways Weezy can benefit things:\n\n\nInspire new rappers. A lot of rappers have named Wayne as an inspiration.\nHe can ‘save lives’ with his music.\n\nDonate money to hurricane relief.\n\n\n\nWordplay:\n\nWeezy uses the homophone: beneficial/been official to give this line some internal rhyme.", "annotation_id": "2885321", "url": "https://genius.com/2885321", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "Amen, so now instead of pledge, we pray, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Amen, so now instead of pledge, we pray, yeah"], "meaning": "Tying in with the previous line about changing the stars on the flag to crosses. Instead of saying the pledge of allegiance we should all pray, since crosses are to Christianity as stars are to U.S.A.", "annotation_id": "1404072", "url": "https://genius.com/1404072", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "President Carter, Pre-President Carter President Carter, Pre-President Carter President Carter, Pre-President Carter President Carter, Pre-President Carter", "vault_lines": ["President Carter, Pre-President Carter"], "meaning": "Not this guy – Dwayne Carter aka Lil Wayne is the “President” of Young Money.", "annotation_id": "342326", "url": "https://genius.com/342326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "Drowning in the political soup", "vault_lines": ["Drowning in the political soup"], "meaning": "Holy wars get overlooked because political wars are more important.\n\nHe might also be talking about troops fighting a supposed “holy war” (Christians vs. Muslims) when they aren’t the crusaders. They’re individuals with their own spirituality drowning in a political shit-swamp of war based on amoral economic and national interests.", "annotation_id": "340422", "url": "https://genius.com/340422", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "The holy war, the spiritual troops", "vault_lines": ["The holy war, the spiritual troops"], "meaning": "Referring to religious warfare, i.e. the fighting in Palestine and Israel over religious differences.", "annotation_id": "340420", "url": "https://genius.com/340420", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "Gorillas in suits", "vault_lines": ["I do this for my Uptown politicians"], "meaning": "Politicians are involved in wars too. They just don’t get their hands dirty.\n\n\n\nThis could also be a play on words with guerrilla warfare.", "annotation_id": "338462", "url": "https://genius.com/338462", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "Uh, and we all want world peace Murder show, I give your ass good seats", "vault_lines": ["Uh, and we all want world peace"], "meaning": "Everyone wants a safer world , but our society is very violent and he’s just giving the people what they want.\n\n\n\nIt could also mean that many people are dying because of the government, given that this is a very politically driven song.", "annotation_id": "338002", "url": "https://genius.com/338002", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "I changed the stars on the flag into crosses", "vault_lines": ["I changed the stars on the flag into crosses"], "meaning": "The stars on the flag stand for the fifty states he changes them to crosses to represent the death and war it took to get them and protect them\n\nNow we pray to the flag instead of pledging allegiance to it.\n\nThis might also be part of an extended metaphor for the cost of war.  He’s talking about changing the stars on the flag to crosses to represent the rows of white crosses found in military cemeteries.\n\nThe next line is an apocalyptic warning that the human race is going to destroy itself soon.  It’s time for allegiance to all humankind, time to pray for peace.", "annotation_id": "337990", "url": "https://genius.com/337990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "I tried to fuck the world and couldn’t even get aroused", "vault_lines": ["I tried to fuck the world and couldn't even get aroused"], "meaning": "The world doesn’t satisfy him anymore. He needs something else to conquer.\n\nHe has the stature of Napoleon with the same “I want everything” mentality.", "annotation_id": "337301", "url": "https://genius.com/337301", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "Walked in the kitchen and found a pot to piss in", "vault_lines": ["Walked in the kitchen and found a pot to piss in"], "meaning": "“Not having a pot to piss in” refers to being poor.\n\nWayne walked in the kitchen and found a way to be rich…probably cooking crack.", "annotation_id": "337281", "url": "https://genius.com/337281", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "They shoot missiles and nukes Taking out such a pivotal group The body count is the physical proof And they thought drugs were killing the youth, [chuckles] Thank you, thank you all, I am President Carter", "vault_lines": ["President Carter, Pre-President Carter"], "meaning": "Gorillas in suits definitely refers to politicians and their involvement in starting wars. The holy war can refer to Israel vs. Palestine, or just the larger “war on terror” that has made many Christians and Muslims feel like they are at war against each other when they are ultimately fighting over the “mythical truth” or something they can’t prove.\n\nThe pivotal group is the youth, because it is the youth that are sent to fight wars, mostly lower class youth that don’t have many other options. Their dead bodies are the proof that the main cause for death is going to war and killing people, not just people in the streets and drugs.\n\nWayne went on about his view on drugs “killing the youth” in the lengthy track; Dontgetit. He talked about how they simply aren’t, and we need to open up about other real crimes, such as rape, and murder.", "annotation_id": "337230", "url": "https://genius.com/337230", "state": "accepted", "votes": 101, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "I say you rappers sweet I pay the incidentals", "vault_lines": ["I say you rappers sweet I pay the incidentals"], "meaning": "This is a play on words with sweet/suite. Wayne damages these wack rappers, so he pays the incidentals. In hotels, incidental fees are charged for any damage done to the suite.", "annotation_id": "337224", "url": "https://genius.com/337224", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "If real shit is dead then nigga I’m a bastard", "vault_lines": ["If real shit is dead then nigga I'm a bastard"], "meaning": "People consider real hip hop to be dead, but Wayne considers himself a direct descendant of it. He’s a bastard, as a son would be if their father had died. Also, Bastard as in Tyler the Creator’s debut album. The previous three lines also reference Odd Future.\n\n\n\nI think Wayne made a mistake here saying “Bastard”. The correct term would be Orphan. As a bastard is someone who’s parents aren’t married, whereas an orphan is someone who’s parents are dead.", "annotation_id": "337108", "url": "https://genius.com/337108", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "Tomorrow never cried, the days of our lives", "vault_lines": ["Tomorrow never cried, the days of our lives"], "meaning": "The future doesn’t care about the past because it’s trying to take its place.\n\nDays of Our Lives is a really famous soap opera and they’re always really dramatic (crying).", "annotation_id": "336732", "url": "https://genius.com/336732", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "The future is born, put the past in the casket", "vault_lines": ["The future is born, put the past in the casket"], "meaning": "To take a line from his associate Drake, Weezy is Off That.\n\nAlso, “future” as in “Odd Future.” The preceding two lines are originally off Earl Sweatshirt’s “Earl”, and the following line mentions Bastard, Tyler the Creator’s debut album.", "annotation_id": "336729", "url": "https://genius.com/336729", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "I got life in my hand", "vault_lines": ["Sitting on the world, I got life in my hand"], "meaning": "A step up from having “the world” in his hand (as the spiritual/hymn goes) Wayne has the concept of life itself in his hand.", "annotation_id": "336701", "url": "https://genius.com/336701", "state": "pending", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "Cause I don’t give a fuck, I put the ass in assassin Smoke you like a blunt then it’s ashes to ashes", "vault_lines": ["Cause I don't give a fuck, I put the ass in assassin"], "meaning": "Just like Earl.\n\nHe’s giving props to Odd Future with:\n\n\nThis Earl line\nThe following line referencing future\nThe Bastard reference a few lines later", "annotation_id": "336621", "url": "https://genius.com/336621", "state": "accepted", "votes": 85, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "[Outro]", "vault_lines": ["I do this for my Uptown politicians"], "meaning": "In a “speech,” President Carter denounces holy wars, arguing they are pointless and destroy lives", "annotation_id": "336107", "url": "https://genius.com/336107", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "line": "[Intro] God bless america... - Carter, are you prepared to take the constitutional oath? - I am... - Will you place your left hand on the Bible and raise your right hand and repeat after me, I... [Chorus]", "vault_lines": ["- Carter, are you prepared to take the constitutional oath?"], "meaning": "The intro and hook are taken from President Jimmy Carter’s Oath of Office of January 20th, 1977.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NUoXXEl8pQc", "annotation_id": "336100", "url": "https://genius.com/336100", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President Carter", "status": "done", "targets": 24, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-president-carter-lyrics", "genius_title": "President Carter", "genius_id": 49156, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President", "line": "Bitch-ass nigga, I ain’t got no master Rich-ass nigga, I got all my masters Bitch-ass nigga, I ain’t got no master", "vault_lines": ["Bitch-ass nigga, I ain't got no master"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne would go on to sell his masters to Universal Music Group for over $100 million in 2020, including songs by Drake and Nicki Minaj.", "annotation_id": "36973489", "url": "https://genius.com/36973489", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President", "line": "Shit, I gotta make them C-notes sing to me", "vault_lines": ["Shit, I gotta make them C-notes sing to me"], "meaning": "A C-note is a hundred-dollar bill. Weezy plays on the word “note” by making his money sing, i.e. he’s got his shit together.", "annotation_id": "21357536", "url": "https://genius.com/21357536", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President", "line": "Flow retarded, I’m on some special ed shit The magnificent, twisted like a dread, bitch And I can get up in the car and drive And if the record is a smash, I can still survive", "vault_lines": ["Flow retarded, I'm on some special ed shit"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is referring to the East Coast rapper Special Ed.\nHe specifically references his track “I’m the Magnificent” from Ed’s debute album Youngest in Charge released in May 16, 1989 when he was only 16 years old.\n\nThe last two lines are almost identical to those in the “I’m the Magnificent” track:\n\nI get in it like a car and drive\nAnd if the record is smash, I can still survive", "annotation_id": "21151687", "url": "https://genius.com/21151687", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President", "line": "Back when Scarface used to sing to me Had me feeling like a G was the thing to be", "vault_lines": ["Back when Scarface used to sing to me"], "meaning": "He’d listen to Scarface, whose popularity was probably at its highest around the time Wayne was growing up.\n\nThis is a reference to a line from “Keep Ya Head Up” by 2Pac.\n\nI remember Marvin Gaye used to sing to me\nHe had me feelin' like black was the thing to be", "annotation_id": "352526", "url": "https://genius.com/352526", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President", "line": "You can see me on the Eastside of New Orleans with a red bitch", "vault_lines": ["You can see me on the Eastside of New Orleans with a red bitch"], "meaning": "Double entendre:\n\nHe’ll be hanging out in that area with a woman of medium-light brown complexion,\n\nand/or\n\ndeclaring his Blood gang affiliation (or that of his female companion) with references to a typically Blood-oriented color (red, natch), and direction (East, or right, which is the side on which Bloods wear their red bandanas.", "annotation_id": "351795", "url": "https://genius.com/351795", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President", "line": "You lookin’ for answers? I don’t got none, huh I’m from New Orleans and New Orleans don’t raise no rats (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["You lookin' for answers? I don't got none, huh"], "meaning": "A “rat” is a slang term for a snitch.", "annotation_id": "276481", "url": "https://genius.com/276481", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "President", "line": "The line of scrimmage is wicked", "vault_lines": ["The line of scrimmage is wicked"], "meaning": "Football reference is continuing, Curren$y already has some hype and gems, people want him more", "annotation_id": "192562", "url": "https://genius.com/192562", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
