{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "Never seen my car before, it’s like a unicorn in traffic", "vault_lines": ["Never seen my car before, it's like a unicorn in traffic"], "meaning": "The car he drives is so rare, that when he’s stuck in traffic it’s like seeing a mythical creature in real life!", "annotation_id": "35506999", "url": "https://genius.com/35506999", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "I got a city, got a ocean, got a lake view", "vault_lines": ["I got a city, got a ocean, got a lake view"], "meaning": "In Trap House Wayne explains he has a house in Miami, LA and New Orleans.\n\nHis city is New Orleans, his Ocean is Miami, and his lake view is LA, which could be a flip on the L.A. Lakers", "annotation_id": "4779385", "url": "https://genius.com/4779385", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "And my role model was a kingpin I say, “Let’s work,” he say, “Let’s work” Let your next work be your best work", "vault_lines": ["And my role model was a kingpin"], "meaning": "In a Rolling Stone interview in 2013, 2 Chainz had this to say after touring with Lil Wayne:\n\nThe guy would get offstage at 11:00, take a shower and rap until noon the next fucking day. And he’s already a millionaire! Having a phone full of millionaires and not being one bothered the hell out of me.\n\nChainz owes some of his drive to the way in which Wayne went about his business when they first hooked up.", "annotation_id": "4779373", "url": "https://genius.com/4779373", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "Stopped by the spot, had to serve Pooh bear He buy one, I front him one, so I left two there", "vault_lines": ["Stopped by the spot, had to serve Pooh bear"], "meaning": "“The Spot” refers to the weed spot, a place where people come to buy and sell drugs.\n\nPooh Bear is a rapper that 2 Chainz, under his previous moniker Tity Boi, has performed with and featured with previously, so there is a double meaning in this line, as he refers to both supplying him with drugs and with a verse (or two in this case).", "annotation_id": "4779363", "url": "https://genius.com/4779363", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "285, 20 pounds of musty", "vault_lines": ["285, 20 pounds of musty"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is 285 pounds in weight, but 20 pounds of that is weed smoke", "annotation_id": "4779354", "url": "https://genius.com/4779354", "state": "accepted", "votes": -4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "The boot, the battlefield", "vault_lines": ["The boot, the battlefield"], "meaning": "Weezy simultaneously alludes to the fact that he kills other rappers in the recording booth, and uses wordplay to allude to his hometown:\n\nLil Weezy-ana, the boot nigga, steel toe\n\n“The Boot” is the nickname for Waynes home state, Louisiana. Hollygrove is known for it’s high crime rate, which is why Lil Wayne calls it a battlefield.", "annotation_id": "4777761", "url": "https://genius.com/4777761", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "And I’m sorry for the wait, too", "vault_lines": ["I'm sorry if you hate you, and I'm sorry for the wait, too"], "meaning": "This is the 2nd installment of his Sorry 4 The Wait mixtape series. He’s also apologetic fans have to wait for his new album, Tha Carter V. The album was expected to drop back in October of 2014, but issues with Cash Money forced album delays.", "annotation_id": "4770795", "url": "https://genius.com/4770795", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "Big dog in this shit, like a Husky", "vault_lines": ["Big dog in this shit, like a Husky"], "meaning": "Huskies are pretty big dogs. 2 Chainz could also be comparing himself to a husky that pulls sleds in competitions like Iditarod. Siberian Huskies are one of the two types of dogs allowed to race in the Iditarod.", "annotation_id": "4761914", "url": "https://genius.com/4761914", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "Watch these snitches, man, these rats think they Mighty Mouse", "vault_lines": ["Watch these snitches, man, these rats think they Mighty Mouse"], "meaning": "Snitches and rats both mean the same thing – someone who informs law enforcement about someone else’s wrongdoings.\n\nWayne finds them amusing and compares their false sense of confidence to Mighty Mouse, an animated mouse superhero from the 1940s-60s.", "annotation_id": "4760521", "url": "https://genius.com/4760521", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "Flag red, like I’m Russian, call me Vladimir", "vault_lines": ["Flag red, like I'm Russian, call me Vladimir"], "meaning": "Weezy is outspoken about his blood gang affiliation and continues flaunting that here. His bandanna is red like the Russian flag; Vladimur Putin is Russia’s president.\n\nWayne is surely referencing the former Soviet Union, which is all red with the sickle, and not the current Russian Federation flag:", "annotation_id": "4758823", "url": "https://genius.com/4758823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "These niggas got fast careers, fast as Batmobiles", "vault_lines": ["These niggas got fast careers, fast as Batmobiles"], "meaning": "Batmobiles are car driven by the masked adventurer Batman, usually represented in films and comics as a large, and fast ones.\n\nOther rappers around Wayne has short-lived careers, whereas he has proved that he is clearly in the rap game for the long run.", "annotation_id": "4758108", "url": "https://genius.com/4758108", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "Please don’t worry, Nancy, all my weed is organic If my children end up smoking I’ll whip they ass if they don’t pass it", "vault_lines": ["Please don't worry, Nancy, all my weed is organic"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the heated debate about legalized marijuana that took place between Conservative television star Nancy Grace and 2 Chainz, whom the song features. Nancy consistently alluded to children easily obtaining marijuana if the drug continued to be legalized around the United States.\n\n\n\nAlso there’s a wordplay between “passing” and “whip they ass” which is what normally happens when kids don’t pass in school.", "annotation_id": "4756706", "url": "https://genius.com/4756706", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "Too much fucking talent, rap Shakespeare, go Hamlet", "vault_lines": ["Too much fucking talent, rap Shakespeare, go Hamlet"], "meaning": "In the lead up to Tha Carter V’s announced December release, Weezy tweeted “Much luv for Professor Kreston Kent” https://twitter.com/liltunechi/status/536062593677680641 author of “The Literary Genius of Lil Wayne: The case for Lil Wayne to be counted among Shakespeare and Dylan”\n\n\n\nWeezy has never been one to stay too humble when it comes to his skills as a rapper, and he takes that a step further by adopting Professor Kent’s comparison to the nearly universally renowned poet William Shakespeare.\n\n\n\nWayne finishes the line off by mentioning Hamlet, of one of Shakespeare’s more popular plays, and using it as an extension of the popular phrase “go HAM”", "annotation_id": "4756569", "url": "https://genius.com/4756569", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "line": "From New Orleans to the A, TRU", "vault_lines": ["From New Orleans to the A, TRU"], "meaning": "Though New Orleans, Louisiana, isn’t very far from Atlanta, Georgia, Weezy shouts out these two cities as they are his and 2 Chainz’s birthplaces, respectively.\n\n\n\nThe “TRU” at the end of the line is a reference to 2 Chainz’s adlib/The Real University", "annotation_id": "4756491", "url": "https://genius.com/4756491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Preach", "status": "done", "targets": 14, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-preach-lyrics", "genius_title": "Preach", "genius_id": 685085, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pray to the Lord", "line": "But in this game of life, I don’t make the rules Shit, so that’s why I get twisted So I can’t feel it when it hits me", "vault_lines": ["But in this game of life, I don't make the rules"], "meaning": "This is one of several indications given by Wayne that the true reason for his prolific drug use is not for recreational purposes but, rather, for avoiding the difficult aspects of life, such as the loss of loved ones.\n\nIn Real Rap (A.K.A. Amen), Wayne similarly illustrates that:\n\n…So much shit just sit on this mind of mine,\nI think about it all the time\nI drink about it all the time, I smoke back to back\nBecause if my thoughts got to me, I’d be in this rap…", "annotation_id": "33465556", "url": "https://genius.com/33465556", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pray to the Lord", "line": "But I see death around the corner", "vault_lines": ["But I see death around the corner"], "meaning": "“Death Around the Corner” is the title of slain rapper Tupac from “Me Against The World.” The album theme of paranoia ties in with the paranoia apparent on “Pray To The Lord”…", "annotation_id": "14960884", "url": "https://genius.com/14960884", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pray to the Lord", "line": "I made that bed and I should rest in peace", "vault_lines": ["I made that bed and I should rest in peace"], "meaning": "This is a play on the idiom “You made your bed, now lie in it”. The meaning is that your past decisions have shaped your future, and you have to accept the blame for the mistakes you have made.\n\nIn this case, Wayne realizes that his old lifestyle may cut his life short, and this song shows him accepting that fact.", "annotation_id": "3303061", "url": "https://genius.com/3303061", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pray to the Lord", "line": "Before I sleep I pray to the Lord, my soul to keep And if I should die, before I wake I pray to the Lord, my soul to take For goodness’ sake, before I sleep I pray to the Lord, my soul to keep And if I should die, before I wake I pray to the Lord, my soul to take, for goodness’ sake", "vault_lines": ["I pray to the Lord, my soul to keep"], "meaning": "This is the “Christian Child’s Prayer”:\n\nNow I lay me down to sleep,\nI pray the Lord my soul to keep;\nIf I die before I wake,\nI pray for God my soul to take\n\nEvery night before he goes to bed he thanks God for everything he has and prays that he will go to heaven if he happens to die in his sleep.", "annotation_id": "1038936", "url": "https://genius.com/1038936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pray to the Lord", "line": "I’m tryin’ live right, stay on the drum beat But I’m in the fast lane, in the front seat", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryin' live right, stay on the drum beat"], "meaning": "He’s trying his best to live a great life, but being the face of rap is restricting him.", "annotation_id": "248695", "url": "https://genius.com/248695", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pray to the Lord", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-pray-to-the-lord-lyrics", "genius_title": "Pray to the Lord", "genius_id": 49015, "source": "api"}
