{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Power", "line": "Free C-Murda! Antwan we in here!", "vault_lines": ["Antwan we in here!"], "meaning": "C-Murder is Master P & Silk The Shocker’s brother. He is also a former member of the group Tru. He was convicted in 2002 of the beating and shooting of a 16 year old fan at Harvey, Louisana nightclub. Interesting to note, since Percy and Corey’s relationship as of late has been strained, with the latter calling the other a ‘black sheep’ of the family. He is currently serving a life sentence in Angola.", "annotation_id": "4673053", "url": "https://genius.com/4673053", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Power", "line": "Split your avocado, hair trigger, Polamalu", "vault_lines": ["Split your avocado, hair trigger, Polamalu"], "meaning": "In this case, avocado refers to a persons head, meaning that Lil Wayne will take someones head off. A hair trigger is used to describe the trigger on a gun that does not take a lot of pressure to fire.\n\n\n\nThis has Lil Wayne making a reference to the Pittsburgh Steelers safety, Troy Polamalu who is popularly known for his impressive head of hair, which is 32 inches!. In 2010, it was said by Polamalu that his most recent haircut was 7 or 8 years prior!\n\nBeing a diehard Packers fan, Lil Wayne did make a remix to Wiz Khalifa’s breakout single, “Black and Yellow”, titled “Green and Yellow”. In the track, Lil Wayne had something to say towards Troy Polamalu.\n\nWe knocked the Eagles and the Falcons and the Bears off\n  Now we bout to cut Troy Polamalu hair off", "annotation_id": "4671102", "url": "https://genius.com/4671102", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Power", "line": "I got all this power I got all this powder, plus I got all these downers I got heavy fire power, I put the “pow” in power", "vault_lines": ["All I want is power"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne’s net worth stands around $140 million. Also, Weezy owns $150,000 teeth. If we are sticking to the concept of money being power, then take a gander at Lil Wayne’s Miami beach house.\n\n\n\nIt’s no secret that Lil Wayne likes shooting, as he explains in many of his songs. Speaking of fire power, we can’t forget that Wayne is the fireman.", "annotation_id": "4671056", "url": "https://genius.com/4671056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Power", "line": "And nobody gave me nothin, I started with a dream Nigga call me Benson, way I put together this team We all came from the struggle, but I came from the cream They say the cream rise to the top, mothafucka what you mean?", "vault_lines": ["And nobody gave me nothin, I started with a dream"], "meaning": "Master P was raised in the Calliope Projects, which is very well known for it’s high crime rate. When his grandfather passed the way, he took the $10,000 given to him, and opened a record store, which eventually alluded to him starting his own record label, No Limit Records.\n\n\n\nHe nods to the fact that he didn’t grow up in the struggle, and he was well raised. Master P had a good education, and even had a brief NBA career. Master is more focused on the fact that he is where he is now, as opposed to where he started from.", "annotation_id": "4671008", "url": "https://genius.com/4671008", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Power", "line": "All I want is power Get this, get this money by the hour That power, that power, that power All I want is this power Money brings me this power", "vault_lines": ["All I want is power"], "meaning": "Master P has a net worth of 350 million. That is quite a lot, and considering that money is power, it seems that Master P has already accomplished his goals here, in the attempt at getting power.\n\n\n\nHere is a photo of Master P’s house, which was put on MTV Cribs a few years back. It doesn’t take that hard of a look to say that with this house, you clearly make yourself powerful!\n\n\n\nActually, Master P has been able to make other rappers want his house, and has clearly made an impact on other rappers lives.\n\n\n\nHe also shouts out Money Mafia, which is the mixtape that this single will appear on.", "annotation_id": "4670953", "url": "https://genius.com/4670953", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Power", "line": "Used to sell fake crack for soap They don’t make soap like that no more", "vault_lines": ["Used to sell fake crack for soap"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne used to sell soap to junkies telling them it was crack. He then flips the expression “they don’t make em like that no more.”\n\nDouble Entendre:\n\n\nHe is talking about the way he used to mislead people with his crack which was actually soap. Lil Wayne is rich now so he doesn’t need to sell dope anymore, or should i say soap.\nHe is talking about himself. Lil Wayne has received a lot of negative attention these last few years and people start forgetting what he did for the game with his style and work ethic. He just wants to remind the listener (possibly Baby) that you won’t find anyone like him anytime soon.", "annotation_id": "4667137", "url": "https://genius.com/4667137", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Power", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Money-mafia-power-lyrics", "genius_title": "Power", "genius_id": 662448, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "I just want my check, I don’t want a trial", "vault_lines": ["I just want my check, I don't want a trial"], "meaning": "Referring to his situation with Birdman. Birdman owed him millions of dollars at the time this song was released", "annotation_id": "38784956", "url": "https://genius.com/38784956", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "I just want a sip, I don’t wanna drown I just want the lean, I don’t wanna bounce", "vault_lines": ["I just want a sip, I don't wanna drown"], "meaning": "Wayne wants to keep drinking lean (I just wanna sip/lean), but he doesn’t want to overdose and die (I don’t wanna drown/bounce)", "annotation_id": "17827315", "url": "https://genius.com/17827315", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "My soda so dirty, I can’t even lie", "vault_lines": ["My soda so dirty, I can't even lie"], "meaning": "A reference to Future’s mixtape Dirty Sprite.\n\n\n\nWhen Lil Wayne drinks soda, he always puts cough syrup and makes lean instead, hence making his soda “dirty”.", "annotation_id": "8208170", "url": "https://genius.com/8208170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "When I need peace of mind I just pour up a lot I pour up a lot", "vault_lines": ["I pour up a lot"], "meaning": "When Tunechi needs “peace of mind” (peace of mind means to be relaxed,to free your mind from everything) he pours up a lot.He pours “Purple Drank”. Purple drank is a mix of promethazine and codeine and often times sprite. It is also known as Codeine, a cough syrup.", "annotation_id": "7994380", "url": "https://genius.com/7994380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "I pour up a lot, past, present, future", "vault_lines": ["I pour up a lot, past, present, future"], "meaning": "Weezy started sippin' syrup over a decade ago, he explained why he started in 2011:\n\nI don’t do this to be cool, I did this because I was sick.. I started drinking it because I was from the south. I was also young and I listened to Pimp C, and it made me wanna drink lean.\n\nHe tried to stop over the years, but he couldn’t:\n\nFeels like death in your stomach when you stop, everybody wants me to stop all this and all that. It ain’t that easy\n\nEven though he had to stop in 2013 due to having seizures, he said that lean got nothing to do with it, and this song proves that he picked up the cup again. He promised to sip lean until he dies.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QEoPOqOSZcA", "annotation_id": "7918975", "url": "https://genius.com/7918975", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "As soon as I seen niggas sippin’ green I was like, “where they do that”", "vault_lines": ["As soon as I seen niggas sippin' green"], "meaning": "The new brand of promethazine and codeine that is made by Caraco Pharmaceuticals is green.", "annotation_id": "7915028", "url": "https://genius.com/7915028", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "I pour up a lot", "vault_lines": ["I pour up a lot"], "meaning": "This song is an ode to lean, also known as purple rain or dirty Sprite. Lean, a drink that originated in Houston, is mixing promethazine and codeine into a soft drink.\n\nLean is particularly common in hip-hop culture. It’s permeated every corner of the rap game. Trap god Future basically lives off the Purple Drank, while Macklemore struggled with an addiction to it as chronicled by “Otherside” and “Starting Over”. Wayne’s own addiction to lean is well-documented. He has twice been hospitalised for seizures after sipping the syrup.", "annotation_id": "7913589", "url": "https://genius.com/7913589", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "D’usse, D’usse, when I get home I’mma throw up these shots", "vault_lines": ["D'usse, D'usse, when I get home I'mma throw up these shots"], "meaning": "Founded in 2012, D'usse is a drink that is made of Cognac. Wayne is a big fan of this drink, seeing that he even made a song called “D'usse”.", "annotation_id": "7911670", "url": "https://genius.com/7911670", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "Stomach in knots, thought I need some drank I’m stuck in my bed and the dopeman said all he got is red If I don’t do red, Lord, I don’t do red I don’t do yellow, no, I don’t do that I don’t do Qualitest, I don’t do Hi-Tech I need that Act", "vault_lines": ["Stomach in knots, thought I need some drank"], "meaning": "One of the withdrawal symptoms of Lean is severe stomach pain. Wayne calls his dealer over, but this dealer doesn’t have Wayne’s preferred brand, Actavis, known as Purple.\n\nRed refers to Hi-Tech, another brand of cough syrup not as strong as Actavis. Tussionex is yellow, and doesn’t include Wayne’s preferred drug, which is codeine. It uses Hydrocordone, which produces itchiness. Qualitest is another brand of cough syrup.", "annotation_id": "7911321", "url": "https://genius.com/7911321", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "I could have swore I saw Pac", "vault_lines": ["I could have swore I saw Pac"], "meaning": "Wayne is so high off his purple drank that he can swear that he saw the rap icon Tupac Shakur. Even though Pac died on September 13, 1996 in Las Vegas, NV, there have been reports that he is still alive living in Cuba. Is Wayne tripping or not?\n\nMay also mean Wayne got so high he ascended to heaven, and saw the deceased legend.", "annotation_id": "7911204", "url": "https://genius.com/7911204", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "I open the soda, I get the codeine and I pour up a lot I pour up a lot, I pour up a lot", "vault_lines": ["Got my codeine and I poured up a lot"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is making Purple Drank, or syrup. He is putting ice in his double cup then filling it with soda, and he pours a lot of syrup which would affect him later in life.", "annotation_id": "7909564", "url": "https://genius.com/7909564", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "Chinese AK just do what I say and nobody die", "vault_lines": ["Chinese AK just do what I say and nobody die"], "meaning": "Although the AK-47 is primarily a Russian Assault Rifle, it is shipped to countries all over the world, each making their own variants. The Chinese one is called the Type 56.\n\n\n\nDuring the Communist Revolution in China under Mao Zedong, guns were often used to get people to follow commands. Likewise, Lil Wayne can get people to listen to him with his gun.", "annotation_id": "7909547", "url": "https://genius.com/7909547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "Could have swore I saw Spock", "vault_lines": ["Could have swore I saw Spock"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne just got high from drinking all of that codeine. The side effects of codeine include hallucinations. In this case, Lil Wayne saw Spock, a fictional character from Star Trek. Star Trek is also a show set in space, hence Wayne was so high he ascended outside the Earth’s atmosphere. The man who played Spock, Leonard Nimoy, passed away before this album was released. Wayne saw Nimoy as well as Pac when he ascended to heaven.", "annotation_id": "7909538", "url": "https://genius.com/7909538", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "And all you lookin’ ass niggas look at me now I’m sure you gon’ watch, you boring, I’m not I’m scoring a lot, ignoring the thots", "vault_lines": ["And all you lookin' ass niggas look at me now"], "meaning": "Weezy is a veteran in the rap game, beginning at the tender age of 8. Through his career he has influenced a lot of rappers (especially in his prime) and he wants the new and upcoming rappers to watch and learn from him. While some of them are going to clubs and partying, Weezy is working hard and giving his fans music.\n\nI’m grindin’, I’m grindin’, I’m grindin’ I promise", "annotation_id": "7909519", "url": "https://genius.com/7909519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "I start hopping around like Jiminy Cricket", "vault_lines": ["I start hopping around like Jiminy Cricket"], "meaning": "Jiminy Cricket is a fictional character adapted by Disney into the animated film Pinocchio. As a cricket, Jiminy is known for hopping.\n\nSo going back to the previous lines, Wayne will disappear like an insect if the police are looking for him.", "annotation_id": "7909502", "url": "https://genius.com/7909502", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "My shooters don’t listen I tell ’em you cool, but still they don’t listen I cut on the news, and they say you missin’ And I can’t stop grinnin’ like, “nigga, we did it” And they show police fishin’ And searching under bridges when they say no witness", "vault_lines": ["My motor don't stop"], "meaning": "Wayne is creating a scene. He tells his shooters you’re cool, but they don’t listen and kill you anyway. Wayne then turns on the news as they discuss your disappearance. Police are fishing and searching under bridges for your body. The news announces that there are no witnesses and Wayne jumps around with joy, knowing he successfully got away with murder.", "annotation_id": "7909470", "url": "https://genius.com/7909470", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "We got that white girl workin’ like Hooters", "vault_lines": ["We got that white girl workin' like Hooters"], "meaning": "White girl is slang for cocaine. Weezy even has a song called “White Girl”, and you know what it’s about. Hooters is a restaurant/bar where the people who work there are woman (with pretty hot uniforms), Weezy’s got a few girls that work for him like they work in Hooters.", "annotation_id": "7909450", "url": "https://genius.com/7909450", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "line": "Syrup and sprite, turn that shit fuschia", "vault_lines": ["Syrup and sprite, turn that shit fuschia"], "meaning": "The color Fuchsia is a deeper shade of the color pink. Wayne is saying he poured up a lot of syrup into his soda resulting in the deeper easter pink.\n\n\n\nAlso presented here is a play on words since “Fuchsia” sounds like “Future” when mumbled and Future is known for drinking lean and being heavily influenced by Wayne.", "annotation_id": "7909417", "url": "https://genius.com/7909417", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pour Up", "status": "done", "targets": 18, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-pour-up-lyrics", "genius_title": "Pour Up", "genius_id": 2321983, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "I just looked at your bitch and got eye-fucked", "vault_lines": ["I just looked at your bitch and got eye-fucked"], "meaning": "“Eye-fucking” refers to having sex with someone with just their eyes. Your bitch cheated on you just by looking into Wayne’s eyes because he is irresistible.", "annotation_id": "22798603", "url": "https://genius.com/22798603", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "I just looked in the mirror, got star struck", "vault_lines": ["I just looked in the mirror, got star struck"], "meaning": "Wayne is such a huge star that even “he” gets star struck.", "annotation_id": "22798585", "url": "https://genius.com/22798585", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "Uh, hundred thousand on a small ass chain Hundred thousand on a bottle champagne Half a million for a watch with no diamonds Brought cash to the jewelers, still had change", "vault_lines": ["Uh, hundred thousand on a small ass chain"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is worth 150 million USD. He lives the highest lifestyle and buys the best things. “Hundred thousand on a small ass chain” refers to his drip being so high standard that $100,000 is “small” to him. He’ll also spend $100,000 on a bottle of champagne, $500,000 on a watch with no diamonds. He’s saying this stuff is not special to him and will spend that with ease. He’ll go to the jewellers and have change – furthering this concept. Spending this money is average to him.", "annotation_id": "22798527", "url": "https://genius.com/22798527", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "My warrant’s clear as day like Doris is", "vault_lines": ["My warrant's clear as day like Doris is"], "meaning": "Wayne uses a pun on the actress Doris Day’s name, to complete a simile which compares Wayne’s free and “clear” legal status (for now) to the expression “clear as day”.\n\nLil Wayne could also depict his warrant as clear as the skin of Dr. Dorris Day’s patients. Dr. Dorris is an expert skin care author, and one of New York City’s elite dermatologists.", "annotation_id": "7336174", "url": "https://genius.com/7336174", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "Pray more than sometimes", "vault_lines": ["Pray more than sometimes"], "meaning": "Wayne encourages his son to pray not just sometimes, but all the time. Wayne does profess to believe in God, so he probably believes what the Bible has to say in 1 Thessalonians 5:16-18 about praying without ceasing:\n\nRejoice always, pray without ceasing, give thanks in all circumstances; for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus for you.", "annotation_id": "7272037", "url": "https://genius.com/7272037", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "Take dirt, make a mud pie", "vault_lines": ["Take dirt, make a mud pie"], "meaning": "Wayne often alludes to his inherent ability to take something valueless, and make something valuable from it.  One example of a similar sentiment Wayne rapped years prior:\n\nhttps://genius.com/2256/Lil-wayne-a-milli/Bitch-i-can-turn-a-crack-rock-into-a-mountain-dare-me\n\nChanging “dirt” to a “mud pie” is another symbol for taking “nothing” and making “something” – or another way of picturing it is the everpresent theme of “rags-to-riches” in rap.", "annotation_id": "7255862", "url": "https://genius.com/7255862", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "When the cops come, you tongue-tied", "vault_lines": ["When the cops come, you tongue-tied"], "meaning": "To be “tongue tied” means you are unable or unwilling to speak.  Therefore, echoing the unwritten but widely understood rule; Wayne is telling associates of his that if the police attempt to speak with them, they better have nothing to say.\n\nWayne has been adamant and consistent in his violent disdain of snitches:\n\nAll rats gotta die, even Master Splinter", "annotation_id": "7255836", "url": "https://genius.com/7255836", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "My presidential said it’s crunch time", "vault_lines": ["My presidential said it's crunch time"], "meaning": "These lyrics share a similar sentiment to the idiom, which relates to human awareness of an hourglass' continuously falling grains of sand, and the effect that awareness can have on our mental state since we know that our time is limited, yet more of it passes by every moment.\n\nHis Presidential series Rolex watch is metaphorically standing over his shoulder, reminding him that he has money to bring in; it’s time to get back to the grind.", "annotation_id": "7255806", "url": "https://genius.com/7255806", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "I lost appeal The bullshit cost me a mill It brought me to tears I came home and bought me a crib", "vault_lines": ["The bullshit cost me a mill"], "meaning": "Wayne lost his court appeal when he was found guilty of gun charges and sentenced to jail at Riker’s Island.\n\nBetween the legal fees and paying his lawyers, the court case ended up costing Wayne a good deal of cash; meaning he fought hard against the law, but he still lost in the end.\n\nHis jail sentence affected him deeply and emotionally. First he cried it out. Then he went and bought a brand new house in an effort to feel better (AKA retail therapy, but Wayne’s is on a baller scale, of course).", "annotation_id": "7250141", "url": "https://genius.com/7250141", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "[Verse 1]", "vault_lines": ["Who the fuck wanna race? Put your money up"], "meaning": "The song’s instrumental was produced by Develop, whose notable productions are Eminem’s “Rap God”, and Lil Wayne’s “Fireman”. His name is usually stylized as “DVLP” and is pronounced ‘Develop’.\n\nDVLP has been Working on Tha Carter V, and slated to make C5’s final tracklisting. As seen in Lil Wayne’s weekly vlog series “Weezy Wednesdays”, Wayne previewed an, at that time, unfinished record called “Side Bitch”, which is produced by DVLP.", "annotation_id": "7249769", "url": "https://genius.com/7249769", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "Uh, one time For the hustlers and the young moms", "vault_lines": ["For the hustlers and the young moms"], "meaning": "Wayne is shouting out people who hustle and young mum’s because those are the people who are actually trying to do something with their lives, and struggle daily.", "annotation_id": "7244870", "url": "https://genius.com/7244870", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Post Bail Ballin", "line": "Glass house on the block, five floors in it", "vault_lines": ["Glass house on the block, five floors in it"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne purchased his mansion back in 2006 for the price of $12 Million. He then decided to sell his home for $18 Million, which is $6 Million more than the price he purchased it.\n\nTunechi’s home is filled with glass surrounding property itself with 5 stories.", "annotation_id": "7230870", "url": "https://genius.com/7230870", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
