{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "When it comes to the bread, I got the keys to the bakery", "vault_lines": ["When it comes to the bread, I got the keys to the bakery"], "meaning": "Bread is slang for money, and Weezy is saying he has keys to the bakery where there is lots of bread or in his case, money.", "annotation_id": "15655249", "url": "https://genius.com/15655249", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "I live by these rules only: money over bitches (Ha) And it been like that ever since I could remember", "vault_lines": ["I live by these rules only: money over bitches (Ha)"], "meaning": "2Pac’s slogan, which has been whole-heartedly embraced by Lil Wayne and his crew. Curren$y can be citing Pac as one of his oldest influences.\n\n#M.O.B = Money Over Bitches", "annotation_id": "2160260", "url": "https://genius.com/2160260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "I just copped me some purp’ (Purp’), I’m ’bout to open up (Chyeah)", "vault_lines": ["I just copped me some purp' (Purp'), I'm 'bout to open up (Chyeah)"], "meaning": "Mack’s just grabbed some codeine, otherwise known as purp, and is feeling good.\n\n\n\nThere’s also some wordplay – copped is slang for arrested, and purp is slang for criminal. Mack’s just arrested a criminal, and is about to open up the prison.\n\nOf course, what Mack is really opening up is his great prices.", "annotation_id": "2160181", "url": "https://genius.com/2160181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "Young Money fly boys, mami—weed a different breed", "vault_lines": ["Young Money fly boys, mami—weed a different breed"], "meaning": "Curren$y is shouting out Young Money Entertainment, Lil Wayne’s record label. They’re all pretty fly on there.\n\nCurren$y is outlining his life: mammies/girls and lots of special-breed weed.\n\nCurren$y is also suggesting that he and Weezy are of a different breed.", "annotation_id": "2160170", "url": "https://genius.com/2160170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "Now, ever since I could remember, I been poppin’ them bottles (Young Money) Pop— Poppin’ them bottles, pop— poppin’ them bottles Now, ever since I could remember, I been smokin’ that ’dro (Shout-out my nigga Willie the Kid! Shout to The Replacements! AMG!) With my motherfucking pistol in my hand, in my hand (Dr— Dramatic, nigga! Dramatic!) Now, ever since I could remember, I been poppin’ them bottles (My niggas up next! Yeah) Pop— Poppin’ them bottles, pop— poppin’ them bottles (Young Money! Oww!) Now, ever since I could remember, I been smokin’ that ’dro (Cash Money, haha! Mr. Game Seven!) With my motherfucking pistol in my hand, in my hand (Weezy, talk to ’em! Gangsta Gri-Zillz!)", "vault_lines": ["Now, ever since I could remember, I been poppin' them bottles (Young Money)"], "meaning": "Ever since Lil Wayne was young, he’s been popping bottles – drinking – and smoking marijuana, all with his gun in hand.\n\nHe had a early start on his career, at age 15 he joined the Hot Boys and dropped the album Get It How U Live!", "annotation_id": "2157967", "url": "https://genius.com/2157967", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "Well, they know me as lil’ Curren$y, but some call me “The Hot Spitta”", "vault_lines": ["Well, they know me as lil' Curren$y, but some call me \"The Hot Spitta\""], "meaning": "Like Lil Wayne starts his verse off with referencing DJ Pauls original verse, Curren$y refers to Juicy J’s verse.\n\nWell you know me by the Juice man hangin out with Big Triece\nStandin on tha porch, drinkin liquor, drunk, smokin' weed", "annotation_id": "2157809", "url": "https://genius.com/2157809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "Sittin’ in the Chevy on three wheels, like a tricycle", "vault_lines": ["Sittin' in the Chevy on three wheels, like a tricycle"], "meaning": "Flipping switches in his Chevy – hitting that three-wheel motion.\n\nBecause of the hydraulics, he’s probably cruising in a low-rider Chevy.", "annotation_id": "511186", "url": "https://genius.com/511186", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "Riding in the big boys, sitting on them grown folks", "vault_lines": ["Riding in the big boys, sitting on them grown folks"], "meaning": "‘Big Boys’ are cars such as the Phantom or the Maybach, which are literally ‘bigger’ than your average Benz, Porsche or other luxury ride.\n\nSee Weezy’s lines from Hustlin:\n\nIn the Phantom\nBitch so big I’ll probably get lost\n\n‘Grown Folks’ are rims that are 22 inches or bigger. Over 21s are adults, much like Wayne’s rims.\n\nWayne is also suggesting that he is better than the best, riding on top of them.", "annotation_id": "357784", "url": "https://genius.com/357784", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "And you ain’t got to go to Mickey-D’s for quarter-pounds (Ugh)", "vault_lines": ["And you ain't got to go to Mickey-D's for quarter-pounds (Ugh)"], "meaning": "McDonald’s sells quarter pound burgers, but Mack Maine also has a certain “quarter pound” for you – one made of weed! Mack both deals with the street dealers and is a drug lord himself, giving him the ability to give out small ounces and full size units without his dealers having to go anywhere else. That’s business!", "annotation_id": "311929", "url": "https://genius.com/311929", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "I guess I’m the number-one Lakers fan Yellow bottle, yellow bottle; purple bag, purple bag", "vault_lines": ["I guess I'm the number-one Lakers fan"], "meaning": "The Lakers colors are yellow and purple, one of Wayne’s more hated teams. Still, he seems like a superfan – he’s always surrounding with things that are their colors! Whether sipping on the yellow-bottled Aces champagne or smoking Purple Kush, he doesn’t even care – he’s getting to the money.", "annotation_id": "168351", "url": "https://genius.com/168351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Poppin Them Bottles", "line": "These niggas out ‘chere trippin’, sellin’ keys to them agencies", "vault_lines": ["These niggas out 'chere trippin', sellin' keys to them agencies"], "meaning": "Drug dealers are being foolish, selling kilos of cocaine to the police, or numerous other federal agencies.\n\n“Ki’s” is slang for a kilo of cocaine which ties into the literal use of the word “key” in the previous line.", "annotation_id": "168346", "url": "https://genius.com/168346", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
