{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That Pussy", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-pop-that-pussy-lyrics", "genius_title": "Pop That Pussy", "genius_id": 28667, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Ass so fat need a lap dance", "vault_lines": ["Ass so fat need a lap dance"], "meaning": "Referencing the hook from the 2011 Tyga song, “Lap Dance”.\n\nBenzo, batman, thick ho, lap dance\nAss so fat need a lap dance\nAss so fat I need a lap dance", "annotation_id": "17747764", "url": "https://genius.com/17747764", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m 5'5\" but I could 6-9", "vault_lines": ["I’m 5'5\" but I could 6-9"], "meaning": "Wayne makes a play on numbers. While he is only the average male height he is still tall enough to 69. 69 is a sexual position that involves the couple laying down into a 69 position where they are facing each other crouches performing oral sex on each other, this would obviously be easier if one was taller but Wayne can still do it well despite only being 5'5.\n\nWeezy has rapped about being successful despite not being tall is previous songs, such as Rick Ross’s 2008 song “Luxury Tax”:\n\nThey said I couldn’t play football, I was too small\nThey said I couldn’t play basketball, I wasn’t tall\nThey said I couldn’t play baseball at all\nAnd now every day of my life, I ball", "annotation_id": "14100496", "url": "https://genius.com/14100496", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Motherfucker I’m on my skateboard Watch me do a trick, ho", "vault_lines": ["Motherfucker I'm on my skateboard"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is a avid lover of skateboarding. He even has his own private skate park in his house.\n\nIn an interview with ESPN he shows off his skating prowess and explains:\n\nThe moment I decided I wanted to skate I was watching Alex Miller a lot of T.V like I didn’t even know you could do this, I didn’t even know you could jump off stairs and I didn’t know you could skateboard at this age, where’s you parents?\n\nHe also explains:\n\nYou know in music we have restrictions, we have limits that you can’t do this because you want to be considered this or you can’t do this cause you’re gonna be considered that. In skateboarding you can just be free. What I can get from skateboarding that I can’t get from music is natural satisfaction.\n\nOn the cover of his Dedication 4 mixtape he is depicted holding a skateboard.", "annotation_id": "14100436", "url": "https://genius.com/14100436", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Shout out to Uncle Luke (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Shout out to Uncle Luke (Huh)"], "meaning": "“Pop That” samples the 1992 track “I Wanna Rock (Doo Doo Brown)” by rapper Uncle Luke. Ross shouts him out to credit the owner of the original sample.", "annotation_id": "14072571", "url": "https://genius.com/14072571", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Bitches know I’m that nigga, talkin’ four-door Bugatti", "vault_lines": ["Bitches know I'm that nigga, talkin' four-door Bugatti"], "meaning": "Bugatti is a high-end French car manufacturer popular among rappers. Ross is an avid car collector (you can view his collection here) he owns, several Maybachs, Lamborghinis, BMWs, and of course Bugattis.  His love for cars is so great he even named his Maybach Music Label after the Maybach brand.\n\n\n\nA few months prior to this song’s release in January, 2013  Ross also appeared on the popular Ace Hood song “Bugatti” which also featured Future.", "annotation_id": "14072232", "url": "https://genius.com/14072232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Dropped Take Care, bought a mothafuckin’ crib", "vault_lines": ["Dropped Take Care, bought a mothafuckin' crib"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing his second studio album, Take Care which was released on the 15th of November, 2011 through Cash Money Records.\n\nThe sophomore album sold over 631,000 copies in its first week and in August of 2015 it was reported that the album had sold over 4,000,000 copies.\n\nThe album has gone 4X platinum in the U.S due to its very high sale numbers.", "annotation_id": "13232699", "url": "https://genius.com/13232699", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Bitch, I ball like two eyelids", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I ball like two eyelids"], "meaning": "Here, Wayne uses the homophone of “I” and “eye” to describe how much he balls. According to his net worth, he definitely has the ballin' aspect covered, much like an eyelid covers an eyeball. Wayne goes on to use other ocular metaphors later in his career.\n\nIf you don’t see what I’m sayin'\nI give your ass a fuckin' eye exam", "annotation_id": "11665026", "url": "https://genius.com/11665026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "It’s Weezy F, fuck hoes", "vault_lines": ["It's Weezy F, fuck hoes"], "meaning": "One of Lil Wayne’s many nicknames is Weezy F Baby. In this case the F is for “fuck hoes.” It’s been used for “finisher”, “fuck you', and various others.", "annotation_id": "1894698", "url": "https://genius.com/1894698", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Top off like Wallace", "vault_lines": ["Top off like Wallace"], "meaning": "https://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5237526654001", "annotation_id": "1773952", "url": "https://genius.com/1773952", "state": "verified", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Got a Brinks truck in my pocket (Pocket)", "vault_lines": ["Got a Brinks truck in my pocket (Pocket)"], "meaning": "A Brinks truck is one that transports large amounts of money to/from places. Essentially, he has a lot of money in his possession.", "annotation_id": "1045116", "url": "https://genius.com/1045116", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "And, nigga, you’s a square And I will twist you like in a Rubik’s", "vault_lines": ["And, nigga, you's a square"], "meaning": "A Rubik’s Cube is a square puzzle. The goal is to twist in order to match all the colors on every side. Wayne will fuck you up to look like this:\n\n\n\nHe has also used the twist/Rubik’s pun in Birdman’s song “Fire Flame.” .", "annotation_id": "1024491", "url": "https://genius.com/1024491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Car’s tinted like Barack", "vault_lines": ["Car's tinted like Barack"], "meaning": "His windows are tinted super dark black just like the President’s windows so no one can see inside.\n\n\n\nThis line may also be referring to the colour of Barack Obama’s skin, meaning he is not fully black but has a ‘tinted’ skin colour, shaded white.", "annotation_id": "964136", "url": "https://genius.com/964136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Sorry that’s a habit, smoke a spliff and then I vanish", "vault_lines": ["Sorry that's a habit, smoke a spliff and then I vanish"], "meaning": "Rozay hits it and quits it: smoke’s a bitch’s weed, and then displays his disappearing act.\n\n\n\nOne could even say that he kept a “magician theme” over the last few lines: rabbits, disappearing, smoke?", "annotation_id": "944305", "url": "https://genius.com/944305", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Shout out my bitches too (Huh) We the 2 Live Crew Two for me, two for you (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Shout out to the infernos"], "meaning": "Ross puns on the name of his Miami rap forbears, 2 Live Crew.  The Crew’s head honcho was Luther Campbell, a.k.a. Uncle Luke, whose solo work is sampled in this very song", "annotation_id": "927296", "url": "https://genius.com/927296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "What you twerkin’ with?", "vault_lines": ["What you twerkin' with?"], "meaning": "Twerkin' is dancing that involves showing off your rear…ah hell, just go and watch some\n\nBesides being about twerking, it’s a play on words: “What you working with?” has commonly been used in rap songs to inquire about how well a woman can move her woman parts. French is asking her a question, knowing that the answer will come in the form of POPPING THAT.", "annotation_id": "927285", "url": "https://genius.com/927285", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Bitch! Stop talkin’ that shit And suck a nigga dick for some Trukfit", "vault_lines": ["Bitch! Stop talkin' that shit"], "meaning": "Wayne is referencing one of the most famous chants in all of bounce music; the New Orleans-created subgenre where Cash Money Records first made its name.  He has called back to this chant on previous occasions. This time, Wayne uses it to reference his own clothing line. (The original is “suck a nigga dick for an outfit.”)", "annotation_id": "926171", "url": "https://genius.com/926171", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I am rich like a bitch", "vault_lines": ["I am rich like a bitch"], "meaning": "This line makes no sense, partly because it was first said by Lil B. Weezy is infamously known for biting lyrics occasionally, so this shouldn’t be too shocking.\n\nLil B said this line in his song “Pretty Bitch” at the 2:48 mark.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vAYrMJWvC44\n\nLil B and Lil Wayne worked together on Wayne’s “Grove Street Party” which is on Weezy’s Sorry 4 the Wait mixtape. Lil B spit a very…based verse, and it may have impressed Wayne to the point of using one of his lines.\n\nMost likey, this is actually a reference to “I’m RICHHHHH BITCH”, the classic saying from Chappelle Show.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMFJBd40Awo", "annotation_id": "852007", "url": "https://genius.com/852007", "state": "accepted", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m a beast, I’m off the leash", "vault_lines": ["I'm a beast, I'm off the leash"], "meaning": "Very reminiscent of Wayne’s verse on We Takin' Over:\n\nI am the beast, feed me rappers or feed me beats  I’m untamed, I need a leash", "annotation_id": "844634", "url": "https://genius.com/844634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "It’s Truk the world It’s Truk yo girl", "vault_lines": ["It's Truk the world"], "meaning": "Wayne likes to use the word “Truck” instead of “fuck” as the slogan for his clothing brand Trukfit.\n\nHe uses it the exact same way in “My Homies Still.”", "annotation_id": "844073", "url": "https://genius.com/844073", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "YMCM beat that pussy up, stop playin’", "vault_lines": ["YMCM beat that pussy up, stop playin'"], "meaning": "Young Money Cash Money Billionaires (YMCMB) is Wayne’s label.\n\n\n\nHe plays off the last letter in “YMCMB”. Instead of stating the “B” he uses a word that starts with the letter “b”. .", "annotation_id": "843982", "url": "https://genius.com/843982", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "It’s French Montana, fuck Joe", "vault_lines": ["It's French Montana, fuck Joe"], "meaning": "Weezy says that French Montana is better than Joe Montana, one of the best quarterbacks of all time…", "annotation_id": "843930", "url": "https://genius.com/843930", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Feed them bitches carrots (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Feed them bitches carrots (Huh)"], "meaning": "Reference to oral sex, as carrots are also quite phallic; since the next line reveals this couplet to be about sex, “feeding” women “carrots” can be read as the conventional oral foreplay foreshadowing the next line’s intercourse.\n\nAlso a play on the word carrot/carat. Meaning the diamonds that he gives to his women and the rabbit reference in the next line\n\nThis is also a reference to the fact that rabbits mainly eat carrots, as rabbits are mentioned in the following line.", "annotation_id": "843920", "url": "https://genius.com/843920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m Young Papi, Champagne", "vault_lines": ["I'm Young Papi, Champagne"], "meaning": "Drake’s Instagram is Champagnepapi\n\nHe is also using ‘Papi’ as a pseudo-homophone for ‘Pop That’", "annotation_id": "843055", "url": "https://genius.com/843055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m the life of the party, let’s get these hoes on the Molly", "vault_lines": ["I'm the life of the party, let's get these hoes on the Molly"], "meaning": "Molly is a Pure form of MDMA (ecstasy), usually a free powder or in capsules. Oftentimes MDMA is sold as molly. Should be white in color (when it’s pure) but is more often beige or yellow-brown, and sometimes brown or rarely gray.\n\nIronically, Ross would later get in serious trouble for rapping about giving a girl molly.", "annotation_id": "842998", "url": "https://genius.com/842998", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Don’t stop, pop that, don’t stop Pop that, pop that, pop that", "vault_lines": ["Don't stop, pop that, don't stop"], "meaning": "Here is where the sample came from: Uncle Luke – “I Wanna Rock (Doo Doo Brown).” Classic.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jzHeR-PTVtY&feature=results_video&playnext=1&list=PL21B2E18688750B93", "annotation_id": "842483", "url": "https://genius.com/842483", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Money ain’t a thing but a chicken wing", "vault_lines": ["Money ain't a thing but a chicken wing"], "meaning": "“Ain’t no thing but a chicken wing” is southern slang that has been around for a while. It even found it’s way into the Outkast song “Ain’t No Thang” where it can be heard in the chorus. .", "annotation_id": "842474", "url": "https://genius.com/842474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "That’s gangsta: Al Capone", "vault_lines": ["That’s gangsta: Al Capone"], "meaning": "Al Capone is an old, Prohibition-era gangster who led a crime syndicate.\n\n\n\nFUN FACT: Al Capone’s physical and mental health deteriorated under the effects of neurosyphilis. Guess he really did “fuck a bitch and [be] gone.”", "annotation_id": "842311", "url": "https://genius.com/842311", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I make that pussy spit like Bone I’m talkin’ ’bout bone, bone, bone bone", "vault_lines": ["Pop that pussy, pussy"], "meaning": "A shout out to the Bone Thugs-n-Harmony, saying he makes girls come like how Bone Thugs rap (VERY fast). “Spitting” is his way of saying “squirting.”\n\n\n\nHe also said “bone” 5 times: one for each member of the group.", "annotation_id": "842299", "url": "https://genius.com/842299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Then beat that pussy like Klitschko", "vault_lines": ["Then beat that pussy like Klitschko"], "meaning": "He beats it up like the boxing Klitschko brothers.\n\n\n\nAlso, Wayne is playing on the sentence, using ‘pussy’ and ‘KLIT(clit)schko’.\n\nFun Fact: Wladimir Klitschko’s partner Hayden Panettiere is much smaller than him, so with that size difference, you can imagine him beating it up.", "annotation_id": "842277", "url": "https://genius.com/842277", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m fuckin’ with French, excuse my French", "vault_lines": ["I'm fuckin' with French, excuse my French"], "meaning": "A play on the phrase “excuse my French” which basically just means “sorry for cursing” (since he just said “fuckin' with French). Excuse My French is also the name of French Montana’s debut album.", "annotation_id": "842265", "url": "https://genius.com/842265", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Film it, film it, this bitch want me to film it Ballin’, ballin’ like I play for New England", "vault_lines": ["Film it, film it, this bitch want me to film it"], "meaning": "In their 2007 season, the New England Patriots started their season off with some controversy. In Week 2 head coach Bill Belichick and the Patriots were penalized by the NFL for their involvement in the videotaping of opponents' defensive signals from an unauthorized location in their Week 1 game against the New York Jets, referred to in the press as Spygate.\n\nThis line may also be referring to a horny female wanting Rick Ross to video record their sexual encounter.\n\nIronically, the New England Patriots NFL team has the best record in the league since 2001, and is the second most valuable team in the league according to Forbes and in those particular terms, Rozay does his fare share of winning.", "annotation_id": "842260", "url": "https://genius.com/842260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Local club in my city, I fell in love with a stripper", "vault_lines": ["Local club in my city, I fell in love with a stripper"], "meaning": "In January, Ross threw his birthday party at Amnesia in South Beach.\n\nLike T-Pain, he’s in love with a stripperrr", "annotation_id": "842252", "url": "https://genius.com/842252", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m in that white ghost chasin’ Pac-Man Hundred out the lot,", "vault_lines": ["I'm in that white ghost chasin' Pac-Man"], "meaning": "Rolls-Royce Phantoms, (in this case a $100.000 one,) have the nickname “Ghosts”, but they actually make a Ghost which is new to the RR lineup. French may be referring to either one.\n\n\n\nIn the arcade game Pac-Man, ghosts chase PacMan around the game. Although there is technically no white ghost, he is referring to the ghosts in general", "annotation_id": "842192", "url": "https://genius.com/842192", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m Young Papi, Champagne", "vault_lines": ["I'm Young Papi, Champagne"], "meaning": "One of Drake’s well known monikers (and Instagram name), especially around the ova circle is “Champagne Papi” which refers to his extensive love for wine and champagne.", "annotation_id": "840125", "url": "https://genius.com/840125", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Money comin’, money goin’, ain’t like you could take it with you (Alright)", "vault_lines": ["Money comin', money goin', ain't like you could take it with you (Alright)"], "meaning": "Drake and his crew are making money but spending it too because, like the line from the musical says, you can’t take it with you (when you die)\n\nDrake might be Jewish, but this is also a lesson from the New Testament, 1 Timothy 6:7\n\nFor we brought nothing into this world, and it is certain we can carry nothing out.\n\nPotentially a response to Pusha T, who said in Exodus 23:1 wealth don’t buy health, drake is telling him he would rather spend it he can’t take it with him", "annotation_id": "840094", "url": "https://genius.com/840094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Greystone, twenty bottles that’s all me", "vault_lines": ["Greystone, twenty bottles that's all me"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to the extremely popular Greystone Manor nightclub in Hollywood. He is usually there on Sundays as it’s a hip-hop night. Proof: http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UXgQ4BFGNH4", "annotation_id": "839759", "url": "https://genius.com/839759", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "One of my closest dawgs got three kids and they all three But we always been that type of crew that been good without a plan B, so", "vault_lines": ["One of my closest dawgs got three kids and they all three"], "meaning": "Drake’s crew has never been the type to need a backup plan, while also throwing in the Plan B line relating to his homie and his kids.\n\nNotice the slick homophone of “been good” and “be in good” – as in they get shit done without a back-up plan, the same way they be in “good” (pussy) without the morning-after pill.", "annotation_id": "839720", "url": "https://genius.com/839720", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Only thing you got is some years on me Man, fuck you and your time difference", "vault_lines": ["Only thing you got is some years on me"], "meaning": "Seems like lines directed at Pusha T, considering Pusha had some words for Drake recently. Also, Pusha is 35, while Drake is 25.\n\nDrake is also referencing Pusha T’s “I Don’t Like” verse, when Pusha says “Dope money, coke money/Hublot, my watch better.”\n\nBut besides Pusha, this is a possible shot at a few rappers older than him or have been/were rapping before him (i.e. DMX, Fabulous, Common, Ludacris). .\n\nNote: Pusha might’ve shot back at Drake with this line from “Blocka”. Both lines use “fuck you and your…”\n\nI ball hard and you bench ride, so fuck you and yo' bassline!", "annotation_id": "839716", "url": "https://genius.com/839716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Gettin cheddar packs like K.D., OKC that’s player shit", "vault_lines": ["Gettin cheddar packs like K.D., OKC that's player shit"], "meaning": "Drake tweeted this line not too long ago.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/209186783970340865\n\nDrizzy gets cheddar (money) like KD which stands for both Kraft Dinner, a brand of macaroni and cheese, and NBA player Kevin Durant. OKC is Durant’s team, Oklahoma City, and also means “Okay, see that’s player shit”.\n\nThe Oklahoma City reference does not come out of the blue.  Drake and his entourage shut down an Oklahoma City night club after massive amounts of marijuana smoke was seen coming out of the VIP section. Drake & Co escaped unscathed, however, the night club owner is suing for damages.\n\nKevin Durant is loving the exposure: https://twitter.com/KDTrey5/status/244635730364731392\n\nIt should also note that calling Kraft Mac and Cheese “KD” is a Canadian thing.\n\nAlso Kevin Durant and Drake had the same net worth at the time.", "annotation_id": "839696", "url": "https://genius.com/839696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "We don’t dress alike, we don’t rap alike I shine different, I rhyme different", "vault_lines": ["We don't dress alike, we don't rap alike"], "meaning": "Drake has often been accused of stealing the “Supa Dupa flow” style that he used early in his career.", "annotation_id": "839690", "url": "https://genius.com/839690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I hope you pussy niggas hatin’ never make a nickel (Right)", "vault_lines": ["I hope you pussy niggas hatin' never make a nickel (Right)"], "meaning": "Drake is taking a subliminal shot at numerous rappers dissing him right now (Pusha-T, Fabolous, and all others )\n\nAlso many believe that some rappers will create beef with another rapper to promote an album. Drake believes that Common did this with “Sweet” (before they squashed their beef) as he stated on “Stay Schemin”\n\nThis is also a play on the expression ‘I hope you never make a dime’. By saying nickel instead of dime, Drake shows his true dislike of his haters.", "annotation_id": "839682", "url": "https://genius.com/839682", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "OVO, that’s major shit, Toronto with me, that’s mayor shit", "vault_lines": ["OVO, that's major shit, Toronto with me, that's mayor shit"], "meaning": "OVO (Drake’s music group October’s Very Own) is up and rising and becoming a major part of his career.\n\nToronto is his hometown and he will never forget that. Watch out, Rob Ford!", "annotation_id": "839679", "url": "https://genius.com/839679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m about bein’ single, seein’ double, makin’ triple (Right)", "vault_lines": ["I'm about bein' single, seein' double, makin' triple (Right)"], "meaning": "Drake is all about no strings attached relationships (I mean, you only live once right?), getting drunk, and making three times as much money. Single, double, triple. Get it?", "annotation_id": "839673", "url": "https://genius.com/839673", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I go by the name Lil Tunechi", "vault_lines": ["I go by the name Lil Tunechi"], "meaning": "One of Lil Waynes many nicknames, ‘@LilTunechi’ is also his Twitter handle. It’s comprised of ‘Tune’ which was a nickname given to Wayne by his grandmother, and ‘chi’ which was added by Wayne to make it sound like ‘Gucci’, the clothing brand.", "annotation_id": "839651", "url": "https://genius.com/839651", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
