{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop Bottles", "line": "I am the Birdman", "vault_lines": ["I am the Birdman"], "meaning": "Birdman makes sure to make his identity (Birdman) clear, just in case the listener didn’t know or needed confirmation.", "annotation_id": "35138578", "url": "https://genius.com/35138578", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop Bottles", "line": "I made too much money, I ain’t make enough yet", "vault_lines": ["I made too much money, I ain't make enough yet"], "meaning": "Whereas a normal rapper would say that they made too much money and leave it at that, or say that they made too much money and explain how that is a bad thing, Birdman instead choses to pose an interesting paradox, claiming that although he has made too much money, he has simultaneously has not made enough. With this line, Birdman challenges the listener to think: how is it possible that he has simultaneously made too much and too little money? Ultimately, Birdman does not resolve this paradox, leaving it up to the listener. Clever bars like these are why Birdman is widely considered one of the greats.", "annotation_id": "35138491", "url": "https://genius.com/35138491", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop Bottles", "line": "I lost too many friends, but I won too many bets", "vault_lines": ["I lost too many friends, but I won too many bets"], "meaning": "Birdman briefly shouts out those who have died, but draws a direct contradiction with the amount of money that he’s made, saying that even though he has undergone emotional turmoil, it has not prevented him from finding financial success.", "annotation_id": "35138480", "url": "https://genius.com/35138480", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop Bottles", "line": "I ain’t got a lot of Nikes but I got a lot of checks (money)", "vault_lines": ["I ain't got a lot of Nikes but I got a lot of checks (money)"], "meaning": "Birdman claims that he does not have a lot of Nikes, a popular shoe brand, but that he does have a lot of checks (with an ad-lib saying “money” clarifying that he is referring to the financial term). This is a clever line, as the Nike logo’s swoosh looks similar to a check mark. Even though Birdman does not have lot of Nikes, presumably out of personal preference (given his money, he could likely afford as many Nikes as he wants), he has money nevertheless.", "annotation_id": "35138458", "url": "https://genius.com/35138458", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop Bottles", "line": "From shittin’ in a cell, to shittin’ on a jet", "vault_lines": ["From shittin' in a cell, to shittin' on a jet"], "meaning": "Birdman cleverly doubles up on the cell-jet comparison, going from merely sitting in a cell/jet to shitting in a cell/jet, showing how life in both a cell and a jet are not always glamorous.", "annotation_id": "35138448", "url": "https://genius.com/35138448", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
