{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop Bottles", "line": "All my cars automative, automatic No lie, we don’t even drive no Aston", "vault_lines": ["All my cars automative, automatic"], "meaning": "The DBS – Aston Martin’s most baller model – doesn’t come in automatic, so even though it’s a nice car, he’s not interested\n\n(Birdman likes to have a free hand while driving to give thigh massage, wave to friends, and – most importantly – play with his iPhone)", "annotation_id": "3747", "url": "https://genius.com/3747", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop Bottles", "line": "So many niggas from my hood on they back So many niggas from your hood on they back That’s why we so paid and it be like that I’d rather pop a bottle, before I pop a gat", "vault_lines": ["So many niggas from my hood on they back"], "meaning": "Birdman is like Gandhi; so many people from all of our hoods are now dead, and Birdman knows that these dead men have enabled his rise\n\nHe doesn’t want to increase the death toll needlessly, so he prefers to celebrate life by popping champagne rather than to propagate death by shooting guns", "annotation_id": "3741", "url": "https://genius.com/3741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop Bottles", "line": "So I scratch, and yes, Junior is the best", "vault_lines": ["So I scratch, and yes, Junior is the best"], "meaning": "Clever pun here with scratch: scratch-off lottery tickets make you rich (if you win). “Scratching” is also synonymous with “hustling”\n\nHowever, it also means “from scratch” as in “making something from scratch”. “Jr.” (Lil Wayne) – who Birdman is claiming to have “scratched”, i.e. made from scratch – became more successful than Birdman ever was. Weezy is ultimately Birdman’s greatest venture", "annotation_id": "3738", "url": "https://genius.com/3738", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pop Bottles", "line": "Straight up out that water with my Marc Jacobs goggles", "vault_lines": ["Straight up out that water with my Marc Jacobs goggles"], "meaning": "In Wayne’s world “the water” means the hood in New Orleans, (which was underwater after Katrina, built on top of water etc.). So he’s sayings he is straight out of the N.O. hood wearing expensive sunglasses\n\nWayne in Marc Jacobs “goggles”:", "annotation_id": "3708", "url": "https://genius.com/3708", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
