{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Checking in the same hotel, in the same suite, bitch Same balcony, like, “Assassinate me, bitch”", "vault_lines": ["So assassinate me, bitch"], "meaning": "Martin Luther King, Jr. was shot to death while he was standing on the balcony of room 306 at the Lorraine Motel in Memphis, Tennessee. James Earl Ray was believed to have been behind King’s assassination, and was found not guilty at his trial.\n\n\n\nKing and affiliates standing on the balcony where he would be shot in the face only moments later.", "annotation_id": "17552297", "url": "https://genius.com/17552297", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "I don’t rap, I film movies With my rap", "vault_lines": ["I don't rap, I film movies"], "meaning": "Lil Tunechi’s art defies easy categorization, and his lyrics frequently have a cinematic quality; hence, e.g., the encouragement from “I’m Me,” a track originally also intended for inclusion on Tha Carter III, to “let your eyes listen”.", "annotation_id": "14512806", "url": "https://genius.com/14512806", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "[Chorus: Betty Wright & Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": ["But the bitch say I'm hot, and I say, \"No, bitch, I'm blazin'\""], "meaning": "As StreetRunner told XXL:\n\nBetty Wright’s one of the old school singers from the late ‘60s/early ‘70s. I wanted that big old school voice. My attorney was doing some things for her and he mentioned her. She’s from Miami so I was able to just get the mp3 of the hook. I told [Lil Wayne’s engineer], Fabian, when we were going to mix down, “We gotta make her sound like a sample.” He put the effect to her voice to make it sound big, but at the same time gave it a little dirt with the record crackle in there. Once Wayne heard that it was a wrap. It kind of made it new a new record. The drums were the same [as when Wayne first recorded it], but I added the guitars, more strings, and put Betty Wright on it. Sometimes that’s good to do if you don’t change the feel because you can make the artist fall back in love with the record if they were sort of losing their interest.\n\nUnfortunately, the content of Wright’s part was too similar to the uncredited Rolling Stones song “Play With Fire,” and the entire song was removed from the album due to a lawsuit.", "annotation_id": "4187753", "url": "https://genius.com/4187753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "And she don’t play neither", "vault_lines": ["And she don't play neither"], "meaning": "Wayne’s mother Jacida Carter also known as  ‘Cita’, is just as outspoken and brave as her son. She released this statement after false rumors of Weezy’s death were spread through the media in 2013:\n\n“Fuck all you greedy whore lying media scum, taking my poor baby’s lil’ drug problem and blowing it up like that!", "annotation_id": "3289286", "url": "https://genius.com/3289286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "You follow and I lead you, straight to the needles", "vault_lines": ["You follow and I lead you, straight to the needles"], "meaning": "Wordplay:\n\n\nJuxtaposing words: follow/lead.\n\n\n\nInternal Rhyme:\n\nYou follow and I lead you straight to the needle\n\nMetaphor:\n\n\nWeezy compares ‘the needle’ to death. The needle of death is likely referring to the lethal injection.", "annotation_id": "2874800", "url": "https://genius.com/2874800", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Braveheart, bitch, like the times are medieval", "vault_lines": ["Braveheart, bitch, like the times are medieval"], "meaning": "Like the leader of Braveheart had to overcome immense challenges to reach his goal, Wayne had to overcome the struggles of pushing drugs on the streets.", "annotation_id": "1674375", "url": "https://genius.com/1674375", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "[Verse 3: Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": ["But the bitch say I'm hot, and I say, \"No, bitch, I'm blazin'\""], "meaning": "This verse was originally from the song ‘’World Of Fantasy‘’ off ‘'The Drought Is Over 2’‘.", "annotation_id": "1586876", "url": "https://genius.com/1586876", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Forced into evil, it’s all in your head It’s all so cerebral,", "vault_lines": ["Forced into evil, it's all in your head"], "meaning": "The cerebellum is a region of the brain that plays an important role in motor control – obviously located in the brain.\n\nWayne proclaims that getting “trapped” into the drug game is just an illusion they use to try and keep themselves in. It’s not hard to stop selling and get out like Wayne did.", "annotation_id": "1103784", "url": "https://genius.com/1103784", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "And you know what they say, when you great It’s not “murder,” it’s “assassinate” So assassinate me, bitch", "vault_lines": ["And you know what they say, when you great"], "meaning": "If you’re great in the eyes of the public (Like historic figures such as John F. Kennedy, Abraham Lincoln and Martin Luther King, JR), if you get murdered, there’s always one term the media loves to use: assassination.\n\nLil Wayne, at this point of his career, was also held in high regards when it came to hip-hop, possibly rivaling the before mentioned The Notorious B.I.G, who infamously started the saying “You’re nobody till somebody kills you”, in his song of the same name.\n\nSince he’s so great at this time, he feels like somebody is going to assassinate him so they can get famous, and boldly dares them to try to do so.", "annotation_id": "1036010", "url": "https://genius.com/1036010", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Bitch, I Kix it No cereal", "vault_lines": ["bitch, I Kix it"], "meaning": "Repeating the line above, “I kick it”.\nBut no, not the cereal silly!", "annotation_id": "1012888", "url": "https://genius.com/1012888", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Standin’ on the corner sellin’ porcelain to people", "vault_lines": ["Standin' on the corner sellin' porcelain to people"], "meaning": "Wayne used to sell drugs on corners to people. When you make crack, you have to cook it, similar to the process for creating porcelain dishes. It goes from a powder to something hard. Crack is also bright white, the same pure color as fine porcelain.", "annotation_id": "962918", "url": "https://genius.com/962918", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "’Cause I’m doing the same shit Martin Luther King did", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I'm doing the same shit Martin Luther King did"], "meaning": "Wayne is having a giant impact on the world. Wayne’s album Tha Carter III sold 1 million copies in it’s first week, so yeah, I guess you can say Wayne’s had quite the impact.", "annotation_id": "957498", "url": "https://genius.com/957498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Well, where I’m from, you’re nobody ’til you kill somebody", "vault_lines": ["Well, where I'm from, you're nobody 'til you kill somebody"], "meaning": "This line is a play on The Notorious B.I.G. song You’re Nobody (Til Somebody Kills you) (which is explained in the line above). Where Wayne grew up (New Orleans) instead of being unknown until you get killed, it is the opposite, you are unknown until you kill someone.", "annotation_id": "957496", "url": "https://genius.com/957496", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "”That’s too explicit”, well, why you listenin’?", "vault_lines": ["\"That's too explicit\", well, why you listenin'?"], "meaning": "If you don’t like it, don’t listen to it.\n\nCoincidentally, one of Abkco’s complaints in their copyright lawsuit that go this song removed from the album was (via Rueters):\n\nAbkco also said that Lil Wayne’s version uses “explicit, sexist and offensive language” and could lead the public to believe the company and the Rolling Stones approved of and authorized the new version.", "annotation_id": "957493", "url": "https://genius.com/957493", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "So you’ve got so many diamonds You wear all the finest clothes And your grill is shining As you’re driving down the streets of gold But you can’t blame me If I set this stage on fire", "vault_lines": ["So you've got so many diamonds"], "meaning": "In “Play With Fire,” The Rolling Stones sang (bold for similarities):\n\nWell, you’ve got your diamonds and you’ve got your pretty clothes\nAnd the chauffeur drives your car\nYou let everybody know\nBut don’t play with me, cause you’re playing with fire\n\nAs a result, Abkco Music Inc sued for copyright infringement and unfair competition, and the song had to be removed from the album.", "annotation_id": "364774", "url": "https://genius.com/364774", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Some say the X makes the sex spec’", "vault_lines": ["Some say the X makes the sex spec'"], "meaning": "A reference to the Notorious B.I.G.’s song “Fuck You Tonight”", "annotation_id": "120087", "url": "https://genius.com/120087", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "3 Peat", "vault_lines": ["But the bitch say I'm hot, and I say, \"No, bitch, I'm blazin'\""], "meaning": "A song on Tha Carter III.  The term ‘3-peat’ means to do the same action three times in succession, in this case Wayne is talking about releasing the third in his series of Tha Carter albums. Tha Carter III went 3x Platinum.", "annotation_id": "113464", "url": "https://genius.com/113464", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Osh B’Gosh,", "vault_lines": ["But the bitch say I'm hot, and I say, \"No, bitch, I'm blazin'\""], "meaning": "OshKosh B'Gosh is a children’s clothing company.\n\n\n\nInstead of saying “Oh my gosh”, Lil Wayne uses a variation of the company’s name.", "annotation_id": "113461", "url": "https://genius.com/113461", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Posh Spice husband Couldn’t kick it like I kick it,", "vault_lines": ["Couldn't kick it like I kick it,"], "meaning": "David Beckham, that is…\n\n\n\nPosh Spice’s husband, David Beckham, plays soccer. “Kick” is used a double entendre here, as kicking a ball is Beckham’s job and kicking rhymes is Weezy’s job.", "annotation_id": "96653", "url": "https://genius.com/96653", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Momma named Cita—I love you, Cita", "vault_lines": ["Momma named Cita—I love you, Cita"], "meaning": "Wayne’s mothers name is Ms. Cita. He loves his momma. This begins by highlighting the close relationship he & his mother shared.", "annotation_id": "55123", "url": "https://genius.com/55123", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Straight off the corner of Apple and Eagle", "vault_lines": ["Straight off the corner of Apple and Eagle"], "meaning": "Wayne grew up on Eagle Street in New Orleans' Hollygrove neighborhood. He sold drugs at the corner of Apple St. and Eagle St.", "annotation_id": "55121", "url": "https://genius.com/55121", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "They say, ”You’re nobody ’til somebody kills you", "vault_lines": ["They say, \"You're nobody 'til somebody kills you"], "meaning": "You aren’t successful unless you’re successful enough that someone would be willing to kill you out of jealousy\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to “You’re Nobody (Til Somebody Kills You)” by Notorious B.I.G.", "annotation_id": "55110", "url": "https://genius.com/55110", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Like, what the fuck you expect? I’m a motherfuckin’ Cajun", "vault_lines": ["Like, what the fuck you expect? I'm a motherfuckin' Cajun"], "meaning": "Cajuns is a region of Southern Louisiana known as Acadiana. Wayne, a native of New Orleans, which many consider to be in the jurisdictions of Acadiana, is including himself in this French culture, that also plays a major part in identity and culture of New Orleans. Cajun food and attitude is hot and spicy, just like Wayne – he’s always on fire.", "annotation_id": "51559", "url": "https://genius.com/51559", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Call me Knievel", "vault_lines": [", you could call me"], "meaning": "Evel Knievel, the late famous daredevil.", "annotation_id": "50605", "url": "https://genius.com/50605", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Playing with Fire", "line": "Married to the game, divorced the cathedral", "vault_lines": ["Married to the game, divorced the cathedral"], "meaning": "Dependence on selling drugs has shaken his faith in God, and his focus became making money. A popular analogy in rap is “married to the money, but in order for him to be fully committed to said money, he had to divorce or separate himself from religion.” It’s the only way to stay faithful.\n\nThis also plays off of the “medieval” reference above – most of the big cathedrals were built during the High Middle Ages.", "annotation_id": "50602", "url": "https://genius.com/50602", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
