{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pistoolloop", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-pistoolloop-lyrics", "genius_title": "Pistoolloop", "genius_id": 540547, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pistol On My Side (P.O.M.S.)", "line": "Pistol in my briefs, you don’t wanna get this brief message", "vault_lines": ["Pistol in my briefs, you don't wanna get this brief message"], "meaning": "This is a play on words from Wayne he has a pistol in his briefs (underwear) and is simply saying you don’t want this brief message meaning his pistol", "annotation_id": "15380734", "url": "https://genius.com/15380734", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pistol On My Side (P.O.M.S.)", "line": "Nina on my side, but she say you can call her “Nine” (Damn)", "vault_lines": ["Nina on my side, but she say you can call her \"Nine\" (Damn)"], "meaning": "Nina is a Spanish female’s name. The name however is also used as a slang term for a 9 mm handgun. This allows the term to be used with much versatility. Nina, in this case, refers to Lil Wayne’s 9 mm, which he let’s us know is “on [his] side”.", "annotation_id": "15373105", "url": "https://genius.com/15373105", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pistol On My Side (P.O.M.S.)", "line": "Tunechi in this bitch, eyes lookin’ like Konnichiwa (What?)", "vault_lines": ["Tunechi in this bitch, eyes lookin' like Konnichiwa (What?)"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is known for his avid drug use, meaning he his high off of the influence of drugs almost all of the time. When Wayne is so high, his eyes are hanging low and barely open.\n\nKonnichiwa is a common greeting for “hello” in Japan and Wayne is comparing his eyes being closed to those of a Japanese person.", "annotation_id": "15372819", "url": "https://genius.com/15372819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pistol On My Side (P.O.M.S.)", "line": "Pistol on my side, you don’t wanna hear it harmonize (Say what?)", "vault_lines": ["Pistol on my side, you don't wanna hear it harmonize (Say what?)"], "meaning": "The base word of harmonize is ”harmony”. The definition of harmony is the combination of simultaneous musical notes in a chord.\n\nWayne is telling his adversaries they do not want to hear the pistol “harmonize”, meaning his pistol will be joining the sounds of his people’s pistols.", "annotation_id": "15372765", "url": "https://genius.com/15372765", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pistol On My Side (P.O.M.S.)", "line": "Pistol on my side, you don’t want that thing to scream at ya (Oh) Laughin’ when you die, boy, my pistol a comedian (Brr) Pistol on my side, now he lyin’ like the media (Work)", "vault_lines": ["Pistol on my side, you don't want that thing to scream at ya (Oh)"], "meaning": "In this extended simile, Wayne “personifies” his pistol, which is a fancy way of saying that he presents his weapon as an alive person.\n\nWith that in mind, “screaming” means that it’s firing, while it continues to fire even after somebody’s killed and when it’s time for the police report, it is nowhere to be found.\n\nScreaming at people, laughing at the dead and telling lies… Mr. Pistol sounds like a bit of a douche…", "annotation_id": "15369712", "url": "https://genius.com/15369712", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pistol On My Side (P.O.M.S.)", "line": "Numbers don’t lie, the Number One Stun— never mind (Goddamn)", "vault_lines": ["Numbers don't lie, the Number One Stun— never mind (Goddamn)"], "meaning": "Put by Jay Z himself;\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FIwxIobtab4\n\nWith 138 total entries on Billboard’s Hot 100, 20 of them being in the top 10 and with three #1 albums, all amongst other achievements, Wayne’s case is no different.\n\nWith a long lasting career and a huge musical catalogue, his work ethic is undeniable. Since he has also birthed Drake and Nicki Minaj’s extremely successful careers too, he might as well be the “Number One Stunna”, a nickname mostly used for his mentor, Bryan “Birdman” Williams.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RfYFnQaGXEI\n\nThe “never mind” at the end of the line indicates that Wayne probably isn’t very fond of that nickname after all, since the infamous Cash Money fallout.", "annotation_id": "15369615", "url": "https://genius.com/15369615", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
