{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "She said she wanted sprinkles, I said sprinkles are for winners", "vault_lines": ["She said she wanted sprinkles, I said sprinkles are for winners"], "meaning": "“Sprinkles are for winners” is a reference to the Progressive Insurance commercial, “After School Special.”\nhttps://youtu.be/Bw_Vdno_xMA", "annotation_id": "22216756", "url": "https://genius.com/22216756", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "I’ve come to a stage in my life And I just can’t let my life boo me off stage, no Tuxedo on and a cumberbund Fingers crossed behind my back On the corner, watching my money come", "vault_lines": ["I've come to a stage in my life"], "meaning": "Wayne feels like he’s coming to a point in his life where he has to step out completely on his own. He doesn’t want a few bad things that happened in his life to keep him from being the best at what he does. He’s determined to do it formally and professionally. The tuxedo and cummerbund may also symbolize how he is “married to the money.”\n\nThis might be a shot at Young Thug who was booed on stage while performing at Southern University in April, the same night that shots were fired at Lil Wayne’s tour bus after his performance in Atlanta.", "annotation_id": "7463348", "url": "https://genius.com/7463348", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "Molly in the Kool-Aid, we put molly in the Kool-Aid, uh", "vault_lines": ["Molly in the Kool-Aid, we put molly in the Kool-Aid, uh"], "meaning": "Weezy seems to be attempting to date rape his girl. For those who do not know, date raping is when you spike ones drink in order to get them to consent to intercourse.\n\nWayne probably chose Kool-Aid for a reason. For a start, he may be represent his red, Blood Gang. Also, Wayne, who buys into a lot of stereotypes, might be utilizing the African American Kool-Aid stereotype.", "annotation_id": "7451790", "url": "https://genius.com/7451790", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "Ooh, I’m on a new wave", "vault_lines": ["Ooh, I'm on a new wave"], "meaning": "Wayne is living and rapping differently than he was before. “New wave” is generally slang used for saying that one is living differently.\n\nWayne could also continue the film theme he has been using for the last several lines; using the phrase “New Wave”, which is an artistic movement that arose in film during the 50’s and 60’s in France.\n\nWeezy uses the idea of a “new wave” to describe his own style as well; not only he is associating his own artistic creativity with the new styles and techniques brought into film-making by new cinema wave, but also generally, it indicates that Wayne is on the cutting edge or ahead of the curve, mentally and socially.", "annotation_id": "7270328", "url": "https://genius.com/7270328", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "But I gotta get that paper, baby, that paper, baby That paper, baby, that paper, baby ’Cause this game fuck everybody, this game fuck everybody Gotta get that paper, baby, that paper, baby, that paper, babe Yeah, ’cause these streets fuck everybody, these streets fuck everybody Gotta get my paper, babe, my paper, babe, my paper, babe Yeah, ’cause these hoes fuck anybody, these hoes fuck anybody Gotta get my paper, baby, my paper, baby, my paper, baby Yeah, ’cause these hoes fuck anybody, these hoes fuck anybody And I don’t wanna do it no more, no Hold up, bae, I don’t wanna do it no more, no Hold up, wait, I don’t wanna do it no more, no Hold up, bae, I don’t wanna do it no more, no But I gotta get my paper, babe, uh", "vault_lines": ["But I gotta get that paper, baby, that paper, baby"], "meaning": "“Paper” is common slang for money. Wayne was famously screwed over by Cash Money Records and its co founder, Bryan “Birdman” Williams in 2014. In a 21-page document, Wayne sued Cash Money for $51 million, citing a wide range of alleged financial misdeeds. “The game” is common terminology for the rap business. Wayne has been “fucked” by the game, and the only consolidation is “paper,” in this case $51 million.\n\nIn this hook, Wayne also outlines that he’s been getting fucked his whole life, by the streets and, more literally, by “hoes.” The “hoes” in this line could serve as a diss towards Cash Money Records, or literally mean slutty women or prostitutes, the latter of which will fuck anyone with enough “paper.”\n\nWhen Wayne exclaims that “I don’t want to do it no more,” he is expressing one of the main themes of the album: freedom. In fact, The album is titled The Free Weezy Album. Wayne is tired of being screwed over, but the money keeps him going.", "annotation_id": "7234109", "url": "https://genius.com/7234109", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "World on my back, shit feel like a mink", "vault_lines": ["World on my back, shit feel like a mink"], "meaning": "“World on my back” is a reference to the myth of the Titan Atlas, who was forced to hold the sky on his back for surviving.\n\nMink coat is a fur jacket made from the hide of a mink, a weasel-like animal. It is known for being one of the heaviest types of clothes.\n\nWayne is living in a crooked world, has a lot of pressure on him, and everyone is depending on him. He plays on words by expressing how he mentally got the world on his shoulders, as if he is physically wearing a mink.\n\nMink is very comfortable and luxurious, so he’s saying that for him, even carrying the ‘weight of the world’ on his shoulders is no trouble, it feels like an expensive fur coat, not like a burden.\n\nTunechi has a similar line of this in “God Bless Amerika”, which is off IANAHB II:\n\nIt’s a cold world, I put on a mink", "annotation_id": "7230157", "url": "https://genius.com/7230157", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "Free Weezy Mula", "vault_lines": ["She on her back screaming she love me, yeah"], "meaning": "Weezy is finally free from his Cash Money problems, being that this album is released by Young Money Entertainment.", "annotation_id": "7225280", "url": "https://genius.com/7225280", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "Yesterday, I met a woman on the stairs that wasn’t there She wasn’t there again today I really hope she go away", "vault_lines": ["Yesterday, I met a woman on the stairs that wasn't there"], "meaning": "Reference to a poem “Antigonish” by William Hughes Mearns, the first stanza of which is:\n\nYesterday upon the stair\nI met a man who wasn’t there\nHe wasn’t there again today\nI wish, I wish he’d go away\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Sx3Zr0kwZCw\n\nThis poem is about a ghost of a man roaming the stairs of a haunted house. It is surely straightforward and without depth. The feeling that remains is indeed deep, ominous and even slightly melancholic.\n\nLil Wayne feels haunted by this woman who doesn’t exist, and hopes to be left alone. It could also allude to the latest problems with Birdman, and Cash Money.", "annotation_id": "7224505", "url": "https://genius.com/7224505", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "Wait, bitch [Verse 1] I hop in my Phantom and drive ’til my phone start roamin’, yeah Lord, I don’t wan’ talk to nobody, I want my moment, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I hop in my Phantom and drive 'til my phone start roamin', yeah"], "meaning": "A phone goes into roaming mode when it’s taken outside of its geographical coverage area. In other words, Wayne’s willing to drive to another country to get some peace of mind.", "annotation_id": "7221907", "url": "https://genius.com/7221907", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "Please pardon my restroom, but Tunechi got the longest shit list, uh", "vault_lines": ["Please pardon my restroom, but Tunechi got the longest shit list, uh"], "meaning": "A “shit list” is a metaphorical list of people who you dislike/have beef with. Considering all the recent events, it’s pretty fair to say that Wayne’s list has probably gotten longer.", "annotation_id": "7221856", "url": "https://genius.com/7221856", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "I been out here doing me by myself, nigga, no special features", "vault_lines": ["I been out here doing me by myself, nigga, no special features"], "meaning": "He got his name out on the streets with just being himself, and without any help of others.\n\n\n\nAs said in https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-by-myself-lyrics/ he really doesn’t need anybody!", "annotation_id": "7221760", "url": "https://genius.com/7221760", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "It’s all about the Benjamins, no disrespect to Aretha", "vault_lines": ["It's all about the Benjamins, no disrespect to Aretha"], "meaning": "Wayne’s all about his money – Benjamin Franklin is pictured on the $100 bill. Aretha Franklin’s most notable hit is her 1967 release, “Respect.”\n\nNote the extra allusion to Diddy’s “It’s All About the Benjamins.”", "annotation_id": "7221170", "url": "https://genius.com/7221170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Pick Up Your Heart", "line": "I moved to Cali, had to leave the beach alone", "vault_lines": ["I moved to Cali, had to leave the beach alone"], "meaning": "Wayne has a house in LA, and he recently put his Miami mansion up for sale after he was targeted for “swatting” and suspicious people roaming the property.\n\nAlso notice the homophone of beach/bitch. He had to leave the old bitch, as he mentioned in the previous line being with a new one.", "annotation_id": "7220152", "url": "https://genius.com/7220152", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
