{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Piano Trap", "line": "They shoot like Türkoğlu", "vault_lines": ["Them Uzis get so surgical, shooters, they shoot like Türkoğlu"], "meaning": "Wayne refrences Hedo Türkoğlu, the Turkish NBA player who played for 15 seasons on teams like the Raptors, Magic, and Clippers.", "annotation_id": "19907139", "url": "https://genius.com/19907139", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Piano Trap", "line": "Leave it lookin’ like January 2nd, July 5th", "vault_lines": ["Leave it lookin' like January 2nd, July 5th"], "meaning": "January 2nd and July 5th are the days after New Year’s Day and America’s Independence Day, respectively. These two holidays are traditionally celebrated by lighting large amounts of fireworks and firecrackers. The aftermath of these two days are often gunpower, shrapnel, and remnants of explosives scattered around. Wayne’s implying heavy gunfire in the house which he breaks in, leaving it looking like the aftermath of these holidays.", "annotation_id": "19907095", "url": "https://genius.com/19907095", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Piano Trap", "line": "Took a few Ls, without ’em, I couldn’t spell “life”", "vault_lines": ["Took a few Ls, without 'em, I couldn't spell \"life\""], "meaning": "Taking an L is informal for taking a (L)oss or accepting defeat. The same way the word  “life” can’t be spelled without the letter L, Wayne is willing to acknowledge that he did not make it in life without taking any losses or any kind of failure.\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: “Few Ls” speLL Life. 3 Ls in the 2 words.", "annotation_id": "19687292", "url": "https://genius.com/19687292", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Piano Trap", "line": "Banana clip, big banana up in her tailpipe", "vault_lines": ["Banana clip, big banana up in her tailpipe"], "meaning": "A play on words that references two scenes in Beverly Hills Cop:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K7APP2z1yqU\n\nAdditionally, a banana clip goes in an AK-47, one of Lil Tunechi’s favorite topics, the chopper.", "annotation_id": "19428507", "url": "https://genius.com/19428507", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Piano Trap", "line": "You disappear like abracadabra, magic like 32", "vault_lines": ["You disappear like abracadabra, magic like 32"], "meaning": "This line contains a sly reference to Magic Johnson, who’s basketball jersey was number 32.", "annotation_id": "18957182", "url": "https://genius.com/18957182", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Piano Trap", "line": "Mags and millions, man, ask Eminem", "vault_lines": ["Mags and millions, man, ask Eminem"], "meaning": "Here Lil Wayne shouts out his collaborator and peer, Eminem, by playing on words that start with the letter M, similar to Marshall Mathers' initials.", "annotation_id": "18957172", "url": "https://genius.com/18957172", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
