{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "Ice water chest, and my wrist like a cool cup", "vault_lines": ["Ice water chest, and my wrist like a cool cup"], "meaning": "Weezy is here touting the “iciness” (bling value) of his chains and watches.\n\nMy watch an Icee and my chain a Frostee\n- “South Muzik,” Dedication 2\n\nA “cool cup” is a homemade frozen treat (essentially = Kool-Aide frozen in a styrofoam or paper cup).", "annotation_id": "14053635", "url": "https://genius.com/14053635", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "Hip hop is my supermarket Shopping cart full of fake hip-hop artists I’m starving, sorry, I gotta eat all it And I’ll be back in the morning", "vault_lines": ["Hip hop is my supermarket"], "meaning": "A nice variation on Weezy’s frequent theme of devouring the competition. See, for example, the intro to “We Takin' Over (Remix)” from Da Drought 3:\n\nIt’s me, the rapper eater\nFeed me, feed me, feed me!\n\nHere, other, “fake” rappers come off as so many off-brand groceries piled up in Weezy’s shopping cart.", "annotation_id": "14041506", "url": "https://genius.com/14041506", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "This is, this is, this is, this is", "vault_lines": ["This is, this is, this is, this is"], "meaning": "“This is” is a tag Cool & Dre tag sometimes use when they produce a track. Dre is the one who says it usually.\n\n\n\nCool (right) & Dre", "annotation_id": "9226140", "url": "https://genius.com/9226140", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "And you ain’t shit if you ain’t never been screwed up", "vault_lines": ["And you ain't shit if you ain't never been screwed up"], "meaning": "Here he’s quoting the chorus from his 2007 song with Trae;\n“Screwed Up”", "annotation_id": "63244", "url": "https://genius.com/63244", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "Lock, load, ready to aim at any target", "vault_lines": ["Lock, load, ready to aim at any target"], "meaning": "Mercilessly (like a martian) Wayne will target any rapper and tear them up and their beats too; he does this on his 2009 Mix-tape: No Ceilings", "annotation_id": "36165", "url": "https://genius.com/36165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "We are not the same, I am a Martian We are not the same, I am a Martian", "vault_lines": ["We are not the same, I am a alien"], "meaning": "One of the ever popular Weezy phrases;\n\n\nWayne’s indicating that he can’t be compared with us mere mortals, he’s from a whole different planet and for that reason there is no relationship to be made\nBeing the only one of ‘his’ kind makes him totally original\nNeither is he empathic towards us-Martians show no mercy towards the human race, this is why he won’t think twice about eating other rappers", "annotation_id": "36163", "url": "https://genius.com/36163", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "And I’m hotter than summer rain like Carl Thomas", "vault_lines": ["And I'm hotter than summer rain like Carl Thomas"], "meaning": "Reference to the hit song “Summer Rain”, by Carl Thomas.", "annotation_id": "36158", "url": "https://genius.com/36158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "And yeah, I’m a bear, like black and white hair, so I’m polar", "vault_lines": ["And yeah, I'm a bear, like black and white hair, so I'm polar"], "meaning": "Polar Bears look deceptively cute and harmless but really, they’re the biggest, baddest bears in existence, they have black skin and their fur’s white in appearance but is actually colourless.\n\n\n\nBUT has Wayne has confused polar bears with panda bears?\n\n\n\nSurely not?? Comparing himself to a mild-mannered, bamboo-eater wouldn’t be much of a boast.\n\nMore tricky wordplay: Wayne likely gravitated to “polar” because of the allusion to being “icy cool”, also black and white are polar opposites. Wayne’s known to have bipolar (having relating to two extremities) views of himself; bright and dark, hot and cold.", "annotation_id": "36146", "url": "https://genius.com/36146", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "I am so far from the othars, I meant others", "vault_lines": ["I am so far from the othars, I meant others"], "meaning": "Wayne’s ahead of all other hip hop artists\n\nOthers was mispronounced, in this case done purposely to rhyme with solar. Also  done in Mr Carter, Barry Bonds and I’m sure there’s more", "annotation_id": "36136", "url": "https://genius.com/36136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "I’m used to promethazine in two cups, I’m screwed up", "vault_lines": ["I'm used to promethazine in two cups, I'm screwed up"], "meaning": "Lil' Waynes vice-Promethazine aka: purple drank(in some brands purple dye’s added to it), syrup, sizzurp or lean (cough syrup) was made widely popular around 1990, it was and still is taken, as a recreational drug, to get high or screwed up. Drunk from one styrofoam cup inside another to stop your straw from going through the cup or just stopping the syrup from seeping through and spilling sticky liquid all over ya new kicks…Fuuuck that!\n\n\n\nThis album (Syrup Sippin' Nigga) is said to be the closest you can get to “sippin' syrup” without actually doing it", "annotation_id": "36128", "url": "https://genius.com/36128", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "Phone home (Weezy) Phone home (Weezy) Phone home (Weezy) Phone home (Weezy)", "vault_lines": ["This is, this is, this is, this is"], "meaning": "A reference to E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial, where the title alien said “E.T. Phone Home” to express how he wished to communicate with the members of his planet of origin. Just another way of saying that Wayne isn’t human and that he’s not amongst his own kind.\n\n\n\nWayne goes on in later albums to describe that he is not a human being, in a sense that he is different than other rappers.", "annotation_id": "36124", "url": "https://genius.com/36124", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "I could get your brains for a bargain like I bought it from Target", "vault_lines": ["I could get your brains for a bargain like I bought it from Target"], "meaning": "Weezy hire someone to splatter your brain for cheap!\n\nTarget, a chain of discount stores founded in Minnesota in 1902 (back then it was called the Dayton Day Goods Company)", "annotation_id": "36025", "url": "https://genius.com/36025", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "No brake lights on my car rear", "vault_lines": ["No brake lights on my car rear"], "meaning": "Not only is this ‘no break lights’ scenario extremely ghetto but take car rear, put it together; carrear adjust the spelling; career Tada!\nIt’s Weezys own Phone Home homophone!\n\nThere will be no break lights, slowing down or stopping, for Mr. Carter’s success in his career\n\n\n\nImagine driving behind someone without break lights…this is Wayne’s way of life you can always be prepared for shock, awe and unpredictability. He just keeps accelerating, never slowing down.\n\n[No]homophone!", "annotation_id": "36000", "url": "https://genius.com/36000", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "I get bread like cold cuts", "vault_lines": ["I get bread like cold cuts"], "meaning": "Bread: a slang term for money, like the breadwinner bringing home the main supply of income.\nWayne sees as much bread as cold cuts would in a sandwich (in case you don’t know cold cuts are sliced cold meats often found in a supermarket deli).\nYou could almost say Wayne and money go together", "annotation_id": "35729", "url": "https://genius.com/35729", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "Young college Student, who done just flipped the game like Houston", "vault_lines": ["Student, who done just flipped the game like Houston"], "meaning": "Reference to young Houston, College Tour rapper; Lil' Flip who got his name from being able to “flip” his style effortlessly.", "annotation_id": "35720", "url": "https://genius.com/35720", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "We are not the same, I am a alien Like Gonzales", "vault_lines": ["We are not the same, I am a alien"], "meaning": "Lil; Wayne replaces the word ‘Martian’, from a popular phrase of his (“We are not the same I am a Martian”) with ‘Alien’ or to relate himself to Elian Gonzales, a 5 year old sole survivor of a refugee boat that sunk in a storm on its way to the States. Elian, now in Cuba, with his Father, is seen as a hero\n\nIronically Elian is an Alien, in the legal sense, as he stayed with relatives in Florida without having permission from the country. As we know Wayne also likes to refer to himself as an Alien (Martian).\n\nWayne’s one to persevere, fight and survive; natural disasters aint enough to stop him!", "annotation_id": "35715", "url": "https://genius.com/35715", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Phone Home", "line": "I’m rare, like Mr. Clean with hair", "vault_lines": ["I'm rare, like Mr. Clean with hair"], "meaning": "Mr. Clean is a commonly used household cleaning product and the first to be packaged in a plastic bottle.\nThe logo/mascot is usually a clean-shaven bald guy but on rare occasions he’s drawn with hair.", "annotation_id": "35688", "url": "https://genius.com/35688", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
