{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Perfect (Remix)", "line": "Bitch, I did it, I made it, I’m loved and I’m hated I started from the bottom, now my neighborhood is gated", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I did it, I made it, I'm loved and I’m hated"], "meaning": "This opening line is reminiscent of Drake’s “Started from the Bottom”. Logic celebrates the fact that he began his career with nothing, living in low-income housing, and now has a security gate surrounding his property, a sign that the young rapper has truly made it.", "annotation_id": "25662161", "url": "https://genius.com/25662161", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Perfect (Remix)", "line": "Ayy, wake up, wake up, get your cake up Cut it up like it’s cocaine, shake up All the streets with all these beats", "vault_lines": ["All the streets with all thеse beats"], "meaning": "Logic talks about this in his No Pressure Breakdown stream:\n\nIt’s almost like a bit of an ode to…“wake up, wake up, wake up, it’s the 1st of the month”\n\nHe talks about how this is somewhat a reference to “1st of Tha Month” by Bone Thugs N Harmony.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4j_cOsgRY7w\n\n(copy and pasted from Stupid_genius29\n in the original Perfect song.)", "annotation_id": "24377704", "url": "https://genius.com/24377704", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Perfect (Remix)", "line": "Feel like every other day, me and somebody new related You’re my sister, cousin, brother from the other side? (The other side) Well, I don’t know who told you that (My mama) Well, she fucking lied", "vault_lines": ["Feel like every other day, me and somebody new related"], "meaning": "Logic touches on the fact that people will use whatever relation they have to a celebrity for their own personal gain. He talks about it in his No Pressure Breakdown:\n\nI can’t tell you how many shows I’ve been to, and it’s like “Yo, I’m your sister’s cousin’s uncle’s neice’s nephew’s fuckin…”", "annotation_id": "24377686", "url": "https://genius.com/24377686", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Perfect (Remix)", "line": "They say, “Drink to your accomplishments,” so every night I’m faded", "vault_lines": ["They say, \"Drink to your accomplishments,\" so every night I'm faded"], "meaning": "Logic pays homage to Drake and in particular his track “Headlines” in which Drake spits,\n\nDrinkin' every night because we drink to my accomplishments\nFaded way too long, I’m floatin' in and out of consciousness''\n\n(copy and pasted from  r_kumar109 in the original Perfect song.)", "annotation_id": "24377681", "url": "https://genius.com/24377681", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Perfect (Remix)", "line": "Tunechi", "vault_lines": ["Perfecto, that's foreign, Tunechi"], "meaning": "Tunechi, or Lil Tunechi, is a nickname for Dwayne Michael Carter Jr., AKA Lil Wayne, the famous American rapper. Tunechi is also a slang term for synthetic marijuana, sometimes called spice or K2.", "annotation_id": "24209615", "url": "https://genius.com/24209615", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Perfect (Remix)", "line": "VVS in my JID, that’s perfect", "vault_lines": ["VVS in my JID, that's perfect"], "meaning": "VVS stands for “very very slightly included” referring to diamonds and how they are graded. JID stands for “Jacob Issacharoff Diamonds” which is the name of a Diamond retailer.", "annotation_id": "21548586", "url": "https://genius.com/21548586", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Perfect (Remix)", "line": "Me and Nicki got a couple bitties twerking", "vault_lines": ["Me and Nicki got a couple bitties twerking"], "meaning": "This verse was likely recorded after Ferg and Nicki released a song called “Move Ya Hips” also including a verse from MadeinTYO. It debuted at 19 on Billboard, and Barbs were very frustated at Ferg because they believe that he didn’t submit website sales of the song. A video was also released, and not received well. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ArYlvBGI5Vk&ab_channel=asapfergVEVO", "annotation_id": "21546550", "url": "https://genius.com/21546550", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
