{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Peggy Bundy", "line": "Brr, hello? I thought a broke nigga said something", "vault_lines": ["Brr, hello? I thought a broke nigga said something"], "meaning": "“Brr” as in a phone ringing “hello?” As a greeting “?” Because that greeting was unanswered “I thought a broke Nigga said something” as in he thought but he knows nipsey hustle 8 million dollars net worth vs his 170 million dollar net worth said nothing because followed by the next line…", "annotation_id": "29500262", "url": "https://genius.com/29500262", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Peggy Bundy", "line": "I act like it’s sweet, I treat the Lambo like a Nissan", "vault_lines": ["I act like it's sweet, I treat the Lambo like a Nissan"], "meaning": "Tune is makin a double entendre referencing exodus 12:1 – 20 the instructions for the first Passover by Moses when he tells the Israelites how to treeat the lamb on the first of Nisan , the Kabbalistic / spiritual Jewish new year around march or April.", "annotation_id": "22679883", "url": "https://genius.com/22679883", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Peggy Bundy", "line": "And I’m about to do it, I did it", "vault_lines": ["That's true as religion, and I'm about to do it, I did it"], "meaning": "Lil wayne almost lost his breath.. this is where the rest us wouldn’t  have did it under the pressure of that long chain of words, but he was about to do it… and he did it! Piecing the song together to make a rap song that became “Peggy Bundy”", "annotation_id": "21537874", "url": "https://genius.com/21537874", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Peggy Bundy", "line": "I get high and incoherent,", "vault_lines": ["I get high and incoherent,"], "meaning": "“I get high and incoherent” might be incorrect. instead I believe he may have said, “I get high and coherent”\n\nI believe this because lil Wayne’s signature (the flick of a lighter, followed by a blunt being lit) can be heard in almost all his singles, mixtapes, albums and features. With reference to one of his glimpses into how he records his music in his song “TINA Turn Up Needs A TUNE Up” https://youtu.be/H71OPcYRfsc?t=17 , Lil Wayne gets high before and during his songs. It’s known that lil Wayne does not write his music https://youtu.be/KG2S9EUE0gA .\n\nFor some, weed can enhance the ability to freestyle,  this may be case for the Cosmic Rapper himself. This has nothing to do with Weezy’s ability to rap when his not high.\n\nOf cause it my be that he really did say “I get high and incoherent” it could very well explain the word “damn”  that followed the line; just as every line that  came before had coherent expletives interjections behind ideas he does agree with (i.e. “Kobe died, shit all mysterious, damn”), and the “Yeah’s following what he approves, (i.e. \"Broke niggas start disappearing, yeah).", "annotation_id": "21537134", "url": "https://genius.com/21537134", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Peggy Bundy", "line": "Back in my hood, niggas used to call me Fred Durst ’Cause I had that rock white", "vault_lines": ["Back in my hood, niggas used to call me Fred Durst"], "meaning": "Fred Durst is the lead singer / rapper of the mid 90’s white rock group, Limp Bizkit. Fred was mostly known for wearing his red baseball cap backwards.", "annotation_id": "21483764", "url": "https://genius.com/21483764", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Peggy Bundy", "line": "I hop on my skateboard and shred something", "vault_lines": ["I hop on my skateboard and shred something"], "meaning": "Shredding is a term used to describe skating or surfing with exaggerated movements. Lil Wayne has a thing for skating—not only did he drop a four-track EP titled Skateboard Weezy in July of 2020, but he also uploaded a skating compilation to his YouTube channel in 2018.", "annotation_id": "21483400", "url": "https://genius.com/21483400", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Peggy Bundy", "line": "Bae you too delicious, bae, I’m the key, you the ignition", "vault_lines": ["Bae you too delicious, bae, I'm the key, you the ignition"], "meaning": "Most likely a nod to R. Kelly’s 2002 smash hit “Ignition (Remix)” or the original. A euphuism for sex, Kelly sings on the remix:\n\nI’m about to take my key and\nStick it in the ignition\n\nAnd on the original:\n\nLet me stick my key in your ignition, babe\n\nIt’s important to note that Wayne and Kelly had an extensive history of beef starting in 2003 after Kelly didn’t come through with their collaborative record that was planned. On Wayne’s 2007 track “Dipset”, he rapped:\n\nJust shot a video with R.Kelly but No Homo though\nReally didn’t wanna do it\n\nAnd on Wayne’s 2009 track “Bad Side”:\n\nAnd I believe that I can fly\nNot like R.Kelly, he a damn lie\n\nDespite this, the beef has since been put away; in 2012, Wayne said he “would love to work with R. Kelly.” They would collaborate on the 2013 song “We Been On”.", "annotation_id": "21472366", "url": "https://genius.com/21472366", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Peggy Bundy", "line": "Money jumping call it Bunny Bread Me and money, we like bread and butter", "vault_lines": ["Money jumping call it Bunny Bread"], "meaning": "Bunny Bread is a popular Midwest producer of bread best known for its cartoon bunny seen on its wrapping.\nhttps://images.app.goo.gl/k95anCxsXpAhX1rM9\n\n“Bread” is a slang term for money, with “ money jumping” —bunnies are known for their vertical leap— being a common phrase used in hip-hop to describe growing wealth.\n\nWayne flips “bread” again, using the idiom “bread and butter,” which is usually linked to low levels of difficulty —in this case, its easy for Wayne to obtain his money— or someone’s most favorable state.", "annotation_id": "21472045", "url": "https://genius.com/21472045", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Peggy Bundy", "line": "Kobe died, shit all mysterious, damn", "vault_lines": ["Kobe died, shit all mysterious, damn"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne says ever since the death of NBA-star Kobe Bryant, things have turned strange and mysterious. Most likely due to the COVID-19 pandemic. Both occurring in 2020.", "annotation_id": "21462265", "url": "https://genius.com/21462265", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Peggy Bundy", "line": "You know that the coupe is on blades I’ma come through sittin’ on scissors", "vault_lines": ["The coupe is on skinnies, you know that the coupe is on blades"], "meaning": "Blades are a type of rim for cars popularized by Southern car culture, especially in cities like New Orleans among others, where Wayne hails from. They are often referred to as “scissors” because of the shine they give off while in motion, akin to something cutting or chopping up.", "annotation_id": "21460445", "url": "https://genius.com/21460445", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
