{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Party Like A Rockstar (Remix)", "line": "Braids", "vault_lines": ["It ain't the braids"], "meaning": "The line is “it ain’t the Braves that got the A rockin Mohawks.”\n\nIt’s a reference to the Atlanta Braves baseball team, whose mascot was Chief Noc-a-homa (knock a homer), a depiction of an Indian Brave with a tribal Mohawk. The mascot has changed since the song was released.", "annotation_id": "40373964", "url": "https://genius.com/40373964", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Party Like A Rockstar (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 2: Lil Wayne]", "vault_lines": ["Got diamond wallet chain, diamond watch, neck, and ring"], "meaning": "This was Lil Wayne’s first foray into the rock genre, not counting the rock remix of “Stuntin' Like My Daddy” from the year before.\n\nHe would continue to dabble in the genre by featuring on Chamillionaire’s “Rock Star” later in 2007, Fall Out Boy’s “Tiffany Blews” in 2008, Kevin Rudolf’s “Let It Rock” in 2008 and “I Made It (Cash Money Heroes)” in 2010, and Limp Bizkit’s “Ready To Go” in 2013.\n\nHe would even go on to record and release his own rock album, Rebirth, in 2010.", "annotation_id": "27630114", "url": "https://genius.com/27630114", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Party Like A Rockstar (Remix)", "line": "I got an icebox where my heart used to be, huh", "vault_lines": ["I got an icebox where my heart used to be, huh"], "meaning": "A reference to Omarion’s 2006 single, Ice Box, where he sings “I got this ice box where my heart use to be”.\nhttps://youtu.be/jQybgJCswF0", "annotation_id": "26933456", "url": "https://genius.com/26933456", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Party Like A Rockstar (Remix)", "line": "We on fire, the black Red Hot Chili Peppers", "vault_lines": ["We on fire, the black Red Hot Chili Peppers"], "meaning": "Chamillionaire, who is featured on this song, said something very similar on his song, “Rock Star” also featuring Lil Wayne and released the same year.\n\n“ Chamillitairy Mayne\nYoung Money, we the new Red Hot Chili Peppers\nWe on fire”", "annotation_id": "19151665", "url": "https://genius.com/19151665", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Party Like A Rockstar (Remix)", "line": "They just do what I say, jack, like Wheel of Fortune", "vault_lines": ["They just do what I say, jack, like Wheel of Fortune"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Jack Leslie Clark, who was an announcer on Wheel Of Fortune.", "annotation_id": "19151638", "url": "https://genius.com/19151638", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Party Like A Rockstar (Remix)", "line": "Get on my bus and go hit the mall And buy your earring the size of a crystal ball", "vault_lines": ["Get on my bus and go hit the mall"], "meaning": "Chamillionaire made so much money, he can go buy anything he wants to- even an earring with a rock as big as a fortune-teller’s ball.", "annotation_id": "1176504", "url": "https://genius.com/1176504", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
