{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paradice", "line": "Blisters on my knees, from beggin’ for forgiveness", "vault_lines": ["Blisters on my knees, from beggin' for forgiveness"], "meaning": "Wayne has been praying on his knees for such a long period of time, that blisters have now formed on his knees.", "annotation_id": "11448424", "url": "https://genius.com/11448424", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paradice", "line": "I’m tired of hearin’ the same song, who told the DJ ”Bring it back”?", "vault_lines": ["I'm tired of hearin' the same song, who told the DJ \"Bring it back\"?"], "meaning": "Possibly a reference to one of Lil Wayne’s earliest and most famous hits, “Bring It Back”\nHe has played it so many times over the years that he doesn’t like it anymore.", "annotation_id": "18961254", "url": "https://genius.com/18961254", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paradice", "line": "Cut school, sell crack, sorry, I’m just thinkin’ back", "vault_lines": ["Cut school, sell crack, sorry, I'm just thinkin' back"], "meaning": "Wayne is reminiscing on when used to skip school to sell weed and crack to make money for him and his family. He sold drugs before and during his high school days when he grew up in Hollygrove, Louisiana.", "annotation_id": "15533865", "url": "https://genius.com/15533865", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paradice", "line": "Dead Presidents, bullet in Abraham Lincoln hat", "vault_lines": ["Dead Presidents, bullet in Abraham Lincoln hat"], "meaning": "PROPOSED SUGGESTION:\n\nIt’s pretty self explanatory, Lincoln’s a dead president his cause of death was a bullet to the head. Dead presidents is slang for money lol this didn’t even need An annotation", "annotation_id": "198452", "url": "https://genius.com/198452", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paradice", "line": "He was a young boy in pursuit of money and fame And he would do anything he could to kill the pain When everybody know your moves, they speak of your name And, oh, all over the late night local news, I heard him scream", "vault_lines": ["He was a young boy in pursuit of money and fame"], "meaning": "This verse mirrors the first verse talking about a young girl going through the pursuit of money and fame, except this time it’s a young boy.\n\nWayne is comparing people in poverty who take drugs to numb the pain of their life to celebrities who use drugs as recreation and end up on the local news and get thrown in jail.\n\n\n\nIt’s an interesting juxtaposition; less-fortunate people take drugs because they are unhappy with their life and want money/fame. However people who do have money and fame are also unhappy with their life and often take drugs to numb the pain of their life as well.", "annotation_id": "2739793", "url": "https://genius.com/2739793", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paradice", "line": "Oh no, this ain’t paradise! Oh no, this ain’t paradise! Oh no, this ain’t paradise! (Yeah) Oh no, this ain’t paradise! Oh no, this ain’t paradise! You know, this ain’t paradise", "vault_lines": ["This ain't paradise; no, this ain't paradise"], "meaning": "Hollywood ain’t a paradise. It’s actually a sort of Hell.\nThis theme is common throughout many songs in music:\n\n\nNot all that glitters is gold\"\n\nHollywood is not America\"", "annotation_id": "226049", "url": "https://genius.com/226049", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
