{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paint Tha Town", "line": "Cincinnati reds hat, tilt that bitch to the right", "vault_lines": ["Cincinnati reds hat, tilt that bitch to the right"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is affiliated with the Bloods gang, whose members often wear red to show allegiance. Weezy is most notably seen wearing a Cincinnati Reds hat in the “Lollipop” music video.", "annotation_id": "41216724", "url": "https://genius.com/41216724", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paint Tha Town", "line": "All of you suckas pussy, none of you pussy’s tight", "vault_lines": ["All of you suckas pussy, none of you pussy's tight"], "meaning": "Crazy diss from Wayne here. He calls his enemies pussies, a common insult in hiphop culture. He then gives a double entendre playing with the word pussy. He says these pussies aren’t tight which has two meanings:\n\n\nsexual connotation; tight pussy is considered desirable and more pleasurable during intercourse. Wayne says these guys are just as bad as loose pussy; which is quite the diss\nslang meaning; tight basically means cool. Wayne says none of these guys are cool.", "annotation_id": "35893670", "url": "https://genius.com/35893670", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paint Tha Town", "line": "You find me on the chopper With my chopper non-stopper, check the roof bitch already chop em", "vault_lines": ["You find me on the chopper"], "meaning": "Chopper is a slang for an AK-47 assault rifle. To ‘Chop off the roof’ means to make the car convertible, meaning the roof is down.", "annotation_id": "2940170", "url": "https://genius.com/2940170", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paint Tha Town", "line": "Holla at you soo woo, that’s the new slang dummy", "vault_lines": ["Holla at you soo woo, that's the new slang dummy"], "meaning": "“Soo woo” is a greeting call made from a Blood to another Blood – Wayne and Game even collaborated and dedicated a song to this phrase.\n\nhttp://screencast.com/t/hJgZfovzG", "annotation_id": "2905109", "url": "https://genius.com/2905109", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paint Tha Town", "line": "Rag in my pocket, what color is that motherfucker?", "vault_lines": ["Rag in my pocket, what color is that motherfucker?"], "meaning": "The Game is from Compton, which is home to both the Bloods and the Crips. Since Game is affiliated with the Bloods, he would wear a red rag in his pocket.", "annotation_id": "2905037", "url": "https://genius.com/2905037", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paint Tha Town", "line": "I let Marley shoot ’em, cause I’m an convicted felon", "vault_lines": ["I let Marley shoot 'em, cause I'm an convicted felon"], "meaning": "Marley G is Lil' Wayne’s right hand man (and/or goon) — he does Weezy’s dirty work, Lil Wayne calms Marley on several songs, saying “Marley don’t shoot ‘em”\n\nIn October 2009 Dwayne Micheal Carter Jr. Plead guilty to attempted criminal possession of a weapon. In March of 2010 Lil Wayne was sentenced to a year in prison, which he served in Rikers Island. Wayne was released from Rikers Island prison facility on November 4, 2010 after serving eight months of his year-long sentence.[", "annotation_id": "2025522", "url": "https://genius.com/2025522", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paint Tha Town", "line": "I’m Piru, all red nigga", "vault_lines": ["I'm Piru, all red nigga"], "meaning": "Wayne has been sworn in as an official affiliate to the MOB St Piru (Piru St Bloods were the first ever bloods) bloods in Compton by his old friend Term aka El Jefe back in 2005.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dXJZnWtuI9I\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zNWbldXf3_g", "annotation_id": "2011345", "url": "https://genius.com/2011345", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Paint Tha Town", "line": "For the money motherfucker, Wall Street cash", "vault_lines": ["For the money motherfucker, Wall Street cash"], "meaning": "A reference to Game’s Black Wall Street record label, as well as to the fact that he and Wayne are both very wealthy.", "annotation_id": "2009070", "url": "https://genius.com/2009070", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
