{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "She’s somethin’ to do when there’s nothin’ to do We so ugly and cute, but the love is the proof", "vault_lines": ["She's somethin' to do when there's nothin' to do"], "meaning": "This exemplifies Wayne’s uncertainty about the situation: first, he characterizes this woman as a mere pastime, but then notes that the apparent love they share is evidence that the relationship is worth it. He also mentions the polarity of their interaction — at their worst, they’re “ugly,” but they make up for it when they’re “cute.”", "annotation_id": "8762417", "url": "https://genius.com/8762417", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "Never chucking the deuce, never comin’ unloose, woo Put my tongue in her noose, out my thumb in her ’boose Make her jump through the roof, now she touchin’ the moon And she love when we spoon, she gon’ cum and boo-hoo When she cummin’, it’s through", "vault_lines": ["Never chucking the deuce, never comin' unloose, woo"], "meaning": "Lil' Wayne here has made a clearer decision about the future of this relationship — after a particularly satisfying sexual encounter (which features some particularly vivid anal play that he claims has rocked her world), he’s going to break things off. He is relatively cavalier about this choice, despite this woman crying due to the disrespect and lack of intimacy immediately after orgasm.", "annotation_id": "8762389", "url": "https://genius.com/8762389", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "If she love it, I like it, husband and wifey We do what we do, we do how we do But we makin’ it through, and the bedroom a zoo We fuss for a few, then we fuck for a truce, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Fuckin' and fightin', fuckin' and fightin', yeah, fuck it"], "meaning": "This dramatizes the conflict of the relationship (that is, the “fightin'”) — the couple persists in spite of clear imbalance between them (purportedly due to the fact that they are legally married).\n\nThis conflict has even made its way into their sex life — the quarrels and coitus have become so wrapped up in each other that they’re basically inseparable. As such, it’s gotten so wild that Lil' Wayne likens their intimacy to a zoo.", "annotation_id": "8762347", "url": "https://genius.com/8762347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "You woulda held me back and you wouldn’t let me go You woulda told me, “No,” you would have told me, “Yes” Woulda stayed the night, then we’d probably have sex And we know it ain’t right but there’s stuff that comes next (Hahaha)", "vault_lines": ["You woulda held me back and you wouldn't let me go"], "meaning": "Zayn knows that if he were to break up with his partner, she would prevent him from leaving, which he doesn’t want. The duality of her affirmation/rejection parallels the duality of their complicated intimacy.\n\nIf he had been drawn in by her pleading, they would’ve ended up having sex again — which they both know means getting sucked back into the paradise/warzone dichotomy described throughout the song. Zayn knows that as raw, pure, reckless, and united as their love has been, it’s time to move on.", "annotation_id": "8756364", "url": "https://genius.com/8756364", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "I got too many seeds, they all gotta grow No, I didn’t conceive, but I got one goal And yes, I felt the seed, but I don’t no more Now I’ll fuck her ten times ’cause I don’t get bored (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I got too many seeds, they all gotta grow"], "meaning": "Zayn puns on “seed” — first, with a sexual connotation (referring to semen), and noting that he wants to spread his “seed” and ejaculate repeatedly without impregnating anyone, so that he can stay focused on his career goals. (His former friend and ex-bandmate Louis Tomlinson hasn’t been so lucky.)\n\nThen, he refers to the “seed” of their love (i.e., something to grow within their relationship). While at first, he felt that spark, now his interest in her is purely sexual. That being said, he does give her the credit that sex with her is consistently interesting.", "annotation_id": "8740932", "url": "https://genius.com/8740932", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "If anybody knows, that’s just how the game goes In a few weeks she’ll be somebody’s, yo", "vault_lines": ["If anybody knows, that's just how the game goes"], "meaning": "Zayn says if anybody understands what life means, then they’ll understand that this volatility is par for the course. He knows that in a few weeks, they’ll have broken up and this woman will have moved onto someone else.", "annotation_id": "8740629", "url": "https://genius.com/8740629", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "Fuckin’ and fightin’, fuckin’ and fightin’, yeah, fuck it", "vault_lines": ["Fuckin' and fightin', fuckin' and fightin', yeah, fuck it"], "meaning": "Lil' Wayne’s verse begins by referencing Zayn’s original chorus — the bedroom remains a place of both sexual pleasure and personal conflict.", "annotation_id": "8730255", "url": "https://genius.com/8730255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "It’s our paradise (Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh), yeah And it’s our war zone", "vault_lines": ["It's our paradise and it's our war zone (Pop, pop, pop, pop, pop, pop, brr, paradise and our war zone)"], "meaning": "Zayn describes the connection he shares with his lover. He knows the catharsis that can accompany “pillow talk”—the release of stress (and perhaps tears), the ability to let go with your partner and feel secure and safe.\n\nHe’s able to be fully in the moment with his partner and enjoy their sex completely (it’s so loud that it pisses off the neighbors).\n\nZayn also describes the bedroom as a place of a certain kind of duality. It is wholly pure and yet delightfully sinful; a paradise, as well as a war zone. Their time together — as raw, reckless and unadulterated as it is — is also the purest expression of love and unity.\n\nZayn saying “fucking” reflects his newfound freedom now that he’s no longer in 1D. He told Billboard:\n\n[In One Direction] we weren’t allowed to say certain things, or word lyrics the way we would want to… I’m enjoying what I’m doing. I’m not censoring myself anymore, so I’m not tired. I love it.", "annotation_id": "8727936", "url": "https://genius.com/8727936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "I love to hold you close, tonight and always I love to wake up next to you", "vault_lines": ["I love to hold you close, tonight and always"], "meaning": "Zayn doesn’t just want to hook up tonight, he wants to wake up together in the morning, a true sign of intimacy.\n\nZayn’s said more than once that the bedroom is a very important place for him. He told The Fader that he almost missed his X-Factor interview because he was sleeping:\n\nI was a lazy teen. If I was in control of me going to audition for X Factor, I would have never gone because I would have never got up on the day of the audition at four in the morning. The reason I woke up is because my mom came in the room and was like, ‘You have to go audition for this show.'\n\nhttps://twitter.com/zaynmalik/status/25668747696021504", "annotation_id": "8727934", "url": "https://genius.com/8727934", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "I’m seeing the pain, seeing the pleasure Nobody but you, ’body but me, ’body but us, bodies together (He the one, she the two)", "vault_lines": ["I'm seeing the pain, seeing the pleasure"], "meaning": "The intimacy that comes with sex allows Zayn and his partner to experience complicated emotions together. The foreplay, the sex itself—they’re all ways of forging a deeper connection.\n\nDoes Zayn himself share this kind of intimacy with Gigi Hadid, who stars in the video with him? In an interview with Zane Lowe, Zayn said that he and Gigi Hadid are just friends, but the video and rumors have suggested more. In late December 2015, Zayn posted an Instagram of the two cuddling.", "annotation_id": "8727933", "url": "https://genius.com/8727933", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "PILLOWTALK (Remix)", "line": "Climb on board (Mula, baby) We’ll go slow and high tempo (Yeah) Light and dark Hold me hard and mellow", "vault_lines": ["Climb on board (Mula, baby)"], "meaning": "Zayn invites his lover to go on a journey with him. He’ll make love passionately—fast and slow, day to night. Zayn’s ready to really connect; the physical act helps them experience the deeper feelings.\n\nZayn’s been very open that the song is explicitly about sex, and that he’s excited to be free of censors for the first time in his career. In his first single as a solo artist, Zayn shows a vulnerable and mature side that he was previously unable to share with the world.", "annotation_id": "8727932", "url": "https://genius.com/8727932", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
