{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Oxy", "line": "I just told Richie we rich", "vault_lines": ["I just told Richie we rich"], "meaning": "This producer tag is for Tony Son, popularly known as Richie Souf and voiced by Atlanta native, Gunna. Richie has production credits for artists such as Gunna, Chris Brown, Future, Playboi Carti, and many more artists.\n\nFuture and Richie have many officially released collaborations such as “All da Smoke,” “Please Tell Me,” “Ain’t Coming Back,” and more.", "annotation_id": "26807083", "url": "https://genius.com/26807083", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Oxy", "line": "Got Versace carpet", "vault_lines": ["I see funny faces"], "meaning": "Versace is a luxury Italian clothing producer, founded in 1978. It produces mostly leather-like clothing & suits for men.\nMedusa is a character from Greek mythology and she would turn people who gaze at her into stone.", "annotation_id": "21826563", "url": "https://genius.com/21826563", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Oxy", "line": "Bentley with the roof", "vault_lines": ["Bentley with the roof"], "meaning": "Bentley Motors Limited, the world’s widest range of handcrafted cars, is a British luxury vehicle manufacturer that was founded in 1919 and markets SUVs and numerous car models.\n\n\n\nPictured: Bentley Motors' Logo 1945-Present.", "annotation_id": "21826546", "url": "https://genius.com/21826546", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Oxy", "line": "It’s lonely at the top, we hold hands and Geronimo", "vault_lines": ["It's lonely at the top, we hold hands and Geronimo"], "meaning": "Screaming, “Geronimo!”, is used in the US Army airborne units as an exclamation. One of the explanations is that it refers to a native American chief called Geronimo since they watched the movie Geronimo: The Story of a Great Enemy the day before jumping in 1940.", "annotation_id": "21808092", "url": "https://genius.com/21808092", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Oxy", "line": "Pocket watchin’, pick a pocket Richard Mille prolly", "vault_lines": ["Pocket watchin', pick a pocket"], "meaning": "Richard Mille is a luxury brand founded in Switzerland by Richard Mille and Dominique Guenat in 2001. They produce watches and clocks.", "annotation_id": "21607359", "url": "https://genius.com/21607359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Oxy", "line": "Oxy-Oxy, Oxycontin", "vault_lines": ["I see funny faces"], "meaning": "Oxycodone, sold under the brand name OxyContin (or “Oxy” in short) among others, is an opioid medication used for treatment of moderate to severe pain, and is a commonly abused drug.", "annotation_id": "20299889", "url": "https://genius.com/20299889", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Oxy", "line": "Crank that ho, John Gotti", "vault_lines": ["Crank that ho, John Gotti"], "meaning": "John Gotti was an Italian-American gangster who was the boss of the Gambino crime family in New York City in the 1960s, 70s, and 80s.\n\nFuture previously mentioned Gotti in his song “Karate Chop” off the album F.B.G. The Movie saying,\n\nSlang a bunch of narcotics\nPull up in the new ‘rrari\nLivin’ like John Gotti\nChoppin' bricks like karate", "annotation_id": "15635631", "url": "https://genius.com/15635631", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Oxy", "line": "Catch it, Jeremy Shockey", "vault_lines": ["Catch it, Jeremy Shockey"], "meaning": "Jeremy Shockey is a former football tight end. Before being drafted in 2002 by the New York Giants, he played college football at the University of Miami. Following playing for the Giants, Shockey then played for the New Orleans Saints and the Carolina Panthers.", "annotation_id": "15609322", "url": "https://genius.com/15609322", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
