{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Out West", "line": "Take a picture, say, “Cheese,” decompose, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Take a picture, say, \"Cheese,\" decompose, nigga"], "meaning": "Wayne uses a term commonly used by photographers to tell the people in the photo to pose, adding with decom'pose' which is what a dead body would do.", "annotation_id": "24424236", "url": "https://genius.com/24424236", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Out West", "line": "Nina take his soul away ’cause she a soul sister", "vault_lines": ["Nina take his soul away 'cause she a soul sister"], "meaning": "A Nina or Nina Ross is a 9mm gun. Knowing that, a gun will take your life/soul away. Nina is also a female name, so she is a soul sister.", "annotation_id": "22747828", "url": "https://genius.com/22747828", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Out West", "line": "No Ceilings 3, Euro, HoodyBaby, Gudda Gudda", "vault_lines": ["No Ceilings 3, Euro, HoodyBaby, Gudda Gudda"], "meaning": "Khaled creates a perfect segue into the next track, “CHURCH” which happens to feature Euro, Hoody Baby, and Gudda Gudda.", "annotation_id": "21473097", "url": "https://genius.com/21473097", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Out West", "line": "I was tryna kill ya, no brainer, scarecrow (Oh, ayy)", "vault_lines": ["I was tryna kill ya, no brainer, scarecrow (Oh, ayy)"], "meaning": "Young Thug was allegedly involved in a hit put out that resulted in Wayne’s tour bus being shot up in 2015 in Atlanta, Thug’s hometown, although the shooting’s target has remained unclear over the years.\n\nIn the classic 1939 film The Wizard of Oz, the Scarecrow lacks a brain but was ultimately given a diploma to certify his intelligence and problem-solving skills.", "annotation_id": "21466081", "url": "https://genius.com/21466081", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Out West", "line": "I want you six feet under that Earth (Bitch) I put your picture on front of that shirt (Bitch) I let my bitch sleep in one of them shirts And she let me piss and cum on that shirt (Bitch)", "vault_lines": ["I want you six feet under that Earth (Bitch)"], "meaning": "Wayne is saying he will kill you, your homies will make t-shirts with your picture on the front in your honor, his bitch will get one of these shirts, and he will piss and cum on it while he fucks her to disrespect your memory.", "annotation_id": "21461475", "url": "https://genius.com/21461475", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Out West", "line": "I might shoot up the casket Shoot up the funeral, shoot up the pastor (Buh)", "vault_lines": ["I might shoot up the casket"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is likely referencing his Funeral album, which released in early 2020.", "annotation_id": "21461304", "url": "https://genius.com/21461304", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Out West", "line": "I’m boutta feel like the cameraman, nigga ’Cause I’m ’bout to shoot with a Canon (Yeah) I got the Uzi with the banana clip You get the fruit like you Adam, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I'm boutta feel like the cameraman, nigga"], "meaning": "While most of the first half of this verse is merely comprised of clever “I will shoot wherever you are” metaphors and similes, these two lines specifically also make reference to Lil Uzi Vert and Don Cannon while doing so as a double-entendre. And, by a stretch perhaps, the latter line may also reference Uzi’s recent collaborator Adamn Killa.\n\nThe first line here makes reference to cameramen shooting photos, incorporating popular camera-brand Canon into the bar. The second line is a metaphor where Wayne pretends a banana clip actually shoots bananas (which Wayne has done before), so the person on the receiving end gets the fruit (bullet).", "annotation_id": "21460360", "url": "https://genius.com/21460360", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
