{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Original", "line": "I made something out of nothing, thanks for nothing", "vault_lines": ["I made something out of nothing, thanks for nothing"], "meaning": "Wayne takes two popular phrases:\n\n“Make something from nothing”\n\nand\n\n“Thanks for nothing”\n\nAnd incorporates them into one punchline illustrating his rise to the top which started from nothing with no handouts along the way", "annotation_id": "505941", "url": "https://genius.com/505941", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Original", "line": "Buckwheat and his friend Alfalfa Couldn’t do nothing with this little rascal", "vault_lines": ["Buckwheat and his friend Alfalfa"], "meaning": "Buckwheat and Alfalfa were characters in the long-running series of comedic short films known as Our Gang, and also as The Little Rascals", "annotation_id": "499697", "url": "https://genius.com/499697", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Original", "line": "Back to the top from the jail house", "vault_lines": ["Back to the top from the jail house"], "meaning": "Mystikal’s biggest-selling album, 2000’s double-platinum Let’s Get Ready, contained the huge hit “Shake Ya Ass”", "annotation_id": "498872", "url": "https://genius.com/498872", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Original", "line": "The ape man taught Tarzan -- how the fuck you better than me?", "vault_lines": ["The ape man taught Tarzan -- how the fuck you better than me?"], "meaning": "Mystikal makes a pointed metaphorical point here – Tarzan may come to be known popularly as the “king of the jungle”, but he was raised by apes who taught him everything he knew.  Similarly, how could any (presumably white) person claim to get one up on Mystikal, who presents himself here as an authentic source for rap culture", "annotation_id": "498790", "url": "https://genius.com/498790", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Original", "line": "Original, real nigga from the start", "vault_lines": ["Original, real nigga from the start"], "meaning": "Bryan “Baby”/“Birdman” Williams is a true O.G. of New Orleans rap, having founded the Cash Money label in 1990.  He has also been a recording artist since 1993", "annotation_id": "498307", "url": "https://genius.com/498307", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Original", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Mystikal-original-lyrics", "genius_title": "Original", "genius_id": 61417, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "I’m off drugs and a bunch of shots After party at my crib, oh, with a bunch of thots (Ha-ha) So order more bottles, don’t care what the cost", "vault_lines": ["I'm off drugs and a bunch of shots"], "meaning": "When G is in control, the party never ends. The team goes from the club, to the strip club, then to G’s new crib while the night is still young. G keeps the night going by ordering more bottles, buying more drugs and inviting more girls because doesn’t care of the cost as long as he is having a good time.", "annotation_id": "16638645", "url": "https://genius.com/16638645", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "So if you want this cash, you gotta show some more That private dance is through that corridor (Let’s go)", "vault_lines": ["So if you want this cash, you gotta show some more"], "meaning": "G-Eazy has already used a lot of cash to throw around, so as the night progresses he becomes more stingy with his money. While still willing to use his cash, he wants to see and get more out of the strippers he is with.\n\nDown the corridor is a private room that Gerald will take this girl to for some close and personal action. He can easily afford the higher cost, and may impress her enough to take her home.", "annotation_id": "16638631", "url": "https://genius.com/16638631", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "I’m popping champagne, now I’m pouring more I just ran out of ones it’s time to order more", "vault_lines": ["I just ran out of ones it's time to order more"], "meaning": "Since G loves expensive champagne in his cup he keeps the party going bringing more and more of it out. And when he runs out of one’s from his duffel bag he can just order more in and celebrate through the whole night.\n\nG has been on the grind for years and now he is showing off his prowess that he can spend his money on strippers and drugs for a good time.", "annotation_id": "16638618", "url": "https://genius.com/16638618", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "[Intro: Starrah] Cut it up I got racks on the menu She need more, shawty, cash on the menu Show some more, need that ass on a menu Make it clap we got cash on the menu [Chorus: Starrah] Oooh, fuck around and order more money Oooh, fuck around and order more Oooh baby, we gon’ order more money Oooh, fuck around and order more", "vault_lines": ["I got racks on the menu"], "meaning": "When G-Eazy and Starrah hit the club, they are going to keep bringing the cash in and throw it at strippers until their hearts are content. In return G and his crew expect to get some personal or even private action with girls dancing all over them.\n\nWith the motif of darkness spread throughout When It’s Dark Out, these late nights at the club recur throughout the album in songs like “You Got Me.”", "annotation_id": "16615624", "url": "https://genius.com/16615624", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "Took her straight to the Fountainbleau,", "vault_lines": ["Took her straight to the Fountainbleau,"], "meaning": "The Fontainebleau is a popular hotel in Miami.", "annotation_id": "9161553", "url": "https://genius.com/9161553", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 1: G-Eazy]", "vault_lines": ["I just ran out of ones it's time to order more"], "meaning": "In the original version, this is the second verse. It’s possible G-Eazy chose this to be the one for the remix because he likes it more than the first, or to give a feeling of extent to the song, as after his last verse comes Gotti and Wayne.", "annotation_id": "8976444", "url": "https://genius.com/8976444", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "Coming home on that Bay Bridge (Aye) 2 AM on them city nights, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Coming home on that Bay Bridge (Aye)"], "meaning": "The Bay Bridge is the famous bridge that connects San Francisco to Oakland in the Bay Area. Returning to Oakland, he uses this bridge to get to and from the city, especially on late nights.\n\nHe is often out into the early hours of the morning partying and having fun in the city, but when it’s all over he drives back to where he’s from to turn in for the night.\n\nIt’s, four in the morning I’m looking for drugs\nAlready faded increasing my buzz\nWorking it off I’ll be at the clubs\nEvery weekend this is what I does", "annotation_id": "8952710", "url": "https://genius.com/8952710", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "My neighbor is a bitch, they tried to call the cops (You bitch) Fuck you I’m living life, all good don’t need advice", "vault_lines": ["My neighbor is a bitch, they tried to call the cops (You bitch)"], "meaning": "In G-Eazy’s video “The Rise” Episode 1 – he reminisced that his neighbors used to hate him because of the noise coming from the studio. After begging him to keep it civil, they are often forced to call the cops to shut down the party.\n\nGerald stays true to his “Me, Myself and I” motto, and doesn’t let anyone else tell him how to live his life. G works very hard and believes that  he deserves to play just as hard , so he can get very upset when cops let him to “tone it down.” G is young, rich and handsome and has gotten this far without advice from others.\n\nListen, I’m tellin' you, it’s my world, I does what I wish to\nIf you’re mad well too bad, sounds like a personal issue", "annotation_id": "8952707", "url": "https://genius.com/8952707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "Charge it to my Black Card", "vault_lines": ["She let me feel that ass soft, charge it to my Black Card"], "meaning": "Launched in 2008, The Visa Black Card is a Visa credit card that allows its members access to various luxuries and rewards. The Black Card is compared to the American Express Platinum Card, and is marketed as a high-end rewards credit card.\n\nDefinitely also a hint at Wayne’s black card, the thing he explains feels like heroin: Extra edit By WubGod", "annotation_id": "8952671", "url": "https://genius.com/8952671", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "Pussy is my favorite vice, I see you, I get enticed (Yeah) Them titties nice, tonight, I’ma hit it twice", "vault_lines": ["Pussy is my favorite vice, I see you, I get enticed (Yeah)"], "meaning": "A vice is something shady you take pleasure in. When G-Eazy sees a girl he wants, he gets into lady killer mode, and runs his game on her to get her home.\n\nG’s stamina is not to be questioned. When he takes girls home with him he goes as many rounds as he wants with them. Only the finest women get to round three with him, but because he likes this girl’s breasts he is going to take her at least twice.\n\nYeah, that girl you got is nice, I already had her twice", "annotation_id": "8906079", "url": "https://genius.com/8906079", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Order More (Remix)", "line": "That money doesn’t matter, I’ll make it back mañana", "vault_lines": ["That money doesn't matter, I'll make it back mañana"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne isn’t short on cash by any means; Bankrate predicts that his net-worth is currently $150 million.\n\nMañana means “tomorrow” in Spanish, so Wayne is saying that it doesn’t matter if he throws away his cash because he’ll have it back the day after anyway.", "annotation_id": "8906038", "url": "https://genius.com/8906038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
