{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "I’m a Scarface, nigga, fuck your human race, nigga (Fuck your human race)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a Scarface, nigga, fuck your human race, nigga (Fuck your human race)"], "meaning": "A dig at Pharrell… Pharrell released a collab with Adidas, the Nmd Human Race shoes.", "annotation_id": "35469167", "url": "https://genius.com/35469167", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "I capitalize off my own mistakes, you lowercase, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I capitalize off my own mistakes, you lowercase, nigga"], "meaning": "Weezy would gladly write down and learn from his own mistakes to better himself in the future.\n\nAlso note the capitalize (uppercase)/lowercase wordplay, which Wayne uses to suggest his opponents would not learn from their own mistakes.", "annotation_id": "29943220", "url": "https://genius.com/29943220", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Only smoke on gas, no brakes, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Only smoke on gas, no brakes, nigga"], "meaning": "“Smoking gas” means smoking weed, and Lil Wayne twists this to also refer to driving a car metaphorically, saying that nothing can stop him.", "annotation_id": "19415378", "url": "https://genius.com/19415378", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Hungry, bullets eatin’ off your chest-plate, nigga (Rrr)", "vault_lines": ["Hungry, bullets eatin' off your chest-plate, nigga (Rrr)"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is shooting at someone wearing body armour, or a “chest-plate”. Nice play of words with hungry bullets eating off a plate.", "annotation_id": "19415370", "url": "https://genius.com/19415370", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Yeah, if it’s beef, we over-ate, nigga (Ate, nigga)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, if it's beef, we over-ate, nigga (Ate, nigga)"], "meaning": "Wayne is telling us how little shits he gives about beefing with you, since he over ate the beef already.", "annotation_id": "19412446", "url": "https://genius.com/19412446", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Celebratin’ like he got a cold case, nigga (Oh!)", "vault_lines": ["Celebratin' like he got a cold case, nigga (Oh!)"], "meaning": "A cold case is a case which remains unsolved and has no leads so it is no longer under investigation.\n\nSo, the guy is celebrating like he’s got away with a crime he committed.\n\nAlso, a ‘cold case’ could also refer to a cold case of beer. Clever double meaning.", "annotation_id": "17901567", "url": "https://genius.com/17901567", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "These pay cuts bleed through the Band-Aid, nigga (Damn)", "vault_lines": ["These pay cuts bleed through the Band-Aid, nigga (Damn)"], "meaning": "This line is a double entendre.\n\n  First he is referencing the much publicized contract/lawsuit issue with fellow rapper Birdman and Cash Money Records. Pay cuts are a reference to the money that was owed to him by the label. It’s bleeding through the Band-Aid meaning they can’t hold the money back, can’t suppress or hold back the flow of it any longer, much like a Band-Aid unable to stop the bleeding from a cut or wound. Lil Wayne was awarded $10 million dollars in the settlement of that lawsuit in 2018, in addition to being awarded the Young Money label.\n\nThe second is that it is a reference to the gang, the Bloods, who Lil’ Wayne has referenced in many of his past songs. Blood (*) flowing through a Band-Aid would result in it turning red in color, which is a color associated with Blood members.\n  In this case “Band-Aid” is used as a stand in for a bandage, something that would be used to stop a bleeding wound. Bandages can often be fashioned by tying a cloth or rag over a wound. The red bandannas prominently worn by Blood gang associates are often referred to as “red rags”.\n\n *There is a flip with the use of the word “bleed” in place of Blood.", "annotation_id": "16566008", "url": "https://genius.com/16566008", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "So walk it like you talk it, sashay, nigga", "vault_lines": ["So walk it like you talk it, sashay, nigga"], "meaning": "Sashay is a pretentious and exaggerated walk that models use on a runway. Therefore, Wayne is telling the listener to back up their words with action and to do so with finesse.", "annotation_id": "16331130", "url": "https://genius.com/16331130", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Federales on my ass, fuckin’ had a boat chase, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Federales on my ass, fuckin' had a boat chase, nigga"], "meaning": "Federales is a Spanglish word used in an informal context to denote security forces operating under a federal political system.\n\nLil Wayne has a history of getting in trouble with the law, and was even in 2017 named in a federal drug investigation report, along with fellow musician Chris Brown.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YQsMqRvPzRw", "annotation_id": "15938883", "url": "https://genius.com/15938883", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Kick push, that means grind and get paid, nigga (Paid)", "vault_lines": ["Kick push, that means grind and get paid, nigga (Paid)"], "meaning": "This alludes to Wayne’s skateboarding lifestyle, kick push has numerous ties to the skate community. Wayne creates a double entendre by using the word “grind,” meaning either he is working hard, or grinding a rail/edge with his skateboard.", "annotation_id": "15644939", "url": "https://genius.com/15644939", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "’96 Dom P, I have that with Corn Flakes", "vault_lines": ["'96 Dom P, I have that with Corn Flakes"], "meaning": "Another big flex on Wayne’s part.\n\nDom P is short for Dom Perignon which is a vintage, French champagne. The wine is aged, and usually the older the wine is, the higher the price.\n\n\n\nHim saying that he puts Dom in his cereal shows how little he cares about how expensive the champagne is, and treats it as if it was milk.", "annotation_id": "15481723", "url": "https://genius.com/15481723", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Got Mack with me up in this bitch and a MAC just in case, nigga (MAC)", "vault_lines": ["Got Mack with me up in this bitch and a MAC just in case, nigga (MAC)"], "meaning": "Mack Maine is Lil Wayne’s long time friend and president of Wayne’s label, Young Money Entertainment.\n\n\n\nFurthermore, Wayne’s not afraid to pack a firearm, such as a MAC-10, for protection. He was arrested in 2009  for gun possession and served time at Rikers Island.\n\nhttps://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/lil-wayne-pleads-guilty-to-gun-charges-faces-year-in-prison-94325/", "annotation_id": "15480845", "url": "https://genius.com/15480845", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "I stick her hands in the fan blades, nigga That’s when she told me where her man stayed, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I stick her hands in the fan blades, nigga"], "meaning": "This picture Wayne visually paints here is reminiscent of “Mona Lisa” a song from earlier in the album which tells  a story of a deceptive woman who sets her boyfriend up for a robbery.\n\nWeezy uses a very mild form of torture on a woman that he’s with (sticking her hand in the fan) to get her to reveal where her boyfriend lives.", "annotation_id": "15474346", "url": "https://genius.com/15474346", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Lookin’ like a open safe, nigga (Safe) We in this bitch, lookin’ like Miss Oprah’s safe, nigga (We’re safe)", "vault_lines": ["We in this bitch lookin' like a open safe, nigga (Open)"], "meaning": "“Looking like an open safe” means that Weezy looks like money, however looking like Oprah’s safe is a whole other story.\n\nOprah Winfrey is an extremely successful former talk show host, entrepreneur and philanthropist, who became one of the world’s 500 richest people with a net worth of $4 billion in 2018, just days before Tha Carter V dropped.", "annotation_id": "15474300", "url": "https://genius.com/15474300", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Bumbu out the glass, no chase, nigga (Bumbu)", "vault_lines": ["Bumbu out the glass, no chase, nigga (Bumbu)"], "meaning": "Bumbu Rum is an alcoholic beverage that has been produced as a “small batch, limited production run”.\n\nIn 2018 Weezy starred in the companies first ever commercial, which featured his hit song Lollipop.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UPfnlV-qbp4&frags=pl%2Cwn", "annotation_id": "15474251", "url": "https://genius.com/15474251", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "All eyes on me, get the mace, nigga (Agh)", "vault_lines": ["All eyes on me, get the mace, nigga (Agh)"], "meaning": "This line is a reference to some classic 90’s rap, 2Pac’s classic song and album “All Eyez On Me”, and Bad Boy signee Ma$e.", "annotation_id": "15474220", "url": "https://genius.com/15474220", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Tattoos on my face, nigga (Mm) Grill shinin’ in your face, nigga (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Tattoos on my face, nigga (Mm)"], "meaning": "Although not the first rapper to begin either of these trends, Weezy certainly popularized face tattoos and grills, trends that would set the precedent for basically every new generation rapper.\n\nhttps://imgix.ranker.com/user_node_img/50017/1000334552/original/four-tears-photo-u1?w=650&q=50&fm=jpg&fit=crop&crop=faces\nThis was one of the most iconic pictures of Wayne, showing the intricate details of his original face tattoos, as well as the quality of his diamond grill.\n\n\n\nWayne was also known for having the most iced out set of grills at the time, getting them permanently implanted in 2009.\n\n\n\nAt the time of Tha Carter V release, Wayne still has the signature grills, but many, many more face tattoos.", "annotation_id": "15474164", "url": "https://genius.com/15474164", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "She gon’ suck the prototype then swallow all the proteges, nigga", "vault_lines": ["She gon' suck the prototype then swallow all the proteges, nigga"], "meaning": "He’s referring to a woman performing oral sex on him. She will suck the prototype “him” and swallow the protégés (his potential offspring).\n\nA protégé is a person who is guided and supported by an older and more experienced or influential person.\n\nDrake and Nicki Minaj are some of Wayne’s well-known protégés.", "annotation_id": "15473425", "url": "https://genius.com/15473425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "line": "Snoop Dogg, murder was the case, nigga (Yeah, case)", "vault_lines": ["Snoop Dogg, murder was the case, nigga (Yeah, case)"], "meaning": "“Murder Was the Case” is a song by rapper Snoop  Dogg from his debut album Doggystyle. Doggystyle was released on November 23, 1993, by Death Row Records and Interscope Records.", "annotation_id": "15467987", "url": "https://genius.com/15467987", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Safe", "status": "done", "targets": 19, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-open-safe-lyrics", "genius_title": "Open Safe", "genius_id": 3088538, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Letter", "line": "Sometimes our loved ones don’t love us", "vault_lines": ["Sometimes our loved ones don't love us"], "meaning": "There are two meanings here.\nThe first is the obvious meaning that the people we love do not always love us.\nThe second refers to the preceding line and means that even though strippers love ones (dollars), the money doesn’t love them and will not always bring them happiness.", "annotation_id": "22478182", "url": "https://genius.com/22478182", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Letter", "line": "Price tags no mistakes, somebody payin’ for ’em", "vault_lines": ["Price tags no mistakes, somebody payin' for 'em"], "meaning": "Wayne might be referring to someone with a bounty on their head or price tag. While often times people will double check a price tag when it’s so high, Wayne does the same with the bounty. Pay in this context has a double meaning, 1) like the phrase “you’ll pay for this” and 2) someone is paying to have them killed", "annotation_id": "16016047", "url": "https://genius.com/16016047", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Letter", "line": "I talked to God the other day, he say he got a nigga So, I look death up in her eye and then I wink", "vault_lines": ["I talked to God the other day, he say he got a nigga"], "meaning": "Wayne might be referring to a time he contemplated suicide but prayed to God for help. He saved him so Wayne told death not today.", "annotation_id": "16015993", "url": "https://genius.com/16015993", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Letter", "line": "But understand looks are deceiving Lookin’ like I’m lookin’ for some grievance", "vault_lines": ["But understand looks are deceiving"], "meaning": "Wayne starts with the aphorism “looks can be deceiving” to say that although he might seem like he’s looking for pity or a hand out, he is not at all. He just feels compelled to express his darkest thoughts—thoughts that listeners might be surprised to hear and would identify with.", "annotation_id": "16015813", "url": "https://genius.com/16015813", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Letter", "line": "Doctor ain’t prescribin’ what he ain’t realizin’ Pain inside me got me thinkin’ ’bout me Tryna hang my body,", "vault_lines": ["Doctor ain't prescribin' what he ain't realizin'"], "meaning": "A doctor can only prescribe you medicine if he/she knows the source of the illness. In Wayne’s case, he’s been through so much trauma throughout his life it’s hard for him to be diagnosed…this is some real shit", "annotation_id": "15638764", "url": "https://genius.com/15638764", "state": "pending", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Letter", "line": "So if a nigga kill me, hope he mean it I just hope I die for a reason They probably won’t miss me ’til they need me Have problems with admittin’ that they need me, Lord", "vault_lines": ["So if a nigga kill me, hope he mean it"], "meaning": "Within these powerful lines, Wayne implements a concept that has been absent from prior records. This being his mortality. Although he has mentioned his suicide before he now is referring to the thought of being killed.\n\nThese lines might also be a reference to the recent news of Birdman setting up an attempted murder by the shooting of Wayne’s tour bus.", "annotation_id": "15529433", "url": "https://genius.com/15529433", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Letter", "line": "You know, when he told me Toya was havin’ a baby, I say, “Y’all young. You know y’all young.” But I said, “Be the best father you can be,” you know. And truly, he is that", "vault_lines": ["Sometimes I feel like I ain't shit"], "meaning": "In the outro of “Open Letter,” Ms. Cita remembers the time Wayne told her that he was having a child with Antonia Wright, who became pregnant at the age of 14. At 16, Weezy became a father to his first child, Reginae Carter, who is also featured on Tha Carter V.", "annotation_id": "15473987", "url": "https://genius.com/15473987", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Letter", "line": "I live and I learn, then die tryna teach ’em, Lord Die tryna reach ’em They care more about how much I leave than Where I leave it I hope I leave more of an impression on my kids To be destined to have blessings to believe in, Lord", "vault_lines": ["I live and I learn, then die tryna teach 'em, Lord"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has previously lived a hard life which he learned from and would now do anything, even die, to teach those lessons to his children.\n\nAlthough by saying “where’d I leave it”, he implies that he doesn’t care much about material things and has immense wealth, he hopes that he can use this wealth to leave the impression on his kids that they can be successful and do whatever they want, and that they aren’t just concerned with how much money he left them.\n\n\n\nWayne and his kids, Reginae, Dwayne III, Neal & Cameron", "annotation_id": "15473530", "url": "https://genius.com/15473530", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Wayne", "song": "Open Letter", "line": "Just got off the phone with my daughter Told her, ”I won’t hesitate to fuck a young nigga up”, Lord", "vault_lines": ["Just got off the phone with my son"], "meaning": "Wayne is likely talking about his oldest child and daughter Reginae, who is featured on “Famous.”\n\n\n\nReginae is in a public relationship with YFN Lucci, but that won’t stop Wayne from dealing with him or anyone else that mistreats his daughter.", "annotation_id": "15470901", "url": "https://genius.com/15470901", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
